-- QuestLocFlavor (generado 2026-10-17): objetivos completos, con dialogos, solo para narrar.
_G.QuestLocFlavor = _G.QuestLocFlavor or {}
QuestLocFlavor[4] = {
[2000]={"Gandalf stands by the Pillar of the Hand, on the way to Isengard.","Book 14, Chapter 3: The Flooded Ring","The very walls of Isengard have been damaged by some mighty force","A curious stillness covers the land, and pools of water stand near the road","'Well hello there!'","'We have several purposes now within the Ring of Isengard. May they all come to successful conclusion!\
\
'Ride north along the road to Isengard, and stay alert! We do not know what we will find as we approach Saruman's lair.'","'Hello there! It's been a long time, ${PLAYER}! I hope you are well.'","'Hello there!'","'I spoke briefly with Halbarad, and if I had business within Isengard before now I count it double. We must find if Lothrandir still lives within the Ring, ${PLAYER}. Let Gandalf speak with Saruman for weeks, if that is his desire; my thoughts are of my kinsman. I have not seen him for many years, but Lothrandir has been a friend for longer than that and I will not abandon him.\
\
'Let us ride along the road to Isengard! I am most curious to see what it is we will find.'","Talk to Gandalf by the Pillar of the Hand","Many purposes now collide within the Ring of Isengard.","You have found Merry and Pippin at the gate of Isengard.","Aragorn has asked you to ride along the road to Isengard, and to keep your eyes peeled as you go.","Ride along the road north to Isengard, and remain alert","'Look who it is, Merry!'","Gandalf has warned you that you might not recognize Isengard since last you saw it.","Ride north to the gate of Isengard","'Isengard has been much changed since last you beheld it, ${PLAYER}. You may not recognize it. I dare say Saruman himself does not, though he brought it upon himself.'"},
[2002]={"'The look on your face is quite a thing to see, my confused friend! Welcome to Isengard! You have had a number of adventures, I expect, and would you believe that we have as well? We have all come a long way from Lothlórien, haven't we?\
\
'Much of the trip was rather unpleasant, owing to our new friends Uglúk and Grishnákh. I suppose they're old friends now; we shan't be seeing them again, and that is a relief. Treebeard and Quickbeam are nice fellows, if a little odd. And I do believe I have grown several inches taller!'\
\
Pippin laughs at your confused look.\
\
'I don't mean metaphorically, ${PLAYER}, though perhaps I have at that. I mean that I actually have grown taller!'","The gate-house is filled with rubble, and the flood-waters have reached here too","'We found some pipe-weed inside the gate-house. Go inside and bring some more of it out here, and I will try to tell you the tale properly.'","'I think Pip is trying to confuse you on purpose, ${PLAYER}. He gets the chance to do that so infrequently that he delights in it whenever the opportunity presents itself.\
\
'It seems we have gone from the fire back into the frying pan, for once! Pip and I were dragged halfway across Rohan by our captors, and though we have arrived at Isengard, it was in the strong hands of a friend and not at the whips of Saruman's Orcs! It was Treebeard who brought us here, you see, and he is... well, he is Fangorn and Fangorn is he, apparently!\
\
'This is more difficult than I expected when I began to tell it! We found some pipe-weed inside the gate-house. How about you bring some more out here and I will try to tell it properly?'","'Would you go into the gate-house and bring out some more of the pipe-weed we found? It reminds me of the comforts of home, even in such a place as this!'","Book 14, Chapter 4: Took and Brandybuck","'Aragorn does not look pleased. To be fair, he often looks this way, but I suspect he is less pleased than usual!'","Pippin smiles at you amiably.","Merry and Pippin have made themselves quite at home at Isengard, but much of their story is still a mystery to you.","Bring the pipe-weed to Merry outside the gate-house","Aragorn is outside the gate-house at Isengard, and wears a concerned expression.","Merry is outside the gate of Isengard.","Enter the gate-house and look for the pipe-weed Merry mentioned","'That pipe-weed was not grown at Isengard, and it does not bear a resemblance only to that of the Southfarthing. That weed has come from the Shire, which means that Saruman has had his eye upon that land for some while, at least. I do not like that at all.\
\
'If our fortune holds, the Wizard will have no further chance for mischief. His interest in the Shire may have extended only to its pipe-weed.'","'Merry and I have been through a great deal. And I really am taller now! Can you not tell?'","'Strider always looks so grim.'","Aragorn nods at you, but says nothing.","'Ah, very good, my friend! This is a very high-quality pipe-weed of the sort they grow in the Southfarthing, back home. Allow me to refill my pipe and I can resume my story. I was going to tell you about Treebeard and the Ents, I believe. Let me see...\
\
'But it seems that Aragorn is troubled about something. Perhaps you should speak with him first, and I will continue my story when he has a happier look about him!'","Merry asked you to go inside the gate-house and bring out some more of the pipe-weed they found there."},
[2003]={"Elrond se encuentra en la biblioteca de la Última Morada, en Rivendel.\
\
Deberías volver con Elrond de inmediato y contarle lo que has descubierto.","Habla con Elrond","El diario de Laerdan contenía una horrenda descripción de su encarcelamiento y tortura en Sammath Baul.","No aprendes nada más del diario de Laerdan aparte de los detalles de su encarcelamiento y de sus encuentros con Amarthiel y Narmeleth, reales o imaginados. Elrond quizá entienda estas cosas mejor que tú.","'¡Ay! Estas son noticias tristes y terribles las que traes, ${PLAYER}. Ahora comprendo cómo fue quebrado Laerdan. Los males de Angmar son verdaderamente grandes si pueden convertir el amor de un padre por su hija en un arma terrible.\
\
'Esto presagia un mal aún mayor...'","Libro 14, Capítulo 5: La caída de Laerdan"},
[2004]={"'Hrum, hoom, hoom. The work of the Ents here is done, but Gandalf's work is only beginning. Yours too, perhaps. I do not understand this desire for... burárum... adventure. Do you not enjoy standing in a green field with the sunlight on your face? Do you not enjoy drinking deeply of cold mountain waters?'\
\
Treebeard rumbles for a moment.\
\
'It is no matter. The waters will cleanse this place, but some Orcs may still linger. Search the surface and see what you find. Gandalf tells me a friend of yours was imprisoned here. I hope you find some sign of him. We Ents allowed a number of Dunlendings to leave in peace, but saw no other friendly folk.'","Gandalf listens to your account closely, especially the last words of the dying Orc.\
\
'It is said that the last words spoken by the dying are the truest you will ever hear, and I do not doubt that this Orc believed them. But I do not.'","Almost every bone in this Orc's body seems to be broken. What could have done this?","Book 14, Chapter 5: Wizard to Manage","Treebeard believes you should search within the Ring of Isengard for any sign of your captive friend.","'Find Gandalf and see what he thinks we should do about Saruman. He went on ahead, to the base of Orthanc.'","Treebeard is by the base of Orthanc.\
\
Gandalf has asked you to speak with Treebeard while he considers what to do about Saruman.","Explore north of Orthanc","An Ent lies here, his skin burned and scorched","Talk to Gandalf by the base of Orthanc","Aragorn is concerned that Saruman may have further tricks up his sleeve.","'For now I must think. Leave me in peace!'","Gandalf is at the base of Orthanc, considering what to do about the Wizard waiting within.","'This sight fills me with sorrow, ${PLAYER}. Do you think Saruman understands what he has taken from this world? He must not. How could he?'\
\
Calenglad looks around at the still waters.\
\
'I heard Gandalf say that Ents are slow to be roused, but when they are there is little that can stand before them. I see it is true, but my heart goes out to this one, who will not return from this ring of stone.'","'Hrum, hoom, hoom.'","Explore west of Orthanc","Explore south of Orthanc","Talk to Treebeard at the base of Orthanc","'Aragorn is right to advise caution. Saruman has suffered a defeat, it is true, but we must not be over-confident or it will be no lasting defeat. He is cunning and full of tricks, and even a cornered beast can do great harm. Indeed, that is when it is most dangerous!'\
\
You tell Gandalf that Aragorn said much the same, and the Wizard smiles briefly.\
\
'Good! It seems he has learned something from me after all. But this is no time for idle talk. There is a Wizard to manage now. Speak to Treebeard. I must think on our next step.'","The Orc laughs weakly, and breathes his last","'Search the surface and see what you find. Gandalf tells me a friend of yours was imprisoned here. I hope you find some sign of him. We Ents allowed a number of Dunlendings to leave in peace, but saw no other friendly folk.'","'Saruman seems to be in a tough position, but I would counsel caution in our dealings with him. I do not doubt his ability to strike even now, and a cornered beast can still do great harm.\
\
'Gandalf went ahead to the base of Orthanc. Find him and see what he thinks of the situation.'","'You... filth. Come to finish the job? My time is through... curse the trees!'\
\
The Orc coughs again, and a deathly rattle passes his lips. He will not last long. Despite the pain he feels, the Orc musters enough strength to laugh coarsely.\
\
'You think... only my kind perished... when the flood came? There were prisoners... in the pits... and now they are drowned rats! Their lives... are on your conscience... wretched ${RACE}!'","This must have been the site of a great battle, for many corpses float in the water here","Gandalf is at the base of Orthanc, waiting to hear what you discovered in your search of the flooded Ring.","Talk to Gandalf at the base of Orthanc","A nearby Orc coughs up blood and snarls weakly at you","'I am saddened by the passing of Beechbone. He was a handsome Ent, and took good care of his flock. He did much good in his life, and no less than on his last day, when he trumpeted victory within the stone walls of Isengard.'"},
[2005]={"Find the entrance to the Isengard Depths, north of Orthanc","Surly scavengers can be found throughout the Isengard Depths.\
\
Golodir has asked you to defeat the scavengers that lurk within the flooded depths of Isengard, for one of them might know of Lothrandir's location, if the Ranger still lives.","A key drops from the scavenger's hand. Could Golodir have been right?","Defeated surly scavenger (${NUMBER}/6)","'One of these scavengers may have picked up the key to whatever cell holds our friend, if one does. I will keep searching, as will others of the company, and you should do the same! Defeat these scavengers and see what you can find.'","Talk to Golodir in the Isengard Depths","'An Orc gains nothing by being truthful to us, but may derive satisfaction by bringing us sorrow. I believe Lothrandir survives, but if he is not brought into the light soon it may become too late to save him. North of the tower you will find an entrance to depths below Isengard. Search the watery deeps for some news of Saruman's captive. He may yet live, if we hurry.'","Golodir is in the flooded depths beneath Isengard, waiting to hear the results of your search.","An entrance to the Isengard Depths can be found north of the tower.\
\
Gandalf believes Lothrandir may still live, and wants you to search for news of him in the caverns below Isengard.","Book 14, Chapter 6: The Drowning Pits","You steel your resolve and prepare to enter the flooded deeps below Isengard","Golodir also searches the Isengard Depths for news of Lothrandir.","'You found a key? Very good, very good. It is possible it will open the way to Lothrandir. I have found half a dozen keys already, and matching doors for half of those, but still no sign of my kinsman. Still, one of these may prove to be the one.'","'I believe Lothrandir survives, but if he is not brought into the light soon it may become too late to save him. North of the tower you will find an entrance to depths below Isengard. Search the watery deeps for some news of Saruman's captive. He may yet live, if we hurry.'","'If Lothrandir is down here, we will find him, ${PLAYER}. This pit has seen better days, but it will see worse still if our friend has come to harm. What few of Saruman's lackeys still lurk in the depths no longer carry out his will. They seem to be busy scavenging for treasure and fighting among themselves o'er it. Fools!\
\
'Many doors remain locked to us, and it could be one of these scavengers has picked up the key to whatever cell holds our friend. I will keep searching, as will others of the company, and you should do the same! Defeat these scavengers and see what you can find.'","Gandalf does not believe that Lothrandir perished beneath Isengard, and wants you to search for him.","Defeat surly scavenger (${NUMBER}/6)","Defeat surly scavenger (5/6)"},
[2006]={"'Por lo que me has contado, creo que Amarthiel ha engañado a Laerdan para que le lleve a ella a Narchuil. Temo que esté caminando directo hacia una trampa...'","Elrond se encuentra en su biblioteca en la Última Morada de Rivendel.\
\
Elrond desea hablar contigo acerca de lo que ha descubierto en el diario de Laerdan.","Habla con Elrond","Libro 14, Capítulo 6: El destino de Laerdan","Habla con Elrond sobre el destino que puede aguardar a Laerdan y experimenta 'Sesión: El destino de Laerdan' o lee la versión abreviada","Elrond está en su biblioteca en la Última Morada de Rivendel.\
\
Has hablado con Elrond sobre el destino de Laerdan, llegando a una conclusión funesta.","Creyendo que solo Narchuil puede restaurar la mente quebrada de su hija Narmeleth, Laerdan viaja a las antiguas forjas de anillos de Eregion. Cuando llega y se enfrenta al engaño de Amarthiel, lucha valerosamente, pero tiene pocas esperanzas y termina siendo superado.\
\
Ahora Amarthiel solo necesita reforjar las dos mitades rotas de Narchuil usando artes prohibidas para cumplir sus fines malignos...","Elrond quedó alarmado por la entrada del diario que le describiste, temiendo lo peor para Laerdan.","'Temo lo que está por venir, ${PLAYER}. El diario de Laerdan me llena de profunda desazón. Me preocupa que los engaños de Amarthiel conduzcan a Laerdan a un final terrible.\
\
'¿Me escucharás?'","'Pensar en el destino de Laerdan me aflige, pero no podemos quedarnos estancados en ello. Mayor aún es la amenaza que Amarthiel representará si Narchuil llegara a caer en sus manos.'"},
[2007]={"Talk to Halbarad north-west of Orthanc","Talk to Halbarad north-west of Orthanc, within the Ring of Isengard","'Golodir sends more keys? Very well. There are doors enough, that is certain. Lothrandir must be behind one of them. Speak to me when you are ready to search another building in the wall for my lost kinsman.'","Book 14, Chapter 7: Lothrandir","'Are you ready to continue the search for Lothrandir? We must remain hopeful, ${PLAYER}, though the search has been fruitless to this point. There are still many buildings in Isengard where he may be held, and we will search them all if we must.'","Halbarad has found a number of locked doors behind one of which Lothrandir might be held.","Halbarad is in the Ring of Isengard, north-west of Orthanc, looking for Lothrandir.\
\
Halbarad is waiting to go with you to search further buildings in Isengard for Lothrandir.","'I have exhausted most of the locked doors here in the depths, ${PLAYER}. Return to the surface and find Halbarad. There are some buildings in the wall to which he has not yet gained entry, and these keys may unlock some of those.\
\
'Before I left him, he said he was planning to search the buildings north-west of the tower. That is where you should seek him.'","'Return to the surface and find Halbarad. There are some buildings in the wall to which he has not yet gained entry, and these keys may unlock some of those.\
\
'Before I left him, he said he was planning to search the buildings north-west of the tower. That is where you should seek him.'","Halbarad is in the Ring of Isengard, north-west of Orthanc, looking for Lothrandir.\
\
Golodir has asked you to return to the surface and to help Halbarad with his search for the captive Ranger.","Halbarad is north-west of Orthanc.","'I cannot overstate my joy at Lothrandir's safe return, ${PLAYER}! I do not forgive Gun Ain her crimes, but I hope that the new woman that is Mercy finds some measure of peace. She has no place in Isengard any longer, and the path she takes from here will determine whether she ever finds another.'","Talk to Halbarad and continue his search for Lothrandir"},
[2008]={"'Encuentra al elfo Eglamír del que te hablé. Puede que pueda ayudarnos. Quizá lo encuentres, o halles noticias sobre él, en Celondim.'","Busca a Eglamír en Celondim","'No tengo muchas dudas sobre las intenciones del Enemigo, aunque no sé si llegarán a cumplirse. Esa es nuestra única esperanza.\
\
'Queda en Rivendel mucho del saber de los Anillos de Eregion, pues yo mismo lo escribí, y gracias a los esfuerzos de muchos se ha traído aún más aquí. Por desgracia, este saber revela poco que pudiera decirnos cuáles son los planes de Angmar.\
\
'Por fortuna, mi estudio del saber ha revelado una pista, un nombre. Ese nombre es Eglamír, sin duda un elfo que fue un amigo de confianza de Celebrimbor. Él podría tener conocimientos que te ayuden. Si aún se encuentra en la Tierra Media, puede que esté en Celondim. Muchos elfos pasan por allí antes de continuar hacia el sur, hacia los Puertos Grises. Viaja allí y, si lo encuentras, averigua qué ayuda puede prestarte en tu misión.'","El diario de Laerdan trae a Elrond preocupaciones mayores que solo el destino de Laerdan...","'Buscas conocimiento sobre la forja de anillos y sobre las antiguas forjas en ruinas de Mirobel. Te rechazaría de no ser porque el maestro Elrond te ha enviado. Él fue un gran amigo de Celebrimbor, así que te brindaré toda la ayuda que pueda.'","Elrond habló de un elfo llamado Eglamír que podría vivir en Celondim, en Ered Luin, muy al oeste de Rivendel y del Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Elrond te contó que Celebrimbor, sabiamente, no registró muchos de los detalles de la forja de anillos en el saber de Eregion. Sin embargo, Elrond encontró numerosas referencias a un elfo llamado Eglamír que podría saber más.","Libro 14, Capítulo 7: Los estragos del tiempo"},
[2009]={"Talk to Pippin by the foot of the steps","'Saruman's power is at an end. He will do us no more harm this day.'","Aragorn listens to your account of Lothrandir's rescue.\
\
'I am pleased to hear my kinsman is safe! I wished often that my friends might be close at hand, but I did not give voice to that desire, for I would not have wanted them put in danger. It is well that Lothrandir has emerged from the pit of Isengard unharmed.\
\
'Saruman emerged too, but not for long, and though he has returned to the tower I feel that his threat is ended! Gandalf will tell you more, if you would listen. I suspected some further mischief of Saruman, and I was not wrong to expect it! But all is ended now, and safely.'","'Gandalf will tell you more of what happened. I suspected some further mischief of Saruman, and I was not wrong to expect it! But all is ended now, and safely.'","Lothrandir has been rescued from the clutches of Saruman, but what has become of the Wizard himself?","Aragorn is on the stairs at the base of Orthanc.","Talk to Théoden on the steps of Orthanc","'Lothrandir suffered greatly at the hands of his captors, but his will remains strong, and I am certain he will recover from their torments. But what has become of Saruman? A crowd gathers by the foot of Orthanc. Go learn from them what has happened, and I will rejoin you shortly!'","Talk to Aragorn at the base of Orthanc","Talk to Gandalf on the steps of Orthanc","'The most peculiar thing happened, ${PLAYER}. Saruman and Gandalf engaged in a debate a few moments ago, and just when Gandalf seemed to get the upper hand, this object came hurtling down toward us from an upper window! It hit no one, thank goodness, but it would have quite hurt had the aim been better.\
\
'It was a dark globe of crystal, but with a fiery core deep in its heart. I picked it up and it seemed much heavier than its size. Very odd. I carried it up the steps to give it to Gandalf, but when he saw what I bore he hurried down and took it from me quickly. He says it was thrown not by Saruman but by Gríma Wormtongue, who I had the distinct displeasure of meeting just yesterday.\
\
'The globe is a mystery. I wonder what it was?'","Book 14, Chapter 8: Allies of the King","'Gandalf says that Saruman can do us no more harm, but I do not know if he is right.'","Halbarad has come to the base of Orthanc.","'Saruman has come to the end of his power, ${PLAYER}. I think he will no longer be a danger to Rohan.'\
\
Gandalf sighs heavily, and you are surprised to see a deep sadness in his eyes.\
\
'I offered him his freedom, but after working such deceits as he has done for so long he did not see that it was an offer made in good faith. The treacherous see only treachery, and so it was with Saruman at the end. He has his life, but I fear he will not see this as a mercy. I have cast him from the order and from the White Council. His staff is broken, and he will work no further plots.\
\
'But he has his life. He will remain within Orthanc, and think on his old designs, and mourn. But he will no longer endanger Rohan, and I think he knows that if Mordor does have victory in the days ahead, the servants of that land will not forget the treacheries he worked on his own behalf.'","'I cannot help but wonder about that dark crystal globe. What was it, do you think?'","'The Riddermark has suffered greatly at the hands of Saruman, but it will suffer no longer. He is locked in his tower, and Gandalf has cast him from the Order of the Wizards.\
\
'The traitor used one last weapon, and it may have been his deadliest: the power of his voice. I know the extent of his crimes, and even so I nearly succumbed to the soothing persuasion of his words. We are fortunate Gandalf was here and could shatter the reverie.'","'Is it true? The threat of Isengard has ended? Saruman has occupied our thoughts for so long, and caused so much hardship, I never believed he would not!\
\
'We have come so far, ${PLAYER}: from Rivendell, through Hollin, into Enedwaith and Dunland, and here at last to the stronghold of Saruman. Many of my kin fell along the way, but each of them, all of them, were allies of the king to come: Aragorn, son of Arathorn, heir of Isildur.\
\
'You, too, have been a friend of Aragorn, and to all the Grey Company. I thank you, ${PLAYER}. Wherever our road leads now, know that you have my thanks and my friendship.'","Gandalf, Théoden, and Pippin all witnessed the confrontation with Saruman and wish to speak with you about the Wizard's schemes.","'A crowd has gathered at the foot of Orthanc. Go there and see what has happened, and I will rejoin you shortly.'","Talk to Halbarad by the base of Orthanc"},
[2010]={"'¡Saludos, ${PLAYER}! ¿Buscas todavía más aventuras en las Quebradas de los Túmulos?'","'¿Qué? ¿Quieres ir a las Quebradas de los Túmulos para encontrar algún tipo de herramienta? Ya hemos tenido suficientes problemas con espectros en esta ciudad.\
\
'Si quieres saber algo sobre esos viejos túmulos, ve a molestar a Newbold Cortahoja, en el Archivo de la Escalera de los Eruditos.'","Libro 14, Capítulo 8: Un Amigo de los Elfos de Eregion","'Habla con la gente de Bree y ve si puedes averiguar la ubicación del túmulo del que te hablé.'","Descubre a alguien en Bree que tenga conocimiento sobre las Quebradas de los Túmulos","Newbold Cortahoja se encuentra en el Archivo de la Escalera de los Eruditos, en Bree.\
\
Te aconsejaron buscar a Newbold Cortahoja para averiguar más sobre la ubicación de la herramienta de forja de Celebrimbor.","'Las Quebradas de los Túmulos son un lugar oscuro, lleno de cosas malignas. No importa cuánto intentemos purificarlas, el terror persiste. ¿Qué puedes hacer para expulsar algo que ya está muerto?\
\
'Si necesitas encontrar un túmulo específico, será mejor que preguntes a Newbold Cortahoja, en el Archivo de la Escalera de los Eruditos.'","'Hablaré poco del saber de los Anillos de Eregion. Es un conocimiento peligroso, aprendido del Señor Oscuro, y no debería explorarse más.\
\
'No obstante, te diré esto: en los días de Eregion, nuestro señor Celebrimbor le entregó a un Amigo de los Elfos —un hombre de las Tierras de Bree— una de sus herramientas de forja. Esperaría que dicha herramienta hubiese sido enterrada con él, como es costumbre entre los Hombres.\
\
'Seguramente puedas encontrar en Bree a alguien que conozca la ubicación del túmulo donde yace la herramienta de forja. Quizá alguien en su Ayuntamiento, algún cliente de la posada, o incluso algún miembro de su Guardia.'","Para aprender más sobre el saber de los Anillos de Eregion, Elrond te envió a Eglamír, un elfo de Eregion que ahora reside en Celondim.","Bree se encuentra en las Tierras de Bree, muy al este de Ered Luin.\
\
Eglamír habló poco del saber de los Anillos de Eregion, pero sí te dijo que el herrero de anillos Celebrimbor entregó una herramienta de forja a un hombre de las Tierras de Bree. Sugiere que encuentres a alguien en Bree que sepa dónde está el túmulo de aquel hombre.","'Bueno, ¿qué era lo que querías otra vez? Ah, ¡las Quebradas de los Túmulos! ¿Por qué no lo dijiste antes? Ese lugar tiene mala fama, si no te molesta que lo diga, y yo me mantendría lejos de allí.\
\
'Pero si de verdad quieres saber más sobre esos túmulos, deberías hablar con Newbold Cortahoja, allá arriba en el Archivo de la Escalera de los Eruditos.'","Habla con Newbold Cortahoja"},
[2011]={"Habla con Newbold Cortahoja en Bree","'La tumba que buscas se encuentra junto a la entrada de los túmulos de Haudh Iarchith, en el sur de las Quebradas de los Túmulos.'","'¿Así que buscas información sobre la herramienta de forja de Celebrimbor y Maenadar el Artesano? Conozco bien esa historia.\
\
'Lamentablemente, no será fácil encontrar la herramienta, si es que aún existe. Fue enterrada junto a Maenadar en Haudh Iarchith, que desde entonces se ha visto infestada de espectros de la peor calaña.\
\
'Haudh Iarchith se encuentra en la parte sur de las Quebradas de los Túmulos, y la tumba de Maenadar está junto a su entrada, en el seno de un túmulo mayor. Sé prudente en tu viaje... los muertos no reciben bien a les visitantes.'","Newbold Cortahoja está en el Archivo de la Escalera de los Eruditos, en Bree.\
\
Llegaste demasiado tarde a la tumba de Maenadar y la encontraste saqueada. Angmar llegó primero. Deberías regresar con Newbold Cortahoja para averiguar si sabe algo más.","Eglamír te envió en busca de alguien con conocimiento de las Quebradas de los Túmulos y de la herramienta de forja de Celebrimbor.","La tumba de Maenadar el Artesano fue perturbada recientemente y todas las reliquias que pudieran haber reposado allí han sido retiradas...","Encuentra la tumba de Maenadar el Artesano","La tumba está vacía de reliquias","La tumba de Maenadar se encuentra en el pequeño túmulo junto a la entrada de Haudh Iarchith, en la parte sur de las Quebradas de los Túmulos.\
\
Newbold Cortahoja te dijo que la herramienta de forja puede encontrarse en la tumba de Maenadar el Artesano.","'Es una lástima, ${PLAYER}. Cada vez llegan más viajeros siniestros desde el sur, y no sería extraño que algunos fueran saqueadores de tumbas.'","Libro 14, Capítulo 9: Los Túmulos de Haudh Iarchith"},
[2012]={"'Narmeleth habrá llegado a estas alturas. Ve a la antigua habitación de su padre y escucha lo que tiene que decir sobre la situación aquí en Angmar. Espero que sepas lo que estás haciendo, ${PLAYER}, porque todavía tengo mis reservas de que realmente haya abandonado sus viejas costumbres.'","Narmeleth está en la habitación antigua de su padre en Gath Forthnír, en las tierras del norte de Angmar.\
\
Narmeleth te ha dicho que hables con Golodir y averigües qué ha pasado con la espada rota de Dúnachar.","'¿Narmeleth ha encontrado un plan para librarnos de Mordirith? Estoy listo para escucharlo.'","Narmeleth cree que conoce la debilidad de Mordirith.","Golodir está en su habitación en Gath Forthnír.\
\
Narmeleth te ha dicho que hables con Golodir y averigües qué ha pasado con la espada rota de Dúnachar.","'Gracias por hablar en mi nombre, ${PLAYER}. Desde aquí podemos poner en marcha el plan para derrotar a Mordirith finalmente.\
\
'Las últimas palabras de mi padre me revelaron cómo se puede derrotar a Mordirith. Aunque ha regresado de Minas Morgul con gran poder, todavía lleva la cicatriz de la espada de Golodir, Dúnachar, que lo atravesó y lo envió de vuelta a su malvado amo.\
\
'Si presentamos este arma ante él, incluso en su estado roto, la memoria de su herida será suficiente para hacer que Mordirith dudé.\
\
'Habla con Golodir para ver qué ha pasado con la espada rota de Dúnachar.'","Habla con Narmeleth en Gath Forthnír","Libro 15, Capítulo 10: La espada rota de Dúnachar","'Es un destino extraño, tanto Laerdan como yo perdemos hijas a causa de Angmar.'"},
[2013]={"Golodir está en Gath Forthnír, en las tierras del norte de Angmar.\
\
Debes volver a Golodir con la empuñadura rota de Dúnachar.","Narmeleth piensa que el hecho de mostrar la empuñadura rota de Dúnachar a Mordirith debilitará su voluntad.","'Con la empuñadura de Dúnachar, pondremos fin definitivo a Mordirith.'","Recupera la empuñadura rota de Dúnachar","'¿No has encontrado la espada todavía, ${PLAYER}?'","La tumba de Lorniel se encuentra en las colinas del norte de Gorothlad, al sur de Nan Gurth en Angmar.\
\
Golodir te ha dado la ubicación de Dúnachar y te ha otorgado permiso para recuperarlo.","La empuñadura rota de Dúnachar recuperada","'Confío en que la empuñadura no fue demasiado difícil de encontrar?'","Libro 15, Capítulo 11: El regalo final de un padre","Lleva la empuñadura a Golodir","'La tumba de Lorniel se encuentra en las colinas del norte de Gorothlad, al sur de Nan Gurth.'","Golodir escucha tu relato del plan de Narmeleth y asiente.\
\
'Llevé la empuñadura rota de Dúnachar conmigo cuando enterré a mi querida Lorniel, y junto a su tumba sigue estando. Después de su muerte la llevamos lo más lejos que pudimos bajo el amparo de la oscuridad; descansa en la cima de una colina en las laderas del norte de Gorothlad.\
\
'Si la espada de Dúnachar te ayudará en tu lucha contra Mordirith, te doy permiso para recuperarla.'"},
[2014]={"Habla con Glorfindel en Rivendel","'No te dejes oprimir por el dolor, ${PLAYER}. Narmeleth vivirá de nuevo en las Tierras Inmortales y Eärnur encontrará la paz que perdió hace tanto tiempo...'","Habla con Failloth en Rivendel","Narmeleth está en Gath Forthnír, en las tierras del norte de Angmar.\
\
Ella te ha pedido que reúnas amigos y hables con ella de nuevo para comenzar el asalto final.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está destinada a una comunidad. Si eliges emprender esta misión solo, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'¿Has encontrado la empuñadura de Dúnachar, ${PLAYER}?'","'La muerte de Narmeleth me duele, aunque pueda parecer extraño decir algo así después de todo el mal que hizo. La caída de Mordirith es una esperanza más allá de la esperanza, y la destrucción de Narchuil y Mordrambor será una bendición para nuestros esfuerzos en Angmar.\
\
'Lleva la noticia de la caída de Mordirith a Rivendel, porque aliviará los consejos de los muchos que todavía deben pensar en el norte.'","Habla con Elrond en Rivendel","'Narmeleth te está esperando.'","Failloth está en la plaza de la Última Morada en Rivendel.\
\
Elrond te dijo que recuperaras el legado de Laerdan de Failloth, la encargada de Rivendel.","'Las palabras de Glorfindel han demostrado su sabiduría, ya sea por mano de Narmeleth o por ninguna, aunque es evidente que también desempeñaste un papel importante en la caída de Mordirith, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'No te cargues con la opresión de la tristeza. Con el sacrificio noble de Narmeleth, ella se ha redimido y ha ganado un lugar entre los más grandes de nuestro pueblo en las Tierras Inmortales.\
\
'Nuestro enemigo del norte ha sido finalmente derrotado. Creo que tal fin le ha sido impuesto que ya no causará problemas en la Tierra Media; Eärnur puede finalmente descansar en paz.\
\
'Parece que Laerdan tiene una última parte que jugar en todos estos eventos. Mientras Failloth, una de las encargadas, estaba limpiando las habitaciones de Laerdan, se encontró un paquete dirigido a ti, ${PLAYER}. Parece que él lo dejó para ti antes de partir para Eregion.\
\
'He pedido que el paquete permanezca en el cuidado de Failloth hasta tu regreso a Imladris. Ahora que has llegado, deberías buscarla y reclamar el legado de Laerdan.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir? Bien... no hay más tiempo que perder, y tenemos un largo camino por recorrer.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está destinada a una comunidad. Si eliges emprender esta misión solo, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'Lleva la noticia de la derrota de Mordirith al maestro Elrond en Rivendel, ${PLAYER}.'","Habla con Golodir en Gath Forthnír","Narmeleth busca poner fin a Mordrambor y Mordirith de una vez por todas.","'Failloth, la encargada, debería estar en la plaza de mi casa. Búscala cuando tengas un momento, ${PLAYER}.'","'Pensé que no volvería a ver esta empuñadura. Su peso me trae recuerdos tanto dolorosos como reconfortantes. Esta espada me sirvió durante mucho tiempo antes de ser destruida por el Falso Rey.\
\
'Entrega la empuñadura a Narmeleth. Ella se ha estado preparando para el asalto final y te espera regresar.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está destinada a una comunidad. Si eliges emprender esta misión solo, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Gath Forthnír está en las tierras del norte de Angmar.\
\
Golodir te dijo que llevaras la empuñadura a Narmeleth en Gath Forthnír.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está destinada a una comunidad. Si eliges emprender esta misión solo, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'Puedes encontrar a Elrond en la biblioteca de la Última Morada, ${PLAYER}.'","Entrega la empuñadura a Narmeleth","'¡Ay! ¡Mordirith ha caído! Estas son grandes noticias en verdad, aunque tejidas con tragedia, como todas las cosas en estos días de lucha. Narmeleth era una elfa valiente, fuerte más allá de la medida de los sabios.\
\
'Lleva la noticia al maestro Elrond. Debería escuchar estas palabras de alguien que fue testigo del evento!'","Rivendel está en la esquina noreste del Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Golodir te envió a hablar con Glorfindel y traerle noticias de la derrota de Mordirith.","'¡La empuñadura de Dúnachar! Confío en que no fue demasiado difícil de encontrar?\
\
'Reúne compañeros y habla conmigo otra vez cuando puedas atacar Gador Gúlaran. El tiempo se está agotando, y nuestro camino será largo y peligroso.'","Gath Forthnír está en las tierras del norte de Angmar.\
\
Debes hablar con Golodir en Gath Forthnír.","Ataca Gador Gúlaran","'¿Eres ${PLAYER}, no es así?'","Elrond puede ser encontrado en la Última Morada en Rivendel.\
\
Glorfindel te dijo que entregaras tus noticias al maestro Elrond.","libro 15, Capítulo 12: Solo queda una esperanza","'¿Has llevado tus noticias a Glorfindel en Rivendel? Él querrá saber de todo lo que ha pasado desde que estuviste por última vez en ese lugar.'"},
[2015]={"Habla con Glorfindel en Rivendel","Glorfindel puede encontrarse fuera de la Última Morada hacia el sudeste, mirando hacia las Cataratas de Imladris.\
\
Elrond te ha pedido que hables con Glorfindel.","Habla con Narmeleth en Delossad","'Ten cuidado cuando hables con Amarthiel, ${PLAYER}.'","'¿El señor Glorfindel te ha pedido que interrogues a Amarthiel?\
\
'Delossad está al suroeste de Rivendel, en el Tâl Bruinen.'","Delossad está al suroeste de Rivendel en el Tâl Bruinen, al este de la cabaña de Garbert.\
\
Glorfindel te ha pedido que interrogues con Narmeleth en Delossad.","'Delossad está al suroeste de Rivendel, en la región deL Bosque de los Trolls llamada Tâl Bruinen.'","'Glorfindel puede encontrarse fuera de la Última Morada hacia el sudeste, mirando hacia las Cataratas de Imladris.'","'Estoy preocupado, ${PLAYER}, como estoy seguro de que tú lo estás, por la captura de Amarthiel. Aunque ha sido despojada de Narchuil, aún puede representar una amenaza para los desprevenidos.\
\
'No es una decisión menor decidir el destino de Amarthiel. Pero hay otros asuntos urgentes; he recibido noticias extrañas de mis exploradores en el sur. Debo ocuparme de estas cosas, así como de otras, y he encomendado el caso de Amarthiel al señor elfo Glorfindel. Mira qué consejo puede darte, y tal vez puedas ofrecerle tu ayuda para emitir su juicio.\
\
'Puedes encontrar al señor Glorfindel fuera de mi casa, hacia el sudeste.'","Elrond comparte tus preocupaciones sobre Amarthiel y ha pedido al señor Glorfindel que se ocupe de este asunto.","Libro 15, Capítulo 1: Un destino extraño","'La cuestión de Amarthiel es muy grave. Es un destino extraño que Amarthiel, o Narmeleth como ahora desea ser llamada, esté otra vez encarcelada donde fue retenida durante tanto tiempo...\
\
'Es necesario interrogarla; el Maestro Elrond me ha pedido que me ocupe de este asunto de inmediato, pero tengo muchas otras obligaciones. Te pediría que fueras a hablar con ella; quizás puedas obtener información útil de Amarthiel.\
\
'${PLAYER}, ten cuidado con sus palabras. Esto podría ser otra trampa suya, aunque mi corazón me dice que habla con sinceridad.'","Estoy sorprendido, ${PLAYER}. No pensé que fueras tú quien decidiera venir a escuchar la historia de una doncella elfa quebrantada.'"},
[2016]={"'Aunque pocos lo crean, me he liberado del mal que una vez me atrapó. Fue como el levantamiento de un velo y la liberación de las cadenas que me mantuvieron durante tanto tiempo. Ya no estoy consumida por el anillo Narchuil, ni por el deseo de poseerlo.\
\
'Tengo noticias terribles -- una advertencia para aquellos que quieran escuchar: Como Amarthiel, había oído susurros de una ciudad oculta de los Dúnedain, Esteldín. Envié a un maestro espía para descubrir su ubicación, y ahora seguramente ya la han encontrado. \
\
'Los montaraces deben ser advertidos de esta amenaza; si el espía logra infiltrarse en Esteldín, moverán una gran fuerza contra ella en secreto. Viaja a las Quebradas del Norte y advierte al líder de este campamento sobre la traición que he sembrado.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Viajarás automáticamente a Esteldín en las Quebradas del Norte cuando aceptes esta misión.</rgb>","Esteldín está en las Quebradas del Norte, una tierra al noroeste del Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Narmeleth desea que viajes a Esteldín y adviertas a Halbarad sobre el espía.","'Debes apresurarte. Esteldín no tiene tiempo para esperar.'","Habla con Halbarad en Esteldín","'Solo sé que Esteldín se encuentra en algún lugar de las Quebradas del Norte.'","Libro 15, capítulo 2: Una amenaza para los Dúnedain","'¿Qué te trae a Esteldín hoy, ${PLAYER}?'","Narmeleth ha abandonado sus caminos malvados y ha ofrecido su conocimiento para ayudar a los Pueblos Libres."},
[2017]={"Halbarad está en Esteldín, en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Vuelve a hablar con Halbarad para informarle de que uno de los refugiados ha desaparecido.","'No he visto nada extraño desde que dejé Angmar, ${CLASS}.'","Habla con los refugiados (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Debes ayudar a demostrar que Narmeleth dice la verdad interrogando a los refugiados de Angmar.","'Debemos descubrir la verdad en este asunto, ${PLAYER}.'","Los refugiados están fuera de la biblioteca, cerca de la sala de artesanía, viendo a los montaraces entrenar, y junto al maestro de establos en Esteldín.\
\
Halbarad no está convencido de las intenciones de Narmeleth, pero te ha permitido interrogar a los refugiados de Angmar.","'¿Un espía? ¿Entre nosotros aquí en Esteldín? Parece poco probable que un espía pueda penetrar nuestras filas, y aún menos probable dada la fuente de esta información...\
\
'Si insistes en seguir con el asunto, ve a hablar con los refugiados que fueron rescatados recientemente de Angmar. Sin duda descubrirás que son simples pastores y agricultores.\
\
'Habla con los refugiados fuera de la biblioteca, cerca de la sala de artesanía, viendo a mis parientes entrenar, y junto al maestro de establos... aunque veo poca sabiduría en confiar en las palabras del enemigo, ${PLAYER}.'","'¿Un espía? Mira, he visto muchas cosas, pero no un espía.'","'Ni siquiera sé cómo reconocer lo que buscas, ${CLASS}. No soy más que un simple granjero.'","Libro 15, Capítulo 3: La carga de la prueba","'Veo poca sabiduría en confiar en las palabras del enemigo, ${PLAYER}, pero puedes encontrar a los refugiados fuera de la biblioteca, cerca de la sala de artesanía, viendo a mis parientes entrenar, y junto al maestro de establos.'","'¿Uno de los refugiados ha desaparecido?'","Habla con Halbarad en Esteldín","Alis ha desaparecido"},
[2018]={"Encuentra a la refugiada desaparecida","Libro 15, Capítulo 4: El destino de Esteldín","'Busca en el paso más al este hacia Angmar a la refugiada desaparecida, ${PLAYER}.'","Halbarad te ha pedido que busques a la refugiada desaparecida y la lleves de vuelta a Esteldín.","La refugiada puede encontrarse en el paso más al este entre las Quebradas del Norte y Angmar.\
\
Halbarad te ha pedido que busques señales de la presencia de la refugiada desaparecida.","'Aquellos a quienes tomamos bajo protección aquí en Esteldín no pueden partir sin mi permiso bajo pena de muerte. Esta es la ley, y nos ha protegido y mantenido ocultos de nuestros enemigos.\
\
'Es probable que esta refugiada solo esté regresando a su hogar y que no sea una espía, pero aún así debe ser juzgada por romper las leyes de Esteldín.\
\
'Busca en el paso más al este hacia Angmar y trae de vuelta a la refugiada, ya sea espía o no.'","'¡Alis era una espía! Lamento haber desconfiado de tu consejo, aunque sin duda incluso los Sabios no habrían esperado una ayuda de este tipo de un aliado tan inesperado.'","Espía refugiada derrotada","'Estos son tiempos extraños, con aliados aún más extraños, ${PLAYER}.'","Halbarad está en Esteldín, en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Deberías volver a Halbarad e informarle que la refugiada era una espía.","Habla con Halbarad en Esteldín","'¡Depón tus armas y vete, ${CLASS}. No me detendrán!'"},
[2019]={"'Me alegra que al menos una de mis malas acciones haya sido enmendada. Sin embargo, hay tantas otras cuyo peso debo soportar por el resto de mis días, por pocos que sean...'","Habla con Narmeleth en Delossad","'Esteldín permanece escondida, y aunque me alegra que se haya evitado el desastre, todavía no confío completamente en el consejo de Amarthiel... no, Narmeleth, que durante tanto tiempo nos trajo conflictos y guerras.\
\
'Puede que todavía tenga una gran cantidad de información para ofrecer a nuestra causa, así que puedes regresar a Delossad con mis agradecimientos, pero ten cuidado. No estoy completamente convencido de que se pueda confiar en ella en todos los asuntos y de que esto no sea algún gran plan del enemigo.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Viajarás automáticamente a Delossad en Tâl Bruinen cuando aceptes esta misión.</rgb>","La advertencia de Narmeleth sobre el espía resultó ser cierta y demostró sus buenas intenciones a Halbarad.","'Delossad se encuentra en Tâl Bruinen, al sur del Bosque de los Trolls y al sureste de las Quebradas del Norte.'","Narmeleth está en Delossad, en Tâl Bruinen.\
\
Halbarad te ha pedido que le des las gracias a Narmeleth por su ayuda para salvar a Esteldín.","'Todavía no confío completamente en los consejos de Narmeleth, pero en esto, ella demostró ser digna.'","Libro 15, Capítulo 5: El Anillo de la Verdad"},
[2020]={"Narmeleth permanece prisionera en Delossad, al sur del Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Ve a hablar con Narmeleth para que te cuente su trágica historia.","Habla con Narmeleth en Delossad","Libro 15, Capítulo 6: Hija de la discordia","'Era joven e ingenua, y Sauron me enseñó los secretos de la fabricación de anillos, y por eso caí en su trampa. Con su ayuda, forjé un anillo potente, lo suficientemente poderoso como para influir en los corazones y las mentes de quienes me rodeaban. Sin embargo, él no vio en mí la habilidad de una herrera de anillos, sino la destreza de una guerrera, cruel y hermosa.\
\
'Pero las violentas pérdidas de Narchuil y mi padre me han purgado del hechizo y el espíritu que me ataban a la voluntad de Sauron. Soy verdaderamente libre, aunque he pagado un precio amargo por mi locura hace tantos años.\
\
'Lamento todas las acciones que realicé bajo el hechizo de mi locura. Cada muerte a mi mano es un peso aplastante que llevaré para siempre, incluso hacia las Tierras Inmortales, si alguna vez se me permite entrar en esos sagrados salones.'","'Me alegra que hayas regresado, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'No siempre fui como me has conocido, porque aunque estaba condenada al fracaso, las intenciones de mi corazón siempre fueron verdaderas. Lástima que las sombras corrompan incluso los objetivos más nobles.\
\
'Tengo mucho que contar, si quieres escucharme.'","Delossad está en el Bosque de los Trolls, al suroeste de Rivendel.\
\
Narmeleth desea hablar contigo allí.","Escucha el relato de Narmeleth y experimenta 'Sesión: Hija de la discordia' o lee un relato abreviado","La verdad de la advertencia de Narmeleth le ha ganado cierta confianza.","'Me ha costado muy caro liberarme del Señor Oscuro.'","'He tenido mucho tiempo para reflexionar: sobre aquellos a quienes he herido, sobre el sufrimiento infligido por mi causa, y mis pensamientos se vuelven a menudo hacia mi padre que está perdido.\
\
'Si me prestas atención, te contaré mi caída. Me gustaría mucho expresar toda la historia a otro antes de que pase al olvido.\
\
'¿Me escucharás, ${PLAYER}?'","Durante la Segunda Edad, el Señor Oscuro llegó a Eregion con una apariencia noble para seducir a los Elfos con la promesa de un conocimiento secreto. Cautivó a Narmeleth, alejándola de la protección de su padre Laerdan y del pueblo de Celebrimbor, y las semillas de su corrupción son sembradas..."},
[2021]={"Glorfindel está en Rivendel, al sureste de la casa de Elrond.\
\
Narmeleth te ha pedido que hables con Glorfindel de su parte.","'Habla con el señor Glorfindel de mi parte... Me gustaría hacer algo de bien para redimir parte de mis malas acciones que he cometido en este mundo.'","'${PLAYER}, me gustaría participar en la lucha contra el mal que he creado. Mordirith ha recuperado Narchuil, y sin duda buscará usar sus poderes pronto.\
\
'Mordrambor es arrogante, pero tiene habilidad en las Artes Oscuras del Enemigo y no es menos malvado que su maestro. Él también sigue siendo una amenaza que permití que persistiera.\
\
'Me gustaría ayudar a sanar las heridas que he infligido al mundo, incluso si es con el acto más pequeño. Si pudieras hablar con Glorfindel por mí, aceptaré mi juicio, sea cual sea.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Viajarás automáticamente a Rivendel en el Bosque de los Trolls cuando aceptes esta misión.</rgb>","Habla con Glorfindel","Libro 15, Capítulo 7: El Concilio Final","'Una buena acción no borra todo lo que hizo como Amarthiel, sin importar el nombre que se dé ahora, pero reflexionaré sobre todo lo que me has dicho.\
\
'El maestro Elrond ha pedido que Narmeleth sea juzgada, y me gustaría que me acompañaras mientras la interrogan.'","Glorfindel está en Rivendel cerca de las cataratas de Imladris, al sureste de la casa de Elrond.\
\
Deberías volver y hablar con Glorfindel en Rivendel.","Acompaña a Glorfindel al Concilio Final","'Tenemos mucho que hacer, ${PLAYER}.'","Narmeleth te contó la trágica historia de su caída y su transformación en Amarthiel, la Campeona de Angmar.","'Por tu palabra, ${PLAYER}, Narmeleth es libre. Si no fuera por tu excelente reputación entre los míos, no habría permitido su partida.\
\
'Pero escúchame bien antes de partir: ten cuidado y mantente vigilante. Aunque mis pensamientos me aconsejan confiar en que no queda traición en Narmeleth, percibo que el deseo de Narchuil no la ha abandonado por completo.'","Acompañaste a Glorfindel al Concilio final"},
[2022]={"Habla con Narmeleth en Delossad","Libro 15, Capítulo 8: Solo lo justo","Delossad se encuentra en el sur del Bosque de los Trolls, al suroeste de Rivendel.\
\
Narmeleth ha pedido hablar contigo de inmediato.","'Debemos ser rápidos si esperamos detener a Mordirith. Solo conozco un lugar en el que podría albergar a su repugnante montura. En lo profundo de Barad Gúlaran, Mordirith tiene una guarida secreta: Gador Gúlaran. El camino hacia allí está lleno de peligros, pero quizás podamos coger a Mordirith desprevenido. No habrá previsto que confiarías lo suficiente en mí para permitirme regresar a Angmar, y esta desconfianza será su perdición.\
\
'Empecemos nuestros últimos preparativos.'","'Podemos comenzar nuestros últimos preparativos.'","'Delossad se encuentra en el sur del Bosque de los Trolls, al suroeste de Rivendel. Allí encontrarás a Narmeleth.'","El concilio de Glorfindel decidió liberar a Narmeleth de su prisión y pedirle que ayudara a combatir a Mordirith.","'Narmeleth ha enviado un mensaje diciendo que desea hablar contigo, ${PLAYER}. Quiere comenzar los preparativos para el viaje de inmediato y te pide que regreses a Delossad lo más rápido posible.\
\
'Por favor, no olvides mi consejo y ten cuidado al tratar con Narmeleth en caso de que nos estén engañando. Aunque parezca haber cambiado, uno no se adentra tan profundamente en el reino de la Sombra sin encontrar sus manos para siempre manchadas por su influencia.\
\
'Temo que tu camino esté lleno de peligros, pero espero que encuentres luz en la oscuridad cuando todo haya terminado.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Viajarás automáticamente a Delossad en Tâl Bruinen cuando aceptes esta misión.</rgb>"},
[2023]={"Habla con Golodir en Gath Forthnír","'Gath Forthnír está en el norte de Angmar, al noreste de Imlad Balchorth.'","Narmeleth está lista para comenzar su viaje a Angmar.","'¿Amarthiel? ¿En Gath Forthnír? ¡Lo prohíbo! ¿Deberíamos también preparar habitaciones para Mordrambor y Mordirith? No permitiré que mis enemigos estén dentro de las murallas del bastión cuyas puertas han sido defendidas por aquellos cuya sangre ha derramado.\
\
'No, quizás hablé demasiado rápido. Lo siento, ${PLAYER}. Recuerdo los largos años en los que Laerdan trató de liberar a su hija del mal que la consumía, incluso a su propia perdición. Como último favor a mi querido amigo, albergaré a Narmeleth en Gath Forthnír.'","Gath Forthnír está en el norte de Angmar, al noreste de Imlad Balchorth.\
\
Narmeleth está lista para viajar a Gath Forthnír y hablar con Golodir.","'Ahora podemos hacer el viaje a Gath Forthnír en Angmar, donde mi padre se escondió durante tanto tiempo, esperando mi regreso. Desde Gath Forthnír, podremos formar nuestro plan de ataque.\
\
'Tendrás que ir por delante y llevar la palabra a Golodir. Dudo que esté ansioso por permitir mi admisión en Gath Forthnír, pero es un buen hombre. Habla con Golodir y pídele que me deje entrar, y lo seguiré si lo permite.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Viajarás automáticamente a Gath Forthnír en Angmar cuando aceptes esta misión.</rgb>","Libro 15, Capítulo 9: El regreso de una campeona","'Si puedo ayudarte, lo haré, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[2024]={"Los hombres demacrados residen probablemente en las ruinas, al este de Haragmar.\
\
Radagast te habló de los hombres demacrados, nigromantes al servicio de Sauron, responsables de la aparición de estos tumularios. Te pidió que derrotaras a los cantores de guerra y le trajeras sus sellos. Así podrá determinar a qué Señor Demacrado sirven.","'Necesito los sellos de los cantores de guerra para poder determinar a qué Señor Demacrado sirven. Busca estas criaturas en las ruinas al este de Haragmar.'","Radagast está preocupado por la causa de la corrupción en los pantanos. Siente que los tumularios son un síntoma de un mal mayor.","Lleva los sellos a Radagast el Pardo en Ost Guruth","Libro 2, Capítulo 10: Los criadores de los Muertos","Sellos de hombres demacrados recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Estos sellos llevan la marca de Ivar Manosangrienta. Es un poderoso señor de los hombres demacrados, una criatura peligrosa y vil. Él está detrás de la corrupción del Pantano Rojo.\
\
'¿Por qué una criatura como Ivar viajaría tan lejos desde Angmar? Tal vez por poder. Pero, ¿qué lo atrajo hasta aquí?'","'El gran número de tumularios en Haragmar indica la presencia de hombres demacrados, viles nigromantes al servicio del Señor Oscuro. En tiempos antiguos, habitaban en el reino de Angmar, pero el Consejo Blanco creía que todos ellos estaban destruidos. Claramente, estaban equivocados.\
\
'Sólo los más fuertes de los hombres demacrados, los Señores Demacrados, tienen el poder de invocar a los espíritus del Reino de las Sombras. Los cantores de guerra llevan el sello de su señor demacrado. Busca en las ruinas al este de Haragmar, derrota a estas criaturas y tráeme sus sellos.\
\
'Debemos averiguar a qué Señor Demacrado sirven estas criaturas.'"},
[2025]={"'Esta tierra ha sido el escenario de muchas batallas en el pasado. Algunos dicen que el pantano toma su nombre de la sangre de los hombres caídos que tiñen la tierra de rojo. Pero mi conocimiento de la historia del pantano es limitado.\
\
'Sé de un hombre llamado Aric, un sabio de los Eglain, aunque solo por reputación. Es un hablador de piedras, un erudito que estudia las piedras y recoge conocimiento de sus marcas. Aric sabe mucho sobre la tradición local.\
\
'Viaja a él y pídele su ayuda. Actualmente reside al sur de aquí, más allá de Talath Gaun, en Harloeg. Puede proporcionarnos el conocimiento que buscamos.'","Radagast quiere descubrir qué atrajo a una criatura como Ivar al Pantano Rojo. Cree que uno de los Eglain podría proporcionar información.","'Sé mucho sobre estas tierras, sí. ¿Sabes de dónde proviene mi conocimiento?\
\
'Los muertos guardan secretos... grandes secretos, terribles secretos. Secretos que atesoran en su pecho como el fuego en un día de invierno. Los recuerdos mantienen sus corazones calientes, ¿sabes? No, quizás no lo sepas.\
\
'Pero lo sabrás. Oh sí, creo que lo sabrás.'","Libro 2, Capítulo 11: El Intérprete de Piedras","Aric se encuentra al sur de Ost Guruth, más allá de Talath Gaun, en Harloeg.\
\
Radagast habló de un hombre llamado Aric el Intérprete de Piedras... Este último podrá contarte la historia del Pantano Rojo.","Habla con Aric el Intérprete de Piedras en Harloeg","'Tienes que encontrar a Aric el Intérprete de Piedras. No tenemos tiempo que perder.'"},
[2026]={"Libro 2, Capítulo 12: El desafío de un hombre muerto","'Puedes aprender muchas cosas de los muertos. Pero hay un espectro problemático llamado Emelin que resiste todos los intentos de comunicación. Quizás tú tengas éxito donde yo no lo he tenido.\
\
'Emelin es... difícil. Está atado por su orgullo y considera a los vivos como seres despreciables. Si puedes demostrar tu valía ante él, esto podría otorgarte suficiente estatus a sus ojos para que te preste ayuda.\
\
'Ten cuidado cuando hables con él. Intentará ganarse tu confianza con palabras agradables y luego te enviará a tu perdición. Lo encontrarás en las ruinas de Ost Haer.'","Mientras investigabas el origen de los espectros del Pantano Rojo, Radagast te envió a un hombre llamado Aric el Intérprete de piedras. Aric insinuó que los muertos podrían tener las respuestas que buscas.","'Emelin es un tipo astuto y guarda bien sus secretos.'","'Tú respiras y aun así deseas hablar conmigo? No eres como el hombre llamado Aric. Él es sabio en las piedras y conoce los secretos de esta tierra. Pero incluso a él lo desprecio por su carne tibia y su mirada clara.\
\
'La sabiduría será tuya si demuestras ser digno. ¿Te atreves a enfrentarte a mis guerreros? Si sales victorioso, te ayudaré en tu misión.\
\
'Pero si fracasas, este día será el último que conocerás...'","Habla con Emelin en Ost Haer","Habla con Emelin","Has vencido a los hombres de Emelin","Emelin acecha la zona llamada Ost Haer.\
\
Aric habló de una sombra llamada Emelin. Si demuestras tu valía ante la sombra, quizás te dé la información que buscas.","Emelin acecha la zona llamada Ost Haer.\
\
Emelin te ha encargado que derrotes las apariciones de sus guerreros muertos. Si lo consigues, te ayudará. Si fracasas, puedes perecer.","'Todavía estás vivo para respirar, aunque sea de forma áspera y tosca. Descansa y escucha mis palabras.\
\
'He cometido actos terribles en nombre de los reyes de antaño. Mientras el mal corrompía estas tierras, mis hombres y yo permanecimos de brazos cruzados, ignorando nuestro deber. Ahora, la Doncella Roja está al servicio de Angmar, algo que juramos impedir. Iarwain Ben-adar nos ha condenado a vivir como medio muertos por nuestra falta.\
\
'¿Lo entiendes? Te ayudaré a romper mi maldición, pero tendrás que demostrar que mereces mi ayuda.'"},
[2027]={"'Regresas de la batalla y el señor de los túmulos ya no está con nosotros. Ahora hablaré del pasado y de lo que está por venir.\
\
'El Arnor antiguo se mantuvo durante mucho tiempo, pero fue dividido. Surgieron tres reinos: Arthedain, Cardolan y Rhudaur... pero la luz de Arnor se apagó, y es fácil tentar los corazones de los Hombres para hacer obras oscuras.\
\
'Rhudaur se volvió contra nosotros, el reino de Arthedain, porque nuestros hermanos Dúnedain fueron derrocados por un malvado cacique de los Montañeses al servicio de Angmar. La advertencia llegó demasiado tarde... para la doncella, para nosotros.'","Derrota a Brudhraw","Libro 2, Capítulo 13: En la Emprise del Señor demacrado","Los tumularios y su líder se encuentran al oeste de Ost Haer, en Nindor.\
\
Emelin te dijo que el Señor demacrado Ivar Manosangrienta reanima cuerpos para ser sus soldados. Debes eliminarlos a ellos y a su líder, un ser llamado Brudhraw.","Emelin te habló de su fracaso al proteger a una de las Doncellas del Río y de la maldición que él y sus hombres sufrieron como consecuencia. Aceptó ayudarte si cumplías una tarea para él.","Habla con Emelin en Ost Haer","Emelin está en Ost Haer, al norte.\
\
Has vencido al señor de los túmulos Brudhraw. Ahora deberías regresar junto a la sombra llamada Emelin.","'¡Mata lo que no vive! ¡Lucha contra lo que no sangra! Una tarea imposible para algunos, pero no para ti.'","Brudhraw derrotado","'Esta tierra fue corrompida por la guerra que aquí se desató. Sangre, mucha sangre, se derramó en las fuentes de la Dama, hasta que todo se volvió rojo y las fuentes se convirtieron en un pantano. La Dama, cuyo nombre no se recuerda, se convirtió en la Doncella Roja, una criatura perdida y corrupta. Ivar Manosangrienta llegó no hace mucho y la despertó de nuevo, reclamando poder sobre ella. Ahora Ivar es una amenaza mayor que nunca lo fue.\
\
'Debes enfrentarte a él para restaurar el equilibrio entre el Hombre y la Naturaleza. Hasta que la Doncella Roja sea redimida o destruida, mis hermanos y yo estamos condenados a este estado miserable.\
\
'El oeste es donde debes viajar para destruir al señor de los túmulos Brudhraw y a sus soldados. Sirven a la Mano Sangrienta y deben ser destruidos.'"},
[2028]={"Radagast el Pardo está en la torre al final de la vía principal de Ost Guruth.\
\
Emelin te contó su triste historia y te instruyó para que regresaras junto a Radagast el Pardo.","'Sí, es un destino terrible para cualquiera, y este Ivar es un enemigo temible. Rezo para que esos jóvenes sean encontrados sanos y salvos.\
\
'Ah, ¡pero tú no lo sabes! Dos valientes jóvenes Eglain partieron para salvar Ost Guruth. Ignoran los peligros que enfrentan y deben ser apartados de su misión.\
\
'El orgullo y el honor los impulsan, ¡pero solo la muerte les espera!'","Has derrotado al señor de los túmulos y has traído un atisbo de paz a Emelin y sus hombres, los guerreros caídos de Arthedain.","'Vuelve junto a tu amo. No sé quién es, pero como no hay paso al sur, debe estar al norte.'","Habla con Radagast el Pardo en Ost Guruth","Libro 2, Capítulo 14: Historia de la Doncella Roja","'Las guerras corrompieron esta tierra, ahogándola en la sangre de inocentes. La Dama también se ahogó, asfixiada por la muerte y el mal mientras nosotros no hacíamos nada para salvarla. Fallamos a nuestro deber dos veces y fuimos maldecidos siete veces por aquel a quien los Elfos llaman Iarwain Ben-adar.\
\
'Cuando la Dama se convirtió en la Doncella Roja, trajo aún más ruina a su propio hogar, a la tierra y a las bestias. Era terrible y no nos atrevimos a enfrentarnos a ella. Cuando ya no había más sangre viva que derramar, ella durmió... hasta que Ivar la despertó una vez más.\
\
'Esa es mi triste historia. Ahora ve, regresa junto a tu amo y háblale de este secreto pasado. Recuerda nuestro destino, ${CLASS}, y no falles en tu deber.'"},
[2029]={"Radagast te ha dicho que miembros de los Eglain, liderados por Elsa y Eriac, han entrado en Agamaur, los pantanos del norte del Pantano Rojo.","'Tienes que hablar ahora con Radagast; está dentro de la torre del campamento.'","Radagast el Pardo se encuentra en la torre al final de la avenida principal de Ost Guruth.\
\
Radagast el Pardo espera para llevarte al paso hacia Agamaur. Cuando estés preparado para partir, vuelve a hablar con Radagast.","'Sí, sí, esto servirá muy bien. Me quedaré aquí y ayudaré a los Eglain a luchar contra Ivar. No puedo permitir que criaturas inocentes sean utilizadas para fines tan malvados.'","'Dos jóvenes y testarudos Eglain, Elsa y Eriac, entraron en Agamaur con un pequeño grupo. Buscaban la fuente del poder que amenaza a su pueblo, pero si el Señor Demacrado Ivar ha llegado a Agamaur, temo que se enfrentan a un poder que no pueden superar. Necesitan tu ayuda.\
\
'El Pantano Rojo está dividido en dos regiones. Los pantanos del sur, Haragmar, los conoces. Elsa y Eriac entraron en Agamaur, los pantanos del norte, a través del Paso Rojo. Es un paso conocido solo por los Eglain... y por mí mismo.\
\
'Yo te acompañaré, porque la sombra que ha llegado a Agamaur es demasiado poderosa para que la enfrentes solo. No hay forma de saber qué mal nos espera en el pantano. Vuelve a verme cuando estés preparado para partir.'","Habla con Elsa en Agamaur","Elsa se encuentra en el campamento, dentro de las ruinas.\
\
Deberías hablar con Elsa sobre tu victoria en Agamaur.","Habla con Radagast el Pardo en Agamaur","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para partir? ¡Bien! Debemos irnos de inmediato... temo que el tiempo se acabe para nuestros jóvenes amigos eglain.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta instancia solo puede completarse en solitario. No debes estar en una comunidad para iniciar esta instancia.</rgb>","'Gracias de nuevo por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}. Ahora deberías hablar con Radagast el Pardo; te está esperando en la torre del campamento.'","Libro 2, Capítulo 15 (Solo): El Paso Rojo","Los Eglain y las sombras de Arthedain han establecido un pequeño campamento en las ruinas. Elsa te espera para hablar contigo.\
\
Tu combate contra las aguas oscuras de Ivar ha sido una victoria, o eso parece. El Señor Demacrado se retiró hacia el norte, perseguido por Radagast el Pardo, y no ha sido visto desde entonces.","Habla con Radagast el Pardo en Ost Guruth"},
[2030]={"Radagast te ha dicho que miembros de los Eglain, liderados por Elsa y Eriac, han entrado en Agamaur, los pantanos del norte del Pantano Rojo.","'Tienes que hablar ahora con Radagast; está dentro de la torre del campamento.'","Radagast el Pardo se encuentra en la torre al final de la avenida principal de Ost Guruth.\
\
Radagast el Pardo espera para llevarte al paso hacia Agamaur. Cuando estés preparado para partir, vuelve a hablar con Radagast.","'Sí, sí, esto servirá muy bien. Me quedaré aquí y ayudaré a los Eglain a luchar contra Ivar. No puedo permitir que criaturas inocentes sean utilizadas para fines tan malvados.'","'Dos jóvenes y testarudos Eglain, Elsa y Eriac, entraron en Agamaur con un pequeño grupo. Buscaban la fuente del poder que amenaza a su pueblo, pero si el Señor Demacrado Ivar ha llegado a Agamaur, temo que se enfrentan a un poder que no pueden superar. Necesitan tu ayuda.\
\
'El Pantano Rojo está dividido en dos regiones. Los pantanos del sur, Haragmar, los conoces. Elsa y Eriac entraron en Agamaur, los pantanos del norte, a través del Paso Rojo. Es un paso conocido solo por los Eglain... y por mí mismo.\
\
'Yo te acompañaré, porque la sombra que ha llegado a Agamaur es demasiado poderosa para que la enfrentes solo. No hay forma de saber qué mal nos espera en el pantano. Vuelve a verme cuando estés preparado para partir.'","Habla con Elsa en Agamaur","Libro 2, Capítulo 15: (Comunidad) El Paso Rojo","Elsa se encuentra en el campamento, dentro de las ruinas.\
\
Deberías hablar con Elsa sobre tu victoria en Agamaur.","Habla con Radagast el Pardo en Agamaur","'Gracias de nuevo por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}. Ahora deberías hablar con Radagast el Pardo; te está esperando en la torre del campamento.'","Los Eglain y las sombras de Arthedain han establecido un pequeño campamento en las ruinas. Elsa te espera para hablar contigo.\
\
Tu combate contra las aguas oscuras de Ivar ha sido una victoria, o eso parece. El Señor Demacrado se retiró hacia el norte, perseguido por Radagast el Pardo, y no ha sido visto desde entonces.","Habla con Radagast el Pardo en Ost Guruth","'¿Estás preparado para partir? ¡Bien! Debemos irnos de inmediato... Temo que el tiempo se esté acabando para nuestros jóvenes amigos Eglain.'"},
[2031]={"'Si Elsa va a conseguir las provisiones que necesita, tendrás que llevarle su carta a Frideric. ¡Por favor, date prisa y llévasela!'","'Por favor, asegúrate de que Frideric reciba mi carta. Es vital que recibamos suministros adicionales.'","'Aún hay esperanza de que podamos derrotar el mal en Agamaur.'","Con la ayuda de las sombras de Arthedain, los Eglain resistieron las fuerzas de Ivar.","'Esperamos noticias de Elsa y Eriac. Parece que has sobrevivido a tu incursión en el Pantano Rojo, ¿pero qué hay de ellos?'","'El mago Radagast ha ido al pantano para ayudar a los Eglain que están allí.'","'Has hecho mucho para ayudarnos a mantener este punto de apoyo en Agamaur, ${PLAYER}. Gracias. Si queremos mantener esta posición, necesitaremos suministros.\
\
'Lleva esta carta a Frideric y este paquete a mi hermana Hana para que sepa que sigo vivo. Ella está sola ahora, y me preocupa por ella.\
\
'Al sur hay un pasaje que te llevará de vuelta a Haragmar, la parte sur del Pantano Rojo. Desde allí, ve hacia el oeste y encontrarás el camino de regreso a Ost Guruth. ¡Apresúrate y avisa a mi gente que todo está bien... por el momento!'","'¡Reuniré de inmediato las provisiones para Elsa y Eriac!'","'Gracias por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}.'","Lleva la carta de Elsa a Frideric el Anciano","'¿Mi hermana está bien? Me alegra mucho oírlo. ¿Qué es lo que me traes?\
\
'Muchas gracias por traerme esto. Temo por mi hermana, porque el pantano es un lugar amenazante y lleno de terrores, pero sé que lo que hace es por el bien de los Eglain.\
\
'Ahora supongo que deberías llevar la carta de Elsa a Frideric.'","Lleva el paquete de Elsa a Hana","'Oh, estoy bien. Pero creo que Elsa te pidió que hicieras algo, ¿no?'","'Deberías ir a hablar con Elsa.'","'¡Cruzar el pantano no es fácil, ${PLAYER}! Has demostrado un valor notable. Ah, sí, Elsa lo confirma en su carta. Habla muy bien de ti.\
\
'Comenzaré a preparar un envío de suministros para Elsa y Eriac.'","Libro 2, Capítulo 16: Agamaur asegurado","'Los Eglain y nuestros aliados de Arthedain pudieron detener las fuerzas de Ivar... al menos por el momento.\
\
'Necesito ir a otro lugar y debo despedirme por ahora. Ahora vete, Elsa desea hablar contigo de nuevo.'","'Mi hermana está en el pantano, luchando para proteger a nuestro pueblo del mal que hay allí.'","Habla con Elsa la Valiente","El pasaje a Haragmar está al sur. Ost Guruth está al oeste de Haragmar.\
\
Elsa te dio una carta para entregar a Frideric solicitando suministros para su campamento. También te pidió que entregaras un paquete a su hermana, Hana. Ambos se encuentran en Ost Guruth.","'Tienes que llevar esa carta al anciano de los Eglain, Frideric.'","'Dirígete al sur hasta el muro. Allí encontrarás un pasaje que te llevará a Haragmar, el pantano del sur. Desde allí, Ost Guruth estará al oeste. Los demás pueden estar preocupados, así que date prisa.'","'Nos has traído aliados extraños... que sean tan fuertes como aterradores.'","Frideric está en el patio de Ost Guruth.\
\
Hana se alegró de recibir el paquete de Elsa y de saber que ella está cuidando de ella y de todos los Eglain.","Recogida de la carta y el paquete de Elsa","'Nos habríamos perdido sin tu ayuda.'","Elsa está en el campamento de Agamaur.\
\
Radagast te agradeció por tu ayuda y te pidió que hablaras con la mujer Eglain llamada Elsa.","'¡Gracias por traer el regalo de Elsa!'"},
[2032]={"Derrota a los gredbyg dentro de la Gran Excavación (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Esta sala está impregnada de historia! ¡Llena mi corazón de asombro!'","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has derrotado a muchos de los gredbyg en la Gran Excavación, ayudando a que el área sea más segura para los enanos de Bósi.","Bósi ha establecido su centro de mando en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, una sala de guardia que alguna vez se utilizó para vigilar tres pasajes que conducen más profundamente en Moria.","'¡Buen trabajo! Siempre eres alguien útil en la necesidad, y estoy a tu servicio. ¡Continúas impresionándome con tu fervor inextinguible hacia nuestra causa!'","'Nos hemos establecido en Moria, ${PLAYER}, y organizaremos incursiones más profundas desde esta sala, la Cámara de la Encrucijada. Esta Cámara fue una vez una sala de guardia para vigilar los tres pasajes justo al sur, pero ha estado vacía durante muchos años.\
\
'Muchas criaturas han prosperado en la oscuridad durante la larga ausencia de los enanos, especialmente los gredbyg, insectos feroces y repugnantes nacidos de las profundidades.\
\
'Busca todas las variedades de gredbyg en los Niveles Occidentales, al sur y al oeste de esta sala, y elimínalos. Este será el primer pequeño paso para reclamar la Gran Excavación para mi pueblo. Hay mucho por hacer antes de que se pueda lograr un progreso real.'","Gredbyg derrotados dentro de la Gran Excavación (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Libro 2, Capítulo 1: Nuevos Residentes","'Los gredbyg son feroces y mortales, como has descubierto.'","Los gredbyg se pueden encontrar por toda la Gran Excavación, al sur y al oeste de la Cámara de la Encrucijada.\
\
Bósi te ha pedido que elimines a los feroces gredbyg dentro de la Gran Excavación. Estos insectos representan una amenaza para la seguridad de los enanos.","'Los gredbyg se pueden encontrar por toda la Gran Excavación y deben ser eliminados. Viaja al sur y al oeste de esta sala hacia la Gran Excavación, y elimina cualquier gredbyg que encuentres correteando por el camino.'"},
[2033]={"Orcos de la Mano Blanca combatientes a distancia derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Elimina a los orcos de la Mano Blanca combatientes cuerpo a cuerpo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Libro 2, Capítulo 1: El levantamiento de los orcos","Candaith, el Montaraz que vigila el Gran Camino del Este mientras atraviesa las Tierras Solitarias, se ha enterado de la presencia de orcos en las Colinas de los Vientos.","Los orcos de la Mano Blanca infestan las Colinas de los Vientos, al oeste del campamento de Candaith.\
\
El Montaraz Candaith te ha ofrecido su ayuda para encontrar a Radagast el Pardo a cambio de que le ayudes contra los orcos de las Colinas de los Vientos.","Candaith está en su campamento, al pie de la Cima de los Vientos, en las Colinas de los Vientos.\
\
Mientras luchabas contra los orcos, Candaith comenzó su búsqueda de Radagast el Pardo.","Orcos de la Mano Blanca combatientes cuerpo a cuerpo derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Busca orcos en las Colinas de los Vientos, al oeste de mi campamento, y reduce su número. Mientras tanto, comenzaré mi búsqueda de Radagast el Pardo.'","'Algo ha dado a los orcos y Trasgos un nuevo propósito y los ha impulsado a adentrarse en las tierras salvajes.'","'La palabra de Saeradan llega tarde a las Tierras Solitarias. Si Radagast el Pardo ha pasado por estas tierras, tal vez no todo esté perdido. Acabo de regresar de un viaje por tierras lejanas al este, tierras firmemente dominadas por el mal. Al volver de ese viaje, para mi consternación, me enteré de que el mal no se agita solo en el Este.\
\
'Ahora los Trasgos vagan al sur, mientras que sus primos mayores y más feroces entre los orcos se extienden por las Colinas de los Vientos como una plaga que se pudre.\
\
'Debo encontrar el cuerpo principal de los orcos. Si me ayudas a rechazar al Enemigo en estas colinas, comenzaré la búsqueda de Radagast el Pardo. ¿Qué dices?'","Habla con Candaith en su campamento","'El mal se extiende por todas las tierras, ${PLAYER}. La seguridad se desvanece.'","Elimina a los orcos de la Mano Blanca combatientes a distancia (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Te doy las gracias, ${PLAYER}, pero mi gratitud se ve ensombrecida por la preocupación... Hasta hoy nunca había visto un grupo de orcos como este en Eriador: están organizados y bien aprovisionados. Han establecido su campamento en una de las entradas del Paso de Moscagua y el símbolo que llevan en sus estandartes y escudos me es totalmente desconocido.\
\
'Son muchos en ese campamento, pero llegará el día en que podamos expulsarlos aullando de las Tierras Solitarias. No hoy, me temo, pero quizás no dentro de mucho. Hay otro asunto que reclama nuestra atención, un asunto urgente. Nos ocuparemos más tarde de la destrucción de su campamento del Paso de Moscagua.'"},
[2034]={"'¿Qué ocurre, Egfrith? ¿Has visto este emblema antes?'","Egfrith sugirió que te encargues de los orcos en las hogueras al oeste, al otro lado del puente roto, para que los tres puedan planear vuestro paso por la ciudad ocupada y más allá.","'¿Qué sabes de este símbolo, esta Mano Blanca? Orcos que la portan han aparecido últimamente en Rohan, y muchas son las aldeas y granjas que han atormentado a lo largo de la Marca de los Jinetes. La enfermedad del rey le impide enfrentarse adecuadamente a estos saqueadores, y cada día el reino se vuelve más débil, más frágil. ¿Pero quién comanda esta tribu contra mi gente?'\
\
Meneldir te lanza una mirada de advertencia, y tú explicas a Egfrith que los Uruks de la Mano Blanca deben servir a algún poderoso caudillo de su propia especie. Ella apoya una mano en el pomo de su espada.\
\
'Sí, ese suele ser el modo de los de su clase. Aun así, los orcos aquí en Tharbad no necesitan servir bajo la Mano Blanca para poner en peligro mi misión y la tuya. Hay otras hogueras al oeste, al otro lado del puente roto, y si despejas a sus defensores descansaremos mejor y estaremos más preparados para viajar por la ciudad con seguridad.'","Ayuda al hombre que combate con los orcos al oeste","'¡Salve, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, si eso eres! Estoy muy lejos de mi hogar en Gondor, pero si eres ${PLAYERNAME:enemigo[m]|enemiga[f]} de los orcos, eso ya nos une. Por tu equipo veo que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un viajero[m]|una viajera[f]}, y no desconoces la lucha ni las penurias. Así es también para mí, aunque soy nuevo en esta tierra.'","Meneldir y Egfrith descansan en la ribera norte del Gwathló.","Habla con Egfrith en la ribera norte del Gwathló","El hombre ha vencido a los orcos, pero te observa con cautela cuando te acercas","Habla con Meneldir en la ribera norte del Gwathló","El desconocido te observa con cautela.","Egfrith se sobresalta de pronto","Tus compañeros han oído orcos merodeando por las ruinas de Tharbad, lo que podría significar problemas para los habitantes del Antiguo Cardolan y de las Tierras de Bree al norte.","La ropa de viaje que viste el hombre no puede ocultar que es un guerrero experimentado. Los cuerpos de los orcos a sus pies también lo dejan claro.","Libro 2, Capítulo 1: Algo Acecha en Tharbad","Un hombre lucha con orcos al oeste del puente roto en Tharbad. ¡Podría necesitar tu ayuda!","La luz brilla sobre las armas de un hombre que lucha más al oeste","Explora las hogueras al oeste del puente roto en Tharbad","'Los orcos aquí en Tharbad no necesitan servir bajo la Mano Blanca para poner en peligro mi misión y la tuya. Hay otras hogueras al oeste, al otro lado del puente roto, y si despejas a sus defensores descansaremos mejor y podremos viajar con más seguridad por la ciudad.'","Derrota orcos en las ruinas de Tharbad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ayudaré a tu amigo a asegurar que este campamento permanezca desocupado por quienes lo hicieron, si tú cazas a los orcos que merodean por la ciudad. Nos quedaremos aquí solo el tiempo suficiente para secar nuestras ropas y recuperarnos del cruce, y cuantos menos orcos haya entre nosotros y el camino del norte, mejor.'","'¿Cómo te fue contra los orcos, ${PLAYER}? ¿Llevaban el emblema que vimos en los Uruks de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes?'\
\
Le dices a Meneldir que los orcos que merodean la ciudad en ruinas no parecen llevar la marca de la Mano Blanca y que, según tus ojos, pertenecen a otras tribus orcas.","'Puedo oír orcos merodeando entre las ruinas de la ciudad, y si no montamos guardia podrían sorprendernos mientras descansamos del cruce. Se han convertido en una amenaza creciente en mis propias tierras, y el rey no tiene fuerzas para oponérseles; Rohan sufre.\
\
'Ayudaré a tu amigo a asegurar que este campamento permanezca desocupado por quienes lo hicieron, si cazas a los orcos que merodean la ciudad. Nos quedaremos aquí solo lo suficiente para secar las ropas y recuperarnos del cruce, y cuantos menos orcos haya entre nosotros y el camino del norte, mejor.'","Has derrotado orcos en Tharbad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Oíste combates al oeste? ¿Quizás un aliado necesita ayuda?'","'¿Combate? ¿Al oeste? ¡Podría ser un aliado que necesita ayuda!'","'Debe de haber orcos en las hogueras al oeste, al otro lado del puente roto. Derrótalos y nuestro paso por la ciudad podría permanecer desapercibido.'","Habla con el desconocido que mata orcos en Tharbad","Los orcos merodean las ruinas de Tharbad y deben ser enfrentados por cualquier persona decidida que los encuentre."},
[2035]={"Noreth is the captain of the Rosigil, the easternmost of the ships docked at the wharf at Dol Amroth.\
\
You have done as Captain Noreth asked, and should now speak with her about what you saw.","The deck of the Alphroval, northernmost of the ships docked at the wharf in Dol Amroth, will give you a good vantage from which to look at the Sea-gate.\
\
Captain Maeral wants you to look at the Sea-gate from where you stand on the deck of his ship.","Noreth wants you to stand on the deck of her ship and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> through the Sea-gate","'You see the truth of it? Numerous Corsair ships lie beyond the Sea-gate, and every unfriendly eye on the deck of each is trained upon that narrow space. Any Gondorian ship that tries to pass into open water would be savaged by the weapons of Umbar before reaching freedom or launching any attack.\
\
'We are hemmed in and cannot escape. If you speak to Captain Noreth of the Rosigil, she will tell you much the same.'","Noreth is the captain of the Rosigil, the easternmost of the ships docked at the wharf at Dol Amroth.\
\
Lothíriel has asked you to visit the captains at the wharf, in order to assess the sea-worthiness and battle-readiness of their ships.","'<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> to the Sea-gate, if you wish to know the truth of the situation we face.'","'See how that monster makes the other ships look like children's toys floating in a stream? That is the flagship of the Umbar fleet, Nûluzimir in their tongue: 'Night-jewel.'\
\
'Many Gondorian ships have succumbed to the attacks of the Night-jewel during the years since the disappearance of Thorongil, greatest foe of the Corsairs! Would that he had returned before the Night-jewel was constructed, and might have prevented it! But none have seen Thorongil since he routed the Corsairs almost forty years ago. He is likely dead.\
\
'I would not sail my ship against the Night-jewel unless I wanted her to lie on the sea-bottom, ${PLAYER}. None of our ships are a match for that one, not even Cirnaith's Súlrohir. Speak to him and see if he thinks otherwise.'","You see the gathered Corsair fleet beyond the Sea-gate","Lothíriel knows that further battles approach, and she wants you to judge the sea-power currently at her disposal in Dol Amroth.","'We are hemmed in and cannot escape. If you speak to Captain Noreth of the Rosigil, she will tell you much the same.'","Maeral is the captain of the Alphroval, the northernmost of the ships docked at the wharf at Dol Amroth.\
\
Lothíriel has asked you to visit the captains at the wharf, in order to assess the sea-worthiness and battle-readiness of their ships.","'Go to the Wharf and speak to the captains of the ships moored there. They will know the sea-worthiness of their own ships, and whether they might be made battle-ready.\
\
'The true sea-power of Gondor is harboured at the city of Pelargir, but that port is far to the east and we cannot depend upon its ships for aid in time.'","You see an enormous ship, larger than the rest. It must be the flagship of Umbar","Talk to Captain Noreth of the Rosigil, the easternmost ship docked at the wharf","The deck of the Rosigil, easternmost of the ships docked at the wharf in Dol Amroth, will give you a good vantage from which to look through the Sea-gate, there to see whatever it is that Captain Noreth wants you to see.\
\
Captain Noreth wants you to look through the Sea-gate from where you stand on the deck of her ship.","'The daughter of Imrahil wishes to know how much sea-power she commands? Very little, truth be told. I am afraid the Alphroval and these few others will have to stand for her fleet, unless she can request aid from Pelargir.\
\
'<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> to the Sea-gate, if you wish to know the truth of it.'","'I know that further battle with the Corsairs is unavoidable, ${PLAYER}. As ruler of the city, it is my task to defend the people of Dol Amroth for as long as I am able. To do that, I must learn what I can of our weaknesses and our strengths. May our strengths outnumber our weaknesses, as unlikely as that may seem!\
\
'If you will help me in this, go to the Wharf and speak to the captains of the ships moored there. They will know the sea-worthiness of their own ships, and whether they might be made battle-ready.\
\
'The true sea-power of Gondor is harboured at the city of Pelargir, but that port is far to the east and we cannot depend upon its ships for aid in time.'","Book 2, Chapter 1: The Ships of Gondor","Talk to Captain Maeral of the Alphroval, the northernmost ship docked at the wharf","'Lothíriel wants a report from the captains of the ships docked at her city? There are no good tidings, friend. If there is any good fortune here it is that very few ships are trapped at the wharf, and most of Gondor's fleet must be found at the port city of Pelargir, to the east.\
\
'They are too far away to help us here, but at least those ships are not caught like rabbits in a trap, as we are. It is hopeless!'","'I have only met Captain Cirnaith of the Súlrohir in passing, but I do know that he sent his crew into the city to make what merriment they might. He must believe there is nothing they can do ship-side to face the dangers that approach.'","Maeral is the captain of the Alphroval, the northernmost of the ships docked at the wharf at Dol Amroth.\
\
You have done as Captain Maeral asked, and should now speak with him about what you saw.","'<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> through the Sea-gate and you will see why we cannot hope to leave the city that way.'","Cirnaith is the captain of the Súlrohir, the southernmost of the ships docked at the wharf at Dol Amroth.\
\
Lothíriel has asked you to visit the captains at the wharf, in order to assess the sea-worthiness and battle-readiness of their ships.","Talk to Captain Cirnaith of the Súlrohir, the southernmost ship docked at the wharf","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> at the Sea-gate from the deck of the Alphroval","'Before I became captain of my own ship, I served two years before the mast on the Alphroval. I know Maeral to be a wise captain and judge of the seas, but he is prone to recklessness. If he believes passage through the Sea-gate is a foolish journey, it must truly be so.\
\
'Do you see the mighty ship in the waters outside the city? <rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> through the Sea-gate and tell me what you see.'"},
[2036]={"En su búsqueda de señales de Radagast, Candaith siguió a un mensajero que salía del campamento orco en el Paso de Moscagua, pero no pudo averiguar qué mensaje llevaba el orco antes de que su cacería se interrumpiera por los crebain alados.","'Estas órdenes están escritas en la lengua negra, ${PLAYER}, una lengua que nunca he deseado aprender. Debería haberme preparado para esto, pero esperaba que aprendiéramos algo útil de inmediato. Mientras buscabas estas órdenes, seguí las huellas de Radagast a través de las colinas.\
\
'¡Me encontré con una patrulla de orcos! Me vi obligado a abandonar mi búsqueda y perdí mi arco mientras me escapaba de los orcos bajo la arboleda del bosque. Estuvo muy cerca, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Por tu parte, has hecho un buen trabajo, y pronto entenderemos las intenciones de estos orcos y quiénes son sus líderes.'","'Estos orcos son inusualmente astutos. Ten cuidado, amigo.'","'Ahora ve al oeste, hacia Glumhallow, y busca al mensajero cuya pista tuve que abandonar. Por mi parte, seguiré vigilando sus acciones en el norte. Debemos conocer el alcance completo de esta invasión, ${PLAYER}.'","El mensajero orco se encuentra sin duda en uno de los campamentos enemigos de Glumhallow, al oeste del campamento de Candaith, al pie de la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
Un mensajero orco partió desde el Paso de Moscagua hacia los campamentos orcos dispersos por las Colinas de los Vientos. Candaith te pidió que interceptaras al mensajero orco y que volvieras con sus órdenes.","Recoge las órdenes de los orcos","'Mientras que comencé mi búsqueda de Radagast, cerca del Paso de Moscagua, vi a un mensajero orco partir a gran velocidad. Rápidamente lo seguí, rastreándolo hacia el este a lo largo de la ladera de las colinas y luego hacia el sur, pero mi búsqueda se interrumpió. No pude seguir más lejos, porque unos viles crebain sobrevolaban la zona y no podía permitirme ser descubierto.\
\
'Una vez más, debo pedirte ayuda. El mensajero seguramente lleva consigo órdenes para los campamentos periféricos. Si puedes interceptar al mensajero, tal vez aprendamos la naturaleza de estas órdenes. Así armados, estaremos mejor equipados para hacer frente a la amenaza orca.\
\
'Busca entre los campamentos orcos en Glumhallow, al oeste, y vuelve a mí con las órdenes que este mensajero seguramente posee. Yo buscaré señales del paso de Radagast en otro lugar.'","'Alguna oscura intención mueve a estos orcos, pero no puedo adivinar cuál.'","Lleva las órdenes de los orcos a Candaith","Libro 2, Capítulo 2: Un mensajero orco","Órdenes de los orcos recogidas"},
[2037]={"Recoge las provisiones dispersas al oeste de la posición de Boromir en Tharbad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Debiste haber infundido miedo al corazón de ese ladrón! Este fardo está mucho más liviano que cuando lo robó, y parece que esparció su contenido por las ruinas en su prisa por escapar.\
\
'¿Podrías recuperar mis provisiones perdidas?'","Boromir está al noreste, en Tharbad, evaluando la situación y planificando sus próximos pasos.","Has recuperado el fardo robado y debes devolvérselo a Boromir","Boromir, Capitán de Gondor, ha solicitado tu ayuda para enfrentarse a las dificultades que encontró en Tharbad.","'Este fardo es mucho más liviano que cuando el ladrón lo robó, y parece que dispersó su contenido entre las ruinas en su prisa por escapar.\
\
'¿Podría pedirte que recuperes mis provisiones perdidas?'","En su prisa por escapar, el ladrón orco intentó vaciar parte del contenido del fardo robado, que ahora está esparcido al oeste de la posición de Boromir en Tharbad.","'Me uniría a tu fogata, si crees que sería bien recibido. Si no, continuaré por mi cuenta, pero ha sido un largo camino y no rechazaría una fogata amistosa y una conversación agradable.'","Devuelve el fardo robado a Boromir al noreste","Habla con Meneldir en la ribera norte del Gwathló","Libro 2, Capítulo 2: Boromir, Hijo de Gondor","'¿A quién has encontrado, ${PLAYER}? ¿Quién se acerca así a nuestra fogata?\
\
'No esperaba ver a un soldado de la Ciudadela tan lejos de su hogar.'","'Boromir es mi nombre, y he venido desde Minas Tirith tras un largo camino en una misión urgente. El cruce del río resultó traicionero y me vi obligado a abandonar mi corcel. Tropecé con orcos entre las ruinas y uno de sus cobardes ladrones robó mi fardo. Cuando lo recupere, reanudaré mi misión.\
\
'Si atrapas a este ladrón por mí, te estaré en deuda, mi buen ${RACE}.\
\
'Creo que huyó hacia el suroeste.","El ladrón orco que huyó con el fardo de Boromir probablemente esté al suroeste de su posición en Tharbad.","'Tropecé con orcos entre las ruinas, como puedes ver, y uno de sus cobardes ladrones robó mi fardo. Cuando lo recupere, reanudaré mi misión. Si atrapas a este ladrón por mí, te estaré en deuda.\
\
'Creo que huyó hacia el suroeste.'","Has recogido las provisiones dispersas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recupera el fardo de Boromir del ladrón orco en algún punto al suroeste","Lleva las provisiones dispersas a Boromir en su posición en Tharbad, al este","Boromir ha accedido a volver contigo para conocer a tus compañeros mientras decide su próximo paso.","''¡Gracias por esto, mi ${PLAYERNAME:nuevo amigo[m]|nueva amiga[f]}! Te estoy en deuda. Y además, debo pedirte disculpas, pues estaba tan sorprendido de verte que ni siquiera pregunté tu nombre. Te ruego que me lo digas ahora y perdona mi descuido.\
\
'¿? Es un honor conocerte, . ¿Dices que tus compañeros están cerca? Me uniría a ellos en su fogata, si crees que sería bien recibido. Si no, continuaré por mi cuenta, pero ha sido un largo camino y no rechazaría una fogata amistosa y una conversación agradable.'","Regresa con Meneldir y Egfrith a la ribera norte del Gwathló","Boromir está al este, en Tharbad, evaluando la situación y planificando sus próximos pasos.","Meneldir se pone de pie de un salto cuando tú y Boromir se acercan","Meneldir mira a Boromir con sospecha, entornando los ojos."},
[2038]={"Return to the Súlrohir and study the situation","Talk to Lothíriel in the Great Hall","Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth.\
\
You have a message for Lothíriel from an emissary of Umbar, asking her to treat with his master on the deck of the flagship Night-jewel.","'I bring a message for the ruler of this city. Can you take me to this man?'\
\
Umer sees something in your eye, and smirks.\
\
'So it is true: a woman rules this city? Bring me before her and I will deliver my message.'\
\
You tell the emissary that you will bring the message, but not the messenger. He nods, apparently impressed with your response.\
\
'Tell her this, then: Balakhôr the Scourge, Heir of Castamir and ruler of every Gondorian shore licked by the waves, invites her to treat with him on the deck of the mighty ship Nûluzimir. I will await your response.'","The ships docked at Dol Amroth are trapped at the wharf by the Umbar fleet, unable to leave.","Umer, an emissary of Umbar, has passed through the Sea-gate under a flag of peace. He wishes to speak with you on the docks on the eastern side of Dol Amroth.","Crew of the Súlrohir returned (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I did not think there was much to be gained by keeping my crew here, and the sight of the fleet beyond the Sea-gate seemed likely to put my men in poor spirits. I gave them leave to find what merriment they might in the city.\
\
'But if Lothíriel has not given up hope, I fear their absence will prove an embarrassment to me! Go to the Harper's Court, on the west side of the city, and tell my crewmen to return to the Súlrohir! We will do what we can to make her ready for battle, as unlikely a victory as that seems to be.'","'How do the ships fare, ${PLAYER}? Is it as grim an outlook as I have heard?'\
\
You tell Lothíriel what you witnessed at the wharf.\
\
'That is a fair measure of what I expected. But I see that you have more to say. What else can there be?'","Find crew of the Súlrohir and tell them to return to the ship (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have sent the crew of the Súlrohir back to their ship, and should now return to the wharf on the eastern side of Dol Amroth and see if the situation has changed.\
\
There has been a commotion on the jetty that points north-east into the water. You should investigate and learn what has happened.","'I have come to Dol Amroth to advise Lothíriel. Neither her people nor mine approve of this, but I care not.'","'You must bring that message to Lothíriel, ${PLAYER}. Do not worry! We will watch these treacherous snakes and ensure they do not try anything.'","The crew of the Súlrohir are making as much merriment as they can in the Harper's Court on the west side of the city of Dol Amroth.\
\
Captain Cirnaith, fearing embarrassment, wants you to recall his crew to the Súlrohir.","'We were on our way back to the Súlrohir when we beheld this sight! Noreth is not our captain, but we would not stand by while she faces down this creature of Umbar!'","'If Lothíriel has not given up hope, I fear the absence of my crew will prove an embarrassment to me! Go to the Harper's Court, on the west side of the city, and tell my crewmen to return to the Súlrohir! We will do what we can to make her ready for battle, as unlikely a victory as that seems to be.'","Talk to Umer, the Emissary of Umbar","Book 2, Chapter 2: Two Messengers","'This is my message: Balakhôr the Scourge, Heir of Castamir and ruler of every Gondorian shore licked by the waves, invites the ruler of this city to treat with him on the deck of the mighty ship Nûluzimir. I will await your response.'","'Be careful, friend! These Corsairs passed through the Sea-gate under a flag of peace, but I do not trust them and you would be wise not to do so either!'"},
[2039]={"Libro 2, Capítulo 3: Muy Lejos de Gondor","Boromir descansa en la ribera norte del Gwathló, relatando su viaje a ti y a tus compañeros.","Habla con Boromir en la ribera norte del Gwathló.","Meneldir desconfía un poco del Capitán de Gondor y le ha pedido oír la historia de su viaje hacia el norte, y la razón de él.","Habla con Boromir y escucha el relato de su viaje.","'Más allá del Paso de Rohan, los amplios campos de Enedwaith se extendían ante mí, y no vi señal de problemas durante incontables millas. Me pareció una tierra vacía, y los días pasaron bajo cielos despejados mientras avanzaba hacia el norte.\
\
'Pero al descender la pendiente hacia las ruinas de Tharbad, supe que el cruce del río sería difícil. Liberé a mi corcel, enviando su mirada hacia las abundantes hierbas de la Ciénaga de los Cisnes antes de dejarlo partir, y yo mismo hice el cruce. Poco después, fui atacado por orcos, y fue entonces cuando me encontraste, ${PLAYER}.'","'Mis razones son mías, forastero, pero como ${PLAYER} ya me ha demostrado ser de ayuda, confiaré en que sus amigos también lo sean.\
\
'Te contaré la historia de mi viaje, al menos tanto como vuestra fogata parezca merecer. He visto fuegos más grandes, más brillantes y más cálidos, pero esta ha sido una tierra fría, y hasta un fuego pobre es mejor que ninguno.'","Meneldir ha pedido al Capitán de Gondor que relate la historia de su viaje hacia el norte, y Boromir parece dispuesto a contarla.","'Puedes sentarte junto a nuestra fogata, Capitán de Gondor, si estás dispuesto a contarnos la historia de tu viaje hacia el norte. Me interesa conocer las razones que te han traído aquí.'"},
[2040]={"Lothíriel listens impassively as you give her the message from the emissary of Umbar.\
\
'Thank you for bringing this message to me. Something must be done, that much is certain! But what, I wonder?'","You tell Lothíriel of Balakhôr's plan to destroy the Gondorian fleet at Pelargir, and she nods.\
\
'That is what I suspected, but it is good to hear it directly. It seems that Balakhôr is content to keep the ships of Dol Amroth trapped in the city, and will sail with as much force as he can spare to Pelargir, where he will try to take the rest of the fleet unawares.\
\
'I need you to ride there and warn them, ${PLAYER}! Travel through the Ringló Vale and Dor-en-Ernil, telling the people there to seek shelter from their foes, and come to Pelargir as quickly as you can.\
\
'I have not been to the Ringló Vale for some months, but I remember the town of Ethring will be on your way. Stop there on your journey and tell them what is happening, and to be strong for my father's sake, and for mine!'","Talk to Tologlor in Ethring","The town of Ethring is in the Ringló Vale, on the road to Pelargir.\
\
Lothíriel has asked you to travel through the Ringló Vale and Dor-en-Ernil to help the folk of those lands and bring warning to the people of Pelargir.","'You have the look of an adventurer! Have you ever seen anything like this before? The sun never rose this morning! Some evil has been unleashed upon us!'","Talk to Noreth on the docks","Book 2, Chapter 3: Balakhôr the Scourge","The skies over Ethring are covered in shadow","Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth.\
\
Balakhôr the Scourge has boasted of his plan to you, and now that you know his course you should bring word of it to Lothíriel.","You were cast from the deck of the Night-jewel, and have managed to struggle back to the dock.\
\
Captain Noreth has fished you from the water, and wants to hear what happened on the Night-jewel.","Talk to Lothíriel and help her decide what to do about Balakhôr's proposal","'I have not been to the Ringló Vale for some months, but I remember the town of Ethring will be on your way. Stop there on your journey and tell them what is happening, and to be strong for my father's sake, and for mine!'","'Did you learn anything of Balakhôr's plans? You should bring word of them to Lothíriel at once!'","'I value your opinion and place it among the ranks of my other advisors. If you can spare the time, I could use your counsel, ${PLAYER}.'","Tologlor in the town of Ethring has tried to catch your eye. His expression is one of frightened concern.","Lothíriel needs your help to decide what should be done.\
\
Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth, considering Balakhôr's proposal.","Travel to the town of Ethring, in the Ringló Vale","Talk to Lothíriel in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth","Balakhôr the Scourge has sent an emissary to Dol Amroth to request that Lothíriel come to treat with him on the deck of his flagship, the Night-jewel.","'I deem you were near the end of your strength when I pulled you from the water, ${PLAYER}. Any delay and I do not know that we would have gotten to you in time.\
\
'Curse Balakhôr and all his kind! Mark my words well: that scoundrel will pay for this betrayal. This is the sort of treachery I would expect from anyone calling himself 'Heir of Castamir!'\
\
'Did you learn anything of his plans? You should bring word of them to Lothíriel at once!'"},
[2041]={"'Los orcos que seguía me habrían pasado desapercibidos si no hubiera viajado con ellos el maestro de guerra. \\qUzorr,\\q le llamaban y le mostraban el respeto que su especie reserva a los más fuertes y feroces de sus guerreros.\
\
'Es probable que Uzorr haya regresado a la Grieta Desolada, en el Paso de Moscagua, ya que parecía ser su territorio. Debe morir y hay que recuperar las órdenes que le fueron dadas.\
\
'La Grieta Desolada está al noroeste de aquí, en el extremo noreste del Paso de Moscagua, rodeado por un cuerpo de agua poco profundo. Mata al maestro de guerra Uzorr y busca una carta o algo parecido cerca de él. Vuelve a verme cuando hayas salido victorioso y hablaremos sobre lo que debemos hacer. La Grieta Desolada es probablemente un lugar peligroso, ${PLAYER}, ten cuidado. Yo continuaré mi búsqueda de Radagast.'","Maestro de guerra Uzorr derrotado","'Encuentra al maestro de guerra Uzorr y mátalo. Debemos debilitar su posición. Sin Uzorr para comandar la Grieta Desolada, estarán indefensos. Busca también una carta que contenga sus órdenes.\
\
'La Grieta Desolada está al noroeste de aquí, en el extremo noreste del Paso de Moscagua.'","Derrota al maestro de guerra Uzorr","'El maestro de guerra Uzorr se encuentra en algún lugar de la Grieta Desolada, al noroeste. Mátalo y recupera cualquier carta que pueda contener alguna pista sobre la identidad de su maestro. Puede que no lleve una carta así, pero no estará lejos.'","Órdenes del maestro de guerra Uzorr obtenidas","Libro 2, Capítulo 3: Maestro de guerra Uzorr","Consigue las órdenes del maestro de guerra Uzorr","Lleva la carta orca a Candaith","Candaith está en su campamento, al pie de la Cima de los Vientos, en las Colinas de los Vientos.\
\
Has salido victorioso contra el maestro de guerra Uzorr y has obtenido una carta que seguramente contiene sus órdenes del poder que comanda a los orcos que se han aventurado en las Tierras Solitarias.","El maestro de guerra Uzorr se encuentra en la Grieta Desolada, al noroeste del campamento de Candaith, al pie de la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
Candaith te ha pedido que encuentres y mates al maestro de guerra Uzorr y que busques en el campamento una carta que contenga sus órdenes.","'El maestro de guerra Uzorr no nos molestará más, ${PLAYER}. ¡Te lo agradezco sinceramente!'","Candaith ha sabido de la existencia de un maestro de guerra entre los orcos llamado Uzorr. Su derrota sería un golpe fatal para ellos.","'Los orcos de la Grieta Desolada son fuertes y feroces.'","'Otra carta escrita en Lengua Negra, ${PLAYER}, cuyo significado se me escapa, al igual que el de la otra. Sin embargo, esta lleva la marca de la Mano Blanca.\
\
'Debo saber qué mensaje contiene esta carta, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Esta no es una tarea para ti, ${PLAYER}. Por fin he descubierto información sobre el paradero de Radagast, pero hay algo que deberías ver primero.'"},
[2042]={"'¿Has encontrado algo? Déjame ver ese calco de roca que has hecho.\
\
'Las runas son comunes, pero no sé lo que significan. Me temo que esto no me dice mucho sobre el relámpago, ${PLAYER}, pero sí me dice algo sobre su origen. Probablemente la misma persona que te envió a mí.'","El campamento de Candaith está al pie de la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
Has encontrado una roca cubierta de runas y has hecho un calco de las marcas. Deberías volver a ver a Candaith, tal vez él sepa algo sobre el significado de estas runas.","La Cima de los Vientos se alza sobre el campamento de Candaith.\
\
Candaith te pidió que buscaras en la Cima de los Vientos algo fuera de lo común y que le trajeras cualquier noticia o prueba que pudieras encontrar.","'Ese es el problema con las runas. Puede que sepas lo que dicen... pero no lo que significan.'","'¿No has encontrado nada? Ve y busca más de cerca. Debe haber algo inusual en la cumbre que nos hable de lo que ocurrió.'","Lleva el calco de roca a Candaith","Has tomado un calco de las runas en la roca y lo has guardado en tu mochila","Mientras Candaith regresaba de su viaje por las tierras del este, vio destellos de luz blanca en la cumbre de la Cima de los Vientos, como relámpagos, aunque no había tormenta.","'Todavía no entiendo qué eran esas luces en el cielo, sobre la Cima de los Vientos.'","'Algo ocurrió en la cumbre de la Cima de los Vientos esa noche, ${PLAYER}, y quiero saber de qué se trataba. Busca en la cima algo fuera de lo común y vuelve a verme si encuentras algo.'","'Mientras regresaba de las tierras del este, vi en la noche una sucesión de relámpagos de un blanco cegador en la cumbre de la Cima de los Vientos, y sin embargo no había ni una sola nube en el cielo, y no se oía ningún trueno.\
\
'Creo que, esa noche, Amon Sûl fue visitada por una tormenta nada común. Me gustaría que fueras a explorar las ruinas que se alzan en la cima de la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
'Si encuentras algo fuera de lo común, vuelve a verme inmediatamente.'","Libro 2, Capítulo 4: Una luz en la oscuridad","Busca en la cima de la Cima de los Vientos algo inusual"},
[2043]={"Relit standing torches in Ethring (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Is this some sorcery? Do our foes have the power to blanket the skies in shadow? How can we hope to fight against such evils, even with such strong men as Prince Imrahil taking up the sword?\
\
'The continuing night has caused the Orcs to grow more bold, and they have come down out of the mountains after a respite of many years. If you truly are an adventurer, you would do a great service to my people by slaying these creatures and driving them back into the mountains. Look for the vile creatures to the north-east of town.\
\
'We could also use a supply of suitable tinder. If the darkness does not abate soon, we will have need to keep the torches lit.'","Dark shadows cover the skies of the Ringló Vale, and the people of Ethring fear what it might mean.","The torch illuminates the surrounding area","The torch sputters to life","Defeat Orcs in the Ringló Vale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Yesca adecuada para el fuego recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If the darkness does not abate, we will need to keep a store of tinder with which to light the torches of Ethring. Please take some of the wood you have collected and relight any of the torches that have gone out.\
\
'The shadow may be unrelenting, but we will not cower before it. We will drive it back with light wherever we are able!'","Defeated Orcs in the Ringló Vale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tologlor is at the entrance of the town of Ethring, waiting for you to return with news of your successes against the Orcs. He also awaits delivery of any suitable tinder you have found.","The light of the torch blazes against the darkness","The light of the torch keeps the darkness at bay","Bring suitable tinder to Tologlor at the entrance to Ethring","'Thank you for lighting the torches around town. Will this night ever end? When will we see the sun again?'","Book 2, Chapter 4: The Dawnless Day","Relight standing torches that have gone out in Ethring (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Tologlor at the entrance to Ethring","Recoge yesca adecuada para el fuego (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The continuing night has caused the Orcs to grow more bold, and they have come down out of the mountains after a respite of many years. If you truly are an adventurer, you would do a great service to my people by slaying these creatures and driving them back into the mountains. Look for the vile creatures to the north-east of town.\
\
'We could also use a supply of suitable tinder. If the darkness does not abate soon, we will have need to keep the torches lit.'","'Thank you for teaching the Orcs we will not allow them to overrun the Vale. Whether that lesson proves more convincing than that they are given by the continuing night that blankets the sky, well... we will have to see.\
\
'If the darkness does not abate, we will need to keep a store of tinder with which to light the torches of Ethring. Please take some of the wood you have collected and relight any of the torches that have gone out.\
\
'The shadow may be unrelenting, but we will not cower before it. We will drive it back with light wherever we are able!'","Tologlor is at the entrance to the town of Ethring, in the Ringló Vale.\
\
You have lit some of the torches throughout Ethring, trying to drive back the darkness that overpowers the Vale and its people.","Standing torches can be found throughout Ethring. You should relight any of them that have gone out.","Orcs can be found to the north-east of Ethring, in the Ringló Vale. Suitable tinder can also be found to the north-east.\
\
Tologlor has asked you to defeat Orcs made bold by the continuing night that blankets the Ringló Vale, and to gather suitable tinder to light the town's torches."},
[2044]={"'Deberíamos derrotar a más criaturas entre nosotros y los muros norteños de la ciudad, y sugiero explorar las brechas en el muro exterior en varios lugares antes de dejar Tharbad atrás. Una vez logrado, podremos reunirnos justo al norte de la ciudad para planear nuestro curso.'","'Entonces nuestros caminos seguirán juntos, por un tiempo.'","Meneldir ha pedido hablar contigo a cierta distancia de los demás, justo al noreste del campamento.","Meneldir no está del todo convencido de que Boromir sea de fiar: ¿deberíais viajar juntos los cuatro desde Tharbad?","Meneldir desea hablar contigo sobre sus inquietudes acerca de Boromir, el Capitán de Gondor.","Encuentra una brecha en el muro exterior de Tharbad más hacia el oeste","'Mi viaje termina en un valle oculto, más al norte de lo que este mapa indica. Quizá Meneldir revele un segundo mapa al acercarnos a las Tierras de Bree, y ese marque mi destino. Pero quizá no: mi padre dijo que el valle estaba oculto.'","'¿Has decidido que viajemos juntos? Creí que tu amigo sugeriría que no, pero me parece bien, por ahora. Si mi propio camino no coincide con el vuestro, partiré sin resentimiento.'\
\
Boromir despliega el mapa del Antiguo Cardolan y lo estudia brevemente antes de devolvértelo.\
\
'Mi viaje termina en un valle oculto, ${PLAYER}, más al norte de lo que este mapa indica. Quizá Meneldir revele un segundo mapa cuando nos acerquemos a las Tierras de Bree, y ese marque mi destino. Pero quizá no: mi padre dijo que el valle estaba oculto.'","'Viajaremos juntos.'","'Me alegra oír que Meneldir no rechazará al Capitán de Gondor, pues los Hombres de esa tierra son guerreros fuertes y fieles, y en días pasados fueron firmes amigos de Rohan, y nosotros de ellos.'\
\
Egfrith despliega el mapa de Cardolan y frunce el ceño.\
\
'Estos nombres me son desconocidos, ${PLAYER}, tan distintos de los de mi propia tierra. No puedo siquiera imaginar cómo pronunciar algunos de estos lugares en voz alta. Boromir no es el único de nosotros que está lejos de su hogar.\
\
'Seguiré a Meneldir hasta que encontremos a los Montaraces del Norte, pues Rohan se marchita en mi ausencia, y si no puedo volver con lo que busco temo que el reino morirá.'","'Ese es mi relato. Sin duda habrás oído historias más emocionantes que esta, y si hablara de nuestros grandes esfuerzos en defensa de Gondor oirías una de ellas. Pero el tiempo apremia.'","Muestra el mapa a Boromir en el campamento","Hacia el noroeste ves actividad entre edificios alejados de Tharbad","'No sé si podemos confiar en este Capitán de Gondor, ${PLAYER}. ¡Recuerda las palabras de Bregoleth! Nos dijo que guardáramos nuestra confianza con cautela, pues incluso aliados aparentes podrían albergar traición en sus corazones. ¡Y no excluyo a Egfrith de esta advertencia! Pero Boromir cabalgó justo junto a Isengard en su camino hacia el norte, y admitió que habló con Saruman. ¿Cómo podemos confiar en que su conversación con el Mago Blanco fue como la describe? No podemos.\
\
'Creo que deberíamos guardar lo que sabemos de la Mano Blanca solo para nosotros, por ahora, en caso de que Boromir haya caído bajo la influencia del mago traidor. Podemos viajar juntos, al menos hasta llegar a las Tierras de Bree y a los Dúnedain, pero debemos vigilar a ambos de nuestros compañeros. Bregoleth creía que nos encontrábamos en el mismo borde del peligro, y creo que dijo la verdad.\
\
'Toma este mapa de Cardolan. Muéstraselo a los demás y ve qué recomiendan como rumbo.'","Meneldir y los demás planearon reunirse contigo en el camino al norte de Tharbad.","Habla con Meneldir en el campamento","Meneldir aprieta en tus manos un mapa viejo y descolorido del Antiguo Cardolan","Enemigos derrotados en Tharbad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Podría hablar contigo a solas un momento, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Caminemos hacia el noreste, justo allí.'","'Caminemos hacia el noreste, justo allí.'","Reúnete con Meneldir a poca distancia de los demás, hacia el noreste","Muestra el mapa a Egfrith en el campamento","Boromir permanece en la fogata cerca de la ribera norte del Gwathló.\
\
Meneldir te entregó un mapa gastado del Antiguo Cardolan para mostrárselo a Boromir y a Egfrith.","'¿Entonces estamos de acuerdo? Nuestro camino nos lleva al norte, y eso significa que debemos atravesar la ciudad y avanzar hacia el norte por el Camino Verde en dirección a las Tierras de Bree.\
\
'Deberíamos derrotar a más criaturas entre nosotros y los muros norteños de la ciudad, y sugiero explorar las brechas del muro exterior en varios lugares antes de dejar Tharbad atrás. Una vez hecho eso, podremos reunirnos justo al norte de la ciudad para planear nuestro rumbo.'","Boromir, con su relato concluido, estudia los rostros de tus compañeros. Meneldir le devuelve la mirada con estoicismo.","'Y ahí queda Tharbad detrás de nosotros, ${PLAYER}. Si el cruce del Aguagrís resulta ser lo peor de nuestro viaje, me consideraré afortunado. Temo que no será así, aunque probablemente sí será lo más húmedo. ¿A Tegwyn no le gustaba la humedad y el frío del Aguaestancada? Es afortunado de no haber tenido que cruzar el Aguagrís, y bajo la atenta mirada de sus padres pasarán muchos años antes de que pueda hacerlo.\
\
'Pero ahora debemos volver nuestra mirada a nuestro propio camino. Cardolan nos espera, y dentro de sus límites encontraremos a mi amigo Narndir, quien sabrá la ubicación del caudillo de los Dúnedain. Entonces se cumplirá el propósito de Egfrith, y también el nuestro. Quizá entonces Boromir pueda ser encaminado por el rumbo correcto, y tú y yo cenaremos en el Poney Pisador antes de separarnos.\
\
'Pero aún no estamos allí. Debemos dar un paso a la vez, para no tropezar con nuestros propios pies.'","Libro 2, Capítulo 4: Las Palabras de Bregoleth","Habla con Meneldir en el camino justo al norte de Tharbad","Egfrith permanece en la fogata cerca de la ribera norte del Gwathló.\
\
Meneldir te dio un mapa gastado del Antiguo Cardolan para mostrárselo a Boromir y a Egfrith.","'Muestra ese mapa a los demás y ve qué recomiendan como rumbo.'","Las colinas onduladas de Páramo Rojizo podrían ocultar cualquier cantidad de peligros","'Ese es el relato de mi viaje hacia el norte, tal como ha sido hasta el día de hoy.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Mira</rgb> hacia la campiña circundante","Meneldir sugirió que explores la campiña fuera de Tharbad desde diversos lugares dentro de la ciudad, derrotando a los enemigos que encuentres allí, para asegurar tu paso por la ciudad inundada.","Encuentra una brecha en el muro exterior de Tharbad al noroeste","Meneldir ha regresado al campamento.","Esta brecha en el muro debería proporcionar una buena vista de la campiña","Habla con Meneldir","Habla con Meneldir hacia el noreste, lejos de tus otros compañeros"},
[2045]={"Mientras escalabas la Cima de los Vientos, Candaith trabajó arduamente para traducir la carta que recuperaste de la Grieta Desolada. Su traducción está completa y las noticias que descubrió son graves.","'Tienes mi más sincero agradecimiento, ${PLAYER}. Los Orcos del sur no avanzarán más en las Tierras Solitarias.'","Candaith está en su campamento al pie de la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
Candaith te espera para hablar sobre los extraños eventos que ocurrieron en la cima de Amon Sûl.","Habla con Candaith","Libro 2, Capítulo 5 (Comunidad): Recuperar la Cima de los Vientos","'Tenemos que mantenernos vigilantes, por supuesto. No bajes la guardia.'","Candaith está en su campamento al pie de la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
El montaraz Candaith te pidió que lo ayudaras a expulsar una compañía de Orcos de la Cima de los Vientos. Te dijo que reuniera aliados y regresaras a él cuando estuvieras preparado.","Habla con Candaith y recupera la Cima de los Vientos con una comunidad","'No te preocupes por los Orcos que quedan. Están tan lejos de las tierras del sur que se extinguirán uno por uno, y ya no representarán una amenaza para los viajeros de las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
'Hemos ganado una batalla decisiva, amigo mío. ¡Te has ganado un merecido descanso, creo, porque la gran amenaza que representaban estos Orcos ha terminado!\
\
'Ahora, déjame ayudarte en tu empeño de encontrar a Radagast el pardo.'","'${PLAYER}, tengo noticias de Radagast, pero debo pedirte ayuda una vez más. La carta que recuperaste de la Grieta Desolada habla de los verdaderos objetivos de los Orcos: ¡tomar el control de Amon Sûl! Las fuerzas Orcas se moverán hacia la cresta de Amon Sûl bajo la cobertura de la noche y se moverán en un gran grupo, estableciendo pequeñas unidades a lo largo de los caminos desde esa fuerza mayor.\
\
'No podemos enfrentarnos a la fuerza cuando están reunidos, pero sí una vez que están divididos. Quieren establecer un campamento que les permita tener una ventaja sobre todas las Tierras Solitarias. ¡Debemos frustrar sus planes, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Reúne aliados y vuelve a verme cuando estés listo. ¡Juntos escalaremos Amon Sûl y derrotaremos a Rigûl, su líder, antes de que pueda llevar a cabo los planes malvados de su amo!'","'Si estás preparado, te guiaré. ¡Debemos ser rápidos, o los Orcos podrían tener éxito en sus malvados planes!'"},
[2046]={"Mientras escalabas la Cima de los Vientos, Candaith trabajó arduamente para traducir la carta que recuperaste de la Grieta Desolada. Su traducción está completa y las noticias que descubrió son graves.","Libro 2, Capítulo 5 (Solo): Recuperar la Cima de los Vientos","'Tienes mi más sincero agradecimiento, ${PLAYER}. Los Orcos del sur no avanzarán más en las Tierras Solitarias.'","'${PLAYER}, tengo noticias de Radagast, pero debo pedirte una vez más ayuda aquí. La carta que recuperaste de la Grieta Desolada habla del verdadero objetivo de los orcos: ¡tomar el control de Amon Sûl! Fuerzas orcas se moverán hacia la cresta de Amon Sûl bajo la cobertura de la noche y avanzarán en un grupo numeroso, estableciendo pequeñas unidades a lo largo de los senderos desde esa fuerza principal.\
\
'No podemos enfrentarnos a la fuerza cuando esté reunida, pero sí cuando se haya fragmentado. Desean establecer una base que les permita obtener ventaja sobre toda las Tierra Solitarias. ¡Debemos frustrar sus planes, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Regresa a mí cuando tengas todo listo. ¡Juntos ascenderemos Amon Sûl y derrotaremos a Rigûl, su líder, antes de que cumpla la voluntad de su amo!'","Habla con Candaith","Candaith está en su campamento al pie de la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
Candaith te espera para hablar sobre los extraños eventos que ocurrieron en la cima de Amon Sûl.","'Tenemos que mantenernos vigilantes, por supuesto. No bajes la guardia.'","'No te preocupes por los Orcos que quedan. Están tan lejos de las tierras del sur que se extinguirán uno por uno, y ya no representarán una amenaza para los viajeros de las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
'Hemos ganado una batalla decisiva, amigo mío. ¡Te has ganado un merecido descanso, creo, porque la gran amenaza que representaban estos Orcos ha terminado!\
\
'Ahora, déjame ayudarte en tu empeño de encontrar a Radagast el pardo.'","Habla con Candaith y recupera la Cima de los Vientos","'Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}, te guiaré. Debemos ser veloces, o los orcos podrían tener éxito en cualquier vileza que planeen.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión solo puede intentarse en solitario.</rgb>","Candaith está en su campamento al pie de la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
El Montaraz Candaith te pidió que lo ayudaras a expulsar a una compañía de orcos de la Cima de los Vientos."},
[2047]={"Search the Corsair camp to the north-east of Linhir for Roniel","Defeat Haradrim in Dor-en-Ernil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If your travels take you in that direction, will you consider finding my brother Ingalad in Linhir? He is a good man, stern and tough, but who can be prepared for the onset of unending night? It would ease my mind some if I knew you would check on him and ensure his safety.'","'The Corsair fleet is making poor time on its way to Pelargir, for they often stop to pillage the coastline. They believe victory is so near they need not hurry, and I fear they are right.\
\
'I do not want to weigh you down with our troubles, ${PLAYER}, for you have already been a help, but...'\
\
He trails off, but your reassuring nod prompts him to speak again.\
\
'A child has gone missing. No one knows for certain if she is lost, but none have seen her since the last Corsair attack. If you could investigate their camp to the north-east, I would be in your debt. My friends have already suffered so much of late. Losing their child, Roniel, would be the gravest hurt of all.'","Defeated Corsairs in Dor-en-Ernil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ingalad has told you of a lighthouse to the south-west, from which you might get a good view of the progress of the Corsair fleet. He also wishes for you to defeat the Corsairs and Haradrim that plague Dor-en-Ernil.","The yellow-haired doll has seen better days. Did Roniel drop her here?","If Roniel did flee Linhir to the north-east, and dropped her doll as she passed the Corsair camp, she may have continued in that direction. You should continue your search to the north-east.","'If you seek to learn the progress of the Corsair fleet, there is a lighthouse to the south-west that would provide a good vantage point. The way will be thick with Corsairs and Haradrim, and perhaps your efforts against them will ease our burden somewhat.'","Collect ragged doll from the Corsair camp","'You are not like the others that have come to these lands of late, young one. I sense in you a concern for this child. Fear not! I have lulled her to sleep with my song. She will not wake until she is rested, and the cares that spurred her here are eased. She is safe.\
\
'I am Roamingstar. What is your name, and what is that figure you carry?'\
\
As if under some enchantment, you speak your name and hand Roamingstar the yellow-haired doll. She stares at it with curiosity and sadness. After a time, she gently sets it down next to Roniel's sleeping form.","'Please find my Roniel! None have seen her since the Corsairs attacked us, and I am at the end of my wits!'","Talk to Roamingstar by the Gilrain","A ragged doll in the Corsair camp north-east of Linhir has caught your attention","'This endless shadow seemed to flow out of the south-east, ${PLAYER}. Does it cover Dor-en-Ernil as well as the Vale? I have family in the town of Linhir, to the south, and I worry for their safety.\
\
'If your travels take you in that direction, will you consider finding my brother Ingalad in Linhir? He is a good man, stern and tough, but who can be prepared for the onset of unending night? It would ease my mind some if I knew you would check on him and ensure his safety.\
\
'I would not normally ask for such a favour, but these are unusual times, are they not? I never believed we would see a day without the sun, and yet here it is!'","Roniel is not here, but a ragged doll catches your eye. Did it belong to her?","'A child has gone missing. No one knows for certain if she is lost, but none have seen her since the last Corsair attack. If you could investigate their camp to the north-east, I would be in your debt. My friends have already suffered so much of late. Losing their child, Roniel, would be the gravest hurt of all.'","You tell Ingalad that his brother asked you to check on him.\
\
'I am doing as well as I can under the shadow of this oppressive night, but that is not the only worry occupying my mind. We are beset by foes on all sides, and they press us most cruelly. Corsairs harry our coast, and the Haradrim they bring on their ships disembark and burn our fields.\
\
'If you seek to learn the progress of the Corsair fleet, there is a lighthouse to the south-west that would provide a good vantage point. The way will be thick with Corsairs and Haradrim, and perhaps your efforts against them will ease our burden somewhat.'","Ingalad is in the town of Linhir.\
\
You have scouted the progress of the Corsair fleet and defeated many of the foes that plague Dor-en-Ernil.","Ingalad is somewhere within the town of Linhir, in Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Tologlor of Ethring has asked you to check on his brother Ingalad in the town of Linhir.","Defeated Haradrim in Dor-en-Ernil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A beautiful woman stands by the river, keeping watch on the sleeping Roniel. You should learn what you can about this woman.","Tologlor has asked you to check on his brother Ingalad in the town of Linhir, to the south of Ethring in Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Tologlor is worried for his brother, who lives in the town of Linhir.","Find Barad Rill, the lighthouse in Dor-en-Ernil, to the south-west of Linhir","Book 2, Chapter 5: Beset By Foes","The darkness that covers the Ringló Vale flowed out of the south-east. What evil has the shadow wrought in Dor-en-Ernil?","You have found the town of Linhir, which straddles the River Gilrain","Ingalad believes that Roniel may have fallen prey to Corsairs at a camp to the north-east, and wants you to search for the child.","Defeat Corsairs in Dor-en-Ernil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A girl sleeps by the banks of the river. You have found Roniel.","Travel to the town of Linhir, in Dor-en-Ernil","Talk to Ingalad in Linhir","The lighthouse has been toppled. Beyond, the Corsair fleet continues on its course","Continue searching north-east of the Corsair camp for Roniel"},
[2048]={"El aire está silencioso, el viento quieto. ¿Dónde están los guardias?","'¡No hablo con nadie!'","Boromir está dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada.","'¿Por qué vienes a molestarme? ¡No hablo con nadie!\
\
'No desde que...'","'Quizá debería saber los nombres de tus compañeros.'","'Debo hablar con este anciano y descubrir qué le sucedió.'","Maddoc te da una jarra de cerveza con un fuerte aroma a canela","'No parece haber mucha alegría aquí, al parecer.'","'Espero que no tratéis con demasiada dureza al viejo Aberthol. Es un hombre peculiar, pero pese a su rareza la mayoría de la gente de Herne le tiene cariño....... y siempre ha traído su clientela a la Posada de la Encrucijada, cosa que agradezco.\
\
'Permíteme darte una jarra de su cerveza especiada favorita. Quizá le suelte la lengua. Para ser sincero, eso no suele ser un problema para nuestro Aberthol, pero puede que no quiera hablar sobre lo que le ocurrió aquella noche. La cerveza puede hacerlo más propenso a contarlo.'","Habla con Boromir dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada","Aberthol te observa con nerviosismo","'Si este hombre habla con sinceridad, parece que algún mal vino a Herne....... pero ¿qué pudo haber sido? ¿Y es la misma presencia que describe Boromir?'","'¿Son todas las tabernas del norte tan....... silenciosas?'","'Hace cuatro noches, algo... maligno... pasó por el centro de Herne. Nadie sabe exactamente qué pudo ser, pero cada noche desde entonces un miedo terrible ha tomado la aldea. El viejo Aberthol dice que vio algo esa noche, pero....... no sé. Fue aventurero en su juventud, pero tiene tal fama de fabulador que siempre ha sido difícil separar la verdad de la mentira en sus relatos.\
\
'Pero algo sucedió aquella noche, y la aldea no ha sido la misma desde entonces. Será mejor que sigáis vuestro camino, tú y tus amigos, antes de que regrese la oscuridad.'","Entra en la Posada de la Encrucijada, la taberna de Herne, en busca de respuestas","Maddoc te indica cómo encontrar la casa de Aberthol en la parte norte de Herne","Libro 2, Capítulo 5: La Posada de la Encrucijada","Habla con Aberthol dentro de su casa","Meneldir está dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada.","'Aberthol vive en la parte norte de nuestra aldea. Trátalo con amabilidad, por favor. Le tenemos afecto, pese a sus rarezas.'","La Posada de la Encrucijada, la posada en el cruce de caminos, está cerca del camino del sur que pasa por Herne.\
\
Algo ocurrió en Herne que ha alterado a sus habitantes. Quizá las respuestas estén dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada, la posada en el cruce.","'Será mejor que te marches. ¡Este es un mal momento para pasar por Herne! ¡Créeme!'","'Debo hablar con este hombre y saber qué le ocurrió.'","Coloca la jarra de cerveza especiada sobre la mesa de Aberthol","Aberthol está dentro de su casa, observándote a ti, a tus compañeros y a la jarra de cerveza especiada que le trajiste.","'¿Boromir, dices? ¿Seguro que no eres el mismo Boromir, hijo del Senescal de Gondor? Hace unos veinte años viajé por las tierras del sur, de aventuras, ya sabes, y tuve el privilegio de conocer al Senescal. Recuerdo a sus hijos, ambos de porte noble; ¡te pareces al mayor de los dos! Pero viajas en secreto ahora, por lo que parece. No diré más al respecto. ¡Un Guardia de la Ciudadela —si no su Capitán— en mi propio hogar! Apenas puedo creerlo.\
\
'Y Egfrith, ¡una orgullosa mujer de Rohan! En los días de mi juventud cabalgué por la Marca de los Jinetes a galope alegre. ¿Sigue siendo Théoden el rey de Rohan? Era una tierra hermosa, y él era severo pero fuerte, amado por su pueblo y respetado por sus enemigos. Debe seguir siendo así.'\
\
La expresión de Egfrith se endurece, pero no dice nada. Aberthol continúa.\
\
'Os diré lo que me ocurrió. Con tan finos protectores en mi hogar, ¿qué tengo que temer?'","El interior de la posada está oscuro y silencioso","'Nuestro primer destino será la aldea de Herne, un pueblo de granjeros y comerciantes que creció en un cruce de caminos al noroeste de aquí, donde el Camino Verde que viene del sur se encuentra con la carretera que llega del norte desde Enedwaith. Cuando vine por última vez, la taberna de Herne era un lugar agradable, aunque no podía competir con el Poney Pisador en entretenimiento y compañía. La Posada de la Encrucijada se llamaba, un edificio de dos plantas cerca de la puerta sur.\
\
'Partamos.'","'Espero que Aberthol hable contigo, y quizá puedas tranquilizar su mente.'","'¡No quiero problemas! ¿Puedes dejarme en paz?'","'Hace tiempo que no tengo visitantes. ¿Qué os trae a mi hogar? ¿Queréis oír sobre....... sobre la oscuridad reptante?'\
\
Aberthol tiembla en su silla y toma un trago firme de la cerveza.\
\
'Quizá debería saber vuestros nombres. ¿Quiénes son estos compañeros que traes contigo?'","'Ve con Boromir y Egfrith a hablar con este hombre, ${PLAYER}. Yo preguntaré por Herne a ver qué más puedo aprender de lo sucedido.'","Llamas a Boromir y a Egfrith para que se unan a ti","Aberthol vive en la parte norte de Herne.\
\
Maddoc te contó que algo le ocurrió a Aberthol hace cuatro noches, y el anciano podría hablarte si le sueltas la lengua con una jarra de su cerveza especiada favorita.","Una jarra de cerveza especiada, puesta en su mesa, podría alentarlo a contar lo que le ocurrió.","Aberthol, al parecer sobrecogido por sus visitantes, ahora está dispuesto a contarte su historia.","Presenta a Boromir ante Aberthol","'¡A Herne, entonces! ¿Lo digo correctamente?'","'Algún mal vino a Herne. ¿Es el mismo que encontró Boromir en Gondor?'","Habla con Aberthol dentro de su casa en la parte norte de Herne","El hombre te mira con ojos recelosos y se apresura a entrar en su hogar","'Debería hablar con el anciano mencionado por el posadero. Si su relato coincide con el de mis soldados....... eso me dirá algo del mal que vino a Herne.'","Encuentra la entrada sureste de la aldea de Herne, junto al camino al noroeste de Tharbad","'Tú y tus amigos quizá querráis seguir adelante. Herne ya no es lo que era, y no encontraréis bienvenida aquí.'\
\
Preguntas al posadero qué ocurrió en la aldea, y él frunce el ceño, negando con la cabeza.\
\
'Hace cuatro noches, algo....... mal...g...o... atravesó el centro de Herne. Nadie sabe qué pudo ser, pero cada noche desde entonces un terrible miedo se ha apoderado de la aldea. El viejo Aberthol dice que vio algo esa primera noc...e, ...ero... no sé. Fue aventurero en su juventud, pero tiene tal reputación de contar historias que siempre ha sido difícil separar la verdad de la fantasía.\
\
'Pero algo sucedió esa noche, y la aldea no ha sido la misma desde entonces. Será mejor que sigáis vuestro camino, tú y tus amigos, antes de que regrese la oscuridad.'","'Una mala sensación se ha asentado sobre toda la aldea. No estaba así la última vez que vine.'","Maddoc se aclara la garganta","'Si este hombre habla con sinceridad, parece que algún mal vino a Herne....... pero ¿qué podría haber sido?'","Habla con el aldeano cercano","Aberthol sonríe. 'Eso es distinto', dice","Maddoc, el posadero de la Posada de la Encrucijada, está detrás del mostrador.","Aberthol espera que lo presentes a tus compañeros.","La aldea de Herne se encuentra en el cruce de caminos al noroeste de Tharbad, y la posada allí es un destino popular para viajeros del Viejo Camino del Sur.","'Iré contigo y con Boromir a hablar con este hombre.'","Habla con Maddoc dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada","'Qué nombres de posadas tan pintorescos. ¿La Posada de la Encrucijada? ¿El Poney Pisador? Ninguna será como el Mûmak y la Fortaleza de mi ciudad.'","Herne se encuentra al noroeste de Tharbad, a lo largo del Viejo Camino del Sur.\
\
Meneldir te dijo que cuando vino por aquí por última vez, la posada en el cruce de caminos era un agradable refugio para viajeros, y debería seguir siéndolo.","Algo no va bien en la aldea de Herne.\
\
Quizá uno de los habitantes pueda explicar lo ocurrido.","Presenta a Egfrith ante Aberthol","'Nuestro primer destino será la aldea de Herne, un pueblo de granjeros y comerciantes que creció en un cruce de caminos al noroeste de aquí, donde el Camino Verde que viene del sur se encuentra con la carretera que llega del norte desde Enedwaith.'","Habla con la aldeana cercana","'He visto algo parecido a esto antes, ${PLAYER}. Bueno, digo \\qvisto\\q, pero no lo vi; mejor diría que lo sentí, algo oscuro y maligno; llenó al hombre y al caballo de terror. Defendíamos el río en Osgiliath cuando esta presencia cayó sobre nosotros, y hasta los más valientes fueron sobrecogidos por un miedo terrible. Derribamos el puente tras nosotros y solo unos pocos logramos escapar.\
\
'Nunca he sentido un miedo así antes, ${PLAYER}. Algunos de mis hombres afirmaron que vieron la figura de la que emanaba el terror....... pero no sé si creerlo. ¿Podría ese mal haber venido hacia el norte desde Gondor, de algún modo? En ocasiones sentí que era observado mientras cabalgaba por las tierras va...í...s... ¿o no estaban tan vacías como parecían?\
\
'Debería hablar con el anciano del que habló el posadero. Si su relato coincide con el de mis soldados... eso me dirá algo del mal que vino a Herne.'","'Ve con Boromir y Egfrith a hablar con este hombre, ${PLAYER}. Yo preguntaré por Herne para saber qué más ocurrió.'","'¿Algún mal pasó por Herne, pero la mala sensación permaneció? ¿Qué significa eso?'","Como su vecina, la mujer te fulmina con la mirada y se apresura a entrar en su casa","Habla con Meneldir dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada"},
[2049]={"'Candaith es un buen hombre que ha tomado un riesgo al dar su palabra de que se puede confiar en ti. Por su bien, y por nuestra amistad continua con él, espero que valgas el riesgo.\
\
'Somos un pueblo sencillo que desea mantenerse al margen de la sociedad, pero hay esfuerzos que todos deben emprender para sobrevivir, y te pediremos asistencia para demostrar que eres digno.'","'Puedes usar mi caballo o caminar hasta La Posada Abandonada. Se encuentra al suroeste de aquí, en el borde del Pantano de Moscagua y las Tierras Solitarias, a lo largo del Gran Camino del Este. Debes hablar con Gadaric Mascador y empezar a ganarte la confianza de los Eglain.'","Encuentra a un miembro de los Eglain y pregúntale por el paradero de Radagast el Pardo.\
\
Has trabajado mucho y arduamente para ganarte la confianza de los Eglain. Ahora debes preguntarles por el paradero de Radagast el Pardo.","'Has trabajado duro, y estamos agradecidos por todo lo que has hecho. Pareces tener las mejores intenciones hacia nuestra gente. Por esto, te concederemos el favor que pides.'","Habla con Gadaric Mascador en La Posada Abandonada","Puedes montar el caballo de Candaith o dirigirte a pie a La Posada Abandonada, en el borde de la Pantano de Moscagua y las Tierras Solitarias, a lo largo del Gran Camino del Este.\
\
Candaith te agradeció tu ayuda y advirtió que los Eglain deben entender que tus intenciones son justas antes de permitirte una audiencia con Radagast el Pardo.","'Logré seguir el rastro de Radagast hacia el sur y allí me encontré con amigos, los Eglain, que han hecho de algunas ruinas de las Tierras Solitarias su hogar. Son un pueblo solitario y callado, que ha rechazado las obligaciones sociales por una vida sencilla que arrancan aquí. Los pocos que se aventuran hacia zonas más civilizadas del mundo siguen siendo diferentes de cualquiera que llegarás a conocer.\
\
'Por esa naturaleza, desconfían profundamente de cualquiera que desee tratar con ellos o con sus aliados, y parece que Radagast ha contado con su ayuda no solo ahora, sino también en algún momento del pasado remoto. Me temo que necesitarás ganarte el derecho a hablar con Radagast.\
\
'He hecho mi parte. Mi caballo te llevará hacia el sur y el oeste hasta La Posada Abandonada. Allí deberías solicitar audiencia con Gadaric Mascador. Conocerá tu nombre. Ve con cuidado, ${PLAYER}.'","Libro 2, Capítulo 6: Protegido por los Eglain","Encuentra y habla con un miembro de los Eglain en La Posada Abandonada o en su campamento en Nain Enidh","La investigación de Candaith sobre el paradero de Radagast el Pardo lo llevó al descubrimiento de que está bajo la protección de los Eglain. Ha hablado bien de ti a uno de sus miembros, Gadaric Mascador, pero advirtió que no revelarían la ubicación del Sabio de Pardo sin la seguridad de que tus intenciones son buenas."},
[2050]={"Book 2, Chapter 6: Roamingstar","Roniel has awoken, and you should speak to her and ensure that she is all right.","Roniel stirs. She is nearly awake.","'I thank you for this favour, young one. It has been long years since I cast my eye beyond the banks of the stream. When last I did it brought only grief.'\
\
Sadness wells in the deep pools of Roamingstar's eyes, and her words are nearly whispers.\
\
'An Elf-maid tarried on the banks of Gilrain, lulled to sleep by the beauty of my song. She was reminded of her home, and I delighted in her presence, for my sisters had gone away and I was filled with loneliness.\
\
'But she was needed, and when she awoke the delay had cost her the life of her love. He was an Elf-lord and a prince, Amroth by name, and he waited for her... but she never came. He died believing she was lost forever, and when she awoke it was he who was lost.'\
\
Roamingstar's words trail away into silence. After a moment, the girl Roniel stirs.","'Roniel says she met the river-maiden of the Gilrain, but... she is just a legend, is she not? One of Linhir's traditions involves floating reed baskets on the stream in honour of such a creature, but I did not really believe in the existence of the Five Sisters.\
\
'Is Roniel making up a story? She must be.'","'Oh, hello! Are you a friend of my mother? I was separated from her during the fighting. I ran and ran, and at some point I dropped my doll, but then I was just so tired and fell asleep.\
\
'I think I had a lovely dream, but I cannot remember much of it now. I suppose it is time to return to Linhir. Do you think it is safe? Tell my mother I am on my way home. Her name is Mornil.'","'My daughter Roniel has returned, and she says that you are the one who found her! I am so glad she is safe, and I am grateful for the kindness you have done my family!\
\
'She had an unusual story to tell, and I must say I am not sure I can believe it. Roniel says she met the river-maiden of the Gilrain, but... she is just a legend, is she not? One of Linhir's traditions involves floating reed baskets on the stream in honour of such a creature, but I did not really believe in the existence of the Five Sisters.\
\
'Is Roniel making up a story? She must be.'","Flat stones can be found at several locations to the west of the Gilrain, in Dor-en-Ernil, south-east of Roamingstar.\
\
Roamingstar has given you a number of pebbles to leave on flat stones west of the Gilrain, south of her waterfall glade.","'Oh my! Can it be? I did not think such wonders still existed in this world!'","Roamingstar feels a connexion to the lands through which the Gilrain flows, and has asked you to protect them.","'Leave the pebbles I gave you on flat stones a goodly distance south-east of here, ${PLAYER}. For this small favour you will have the blessing of Gilrain.'","'You did a very good thing today, my friend! Linhir is in your debt.'","Roamingstar is waiting for you to return from the errand on which she sent you.","'Not all who come this way have kindness in their hearts. There are those who wish to harm this land and its people, and they will find no welcome from me or my sisters.'\
\
Roamingstar opens her golden hand, and reveals a number of pebbles. They are worn smooth by the currents of the Gilrain.\
\
'Leave these on flat stones to the south, ${PLAYER}, away from the banks of the river. For this small favour you will have the blessing of Gilrain.'","Roniel's mother Mornil is back in the town of Linhir, in Dor-en-Ernil. She is by the fountain in the north-east court of Linhir.\
\
You have found the missing child and sent her back to her mother.","Talk to Roamingstar by the banks of Gilrain","'I am back, but my mother does not believe I met a river-maiden!'","Talk to Roniel on the banks of the Gilrain","Roamingstar is silent, lost in her thoughts.","Roniel has returned to Linhir, but her mother Mornil does not believe her story.","'I will return to Linhir, but you can lead the way!'","Talk to Roniel in Linhir","Extended Roamingstar's influence (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'I see that Roniel has found her way safely home. I am pleased I was able to restore some measure of happiness to the world.'","Roniel says nothing, but the look on her face is smug and satisfied.","'My mother does not believe me. Well, I think I may be able to convince her!'","Talk to Mornil in Linhir","Roniel sets a small pebble on the edge of the fountain","You have returned Roniel safely to Linhir, and should tell Ingalad of your success.","Leave pebbles on flat stones south-east of Roamingstar (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Ingalad in Linhir"},
[2051]={"'Cuatro noches atrás, tras la puesta del sol, salí de mi hogar para caminar por las calles empedradas de Herne, como es mi costumbre. Esto lo he hecho durante años, cada noche, desde que abandoné la vida de aventurero. Quizás te parezca extraño, pero he descubierto que estos paseos a la luz de la luna mantienen a raya un poco de mi viejo anhelo viajero. \\q¿Será esta la noche en la que siga caminando, Aberthol, viejo amigo?\\q, me he preguntado alguna vez, pero hasta ahora siempre he regresado a mi hogar y el sueño llega pronto.\
\
'Pero esa noche, mientras paseaba por la calle al oeste de mi casa, oliendo las flores nocturnas y escuchando a las ranas en la orilla del río, sentí que algo era distinto. No puedo decirte exactamente qué era, pero me invadió una enorme sensación de... no sé... desasosiego. Lo sentí en el fondo del estómago. Hay un lugar cubierto de hierba a la izquierda entre dos edificios, y allí crece un único árbol. Mi mirada fue atraída hacia él, y mientras observaba te juro que una sombra más profunda se deslizó desde detrás del tronco.\
\
'Emitía un sonido extraño al moverse, un murmullo apenas más allá del límite de mi audición. Me recordó a cuando uno se pierde en bosques lejanos, acechado por una criatura peligrosa que aún no se ve, pero aquello no era un puma. Reuní todo mi coraje, te lo digo, y di media vuelta para correr, pero incluso mientras tensaba los músculos supe que era demasiado tarde. Mientras me quedé petrificado por la sombra que se arrastraba frente a mí, una segunda figura oscura se había acercado por detrás. Esta era enorme, pues cabalgaba sobre un gran corcel negro, pero no podría decirte cómo no oí el sonido de sus cascos sobre el empedrado mientras se acercaba.\
\
'Debo haberme desmayado entonces, pues lo siguiente que recuerdo es que Bledri, uno de los habitantes del pueblo, me sacudía para despertarme, llevando una linterna. Dijo que me encontró tendido al pie del árbol entre esos dos edificios mientras volvía a su casa, y sin señal alguna de ninguna figura oscura. Pero cada noche desde entonces, una terrible sensación de temor ha caído sobre Herne cuando el sol desaparece bajo el horizonte.\
\
'¿Sabéis qué eran, amigos? ¿Se ha visto algo así en Gondor o en Rohan? ¿Qué asunto podría traer criaturas tan terribles hasta Herne?'","Has recogido leña (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Qué aprendiste del anciano, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
Le cuentas a Meneldir el aterrador encuentro nocturno de Aberthol. Él frunce el ceño y se acaricia la barba.\
\
'Esto coincide con la historia que Boromir nos contó sobre el poder que percibió en Osgiliath, pero eso está a leguas de aquí... ¿qué lo ha traído hasta aquí a caballo con tal velocidad? Conozco un nombre de estas criaturas, pero no lo mencionaré aquí.'\
\
Se vuelve hacia el posadero.\
\
'Maddoc, ¿podría pedirte que abras tus puertas a toda la gente de Herne esta noche? Algún mal ha dejado su marca sobre el pueblo, y creo que sería más seguro que todos se resguardaran tras los fuertes muros de la Posada de la Encrucijada esta noche.'\
\
Meneldir vuelve a mirarte.\
\
'En cuanto a nosotros, ${PLAYER}, creo que deberíamos cazar algo en la Pradera de Juncos para reabastecer la despensa de Maddoc, recoger leña para mantener los braseros del pueblo encendidos toda la noche, y avisar a los habitantes que deben refugiarse en la Posada de la Encrucijada esta noche. ¿Qué opinas? No dejaré a esta gente indefensa... no puedo.'","'¿Quieres que la gente de Herne se refugie en la Posada de la Encrucijada esta noche?\
\
'Si no hubiese sentido el terrible temor que cae sobre Herne cuando el sol se pone, quizá me opondría. Pero haré lo que dices, y avisaré a mis vecinos que hagan lo mismo. Algo no está bien en Herne.'","Meneldir está dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada.\
\
Debes regresar con Meneldir y contarle lo que aprendiste de Aberthol.","Meneldir sugirió que tú y tus compañeros cacéis animales en la Pradera de Juncos para obtener carne, recojáis leña para los braseros del pueblo y aviséis a la gente de Herne para que se refugie esta noche tras los seguros muros de la Posada de la Encrucijada.","Habla con Bledri dentro de su casa","Rellena los braseros del pueblo cerca de la Posada de la Encrucijada con leña (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Meneldir dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada y espera a que caiga la noche","Habla con Meneldir fuera de la Posada de la Encrucijada","Los braseros se encuentran frente a la Posada de la Encrucijada en la villa de Herne, esperando que tú y tus compañeros los llenéis con leña.\
\
Meneldir espera mantener a raya los males que amenazan Herne manteniendo los braseros encendidos toda la noche.","Meneldir está dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada.\
\
Los preparativos han concluido, y la noche se acerca.","'Espero que hayamos hecho lo suficiente. Esta noche podría ser difícil.'","Has rellenado los braseros del pueblo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Sabéis qué eran, amigos? ¿Se ha visto algo así en Gondor o en Rohan? ¿Qué podría atraer criaturas tan terribles a Herne?'","'¿Refugiarnos en la Posada de la Encrucijada esta noche? ¡Disparate! Mi familia hará lo que siempre ha hecho: quedarse en nuestro propio hogar. Es cierto que hay un mal presentimiento en Herne últimamente, pero con la puerta atrancada y las velas apagadas, mi familia no tiene nada que temer.\
\
'Otros pueden hacer lo que deseen, pero nosotros no nos esconderemos en la posada toda la noche. ¡Esto es algún ardid de Maddoc para llenar sus arcas, ya verás! Y el viejo Aberthol siempre ha estado loco, ¡pregunta a cualquiera!\
\
'¡Ahora buen día, y no vuelvas a molestarme!'","'¿Los braseros han sido rellenados y la despensa de Maddoc abastecida? Bien. En cuanto a si la gente se refugiará en la Posada de la Encrucijada esta noche, esperemos que la mayoría lo haga. Es por su propio bien, aunque no todos lo crean.\
\
'Hazme saber cuando todo esté listo, ${PLAYER}, y esperaremos a que caiga la noche.'","Has reunido cortes selectos de carne (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolecta leña en la Pradera de Juncos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Quieres que los habitantes se refugien en la Posada de la Encrucijada esta noche?\
\
'Si no hubiera encontrado al viejo Aberthol tendido en el suelo la noche en que esto comenzó, quizá pensaría que no es necesario. Pero creo que algo maligno lo tenía en sus garras, y solo se alejó cuando me acerqué con mi lámpara.\
\
'Avisaré a mis vecinos de tu plan.'","Recolecta cortes selectos de carne de animales en la Pradera de Juncos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Libro 2, Capítulo 6: La Noche de la Espera","Habla con Linnet junto a la fuente en la parte norte de Herne","'Es como temía, ${PLAYER}. Las criaturas que pasaron por Herne hace cuatro noches eran los espectros llamados Nazgûl, y dejaron algo atrás que atrae a los Muertos hacia aquí.\
\
'Pero ¿por qué han vuelto a la vida estas criaturas de leyenda, y adónde se han marchado? Y lo más importante, y que más me preocupa: ¿con qué propósito han llegado tan al norte?'","Meneldir está dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada, esperando oír sobre los preparativos del pueblo para la noche que se avecina.","'En cuanto a nosotros, creo que deberíamos cazar en la Pradera de Juncos para reabastecer la despensa de Maddoc, recoger algo de leña para mantener los braseros del pueblo toda la noche e informar a la gente del pueblo de que deben refugiarse esta noche en la Posada de la Encrucijada. ¿Qué te parece el plan? No dejaré indefensa a esta gente... no puedo.'","Habla con Aldyth dentro de su casa","Aberthol te contó su encuentro con los jinetes oscuros que pasaron por Herne, y del miedo que desde entonces se cierne sobre el pueblo. ¿Puede hacerse algo para salvar Herne?","'Quizá si mantenemos los braseros frente a la Posada de la Encrucijada encendidos toda la noche, mantendremos el mal a raya.'","Meneldir está fuera de la Posada de la Encrucijada tras los sucesos de la larga noche.","Habla con Meneldir dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada"},
[2052]={"Meneldir cree que deberías limpiar la evidencia del ataque de los tumularios en Herne para ayudar a calmar los temores del pueblo.","Meneldir está fuera de la Posada de la Encrucijada en la aldea de Herne.","Con tu ayuda y la de tus compañeros, los aldeanos de Herne sobrevivieron la peligrosa noche.","Boromir está junto al sendero de tierra que lleva al sur hacia Minhiriath.","Has recogido hojas oxidadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Espero no haber hecho mal.'","'Quizás regresó dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada.'","Recoge hojas oxidadas dejadas por los tumularios (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Alto!'","'Boromir tiene razón. No he visto a Egfrith desde que salimos fuera. Pensé que había ido contigo a recoger los objetos caídos de los tumularios, pero dices que no la has visto. ¿Quizás regresó a la posada?'","'Veo la huella de cascos en la tierra. Debió robar un caballo en Herne y ya ha escapado a Minhiriath. Está fuera de nuestro alcance ahora.\
\
'Saruman sabrá lo que buscaba.'","Habla con Meneldir fuera de la Posada de la Encrucijada en Herne","'¿Egfrith? ¿La mujer de Rohan que venía contigo cuando llegaste a Herne? No, no la he visto esta mañana.\
\
'¿Crees que la maldición sobre nuestra aldea ha sido levantada?'","'No puedo creerlo. ¡Nos han tomado por tontos!'","Lleva el equipo descartado a Meneldir en Herne","'Llegamos demasiado tarde.'","'Ella no regresará a Tharbad: el cruce tomaría demasiado tiempo. ¡Debemos alcanzarla por el camino del sur!'","'Deberíamos examinar el acceso norte de la aldea, ya que por allí vinieron los Muertos. Limpiaremos lo que haya quedado de los tumularios para no alarmar aún más a los aldeanos... aunque quizás sea ya demasiado tarde.'","'Espero no haber hecho mal, ${PLAYER}. Ella me dijo que no te diera la carta durante uno o dos días, pero si ya sabes que esperas una carta... no habrá daño en entregártela antes.\
\
'No la leí. Me dijo que no lo hiciera, y su expresión era tan severa que la obedecí. Espero no haber hecho mal, ${PLAYER}.'","La escritura de Egfrith cubre la parte frontal del pergamino","Habla con Meneldir en el borde de Minhiriath","Meneldir está en la aldea de Herne, repasando una y otra vez los sucesos de la noche.","El brazo reptante cierra un puño furioso y deja de moverse","Meneldir está junto al sendero de tierra que lleva al sur hacia Minhiriath.","'¿Qué ha pasado, ${PLAYER}? ¿Encontraste a Egfrith? ¿Está en peligro?'\
\
Le entregas la carta a Meneldir, y mientras la lee su expresión se oscurece, una tormenta de ira cruzando su rostro.\
\
'Esto no puede ser. ¡Esto no puede ser!'","Egfrith te escribió una carta, confiándola a Aberthol.","Aberthol señala una hoja de pergamino boca abajo sobre su mesa","Habla con Boromir fuera de la Posada de la Encrucijada en Herne","'¿Estás bien? Espero no haber hecho mal.'","'¡Rápido!' grita Meneldir, '¡Debemos impedir que escape! ¡Hacia el camino del sur!'","El brazo caído de un tumulario, olvidado durante la batalla, ¡repta para atacar!","Habla con los aldeanos de Herne y averigua qué pasó con Egfrith","'¿La mujer de Rohan? No la he visto esta mañana.'","'Alguno de los aldeanos debió ver a Egfrith en algún lugar. Herne no es tan grande.\
\
'Habla con los aldeanos con quienes hablamos antes, ${PLAYER}. ¡Alguien habrá visto algo!'","Da vuelta al pergamino que Egfrith dejó con Aberthol","'No lo vi venir, ${PLAYER}. Creí que Egfrith era de fiar. No lo vi.'\
\
Boromir habla en voz baja, pero oyes la tensión en su voz.\
\
'Sé lo que debo hacer.'","Habla con Boromir en el borde de Minhiriath","'Estoy seguro de que Egfrith está bien, pero es inquietante que aún no haya vuelto.'","Recoge joyas ajadas dejadas por los tumularios (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Meneldir está en Herne, reflexionando profundamente sobre el ataque de los tumularios de la noche anterior.","Egfrith no parece estar dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada","'¿La mujer de Rohan? No, no la he visto desde que salieron fuera.'","Libro 2, Capítulo 7: Preguntas","Es probable que Egfrith haya huido directamente hacia el sur para evitar el difícil vado de Tharbad.\
\
Tú y tus compañeros debéis intentar impedir que Egfrith escape mientras se dirige a Isengard y a su amo Saruman.","Meneldir no ha visto a Egfrith desde el ataque de los tumularios. ¿Quizás regresó a la posada?","Encuentra a Egfrith dentro de la Posada de la Encrucijada","'Incluso a la luz del día me cuesta creer que tales cosas sean posibles. ¡Antiguos horrores vuelven a recorrer la tierra, y los Muertos caminan!'","Meneldir detiene vuestra persecución de Egfrith","Termina de limpiar tras el ataque de los tumularios","¿Egfrith sirve a Saruman? ¡Debemos decirlo a los demás!","Has recogido joyas ajadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Espero no haber hecho mal, ${PLAYER}. Ella me dijo que no te diera la carta por uno o dos días, pero si ya sabes que esperas una carta, supongo que no habrá daño en entregártela ahora.\
\
'¡No la leí! Me dijo que no lo hiciera, y su expresión era tan severa que la obedecí. Espero no haber hecho mal, ${PLAYER}.'","'Comparto el asombro de Meneldir, ${PLAYER}, pero no me gusta. ¡Dejad que los Muertos duerman, y no atormenten a los vivos! Me llena de repugnancia que semejantes cosas puedan ser.\
\
'Pero ¿dónde está Egfrith? Creí que había ido contigo, pero no ha regresado. ¿Crees que cayó presa de alguno de los tumularios que podríamos haber pasado por alto?'","Egfrith dejó una nota para ti y tus compañeros. Está boca abajo sobre la mesa de Aberthol.","Boromir está en Herne, disgustado por los muertos que caminan y los sucesos de la noche anterior.","Egfrith está desaparecida. Quizá alguno de los aldeanos sepa adónde fue.","Lee las palabras de la carta de Egfrith","'¡Te dije que estaríamos bien! No hacía falta escondernos en la taberna de Maddoc después de todo, y pienso contárselo a todos mis vecinos cuando te hayas marchado.'\
\
Preguntas a Linnet si ha visto a Egfrith esta mañana.\
\
'¿Esa mujer de Rohan que va contigo? Sí, la vi. Fue a ver al viejo Aberthol poco después de que saliera yo. ¡Locos, todos ellos!'","'Este equipo es muy antiguo, ${PLAYER}. Incluso a la luz del día me cuesta creer que tales cosas sean posibles. ¡Antiguos horrores vuelven a recorrer la tierra, y los Muertos caminan!\
\
'Mientras estabas fuera encontré un amuleto en forma de calavera enterrado en la tierra: una tumba poco profunda, justo bajo la capa superior del suelo. Creo que lo dejaron aquí a propósito para atraer a esas criaturas.'","Alcanza a Egfrith al sur de Herne antes de que pueda escapar","'Mis amigos...\
\
'No, no puedo llamaros así, pues nuestra amistad estaba basada en un engaño. Lo siento. Me causa un gran dolor escribir esto, pero no me queda otra opción. No podría perdonarme si os abandonara sin explicación. Pero debo dejaros, porque...'\
\
La tinta aquí está emborronada.\
\
'${PLAYER}, Meneldir del Norte y Boromir de Gondor... mi misión en estas tierras no es la que os dije. Es cierto que nací en Faldham, en los Norcrofts, y que pongo el bien de Rohan por encima de todo, pero mi misión no era buscar a los Dúnedain. El rey Théoden está enfermo, eso es verdad, pero no existe cura para su dolencia, ni en la Marca de los Jinetes ni en la tierra salvaje de los Dúnedain. Se ha debilitado, y él mismo se ha convertido en una grave amenaza para la supervivencia de Rohan. Su pueblo necesita un rey fuerte, pero yace postrado en su lecho. Ha olvidado la fuerza que poseyó antaño y ya no puede guiar a quienes claman por él. En días pasados quizá habría cabalgado a la gloria, para morir en batalla y encender los corazones de los Rohirrim, pero ya no.\
\
'Fue con el Mago Saruman con quien consulté sobre esto, pues ha sido largo tiempo amigo de Rohan, y él confirmó lo que yo temía: es una debilidad de la sangre lo que aqueja a Théoden, y debe correr también por las venas de Théodred, su heredero. El Mago posee gran sabiduría, pues ha vivido muchas vidas, y ve aquello que los demás no conseguimos reconocer: que Rohan mismo sufre una enfermedad. Tratará esta enfermedad con un remedio difícil. Ha reunido numerosos orcos, probablemente de sus guaridas montañosas, y se prepara para enviarlos contra el reino. Por el crisol de esta prueba, los hombres poderosos de Rohan demostrarán quién es lo bastante fuerte para gobernar. Digo \\qhombres\\q, pero quizá sea una reina quien pueda salvar a Rohan de este peligro. Los antiguos linajes no bastan.\
\
'Aun con toda su sabiduría, Saruman no puede ver todo. Cuando Boromir de Gondor cabalgó cerca de Isengard, el Mago quiso saber qué llevó al hijo de Denethor a abandonar su tierra. ¿Estaba en peligro su plan de salvar Rohan? Me encargó seguir al hijo de Gondor hacia el norte y descubrir el propósito de su viaje. Manteniéndome un día detrás de él, fuera de su vista en las tierras vacías, pero siempre lo bastante cerca para seguir su rastro, avancé hasta el cruce del Aguagrís en Tharbad. Allí os encontré, Meneldir y ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Fue un acto desesperado unirme a vuestro grupo, pero temía que Boromir escapara de mi alcance y que fracasara en mi misión. Y aun así fracasé, porque en el breve tiempo que viajamos juntos comprendí lo que llevó a Boromir a estas tierras, tan lejos de su hogar. Viajó estas leguas impulsado por un sueño, por nada tan seguro como la más tenue esperanza de que pudiera ayudar a Gondor. Así ocurre conmigo y con Rohan. Cada uno de nosotros haría lo mismo por su tierra natal.\
\
'Incluso ahora trato de excusar mi traición, como si evitara el juicio no escribiéndola. Mi misión tenía más: una vez descubriera el propósito de Boromir, debía matarlo. No podría haberlo hecho en combate, por toda mi destreza, pero una de estas noches, mientras dormía, podría haberlo logrado.\
\
'Pero no lo haré. Ahora marcho a llevarle a Saruman el conocimiento que ansiaba. Aprenderá algo del sueño de Boromir, y tendrá que bastarle. Creí que podría matar a cualquiera si con ello salvaba mi reino, pero estaba equivocada.\
\
'Ordenaré a Aberthol que os entregue esta carta en unos días. Quiero que sepáis lo que he hecho, y lo que no he hecho, pero no arriesgaré a que me detengáis.\
\
'Por Rohan, siempre,\
\
'Egfrith.'","Meneldir cree que deberías limpiar la evidencia del ataque de los tumularios en Herne para calmar las mentes y temores de los aldeanos."},
[2053]={"Radagast el Pardo vive en reclusión en una torre de las ruinas de Ost Guruth, el lugar que los Eglain llaman hogar. Busca su consejo.\
\
Gadaric y Hunulf Mascador creen que tus intenciones son buenas y te han proporcionado la ubicación de su invitado más estimado.","'Has sido paciente, ${PLAYER}. Debes entender que somos un pueblo solitario. Valoramos mucho a nuestros amigos y los protegemos como podemos.\
\
'Radagast es uno de esos amigos y está aquí por petición de nuestro líder para ayudarnos con un terror que ha despertado de un largo letargo. Se ha instalado en las ruinas de Ost Guruth, el lugar que llamamos hogar.\
\
'Puedes hacer el viaje hacia el este. La ruina se encuentra al norte del Gran Camino del Este, antes de que la carretera serpentee entre los pantanos del norte y del sur. Busca a Radagast en la torre. Quizás haya una forma en la que puedas ayudarle, así como él seguramente te ayudará.'","'Has demostrado una y otra vez la sinceridad de tus afirmaciones, ${PLAYER}. Por lo tanto, es justo que honremos tu solicitud y te proporcionemos la información que necesitas.\
\
'Radagast siempre ha sido un amigo de nuestro pueblo. Viene a nosotros ahora como un favor a nuestro líder, quien lo llamó cuando la fauna de Agamaur se volvió corrupta. Está en estudio privado en la última torre al fondo de las ruinas de Ost Guruth, el lugar que llamamos hogar.\
\
'Ve a buscarlo. Quizás haya una forma en la que ambos puedan ayudarse mutuamente.'","Libro 2, Capítulo 7: Radagast el Pardo","Habla con Radagast el Pardo en su torre de Ost Guruth","'Radagast el Pardo seguramente se encuentra en Ost Guruth, muy al este de la Cima de los Vientos. Si ya se ha marchado, búscalo en el campamento de los Eglain en Agamaur. Puede que pueda decirnos el significado de las runas dejadas en la Cima de los Vientos.'","'Encontrarás a Radagast solo con sus notas y compañeros en la torre al fondo de las ruinas de Ost Guruth. Ve allí y habla con él. Tienes la bendición de los Eglain.'","Has ganado la confianza de los Eglain, y ellos te han confesado que Radagast el Pardo, otro miembro del orden de Gandalf, reside actualmente en una torre de Ost Guruth.","'Si buscas a nuestro visitante, lo encontrarás probablemente en la torre que se alza al final de la avenida principal. Aunque a veces se queda en nuestro campamento de Agamaur.\
\
'¡Apresúrate, sobre todo! No nos gustan los extraños por aquí.'","Habla con Radagast el Pardo","'¿Los Eglain te dejaron entrar? Te estaba esperando, aunque esperaba que llegaras un poco antes. Has tardado en llegar. Entiendo que encontraste algo en la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
'Esta inscripción... creo que es una runa G, una marca utilizada a menudo por Gandalf el Gris, otro de mi orden. A partir de la descripción de esos tres trazos, supuse que él estuvo en Amon Sûl el 3 de octubre, hace apenas unos días.\
\
'Yo también vi los relámpagos en la Cima de los Vientos y temo que Gandalf haya tenido problemas allí. No lo he visto desde que nos separamos en el Vado de Sarn, así que no puedo decirte más sobre él o sus viajes. De este lugar puedo decirte mucho, pero entenderás muy poco.'"},
[2054]={"You have found Thorongil, and he is, as you suspected, Aragorn, son of Arathorn","Talk to Ioron in Linhir","'Ha ha! Welcome, welcome! There is no need to look so crestfallen, my friend! Do not concern yourself with the shadow that covers the sky, for it cannot last forever! The winds of hope are blowing!'\
\
Your puzzled expression prompts Ioron to dance even more vigourously, despite his age. When you offer him a stabilizing hand, he shakes his head.\
\
'No need, friend! I will tell you what has caused the years to drop away from old Ioron, if you will listen!'","Collected Umbar badges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find Thorongil outside Pelargir, in Lebennin","Ioron is south of Ingalad, in Linhir.\
\
The folk of Linhir are concerned for the safety of Ioron, who has been acting peculiarly for several hours.","The man Ioron believed to be Thorongil is in fact Aragorn, son of Arathorn.\
\
Ioron asked you to find Thorongil, great hero of Gondor, and you have found him outside Pelargir.","Bring Southron and Umbar badges to Aragorn outside Pelargir","'A great, silent host swept down from the north, driving fear into the hearts of those engaged in battle at the city, both foe-man and defender alike. The host has moved on to the east, but I saw from afar the man who rode at its head, and I knew him.\
\
'This man bore the very visage of Thorongil, the great hero of Gondor who I saw once in my youth, nearly two score years ago. He it was who gathered the great fleet at Pelargir and sailed it to Umbar, utterly breaking the spirits of the Corsairs and smashing the walls of their fortress. Now he has returned, and the years have not touched him as they have weathered me. His strength remains, timeless and unchanging! He will destroy the Corsairs as he did before.\
\
'So that is why I celebrate, and you should too! Follow in his train, friend, defeat Haradrim and Corsairs in Lebennin, and find him at Pelargir. Show him badges of the enemies you defeat, and he will know the people of Gondor have not forgotten him! Thorongil! Thorongil!'","'It is good to see you again, my friend!'","'It is good to see you again, my friend! I see you have been doing good work throughout these lands. To my sorrow my errand has driven me with such speed I could not slow my pace overmuch to help the good people of Gondor, and I fear there are many sad stories behind me.\
\
'It is time now to try and prevent another. Now we will see if there is any of Thorongil still left within me, I suppose. We must stop the Corsairs here!'","Collect Umbar badges from Corsairs in Lebennin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I know you must continue on your mission to Pelargir, and I will not delay you. But there is one more thing....\
\
'I have heard that an old man of the city, Ioron by name, may have fallen into some madness. He has been hooting and cheering for the past few hours, and folk are afraid he may do some hurt to himself. I would be grateful if you checked on him and ensured that he is of sound mind and no danger to himself or others.\
\
'You will find him south of here. Once you have satisfied yourself that he has not succumbed to madness, continue on to Pelargir with my thanks and my family's.'","The man Ioron believed to be Thorongil may be approaching the gates of Pelargir, in Lebennin.\
\
Ioron asked you to find Thorongil, great hero of Gondor.","'That is why I celebrate, and you should too! Follow in his train, friend, defeat Haradrim and Corsairs in Lebennin, and find him at Pelargir. Show him badges of the enemies you defeat, and he will know the people of Gondor have not forgotten him! Thorongil! Thorongil!'","Collected Southron badges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have heard that an old man of the city, Ioron by name, may have fallen into some madness. He has been hooting and cheering for the past few hours, and folk are afraid he may do some hurt to himself. I would be grateful if you checked on him and ensured that he is of sound mind and no danger to himself or others.'","Book 2, Chapter 7: Thorongil's Visage","Ingalad is very grateful for the help you have provided the people of Linhir, and hopes you can do the same for the folk at Pelargir.","Talk to Ioron, the dancing man in Linhir","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","Corsairs and Haradrim can be found throughout Lebennin.\
\
Ioron wants you to defeat Corsairs and Haradrim throughout Lebennin, bringing the badges of rank they carry to Thorongil outside Pelargir.","Collect Southron badges from Haradrim in Lebennin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ioron stops dancing, but his smile grows wider than ever","Ioron is south of Ingalad, in Linhir.\
\
You have spoken with Ioron and he insists that the winds of hope are on the rise. Has he truly gone mad, as the people of Linhir suppose?"},
[2055]={"Meneldir accedió a reunirse contigo en la puerta norte de Herne, donde ambos continuaréis el viaje para encontrar a su amigo Narndir.","Habla con Meneldir en la puerta este de Herne.","'Ojalá fuera de otro modo, Boromir, pero respeto tu decisión. Buena suerte en tu viaje, y repito tus palabras de advertencia.\
\
'${PLAYER}, a menos que tú también desees dejarme, creo que deberíamos regresar a la puerta este de Herne antes de continuar en busca de mi amigo Narndir, quien podrá guiarnos hasta el caudillo de los Dúnedain.'","Hiriente por la traición de una compañera, el Capitán de Gondor ha decidido continuar su viaje en soledad.","Meneldir está en el camino que conduce a Minhiriath, contemplando la decisión de Boromir.","'Creo que deberíamos regresar a la puerta este de Herne antes de continuar en busca de mi amigo Narndir, quien podrá guiarnos hasta el caudillo de los Dúnedain.'","Reúnete con Meneldir en la puerta este de Herne.","'He estado pensando en Egfrith, ${PLAYER}, y en sus mentiras. Ya hemos pasado por mucho, y aún queda más por delante... no quiero que haya engaños entre nosotros. Los secretos tienden a crecer cuando se los deja en la oscuridad. Un amigo mío los describió como hongos, pero menos sabrosos. Sí, era un hobbit, aunque no es el único pueblo que aprecia los hongos cocidos.\
\
'Pero estoy dando rodeos. Por supuesto que sí.'\
\
Meneldir suspira pesadamente.\
\
'Nací en Tornhad, un asentamiento de los Dúnedain en el Ángulo del Mitheithel, y yo era uno de ese pueblo. Crecí jugando en los bosques y cuevas cercanas, y cuando alcancé la mayoría de edad juré el voto que todos juraban: proteger la línea del rey, como se había hecho durante siglos, y obedecer en todo al caudillo de los Dúnedain y a sus lugartenientes de confianza.\
\
'Fallé en esto, ${PLAYER}. Me ordenaron vigilar cierta casa, pues se temía que trolls hubiesen bajado de las montañas y pudieran poner en peligro a la gente que vivía allí. Dejé que mi vigilancia flaqueara, y en un día nublado los trolls avanzaron mucho más lejos de lo que nadie esperaba y una familia fue asesinada. Rompí mi juramento, y ellos sufrieron las consecuencias de mi fracaso. No me he considerado un Dúnadan desde ese día.\
\
'Narndir y algunos otros prometieron hablar por mí ante el caudillo, pero mi propia vergüenza ardía como un fuego, y huí. No habría vuelto a estas tierras salvo que nuestra advertencia fuera grave... y lo es. Así que ahora lo sabes, ${PLAYER}. Júzgame como quieras, pero la lección de Egfrith me ha mostrado que es mejor que lo sepas.'","Meneldir se reunirá contigo en la puerta este de Herne, donde ambos continuaréis el viaje para encontrar a su amigo Narndir.","Habla con Meneldir junto al borde de Minhiriath.","'Comencé este viaje solo, y debo terminarlo solo.'\
\
Meneldir intenta protestar, pero Boromir levanta una mano.\
\
'He tomado mi decisión. La traición de Egfrith me ha abierto los ojos a la triste verdad de que solo puedo confiar en mí mismo. Si el destino de Minas Tirith está realmente en juego, no puedo arriesgarme a perder esta única oportunidad de evitarlo. Lo lamento. Es mejor que continúe hacia el valle oculto de Imladris... solo.\
\
'¡Les deseo lo mejor a ambos! Tened cuidado si os encontráis en el camino del poder maligno que sentí en Osgiliath, aquel que envió a los Muertos contra Herne.\
\
'Me despido de vosotros, aunque pese en mi corazón... pero debo hacerlo. Adiós.'","'Adiós, mis amigos. Después de esto, creo que no nos veremos nuevamente hasta que nuestros viajes hayan concluido.'","Libro 2, Capítulo 8: Un Viaje en Soledad"},
[2056]={"Aragorn makes ready to lead his forces into the port city of Pelargir and reclaim it from the Corsairs of Umbar.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the battle, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Retaking Pelargir' from the menu. After you successfully complete the battle, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","'Most of the Corsairs have fled in terror, their morale and their resolve broken, but we must be certain they are defeated.'\
\
You tell Aragorn about Balakhôr the Scourge and your encounter on his flagship.\
\
'I think you are right, ${PLAYER}. He is the key to ending the threat of Umbar. We have to find him and put an end to his leadership of the Corsairs.'","Talk to Aragorn at his camp outside Pelargir","The Corsairs have taken the port city of Pelargir, and now the time has come to drive them into the sea!","Book 2, Chapter 8: The Battle of Pelargir","'The Corsairs have occupied the city, looting and pillaging from the moment their feet left the decks of their ships. Let us storm the city and retake it from our enemies! They have burned most of Gondor's fleet, but they will not retain the port!'","Aragorn is outside the city of Pelargir, and wishes to discuss the course of the battle with you.","Complete 'Retaking Pelargir' from the Epic Battles Panel","'The Corsairs have occupied the city, looting and pillaging from the moment their feet left the decks of their ships. Let us storm the city and retake it from our enemies! They have burned most of Gondor's fleet, but they will not retain the port!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the battle, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Retaking Pelargir' from the menu. After you successfully complete the battle, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>"},
[2057]={"'Actúa con toda la rapidez posible y tráeme el musgo de los pantanos.'","Musgo de pantano recogido de nidos de merodeadores de pantano (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'La tierra misma se está volviendo contra nosotros y no sé por qué. Incluso los pastores son sombras retorcidas de lo que solían ser. Hablo de los Merodeadores de pantano, los que cuidan los árboles. \
\
'Si puedo discernir qué está retorciendo a los pastores, tal vez pueda determinar qué está contaminando la tierra. Tráeme el musgo que usan para forrar sus nidos. Deambulan por el pantano al este de aquí.\
\
'Recuerda, no deseo hacer daño a los pastores, sin importar lo confundidos que parezcan. Son víctimas inocentes de la corrupción y no saben el daño que hacen.'","Los merodeadores de pantano vagan por Haragmar, al este de Ost Guruth.\
\
Para entender qué causa la corrupción del pantano, Radagast necesita la musgo presente en los nidos de los merodeadores de pantano.","Una aura de corrupción llevó a Radagast el Pardo al Pantano Rojo. Necesita ayuda para descubrir la fuente de este mal.","'Has hecho bien. Este musgo me ayudará a entender cómo el mal está contaminando el Pantano Rojo.\
\
'Este es solo el primer paso para determinar qué causó que los pastores se volvieran confusos e irracionales.\
\
'Aún queda más por hacer, amigo mío. No será fácil.'","Recoge musgo de pantano de los nidos de merodeadores de pantano (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Radagast espera en Ost Guruth, al oeste de Haragmar.\
\
Deberías regresar junto a Radagast el Pardo con la musgo que has encontrado.","Libro 2, Capítulo 8: El Pantano Rojo","'¡Rápido! Recolecta el musgo de los nidos de los merodeadores de pantano. El tiempo se acaba para estas pobres criaturas.'","Lleva el musgo de pantano a Radagast el Pardo"},
[2059]={"Los tumularios se encuentran más adentro de Haragmar, la parte sur del Pantano Rojo, al este de Ost Guruth.\
\
Radagast te envió de regreso al pantano para derrotar a los tumularios que están ensuciando la tierra con su maldad.","Radagast el Pardo espera en la torre al norte del camino principal de Ost Guruth.\
\
Deberías regresar junto a Radagast el Pardo con noticias de tu batalla contra los tumularios de Haragmar.","'La destrucción de los tumularios solo puede ayudarnos en el futuro. Ahora escucha, porque hay mucho más por hacer.'","Tumularios en Haragmar derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has descubierto tumularios en Haragmar, la parte sur del Pantano Rojo, lo que alarma a Radagast el Pardo. Sospecha que las potencias de Angmar están involucradas.","'Puedo oler la muerte en el musgo, como si hubiera sido arrancado de una tumba antigua. Este hedor a descomposición y maldad no es algo natural. Creo que los tumularios son los culpables.\
\
'Los tumularios son los huesos de los muertos, agitados por espíritus malignos de Angmar y Rhudaur. Las guerras aquí hace mucho tiempo hicieron que Haragmar fuera tan propicio para los tumularios como las Quebradas de los Túmulos al oeste. Regresa a Haragmar, el pantano al este, y destruye estas criaturas repugnantes.\
\
'Si hay tumularios, temo que también haya otras criaturas malignas acechando en el pantano. Por ahora, sin embargo, solo debes preocuparte por los tumularios.'","Derrota tumularios en Haragmar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Libro 2, Capítulo 9: Los muertos hinchados","'Contrario a los vivos, los tumularios se vuelven más fuertes y poderosos con el tiempo. Destrúyelos, mientras determino su origen.'","Habla con Radagast el Pardo en Ost Guruth"},
[2060]={"Habla con Candaith en su campamento de las Tierras Solitarias","Saeradan se encuentra en su cabaña al norte del Camino Verde, en las Tierras de Bree.\
\
Saeradan el Montaraz puede saber dónde deberías reunirte con Radagast el Pardo.","'Has hecho mucho bien por la gente de las Tierras de Bree, pero la Sombra de Angmar se extiende por todas partes. He aprendido de Gwaihir el Señor de los Vientos que otro de mi orden ha encontrado corrupción en las Tierras Solitarias, al este de Bree. Incluso puede estar relacionado con los peligros que encontraste en el Gran Túmulo.\
\
'Por desgracia, Radagast es propenso a vagar y será difícil de encontrar. Te pido que consigas la ayuda de los Montaraces para encontrar su ubicación. Hay uno aquí en Bree, Saeradan, que podrá ayudarte.\
\
'Sal de Bree por la Puerta Oeste y gira al norte por el Camino Verde. Busca a Saeradan en su cabaña al este del Camino Verde, frente al lugar de trabajo de Espinar.'","Habla con Saeradan en su cabaña del Camino Verde","'¿Radagast el Pardo? No lo he visto y no sé nada de su paso, pero últimamente ha llegado un frío y una sombra a estas tierras.'","Radagast el Pardo, junto con los Montaraces del Norte, se ha dirigido hacia el este, a las Tierras Solitarias, en busca del origen de un gran mal.","'Toma mi caballo. Te llevará por el norte de Bree y a través del Paso de Moscagua hasta el campamento de Candaith.'","Libro 2, Prólogo: A la ayuda de la Orden","Candaith se encuentra en su campamento de las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
Saeradan no sabe dónde se dirigió Radagast cuando salió de la cabaña del Montaraz. Sospecha que Candaith, el Montaraz que vigila las Tierras Solitarias, podría tener información sobre el paradero del Mago.","'Con la ayuda de Trancos, la defensa de las Tierras de Bree y sus fronteras recae en Saeradan. Creo que estará dispuesto a ayudarte, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Viaja por la Puerta Oeste de Bree y sigue el camino hacia el norte hasta que veas la granja de Espinar al oeste. Deja el camino y dirígete a la cabaña oculta de Saeradan al noreste de esa granja.\
\
'Habla con Saeradan y pídele ayuda en este asunto.'","'Debo confesar que no sé a dónde se dirigió Radagast cuando se marchó de aquí, aparte de que fue hacia el este, a las Tierras Solitarias. Sé que estaba preocupado por los relámpagos que vio en la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
'Uno de mis parientes, Candaith, ya ha viajado hasta allí para investigar... quizás Radagast se haya unido a él.\
\
'Si lo deseas, mi caballo te llevará al campamento de Candaith.'"},
[2061]={"Halbarad y los Montaraces del Vado de Sarn solicitan tu ayuda para encontrar a sus camaradas desaparecidos y enfrentarse al servidor del Rey Brujo responsable de gran parte de los males que asolaron Cardolan en años pasados, y ahora de nuevo en el presente.","Habla con Halbarad y ve con él a registrar la fortaleza","'No tenemos elección ahora. Debemos buscar a Gorwen y a Meneldir, y esperar no haber llegado demasiado tarde.\
\
'Prepárate, , y habla conmigo cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}. De un modo u otro, esta aventura se acerca a su fin.'","Halbarad se encuentra en el campamento de Gorwen, al sur de Dol Ernil, lamentando la pérdida de Meneldir y la huida del Miedo Gris.","Halbarad se encuentra en el campamento de Gorwen, al sur de Dol Ernil, preparándose para registrar la fortaleza en busca tanto de su Montaraz desaparecido como de Meneldir.","Libro 3, Capítulo 10: Espectro del Miedo Gris","'Registraremos la fortaleza, ${PLAYER}. Esperemos estar preparados para afrontar lo que encontremos.'","Habla con Halbarad en el campamento de Gorwen, al sur de Dol Ernil","'El Miedo Gris ha huido, ${PLAYER}, pero no abandonará su odio hacia esta tierra. Cuando reaparezca, sea donde sea, deberá ser enfrentado de nuevo. Esperemos que haya otros con tu fortaleza, y con la fortaleza de Meneldir, para oponérsele.'\
\
Halbarad asiente con solemnidad.\
\
'Sí, había una fortaleza en Meneldir que no había visto antes. No diré que mis gentes lo juzgaran con excesiva dureza. En su lugar diré esto: sé qué causó que se apartara de los Dúnedain. ¿Te confió a ti esa historia?'\
\
Asientes, recordando el dolor en el rostro de Meneldir cuando ambos se preparaban para tomar el camino fuera de Herne.\
\
'Que dejara flaquear su cautela, y que una familia pagara por ello con sus vidas, es motivo de gran pesar. Pero si hubiera hablado de su error con Aragorn, capitán de los Dúnedain y a quien juramos lealtad, no habría encontrado palabras ásperas. No habría hallado reprensión ni castigo. Habría encontrado palabras de apoyo y comprensión, y quizá lágrimas. Meneldir cometió un error, como todo hombre y mujer que pisan estas tierras ha cometido alguno. Algunos fueron menores, otros mayores, pero lo que verdaderamente importa es cómo aprendieron de los errores cometidos.\
\
'Rompió su juramento no el día en que desfalleció su vigilancia, sino el día en que nos abandonó, el día en que huyó de una familia que lo habría ayudado. Podría haber sido de otro modo, si no se hubiera rendido a la culpa que sentía. No puedo borrar esa deshonra, pero tampoco puedo borrar los actos que realizó en favor de los Dúnedain y del pueblo de Cardolan en estos últimos días. Estas son las cosas que le diría ahora, si pudiera, pero ya es demasiado tarde para tales palabras.\
\
'Antes de que la sombra de su culpa cayera sobre Meneldir, él era un dúnadan. Se alzará un túmulo de piedras en Tornhad en honor de todos los Montaraces que han caído en Cardolan en estos últimos días, y me aseguraré de que Meneldir figure en ese memorial. Fue uno de los nuestros durante un tiempo, y al final luchó por nosotros con un valor que no habríamos esperado.\
\
'Adiós, Meneldir. Descansa en paz.'"},
[2062]={"Halbarad cree que brindarás gran ayuda a los Dúnedain a medida que te fortalezcas y continúes tus aventuras en las Tierras Solitarias o en las Quebradas del Norte.","Halbarad te indicó que te reunieras con otro de los Dúnedain, un montaraz llamado Candaith, que acampa cerca de la base de la Cima de los Vientos, en las Tierras Solitarias.","'Has demostrado ser ${PLAYERNAME:un amigo[m]|una amiga[f]} de los Dúnedain. Te sugiero que ayudes a la gente de las Quebradas del Norte y de las Tierras Solitarias, aumentando tu fuerza y el bien que puedes hacer por quienes habitan esos lugares. Cuando hayas hecho todo lo que esté a tu alcance por ellos, busca al montaraz Candaith, que vigila Amon Sûl, la antigua colina de la Cima de los Vientos, en las Tierras Solitarias. Cuéntale lo que has visto aquí y adviértele de los peligros crecientes que ahora amenazan la Tierra Media.'","Tus aventuras te han hecho más fuerte y aún más ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a ayudar a quienes lo necesitan.","'Hemos demostrado al Miedo Gris que esta tierra no se rendirá sin oponer resistencia, pero parece que otros peligros surgen incluso ahora. Si es cierto que el reino de Angmar vuelve a alzarse y que su nuevo líder sirve al Señor de los Nazgûl... pronto estaremos muy ocupados, .\
\
'Esto es lo que creo que deberíamos hacer. Viajaré a las Quebradas del Norte para ver si hay actividad a lo largo de la frontera con Angmar. Iré con varios de los míos para reforzar la antigua ciudad de Esteldín, abandonada durante muchos años en un paso oculto entre las colinas. Si resulta necesario que vuelva a ser un asentamiento próspero y atraiga la atención de nuevos enemigos lejos de otras aldeas pacíficas... bueno, tomaré esa decisión cuando llegue allí.\
\
'En cuanto a ti, , has demostrado ser ${PLAYERNAME:un amigo[m]|una amiga[f]} de los Dúnedain. Te sugiero que ayudes a la gente de las Quebradas del Norte y de las Tierras Solitarias, aumentando tu fuerza y el bien que puedes hacer por quienes habitan esos lugares. Cuando hayas hecho todo lo que esté a tu alcance por ellos, busca al montaraz Candaith, que vigila Amon Sûl, la antigua colina de la Cima de los Vientos, en las Tierras Solitarias. Cuéntale lo que has visto aquí y adviértele de los peligros crecientes que ahora amenazan la Tierra Media.\
\
'Ve con la buena voluntad de los Dúnedain, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Ojalá volvamos a encontrarnos en tiempos más felices.'","Halbarad te ha reconocido como ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} de los Dúnedain y te ha animado a ayudar a su pueblo siempre que te sea posible.","'¡El Gran Camino del Este ha visto mucho más tránsito de lo habitual en los últimos días! ¿Qué te trae hasta la base de la Cima de los Vientos?'\
\
Explicas brevemente que Halbarad te envió para advertir sobre los peligros crecientes en tierras salvajes y que una nueva sombra se alza en el reino de Angmar. Candaith asiente.\
\
'He oído rumores de que esto podría ser así por parte de otros de mi pueblo que han pasado por aquí, y he visto suficiente maldad con mis propios ojos como para no creerlo.'","Libro 3, Capítulo 11: La amistad de los Dúnedain","Continúa tus aventuras en las Tierras Solitarias o en las Quebradas del Norte y alcanza el nivel 32.","Habla con Candaith en su campamento cerca de la base de la Cima de los Vientos."},
[2063]={"Libro 3, Capítulo 12: En un Valle del Norte","Candaith tiene palabras de advertencia y consejo para ti antes de que partas en el último tramo de tu viaje.","Candaith te sugirió que partieras hacia Rivendel sin demora.","Habla con Candaith y parte hacia Rivendel sin demora.","'Hay un valle oculto en el Bosque de los Trolls, muy al este y más allá del Último Puente, donde mora el más sabio de los Sabios. Su nombre es Elrond, y es el señor de Rivendel. Fue en su casa donde se crió mi capitán Aragorn, y si alguien sabrá qué debe hacerse frente a la creciente amenaza de Angmar, será él. Debes dirigirte a Rivendel.\
\
'Te diré lo que pueda sobre este último tramo de tu viaje, . Habla conmigo cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}.'","'Has tejido un relato notable, , y si deseas que termine aquí, nadie te juzgará por ello. Pero en tus palabras percibo algo más... de hecho, ¡dos cosas!\
\
'Percibo en ti un deseo de aventura, y sigue insatisfecho incluso después de tus pruebas en tierras salvajes. No podrías permanecer mucho tiempo en este refugio pacífico antes de que ese anhelo te impulse una vez más a buscar y enfrentar grandes peligros.\
\
'Y también percibo que deseas continuar tu labor en nombre de los Pueblos Libres de la Tierra Media. Nos adentramos en tiempos peligrosos, y enemigos poderosos buscan recuperar la cima de su poder, alturas que les fueron arrebatadas hace siglos por grandes héroes. ¿Serás tú ${PLAYERNAME:uno de esos héroes[m]|una de esas heroínas[f]} en esta era, ? Me lo pregunto.\
\
'Así que descansa, tanto tiempo como desees, y vuelve a mí cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para retomar tu aventura. La sombra que se alza en Angmar debe ser enfrentada y derrotada, y temo que los Jinetes Negros que inquietaron Cardolan y persiguieron a Frodo Bolsón hasta aquí no han sido vencidos para siempre. Uno de ellos no ha sido hallado.'","'Los orcos se han vuelto más audaces y feroces en los últimos días, pero cuando cruces el Último Puente hacia el Bosque de los Trolls te enfrentarás a un peligro mayor. Algo ha perturbado a las bestias salvajes hasta la locura, y si avanza por delante de ti, podría dejar un gran mal a su paso.\
\
'Que la suerte te acompañe mientras recorres el camino a través del Bosque de los Trolls y comienzas el ascenso hacia Rivendel. El sendero no será fácil, pero Elrond debe saber lo que te ocurrió en Cardolan y conocer la creciente amenaza de Angmar.'","Habla con Elrond en su biblioteca","Elrond se encuentra en la biblioteca de su hogar, en Imladris."},
[2064]={"Haradrim fleeing in the direction of the town of Erynos, east and north of Aragorn's camp, must be defeated before they can bring word of his victory at Pelargir.\
\
Aragorn has asked you to find tracks left by terrified Haradrim near the town of Erynos.","Aragorn is at the Camp of the Grey Host, to the north-west of Pelargir.\
\
You have tracked down and defeated the Haradrim warriors that fled from Pelargir.","'The threat of the Corsairs is over, but many of their allies still live and could endanger my next course, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Several of the Haradrim fled from the city when the Men of the Mountain fulfilled their oath, and I fear they might bring word of the Corsair defeat to the armies of Mordor. I would rather this did not happen, but I cannot spare the time to track all who fled from Pelargir. Will you do this for me, my friend?\
\
'Travel east in pursuit of these terrified Haradrim! I believe they will come to the walls of Erynos before they can break free of their fright. Defeat them and keep word of our victory at Pelargir from reaching unfriendly ears!'","The sorcerer breathes his last, but his mocking smile remains","Find and defeat terrified Haradrim near Erynos (2/3)","You hear a woman's voice hailing you from the town of Erynos, to the north","As you study the tracks, you feel eyes upon you. Someone hides nearby!","Talk to the Haradrim Sorcerer near Erynos","'I saw another one of these invaders nearby. I think he fancies himself a sorcerer of some sort, for he carried many unsavoury trinkets and muttered strange incantations under his breath.\
\
'He crept that way, around the outer wall of Erynos!'","The threat of the Corsairs is over, but Aragorn does not have any time to rest. He has another charge for you, one that must be completed with haste and with utmost secrecy.","'Travel east in pursuit of terrified Haradrim! I believe they will come to the walls of Erynos before they can break free of their fright. Defeat them and keep word of our victory at Pelargir from reaching unfriendly ears!'","Book 3, Chapter 1: A Need for Secrecy","Talk to Thurineth at the gate of Erynos","'Did you put an end to that sorcerer? I did not like the look of his trinkets or the sound of his mutterings!'","Defeated terrified Haradrim (${NUMBER}/3)","Find and defeat terrified Haradrim near Erynos (${CURRENT}/3)","'I watched you fight those evil warriors, hero, and I wanted to thank you for making safe our lands! But that is not all, for if you leave now you leave us still in peril!\
\
'I saw another one of these invaders nearby. I think he fancies himself a sorcerer of some sort, for he carried many unsavoury trinkets and muttered strange incantations under his breath.\
\
'He crept that way, around the outer wall of Erynos!'","Thurineth has some news for you at the gate of Erynos.\
\
You defeated several of the Haradrim that fled from Pelargir, and a woman has hailed you from the gate of Erynos.","Thurineth saw a Haradrim sorcerer creeping around the outer wall of the town of Erynos, and wanted you to defeat him before you leave.","You hear a rustling in the brush. Someone watches you from nearby!","'You may slay my men, hated ${RACE}, and you may end my own life, but you will have no lasting victory. The Great Master we follow is a giver of gifts, and he gives life unending to those who faithfully serve! You could slay all the Corsairs to a man, and all of my own people, but the commanders of the Master's army will always return, even in death!'","Talk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Grey Host","'You found the Haradrim that fled from Pelargir? Very good, ${PLAYER}! I hope this will keep word of our victory here a secret from the enemy. But something troubles you. Share it with me, and we will bear the burden of it together, my friend!'\
\
You tell Aragorn of the sorcerer's words: that the commanders of Sauron's armies cannot be stopped, even by death.\
\
'I confess to you that I have heard these whispers as well, my friend, so I cannot banish the fear of them from your mind. But it does not change my resolve, and I believe it will not change yours, either. We place a greater value on life than does our Enemy, so every loss pains us all the more. But that is our strength as well for we will fight even harder to protect it, even beyond our limits.'\
\
Aragorn smiles.\
\
'Ours is not the real quest, ${PLAYER}, for even if we have all the success we desire, the Enemy will remain. The real quest is elsewhere, my friend, and only its successful completion can end Sauron's evil forever.'"},
[2065]={"'No puedo culpar a mis enanos por su impaciencia por explorar Moria.'","'Hola, ${RACE}. ¿El señor Brogur te envió para ayudarme? Aprecio la oferta, pero no necesito tu ayuda. En las galerías de mis antepasados solo necesito confiar en la fuerza de mi propio brazo.'\
\
Útrygg ladea la cabeza y mira furiosamente a las sombras.\
\
'Puede que haya hablado demasiado rápido, ${RACE}. Hay alguien en las sombras. ¡Prepárate para la batalla!'","'¡El tiempo de los enanos está realmente cerca, ${PLAYER}! Qué ridículo fue temer que alguna maldición pudiera pesar sobre Moria después de todos estos años. Si hubiéramos regresado antes, ¡Moria podría estar prosperando ya!\
\
'Lo hecho, hecho está. Estamos aquí ahora, y muchos de los enanos de nuestra expedición se han aventurado en túneles profundos, buscando grandes riquezas que seguramente yacen intactas dentro de las cuevas de Moria.\
\
'Si te encuentras con Rokur o Útrygg durante sus exploraciones de Zelem-melek, asegúrate de prestarles cualquier ayuda que puedan necesitar. Partieron por el pasaje sur desde la Sala Vigesimoprimera, pero a dónde fueron desde allí no lo sé.'","Encuentra a Rokur y préstale tu ayuda","Brogur está seguro de que el momento se acerca para que los enanos recuperen Moria, y no es el único: muchos enanos están haciendo excursiones peligrosas en túneles profundos.","Libro 3, Capítulo 1: Un explorador demasiado entusiasta","Encuentra a Útrygg y préstale tu ayuda","'Seguramente muchas riquezas se esconden en los lugares oscuros de Moria.'","'¡Regresa con Brogur en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek, camarada! ¡Dile que estoy bien y que no hay motivo para preocuparse!'","'¡Regresa con Brogur en la Cámara de Liderazgo cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek, camarada! ¡Dile que estoy bien y que no hay motivo para alarmarse!'","Rokur y Útrygg están explorando Zelem-melek. Partieron por el pasaje sur que sale de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, pero desde allí nadie sabe a dónde fueron.\
\
Brogur te ha pedido que prestes cualquier ayuda a los enanos Rokur o Útrygg si te encuentras con ellos mientras exploras Zelem-melek.","'Rokur y Útrygg declararon su intención de explorar a fondo Zelem-melek, y se fueron por el pasaje sur que sale de la Sala Vigesimoprimera. Si te encuentras con uno de ellos en tus propias exploraciones, asegúrate de prestarle tu ayuda.'","'Hola, ${RACE}. He estado explorando las galerías perdidas de mis antepasados; ¡es una experiencia extraordinaria! La gran historia de este lugar me llena de respeto a cada paso.'\
\
Los ojos de Rókur se entrecierran y mira fijamente a las sombras.\
\
'¿Escuchaste eso? ¡Hay alguien ahí! ¡Prepárate para la batalla!'","Brogur se encuentra dentro de la Cámara de Liderazgo en de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Has defendido a un enano demasiado entusiasta de ser derrotado por un explorador uruk, y ahora deberías hacer tu informe a Brogur.","'Te debe la vida, ${PLAYER}. Siempre ha sido testarudo e impertinente, pero no puedo culparlo aquí. El deseo de reclamar las riquezas de Khazad-dûm ha cegado a muchos enanos a cuidar de su propia seguridad. Aún así, es afortunado de que hayas llegado cuando lo hiciste; los uruks son feroces y no deben ser subestimados.\
\
'Cuéntame más sobre este explorador uruk. Hay algo en tu historia que me hace reflexionar...'","Has defendido a Rokur del explorador uruk.","Has defendido a Útrygg del explorador uruk."},
[2066]={"Un furioso graznido señala la llegada de espías emplumados.","Meneldir te ha pedido que continúes hacia el norte por el Camino Verde en dirección a las Tierras de Bree.","¿Qué ha descubierto Meneldir?","El cuerpo de un Montaraz yace entre los matorrales.","Meneldir se detiene y mira alrededor, la preocupación marcando su ceño","Meneldir de pronto da un grito y corre hacia el noroeste","Meneldir se ha detenido en el Camino Verde.","Libro 3, Capítulo 1: Los Parientes de Meneldir","'¿Son estos espías emplumados o solo aves carroñeras?'","'Podemos permanecer en el Camino Verde un día más de viaje antes de llegar a las ruinas donde Narndir tiene su campamento. Nuestra advertencia de que Saruman ha traicionado a la buena gente de la Tierra Media debe llegar al caudillo de los Dúnedain, y Narndir sabrá dónde encontrarlo. No será un reencuentro agradable para mí....... pero debe hacerse.\
\
'El camino sale de Herne por el lado oriental, pero rodea la aldea por el norte, y por allí deberíamos ir.'","Meneldir te dijo que sentía ojos observando a los dos. ¿Espías?","'Nuestra advertencia de que Saruman ha traicionado a la buena gente de la Tierra Media debe llegar al caudillo de los Dúnedain, y Narndir sabrá dónde encontrarlo. No será un reencuentro agradable para mí....... pero debe hacerse.\
\
'El camino sale de Herne por el lado oriental, pero rodea la aldea por el norte, y por allí deberíamos ir.'","'¿Sientes eso? Siento ojos observándonos.'","'No....... ¡no! ¿Qué cruel burla es esta?'\
\
Meneldir mira con horror el cuerpo de un Montaraz tendido en la hierba.\
\
'Este es el hombre que buscamos, ${PLAYER}. Este es Narndir.'","Habla con Meneldir junto al cuerpo","'Ve qué puedes encontrar cerca. Quizá alguna pista identifique a este observador invisible.'","Un cuerpo yace aquí entre los matorrales","Averigua lo que Meneldir ha descubierto","Habla con Meneldir en el Camino Verde","Busca en los alrededores con Meneldir","Meneldir está listo para continuar su viaje para encontrar a los Dúnedain en las Tierras de Bree.","Revela espías ocultos cercanos y derrótalos (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Siento ojos sobre nosotros, ${PLAYER}. Alguien nos observa, y me recuerda lo que Egfrith escribió: que siguió a Boromir durante muchos días mientras viajaba por las tierras vacías.\
\
'No, no creo que haya regresado para atormentarnos; estaba decidida a llegar hasta Saruman con lo que descubrió sobre Boromir cuando nos dejó. Pero este podría ser otro espía.\
\
'Ve qué puedes encontrar cerca. Quizá alguna pista identifique a este observador invisible.'","Viaja al norte por el Camino Verde en dirección a las Tierras de Bree"},
[2067]={"'Mientras los ojos de Esteldín se han vuelto hacia el este, las noticias del oeste y del sur me dicen que el Enemigo avanza en muchos frentes. Temo que la fuerza de Esteldín está casi agotada, y solos no podemos enfrentar esta amenaza mayor.\
\
'Debe convocarse un consejo de los Pueblos Libres de las Quebradas del Norte. Pero antes de hacerlo, necesito más información sobre esta amenaza. Debo saber si Fornost, que fue la capital de Arnor en tiempos antiguos, ha caído bajo el dominio de Angmar una vez más. Si el Enemigo ha tomado y fortificado las ruinas de Fornost, estamos en grave peligro.\
\
'Ve a Mincham, un Montaraz que acampa en los Campos de Fornost al oeste, y pídele su ayuda.'","Libro 3, Capítulo 1: El Montaraz de los Campos","'Antes de convocar a los pueblos de las Quebradas del Norte para un consejo, necesitaré más información sobre los movimientos del Enemigo.\
\
'Ve al campamento de Mincham en los Campos de Fornost y pídele su ayuda.'","Según los informes que llegan del oeste y del sur de las Quebradas del Norte, Halbarad cree que el Enemigo avanza en muchos frentes. La fuerza de Esteldín está casi agotada y Halbarad piensa que debe convocarse un consejo de los Pueblos Libres. Antes de hacerlo, desea más información sobre los movimientos del Enemigo.","Mincham se encuentra en su campamento en el extremo sur de los Campos de Fornost.\
\
Halbarad te ha pedido que hables con Mincham para saber si el Enemigo ha retomado las ruinas de Fornost, la antigua capital de Arnor.","'¿El Enemigo ha retomado Fornost de antaño? Sí, por lo que he visto aquí, creo que es muy probable que así sea. Desde este solitario campamento, he visto a los espectros de los Perjurados agitarse y a espíritus caídos de Angmar tomar forma en los Campos.\
\
'También he visto orcos saliendo de las puertas de Fornost. Así que sí, el Enemigo ha tomado Fornost una vez más.\
\
'Lo que no se puede saber es la fuerza del Enemigo dentro de la ciudad en ruinas. Y para eso, necesitaré tu ayuda.'"},
[2068]={"'Nár spent an unusual amount of time at the book-shelves located south-east of here, the ones surrounding the illuminated statue.'","Book 3, Chapter 1: Secrets of Zudrugund","'You will find Frithgeir somewhere within the library here at Zudrugund. Speak to him about Nár; it may be he will reveal the source of his friend's strange knowledge of the paths Elrond bade us keep in mind.'","Nár is somewhere within Zudrugund.\
\
You have searched the book-shelves pointed out to you by Frithgeir, but have learned little that seems relevant to Nár's mysterious knowledge of the Grey Company's intentions.","'Many days I cannot unravel my friend's words. Alas that this is one of those days! Perhaps your Ranger friend, Corunir, will know what to do.'","(You found some torn pages, which seem to have undergone a great deal of use over the years. The words are very large, and every page has an illustration drawn in a fanciful style.)\
\
Kári was a little dwarf.\
Smaller than you or me.\
And wherever Kári went\
He took his axe... or three.\
\
One axe for his left hand.\
One axe for his right.\
One axe to carve the roast\
He ate most every night.\
\
Now one day the Orcs did call.\
They came right up to the gate.\
'Come on out!' they said,\
'We'll have a feast! Don't be late!'\
\
The dwarves knew what that meant.\
They knew it very well.\
If they went to see the Orcs\
They'd not hear the dinner bell.\
\
Do you know what Kári said?\
He said it loud and clear.\
'I will go to see the Orcs,\
And give them things to fear!'\
\
'But you're so little!' said the dwarves.\
They told him not to go.\
But Kári went; he would not stop\
'Till he faced the Orcs below.\
\
The Orcs laughed, 'What can you do?\
Just hold still, we'll get the skewers.'\
They turned their backs, and that was that!\
So we call him Kári Orc-hewer.","'You have spoken with the dwarf Nár again, to no avail? I see. Will he not tell us how he knows of the words of Elrond? Will he not tell us how he knows of the Paths of the Dead? It seems this mystery must remain unsolved for a time yet.'\
\
Candaith sighs, thinking.\
\
'Do you know the story of the Oath-breakers and the Paths of the Dead? Perhaps a recounting of that tale is in order, and you will be more familiar with the puzzle set before us.\
\
'Do you wish to hear it?'","Candaith is at a camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees east of the Dunlending village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin.\
\
Corunir has sent you to speak with Candaith to see if he has thought of a reason for Nár to have mentioned the Paths of the Dead.","(You found a parchment, yellowed and old, tucked away between the covers of a thin book and apparently forgotten.)\
\
Hail, Thráin, King under the Mountain!\
\
Preparations for leaving the Coomb are well underway, and it will not be long before our people are ready to depart for the Blue Mountains. The great wheels in the depths will turn without them; I wonder for how long?\
\
I am writing this letter to express my concern about Nár. You know as well as anyone the things he has seen, and his service to your father cannot be questioned. He deserves much better than he has gotten. He seems not even to see me, these days, though I must endure the retelling of my own exploits two, four, or a dozen years in the past. It makes me sad to think of it now, and his excitement in each recounting, the previous one forgotten, saddens me all the more.\
\
This is why I must ask your permission to remain, when the others go. Nár will not go to the Blue Mountains, and I wish to stay here to look out for him. My son, too, wishes to stay; he is young, and knows nothing of our real home; this to him is no exile, but the Blue Mountains would be. I do not want to deprive Frithgeir of the only home he has known.\
\
I will do whatever you command, of course. But this is my desire, if it be your wish to grant it.\
\
Hervin Drake-slayer","'Nothing you found among the book-shelves strikes me as being relevant to Nár's knowledge of our possible road, ${PLAYER}. Ask the dwarf and see if he can illuminate any of this for us.'","'Ah, Fannar, it has been too long! Trade at Zigil-jabâl continues fine, I trust? Good, good, good.'","Frithgeir has pointed out book-shelves in Zudrugund where Nár has spent time recently, at the shelves south-east of Frithgeir, surrounding an illuminated statue.\
\
You should investigate book-shelves where Nár has shown recent interest, hoping it will prove instructive.","'Did you find anything interesting? You can ask Nár about any of the things you saw, but he may not be able to tell you anything more than you already know.'","'I do not like this, ${PLAYER}. How has Nár come to know of our potential road? That Elrond advised his sons to remember the Paths of the Dead, for we may have need to walk them, was known to but a few, and all of them trustworthy.\
\
'Something is not right about this. It will not be long before we must set out again, but in the time before we do we must learn what we can about Nár's recent activities. There may be some clue in them to reveal the source of his knowledge concerning our errand.\
\
'Speak to Frithgeir about Nár. He proved helpful in returning his friend to clarity, short-lived though it was, and may help us again.'","'Nár's words remain as cloudy as ever. It was worth trying, ${PLAYER}, though it has not borne fruit.\
\
'You should go to Candaith at the camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees east of the Uch-luth village of Lhanuch, and tell him that we are no closer to learning why Nár spoke of the Paths of the Dead. Candaith is a master of lore and may have thought of something.'","Nár nods in your direction, and a wide smile creases his old face.\
\
'You have brought the gem-stones? Good, good! These will do very nicely!'\
\
He seems not to realize that you have brought no gem-stones. This is going about as well as you expected.","Corunir is in Zudrugund, the dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb.\
\
You have spoken to Nár about what you found in the book-shelves you were pointed to by Frithgeir, but have learned little of use. You should report of your efforts to Corunir.","A serious complication has arisen in regard to the quest of the Grey Company: how does the dwarf Nár have knowledge of its potential road?","(A slim book, 'Herbs and Plant-life of the Coomb,' is resting atop several others, as if it had been recently removed and carelessly returned to a shelf.)\
\
It is my hope that these musings on the great variety of plant-life found within the Coomb will be of help to those who, by want or need, find themselves uncertain of a herb's utility or a vegetable's properties. It is clear that such knowledge is fading in my people; Thrór has commanded the opening of a new wing in the mines beneath Zudrugund, but my own studies have been, of a necessity, self-directed. I do not complain! The gems they have taken from the old wing stir my heart as much as they do any of my fellows; but there is as much to be learned from the green as there is from the stone.\
\
But I ramble, as I often do when called upon to defend my interest!\
\
(This is followed by several pages of notes on various plants that grow on the slopes of Thrór's Coomb. One of the pages has been turned sideways and ear-marked, and catches your eye.)\
\
This next herb is easily found throughout the Coomb; simply follow your nose, and on a day of calm weather, its sweet smell will guide you most easily to patches of Hulwul-harâz growing on the grassy slopes. The name, in fact, means 'Sweet Warder,' and the Dunlendings with whom I have spoken believe the smell to drive away evil beings.\
\
When the herb is crushed and added to water containing the petals of the Nijam-mujdu and the fruit of the Kibil-luwz, steeping the solution for an hour produces a strange-smelling brew that I have noted for its ability to provide clarity of thought and heightened reasoning. It does seem that its effectiveness dulls with repeated use, and the brew should therefore not be over-used.","'Yes? I am sorry he upset you. Nár means no harm.'\
\
Frithgeir listens as you recount Corunir's request to know of Nár's recent activities. His brow creases in thought, and he is silent for a moment. When he speaks again, his words come slowly, as if he is unsure they will be of help.\
\
'A few days before Wadu the Dunlending came to Zudrugund, I noticed Nár spending a great deal of time looking through some of the book-shelves for something. I thought it odd, because he generally takes little interest in the books and records here, but he did not speak of it and I did not ask what drove his examination.\
\
'I can tell you which section of shelves it was, but there are a lot of books to go through. I do not know if that will be of any assistance, but you are welcome to seek a common thread if it may be of help to you and your friends. Look at the shelves to the south-east of here, around the illuminated statue.'","Searched book-shelves in Zudrugund (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Search book-shelves in Zudrugund (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Candaith may have thought of something. I hope so, for I am out of ideas! Look for him at a camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees east of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin.'","Frithgeir is in the library at Zudrugund.\
\
Corunir has asked you to speak with Frithgeir about Nár, in hopes that he can reveal the source of his friend's unexpected knowledge of the Grey Company's possible road."},
[2069]={"Talk to Angbor at the Camp of the Grey Host","Aragorn is at the Camp of the Grey Host, waiting for your report on the preparations of the Corsair ships.","'I asked that you help prepare the ships with haste, but I did not expect such speed even from you, ${PLAYER}! I thank you for your efforts and know that we are put in the best position we could be as a result.\
\
'I have given some thought to this next request, my friend, and I hope you agree with me on this. I do not ask you to accompany me on the ships. Instead, I ask you to travel by land through Upper Lebennin and Lossarnach. We must learn the state of the war to the east. The vale of Tumladen and the town of Imloth Melui had strong walls of old, and were used as places of safety for the people in times of war. The people there will tell you much of what has transpired elsewhere in Gondor. Angbor will go that way as well, with his men, and will be a boon companion as you go.\
\
'I have another purpose for you, my trusted friend. I want you to find Gandalf or true-hearted Faramir in Minas Tirith and tell them about our victory here. Tell no others! In Faramir I place the trust I would not give to the father. There is too much I do not know about the situation in the White City.'","'We do not have much time to prepare, but there are a number of tasks I have given my friends to perform that will help us set forth as quickly as possible. Help them with these tasks, if you would, for every moment we hesitate is a moment the Enemy would relish!'","'We still have our own parts to play, and I deem it important that we play them well! I wish to sail up the river on the deck of the Corsair ships, and come by that route to the aid of Minas Tirith. It is my hope that we will arrive in time and with such surprise that we can strike a blow to the fighting will of those who threaten the city.\
\
'We do not have much time to prepare, but there are a number of tasks I have given my friends to perform that will help us set forth as quickly as possible. Help them with these tasks, if you would, for every moment we hesitate is a moment the Enemy would relish!'","Aragorn has a plan: he wishes to sail up the river on the deck of the Corsair ships, coming to the aid of Minas Tirith to the surprise of its enemies.","'Black Sails' quest completed (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Aragorn smiles in farewell","Book 3, Chapter 2: Grey Host, Black Sails","Talk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Grey Host","Complete 'Black Sails' quests for the Grey Company (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'I have heard a great deal about you, ${PLAYER}, and I welcome you as a travelling companion into the lands to the east. If you are half as brave and skilled as Aragorn tells me, we shall have no trouble at all!'","Angbor the Fearless is at the Camp of the Grey Host, waiting to speak with you.\
\
Aragorn is ready to depart for Minas Tirith on the Corsair ships, and has asked you to travel overland with Angbor and his men to learn the state of the war.","Aragorn has asked you to help the members of the Grey Company prepare to depart on the Corsair ships bound for Minas Tirith.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Rangers at the Camp of the Grey Host have begun to perform Aragorn's tasks. Help them with their 'Black Sails' quests to fulfill his wishes.</rgb>"},
[2070]={"'¡No lo entiendo! Todavía estamos a varios días de viaje del campamento donde Narndir vivía, estudiando las ruinas de Cardolan. Siempre estaba escribiendo en ese diario suyo, documentando detalles de artefactos y arquitectura que consideraba dignos de mención. Solíamos recoger pigmentos juntos, él y yo, cuando éramos niños en el Ángulo, pues incluso entonces gastaba tanta tinta que siempre se quedaba sin ella. Narndir...'\
\
Meneldir aprieta las manos en puños.\
\
'¿Puedo pedirte que examines su cuerpo, ${PLAYER}? Yo no puedo hacerlo, pero debemos saber la causa de su muerte.'","El cuerpo de un Montaraz muerto ha revelado que algo terrible ha sucedido a los Dúnedain en Cardolan.","'¿Puedo pedirte que examines su cuerpo, ${PLAYER}? Yo no puedo hacerlo, pero debemos saber la causa de su muerte.'","El cuerpo de Narndir yace junto al camino en Cardolan. ¿Qué le ocurrió a este amigo de Meneldir?","Habla con Meneldir junto al cuerpo","¿Qué ocurrió en el paso del río en el Vado de Sarn para resultar en la muerte de Narndir, tan lejos de su lugar habitual?","El Montaraz Halbarad grita órdenes a los suyos en el Vado de Sarn.","Examina el cuerpo de Narndir","Es evidente que Narndir lleva muerto varios días. Sufrió varios cortes de espada en la espalda, y por las marcas en la tierra a su alrededor parece que fue arrollado por alguien a caballo mientras huía.","Meneldir está junto al cuerpo de su amigo caído, lleno de dolor, ira y confusión.","Viaja al Vado de Sarn y averigua qué ocurrió allí","'No te he visto antes, , pero si eres ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} de los Montaraces del Norte, eres ${PLAYERNAME:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} aquí, aunque estamos muy presionados.\
\
'Pero sí conozco a tu compañero, y me sorprende que haya regresado para mostrar su rostro en estas tierras.'","Hay señales de una batalla reciente en el Vado de Sarn","'No lo entiendo. Narndir no debería haber estado aquí en absoluto, ${PLAYER}. ¿Qué lo trajo tan lejos de su lugar habitual, y quién querría hacerle daño? Además, él no era un cobarde... ¿ante qué enemigo daría la espalda?'\
\
Casi sin pausa, Meneldir responde su propia pregunta.\
\
'Sí, ${PLAYER}, ya conocemos la respuesta: las sombras que Aberthol vio aquella noche en Herne, una de las cuales montaba un gran corcel negro. Ya nombré a esas criaturas una vez, y lo haré de nuevo: Nazgûl. Tal enemigo inspiraría temor incluso en los más firmes de los Dúnedain, y semejante criatura podría arrollar a un hombre que huye y matarlo de un tajo por la espalda. No sería nada para un ser así.\
\
'El Vado de Sarn está al oeste de aquí, y parece que ese podría ser el lugar del que Narndir huyó. A veces ha habido algunos Montaraces en el vado, aunque nunca en gran número. Creo que deberíamos desviar nuestro camino hacia el Vado de Sarn y descubrir qué pudo haber sucedido a sus defensores.'","Habla con Halbarad en el Vado de Sarn","Meneldir murmura unas palabras junto al cuerpo de su amigo, y tú tienes la cortesía de no escucharlas.","Libro 3, Capítulo 2: El Cuerpo entre los Matorrales"},
[2071]={"Mincham se encuentra en su campamento en el sur de los Campos de Fornost.\
\
El Montaraz Mincham necesitará escuchar tu informe sobre las defensas en las puertas de Fornost.","Mincham cree que el Enemigo ha regresado a Fornost, pero no puede determinar la fuerza de las tropas allí, ya que se acercaron a la ciudad desde el norte.","Mata a los Orcos Ongbúrz en las Puertas de Norburgo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Huargos derrotados en las Puertas de Norburgo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Libro 3, Capítulo 2: Las puertas de Fornost","'Temo que la única manera en que aprenderemos la fuerza de las tropas de Angmar dentro de Fornost es probando sus defensas en las Puertas de Norburgo.\
\
'Viaja al norte hasta las puertas y derrota a los orcos y huargos que encuentres allí. Una vez que hayas hecho esto, regresa a mí y informa lo que has encontrado.'","'De verdad tienes un corazón valiente para enfrentar a esas bestias. Tienes mi gratitud, ${PLAYER}. Ojalá hubiera podido hacerlo yo mismo, en vez de enviarte en mi lugar, pero el tiempo y mi herida me impiden empuñar una espada, y mucho menos tensar un arco.\
\
'Por lo que me cuentas, Angmar no envió simplemente una fuerza simbólica a Fornost. No, parece que enviaron un ejército. ¡Fornost ha caído una vez más ante Angmar!'","Mata a los Huargos en las Puertas de Norburgo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Fornost está perdido, y tal vez todo Eriador también....'","'Ahora que el Enemigo ha tomado Fornost una vez más, todo puede estar perdido....'","Orcos Ongbúrz derrotados en las Puertas de Norburgo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'No puedo decirte la fuerza de las tropas de Angmar dentro de Fornost, porque no los vi acercarse. ¡Los orcos y huargos que guardan las puertas deben haber entrado en Fornost desde el norte!\
\
'Temo que la única manera de conocer la verdadera fuerza del Enemigo en Fornost es probar las defensas que los orcos han levantado en sus puertas. Yo lo haría personalmente, pero mi vieja herida me lo impide.\
\
'Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]}, ve a las Puertas de Norburgo al norte de aquí y elimina los orcos y huargos que encuentres. Cuando lo hayas hecho, tráeme un informe de lo que halles.''","Las Puertas de Norburgo se encuentran al norte del campamento de Mincham.\
\
Mincham cree que la única manera de determinar la fuerza de las tropas de Angmar en Fornost es probar las defensas levantadas en sus puertas. Te ha pedido que elimines orcos y huargos y le traigas un informe sobre la resistencia allí."},
[2072]={"Libro 3, Capítulo 3: Caída una vez más","Halbarad se encuentra en Esteldín.\
\
Mincham te ruega que lleves la noticia de la presencia de Angmar en Fornost a Halbarad.","'No te demores aquí, ve a Esteldín y dile a Halbarad lo que hemos aprendido. Un ejército de Angmar se encuentra al norte de las puertas de Fornost. ¡La antigua ciudad ha caído ante el Enemigo una vez más!'","Después de informarle sobre tus batallas contra los orcos y huargos que guardan las puertas de Fornost, Mincham dedujo que era como Halbarad temía: Angmar ha enviado una gran fuerza para reclamar y fortificar Fornost.","'Supongo que podemos estar agradecidos de que ya no somos tan ignorantes de los planes del Enemigo como antes. Sin embargo, la pregunta de cómo enfrentaremos esta amenaza nos preocupa a todos.\
\
'Los pueblos de las Quebradas del Norte deben ser convocados para un consejo y enfrentar esta amenaza. Hay mucho por hacer, y te pediré mucho en los días venideros, si tienes el espíritu dispuesto.'","'¡Rápido, debes regresar con Halbarad en Esteldín y contarle lo que has aprendido aquí: Angmar ha tomado Fornost una vez más!\
\
'Desde un lugar tan fortificado, Angmar podría dominar todo el Norte. Pero hay cosas aún peores de las que preocuparse. Se cuentan historias de un gran mal que habita en los pasillos colapsados y en ruinas de Fornost. ¡Este mal podría ser llamado para servir a Angmar!\
\
'Ve a Esteldín y dile a Halbarad todo lo que has aprendido aquí.'"},
[2073]={"'As we left Minas Tirith, I saw smoke rising from Osgiliath. I hope Faramir holds it still, but I do not know how long even he can last. He is the son of the Steward and very brave, but I have heard that the armies arrayed against us are vast and uncaring. I have heard also that Boromir left on an errand to the north, and has not yet returned. I would feel better for my sons if Boromir returned and stood on the front lines... may it be soon!\
\
'Right now we await word that it is safe to return to the city. Tumladen has enough supplies for its garrison, now absent, so we should be able to stay as long as necessary. But I hope this is resolved quickly.'","'They say the son of the Steward holds Osgiliath, but how long can he hope to stand against all the armies that pour out of the East? That city has changed hands before, but it seems to this old man that the next time it falls may be the last.\
\
'When that happens, I think they will rue sending us away. The White City will have need of folk to wield swords, no matter their ages. Mark my words, and mark them well!'","Find the Crossings of Erui, east of Tumladen","'I have four thousand men with me, and they will travel behind us. It will be slow going for them, so we will ride ahead and see what awaits them. Let us fight the Southrons in Upper Lebennin and clear the way for their swords! Then we will come to Tumladen and see the state of the war.'","'You have done good work here. I suspected that we would find these havens full of refugees from the White City, which means that the war will soon be joined if it has not already begun.\
\
'Four thousand swords travel slowly, but when they arrive they will make all their points, with sharp arguments! We must make sure their path is free of obstruction. There is a good place to cross the River Erui, to the south, but it is held by the Haradrim. Let us go to the Crossings and defeat these Southrons so my army can pass.\
\
'Any Haradrim in Upper Lebennin pose a threat to the Crossings, and they must be stopped!'","Defeated Haradrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Haradrim in Upper Lebennin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Angbor outside the entrance to the vale of Tumladen","'Very good, my friend. You have disrupted the preparations of the Haradrim, and my men will be able to cross the Erui without fear of Southron fortifications. Even a force of four thousand can suffer many losses when attacking a much smaller force, provided the smaller force has time to prepare.'","'Before he departed for Minas Tirith, Prince Imrahil charged me with the defence of the fiefs he left behind. I accepted this duty, knowing it might end in death, and left my son to protect my own lands. I engaged the Corsairs and Southrons at the city of Linhir, but we were heavily outnumbered and our defeat seemed certain.\
\
'And then a new force joined the fray: a vast army of shadows from the forbidden paths under the mountains! They were Dead Men, and they brought death with them, silent and sure. My men cast aside their weapons and fled, but I stood my ground, and when I saw the banner of he who led them I was glad, for it was Aragorn, and he rode 'neath the standard of the King. 'Fearless' he called me, but what man can be afraid when a King has returned to a kingdom that needs him?\
\
'I have four thousand men with me, and they will travel behind us. It will be slow going for them, so we will ride ahead and see what awaits them. Let us fight the Southrons in Upper Lebennin and clear the way for their swords! Then we will come to the vale of Tumladen and see the state of the war.'","Tumladen has become home to many displaced refugees","The road into Upper Lebennin passes through the port-city of Pelargir.\
\
Angbor has asked you to travel east into Upper Lebennin and to defeat many of the Haradrim there.","'Do you plan to travel to Minas Tirith? I would advise you to rethink your course! If the city is not already besieged, it soon will be! Much of my family has been evacuated, but my sons remained behind at the request of their commander. They will defend the city, and are glad for the chance, but I am afraid for them.\
\
'As we left Minas Tirith, I saw smoke rising from Osgiliath. I hope Faramir holds it still, but I do not know how long even he can last. He is the son of the Steward and very brave, but I have heard that the armies arrayed against us are vast and uncaring. I have heard also that Boromir left on an errand to the north, and has not yet returned. I would feel better for my sons if Boromir returned and stood on the front lines... may it be soon!\
\
'Right now we await word that it is safe to return to the city. Tumladen has enough supplies for its garrison, now absent, so we should be able to stay as long as necessary. But I hope this is resolved quickly.'","Talk to White City refugees in Tumladen (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'They say I am too old to fight, even if the desire to protect my home and my family burns as brightly within my bosom as it does within those of younger men. I am not afraid to die, if that death were to be in service of Steward Denethor or his brave sons!\
\
'Still I have been carted here to wait for the end with the children and the women. What justice is there in that? They say the son of the Steward holds Osgiliath, but how long can he hope to stand against all the armies that pour out of the East? That city has changed hands before, but it seems to this old man that the next time it falls may be the last.\
\
'When that happens, I think they will rue sending us away. The White City will have need of folk to wield swords, no matter their ages. Mark my words, and mark them well!'","'I heard there was a Halfling in the White City! I did not see him, but he could not have been much taller than I am, and I wager he will be allowed to fight! Why not me? I heard tell he was a friend of Mithrandir, the Grey Pilgrim. Perhaps that is the reason.\
\
'Some folk have all the good fortune, and leave none for the rest of us! It is not fair!'","'Find the vale of Tumladen in Upper Lebennin, and see how the war has treated the rest of the kingdom. I will follow behind with four thousand swords and strong men to wield them!'","'Four thousand swords travel slowly, but when they arrive they will make all their points, with sharp arguments! We must make sure their path is free of obstruction. There is a good place to cross the River Erui, to the east, but it is held by the Haradrim. Let us go to the Crossings and defeat these Southrons so my army can pass.'","Defeat Haradrim in Upper Lebennin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find the entrance to the vale of Tumladen, in Upper Lebennin","Haradrim threaten to overrun the Crossings of Erui","Aragorn has given you an important mission: to travel by land the route he takes by ship, and come in that way to Minas Tirith to find Gandalf or Faramir.","'Hullo there! You look like a real adventurer! Are you really a hero?'\
\
The boy looks at you with wide eyes and an admiring expression.\
\
'You must be journeying to Minas Tirith! They are going to need you there, I am certain of it! There is going to be a war... it may have already started! Are you going to be in the thick of the fighting? I would be, if they'd let me!\
\
'I heard there was a Halfling in the White City! I did not see him, but he could not have been much taller than I am, and I wager he will be allowed to fight! Why not me? I heard tell he was a friend of Mithrandir, the Grey Pilgrim. Perhaps that is the reason.\
\
'Some folk have all the good fortune, and leave none for the rest of us! It is not fair!'","Many refugees from elsewhere in Gondor can be found throughout the vale of Tumladen.","Angbor has come to the entrance to the vale of Tumladen.\
\
You have learned that folk have been evacuated from Minas Tirith, and the war is about to be joined. You should find Angbor and tell him what you have learned.","Angbor wants you to travel east of Tumladen to the Crossings of Erui, and to defeat the Haradrim camped there.","Defeat Haradrim that threaten the Crossings of Erui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Haradrim hold the Crossings. They must be defeated.'","Talk to Angbor on the small hill west of the Crossings of Erui","The vale of Tumladen is in the northern reaches of Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have defeated many Haradrim in Upper Lebennin and should now find the vale of Tumladen.","Angbor keeps watch on a hill just to the west of the Crossings of Erui.","Book 3, Chapter 3: Fearless"},
[2074]={"La corazonada de Meneldir era correcta. Ahora estará insufrible","Tú y Nethúr habéis salido victoriosos sobre los lobos","Habla con Nethúr al sureste del Vado de Sarn","'Parece que sé de lo que hablo, ¿no es así?'","'Lo sospechaba. Estas criaturas tienen talento para enloquecer a los seres cercanos y dejar tras de sí el caos. Quizá eliminar este amuleto reduzca el asedio de los Muertos sobre los defensores.'","Lleva los alijos de Montaraces que pidió Halbarad al Vado de Sarn","'Gracias por traer estos alijos de suministros. Si es cierto que Saruman y los demás Magos se han vuelto contra nosotros...'\
\
Halbarad sacude la cabeza.\
\
'No es que no desconfíe de tu palabra, , pero Meneldir quebró su juramento y eso es motivo de gran vergüenza para nosotros. No solo para él, sino para todos. ¿No es acaso un fallo de todo un poblado cuando uno de los suyos falta a su deber?\
\
'Pero tal es nuestra necesidad que no puedo rechazar ni siquiera a Meneldir, ¡como era mi primera intención! Los Montaraces están dispersos y en desorden, y necesito a cada hombre. ${PLAYER:Así es, y a cada mujer también[f]|Eso te incluye también}.'","'He dado a Halbarad nuestra advertencia, y aunque no desea creerla, dice haber visto criaturas que portaban la Mano Blanca en días recientes. Pensó que eran dirigidas por uno de los suyos, pero nuestras noticias le han hecho dudar.\
\
'He estado pensando en algo más, ${PLAYER}. ¿Recuerdas el amuleto que encontramos enterrado en Herne? ¿Y si los jinetes dejaron un dispositivo similar aquí también? Creo que deberíamos buscar uno.'","Libro 3, Capítulo 3: Halbarad de los Dúnedain","'${PLAYER}, te pido que ayudes a los defensores del Vado de Sarn y que recojas los alijos de Montaraces; fueron guardados para proporcionar sustento y provisiones si era necesario, ¡y tras el ataque lo es!'","'¿Recuerdas el amuleto que encontramos enterrado en Herne? ¿Y si los jinetes dejaron uno similar aquí? Creo que deberíamos buscar uno.'","La corazonada de Meneldir resultó cierta: los jinetes negros dejaron un amuleto atrás, y probablemente atrajo a los tumularios al Vado de Sarn en los días posteriores al ataque.","Has reunido alijos de Montaraces (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tus dedos cierran sobre algo en la tierra: un amuleto en forma de calavera hecho de hueso","Rebuscas en el montón de tierra pero solo encuentras lombrices","Habla con Meneldir en el Vado de Sarn","Meneldir está en el Vado de Sarn, donde ayuda a sus parientes a recuperarse del ataque reciente.","Lleva el amuleto en forma de calavera a Meneldir en el Vado de Sarn","Halbarad de los Dúnedain organiza la recuperación de los Montaraces encargados de defender el Vado de Sarn tras el ataque ocurrido hace algunos días.","Los Montaraces encargados de la defensa del Vado de Sarn pueden utilizar tu ayuda. Halbarad también pidió que recuperes algunos alijos de suministros cercanos, con los cuales los Dúnedain podrán reabastecer el Vado de Sarn.","La tierra ha sido removida en varios lugares cerca del Vado de Sarn, y Meneldir cree que deberías examinar algunos de esos montículos de tierra. Tiene la sospecha de que los jinetes negros dejaron algo atrás, como hicieron en Herne.","Tú y Galasebdir habéis triunfado sobre los tumularios","Busca la tierra removida alrededor del Vado de Sarn para confirmar la sospecha de Meneldir","'¿Dices que tienes una advertencia para mí, Meneldir? Dila entonces, y márchate. Aún nos recuperamos del ataque contra el vado que nos dejó dispersos y en desorden, y no puedo dedicar demasiado tiempo a quienes rompen sus juramentos.\
\
'Pero podría tener uso para tu acompañante. ${PLAYER}, te pido que ayudes a los defensores del Vado de Sarn y que recojas los alijos de Montaraces cercanos; fueron guardados para proporcionar alimento y suministros si era necesario, ¡y tras el ataque sin duda lo es!'","'Desde que esos terribles jinetes atacaron el Vado de Sarn, hemos oído los aullidos de lobos desde Páramo Rojizo. Algo los ha agitado hasta la locura, y prueban nuestras defensas sin descanso en los alrededores, como nunca antes.'","Recoge alijos de Montaraces no lejos del Vado de Sarn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Desde que los terribles espectros atacaron el vado, hemos soportado el embate de los Muertos. Se alzan y atacan, y aunque los derrotemos, siempre regresan.'","Halbarad supervisa la recuperación de los Dúnedain tras el ataque de los jinetes negros en el Vado de Sarn.\
\
Has recuperado varios alijos de Montaraces y debes llevarlos a Halbarad.","Habla con Galasebdir al noreste del Vado de Sarn"},
[2075]={"Tanto Dori como Hannar deberían estar en Othrikar, que se encuentra al norte de Esteldín.\
\
Halbarad te dijo que los Enanos de Othrikar son buenos barbiluengos que fueron sometidos por los Duramano durante muchos años, aunque recientemente se han liberado de ese yugo. Aunque todavía son presionados por los Duramano, Halbarad te ha pedido que les lleves la noticia del Consejo de Esteldín.","Para enfrentar la amenaza de Angmar, Halbarad ha decidido que debe convocar un consejo de los Pueblos Libres de las Quebradas del Norte: el Consejo de Esteldín.","Libro 3, Capítulo 4, Parte I de III: Un llamado a los Enanos","'¿Buscas a Dori? ¡Por desgracia, Dori ha sido capturado por los Duramano! Un emisario de esos traidores acaba de irse y dijo que si no les entregábamos las minas, Dori sería asesinado.'","'Necesitaremos la fuerza de los enanos para enfrentar la amenaza de Angmar. Viaja a Othrikar y habla con Dori. Si no lo encuentras, habla con un enano llamado Hannar.'","Habla con Dori o Hannar","'Necesitaremos la fuerza de los Enanos de Othrikar si queremos enfrentar la amenaza de Angmar. Los enanos allí son buenos barbiluengos, pero durante mucho tiempo han sido sometidos por los Duramano. Cuando los Duramano mostraron su verdadera lealtad, los barbiluengos los expulsaron de Othrikar.\
\
Aun así, siguen siendo acosados por los Duramano, y solo recientemente uno del Pueblo de Durin de Erebor, Dori, ha venido a ayudarlos. No será fácil convencerlos de que presten su fuerza al Consejo, pero debes intentarlo.\
\
Viaja a Othrikar y habla con Dori. Si por alguna razón no puedes encontrar a Dori, habla con un enano llamado Hannar. Él es quien lidera a los barbiluengos de Othrikar.'"},
[2076]={"Libro 3, Capítulo 4, Parte II de III: Liberando a Dori","'¡No haremos nada hasta que Dori sea liberado!'","Hannar se encuentra en las minas de Othrikar.\
\
Después de escoltar a Dori a un lugar seguro, te dijo que regresaras a Othrikar y hablaras con Hannar.","'¿Un consejo de los Pueblos Libres? ¿Cómo podríamos pensar en un consejo con Dori ausente? Fue solo con la llegada de Dori, y el alijo de gemas que trajo, que la esperanza comenzó a volver a nuestros corazones. Pero Dori ha sido capturado, las gemas perdidas, y la esperanza robada.\
\
'Si esos Hombres, esos Montaraces, desean tener la ayuda de los Enanos de Othrikar, ¡entonces Dori debe ser liberado! Tú -- si eres ${PLAYERNAME:el enviado[m]|la enviada[f]} de los Montaraces -- debes hacer esto si deseas nuestra presencia en este consejo.\
\
'Dori está probablemente siendo retenido en el campamento de los Duramano al oeste de Othrikar. ¡Libera a Dori y escoltalo a un lugar seguro! Una vez que esté libre, tomaremos nuestra decisión con respecto a este consejo tuyo.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Se sugiere que completes esta misión mientras estás en una comunidad. La inspiración te ayudará si eliges emprender este desafío solo o con un grupo más pequeño.</rgb>","'¡Has hecho algo grandioso por los enanos de Othrikar hoy! Dori llegó poco antes que tú y está descansando dentro, pero nos habló de tu valiente rescate. ¡Estamos a tu servicio!'","'¡Ya era hora! Esos Duramano se llevaron el alijo de gemas que traje, tenemos que recuperarlas. ¡Othrikar depende de ellas!\
\
¡Vamos, antes de que los Duramano sospechen!'","Has escoltado a Dori a un lugar seguro","El campamento Duramano donde Dori está retenido se encuentra al oeste de Othrikar. Busca en las ruinas donde Dori está cautivo.\
\
Hannar te dijo que los enanos ni siquiera considerarían ir al Consejo de Esteldín, a menos que Dori fuera liberado de los Duramano. Como enviado de los Montaraces, te dijo que debes liberarlo si esperas contar con el apoyo de los enanos en el Consejo.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides realizarla solo recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Encuentra a Dori","Cuando llegaste a Othrikar, trayendo noticias del Consejo de Esteldín, Hannar te dijo que Dori, el emisario de los barbiluengos de Erebor, había sido capturado por los Duramano."},
[2077]={"Halbarad se encuentra en Esteldín.\
\
Hannar te pidió que informaras a Halbarad que los Enanos de Othrikar han aceptado venir al Consejo.","'¡Mi mano ansía tomar mi hacha y partir a los orcos en dos!'","Libro 3, Capítulo 4, Parte III de III: Los Enanos Vendrán","'¡Malditos Duramano, aliados con Angmar. Dan mala fama a todos los enanos!'","'¡La esperanza renace una vez más en los corazones de los Enanos de Othrikar!'","'¡Primero los Angmarim, luego los Duramano!'","'Espero que todo esté bien en Othrikar. ¡Los enanos allí han sufrido mucho!'","'Antes de retirarse, le conté a Dori tu mensaje sobre el Consejo de Esteldín. Él recomendó que fuéramos, ¡y estoy de acuerdo!\
\
¡Los enanos prestarán su fuerza a este Consejo y liberarán todas las Quebradas del Norte de las garras del Enemigo! ¡Ve ahora y dile a los Montaraces que iremos!'","'¡Son buenas noticias! Con la ayuda de los enanos, nuestras posibilidades de cambiar el rumbo contra Angmar son mucho mayores.\
\
¡Has hecho un gran trabajo hoy, ${PLAYER}, de verdad!'","'Ve ahora, ${PLAYER}, y lleva la noticia a esos Montaraces de que los Enanos de Othrikar acudirán a su Consejo. ¡Las batallas venideras serán gloriosas!'","'¡Gracias por ese magnífico rescate, ${PLAYER}!'","Tras rescatar a Dori de las garras de los Duramano, tanto Dori como Hannar acordaron que los Enanos de Othrikar acudirán al Consejo de Esteldín."},
[2078]={"'Lossarnach is a land of beauty, but we must not slow our steps to admire its sweet-smelling flowers! There will be time enough for that when this war is won! We must go to Minas Tirith. The fields of the Pelennor outside the White City are encircled by a great wall, the Rammas Echor, through which we must pass.\
\
'The south-gate in the Rammas is located in the haven of the Harlond. That is where we must go. First we will do as Aragorn requested, and see how fares the settlement of Imloth Melui, to the north along the road. There is a meeting of roads just south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach. Let us go there and assess the situation.'","The Rammas Echor, which blocks the way to the Pelennor, is besieged by the enemy","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> within the Harlond, near the docks","'Hello there, ${PLAYER}! What good timing! I was just telling these ladies about some of our adventures. Do you remember when we fought off those Corsair raiders together? That was really something, was it not?'\
\
Nethadan already looks happier than you have ever seen him, and his mood only improves when you tell him that the road through the Harlond is closed.\
\
'How unfortunate! How ill-fated! Even so, I think this will be a fine place to stay until the road is clear. This is the perfect place to bring our waggon of valuable healing liquors. Did you know that this town has produced some of the finest healers in all the kingdom?\
\
'Now where was I? Oh yes! I have always sought to provide for my family and my dear old dad. He will never want for nails, for example....'","The docks of the Harlond have been seized by the enemy","You are near the entrance of the Harlond, gateway to the Pelennor","'We are bound for Minas Tirith and its Houses of Healing with a supply of Cemenduril liquor from Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, but I do not know if we will have safe passage. We encountered a traveller on the road who says the Harlond is full of Orcs! Can you investigate if this is so?'","Angbor has asked you to travel to the meeting of the roads just south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach, to learn the state of the war in that land.","Nethadan is somewhere within Imloth Melui, looking for a purchaser for the Cemenduril liquor.","Angbor is ready to cross into Lossarnach, continuing the journey toward Minas Tirith and the onset of war with the forces of evil.","The Harlond appears to have been devastated by the attack of a large force","Book 3, Chapter 4: Another Difficult Road","'I think this will be a fine place to stay until the road is clear. This is the perfect place to bring our waggon of valuable healing liquors. Did you know that this town has produced some of the finest healers in all the kingdom?\
\
'Now where was I? Oh yes! I have always sought to provide for my family and my dear old dad. He will never want for nails, for example....'","Bandron has asked you to go to Harlond and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> at certain locations to determine whether it is safe for him to go that way: the entrance of the city, the docks, and the gate in the Rammas Echor, the Pelennor's encircling wall.","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> within the Harlond, near the entrance of the city","'We cannot return to Galengam without selling his goods, so I sent Nethadan to Imloth Melui to find a purchaser for our Cemenduril liquor. Go north to the town and find my son, for he has not yet returned.'","'Oh, hello there, ${PLAYER}. How have you been keeping? I have been doing well.\
\
'My father was not pleased with me when I returned to him in Tarlang's Neck, but he is always looking for a reason to be unhappy. I told him to look on the bright side, as I do. After all, we will never want for nails! I have never known him to have enough of something before, and now he does. How many can say that? Very few folk!'","'I did not know you travelled with Lord Angbor of Lamedon, ${PLAYER}! It is my honour to serve him in any way I can, and I truly hope you have no tidings of Nethadan that might embarrass me in the presence of my liege!'\
\
Bandron is shaking with obvious terror of what you might say, and he exhales with obvious relief when you tell him that Nethadan believes Imloth Melui will be a good place to stay until the road through the Harlond is open.\
\
'That is my responsible boy! I have often prided myself on the example he sets for others, my Lord Angbor! Why, I think he seeks to model his behaviour after your own son, Drambor. That is my Nethadan, all right!'\
\
Privately, you think to yourself that perhaps both father and son have more in common than either would admit.","'The waggon-driver's son speaks wisdom. I have heard that Imloth Melui is known for the quality of its healers, and the folk here will know the value of the goods on this waggon.'","You are near the docks of the Harlond","'I did not expect to see you again, ${PLAYER}. I am not too proud to tell you that when Nethadan returned to my waggon with that second barrel of nails, I considered giving up on my profession and becoming a recluse then and there! I weighed that course very seriously, but in the end I decided it would be shameful to surrender to such a trial and I remain a waggon-driver.\
\
'My son has done nothing but make me regret that choice ever since! \\qFather, I ate too many apples.\\q \\qFather, I think I have a splinter.\\q \\qFather, I miss the sun.\\q When I was a boy, I would have taken this eternal night with more grace than he does, truly.\
\
'We are bound for Minas Tirith and its Houses of Healing with a supply of Cemenduril liquor from Galengam's Divine and Delicate Draughts, but I do not know if we will have safe passage. We encountered a traveller on the road who says the Harlond is full of Orcs! Can you investigate if this is so? There are three places I would know about, in particular: the entrance to Harlond, the docks, and the gate-house in the Rammas Echor, the wall that encircles the Pelennor.'","You are near the gate in the Rammas Echor","'I did not expect to see you again, ${PLAYER}.'","Bandron is on the road south of Imloth Melui, waiting for his son Nethadan to return.","Find the meeting of the roads just south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach","Talk to Bandron on the road south of Imloth Melui","Bandron and Nethadan have stopped their waggon south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach, and you should find out what has brought them here and why they have stopped.","Bandron is by his waggon in Lossarnach, south of Imloth Melui.\
\
You have investigated the port of the Harlond and found that it is occupied by the enemy. Bandron will not be able to go that way.","A waggon is stopped in the road. You recognize its driver from his exasperated expression","Talk to Angbor on the road south of Imloth Melui","'This waggon-driver serves Galengam, a merchant from my own town of Calembel. I have found Galengam's prices to be rather higher than is fair, and have spoken to the merchant about it before.'","Talk to Nethadan in Imloth Melui","'We must go to Minas Tirith. The fields of the Pelennor outside the White City are encircled by a great wall, the Rammas Echor, through which we must pass.\
\
'The south-gate in the Rammas is located in the haven of the Harlond. That is where we must go. First we will do as Aragorn requested, and see how fares the settlement of Imloth Melui, to the north along the road. There is a meeting of roads just south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach. Let us go there and assess the situation.'","'The Harlond is overrun? If we cannot get to the south-gate in the Rammas, we will not be able to bring our wares to Minas Tirith! What is it like to have good fortune? I would truly like to know, for I have never had it!\
\
'If there is a bright side to this news, it is that I suspected it was so. No ill news is truly surprising to me anymore, ${PLAYER}! We cannot return to Galengam without selling his goods, so I sent Nethadan to Imloth Melui to find a purchaser for our Cemenduril liquor. Go north to the town and find my son, for he has not yet returned.'","'That is my responsible boy! I have often prided myself on the example he sets for others, my Lord Angbor! Why, I think he seeks to model his behaviour after your own son, Drambor. That is my Nethadan, all right!'","Angbor is standing by Bandron's waggon on the road south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach.","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> within the Harlond, near the gate of the Rammas Echor"},
[2079]={"Habla con Halbarad y escucha lo que les sucedió a los Montaraces.","Libro 3, Capítulo 4: La Noche Cae sobre el Vado de Sarn","Halbarad está en el Vado de Sarn.","'La noche había caído el veintidós de septiembre cuando nuestra valentía fue puesta a prueba...'","Habla con Halbarad en el Vado de Sarn.","'El número de los terribles Espectros era nueve, ${PLAYER}, aunque no todos los que defendieron el Vado de Sarn sabían lo que eso significaba, como yo sí lo sabía. Desafiamos a esos Jinetes Negros mientras pudimos, pero ese no es un mal contra el que ningún hombre, ni ninguna mujer, pueda resistir por mucho tiempo. No juzgo a quienes huyeron o se ocultaron; aquellos de los Jinetes que no pasaron al País de los Hobbits persiguieron a los Dúnedain que encontraron en lo salvaje.\
\
'Aún quedan Montaraces en la Comarca, y sé que harán lo que deban para salvar a los hobbits de estos Jinetes Negros. Pero más de mis parientes fueron dispersados por Cardolan por aquellos Jinetes que no cruzaron el Brandivino, y necesitaremos su fortaleza en los días venideros, si todavía viven.\
\
'Eso es lo que necesito de ti y de Meneldir. Necesito que busquéis supervivientes del ataque y averigüéis cómo les ha ido en los días desde que mi gente fue dispersada como hojas al viento. Esto no curará la vergüenza de Meneldir, ni restaurará su juramento roto, pero puede revelar la naturaleza de su corazón. Si todavía guarda amor por sus antiguos parientes, ¡que lo demuestre ayudándolos ahora!\
\
'Tú, ${PLAYER}, eres libre de hacer lo que desees, pero debes saber que nos será de gran ayuda si nos prestas tu mano en esto, y no lo olvidaré.'","Agradecido por la ayuda que brindaste, Halbarad ha accedido a contarte lo que ocurrió en el Vado de Sarn hace apenas unos días.","Halbarad está en en el Vado de Sarn.\
\
Halbarad ha accedido a contarte lo que les sucedió a los Montaraces en el Vado de Sarn hace solo unos días.","'${PLAYER}, te contaré lo que ocurrió durante el ataque, y luego tendré una tarea para que tú y Meneldir la llevéis a cabo. El mal camina por la tierra, y no puedo negar la ayuda de quienes estén dispuestos a combatirlo.'"},
[2080]={"Para enfrentar la amenaza de Angmar, Halbarad ha decidido que debe convocar un consejo de los Pueblos Libres de las Quebradas del Norte: el Consejo de Esteldín.","'Saludos. Ojalá pudiera darte una bienvenida más cálida, pero estos son tiempos oscuros para los Elfos. La sombra del Enemigo se ha alargado, más de lo que cualquiera pensaba, y los Elfos de Lin Giliath han pagado el precio de nuestra complacencia.'","Libro 3, Capítulo 5, Parte I de III: Un llamado a los Elfos","Gildor Inglorion se encuentra en la arboleda élfica de Lin Giliath, al sur de Esteldín.\
\
Halbarad te dijo que la arboleda élfica fue atacada recientemente por Trolls de Piedra. Expresó su preocupación de que los Elfos de Lin Giliath estén demasiado ocupados lidiando con las consecuencias de este ataque como para acudir al Consejo.","'Al sur de Esteldín se encuentra un pequeño refugio de los Elfos. Durante muchos años los Elfos han vivido allí; sin embargo, en días recientes, la mayoría dejó la arboleda. Lo peor es que he oído que los pocos que quedaron fueron asesinados por Trolls de Piedra del Norte.\
\
Es irónico que Gildor Inglorion, un señor elfo de Rivendel, viniera a dar noticias de los movimientos del Enemigo, pero llegó demasiado tarde para salvar a los que quedaban.\
\
Debería ser llamado al Consejo, pero temo que esté demasiado consumido por el deseo de proteger tanto la arboleda como a su gente de su furia. Tu tarea será ir a Lin Giliath y convencer a Gildor de que acuda al Consejo.'","'Sin los Elfos, temo que cualquier campaña que emprendamos contra Angmar fracasará. Debes viajar al sur, a Lin Giliath, y hablar con Gildor Inglorion. Pídele que acuda al Consejo.'"},
[2081]={"'Este Consejo de Esteldín... Ojalá pudiera comprometerme sin reservas, pero no es tan sencillo. Muchos de mi pueblo están casi vencidos por el dolor y la ira por lo ocurrido aquí. Y las amenazas contra Lin Giliath aún no han sido resueltas. Nuestros exploradores me informan que los orcos en Nan Wathren planean atacarnos pronto.\
\
'Dicen los exploradores que estos orcos son liderados por un gran uruk de Angmar llamado Drukordh, que acampa en las partes más profundas de Nan Wathren. Quizá si este uruk fuera derrotado, Lin Giliath estaría lo suficientemente protegido para que yo pudiera acudir a tu Consejo. Es una carga pesada, pero te encomiendo esta tarea si tienes el corazón firme.\
\
'El uruk es un enemigo formidable, así que no deberías enfrentarlo solo. Si debes hacerlo, usa la fuerza de esta piedra élfica para encontrar el poder de prevalecer desde lo más profundo de ti.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Usar la piedra élfica te permite acceder al beneficio de inspiración estando solo o en una pequeña comunidad.</rgb>","'¡Ah, lo has logrado! ¡Escuchamos los lamentos de los orcos desde aquí! Has velado por la seguridad de Lin Giliath, ${PLAYER}, ¡y por ello te doy las gracias!'","Regresa con Gildor en Lin Giliath","'El uruk que lidera a los orcos de Nan Wathren se llama Drukordh. Nuestros exploradores dicen que acampa en los rincones más profundos y al sur de Nan Wathren. Si este uruk fuera derrotado, la amenaza de los orcos contra Lin Giliath disminuiría y yo podría acudir al Consejo de Esteldín.'","¡Drukordh ha sido derrotado!","Libro 3, Capítulo 5, Parte II de III: Cuidando la arboleda","Este parece ser un buen lugar para invocar el poder de la piedra élfica","Gildor se encuentra en Lin Giliath.\
\
Con el uruk Drukordh derrotado, deberías regresar con Gildor y darle esta buena noticia.","Cuando llegaste a Lin Giliath, Gildor te dijo que los orcos al oeste planean atacar la arboleda élfica.","Drukordh se encuentra en los rincones más profundos y al sur de Nan Wathren.\
\
Gildor te dijo que si el uruk Drukordh fuera derrotado, Lin Giliath estaría lo suficientemente seguro para que él pudiera acudir al Consejo de Esteldín. Te advirtieron que no lo enfrentes sin la ayuda de aliados.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Usar la piedra élfica te permite acceder al beneficio de inspiración estando solo o en una pequeña comunidad.</rgb>","Busca y derrota a Drukordh"},
[2082]={"'¡El mensaje que traes es doblemente alegre! ¿El Uruk Drukordh está muerto y los Elfos han aceptado venir al Consejo?\
\
Has hecho un gran trabajo, pues el poder de los Elfos mejorará aún más nuestra situación. ¡Te agradezco por esto!'","Libro 3, Capítulo 5, Parte III de III: El Poder de los Elfos","Tras derrotar al Uruk Drukordh, Gildor te dijo que los Elfos de Lin Giliath acudirán al Consejo de Esteldín.","'Debes ir ahora con Halbarad y llevarle la noticia de que vamos.'","Halbarad se encuentra en Esteldín.\
\
Gildor te pidió que le lleves la noticia a Halbarad de que los Elfos han aceptado venir al Consejo de Esteldín.","'Con el cacique Uruk muerto, Lin Giliath estará al menos un poco más seguro. ¿Pero por cuánto tiempo?'","'Con el Uruk Drukordh muerto, la amenaza de los orcos disminuye y soy libre para acudir al Consejo de Esteldín.\
\
Deberías llevarle la noticia a Halbarad de que asistiremos y que llegaremos pronto.\
\
Tus valientes hazañas pueden ser una base sólida para nuestras defensas.'","'¿Un Consejo de Elfos, Hombres y Enanos? Es algo que no se ha visto en mucho tiempo, creo yo.'"},
[2083]={"'I knew it was you the moment you came to this place! The Rangers of Ithilien have been watching your progress through the woods, speaking of your deeds, and my brother and I have been looking forward to meeting you!\
\
'I am Duilin, and this is my brother Derufin. We are no Rangers! We are from the Blackroot Vale, far west of here, and we marched to Minas Tirith with our father when the beacons were lit. And then... nothing. Sitting in idleness while excitement happens elsewhere has never been to either of our tastes, so we escaped from the White City and crossed the river in secret.\
\
'Now we seek adventure!'","'Faramir has spent more time of late ranging in the woods of Ithilien than he has in the White City. You are welcome to use my boat, and to have this advice: seek for Faramir and his Rangers at Bâr Húrin, to the east. I ask only this: defeat any Haradrim you encounter in Ithilien. They are a danger to my friends and my kingdom.'","Defeat Haradrim in South Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have been given permission to cross into Ithilien and seek Faramir's Rangers at Bâr Húrin, as long as you defeat Haradrim in those woods as you go.","Find the secret ferry among the reeds in the eastern reaches of Lossarnach","Talk to Duilin at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien","Defeated Haradrim in South Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The woman guardedly considers you as you approach","'My scouts learned that a friend to Gondor operates a secret ferry to the east, among the high reeds that border the river. Find her and see if she will bring you across the river into Ithilien, ${PLAYER}.'","Book 3, Chapter 5: Into Ithilien","A friend of Gondor operates a secret ferry across the river among the reeds that border the Anduin, on the eastern side of Lossarnach.\
\
Angbor has asked you to enter Ithilien by yourself while he seeks to assail the Harlond with his army.","Duilin is at the camp of Faramir's Rangers, at Bâr Húrin in South Ithilien.\
\
Duilin of the Blackroot Vale has called your name and beckoned you to speak to him.","'You approach from the west? I have seen precious few foe-men come from that way. Most enemies to Gondor have come from the east. Why do you seek to cross the river?'\
\
You tell the woman that you have important tidings of the war, but have sworn to give them only to Gandalf the Wizard or to Faramir of Minas Tirith.\
\
'I suspected as much, and will not ask for you to break your vow. I have not seen any Wizards in these parts, and the name Gandalf is unknown to me, but Faramir has spent more time of late ranging in the woods of Ithilien than he has in the White City. You are welcome to use my boat, and to have this advice: seek for Faramir and his Rangers at Bâr Húrin, to the east. I ask only this: defeat any Haradrim you encounter in Ithilien. They are a danger to my friends and my kingdom.'","Find the camp of Faramir's Rangers at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien","'Faramir has spent more time of late ranging in the woods of Ithilien than he has in the White City. You are welcome to use my boat, and to have this advice: seek for Faramir and his rangers at Bâr Húrin, to the east. I ask only this: defeat any Haradrim you encounter in Ithilien. They are a danger to my friends and my kingdom.'","Angbor and his four thousand men must get to Minas Tirith, but the only acceptable road for such a force leads through the south-gate of the Rammas, which is held by a large enemy force.","'Enemy forces must have crossed the Anduin and taken the port of the Harlond by surprise. They have had time enough to fortify the south-gate of the Rammas against us. That makes things more difficult to be sure. Only that road can support the movement of my four thousand men. We simply do not have the time or the resources to ferry that many warriors across the Anduin, and moving them through the forests of Ithilien in a wide sweep would be far too slow and take too much time. If we take such a course, the war will be ended before my men get there! No, they must retake the Harlond, and they will need me to lead them in this effort.\
\
'You, however, have another errand. Aragorn wanted you to reach either Gandalf or Faramir? You can take a single craft across the Anduin and move more swiftly than four thousand. You must pass into Ithilien and come by that way to Osgiliath. Meanwhile, my men will assail the Harlond.\
\
'My scouts learned that a friend to Gondor operates a secret ferry to the east, among the high reeds that border the river. Find her and see if she will bring you across the river into Ithilien, ${PLAYER}.'","You have crossed into Ithilien and seek Faramir's Rangers at Bâr Húrin.","Talk to the secret ferrywoman","A Gondorian man calls your name, and beckons to you"},
[2084]={"Habla con Handarod en Sírlond","Handarod te saluda con un gesto cansado","'Salva a los Dúnedain que puedas, ayúdales a recuperarse de sus heridas y devuelve toda la seguridad que puedas a las Quebradas del Sur. Si ves a los espectros..... escóndete, si puedes, pero corre, si debes. Hay un poder y una maldad en ellos que nunca había visto antes.'","Elfos acampan al este del río cerca de Caranost.\
\
Meneldir cree que algunos de los Montaraces dispersos probablemente se dirigieron a uno de los campamentos élficos al otro lado del río desde Caranost.","Handarod cree que otros Montaraces se reúnen en la Granja de Scurloc, al noreste.","'¿Handarod te envió con nosotros? Me alegra saber que aún vive..... demasiados de los nuestros fueron dispersados por el ataque de los terribles Jinetes, y algunos fueron asesinados incluso mientras huían. Los que sobrevivieron se dirigieron a esta granja, y debe haber otros refugios también.\
\
'¿Dije refugios? ¡Ningún lugar es seguro! No he visto señal de los Jinetes en dos días, pero hay orcos y semiorcos reuniéndose en las Quebradas del Sur, y siempre son una amenaza.'","'Si puedes disminuir el número de nuestros enemigos en las zonas circundantes, otros Montaraces podrán llegar aquí a Sírlond.'","Encuentra a los Montaraces que se dirigieron a la Granja de Scurloc, al noreste de Caranost","El Montaraz Malenfang vigila la Granja Scurloc, en las Quebradas del Sur.","Halbarad te encargó prestar ayuda a aquellos de su linaje que fueron dispersados por las Quebradas del Sur tras el ataque de los Jinetes Negros en el Vado de Sarn.","'Estoy agradecido por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}. Quizá más de mis parientes puedan llegar aquí a Sírlond gracias a tus esfuerzos.\
\
'Me ha llegado noticia de otro lugar de reunión de los Dúnedain, en la Granja de Scurloc al noreste. Te pediría que viajes allí y les brindes ayuda similar, para el bien de todos nosotros. Esos espectros siguen merodeando, y ya han matado a muchos de mis amigos.'","'Es bueno ver rostros amistosos después de los días que hemos pasado. Los Montaraces se reúnen aquí para recuperarse de sus heridas, y hasta ahora hemos permanecido fuera de la vista de las terribles sombras que nos persiguieron desde el Vado de Sarn. Somos los afortunados..... no todos mis amigos han tenido tanta suerte.\
\
'Si puedes disminuir el número de nuestros enemigos en las zonas circundantes, otros Montaraces podrán llegar aquí a Sírlond.'","Peligrosos enemigos acechan las Quebradas del Sur, dificultando que los parientes dispersos del Montaraz Handarod lleguen a Sírlond. Él te ha pedido que hagas lo que puedas para ayudar.","'Cuando caminé por última vez las ondulantes colinas de las Quebradas del Sur, había Elfos acampados al este del río, justo al otro lado de Caranost. Comencemos nuestra búsqueda allí.'","Habla con Malenfang en la granja de Scurloc","Enemigos derrotados en las Quebradas del Sur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Handarod reúne a los Montaraces en Sírlond, un campamento élfico al otro lado del río desde Caranost, la antigua capital de Cardolan.","'Toda búsqueda en las Quebradas del Sur debe comenzar cerca de Caranost, ${PLAYER}. Desde allí se domina la vista de las tierras circundantes, y creo que cualquier Montaraz que busque regresar de su huida se dirigirá hacia allí.\
\
'Cuando caminé por última vez las ondulantes colinas de las Quebradas del Sur, había Elfos acampados al este del río, justo al otro lado de Caranost. Comencemos nuestra búsqueda allí.'","Malenfang asiente cuando te acercas.","Meneldir está en el Vado de Sarn.\
\
Meneldir está deseoso de partir en busca de sus parientes dispersos.","Habla con Meneldir en el Vado de Sarn","Derrota enemigos en las Quebradas del Sur que pongan en peligro a los Montaraces dispersos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Muchos de mis parientes fueron dispersados por las Quebradas del Sur tras el ataque, y temo que al menos cuatro de los Jinetes Negros puedan acosar a los Montaraces entre las colinas. Salva a los Dúnedain que puedas, ayúdales a recuperarse de sus heridas y devuelve toda la seguridad que puedas a las Quebradas del Sur.\
\
'Si ves a los espectros..... escóndete, si puedes, pero corre, si debes. Hay un poder y una maldad en ellos que nunca había visto antes.'","El Montaraz Handarod está en Sírlond, esperando noticias de tu éxito en las Quebradas del Sur.","'¡Salve!'","Busca Montaraces dispersos en un campamento élfico al otro lado del río","Malenfang te saluda con un gesto cuando te acercas","Libro 3, Capítulo 5: Las Quebradas del Sur"},
[2085]={"Para enfrentar la amenaza de Angmar, Halbarad ha decidido convocar un consejo de los Pueblos Libres de las Quebradas del Norte: el Consejo de Esteldín.","'Nellie Bosquejo se encuentra en la ciudad de Puente de Caballetes, al suroeste de Esteldín. Te advierto que la amenaza constante sobre su ciudad puede dificultar convencerla de asistir al Consejo.'","'¿Un \\qConsejo de Esteldín\\q? ¿Has perdido el juicio, ${RACE}? ¿No eres consciente de los peligros que enfrenta esta ciudad? ¿De los ataques constantes que debemos soportar?\
\
'Esos orientales, si realmente les importaran las amenazas que enfrenta Puente de Caballetes, nos ayudarían aquí con estos Orcos. ¡No habríamos tenido que sufrir como lo hemos hecho! Yo... ¡hemos perdido a todos nuestros seres queridos!'\
\
'No, no iré a ese Consejo, ni a ningún otro. ¡Y no me convencerás de lo contrario! Ahora, si no tienes más asuntos aquí, déjame ocuparme de la defensa de esta ciudad!'","Nellie Bosquejo se encuentra en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Halbarad te advirtió que Nellie podría estar tan ocupada con la defensa de Puente de Caballetes que no verá la importancia de asistir al Consejo de Esteldín.","'¡No necesito a tus amigos Montaraces!'","Libro 3, Capítulo 6, Parte I de III: Un llamado a los Hombres","Halbarad se encuentra en Esteldín.\
\
Al recibir tu mensaje sobre el Consejo de Esteldín, Nellie Bosquejo se negó rotundamente a venir, diciendo que la defensa de su ciudad estaba por encima de cualquier otra preocupación. Debes regresar con Halbarad y darle su respuesta.","'De todos los que han sufrido en las Quebradas del Norte, quizás el pueblo de Puente de Caballetes sea el que más ha sufrido. Han resistido todos los ataques de los Orcos, pero su número está disminuyendo. De hecho, el alcalde de la ciudad, Lovelle Bosquejo, fue asesinado recientemente y su hija, Nellie, ahora lidera a la gente allí.\
\
'Te pediría que vayas a Puente de Caballetes y hables con Nellie. Necesitaremos su liderazgo en el Consejo.\
\
'Te advierto: aunque su pueblo es el que más puede ganar viniendo, Nellie será la más difícil de convencer. Los ataques constantes impiden que piense en otra cosa que no sea enfrentar la amenaza inmediata.'","'¡Bien, has regresado! No me sorprende que Nellie haya rechazado la invitación al Consejo, pero eso ya no importa.\
\
'Ha llegado la noticia de que un gran contingente de Orcos se dirige a Puente de Caballetes. La gente allí es fuerte, pero temo que no puedan enfrentarse a estos Orcos y al cacique que los lidera.\
\
'Debemos ir en su ayuda.'"},
[2086]={"'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para la batalla que viene? Será difícil y necesitaremos a todos los guerreros que puedas reunir.\
\
¿Estás listo para partir ahora?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Se sugiere completar esta instancia en una comunidad. La Inspiración te ayudará si decides afrontar este desafío solo o con un grupo pequeño.</rgb>","'En el pasado, los orcos que han atacado eran de la tribu Tarkrîp. La sed de sangre de esa tribu suele hacer que se lancen al combate sin pensar.\
\
Los orcos que ahora avanzan sobre Puente de Caballetes parecen ser de la tribu Ongbúrz, más poderosa. Estos guerreros son más fuertes y hábiles. Los habitantes no podrán detenerlos. Enviaría un grupo de mis hombres para ayudar, pero todos están ocupados en el este.\
\
Tú y yo quizá lleguemos a tiempo. Ya has hecho mucho, pero te pido ayuda en esta batalla. Reúne a los guerreros que puedas y vuelve conmigo. Pero apresúrate... Trestlebridge no tiene mucho tiempo.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Se sugiere completar esta misión en grupo. La Inspiración te ayudará si decides afrontar este desafío solo o en una comunidad.</rgb>","Habla con Halbarad","Al regresar de Puente de Caballetes con la negativa de Nellie Bosquejo de unirse al Consejo, Halbarad te informó que una gran fuerza de orcos se dirigía a Trestlebridge.","Libro 3, Capítulo 6, Parte II de III: La Defensa de Puente de Caballetes","'Debo disculparme contigo, pues temo que mi comportamiento hacia ti fue casi imperdonable. Ahora veo que los constantes ataques de orcos no eran nada comparados con lo que Angmar podría traer a este pequeño pueblo.\
\
Tú y el Montaraz Halbarad han arriesgado sus vidas para salvar a mi gente. Te estoy en deuda.'","Viaja con Halbarad a Puente de Caballetes y ayuda en su defensa.\
\
Halbarad te dijo que los orcos que avanzan sobre Trestlebridge son de la tribu Ongbúrz, más poderosa. Los habitantes no podrán defenderse solos. Halbarad te indicó que reunieras aliados y volvieras con él.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides afrontarla solo recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Nellie Bosquejo se encuentra en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Junto a Halbarad, ayudaste a defender Trestlebridge de los orcos que intentaban destruirla. Al final de la batalla, Nellie Bosquejo pidió hablar contigo."},
[2087]={"Libro 3, Capítulo 6, Parte III de III: Los Pueblos Libres de Puente de Caballetes","'¡Te juzgué demasiado severamente antes! Espero que puedas perdonarme.'","'Por favor, lleva el mensaje a Halbarad de que yo mismo asistiré al Consejo y que toda la fuerza que el pueblo de Puente de Caballetes pueda aportar a sus planes lo haremos, con voluntad y gratitud.'","'La deuda que tengo contigo y con los Montaraces no puede pagarse fácilmente, pero espero comenzar a saldarla respondiendo al llamado de Halbarad al Consejo. Toda la fuerza que los hombres de Puente de Caballetes puedan aportar al esfuerzo de Halbarad estará a su disposición.\
\
'Por favor, dile a Halbarad que iré a Esteldín tan pronto como resuelva algunos asuntos aquí. Sigo siendo responsable primero de mi gente, pero ahora veo que los Pueblos Libres de las Quebradas del Norte deben permanecer unidos si queremos seguir siendo libres.\
\
'Gracias, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.''","Después de que tú y Halbarad ayudaron a su pueblo, Nellie Bosquejo juró aportar toda la fuerza que el pueblo de Puente de Caballetes tiene a su causa. Vendrán al Consejo de Esteldín.","'Un Consejo en Esteldín. Si tan solo mi padre estuviera aquí para verlo....'","Halbarad se encuentra en Esteldín.\
\
Nellie Bosquejo te ha pedido que informes a Halbarad que ella asistirá al Consejo de Esteldín.","'Me alegra verte de nuevo. Te agradezco tu ayuda en esa batalla. Sin ti y tus compañeros, seguramente habría caído, al igual que Puente de Caballetes.\
\
'También es bueno saber que Nellie Bosquejo vendrá al Consejo. Es una mujer fuerte y admirable, y daré la bienvenida a ella y a su gente en el conflicto que se avecina.'","'Mi gente es de gran corazón, pero ¿será suficiente para las batallas que se avecinan?'"},
[2088]={"La mesa de la Granja de Scurloc servirá como un buen lugar para ordenar los fragmentos de las órdenes que recuperaste.","Malenfang cree que podrías encontrar más información sobre el propósito compartido de los semiorcos y los trasgos en las ruinas de Haudh Nirui, al noroeste de Amon Firn.","Debes leer el fragmento de pergamino que encontraste en el cuerpo del semiorco.","'Que esto sea una lección para ustedes, trasgos: los grandes tienen formas de tratar la traición, y si trabajan contra sus objetivos, lo que les pasó a los anteriores puede pasarles a ustedes y a los suyos también. Se les dirá lo que necesiten saber cuando lo necesiten, y no antes. El Señor Oscuro nos recompensará por nuestro servicio; ¿por qué otra razón los más Sabios se unirían a él, como nosotros lo hemos hecho?\
\
'Los enanos serán fáciles de manipular. Seguirán a Skorgrím a donde los lleve... sin importar quién dirige a Skorgrím. Confío en que el señor demacrado pueda lograrlo, y eso debería bastarles. El ataque vendrá desde ambas direcciones: bajando desde las Montañas Azules y subiendo por el Camino Verde desde los viejos túmulos. Incluso ahora el Rey Brujo trabaja para alzar a los espíritus de los Muertos. Con la ayuda del Miedo Gris, nadie se opondrá a él, ni a nosotros. Fue el Miedo Gris quien devastó el antiguo reino que se alzaba aquí, ¡y mira lo poco que queda!\
\
'La sombra crece en Angmar, pero necesita tiempo para reunir su fuerza. No mucho... pero tiempo al fin. Para eso estamos nosotros, mi banda y ustedes. No interfieran con los Jinetes o con el Miedo Gris... nadie podría salvarlos entonces, y tampoco querrían ser salvados... solo desearían la muerte. Lo que el Miedo les haría no soporta ser imaginado.\
\
'Así que manténganse apartados. Ellos son los siervos más valiosos del Señor Oscuro. Ustedes y yo solo somos sierpes para ellos, y los gusanos pueden ser aplastados si no saben apartarse. Se nos llamará cuando seamos necesarios.'","'¿Has revisado todos los papeles? Bien, ¿qué dicen?'","Las órdenes que recuperaste han sido reducidas a fragmentos por los trasgos de Haudh Nirui, y será necesario ordenarlas y reconstruirlas antes de poder leerlas.","No del todo...","Registra Haudh Nirui en busca de fragmentos de órdenes dirigidas a los trasgos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Esto podría ser...","'Buena suerte clasificando todos esos papeles, ${PLAYER}. ¡Esperaré tu resumen!'","Lee las órdenes de los semiorcos","Malenfang está en la Granja de Scurloc, esperando ver cualquiera de las órdenes de semiorcos que hayas recuperado.","Se pueden encontrar semiorcos cerca de Amon Firn, en las Quebradas del Sur.\
\
Malenfang te ha pedido que busques cualquier orden que los semiorcos puedan estar llevando.","Encuentras un fragmento de pergamino en el cuerpo del semiorco","Has reensamblado los fragmentos de las órdenes dirigidas a los semiorcos y trasgos de las Quebradas del Sur, colocándolos en una forma legible que parece tener sentido.","Meneldir ha llegado y querrá ver las órdenes que reconstruiste.","Ordena los papeles en la mesa de la Granja de Scurloc","'No me gusta cómo suena eso, ${PLAYER}. No solo los siervos de la Mano Blanca se mueven abiertamente en la Ciénaga de los Cisnes, sino que en Cardolan y más allá hay otros poderes actuando: el Rey Brujo y los Jinetes Negros, trasgos y semiorcos uniendo fuerzas, ¿y ahora una rebelión enana liderada por alguien llamado Skorgrím? A juzgar por su nombre no es un barbiluengo, pero si conduce un ejército desde las Montañas Azules, estaremos en graves problemas, sea quien sea.\
\
'Pero hay algo más también. Estas órdenes hablan de algo llamado \\qel Miedo Gris\\q. Es un título que me resulta familiar, pero no puedo recordar por qué, y eso me inquieta.'","Coloca los fragmentos de las órdenes en la mesa de la Granja de Scurloc","'Si hemos de creer al autor de estas órdenes, quizá sepamos más de los trasgos en las ruinas al noroeste de Amon Firn. ¡Haudh Nirui, se llaman. ¡Esperemos que los trasgos sean tan descuidados con sus propias órdenes como los semiorcos creen que son!'","Has reunido fragmentos de órdenes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Meneldir en la Granja de Scurloc sobre lo que has aprendido.","'¿Semiorcos trabajando con trasgos? Parece que ninguno de los dos bandos está muy contento con ello, pero no puedo deducir cuál es su plan general, ni para quién trabajan. Creo que un semiorco sostuvo la pluma que escribió estas órdenes, no uno de esos terribles Jinetes... pero ¿para quién las escribió?\
\
'Si hemos de creer al autor de estas órdenes, quizá sepamos más de los trasgos que viven en las ruinas al noroeste de Amon Firn. Haudh Nirui, se llaman. ¡Esperemos que los trasgos sean tan descuidados con sus propias órdenes como los semiorcos creen que son!'","Derrota semiorcos en Amon Firn y encuentra cualquier orden que puedan llevar","'Semiorcos se reúnen alrededor de la base de Amon Firn, el Monte de los Muertos, un lugar de mal agüero al este, y algunos se han atrevido a acercarse a esta granja. Sospecho que pueden llevar órdenes que guíen sus movimientos.\
\
'Encuentra esas órdenes, si existen, y tráeme lo que halles. Cuando sepamos qué buscan lograr y cómo sus movimientos se alinean con los de los Jinetes Negros que nos atacaron, podremos oponernos mejor a ellos.'","Ya casi...","Libro 3, Capítulo 6: Peligro en Todas Direcciones","'¿Encontraste unas órdenes en un semiorco? Deberías leerlas y ver qué podemos aprender de sus planes en esta zona.'","Lleva las órdenes de los semiorcos a Malenfang en la Granja de Scurloc","Examina las órdenes reconstruidas en la mesa de la Granja de Scurloc","El Montaraz Malenfang ha aprendido lo suficiente sobre la actividad de sus enemigos en las Quebradas del Sur como para estar preocupado."},
[2089]={"Talk to Duilin at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien","'I can hardly contain my excitement! It is time to hunt the mighty Mûmakil the Haradrim have brought to Gondor!'","You have encountered Duilin and Derufin of the Blackroot Vale, becoming entangled in their quest to hunt the giant Mûmakil the Haradrim have brought to Gondor.","'The people of the Blackroot Vale know of our grand adventures throughout the wild, and certainly speak of the ferocious creatures we have hunted. They will be as nothing compared to the prey we now seek: the mighty Mûmakil!\
\
'The Rangers have seen these great beasts in the service of the Haradrim of the south, but so far none have felled even a single Mûmak. My brother and I will be the first to do so, and we would be honoured for you to accompany us on this hunt!'\
\
You tell Duilin that you are looking for Faramir, and cannot delay from that errand.\
\
'He is not here, but if you help us hunt the mighty Mûmakil, you have my word that the sons of Blackroot will help you find him! Speak to me when you are ready to depart, ${PLAYER}!'","'What a delight! Did you see the size of those Mûmakil? They were even larger than I expected, and twice as ferocious! I am still winded from their pursuit, and I could not be happier about it!'\
\
Duilin's eyes are bright and words tumble from him in an excited torrent.\
\
'Next time we will have one for sure! Their hides are thick, but seeing them up close has shown me where to aim: their eyes! That is the only unprotected spot... I see that now! Oh, what a prize this will be! And certainly it will be pleasant to deprive the Haradrim of such a mighty beast of war. But think of the tales they will sing of my brother and me! And you too, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'But for now we are to help you with an errand of your own, I suppose.'","Book 3, Chapter 6: Sons of Blackroot","Duilin is at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien.\
\
The Mûmak hunt did not go as planned, but Duilin and Derufin do not seem to mind.","Talk to Duilin and hunt the mighty Mûmakil","Duilin is at Bâr Húrin, in South Ithilien.\
\
You have grudgingly agreed to help Duilin and Derufin hunt the mighty Mûmakil, in return for their help finding Faramir."},
[2090]={"'Faramir is in charge of the defence, but we were separated during the fighting and no man has seen him. When last I saw my captain, he was fighting by the south-west wall of Osgiliath in the company of doughty warriors Inthol and Gelnor. If you can find one of them, they may have tidings. Do what you can to slow the Enemy's march and to find Faramir!'","Find Faramir or his men within the Osgiliath Culverts","Dig through the rubble near the fountain east of Gelnor (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You have recovered one of the messages sent by Gothmog to his forces in Osgiliath, and should bring it to Damrod among the culverts beneath the city.","'You there! You are a friend, I can tell from your dress and bearing. You have to help me! I was separated from Faramir and sustained this injury, and it keeps me from doing something that I must!\
\
'Many of the Orkish forces are led by a terrible man clad all in armour. He is Gothmog, and they cower at his approach, but they follow his commands. Runners bring messages from him throughout the city, and I saw one of these runners perish beneath many falling stones near a fountain to the east. I was injured before I could dig through the rubble to find the orders.\
\
'I have overheard the Orcs speaking of a mighty weapon they plan to use against the White City! Go to the fountain and search through the stones for the dead message-bearer. The message he carries might give us knowledge of this weapon!'","'You are a friend? I am Inthol, soldier of Gondor. The pain is still overwhelming, but I feel it less keenly to know there are still good folk fighting to defend the city!\
\
'Captain Faramir is not here, friend. He went north with Gelnor, but they were pursued by a terrible apparition and I do not know what became of them. It was a man, I think, but tall, and clad all in armour. My blood ran cold at the sight of him. The Orcs followed his commands, and they named him Gothmog.\
\
'I would never question Faramir's courage or his resolve, but I hope for his sake, and for Gondor's, that he remained two steps ahead of this terrible commander!'","You find a parchment clutched in a dead hand, buried under stones!","You dig through the rubble, but find nothing of use","Maybe you missed something. Keep digging! (${NUMBER}/3)","Defeat Orcs throughout Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Search the south-western area of Osgiliath for one of Damrod's men","'The fountain is to the east of here! You have to keep digging through the rubble! What if the message that runner carried contains details about the Orkish weapon?'","You have found Gelnor, but he is alone and there is no sign of Faramir","Book 3, Chapter 7: Osgiliath Overrun","Faramir and his men may be found within the Osgiliath Culverts beneath the city, if they still stand against the armies of the enemy.","Talk to Damrod among the Osgiliath Culverts","Gelnor saw an Orc runner crushed beneath falling stones near a fountain to the east, and he wants you to dig through the rubble in search of the message it carried.","A Gondorian soldier clutches at his wounds and beckons to you","Orcs can be found throughout Osgiliath, and Damrod hopes that you might find Faramir or soldiers with news of him in the south-western area of the city.","Bring the Orc-message to Damrod among the Osgiliath Culverts","You have found the city's defenders, but Faramir is not with them","'Captain Faramir is not here, friend. He went north with Gelnor, but they were pursued by a terrible apparition and I do not know what became of them. It was a man, I think, but tall, and clad all in armour. My blood ran cold at the sight of him. The Orcs followed his commands, and they named him Gothmog.\
\
'I would never question Faramir's courage or his resolve, but I hope for his sake, and for Gondor's, that he remained two steps ahead of this terrible commander!'","Inthol told you that he last saw Faramir and Gelnor racing to the north-west area of Osgiliath, pursued by a frightful commander of the enemy forces named Gothmog.","Defeated Orcs throughout Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The men here think Faramir can be found to the north, somewhere in the city of Osgiliath astride the Anduin. The Steward of Gondor charged his son with the defence of Osgiliath, but none here know if he has repelled the enemy. Some speak of a hidden encampment within the culverts beneath the city. If Faramir or his men still defend the city, that is where they will be.\
\
'My brother and I will go with you to Osgiliath. There are certain to be more than enough Orcs for the both of us to hone our skills in battle!'","'These are the men who remain in defence of the city? That means more glory for the rest of us, ${PLAYER}!'","'The men speak of a hidden encampment within the culverts beneath Osgiliath. If Faramir or his men still defend the city, that is where they will be.\
\
'My brother and I will go with you to Osgiliath. There are certain to be more than enough Orcs for the both of us to hone our skills in battle!'","Damrod and the few Gondorian soldiers that still defend Osgiliath can be found among the culverts beneath the city.","Duilin and Derufin have agreed to travel with you to Osgiliath. There you hope to learn the state of the defences and what has become of Faramir.","'You have to help me! I was separated from Faramir and sustained this injury, and it keeps me from doing something that I must!\
\
'Many of the Orkish forces are led by a terrible man clad all in armour. He is Gothmog, and they cower at his approach, but they follow his commands. Runners bring messages from him throughout the city, and I saw one of these runners perish beneath many falling stones near a fountain to the east. I was injured before I could dig through the rubble to find the orders.\
\
'I have overheard the Orcs speaking of a mighty weapon they plan to use against the White City! Go to the fountain and search through the stones for the dead message-bearer. The message he carries might give us knowledge of this weapon!'","Damrod takes the parchment from you and reads the crude writing.\
\
'I cannot read much of this message, but I can understand enough of it to know it means trouble.'","'I gladly welcome your help, even as I fear it comes too late, ${PLAYER}. The city is lost. There are too many Orcs, and every passing hour brings more of their kind, as well as ferocious warriors from the South. I do not hope to save the city, ${CLASS}. Now my hope is to purchase as much time for the defenders of Minas Tirith as I am able. Osgiliath will not be retaken, but until we are slain we might slow the forward march of these foes with our efforts.\
\
'Faramir is in charge of the defence, but we were separated during the fighting and no man has seen him. When last I saw my captain, he was fighting by the south-west wall of Osgiliath in the company of doughty warriors Inthol and Gelnor. If you can find one of them, they may have tidings. Do what you can to slow the Enemy's march and to find Faramir!'","Search the north-western area of Osgiliath for another of Damrod's men"},
[2091]={"Habla con Handarod en Sírlond","Debes llevar el diario al lugar que describe: la esquina suroriental de Tyrn Gorthad","El diario de Narndir describe una ubicación en las zonas surorientales de Tyrn Gorthad.\
\
Debes viajar al lugar descrito por el diario y leer allí las páginas correspondientes.","La escritura es tan evocadora que casi puedes imaginar los horrores que aquí sucedieron","Malenfang está en Scurloc Farm, esperando oír lo que aprendiste de los papeles que descifraste.","'Pensarás que he perdido el juicio', escribe Narndir, 'pero tras tantos estudios siento como si conociera a estas figuras del antiguo pasado. Cuando sufren, sufro. Cuando lloran, lloro. Y cuando triunfan... oh, nadie podría comprender la alegría que siento en sus triunfos, por pocos que fueran en aquellos años oscuros.'\
\
'Siento que los conozco: Amlaith el Constructor, antes Príncipe de Cardolan y luego Príncipe de Arthedain en Fornost. Eldamacil, Príncipe de Rhudaur, fratricida y maldito.\
\
'Y el Príncipe Tarondor, con quien siento un estrecho vínculo. El tercer y más joven hijo del Rey Eärendur de Arnor fue puesto en duda no solo por sus hermanos sino también por su propia gente. Quienes vivían en Cardolan durante su gobierno lo llamaban Tarondor el Añadido, pero era un sobrenombre que superaría. Cuando nobles corruptos prometieron botín a las tribus de montañeses del sur si se alzaban contra el príncipe, él cabalgó y derrotó a los invasores. Las historias de su valor crecieron, y Tarondor el Añadido se convirtió en Tarondor el Franco, amado por su pueblo.\
\
'Así fue que cuando Eärendur, Rey de Arnor y padre de estos tres príncipes, murió de una enfermedad sin nombrar sucesor, hubo más de un pretendiente al trono. Podría haberse derramado sangre entonces, como ocurriría más tarde, pero Amlaith propuso un compromiso. \\qDividamos el reino de Arnor\\q, dijo a sus hermanos, \\qy que cada uno gobierne una provincia en amistad y alianza mutua.\\q\
\
'Tarondor entonces dejó de ser príncipe para convertirse en rey, y fue conocido como el Rey Tarondor II, pues ya había existido otro Tarondor en la línea. Como Rey de Cardolan ordenó construir un trono y forjar una corona en Caranost, y la fortaleza se convirtió en la capital y sede de gobierno del joven reino. Y aun al escribir estas palabras, siento lágrimas aflorar en mis ojos, pues veo la semilla de la traición y la muerte creciendo en los mismos cimientos, y sé lo que habrá de ocurrir.'","'¿Las zonas surorientales de Tyrn Gorthad? ¿Qué podría escribir Narndir sobre ese lugar funesto?'","'Tras la más reciente derrota de Rhudaur', escribe Narndir, 'los ejércitos del Rey Brujo necesitaron tiempo para recuperarse y reconstruirse. Durante ese tiempo, su malvado señor recurrió a la hechicería para atormentar a sus enemigos. En secreto llegó a los túmulos y caminó entre ellos, susurrando a los muertos. Desconocido para quienes vivían cerca, señores y reyes enterrados desde hacía mucho se agitaron en sus tumbas, infestados por espíritus surgidos de las fosas más oscuras de Angmar. A la orden del Rey Brujo emergieron, legiones de Muertos moviéndose en silencio entre la niebla, acechando a cualquiera que se acercara demasiado.'","Debes llevar el diario al lugar que describe: la sala del trono en Caranost","'Esto nos da mucho en qué pensar, pero lo que más me preocupa son estas menciones de algo llamado el Miedo Gris. ¿Es una persona, un espíritu, o algo más? Sea lo que sea, si fue responsable de algún modo de la caída de Cardolan o de la ruptura de Arnor, ¡debemos impedir que repita un mal semejante contra nosotros hoy!\
\
'¿Qué tiene que decir Malenfang sobre esto?'","'¿Narndir escribe sobre un lugar en las zonas surorientales de Tyrn Gorthad? Parece que debemos volver al Camino Verde, ${PLAYER}. Desde allí podremos subir a Tyrn Gorthad, aunque ha sido un lugar abandonado por cientos de años.'","'El Príncipe Amondir desapareció entre los túmulos. Nunca se le volvió a ver.'","La escritura es tan evocadora que casi puedes oír el sonido de la batalla","'¿Alguien o algo llamado el Miedo Gris, dices? No he oído que tal cosa estuviera involucrada con la ruina del antiguo reino, pero no soy un erudito. Deberías hablar con Narndir, si puedes encontrarlo. Siempre tenía un gran interés por la historia de Cardolan, y solía vérsele escribiendo en uno de sus muchos diarios.'\
\
Algo en tu expresión detiene a Handarod, que te mira interrogante. A regañadientes, le cuentas que Narndir fue asesinado por Jinetes Negros durante la huida desde el Vado de Sarn, y que tú y Meneldir descubristeis su cuerpo junto al camino al noroeste de Herne.\
\
'Lamento mucho oír eso, especialmente por Meneldir; sé que eran cercanos. Narndir nunca dijo una mala palabra de Meneldir, aun después de que se marchara. No podía decirse lo mismo de muchos otros.'\
\
Handarod tamborilea distraídamente sus dedos sobre la empuñadura de su espada.\
\
'Quizá Narndir aún pueda ayudarnos, ${PLAYER}. Te hablé de los diarios que llevaba. Bien, sé al menos de un lugar donde escondió algunos. Al este, bajo una de las torres de Caranost, había un hueco. Busca allí y ve si Narndir escribió algo acerca de este Miedo Gris en los años previos a su muerte.'","Contempla la imagen del Rey Tarondor II","'¿El diario de Narndir describe la sala del trono de Caranost? Esa se encuentra muy arriba, en el punto más alto de la ciudad en ruinas. Deberías ir allí y leer lo que Narndir tenía que decir al respecto.'","El diario de Narndir describe la sala del trono de Caranost, ubicada en el punto más alto de la ciudad en ruinas.\
\
Debes viajar al lugar descrito por el diario y leer allí las páginas correspondientes.","'¿Qué escribe Narndir sobre la Batalla del Monte de los Muertos? ¡Ojalá estuviera aquí para contárnoslo en persona!'","Has recuperado el diario de Narndir, en el que registró muchos pensamientos sobre la historia de Arnor y los reinos que le siguieron.","Contempla la imagen del Rey Artandil","'Narndir escribe sobre un sendero claro que asciende por el lado norte de Amon Firn. Cuando estés cerca de la cima de la colina deberías leer el relato correspondiente en su diario.'","Busca el escondite del diario de Narndir","Contempla la imagen de Amondir, Señor de Tyrn Gorthad","Presencia la última aventura del Príncipe Amondir","Habla con Malenfang en la granja de Scurloc","'Después de que el Rey Artandil cayera en el Monte de los Muertos', escribe Narndir, 'fue Amondir, Señor de Tyrn Gorthad y Guardián de los Túmulos, quien reunió lo que quedaba del ejército Cardoladhrim. Gritando el nombre del Rey mientras cargaba, Amondir arremetió contra los hombres de Rhudaur que huían. El hijo de Malgun fue capturado y más tarde rescatado, y se compró una paz costosa entre los reinos.\
\
'La corona de Cardolan fue ofrecida entonces a Amondir, pero él la rechazó. No quiso nombrarse rey y en su lugar tomó el título de Príncipe; gobernaría desde Dol Ernil, su propia fortaleza en Tyrn Gorthad. La primacía de Cardolan decayó, y la línea de Elendil solo se sostuvo ya en Arthedain. Amondir cabalgó a Fornost para ofrecer su lealtad, y con la reunificación de Arthedain y Cardolan bajo Argeleb, el recién coronado Rey de Arnor, hubo nuevamente esperanza para la línea de Elendil y los atribulados reinos de los Dúnedain.\
\
'Pero no duraría, porque había un poder tras la maldad de Rhudaur, y caminaba en secreto.'","'Esta es la sala del trono de Caranost. ¿Qué tiene que decir Narndir sobre ella, ${PLAYER}?'","Handarod está en Sírlond, al otro lado del río frente a Caranost, y puede conocer a alguien que pueda contarte sobre el Miedo Gris.","Narndir guardaba sus diarios en un lugar secreto en las Quebradas del Sur, pero Handarod conocía su ubicación. El escondite está bajo una de las torres orientales de Caranost, en un hueco bajo la torre.","Encuentra el escondite del diario de Narndir en un hueco bajo la torre más oriental de Caranost","'¿El Miedo Gris? No, nunca he oído tal nombre. ¿Podría ser una enfermedad, o algún tipo de mal?\
\
'Recuerdo que había un erudito entre los Dúnedain que vivía entre las ruinas del Antiguo Cardolan, aunque su nombre se me escapa. Handarod tal vez conozca su paradero. ¿No estaba acampado fuera de Caranost? Quizá deberías volver y preguntar por él.'","Dentro del pequeño cofre encuentras un diario encuadernado en cuero, atado con un cordón","La escritura de Narndir ha traído importantes figuras del pasado de Cardolan a tu imaginación en el sitio de la Batalla del Monte de los Muertos, Amon Firn.","'Es difícil escuchar las palabras de mi amigo Narndir y saber que no escribirá más. Guardaré este diario en memoria de él, y lo haría incluso si no necesitáramos el conocimiento que contiene.'\
\
Le entregas el diario a Meneldir y él pasa sus páginas.\
\
'...nunca se le volvió a ver', lee, y pasa la página. Te mira, perplejo.\
\
'¿Qué pasó con el resto del relato de Narndir? Faltan varias páginas aquí. Incluso si ese fuera el final de la historia de Amondir, seguramente Narndir habría escrito más. Mira: la narración continúa aquí, después de las páginas faltantes. Pero ¿qué fue removido, y quién lo removió?'","'¿Qué tiene Narndir que decirnos sobre Tyrn Gorthad? Casi temo escucharlo.'","'Quizá Narndir aún pueda ayudarnos, ${PLAYER}. Te hablé de los diarios que llevaba. Bien, sé al menos de un lugar donde escondió algunos. Al este, bajo una de las torres de Caranost, había un hueco. Busca allí y ve si Narndir registró algo acerca de este Miedo Gris en los años previos a su muerte.'","Lee el diario de Narndir mientras estés en la sala del trono de Caranost, ubicada en el punto más alto de la capital arruinada de Cardolan","Contempla la imagen del Rey Brujo","'Recuerdo que había un erudito entre los Dúnedain que vivía entre las ruinas del Antiguo Cardolan, aunque su nombre se me escapa. Handarod quizá conozca su paradero. ¿No estaba acampado fuera de Caranost? Quizá deberías volver y preguntarle.'","Lee el diario de Narndir mientras estés en las zonas surorientales de Tyrn Gorthad","Debes llevar el diario al lugar que describe, en Amon Firn","'La plaga de los Muertos empeoró', escribe Narndir, 'y ni siquiera los niños de Cardolan estaban a salvo de ella: innumerables niños fueron arrancados de sus camas, o desaparecieron dentro de muros por lo demás firmes e implacables.\
\
'Desesperado por poner fin a esta pesadilla, el Príncipe Amondir emprendió una misión para encontrar la causa de la inquietud de los Muertos. Él era el Señor de Tyrn Gorthad, después de todo, el Guardián de los Túmulos. ¿Qué tenía que temer de la niebla que se asentaba sobre los montículos funerarios? ¿No era su gente la que estaba enterrada allí? ¿No eran sus propios ancestros, su propio linaje, sus propios súbditos?\
\
'Si él no podía aliviar su carga y devolverles la paz, ¿quién podría? Mientras escribo esto, me descubro esperando, contra toda esperanza, que el Señor de Tyrn Gorthad pudiera poner fin a ello. Pero este ha sido mi estudio de toda una vida, y sé cómo termina este relato... y no termina con Amondir, pese a todo su valor y su deber.'","Este lugar coincide con la descripción que te dio Handarod","Habla con Meneldir en las zonas surorientales de Tyrn Gorthad","Contempla la imagen de Amondir","Libro 3, Capítulo 7: La Ruptura de Arnor","La escritura es tan evocadora que casi puedes imaginar al Rey Tarondor II allí.","El diario de Narndir contiene un relato de la Batalla del Monte de los Muertos, y describe un sendero claro en el lado norte de la colina que permite a los viajeros acercarse bastante al monumento en lo alto de Amon Firn.\
\
Debes viajar al lugar descrito por el diario y leer las páginas correspondientes cuando estés allí.","La escritura de Narndir habla de terribles hechos cometidos por fuerzas de gran maldad entre los túmulos de Tyrn Gorthad.","'Arthedain, Cardolan y Rhudaur estuvieron envueltos en sangrientos combates durante casi todos los años de su existencia, escribe Narndir, pero pocas batallas tuvieron un costo como la Batalla del Monte de los Muertos.\
\
'Cuatrocientos años después de que el odiado Eldamacil diera muerte a su hermano Tarondor, otro rey de Rhudaur marchó profundamente en el reino de Cardolan. Fue el rey Malgun quien rompió las puertas de Caranost al frente de un ejército de montañeses. Gran parte de la familia real fue asesinada ese día, pero Malgun no pudo encontrar al Rey Artandil; al percibir que su fuerza estaba a punto de sobrepasarse, el Rey de Rhudaur y sus ejércitos huyeron por las Quebradas del Sur.\
\
'Enloquecido por su pena, el Rey Artandil los persiguió, y por fin los soldados de Cardolan alcanzaron a los Rhudaurrim que huían en una colina entre los túmulos. Se dice que lucharon con tal fiereza que la sangre corrió por los costados de la colina en grandes arroyos, y los cuerpos llenaron las hondonadas a sus pies, y cuando terminó la lucha tanto Artandil como Malgun estaban muertos, habiéndose dado el golpe mortal el uno al otro.\
\
'La colina se conoce hoy como el Monte de los Muertos. Flores rojas brotaron allí desde entonces, y lo hacen hasta el día de hoy. Arranqué una de estas flores una tarde nublada, cuando el cielo estaba gris y parecía que pronto llovería, aunque nunca llovió. Incluyo la flor en mi diario; será un recordatorio de que puede haber belleza incluso en la tristeza.'\
\
Una marchita flor roja está colocada entre dos hojas del diario de Narndir, y cruje al pasar las páginas.","Los trasgos y semiorcos hablan en voz baja acerca de algo llamado el Miedo Gris, un aparente servidor del Rey Brujo responsable de algún mal terrible en los años posteriores a la caída de Arnor.","Meneldir se encuentra cerca, contemplando los túmulos de Tyrn Gorthad.","La escritura de Narndir es tan evocadora que casi puedes imaginar al Rey Tarondor II presente en la sala del trono que estableció en Caranost tras la ruptura de Arnor.","'¿Narndir escribe sobre un sendero claro en la cara norte del Monte de los Muertos? Ese es Amon Firn, ${PLAYER}... un lugar peligroso, muy al este.'","'¿Qué tiene que decir Malenfang sobre esto?'","Este parece ser el lugar del que Narndir escribió","Lee el diario de Narndir mientras estés cerca de la cima de Amon Firn, subiendo por el sendero ubicado en el lado norte de la colina","Lee el diario de Narndir"},
[2092]={"Aragorn se encuentra en una de las habitaciones de invitados de la Casa de Elrond en Rivendel, que se halla en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Halbarad te ha pedido que lleves noticias de la invasión de las Quebradas del Norte a su jefe, Aragorn, y que obtengas su consejo.","'Ya, un grupo de Hombres, Enanos y Elfos mantiene un sector de los campos frente a Fornost.'","'Muchos desafíos esperan a los pueblos del Norte en los días venideros.'","'¡Ojalá pudiera estar allí para ayudar en estos asuntos! Pero parece que mi destino está al sur y no al norte. Compondré un mensaje para Halbarad y le pediré al Maestro Elrond si uno de sus Elfos podría llevarlo a Esteldín.\
\
'Has hecho lo suficiente, ¡y tienes mi agradecimiento! Por ahora, toma el descanso que puedas aquí en Rivendel.'","'Desearía poder estar en Esteldín para liderar a mis hombres, pero, ay, mi destino está en el sur.'","'Mientras espero la llegada de quienes acudirán al Consejo, debo pedirte una última tarea. Mi jefe, Aragorn, debe ser informado de lo sucedido aquí.\
\
'También desearía contar con su consejo, ya que la posición en la que me encuentro es inusual. Aragorn siempre ha sido quien lidera, organiza e inspira. ¡Si tan solo el asunto que está atendiendo no fuera de mayor importancia, él estaría aquí!\
\
'Sin embargo, no puede ser de otra manera. Para ahora, Aragorn debería haber llegado al refugio de Rivendel en el Bosque de los Trolls. Te espera un duro viaje, pero debes llevarle a Aragorn noticias de estos asuntos. Búscalo en una de las habitaciones de invitados de la Casa de Elrond.'","'Se contarán historias de tus hazañas, amigo mío. El nombre de ${PLAYER} no será olvidado.'","'Quienes luchan contra Angmar en Fornost podrían necesitar tu fuerza, si estás dispuesto a ayudarlos.'","Habla con Aragorn en Rivendel.","Los Elfos, Hombres y Enanos de las Quebradas del Norte han acordado asistir al Consejo de Esteldín, pero el jefe de Halbarad aún no ha sido informado de los acontecimientos que han tenido lugar allí.","'Mi jefe, Aragorn, debe ser informado de lo sucedido aquí. Por favor, llévale noticias en Rivendel, el refugio de Elrond el Medio Elfo que se encuentra en el Bosque de los Trolls. Es un largo viaje, pero necesito su consejo si he de afrontar los días venideros. Lo encontrarás en una de las habitaciones de invitados a lo largo del camino que sube por la ladera sur del Valle de Imladris.'","Libro 3, Capítulo 7: El Consejo Reunido","'Este Consejo se ha reunido gracias a ti. Estoy muy agradecido por tus esfuerzos.'"},
[2093]={"'My brother is already searching for adventure throughout the city, ${PLAYER}. We will find him and seek this weapon together!'","'Our enemies have brought a great weapon to Osgiliath, a mighty ram that bears the name 'Grond.' The message you recovered is addressed from Gothmog to 'the master of the great beasts,' and it commands this master to pull the ram through the city to the West-gate. We must assume that Gothmog or his superiors plan to use Grond to smash the gates of Minas Tirith.\
\
'We have to stop it! If this message has not been delivered by another of Gothmog's runners, we have a brief window available to us before Grond begins to move once more. This hunter from the Blackroot Vale has been itching for a chance to prove himself. Take him and find Grond before it leaves the city, and damage or destroy the ram before it reaches the Pelennor. Once it leaves Osgiliath we will not be able to halt its progress, ${PLAYER}!'","Book 3, Chapter 8: Gothmog Appears","'What is wrong? Is everything all right?'","Talk to Damrod among the Osgiliath Culverts","'You look as if you have seen a ghost, ${PLAYER}, and if that terrible apparition's words are to be believed, mayhap you have!\
\
'Is it true? Was this creature spared death? How can we hope to fight against such foes, if even a true strike with a keen blade cannot cure them of this existence?'\
\
You ask Derufin that he not tell anyone of Gothmog's words, and he nods his assent, if reluctantly.\
\
'I suppose that is for the best, but I do not like it. If the armies we face are led by creatures that cannot die, how long must we be expected to fight? How long must we stand, ${PLAYER}? I hope you understand that I am not afraid, but my brother is not as brave as I am, and I fear that he will not be willing to go on endlessly without victory.'","Derufin can be found among the Osgiliath Culverts beneath the city.\
\
Damrod has asked you and Derufin to find the great ram, Grond, and damage or destroy it before it is pulled out of Osgiliath into the Pelennor.","You managed to damage Grond, but learned an unsettling truth about the identity of Gothmog, a commander of the forces in Osgiliath.","'${PLAYER}! Derufin tells me that you were able to do some damage to the great ram, and it will be some time before Grond can be used against Minas Tirith. Why then has the colour drained from your face, and why do you bear that stricken expression?'\
\
The thought of telling Damrod the truth weighs heavily upon you, but you know that the soldier already struggles on with very little hope. To tell him that the leaders of the Enemy's armies cannot be defeated in battle, and that death holds no permanence for such creatures of evil, would dash away any of his hopes that remain.\
\
'Cheer up, ${PLAYER}. Your efforts have bought the defenders of Minas Tirith some time, and those extra hours, however brief, might prove the difference. Evil cannot fight forever. Faramir will be found, and our battles will be won! Get some rest if you can, ${PLAYER}. Soon we will look to joining the defenders of the White City, and our battle will begin anew. But for now you have done well.'\
\
Damrod smiles heartily at you, but you think of the foe that was once Mordirith, and your heart is heavy.","Talk to Derufin among the Osgiliath Culverts and go with him to search for Grond","Talk to Derufin among the Osgiliath Culverts","Damrod is with his men among the culverts beneath Osgiliath.","The forces of the Enemy have brought a terrible weapon to Osgiliath, and you must destroy it before it can be used against Minas Tirith."},
[2094]={"Habla con Handarod en Sírlond","'¡Ahí estás! He estado hablando con Gorwen, una Montaraz que ha asumido la tarea de vigilar Dol Ernil, y ambos estamos interesados en saber si has aprendido algo más del diario de Narndir. Ella no lo conoció en vida, así que le he contado historias de nuestra infancia. Es... es bueno recordar, debo admitirlo. Pero ¿qué has aprendido?'\
\
Le entregas a Meneldir el diario y, siguiendo tus indicaciones, lee varias de sus páginas.\
\
'Ahí está de nuevo: el Miedo Gris. Hay más que aprender sobre este enemigo, lo sé. ¡Pero escucha esto! \\qEl plan de batalla de Angmar era triple, pero el Príncipe Ostir entendió demasiado tarde que más que Amon Sûl estaba en peligro; cabalgó al norte en defensa de la Cima de los Vientos con la mayoría de su escolta, y solo cuando el cielo del sur se llenó de humo de un gran incendio se percató de que Cardolan había sido devastado durante su ausencia. Luchó la Batalla de la Cima de los Vientos con los ojos empañados de lágrimas, y solo cuando terminó le dio su Rey permiso para regresar. Galopó con la máxima urgencia de vuelta a Dol Ernil, pero no estaba preparado para la visión que lo aguardaba en la sala del trono.\\q\
\
'Estas páginas hablan de la sala del trono de Dol Ernil. Allí deberías leer el resto del relato, ${PLAYER}. Gorwen me dice que la sala del trono está al norte de aquí, y subida por varias escaleras.'","Orcos, semiorcos o trasgos en las Quebradas del Sur o en Páramo Rojizo pueden haber robado las páginas perdidas del diario de Narndir, y deberías recuperarlas si puedes.","'Deberíamos volver a Sírlond para hablar con Handarod sobre esto. Él conocía la ubicación donde Narndir guardó este diario. Quizá sepa por qué se retiraron algunas páginas.'","Meneldir te espera en el campamento de Gorwen, al sur de Dol Ernil, para tu regreso tras investigar en la fortaleza.","'¿Meneldir dijo que se reuniría contigo justo al sur de Dol Ernil, en Tyrn Gorthad? Ten cuidado... ese lugar ha sido de mal agüero durante cientos de años.'","La escritura es tan evocadora que casi puedes imaginar la terrible visión que aguardaba al Príncipe Ostir","Una pequeña caja reposa aquí, pero su cerradura está rota y está rodeada de huellas de orco","Has restaurado el diario de Narndir, y quizá ahora puedas descubrir por qué se retiraron páginas de él.","Lee el diario restaurado de Narndir","Los escritos de Narndir han evocado la imagen del Miedo Gris para inquietar tu mente.","'Estas páginas hablan de la sala del trono de Dol Ernil. Es allí donde deberías leer el resto del relato, ${PLAYER}. Gorwen me dice que está al norte, subiendo varias escaleras.'","Libro 3, Capítulo 8: Los Últimos Días de Cardolan","La mesa de la Granja de Scurloc servirá como buen lugar de trabajo para reensamblar el diario de Narndir.","Contempla la imagen del Miedo Gris","'Deberías buscar en esa ruina cuadrada junto al camino en Páramo Rojizo. Tal vez encuentres algo que arroje luz sobre este misterio.'","Has reunido las páginas perdidas del diario de Narndir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Puede que hayas encontrado otro escondite secreto de Narndir, pero es posible que los orcos o sus aliados lo encontraran primero.","'Para cuando por fin llegó a Dol Ernil', escribe Narndir, 'la fortaleza del Príncipe Ostir era una cáscara en ruinas. Su gente yacía amontonada y ensangrentada en las calles, las cabezas de sus defensores clavadas en estacas sobre las puertas. De su madre Luilloth no había señal alguna. Y en el salón destrozado, sentado en el trono de Ostir, estaba el Miedo Gris.\
\
'Dudo en escribir lo que he aprendido, pero debo hacerlo. ¡Debo! Mi deber me obliga a escribirlo, a escribir la verdad. ¿Pero está bien poner en palabras tal horror, tal vergüenza? Lucho conmigo mismo.\
\
'El Príncipe Ostir estuvo en la casa de muerte que era Dol Ernil, miró a los ojos de la criatura que se sentaba en el trono y supo la identidad del Miedo Gris. Era el Príncipe Amondir quien estaba allí, el propio abuelo de Ostir, pero el servidor del mal que lo miraba era un extraño por completo. Con una sonrisa horrible en su rostro burlón, la aparición levantó la mano y señaló al nieto aterrorizado de Amondir.\
\
'Y los Muertos se alzaron.'","Handarod vio una vez a Narndir comportarse de manera extraña cerca de una ruina cuadrada solitaria junto al camino en Páramo Rojizo, al noroeste de Herne.","Busca la extraña ruina cuadrada junto al camino en Páramo Rojizo donde Handarod vio una vez a Narndir comportarse de forma extraña","'Narndir estaba en el Vado de Sarn cuando los Jinetes Negros atacaron, ${PLAYER}, y huyó, como hicieron los demás Dúnedain. Encontramos su cuerpo no muy lejos del Camino Verde, y pensé que quizá se dirigía a los lugares de reunión de su gente. Pero ¿y si no fue así? ¿Y si en cambio iba hacia la solitaria ruina cuadrada que se alza más al sur junto al Camino Verde? Me pregunto...\
\
'Creo que vio el regreso de los espectros y creyó que el Miedo Gris volvería a rondar sus antiguas tierras, Cardolan de antaño. Creo que corría para recuperar las páginas arrancadas de su diario, ${PLAYER}, para que los Dúnedain supieran el terror al que podrían enfrentarse. Quiso armarlos con el conocimiento de lo que podrían hallar, pero fue abatido por los Jinetes Negros, por los Nazgûl, antes de poder llegar al lugar donde escondió el verdadero relato.\
\
'Creo que Narndir conocía el peligro, y murió tratando de advertirnos: el Señor de los Nazgûl planea despertar al Miedo Gris de su letargo, poniendo en peligro a todo el norte.'","Abre la pequeña caja de madera y busca las páginas perdidas del diario de Narndir","La caja de madera está vacía, ya saqueada de su contenido por orcos, semiorcos o trasgos","Las páginas rasgadas encajan a la perfección, y el diario de Narndir ha sido restaurado","Handarod está en Sírlond, el campamento élfico al otro lado del río desde Caranost.\
\
Meneldir se pregunta si Handarod sabrá qué ocurrió con las páginas perdidas del diario de Narndir.","Meneldir te dijo que se reuniría contigo frente a Dol Ernil tras aprender lo que pudieras del diario de Narndir.","'Tras las páginas faltantes, Narndir escribe sobre Dol Ernil, la fortaleza desde la cual gobernaba el Príncipe Amondir. Yo me adelantaré y veré qué puedo aprender allí, pero creo que deberías volver a Sírlond para hablar con Handarod. Él conocía la ubicación del diario. Quizá sepa por qué se retiraron algunas páginas. Si resuelves ese misterio, me reuniré contigo nuevamente frente a Dol Ernil.'","Narndir describe la muerte de Ostir, Último Príncipe de Cardolan, con tal detalle que su relato dolería a cualquier amigo de los Dúnedain o de su pueblo.","'¿Criaturas orcas han saqueado el cofre secreto de Narndir? No faltan esas bestias en las Quebradas del Sur, pero si hallarás lo que buscas entre orcos, semiorcos o trasgos, no puedo decirlo.'","'Los tumularios solo esperaban la orden de su amo', escribe Narndir. 'Ahora surgieron de entre los muertos, incluyendo algunos recién caídos en la reciente batalla, y se lanzaron sobre Ostir y sus caballeros. Preso del pánico, el Príncipe huyó de la fortaleza en llamas, escapando a las Quebradas de los Túmulos, pero tanto daba huir del martillo como correr hacia el yunque. Los Angmarim lo aguardaban allí en emboscada, y entre ellos había montañeses, orcos y cultistas del Rey Brujo. Los Muertos condujeron a la menguante compañía de Ostir directamente hacia esa fuerza enemiga, y allí en la oscuridad, atrapados entre vivos y muertos, murió hasta el último defensor de Cardolan. El Príncipe Ostir pereció al final, sollozando de desesperación mientras uno de los guerreros de Carn Dûm le clavaba una lanza de hierro frío en el corazón. Sus huesos, y los de su compañía, desaparecieron entre las colinas.\
\
'¡Lo he escrito! ¿Es esto lo que querías de mí? ¡Lo he terminado! Mi deber está cumplido... pero el relato es demasiado terrible. Arrancaré estas páginas de mi diario y las esconderé. Sí, que nadie sepa cuán gravemente fallaron los Hombres de Cardolan. Enterraré la victoria del Rey Brujo tan profundamente como pueda enterrarse, y así triunfaré sobre Angmar yo mismo. El Miedo Gris no se ha visto en cientos de años, y no le daré vida permitiendo que este relato sea leído por nadie. Si en los días venideros existe necesidad de estas páginas, las recuperaré yo mismo. Pero no veo tal día frente a nosotros, y eso es una bendición.'","Muestra el diario de Narndir a Meneldir justo al sur de Dol Ernil, en Tyrn Gorthad","Lee el diario de Narndir junto al trono en Dol Ernil","Lleva el diario de Narndir a Meneldir en el campamento de Gorwen, al sur de Dol Ernil","Vuelve a ensamblar el diario de Narndir en la mesa de la Granja de Scurloc","Varias de las páginas siguientes han sido arrancadas del diario. ¿Fueron retiradas por Narndir o por otra mano, y con qué propósito?","Recoge las páginas perdidas del diario de Narndir de los orcos, semiorcos o trasgos en las Quebradas del Sur o Páramo Rojizo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El diario de Narndir describe la sala del trono de Dol Ernil, ubicada al norte del campamento de Gorwen y por varias escalinatas arriba.\
\
Deberías viajar al lugar descrito por el diario y leer allí las páginas correspondientes.","'¿Páginas perdidas? No puedo decir que sepa nada de eso, ${PLAYER}, pero no creo que Narndir arrancara páginas de su propio diario. Alguien más debió retirarlas... aunque no puedo imaginar por qué tal persona devolvería el diario a su escondite.'\
\
Handarod se frota la mejilla, pensando profundamente.\
\
'Hubo un día en que hablé con Narndir y noté que actuaba de manera muy extraña. Lo encontré en el Camino Verde, no lejos de la ruina cuadrada solitaria junto al camino al noroeste de Herne. Ahora que lo pienso, su actitud era muy peculiar, y parecía no ser él mismo. ¿Qué dijo? Algo extraño me dijo, ¡pero no puedo recordarlo!\
\
'Si él retiró páginas de su diario, lo cual no era en absoluto propio de él, ese sería el único día en que lo creería. Ojalá pudiera recordar lo que dijo, pero quizá lo recuerde luego. Deberías buscar en esa ruina cuadrada junto al camino en Páramo Rojizo. Tal vez encuentres algo que arroje luz sobre este misterio.'","Este parece ser el lugar del que Narndir escribió","Meneldir te devuelve el diario","Contempla la muerte de Ostir, Último Príncipe de Cardolan, tal como la describen los escritos de Narndir"},
[2095]={"Meneldir está en el campamento de Gorwen al sur de Dol Ernil, interesado en oír de tus logros por Tyrn Gorthad.","'${PLAYER}, no me he olvidado de ti, ni de la advertencia que nos trajiste sobre Saruman. Permíteme tranquilizar tu mente: parece que él es el único de los Magos que nos traicionó, ¡y agradezcamos a los Poderes que sea así!\
\
'Mientras estabas fuera, un jinete llegó desde el sur: Gandalf el Gris, montado en un poderoso caballo, ¡un corcel de Rohan! Hablamos brevemente, pero fue suficiente para asegurarme de que Gandalf sigue del lado de los Pueblos Libres. Y sin embargo, no todas sus noticias fueron alegres, pues dijo que fuerzas malignas están en movimiento y podrían amenazar la paz y seguridad de toda la Tierra Media; no podía perder más tiempo antes de apresurarse hacia la Comarca en persecución de los Nazgûl que lo precedían.\
\
'Pero ¿qué te trae de vuelta a este lugar?'\
\
Le cuentas brevemente a Halbarad lo que has aprendido del Miedo Gris y que Gorwen y Meneldir creen que aún permanece oculto en algún lugar dentro de la fortaleza de Dol Ernil.\
\
'Estas espadas que me traes serán destruidas, pues las runas que cubren sus hojas son malignas, pero después de encargarme de eso deberás regresar a Dol Ernil. Sí, y no solo: yo y varios de los míos iremos contigo. ¡Temo que los dos que quedaron allí corran gran peligro!'","'Le contaré a Gorwen lo que hemos aprendido de nuestros enemigos, pero ella ha vigilado Dol Ernil durante más tiempo que nosotros. Te sugiero que le preguntes qué es necesario hacer en la fortaleza y en el arruinado Tyrn Gorthad. Veo la mano del Rey Brujo por todas partes, y debemos oponernos a ella, si podemos hacerlo.'","El hedor de muerte y descomposición llena tus fosas nasales al acercarte a esta esquina","Libro 3, Capítulo 9: Muerte en las Quebradas de los Túmulos","Habla con Gorwen en su campamento al sur de Dol Ernil, en Tyrn Gorthad","Recolecta espadas ancestrales entre las ruinas de Tyrn Gorthad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Halbarad sugirió que ambos regresáramos al campamento de Gorwen al sur de Dol Ernil.","'Creo que el Miedo Gris permanece en algún lugar dentro de Dol Ernil... pero ¿dónde?'","Crébain, sabandijas o hombres demacrados derrotados en Tyrn Gorthad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Esto es lo que temía, ${PLAYER}. ¿Algún mal vino a ellos, o partieron imprudentemente en su búsqueda?\
\
'Gorwen, al menos, tendría el sentido de esperar hasta tu regreso, pero de Meneldir no puedo decir lo mismo. Ha huido de su deber antes. ¿No podría hacerlo de nuevo hoy?'","Regresa al campamento de Gorwen al sur de Dol Ernil, en Tyrn Gorthad","El aire bajo la mesa de piedra se siente viciado y estancado","'Esas espadas deberían ser llevadas a Halbarad en el Vado de Sarn, ${PLAYER}. Él sabrá cómo tratarlas, y cuando regreses quizá sepamos dónde encontrar al Miedo Gris. Coincido con Gorwen: la criatura debe estar en algún lugar dentro de Dol Ernil.'\
\
Le dices a Meneldir que tenga cuidado, pues el diario de Narndir pinta un relato aterrador y mortal de la criatura que trajo la muerte a Cardolan y a la línea de sus príncipes.\
\
'Lo haré, seré prudente, no temas. Te veré cuando regreses.'","El Rey Brujo ha obrado gran mal en Tyrn Gorthad, y los Montaraces necesitan tu ayuda para oponerse a sus siervos y a sus oscuros propósitos.","Habla con Halbarad en el campamento de Gorwen al sur de Dol Ernil","'Estas espadas que me traes serán destruidas, pues las runas que cubren sus hojas son malignas, pero después de encargarme de eso deberás regresar a Dol Ernil. Sí, y no solo: yo y varios de los míos iremos contigo. ¡Temo que los dos que quedaron allí corran gran peligro!'","Un aura de temor aprieta tu corazón al acercarte al muro occidental","Tumularios derrotados en Tyrn Gorthad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ve ahora, ${PLAYER}. Te veré cuando regreses.'","Halbarad está en el Vado de Sarn.\
\
Meneldir te pidió que llevaras las espadas ancestrales que recuperaste a Halbarad para que puedan ser destruidas y su mal disminuido.","Lleva las espadas ancestrales a Halbarad para que sean destruidas","Gorwen está en su campamento al sur de Dol Ernil, en Tyrn Gorthad.\
\
Meneldir te pidió que vieras qué ayuda necesita Gorwen para combatir los males de Tyrn Gorthad.","'No es poca hazaña enfrentar los peligros de Tyrn Gorthad y la fortaleza de Dol Ernil, ${PLAYER}. Estoy agradecida por tus esfuerzos en nombre de los Dúnedain.\
\
'Meneldir me ha mostrado el relato en el diario de Narndir sobre el Miedo Gris, y si lo que escribió el erudito es cierto, la criatura es un espíritu surgido de las fosas de Angmar, ligado al cuerpo del Príncipe Amondir. En vida fue el Señor de Tyrn Gorthad, y Dol Ernil fue su hogar. Sin duda este lugar aún tendrá significado para él. ¿Permanece el Miedo Gris dentro de la fortaleza, o la presencia del Rey Brujo y los jinetes de negro ya ha perturbado su letargo?'","Gorwen te dio varias tareas que ayudarán a combatir los males de Tyrn Gorthad.","Un peso desagradable reposa pesadamente sobre las piedras bajo el muro imponente","Habla con Meneldir en el campamento de Gorwen al sur de Dol Ernil","Derrota tumularios en Tyrn Gorthad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Halbarad y algunos de los suyos han llegado al campamento de Gorwen en Tyrn Gorthad, pero tanto Meneldir como Gorwen ya han desaparecido. ¿Han ido a enfrentarse solos al mal?","Derrota crébain, sabandijas o hombres demacrados en Tyrn Gorthad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Espectros acechan Tyrn Gorthad, y hay otras amenazas peligrosas: crébain espías, sabandijas pestilentes y hombres demacrados entre los túmulos. Cada uno causa problemas a los Dúnedain y a sus aliados. Hay espadas dentro de la fortaleza y fuera que desprenden auras aterradoras de maldad, y deben ser reunidas y destruidas pese a sus terribles guardianes. ¿Puede hacerse todo esto?'","Espada ancestral recuperada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gorwen aguarda tu regreso en su campamento al sur de Dol Ernil, en Tyrn Gorthad.","Meneldir y Gorwen se han ido","'Soy más joven que Meneldir por algunos años. Aunque ambos crecimos en el Ángulo del Mitheithel, no lo conocí antes de que nos dejara. Su nombre siempre se decía en susurros, una advertencia a los niños de que no todos debían tomar el juramento, que no todos debían comprometerse a la vida de un Dúnadan.'\
\
Meneldir suspira pesadamente, y Gorwen alza una mano enguantada.\
\
'¡No pretendo herir tus sentimientos, Meneldir! Lo que quiero decir es esto: esperaba un monstruo. Cuando llegaste a mi campamento pensé que debías estar huyendo de dificultades, escapando de algún problema causado por ti mismo. Tales eran las historias que nos contaban en la infancia. Pero en lugar de ello, veo que eres un hombre, no un monstruo, y luchas en nombre de quienes no pueden, dispuesto incluso a regresar con tus antiguos parientes para advertirles, aunque te hieran con lenguas afiladas. Veo honor en eso.\
\
'Pero ahí fuera sí hay monstruos, ${PLAYER}, monstruos de verdad. No necesito oír el relato completo del amigo caído de Meneldir para saberlo, pues ya lo sabía, aunque no en su verdadera extensión o profundidad. Espectros acechan en Tyrn Gorthad, y hay otras amenazas peligrosas: crébain espías, sabandijas pestilentes y hombres demacrados que merodean entre los túmulos. Cada uno causa problemas a los Dúnedain y a sus aliados en estas tierras. Hay espadas tanto dentro de la fortaleza como fuera que desprenden auras aterradoras de maldad, y deben ser recolectadas y destruidas, pese a la presencia de sus terribles guardianes. ¿Puede lograrse todo esto?'"},
[2096]={"'Esteldín envía un mensaje para que vayas allí y te reúnas con Halbarad. Date prisa, porque los fuegos de los orcos arden con fuerza y cada momento que perdemos es otra oportunidad para el Enemigo.'","Sigue el camino hacia el oeste hasta llegar a la Posada Abandonada. Candaith está en un campamento al norte de la Posada Abandonada, al noroeste de la Cima de los Vientos.\
\
Frideric te dijo que un Montaraz desea hablar contigo sobre asuntos urgentes.","Halbarad está en las Quebradas del Norte, al norte de Meluinen.\
\
El amigo Montaraz de Candaith necesita ayuda con urgencia.","'¿Esteldín? Si te necesitan, debes ir. Cuídate, amigo.'","Libro 3, Prólogo: Fuegos en el Norte","'Se ha corrido la voz sobre la ayuda que has prestado a los Montaraces del sur. Aquí, en las tierras del norte, necesitamos tu ayuda más que nunca.'","'He recibido un mensaje de un Hombre. ¿Lo conoces? Es un Montaraz llamado Candaith.\
\
'Los detalles son vagos, pero parece de gran importancia que hables con él. Creo que se trata de los movimientos del Enemigo en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
'Está en un campamento al noroeste de la Cima de los Vientos. Ve hacia el oeste hasta la Posada Abandonada y luego hacia el norte hasta llegar a su campamento.'","Orcos del norte están arrasando las Quebradas del Norte y poniendo todo a fuego y sangre a su paso.","'Deberías ir a ver a Candaith.'","'Ve a Esteldín y reúnte con Halbarad. No hay tiempo que perder.'"},
[2097]={"'I will meet you in the Starkmoor, ${PLAYER}, by the large farm in the north-western reaches. Then we will scout the state of the herds for Lheu Brenin.'","Nona is by the farmland in the north-western reaches of the Starkmoor.\
\
You scouted the farmland in the north-western Starkmoor and should speak with Nona.","Talk to Nona in the Starkmoor","'Danger seems to follow you wherever you go, ${PLAYER}. I like that. I will be Wadu's Ghost and defeat the true enemies of Dunland: faithless clans who swear loyalty to Saruman.\
\
'The land to the west is called the Starkmoor. You say that Lheu Brenin wished to know the state of its herds? There are many herd-animals in the Starkmoor, and he who controls them will have much food production close at hand. Enough for an army? Aye.\
\
'There is a farmhouse in the north-west corner of the Starkmoor, among the hills. I have seen it from afar. I will meet you there, and we can scout for the information Lheu Brenin desires to know.'","There is a farmhouse in the north-western corner of the Starkmoor.\
\
Nona wants you to scout the farmhouse atop the slope to the west to see if it is held by those loyal to Saruman.","Scout the sheep-enclosure","Nona is by the farmhouse in the north-western reaches of Starkmoor.\
\
Nona has agreed to meet you in the Starkmoor to scout for the information Lheu Brenin needs.","'I think this is what Lheu Brenin feared, ${PLAYER}. The farms of the Starkmoor are not held by friendly clansmen any longer.\
\
'The main trading settlement to the south may be similar, but we will not know it without going there.'","Book 4, Chapter 10: Herdsmen of the Starkmoor","The farmhouse has been abandoned by its rightful owners","Some of the sheep have been killed and left to rot","Scout the planted field","Scout the farmhouse atop the north-western hill","Nona has agreed to accompany you on your information-gathering journey through Dunland for Lheu Brenin.","'The farmhouse to the west may be held by those loyal to Saruman. You should investigate and see if it be so.'","'The herds of the Starkmoor feed many of the clans of Dunland. If this farmland is held by those loyal to Saruman, he will have a source of food for his armies, but can also starve those who oppose him.\
\
'Go up to the farmhouse at the top of the slope to the west and see how things stand, ${PLAYER}. You should also scout some of the fields and enclosures nearby, to the west.'","The field is full of grains, planted but yet to be harvested"},
[2098]={"Complete 'The Defence of Minas Tirith' from the Epic Battles Panel","Mithrandir is in the besieged city, at the south-eastern area of the Second Circle.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>","'The enemy forces assault the wall! Prepare to repel them, no matter the cost!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Defence of Minas Tirith' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","The city of Minas Tirith is besieged, and the forces of Mordor assault the wall.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Defence of Minas Tirith' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","'The fighting is fierce, but the enemy has not yet broken our line. Stand, soldiers of Gondor! Do not give in to fear!\
\
'They must be strong. This is the hour, ${PLAYER}!'","'To me, soldiers of Gondor! The enemy forces assault the wall! Prepare to repel them, no matter the cost!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Defence of Minas Tirith' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","Prince Imrahil rallies the defenders of Minas Tirith as the forces of Mordor assault the walls of the city.","Book 4, Chapter 10: The Defence of Minas Tirith","Talk to Mithrandir in the besieged city, at the south-eastern area of the Second Circle"},
[2099]={"Complete 'Hammer of the Underworld' from the Epic Battles Panel","Mithrandir is in the besieged city, at the south-eastern area of the Second Circle.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>","The city of Minas Tirith is besieged, and the great ram Grond creeps closer to the gate.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Hammer of the Underworld' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","'The enemy has repaired the great ram Grond, ${PLAYER}. Great beasts pull it across the Pelennor, creeping ever closer to the city. It must not reach the gate!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>To participate in the defence, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Hammer of the Underworld' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.</rgb>","'A terrible crash! Grond has served its purpose, ${PLAYER}. The spells woven about its length have proven too much for the gates of the city! The darkest hour is at hand.'","Mithrandir rallies the defenders of Minas Tirith as the great ram Grond creeps ever close to the gates of the city.","Book 4, Chapter 11: Hammer of the Underworld","Talk to Mithrandir in the besieged city, at the south-eastern area of the Second Circle"},
[2100]={"'The people of the Starkmoor are on the tipping point, ${PLAYER}. If we can help its people, we may be able to deprive Saruman of the food he needs to feed his armies.\
\
'Travel south to Avardin and help the people there and all throughout the Starkmoor. It may prove the difference in this region.\
\
'Once you are satisfied that you have done all you can to help the people of the Starkmoor, I will meet you where the road passes from the Starkmoor to the Dunbog in the south by a great stone arch, and we will continue our journey together.'","'I am glad you are here. The Dunbog is just ahead.'","Nona is along the road that runs south out of the Starkmoor into the Dunbog, near a natural arch of stone.\
\
Nona has asked you to help the people of the Starkmoor with their problems, especially at Avardin to the south, and to meet her by the road into the Dunbog when you are satisfied.","'Help the people of the Starkmoor as much as you can, ${PLAYER}, especially south of here, at Avardin. We must keep them from allying with Saruman if we can.\
\
'Once you have helped them to your satisfaction, meet me by the road south into the Dunbog from the Starkmoor. There is a great stone arch over the road. That is where I will meet you.'","Book 4, Chapter 11: Into the Dunbog","You should help the people of the Starkmoor before moving south to meet Nona in the Dunbog.","Help the people of the Starkmoor as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Nona by the road into Dunbog"},
[2101]={"Talk to Nona in the Dunbog","'Do you see the scout up ahead, by the large rocky outcropping? I do not know to what clan she belongs. Go see if she is friendly, ${PLAYER}. The people of the Dunbog keep to themselves, and I know little of them, but if Saruman has paid for their loyalty, they are already our enemies.'","The scout stares at you warily, but does not attack","'Scout ahead and see if that look-out is friendly to us. I know little of the Dunbog and do not know what we should expect.'","Judging from the symbols that decorate their camp, these Men are of the Avanc-lûth clan","You have come to the outskirts of the Dunbog on Lheu Brenin's information-gathering errand.","Book 4, Chapter 12: Outliers","Nona is to the north of the rocky outcropping that marks the boundary between the Starkmoor and the Dunbog.\
\
You have scouted the border of the Dunbog and should return to Nona.","Determine whether the scout by the rocky outcropping is friendly","A Dunlending-scout is by the large rocky outcropping that stands by the entrance to the Dunbog, and to the south-west of her is a small camp belonging to her people.","Scout the small camp of Dunlendings south-west of the rocky outcropping","'These people are like my own, ${PLAYER}: they are outliers, on the edge of great danger but not given in to it. May they resist as well as my people have done!\
\
'We must help the Avanc-lûth to stand against Saruman.'"},
[2102]={"'Hullo there, ${PLAYER}. How was your audience with the Steward?'\
\
At the sound of the young hobbit's voice, a tremendous smile brightens your face and you fight the urge to clasp Pippin in a tight embrace.\
\
'What is the joke, ${PLAYER}? I've never seen you this happy! It's a little peculiar, if you ask me, this being war-time and all, but I suppose that's no reason not to look on the bright side, is it?\
\
'You do seem a little flustered, now that I think about it: both happy and sad at the same time, if that makes any sense. I saw you not ten minutes ago, when the Steward summoned you before him. What could you have talked about in so short a time that would work such a change in you?'","Mithrandir is in the besieged city, at the south-eastern area of the Second Circle.\
\
Grond has broken the gate, and now Mithrandir seeks to confront the Witch-king before that terrible foe can enter the city.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>","'To the gate! We must get to the gate!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Peregrin Took at his post in the Seventh Circle","Talk to Mithrandir in the besieged city and travel with him to the gate","Peregrin Took is in the Seventh Circle of the city, at his post.\
\
You have shaken away the remnants of the terrible prophecy Denethor spoke to you, but you cannot forget the images his words raised in your mind. To convince yourself that it was simply a tale, you should find Peregrin and ensure he is well.","Book 4, Chapter 12: The Darkest Hour","'We have to get down to the gate! Talk to me when you are ready, and we will go with haste!'","It is the darkest hour for Gondor and Middle-earth. Has all hope been lost?"},
[2103]={"Help the people of Dunbog as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Nona in Carreglyn","You should help the people of the Dunbog with their worries, then meet up with Nona in the town of Barnavon, in Carreglyn, when you are satisfied.","Book 4, Chapter 13: Land of Iron","'Help the people of the Dunbog stand against Saruman, ${PLAYER}. If he has forgotten them, they could be the surprise allies we need to make him pay for his crimes against my kin.'","'I am glad to see you, ${PLAYER}! From the swamps of the Dunbog to the rocky crags of Carreglyn, we have endured much already. Each step brings us closer to depriving Saruman of his allies.'","You must help the people of the Dunbog as much as you can, then meet with Nona in Carreglyn.","'The people of the Dunbog have been on the edge of the coming conflict for some time, forgotten by all but their nearest neighbours. Did Saruman factor them into his calculations?\
\
'We must help them resist him, ${PLAYER}! They remind me of my own people, estranged from the other clans, and I do not want them to labour alone. Help them resist the Wizard.\
\
'When you are satisfied that you have done all you can for the people of the Dunbog, travel to Carreglyn. I will meet you in Barnavon, for it seems to be a village of some importance, and Lheu Brenin wanted to learn the status of the mines of iron.'"},
[2104]={"'You should find Mithrandir! I know that he is very worried about the city, and about Gondor, and any information you might have about the Steward's state of mind could be useful to him.'","You have heard Denethor's tale of what he expects from the siege of Minas Tirith, and should convey the Steward's words to Mithrandir before the hour grows too late.","Book 4, Chapter 13: Time Yet Remains","'I understand you had an audience with Denethor, ${PLAYER}. I might have given you some wisdom concerning how to handle the Steward, but I was not consulted. I trust you did not spoil any of our plans, or cause any harm that cannot be undone?'\
\
You tell Mithrandir that Denethor spoke to you of many things that he saw within the depths of a palantír. At that, Mithrandir looks up sharply.\
\
'So the Anor-stone did remain within the tower. I wondered if it was so. Denethor has had a stubborn and strong will for all the years of his life, but if he seeks to gain some advantage over the enemy by using the palantír...'\
\
You interrupt the Wizard, and his initial offence is quickly assuaged as you recount the worrying tale of Denethor's prophetic words concerning the siege to come. Mithrandir is silent for a long while. Finally he speaks.\
\
'I do not think he has seen the siege itself in the Anor-stone, ${PLAYER}, and that is very important to us. A palantír cannot be made to lie, though its images might deceive if the user interprets them incorrectly. But I fear that the future in which Denethor believes, while not certain, could still come to pass. There is a question that his tale raises in my mind, a question I had not fully considered before now.\
\
'Where was Rohan? If the events of the coming siege will indeed transpire as Denethor foretells, and Théoden does not come to the aid of Gondor, I fear that the Steward of Gondor may be right. Minas Tirith will fall.\
\
'It is absolutely imperative that you learn what has happened to the Riders of Rohan. They must come to Minas Tirith in time, or all is lost. The siege is still ahead. Time yet remains.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>To be continued in Volume IV, Book 5, 'The Ride of the Rohirrim.'</rgb>","Mithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Peregrin Took has suggested that you tell Mithrandir about your audience with Denethor, the Steward of Gondor.","Talk to Mithrandir in the Court of the Fountain","'Well, it does not matter. Whatever you and the Steward spoke about, it is not my business to hear! I will do as I am told, and though that may not amount to a great service in the tales of heroes, may it prove as useful and as important as any hobbit deserves!\
\
'But you should find Gandalf! I know that he is very worried about the city, and about Gondor, and any information you might have about the Steward's state of mind could be useful to him. Did I say Gandalf? I mean you should find Mithrandir. I will never get used to calling him that, ${PLAYER}. Why does he need two names, anyway? It's not proper!'\
\
You point out that the young Took himself has two names, going sometimes by Peregrin and sometimes by Pippin.\
\
'Well, that's different. That's different! Ah, you got me. Well-played, ${PLAYER}. Well-played indeed.'"},
[2105]={"Nona is in the village of Barnavon, in Carreglyn.\
\
You have retrieved the bribing gold and should bring it to Nona.","'I have spent some time watching the people of Barnavon, ${PLAYER}. Saruman has paid no small sum of gold to the leaders of Barnavon for their loyalty, and I fear what that might buy him.\
\
'The iron mines of Carreglyn are at stake. The men of the upper village will attack you on sight. Defeat them and take the gold with which they have been bribed. Teach them the true cost of forgetting their honour as Men of Dunland.'","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","Bring the bribing gold to Nona","Book 4, Chapter 14: Bribing Gold","'It took so small a sum to buy the loyalty of these men? A dozen curses upon the Wizard for his crimes, but a thousand upon the Dunlendings for forgetting their honour!'","'What is the price of a Dunlending's honour? It is the amount of gold Saruman gave these fools in return for their loyalty. Defeat them and take back this bribing gold.'","Nona wants you to recover some of the gold that has been paid to Dunlendings by Saruman's agents.","Collect bribing gold from hostile Dunlendings in Carreglyn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Oro para sobornos conseguido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hostile Dunlendings in Barnavon carry the gold with which they were bribed.\
\
Nona wants you to defeat hostile Dunlendings throughout Carreglyn, but especially in the upper village of Barnavon, and take the bribing gold from them."},
[2106]={"'Your journey through Dunland for Lheu Brenin is almost at its end, ${PLAYER}? What have you learned of the Dunlending clans?'\
\
Saeradan listens to your report.\
\
'I see. Saruman's influence is greater than we thought. It is good that you sought to help the people resist him, even if it bears little fruit.\
\
'This man here is Théodred, the son of the king of Rohan. He has crossed into Dunland with a small party on a similar mission: to see what is happening in the heart of Dunland.'","'You should go speak with Saeradan. He has been meeting with the party of Rohirrim that have come to Gravenwood. Their camp is east of here.'","You must help the people of Carreglyn stand against Saruman, if you can, and when you are satisfied, Nona thinks you should meet up with the Rangers in Gravenwood.","'This man is Théodred, son of the king of Rohan. He has come into Dunland with a small party of men to gather information.'","Help the people of Carreglyn as much as you can, and when you are ready to move on, find Amlan on the western border of Gravenwood","'I do not think Carreglyn is lost, ${PLAYER}. There are still good people in this land, strong warriors who did not accept gold from Saruman to fight his battles. Help them as much as you can! If we can aid them, they may stay resolute against the Wizard.\
\
'Just inside the boundary of the Gravenwood, to the east, one of your Ranger friends has established a small camp. Once you have helped the people of Carreglyn to your satisfaction, travel east into Gravenwood and meet up with this Ranger.'","'We are well met, ${PLAYER}! It is good to see a friendly face.\
\
'You should speak with Saeradan. A small band of Rohirrim have come to the Gravenwood, and he is meeting with their leader. Their camp is to the east.'","Talk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp","Talk to Théodred at the Rohirrim scout-camp","Book 4, Chapter 15: Friends in the Gravenwood","'Help the people of Carreglyn to stand against their enemies. We must keep them from falling further under the sway of Saruman.\
\
'Once you have aided them as much as you can, travel east across the border with Gravenwood and meet with the Ranger at his camp.'","The Ranger Amlan is east of Carreglyn, just over the border with Gravenwood.\
\
Nona wants you to help the friendly people of Carreglyn as much as you can and to then meet up with the Rangers in Gravenwood when you are satisfied.","'We are met in dangerous times, ${PLAYER}. You run errands for folk long sworn to be the enemies of my people.'\
\
Théodred sighs heavily.\
\
'It has been a long time since the Dunlendings crossed into my father's kingdom with design of conquest. Without the urging I fear Saruman is giving to them, they would not have the courage to do so again. The Wizard has done my people a great wrong with this, and he must pay for it.\
\
'My men and I forded the Isen and came by animal paths into this wood. That is where we encountered Saeradan and learned of his mission. We could use your help, if you can spare it.'","Théodred is at the Rohirrim scout-camp in Gravenwood.\
\
You have encountered Saeradan again and he has introduced you to Théodred, the son of the king of Rohan.","Saeradan is at the Rohirrim Scout-camp, east of Amlan's camp in Gravenwood.\
\
Amlan told you that a small party of Rohirrim have come to Gravenwood and are meeting with Saeradan."},
[2107]={"Aside from the Dunlendings, you feel no unusual or mysterious presence","Check near the mustering tree for signs of a watchful presence","Théodred's men have felt the watchful presence at an old tree to the north-west of his camp, and in the back of Uvel-cadlus, the Dragon-clan camp to the north.\
\
Théodred wants you to see if you can sense a watchful presence at the places his men experienced such feelings.","The woods remain still and quiet. You feel no presence here","Check in the back of Uvel-cadlus for signs of a watchful presence","Talk to Théodred at the Rohirrim scout-camp","'You felt nothing at those locations? Perhaps my men have been too long in this wood. It is taking a toll on even their stout hearts.'","Book 4, Chapter 16: The Watchful Presence","The stillness of Gravenwood has Théodred and his men on edge, and they have asked for your help to set their minds at ease.","'We are all ill at ease in this forest, ${PLAYER}, and your Ranger friend here is not the reassuring sort. My men have reported feeling a watchful presence as they walk beneath the trees. I do not like it.\
\
'I have heard that Saruman can move about, unseen by mortal eyes. Could it be his presence my men have felt?\
\
'If you oppose the Wizard, go to these places and see if you feel a presence at them, as my men do. One of these places is a gnarled tree to the north-west, and the other is a camp of Dunlendings far to the north, Uvel-cadlus, between the arms of the mountains.'","Théodred is at his camp in the eastern reaches of Gravenwood.\
\
You have sought out the watchful presence in Gravenwood, but did not experience anything unusual.","'Go to those places and see if you feel the watchful presence my men experienced. These are the locations: a gnarled tree to the north-west, and the back of Uvel-cadlus, a camp of Dunlendings far to the north.'"},
[2109]={"'I thought that the captive might tell us more about Saruman's plans if he was hungrier. I told Nai to stop feeding him, but now he has taken ill and will not last much longer.\
\
'Come with me to speak with him before he dies. There will be no more chances to learn what the Wizard is up to behind his walls before it comes to open war.\
\
'We will give him a meal if he cooperates. That may be the encouragement he needs.'","Talk to Lheu Brenin and travel with him to speak with the captive","The emissary from Isengard that Lheu Brenin has imprisoned is not doing well, and the leader of the Falcon-clan wants you to try and learn something of Saruman's plans before the captive dies.","'We will go to speak with the captive and learn what we can of Saruman's plans. He does not have long to live, and we must go now or lose the opportunity.'","Talk to Fâsh in Isengard","'How did you lose the meal given to you by the Falcon-clan? I want it!'","<rgb=#FF0000>If you left the Isengard Depths without the Reminder of Captivity in your inventory, go to the cart just to the right of the gate of Isengard and use it to return to the Depths.</rgb>\
\
You have been taken prisoner and brought to Isengard. The Falcon-clan has betrayed you, and you are now the prisoner of Saruman.","'Make yourself at home, little ${RACE}! You now belong to me and will do as I say!'\
\
Fâsh laughs heartily.\
\
'We will find tasks enough to keep you busy, and once you die, someone else will take your place. Sharkû doesn't lack for thralls, little ${RACE}, and there is plenty of work to be done in the pits!'","Lheu Brenin is outside his home in Tûr Morva.\
\
Lheu Brenin has asked you to come with him to speak with his captive.","Book 4, Chapter 18: The Captive"},
[2110]={"Complete 'Heavy Lifting' for your Uruk-hai overseer","You have been imprisoned beneath Isengard and must now report to Fâsh, an Uruk-hai charged with maintaining the work of the Saruman's thralls.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon your Uruk Overseer, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>","'Talk to your overseer and do the work he asks of you! Rattle your shackles if he has wandered off, and that'll draw him near. If it doesn't, he'll have to answer to me!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon your Uruk Overseer, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>","Return to Fâsh in the centre of the caverns","Fâsh has assigned an Uruk-hai to keep an eye on you in the caverns beneath Isengard and to give you work. If your overseer wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.","Complete 'The Slop' for your Uruk-hai overseer","'I did not expect much from you, but you did all right... for a ${RACE}. You must know it is pointless to resist! That's a shame. There's usually some sport in getting the Old Man's thralls to behave.\
\
'Disappointing. But enough of that: time is wasting. You need to come with me. The Old Man wants you.'","Complete 'Kill Ten Rats' for your Uruk-hai overseer","'I've assigned someone to keep an eye on you and give you work. If he's not happy with your work, I will hear about it.\
\
'You don't want that, little ${RACE}.\
\
'If your overseer wanders off for a spot of grub or a swig of brew, rattle your shackles, and he'd better come running. Don't let me see you without him.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon your Uruk Overseer, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>","Book 4, Chapter 19: The Caverns of Isengard","'Talk to your overseer and do the work he asks of you! Rattle your shackles if he has wandered off, and that'll draw him near. If it doesn't, he'll have to answer to me!'","'You have nothing for me.'","Fâsh is in the centre of the caverns beneath Isengard.\
\
You have finished a series of tasks for your Uruk-hai overseer and should return to Fâsh."},
[2111]={"Los enanos Slóthi, Sigdan y Thálfi están en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Bósi teme que la guerra se acerque, y quiere que las defensas de la Gran Excavación estén listas.","'Temo que nos encontraremos con el mismo destino que la expedición de Balin si no nos preparamos para la batalla, ${PLAYER}. Si se le puede creer a Ashpar, la venganza de Mazog, su anfitrión, puede ser rápida.\
\
'No podemos descansar hasta que estemos preparados para lo peor. Debemos estar listos para enfrentar este asalto, y si tenemos suerte no estaremos condenados como Balin, cuyo camino aún era desconocido para él.\
\
'Mis enanos Slóthi, Sigdan y Thálfi aquí en la Cámara de la Encrucijada deben ser informados de la situación. Deberías hacer cualquier cosa que te pidan para ayudarlos a prepararse para la tormenta que se avecina. La Gran Excavación, al menos, estará lista.'","Ayuda a Slóthi con sus preparativos","Ayuda a Sigdan con sus preparativos","'Habla con Slóthi, Sigdan y Thálfi aquí en la Cámara de la Encrucijada y ayúdalos a prepararse para el asalto que temo que se avecina.'","'De hecho, has hecho lo que te pedí; ahora solo puedo esperar que sea suficiente.\
\
'Al menos la Gran Excavación está suficientemente preparada. Tuvimos suerte de que Mazog aún no hubiera dado su paso.'","Bósi se encuentra en la Cámara de la Encrucijada, en la entrada sur del Camino de Durin, al norte de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Has ayudado con los preparativos para que la Gran Excavación esté lista para la guerra y ahora deberías reportarte con Bósi.","Libro 4, Capítulo 1: Preparativos para las galerías occidentales","Ayuda a Thálfi con sus preparativos","La historia registrada en el Libro de Mazarbul ha llenado a Bósi de temor, y sabe que los enanos en la Gran Excavación de Moria deben prepararse para la guerra."},
[2112]={"Check fallen soldier","'We have slowed the enemy's march as much as we could, but now we must see to our own safety. Go now to the Pelennor Fields! We must see if the Causeway Forts have been taken by the enemy. I believe they surely have. Duilin and Derufin will help you in this.'","'How fares Osgiliath and the Causeway Forts? I have seen few survivors! There may still be men out there!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel outside the Causeway Forts on the Pelennor Fields when you accept this quest.</rgb>","'Some of the defenders of the Causeway Forts fled before the encroaching army, and were slain before they reached safety. See if any men survived, and defeat their pursuers. It could be their injuries were grave, but not yet mortal.'","You check for signs of life, but this man has been dead for some time","'You found no survivors? I am not surprised, but I am disappointed to hear that good men of Gondor were bludgeoned or hewn even after death. We needed no further reason to hate the Orcs, but still they provide it for us! We will not forget, and every insult will be repaid ten-fold!'","The safety of Minas Tirith is threatened by the foes that have come to the Pelennor Fields. Men fled from the occupation of the Causeway Forts and fell not far from Osgiliath.\
\
Duilin and Derufin have asked you to search for survivors injured while fleeing from the Causeway Forts, and to defeat foes on the Pelennor.","You check for signs of life, but this man has already succumbed to death","Defeat foes on the Pelennor Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Book 4, Chapter 1: The Broken Causeway","This man did not survive. It seems the enemy hewed his body after he fell","'The city has been lost, ${PLAYER}. Faramir is missing, and his men are dead or captured. We have slowed the enemy's march as much as we could, but now we must see to our own safety. I will bring us by secret passages beyond the enemy camp, and from there we will make our way to the causeway.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel outside the Causeway Forts on the Pelennor Fields when you accept this quest.</rgb>","'This place will be crawling with enemies before long, ${PLAYER}. It is time for us to leave.'","'My brother and I left Minas Tirith to seek adventure and hunt the mighty Mûmakil, and at that time it felt a prison. Now I see the White City on the horizon and it seems a refuge instead! Can its walls stand against the evils we have beheld?\
\
'I cannot stop thinking about that frightful apparition: Gothmog. Is it true he has the power to escape death? What will happen when the great ram Grond is repaired and he brings it across the Pelennor?\
\
'We will do what we must, as always, and not shrink in fear! Truly, we will let it drive us to greater heights of courage! It seems that some of the defenders of the Causeway Forts fled before the encroaching army, and were slain before they reached safety. See if any men survived, and defeat their pursuers. It could be their injuries were grave, but not yet mortal.'","Osgiliath has been lost, and the defenders who still remain in the city must escape to the Pelennor.","Duilin and Derufin are outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern side of the Pelennor Fields.","'There were no survivors? I am sorry to hear it, but I am not surprised it is so.'","Defeated foes on the Pelennor Fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Duilin is outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern side of the Pelennor Fields.\
\
Osgiliath has fallen to the enemy, and the men there can no longer mount an effective resistance.","'Osgiliath has fallen, and its defenders fled in a great rout. They may have purchased some few hours for the people of Minas Tirith, but they paid dearly for it.'","Talk to Duilin outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor Fields","'I hate the Orcs for what they have done, and will not rest until they have paid in full for every life they have extinguished! I know that my brother feels the same!'","Talk to Derufin outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor Fields"},
[2113]={"Halbarad is in the centre of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin.\
\
You have spoken with Prestadír and Braigiar about the paths into Dunland.","'The south-west passage into Dunland will take us through Trum Dreng, ${PLAYER}. It is a forested land, where shadows pool in the hollows between the hills.\
\
'As I scouted ahead, I saw emblems and totems of a horned stag, but few people. They are likely to be on the edge of the conflicts in Dunland, though if it be by their choice or by necessity I did not discover.\
\
'You are welcome to come with my group into Trum Dreng, ${PLAYER}, and we will learn the truth of it.'","'You have heard what we know about our possible paths into Dunland. Each way could be dangerous, and we will not know what awaits us until we get there.\
\
'Which road do you wish to take into Dunland, ${PLAYER}? Each will have its dangers. Make your choice and tell Braigiar or Prestadír which group you will follow: Braigiar if you wish to travel through Trum Dreng, or Prestadír if you wish to enter the Bonevales.'","Talk to Prestadír in Lhanuch","Prestadír and Braigiar, in the centre of Lhanuch, are considering the two paths the Grey Company will take to enter Dunland.\
\
Halbarad has asked you to consult with Prestadír and Braigiar about his proposed routes into Dunland.","'There are two paths that we might take into Dunland. Speak with Prestadír and Braigiar concerning what they have learned about the way into Dunland.'","'Corunir is right. This delay has been costly. If what you say is true, and Saruman does know of our errand, we travel from hardship into even greater peril. And yet, we must not despair or turn from our road, or our brethren will have fallen for naught.'\
\
Halbarad sighs, his brow creased with worry.\
\
'There are two paths we could take into Dunland, and I propose that we split into smaller groups and travel each of these paths...we will be less likely to be noticed as we cross into Dunland.\
\
'Prestadír and Braigiar have scouted our options. Speak with them to hear of the two roads that we might use to enter Dunland.'","Book 4, Chapter 1: The Departure of Lhanuch","'If we had not delayed, we might have left with our fallen brothers, and not without them. Go to Lhanuch and tell Halbarad that I will be there shortly. You will find him in the centre of the village.'","Talk to Halbarad in Lhanuch","'I would be honoured if you travelled with my group into the Bonevales. It is an inhospitable land and barren, and it would be good to have your company.'","'The south-east passage into Dunland will take us through the Bonevales, an inhospitable and barren land. The crags and valleys are dusty and barren, and its people are tough, like coffin nails.\
\
'There are few souls in the Bonevales, few eyes to watch our passage. Caution must be our watch-word, stealth our constant companion. My group would welcome your presence, ${PLAYER}.'","Halbarad is in the centre of the village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin.\
\
You have been told that Halbarad is assembling the Grey Company in preparation for its departure and should travel to Lhanuch for the last of the preparations before departing.","'I would be pleased if you would join my group on the journey into Trum Dreng, ${PLAYER}. Its forested hills are steeped in shadow, cold and mysterious.'","Talk to Braigiar in Lhanuch","The time has come for the Grey Company to travel south into Dunland, continuing its dangerous mission to reach Aragorn in time to be of help.","'We have delayed too long already. I am ready to go, ${PLAYER}. Return to Halbarad in Lhanuch, and we will decide how best to proceed south into Dunland.\
\
'We will leave this place behind, and none too soon! If we had left earlier, we could have left with Candaith and my fallen brothers, and not without them.'"},
[2114]={"Libro 4, Capítulo 1: ¿Dónde está el Caballo y el Jinete?","'Los Nazgûl nunca cruzarán el Bruinen mientras permanezca bajo mi mando.'","Elladan está en su campamento de Thorenhad, en la ladera noroeste de las Gargantas del Bruinen, al norte de las guaridas de osos.\
\
El Señor Elrond te ha pedido que prestes tu ayuda a sus hijos Elladan y Elrohir, quienes actualmente buscan al Nazgûl desaparecido.","Siervos del Enemigo persiguieron a Frodo Bolsón hasta el Bruinen, y aunque el hobbit y sus amigos fueron salvados y las criaturas terribles derrotadas por el poder de Elrond, no todos los Nazgûl han sido localizados.","'Bienvenido a Imladris, ${PLAYER}. Es bueno que hayas venido. Descansa bien, pero no demasiado profundamente ni por mucho tiempo. Necesitamos gente aventurera, pues hay mal más allá del valle.\
\
'No hace más de dos meses, un hobbit llamado Frodo Bolsón y sus compañeros fueron perseguidos hasta el Vado del Bruinen por siervos del Enemigo. Hablo de los Nueve, los Nazgûl, criaturas terribles al servicio de Sauron, y aunque el Bruinen cayó sobre ellos por mi orden, solo hemos encontrado los corceles de ocho. Uno de los Jinetes no ha sido localizado.\
\
'Mis hijos partieron con exploradores unidos a ellos por la amistad para buscar a este Jinete perdido. Te pido que hables con Elladan en su campamento de Thorenhad, entre las Gargantas del Bruinen, y que prestes tu ayuda en la búsqueda. Debemos descubrir adónde ha ido este Nazgûl, y lo más importante, cuáles son sus designios.'","'Mis hijos han establecido un campamento, Thorenhad, en las regiones del norte de las Gargantas del Bruinen. Búscalos al norte de las guaridas de osos y presta tu ayuda a Elladan en este asunto.'","'Mi padre te ha enviado para ayudarnos? Es bueno que hayas venido, pues hemos hecho un descubrimiento inquietante. Parece probable que el Jinete perdido aún se encuentre en algún lugar de la naturaleza salvaje del Bosque de los Trolls.'","'Mis hijos han establecido un campamento en Thorenhad, entre las Gargantas del Bruinen.'"},
[2116]={"Morflak has assigned one of his lackeys to keep an eye on you within the Ring of Isengard.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon Morflak's Lackey, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>","Complete 'Trivial Business' for Morflak's lackey","'You have nothing for me!'","Complete 'Their Best Interests' for Morflak's lackey","Book 4, Chapter 21: Servants of Saruman","Complete 'Raiding the Larder' for Morflak's lackey","'Talk to my lackey and do the work that he gives you. If he's wandered away, rattle your shackles, and he'd better appear. If he doesn't, he'll answer to me!'","'Talk to my lackey and do the work that he gives you. If he's wandered away, rattle your shackles, and he'd better appear. If he doesn't, he'll answer to me!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon your Uruk Overseer, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>","Morflak has assigned one of his lackeys to keep an eye on you within the ring of Isengard and to give you work. If this Uruk-hai wanders off for some reason, rattling your shackles should make him come running.","Return to Morflak within the Ring of Isengard","'Talk to my lackey and do the work he gives you. If he's wandered away, rattle your shackles, and he'd better appear. If he doesn't, he'll answer to me!'","'We are all servants of Sharkû here, but some of us are given more freedom than others. I am one of these, little ${RACE}, and in return I help my friends.\
\
'I have assigned one of my trusted lackeys to watch you while you do my work. If he lets you out of his sight, rattle your shackles to draw him near. If he does this too often he may find himself out of my favour, then out of a head...in that order!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>If you need to resummon Morflak's Lackey, use the Shackles you now have within your inventory and he will appear.</rgb>","Morflak is waiting to speak with you within the ring of Isengard.","'I may have been wrong about you after all. These others complain about the work they do for me, and it is only fear of my retribution that keeps them in line. But you have served me well, and without complaint.\
\
'I do not think you need a shadow any longer. You will stay in line or you will answer to Morflak; that will be guard enough!'"},
[2117]={"'What are you still doing here? You might be under Morflak's protection, for now, but if you cross me, I may forget that for a moment...and a moment is all it would take to ensure you'd never cross me again!\
\
'Go help Barkh in the kitchens!'","Dulan in the kitchens has tried to catch your eye.\
\
You should talk to Dulan and see what he wants.","It is time for you to squeeze out the dirty rag into the slop bucket in the kitchens.","Barkh is in the kitchens below Isengard, south-west of the main cavern.","Return the dirty rag to Barkh in the kitchens","Talk to Barkh in the kitchens","Baldgar wants to speak with you. He is in the dungeons below Isengard.","Fâsh is in the caverns beneath Isengard, accessible by a door directly north of the tower. Once in the depths, you should take the sloping paths downward to Fâsh's command.\
\
Morflak has sent you to deliver a message to Fâsh and to do more work for him.","Barkh is in the kitchens beneath Isengard, south-west of the main cavern.\
\
Fâsh has sent you to help out in the kitchens once again.","Uruk-hai meals can be found on the tables in the kitchens below Isengard.\
\
Dulan has secretly given you a small quantity of poison and wants you to add it to one of the Uruk-hai meals.","Quietly add the poison to an Uruk-hai meal","'Morflak says that you can walk about unguarded? Well, it won't be my hide if you cause trouble.'\
\
Fâsh snorts loudly.\
\
'Go help Barkh in the kitchens. You know where they are. And be quick about it! You might be Morflak's latest pet, but I won't have you getting underfoot and slowing things down!'","You tip the slop into the bucket, and it makes a sickening sound","'Back for more? I'm surprised you're still alive!'\
\
Barkh sneers at you, his fangs bared, and hands you a dirty rag.\
\
'Clean the slop up off the floor. You know how it's done.'","'Be careful...do not let them see you adding the poison...and do not stand so near to me. You will make them suspicious!'","Fill up a bucket of slop from the slop bucket in the kitchens","The floor of the kitchen is covered in slop.\
\
Barkh has given you a dirty rag and wants you to clean the slop up off the floor.","'You have nothing for me.'","Cleaned up piles of slop in the kitchens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You secretly add the poison to the Uruk-hai meal and return to your task","'What is taking you so long? Back to work, vermin! Clean up that slop!'","'Don't give me that dirty rag! Squeeze it out in the slop bucket first!'","'You have managed to slip away from your guard? That is good! That is very good, indeed!'\
\
Baldgar peers from side to side, making sure the guards are out of earshot.\
\
'I am working on a plan to escape, ${PLAYER}, but I could use your help.'","Book 4, Chapter 22: Feed the Prisoners","'Back to work, vermin! Slop still covers this floor!'","'Clean up that slop! You know what to do!'","Clean up piles of slop in the kitchens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dulan has tried to catch your eye. Talk to him without attracting attention","'Go to the caverns and tell Fâsh that he is to keep you busy until I call for you. If he gives you any trouble, you come and let me know.\
\
'You get to the depths by way of a door north of the tower. Once you're down there, keep taking the sloping paths down into the centre of the cavern, where Fâsh has his command.'","'What are you doing? There's slop to clean up!'","Talk to Baldgar in the dungeon","Dulan silently hands you a quantity of poison","'Get to the dungeons! The prisoners need to be fed! If you stay here, I'll make you the main course!'","'You do everything slowly and poorly! Is every ${RACE} as useless as you?\
\
'Go fill up a pan from the slop bucket and carry it to the bucket in the dungeons. It's time for the prisoners to be fed again!'","Talk to Fâsh in the Isengard Depths","'Have you lost your way? The slop bucket is right there! Fill up a pan and bring it to the bucket in the dungeons so the prisoners can be fed! Move, or I'll tan your hide!'","Morflak wants you to report to Fâsh with the message that you no longer need a guard to watch your comings and goings. Fâsh is to keep you busy until Morflak has need of you.","Barkh wants you to fill a pan from the slop bucket in the kitchens and carry it to the bucket in the dungeons from where the prisoners are fed, as you did before.","'Fâsh will give you no trouble, if he knows what's good for him. If he does, you send him to me. He will not defy the will of Morflak.\
\
'Fâsh is in the caverns below. You get to the depths by way of a door north of the tower. Once you're down there, keep taking the sloping paths down into the centre of the cavern, where Fâsh has his command.'","Slop covers the floor of the kitchens below Isengard.\
\
Barkh wants you to clean up the slop.","'Hey...you there...no, don't look at me. I don't want to attract attention.'\
\
Dulan keeps wiping down the table and talks to you out of the side of his mouth.\
\
'I've gotten my hands on a pinch of poison, just a thimble-full. If I give it to you, can you add it to one of the meals for the Uruk-hai? Don't let anyone see you!'\
\
Dulan silently hands you a small half-shell containing a few drops of clear liquid.","Use the slop bucket in the kitchens to squeeze out the dirty rag"},
[2118]={"Baldgar is forming an escape plan, and he says a fellow prisoner is the key to its success.","'Do you see how it was now, friend? I served Saruman well and faithfully for many years, and but for the lies of Gríma, I would still!\
\
'I like you. I will help you escape. There is a way out of the Ring that only I know about; you will not find it without my help! Tell your friend if he can get us to the surface and create some kind of distraction, I can get us beyond the Ring.'","Talk to Acca and experience 'Session: The Wizard's Vale' or read the shortened account instead","The plans of a Wizard cannot remain entirely secret to the steward who runs his household. When Acca learns that Saruman has captured his former ally Gandalf the Grey, the steward finds himself conflicted. It takes little time for such worries to be noticed by one who is only too eager to speak of these doubts to his master...","Book 4, Chapter 23: The Wizard's Vale","'Acca was once the steward of Isengard and ran Saruman's household. He may know something of use to us in planning our escape.'","'Tell your friend that I can help us escape. You will not find the secret way without my help!'","Acca is imprisoned in the dungeons below Isengard.\
\
Acca, once the steward of Isengard, has agreed to tell you the story of his fall.","'I was the steward of Isengard, and this is how I am repaid for my long service! It is all Gríma's doing!\
\
'I will tell you of my fall, if you wish to hear the sad tale. I know secrets, secrets of this place... secrets you might use!'","'The steward will help us? Good. I do not like being so dependent upon him, but it seems that we have no choice.'","'I will tell you the tale of my fall, and you shall judge whether I was treated harshly. Perhaps then, I will share with you my secrets!'","Acca is in the dungeons below Isengard, located in the north-west corner of the main cavern.","Acca has told you the story of his fall and has warmed up to you. He is waiting to speak with you.","Baldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard.\
\
Acca has agreed to help you escape and wants you to tell Baldgar.","Talk to Acca in the dungeon","'One of the other prisoners was once the steward of this place. His name is Acca, and he ran the day-to-day affairs of Saruman's household while the Wizard concentrated on other matters. But Acca fell out of favour with Saruman and is now a prisoner like the rest of us.\
\
'There is little to do in these dungeons but talk, and Acca has boasted that he knows secrets about Isengard that none save Saruman possess.\
\
'Talk to Acca about these secrets. He may reveal something that we can use to escape.'","Talk to Acca in the dungeons","Talk to Baldgar in the dungeon"},
[2119]={"'Acca will tell us the location of the secret way out of the Ring, but we will need two things: a way out of these cells and a large enough distraction to keep the Uruk-hai occupied once we reach the surface.\
\
'When Fâsh took me from my cell to work, I saw some of Saruman's experiments. One of these involved a black powder that, when set aflame, caused a tremendous roar and smoke. Some of the machinery seems to spew this powder. If you can collect enough of it, we could use it for our distraction.\
\
'Your relative freedom of movement can help us here, ${PLAYER}, but you must still keep up appearances. Do not let the Uruk-hai know what you are up to! Report to Sagrúrz by the forges and do his work in addition to collecting the powder for me.'","'The weapons are right there, scattered all over the floor! Pick them up and put them in that empty barrel there.'","Collected piles of black powder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Do the work that Sagrúrz will ask of you, but as you perform his tasks, you should also collect any black powder that you can. Do not let him catch you at this work! It would go badly for us.'","Baldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard.\
\
You have stolen some black powder and should bring it to Baldgar.","'Why are you standing around? Isn't there somewhere that you should be? Stop bothering me!'","'Good, I'm glad you've cleaned up those scattered weapons. That servant who ran for it made it further than they usually do... he made it to that ramp over there. I just wish he hadn't spilled that barrel and caused me this extra work.'\
\
You breathe a sigh of relief. Sagrúrz does not seem to have noticed your theft of the black powder.","Sagrúrz is by the forges in the main cavern beneath Isengard.\
\
Baldgar wants you to do the work Sagrúrz asks of you, but while you are doing that, he also wants you to collect some black powder.","Collect scattered weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected scattered weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Back for more work? There's plenty to do, so don't let me catch you dozing!'\
\
Sagrúrz motions at the scattered weapons near the forges.\
\
'One of the Old Man's thralls dropped a barrel of weapons and tried to run for it. He was... dealt with... but now there are weapons scattered all over the place! Pick them up and put them back in that empty barrel there!'","Return to Baldgar with the stolen black powder","Sagrúrz is waiting to speak with you by the forges in the main cavern beneath Isengard.","Collect piles of black powder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Put the scattered weapons in the empty barrel","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'Well? Put the weapons you gathered up in that empty barrel there! What are you waiting for?'","The empty barrel is near the forges in the main cavern beneath Isengard.\
\
Sagrúrz wants you to put the scattered weapons you collected in an empty barrel.","Talk to Sagrúrz at the forge","'You managed to get some of the powder! Perfect. This is going to be the key to the distraction that we will need once we make it to the surface.'","Book 4, Chapter 24: A Pinch of Black Powder","Weapons are scattered around the floor near the forges. Sagrúrz wants you to pick them up and put them back in an empty barrel. Meanwhile, Baldgar wants you to collect some of the black powder that spews from the works and collects on the floor.","Baldgar has come up with an escape plan, and he wants you to use your relative freedom of movement within Isengard to help him carry it out."},
[2120]={"Thak gave you some trouble when you went to leave the black powder at the war-machine. Now you can either speak to Morflak about Thak, as you threatened, or you can go directly back to Baldgar in the dungeons below Isengard. The door to the depths is north of Orthanc, and Morflak is south-west of the tower.","Baldgar has given you your final instructions for the escape plan: to leave the black powder near one of the great war-machines on the surface, for later ignition.","Morflak stares at you for a long moment.\
\
'It is done. No more words are necessary.'","'What were you doing lingering around there? Explain yourself! I don't like the look of you, ${RACE}. Start talking!'\
\
Thak eyes you hungrily, confident that he has caught you doing something suspicious, so you appease him: you start talking.\
\
You tell him angrily that it is Morflak's will that you walk around Isengard unguarded, and if Thak wishes to question the will of Morflak, you can bring the two together. All of Thak's bluster vanishes in an instant.\
\
'Don't tell him about this! I'm sorry, I didn't mean anything by it. Really! You don't need to trouble Morflak about this!'","The largest of the war-machines is being constructed on the surface, within the Ring of Isengard. The door to the surface is in the north wall of the caverns. The war-machines are south-east of the steps of Orthanc.\
\
Baldgar has asked you to leave the black powder that you collected near the largest of the war-machines under construction. You have enough black powder for four small piles.","'You have done as I asked! Good, good! I hope setting that black powder aflame will be the distraction that we need to make good our escape.'","'The guards do not bring us to work on the surface very often, but the last time that they did, I saw some of the great war-machines being constructed within the Ring. I do not know how close they are to being completed, but if we can do anything to prevent them from leaving Isengard, we surely must.\
\
'What is it they say about birds and stones? I think the black powder you collected might serve as the perfect distraction and also deprive our enemies of one of these war-machines.\
\
'Go to the surface and leave the black powder near the largest of the war-machines, south-east of the steps of Orthanc. The amount you have should suffice for four small piles. We will set the war machines aflame when it is time for us to make our escape. The door to the surface is on the north side of the caverns.'","Find the largest of the war-machines under construction within the Ring","Leave the black powder near the largest of the war-machines under construction","Talk to Baldgar","'Leave the black powder that you collected near the largest of the war-machines being constructed on the surface. You have enough black powder for four small piles. I think the war machines are south-east of the steps of Orthanc. We will set the war machines aflame when the time comes for us to make our escape, then we must trust that Acca's secret way is as secret as he suggests.'","Leave the black powder near the largest of the war machines under construction. Keep sprinkling the powder until it is gone.","You are near enough the war machine to leave the black powder.","Thak has noticed you lingering near the war-machine!","'Ah, you have returned! Were you able to leave the black powder at the place that we spoke about?'","Thak is near the war-machines on the surface, within the Ring of Isengard.\
\
Thak noticed you lingering near the war-machines and has called you to speak with him.","Book 4, Chapter 25: Final Preparations","You have sprinkled the black powder near the largest of the war-machines under construction.","Baldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard. The entrance to the depths is north of the tower of Orthanc.\
\
You have left the black powder near the largest of the war-machines within the Ring and should speak now with Baldgar in the dungeons.","Morflak stares at you for a long moment before speaking.\
\
'Thak gave you some trouble? Doesn't he know you're one of mine? I will have one of my boys take care of him. No one disrespects Morflak!'","Talk to Baldgar in the dungeon","Talk to Morflak","You sprinkle some of the black powder onto the ground","Talk to Thak","'Don't tell Morflak about this little discussion of ours! I didn't mean anything by it!'"},
[2121]={"'I carried you... this far... but this is... the end... for Baldgar son of Beldgar.'","Baldgar is in the dungeons below Isengard.","Talk to Baldgar and carry out the escape plan","When you awaken, you find that you have been carried to the Gravenwood, but Baldgar is near death.","The time has come to carry out Baldgar's escape plan. If all goes well, you will soon be free of Isengard.","Talk to Baldgar in the Gravenwood","'Is this... the end? Where is the reminder... of our captivity?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You need to have the Reminder of Captivity item in your inventory to advance this quest. If it is currently in your Vault, you will need to remove it and bring it to Baldgar to advance.</rgb>","'Are you ready? We will only get one chance at this. We must make it count!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a solo quest and cannot be completed with a fellowship.</rgb>","Book 4, Chapter 26: Escape from Isengard","'There is no sense in delaying this, ${PLAYER}. It is time that we were free of this place. Speak with me when you are ready.'"},
[2122]={"Baldgar is dead. You should return to Théodred's camp in the Gravenwood to learn what has become of the Grey Company during your captivity.","'${PLAYER}, you are alive! We feared the worst. Few of your friends made it out of Tâl Methedras, and the tales of those who did are not encouraging.\
\
'I do not think that the Falcon-clan was with Saruman in the beginning; rather, it seems the tide turned while you were travelling through Dunland. The news you brought Lheu Brenin, that Saruman's influence could be felt everywhere, may have been the information for which he was waiting. A pox on these Dunlendings! They cannot be trusted!\
\
'Very few folk made it out of Tâl Methedras, but some did: the rare few Dunlendings who spoke against the Brenin's decision, and a handful of Rangers. If we work together, we can repay Lheu Brenin for his treachery.'","You have escaped from Isengard with the help of Baldgar, but he did not survive. You should rejoin Théodred at his camp in the Gravenwood to decide what to do next.","Find Théodred at his camp in the Gravenwood and talk to him","Théodred should be at his camp in the Gravenwood.","'Do not weep for me... my friend... it is enough to be... free....'\
\
Baldgar's eyes flutter closed for the last time, and he dies a free man. You decide to return to Théodred's camp in the Gravenwood and see what has become of the Grey Company during your captivity.","Book 4, Chapter 27: Repaying Treachery"},
[2123]={"Théodred wants you to speak to some of the survivors of the Falcon-clan's betrayal of the Grey Company.","Théodred is at his camp in the Gravenwood.","Saeradan, Seren, and Hogawise are at Théodred's camp in the Gravenwood.\
\
Théodred wants you to speak to survivors of the Falcon-clan's betrayal in order to learn what happened while you were imprisoned in Isengard.","'There is no sense in delaying this any further. Your friends are held captive by our shared enemy. This enemy has a strong defensive position, but we have this advantage: we know where he is. Once the Falcon-clan leaves Tâl Methedras, that advantage dissipates. We must deal with them here, before they leave that valley.\
\
'Once the Falcon-clan leaves the valley, my men and I must retreat to hold the Ford. The defence of Rohan is my main object. Until that time, I will help you free your friends.'","Talk to Théodred at the Rohirrim scout-camp","Talk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp","Talk to Hogawise at the Rohirrim scout-camp","'I cannot believe this! How can this have happened?'\
\
The old woman is quivering with anger and grief.\
\
'The Brenin called the heads of households to him, and declared that we were at last ready to reap our reward; we had only to bend the knee to Saruman. But Lheu Brenin himself had said to us the Hebog-lûth would not be the tool of some Wizard! He said it often, and loudly, and we came to believe it!\
\
'I have no love for these Horse-lords, and this strutting princeling least of all, but what can be said? The honour of the Falcon-clan...sold to Saruman? Wulf sought his enemies in open battle! He was no Wizard's hireling!'\
\
Seren chokes back angry tears.\
\
'My boy Anirin has not returned yet from the lands of the Algraig, but his beloved spoke out against this treachery and is still a prisoner! What will I say to him if she dies?'","'You must tell me of your time in Isengard, ${PLAYER}. It cannot have been pleasant, and you were often in my thoughts.\
\
'I heard what happened within Tâl Methedras from Radanir. Some time after you were secreted away to Isengard, he managed to escape the prison-cave with poor Braigiar. The two of them fought their way into the centre of Tûr Morva, but then....'\
\
Saeradan sighs heavily, and he seems in that moment much older than his years.\
\
'Braigiar did not make it. They cut him down in the road, and only Radanir escaped. He has gone back with some of Théodred's men to try and recover Braigiar's body, but they have not returned.\
\
'Many of our friends have fallen, and the rest are still captives of Lheu Brenin. According to Radanir, Halbarad and the sons of Elrond are still alive, but who can say for how long?'","Talk to Seren at the Rohirrim scout-camp","Book 4, Chapter 28: Survivors","'We crossed the Ford of Isen in secret to learn what the Men of Dunland were up to, but it is worse than we suspected. I think it surprised the leader of the Falcon-clan, as well. It seems to me that he was biding his time until the victory of one side seemed assured. Then he needed to simply throw his lot in with the side likely to come out the victor.\
\
'Let us hope that he is mistaken, ${PLAYER}. I think that he is undervaluing the prowess of the Men of Rohan. I would take ten Rohirrim on horseback over a thousand Dunlending wild men. I have spoken with your friend Saeradan, and it sounds like these Rangers are the same. The more of them we free now, the fewer thousands of Dunlendings I need concern myself with! Ha!'","'Seren feels the sting of this betrayal most keenly, ${PLAYER}. Her family is still in peril within Tûr Morva, subject to the whims of Lheu Brenin. She will help us.\
\
'Your friend Saeradan is even now attempting to devise a plan with which we can rescue the Rangers, and I know Hogawise's sword is pledged to the cause as well. Speak with them at once, and we will act.'","'Not every member of the Falcon-clan agreed with Lheu Brenin's decision; those that did not were slain or forced to flee. One of those who escaped is the woman Seren, and it is from her that I have learned much of what befell within Tâl Methedras.\
\
'I had been working closely with your friend Saeradan before you were captured, and he now burns with the desire to free what Rangers still live, if any do. He is very wise, and it seems if there is any hope of rescue he may be able to devise it. Speak with him on this account.\
\
'You might also seek the advice of my trusted friend Hogawise. He excels in battle and has been a boon companion on this excursion into Gravenwood.'"},
[2124]={"'It is time. The preparations are made. Now we must strike.'","You have found Théodred's forward encampment","Travel into Tâl Methedras and find Théodred's forward encampment","From his forward encampment in Tâl Methedras, Théodred makes preparations to launch an attack on Tûr Morva.","Théodred is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras.\
\
You have completed the necessary preparations and are now ready to attempt the rescue of the Grey Company from the prison-caves of Tûr Morva.","Preparations completed for the attack on Tûr Morva (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Théodred has established a small camp within Tâl Methedras from which he and his men will help to save the captured members of the Grey Company.","'Soon, we will mount our attack on the city of traitors, but first we must make ready. We must be not hasty, lest it prove our undoing!\
\
'Help the people at this encampment with their aims. They all desire justice. They will have it! But we must remain cautious, and strike the Falcon-clan only when we are most ready.'","'I sent some of my men into Tâl Methedras to establish a camp, ${PLAYER}. We should go to join them. Pass into Tâl Methedras and follow the road as it approaches the lake.\
\
'From this camp, we can scout the area and make a plan for rescuing the Rangers. Some of your people should already be at this camp, such is the fire in their hearts. Let all who wish to join them do so!'","Théodred is waiting to speak with you at his forward encampment, in Tâl Methedras.","Talk to Théodred at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras","Théodred's men have formed a camp in sight of the lake in Tâl Methedras. You should go there to begin planning the rescue of the Grey Company.","'We must go to the camp that my men have established inside Tâl Methedras. It is to the north and east, in view of the lake. Once we are in Tâl Methedras, simply follow the road to the camp.'","'From this forward encampment, we will mount our attack on the city of traitors! But not yet. We must first take action to scout the area and learn the extent of the Falcon-clan's defences.\
\
'Speak with our allies at this encampment and help them with their aims. It will all be of use when we make our attack.'","Complete the preparations necessary to mount an attack on Tûr Morva (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Book 4, Chapter 29: City of Traitors"},
[2125]={"'Scout the area to our south, and remain on your guard. We must know what the situation here in Trum Dreng may be before we travel south in greater number.'","Scout ahead and help an inhabitant of Trum Dreng","Book 4, Chapter 2: Land of the Stag","Talk to Braigiar in Lhan Tarren, the village of the Stag-clan","'We should leave at once, ${PLAYER}, and pass south into Dunland. We can speak again just inside Trum Dreng.'","Braigiar will speak with you again just across the border of Enedwaith and Dunland, at Dúvispont, in Trum Dreng.","The plains of Trum Dreng lie to the south.\
\
Braigiar has asked you to scout Trum Dreng, keeping an eye out for its residents.","'We have already learned much about Dunland from your brief encounter, ${PLAYER}. There is much we can do here in Trum Dreng to help its people and also to smooth the passage of the Grey Company through this land.'","You have decided to travel with the group heading south into Dunland by way of Trum Dreng, the Land of the Stag.","'Here we are. We have crossed into Dunland, and now find ourselves in the Land of the Stag. Be on your guard. We need to know what the situation here is, and we can only know that by observing its people.\
\
'Scout the area to the south and determine what we will be dealing with as we pass through this land.'","Braigiar is waiting to speak with you just outside Lhan Tarren, the village of the Stag-clan.\
\
You should speak with Braigiar before proceeding.","Talk to Braigiar once you arrive at Dúvispont, in Dunland","'Very good, ${PLAYER}. I welcome you into the group that will travel into Trum Dreng, the Land of the Stag! We will do our best to come that way into Dunland free of danger.\
\
'We will move swiftly and silently, and our company will be in number small enough as to escape prying eyes. Saruman knows that we must pass into Dunland, but the time and manner of our coming is still ours to control.\
\
'Let us be off at once! We can stop and see how things fare once we have crossed into Trum Dreng.'"},
[2126]={"'Poco después de que Frodo Bolsón y su compañía llegaran a Rivendel, mi padre nos envió a buscar señales de los Nazgûl, los Nueve Jinetes del Enemigo. Encontramos los cuerpos de ocho caballos río abajo, pero del último no había rastro alguno. Seguimos buscando, pero no hallamos nada.\
\
'Viajamos muy lejos, hacia tierras del sur, y aun así no encontramos señal del Jinete fugitivo. Solo en nuestro viaje de regreso descubrimos algo: huellas de cascos en el Bosque de los Trolls del Sur, muy al sur del camino. Hay muchos valles estrechos en esa región — el Nazgûl podría yacer allí, oculto de miradas indiscretas, aguardando su momento para atacar.\
\
'Viaja muy al sur del camino en el Bosque de los Trolls del Sur, ${PLAYER}, y busca al Jinete desaparecido. Las ruinas dentro de esos canales estrechos tienen una reputación siniestra. Antaño se llamaba a ese lugar Minas Agor, y puede que el Nazgûl lo haya buscado precisamente por esa razón.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para completarse en grupo, pero puede intentarse en solitario. La piedra que recibes al aceptarla puede usarse para obtener durante un tiempo limitado una mejora que te permitirá beneficiarte de la inspiración aun cuando la comunidad sea de menos de cinco miembros.</rgb>","El cadáver de un caballo negro yace en las ruinas de Minas Agor, situadas entre los estrechos canales del Bosque de los Trolls del Sur.\
\
Debes retirar la brida del cadáver del caballo y llevarla a Elladan.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La Piedra élfica puede usarse para permitirte acceder a la mejora de inspiración mientras juegas en solitario o en una comunidad pequeña.</rgb>","'No has regresado con la brida, ${PLAYER}. ¿Cómo voy a examinarla para comprobar que realmente pertenece al corcel del Nazgûl desaparecido?'","La fuerza hincha tu pecho. Aquí es un lugar donde puedes obtener inspiración.","Libro 4, Capítulo 2: El Jinete Perdido","Retira la brida del cadáver del caballo negro.","Elladan se encuentra en Thorenhad, ubicado entre las Gargantas del Bruinen, al norte de una guarida de osos.\
\
Elladan se sentirá a la vez complacido y turbado al ver la brida del caballo negro, pues significa que el Jinete desaparecido aún se encuentra en algún lugar dentro del Bosque de los Trolls.","Usa la Piedra élfica para invocar tu inspiración interior.","'Debes contarle estas sombrías nuevas a Elladan de inmediato. Confieso que una sombra ha caído sobre mi corazón, pues estas tierras que amo están en peligro por la sola presencia del Nazgûl. ¡Ojalá hubiese sido atrapado en el Bruinen con el resto de sus funestos hermanos!'","Encontrarás inspiración en los lugares más oscuros.","'Tu relato empieza a completar este rompecabezas para mí, ${PLAYER}, y creo que ahora veo lo que ha sucedido.\
\
'Atrapados entre lo que quedaba de la compañía de Frodo y la furia del Bruinen, los Nueve fueron forzados a lanzarse al torrente... pero uno escapó en el caos. Al borde de la muerte, su corcel lo llevó por canales ocultos hasta algún lugar donde, casi sin forma, reunió sus fuerzas.\
\
'Abandonó a su caballo y desapareció en lo salvaje. Sin su capa sería casi invisible para nosotros... una malicia en el viento. Si vuelve a ponérsela, será solo para dar forma a su poder. Eso significa que ha sobrevivido a la prueba indemne y sin duda volverá a atacarnos. Nos estamos quedando sin tiempo, ${PLAYER}.'","Moscas zumban alrededor del cadáver de un caballo negro.","Si no cuentas con una comunidad completa, puedes obtener inspiración.","'¿Has encontrado al caballo negro del Nazgûl? Rápido, ${PLAYER} — regresa a Minas Agor y tráenos la brida del corcel. Debemos estar seguros.'","'Una gran tragedia sobrevino a los moradores de Minas Agor hace mucho tiempo, y el lugar nunca se recuperó del recuerdo de lo que allí sucedió. Si ahora sirve de refugio al Nazgûl desaparecido, parece que su destino no ha cambiado demasiado.\
\
'Encontrarás las ruinas al sur del Gran Camino del Este, que atraviesa el Bosque de los Trolls del Sur, entre los estrechos valles de ese lugar.'","'Descubrimos huellas que llevaban hacia los estrechos valles muy al sur del camino que cruza el Bosque de los Trolls del Sur. Las ruinas de Minas Agor se encuentran dentro de esos canales y tienen un nombre funesto. Puede que el Jinete desaparecido se oculte entre esos muros desmoronados.'","Brida recogida del corcel negro","Las huellas fueron descubiertas muy al sur del camino, y los hijos de Elrond creen que el Jinete desaparecido podría estar oculto en las ruinas de Minas Agor, situadas en los estrechos canales del Bosque de los Trolls del Sur.\
\
Elladan te ha pedido que sigas al Nazgûl hacia el Bosque de los Trolls del Sur.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La Piedra élfica puede usarse para permitirte acceder a la mejora de inspiración mientras juegas en solitario o en una comunidad pequeña.</rgb>","Lleva la brida del corcel negro a Elladan.","Elladan y Elrohir han tenido una búsqueda infructuosa del Jinete desaparecido, pero finalmente los hermanos han hallado algunas huellas de su paso.","'¿El corcel negro del Nazgûl está muerto, en las ruinas de Minas Agor? Debemos estar seguros, ${PLAYER}. Regresa a las ruinas y retira la brida del caballo. Solo entonces podremos confirmar lo que has visto.'","Encuentra alguna señal del Nazgûl desaparecido."},
[2127]={"Talk to Prestadír at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales","Prestadír will speak with you again just across the border of Enedwaith and Dunland, in the Bonevales, west of the road.","Talk to Prestadír just inside the entrance of the Bonevales, west of the road from Enedwaith","You have found the entrance to a hidden valley","'Let us now travel south into Dunland by way of the Bonevales, ${PLAYER}. We will speak again once we cross over, west of the road that enters Dunland.'","Prestadír has asked you to scout the Bonevales and learn what threats may lie in wait here and to help Bledhun and his friends.","'This will be a good place from which to launch our exploration of the Bonevales, ${PLAYER}. We should help the people of the Bonevales as much as we can, for they could be valuable allies against the dangers that await us further south.'","Help Bledhun and his friends, then meet Prestadír at the hidden valley","You have decided to travel with the group heading south into Dunland by way of the Bonevales.","Prestadír is waiting to speak with you at the camp he established in a hidden valley in the Bonevales.","'There is a hidden valley to the south which will serve us well for a camp. Go there, and we will speak again if it be so, but first you should help Bledhun and his friends.'","Book 4, Chapter 2: The Valley of Bones","'We are here, ${PLAYER}. We have crossed over into the Bonevales. We need to know what the situation in this valley may be, and what threats could endanger this leg of our quest.\
\
'Bledhun here tells a tale of mysterious happenings. You should hear him out and do as he says. We will need allies in this land.\
\
'Once you have aided Bledhun and his friends, we can meet up again in a hidden valley to the south. It will be the perfect location from which to scout the twisting ways of the Bonevales. Travel ahead and meet me at the camp there.'","'I am glad that you have chosen to accompany my group into the Bonevales, ${PLAYER}. The road will be dangerous, and I could use your abilities. We will be mostly in the open and exposed unless we are very careful to stay in the shadow of the cliffs.\
\
'We will not travel by the road! I will meet up with you just west of the road as it enters Dunland.\
\
'Let us be off at once! We can assess what awaits us once we cross into the Bonevales.'"},
[2128]={"Talk to Gandalf just inside the entrance to Minas Tirith","'Faramir lives, but that is no natural wound. I hope there is little foundation for my fears, but I will tell you that I have seen one in his condition before.'","Prince Imrahil has dismounted from his steed just inside the gates of Minas Tirith, on the western end of the Pelennor Fields.\
\
You helped save Faramir from death at the hands of the Orcs, but he is grievously wounded. Prince Imrahil of Dol Amroth has borne him back to the city, and wishes to speak with you.","Mount your steed and talk to Derufin outside the Causeway Forts to begin the ride to Minas Tirith","Book 4, Chapter 2: Too Far From the City","'Tell my brother when you are ready to ride to Minas Tirith!'","Gandalf can be found just within the gates to Minas Tirith.\
\
Faramir has suffered an unnatural wound during the retreat from the Causeway Forts, and Gandalf bears a concerned expression.","'I do not want to worry you, ${PLAYER}, but there is something unnatural about the wound suffered by Faramir during his retreat from the Causeway Forts. I have seen a wound of its type before, but this seems to have a greatly-accelerated pace and the healing hands of Elrond are many mountains away.'\
\
Gandalf sighs wearily.\
\
'There were many servants of the Enemy near to Faramir on that field, ${PLAYER}. We must hope that his wound was not caused by a weapon of morgul-make, for there will be no hope of a cure if that be so. I told Imrahil the same as I am telling you: do not speak of this worry to Denethor. It may prove unnecessary, but we must not give him reason to despair for the life of Faramir. The young captain is his only remaining heir, and we need the Steward to focus on the battle that is sure to come if Minas Tirith is to stand.'\
\
Gandalf suddenly stares at you piercingly.\
\
'Of course I am glad to see you, ${PLAYER}! But there is now work to be done, and little time in which to do it! The pleasantries can wait until after the war is done, if that is a boon we are to be given!'","'I wish we had met under different circumstances, ${PLAYER}, but I am glad you came to Faramir's defence when you did. His wound is not deep, but I fear that some fell sorcery remains within it. He swoons, and does not respond to our voices.\
\
'I will bring him to his father in the White Tower. Steward Denethor will want to see what has become of his son. I hope that son and father both will have the strength to come through this. The line is strong; I am sure they will.\
\
'Still, for Faramir to be wounded thus, and so soon after word reached us of his brother's demise... it seems that there will be no end to the challenges set before us in these dark days! I wish we could sit and speak in peace of Dol Amroth my home, but that is a wish that must wait. I go now to the Steward!'","'Quickly, now! Let us ride to the White City! Follow me!'","The forces of the Enemy have taken the Causeway Forts, and now the expanse of the Pelennor lies between you and the walls of the White City.","Talk to Prince Imrahil just inside the entrance to Minas Tirith","'The Pelennor is wide, and it will not be long before it fills with the forces of the Enemy. Climb aboard your steed, ${PLAYER}, and tell me when you are ready to ride to Minas Tirith!'","Derufin is outside the Causeway Forts, on the eastern end of the Pelennor Fields.\
\
Duilin and Derufin are ready to climb aboard their steeds and ride to Minas Tirith. They wait only for your word that you are ready to do the same."},
[2129]={"Book 4, Chapter 30: The Rescue","Talk to Halbarad at the Rohirrim scout-camp","'You and the prince of Rohan have my thanks, ${PLAYER}. These have been dark days, both for my people and for Middle-earth. I am grateful for the lives that you have saved and mourn the friends we have lost.\
\
'Today, we rest. Tomorrow, we will go to the Fords with Théodred. He has aided us; we will then aid him and pass into Rohan to search for Aragorn my chieftain.\
\
'It is a thing of wonder to me that you have seen within the Ring of Isengard and escaped to speak of it. You bring word of the rise of Isengard, but do those tidings hold anything we can use to stop it? Is this notice enough for us to stop the designs of Saruman?\
\
'I hope it is, ${PLAYER}. I fear that it is not. We will speak again soon.'","'I am ready to begin if you are. Let us rescue your friends from the traitorous Falcon-clan.'","Théodred is at the forward encampment in Tâl Methedras.\
\
Théodred is waiting to speak with you about beginning the attack on the prison-caves where the Grey Company is being held.","Théodred is satisfied with the steps you have taken to prepare and is now ready to move on the prison-caves to rescue the Grey Company.","Halbarad is at Théodred's camp in the Gravenwood.\
\
You have come alive out of the prison-caves, along with Halbarad and some other surviving members of the Grey Company.","Talk to Théodred and begin the attack on the prison-caves","'The time is now. We are as ready as we will ever be. Let us move on the prison-caves to rescue as many of your friends as live still to be rescued.\
\
'Speak with me when you are ready.'"},
[2132]={"Talk to Doronir at the Gate of Stars to the Fifth Circle","'I see that Mithrandir has vouchsafed for you, ${PLAYER}, but it is not enough for me to teach you the greater pass-word for this gate. I will teach you the lesser pass-word, as I have been instructed to do for friends of the Wizard that are not known to me. The pass-word is <rgb=#00FF00>Poetry</rgb>. Understand that the lesser pass-words change frequently, so conclude your business here with haste.\
\
'The Fifth Circle of the city is known as the Sages' Tier, and it is a place of learning. Scholars study the stars from its orrery and tower, and natural philosophers make learned arguments within its quiet courtyards. Several archives can be found in the Fifth Circle, as can the Houses of Lore and the scriptorium where copies are made of valued documents and records.'","Talk to Thalgam at the Sword-gate to the Second Circle","'Mithrandir says you are trustworthy? There are some for whom that would not be enough, ${PLAYER}, but it is not my place to deny you. I will teach you the greater pass-word for the Lords' Gate. The pass-word is <rgb=#00FF00>House of Stewards</rgb>. There has been no King for nearly a thousand years, and Gondor is now ruled by a line of Stewards.\
\
'Mere minutes ago, I allowed the Prince of Dol Amroth passage through this gate, and it seemed to me that he bore the body of Faramir, the son of Steward Denethor. I could not tell if there was life in him, but I fear for the line of the Stewards if he should die, or has done so already. It is whispered that Boromir has already fallen.'\
\
Idhir shakes his head with a frown.\
\
'Forgive my gossiping tongue! Beyond this gate is the Fourth Circle, known to folk of the city as the Players' Tier. Minstrels and actors frequent the Court of Voronwë and the Blue Theatre, and their wealthy patrons gather at the baths and guest-houses between performances. The entrance to the great cistern that feeds most of the city is also on this level, but you would be wise to leave it be. The footing can be treacherous, and the Waterstead has claimed more than a few careless lives.'","Talk to Garthor at the Gate of Stones to the Sixth Circle","Talk to Soromar at the Silver Gate to the Third Circle","'Mithrandir's pledge is of value, ${PLAYER}, but I must follow the commands of the Steward. It is his wish that friends of the Wizard learn the lesser pass-word for the Citadel and no other. The pass-word is <rgb=#00FF00>Justice</rgb>.\
\
'The Seventh Circle of the city is called the Citadel, but it is also known as the Stewards' Tier. Some of the common folk refer to it as the Kings' Tier, but that seems distasteful to me. There has been no King in Gondor for many hundreds of years, and the wise rule of the Stewards has served us well, if you ask me.\
\
'The Tower of Ecthelion stands proudly atop the city, a sign of Gondor's might. Steward Denethor rules within the Hall of Kings, but you will only see within at his direct invitation. The path atop the city's pier is patrolled by guards of the Citadel and kept clear of obstructions, if you wish to walk the Ship's Prow and behold the view. Do so in safety, while that is still possible!'","Book 4, Chapter 3: The Seven Gates","'Mithrandir's word is enough for me, ${PLAYER}, and I will teach you the greater pass-word for the Sword-gate. The pass-word is <rgb=#00FF00>Beacons of Gondor</rgb>. Share it with no one!\
\
'Beyond this gate lies the Second Circle of the city, known to the people of Gondor as the Soldiers' Tier. This tier of the city is home to several ale-halls and barracks catering to soldiers and the town-guard, as well as a number of armouries and the Wielding-yard.\
\
'Go in peace, and cause no trouble within the city. We have enough of that to spare, if the scouts can be trusted!'","Thalgam guards the Sword-gate to the Second Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.","Talk to Mithrandir in the Court of the Fountain, in the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith","Idhir guards the Lords' Gate to the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.","Gandalf has arranged for you to be given the pass-words to the gates of the city, so you may travel freely among the various tiers of Minas Tirith.","'I will teach you the greater pass-word for the Silver Gate. The pass-word is <rgb=#00FF00>Anárion</rgb>. You will find it easy to remember, for he was the son of Elendil who ordered the construction of this city. At that time it was called Minas Anor, the Tower of the Sun, though it has since been renamed Minas Tirith, the Tower of Guard.\
\
'Beyond this gate lies the Third Circle of the city, the Craftsmen's Tier. This tier of the city houses shops and smithies, as well as the Clothiers' Market and Fellow-hall. Builders and merchants will find much to attend their needs on this tier of the city, as will any who seek the auctioneers at the House of Clamor.'","Talk to Linharn at the Gate of the Citadel to the Seventh Circle","Mithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the uppermost level of the city.\
\
You have obtained pass-words for the seven levels of Minas Tirith, and should now talk to Mithrandir in the Seventh Circle.","Soromar guards the Silver Gate to the Third Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.","'This is the Gate of Stones to the Sixth Circle of the city, and it is my duty to tell you that Mithrandir's word of your worthiness earns you the lesser pass-word only. Conduct your business with speed and depart. The pass-word for now is <rgb=#00FF00>Vigilance</rgb>.\
\
'The Sixth Circle is known to folk of the city as the Masters' Tier, but few of them ever climb to this gate. The Houses of Healing can be found on this tier, along with the Cold Hall where the dead are brought to be washed, clothed, and prepared for internment in the tombs or, in the case of the common folk, the ossuaries within the Hill of Guard.\
\
'The Dome of the Sun can also be found on this level. That is where the Council of Gondor meets to decide matters of state, and errand-riders bring their resolutions throughout the city and to the other reaches of Gondor. They have had much to discuss of late, and I urge you not to bother them.'","'I have given you my pledge of your trustworthiness. Show it to the guards at each gate and they will teach you the pass-words.'","Garthor guards the Gate of Stones to the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.","'You travel as I do, ${PLAYER}, on the wings of the storm. Men may call you a harbinger of dark times, but in truth we go where we are most needed. Today that is Minas Tirith, the Tower of Guard. You will need to freely travel throughout the city if you are to best serve the people of Minas Tirith. Any obstruction to your free passage will hinder your efforts, and that is a help to the Enemy!\
\
'The city climbs this easternmost spur of the White Mountains, ascending in seven levels, each separated by a gate. Men of Gondor safe-guard greater and lesser pass-words for each gate; the lesser pass-words change frequently, and the greater pass-words remain in use for much longer.\
\
'I will give you my pledge of your trustworthiness. Show it to the guards at each gate and they will teach you the pass-words for each gate. And one more thing, ${PLAYER}. The men of Gondor do not know me by the name Gandalf. They call me Mithrandir, and I invite you to do the same!'","Talk to Idhir at the Lords' Gate to the Fourth Circle","'You were denied the greater pass-words for some of the levels? What rubbish, ${PLAYER}! Denethor seeks to demonstrate his authority. He should be preparing for war with his enemies instead of hindering his allies! It does not matter. For now you have free passage through the city.\
\
'Minas Tirith is strong, and it was built in seven levels with strategic purpose. Did you notice how the gates alternate sides, first on the south, then the north, and then on the south again? Such a design causes the ascending road to pass through the Neaths in the pier at regular intervals, and carving so many arched tunnels in the stone cannot have been easy. It was done at Anárion's command so the city could be easily fortified, and an opposing force would have a long road to march before reaching the heights of the city.\
\
'The walls of the city have never been breached. No enemy has broken the gates. Denethor knows this. He believes that Minas Tirith cannot fall, and that knowledge gives him strength, but it is also a weakness. He refuses the help I might give him, and the help you could provide. I think that is an error.'","Linharn guards the Gate of the Citadel of Minas Tirith.\
\
Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city.","Doronir guards the Gate of Stars to the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Mithrandir has given his word that you can be trusted and should be taught the pass-words for each level of the city."},
[2133]={"Lord Glorfindel se encuentra en Imladris, alto sobre el Bruinen y al este, junto a la cascada fuera de la Última Casa Amigable.\
\
Glorfindel espera hablar contigo a tu regreso del Vado del Bruinen.","'El Vado del Bruinen está al oeste de Imladris, al pie de las empinadas colinas. Allí los Nazgûl fueron detenidos por el poder de mando del Señor Elrond sobre esas aguas, y allí debes sostener en alto el berilo que te di.\
\
'Hablaremos más a tu regreso.'","Lleva el berilo de Glorfindel a Lord Glorfindel.","'Has regresado, ${PLAYER}. ¿Notaste algún cambio en el berilo que te di al llegar al Vado?\
\
'¿El berilo comenzó a brillar? Eso es lo que esperaba, y me alegra que haya sido así, pues será nuestro medio para localizar al Nazgûl que permanece oculto en el bosque.\
\
'Los Nueve, siervos del Enemigo y sombras bajo su gran sombra, son criaturas de tal maldad que la tierra no puede soportar su presencia. Este berilo brillará en los lugares donde hayan estado. Nos permitirá seguir el rastro del Jinete desaparecido.'","Los Nazgûl fueron impedidos de cruzar el Bruinen en este vado.","El Vado del Bruinen está al oeste de Imladris, al pie de las empinadas pendientes.\
\
Lord Glorfindel te ha dado un berilo y te ha pedido que pruebes sus poderes sosteniéndolo en alto en las orillas del Bruinen.","'Bienvenido a Imladris, ${PLAYER}. Son tiempos de problemas, pero por ahora, al menos, el velo de sombra se mantiene alejado y nos encontramos en paz.\
\
'Traes graves noticias de parte de Elladan, pero no son del todo inesperadas. Temía que no todos los Nazgûl fueran detenidos por el Bruinen. Este siervo errante del Enemigo dejará una marca en la tierra —puede que ya lo haya hecho— y podemos usarla para rastrearlo.\
\
'Te doy mi berilo y te pido que lo sostengas en alto en el Vado del Bruinen. Regresa a mí una vez que lo hayas hecho, y hablaremos más.'","Lord Glorfindel se encuentra en Imladris, al este de Thorenhad, contemplando las cascadas junto a la Última Casa Amigable.\
\
Elladan te ha pedido que consultes con el señor Elfo Glorfindel sobre el Jinete desaparecido.","'Sabemos más que antes, ${PLAYER}, pero aún no sabemos lo que debemos, para la seguridad de todos los que viven o viajan por esta región: el paradero del Nazgûl desaparecido. Su corcel fue nuestro mayor aliado en esta búsqueda, pues mientras él podía quitarse la capa y permanecer casi invisible, su caballo era un ser mortal y su rastro físico podía seguirse. Con la criatura ahora muerta, ya sea por agotamiento o a manos de su amo, nuestra capacidad para rastrear al Nazgûl se ha reducido.\
\
'Reducida, pero no perdida. Te pediría que regreses a Imladris y consultes con Lord Glorfindel, pues se le considera muy sabio y puede tener alguna estrategia que aún no hayamos probado. Mantiene estrecho consejo con mi padre y con Mithrandir, y a menudo contempla el agua que cae junto a la casa de mi padre.\
\
'Él podría ayudarnos a encontrar a este Nazgûl desaparecido.'","Elladan se alegró de que hayas encontrado al corcel del Jinete desaparecido, pero no estará satisfecho hasta conocer el destino de su maestro.","Libro 4, Capítulo 3: La Sabiduría del Lord Glorfindel.","'Busca a Glorfindel en Imladris, cerca de las cascadas junto a la casa de mi padre. Suele contemplar el agua que cae y es contado entre los Sabios.'","Sostenés el berilo de Glorfindel en alto, y este brilla con una luz pálida.","'Te estoy esperando para que regreses con el berilo que te di, ${PLAYER}.'","Usa el berilo de Glorfindel en el Vado del Bruinen."},
[2134]={"'Las palabras de Lord Glorfindel son muy sabias, y su regalo de este berilo nos da esperanza de que podamos recuperar la pista de este Nazgûl perdido. Te doy las gracias, ${PLAYER}, pero ahora debo determinar a dónde debemos llevar el berilo para revelar la ubicación del Nazgûl.'","'El campamento de Elladan en Thorenhad se encuentra entre las Gargantas del Bruinen, al oeste de Imladris y al norte de las guaridas de osos. Llévale el berilo y mis buenos deseos, y espero que cada uno dé a los hijos de Elrond lo que necesitan para buscar este mal.'","Lleva el berilo de Glorfindel a Elladan","'He enfrentado a los Nazgûl antes. Son terribles de ver.'","'¿Ha dado fruto la búsqueda del Nazgûl desaparecido?'","Libro 4, Capítulo 4: Recuperando la Pista","Elladan está en Thorenhad, su campamento entre las Gargantas del Bruinen, al norte de las guaridas de osos.\
\
Lord Glorfindel te ha enviado de regreso a Elladan con un berilo, una piedra élfica que brilla cuando se acerca a lugares donde el gran mal ha dejado su marca.","Lord Glorfindel te dio un berilo que brilla cuando se lleva a lugares donde el gran mal ha dejado su marca.","'No suelo adentrarme en la naturaleza salvaje, aunque lo haré cuando la necesidad sea grande, como podrían decirte el Montaraz Aragorn o su pequeño amigo Frodo Bolsón. Los hijos de Elrond son más adecuados para dirigir tu búsqueda del Nazgûl desaparecido.\
\
'Dejo mi berilo bajo tu cuidado por el momento y te pido que lo lleves de regreso a Elladan en su campamento de Thorenhad. Él sabrá dónde debes llevarlo para seguir las huellas del Nazgûl.\
\
'¡Ve con rapidez y con claridad de visión! El berilo te ayudará a encontrar a este sirviente errante del Enemigo, pero me pregunto, ¿qué harás cuando lo encuentres?'","'Hablas del berilo de Lord Glorfindel, pero no lo veo. ¿Lo has extraviado?'"},
[2135]={"The angry Dunlending has been cowed","The village of Galtrev is a village divided. Does it pose a danger to the Grey Company?","Halbarad wants you to talk to the residents of Galtrev in order to learn of the situation in Pren Gwydh.","'You should watch yourself in Galtrev, duvodiad.'","'¡Fuera de aquí!'","Catrin has directed you to speak with Dai, Hulun, or Idwal in Galtrev.","Talk to Catrin in Galtrev","'Leave me, duvodiad! You don't belong here!'","She looks you up and down appraisingly.\
\
'You want to know what is happening in these lands? You are far from home... so far from home. In Galtrev you must not offend the wrong people. It is dangerous to make enemies here, yes it is.\
\
'If you seek information, you seek one of these three: Dai, Hulun, or Idwal. They will teach you about these lands.'","'Someone in the village may tell us what to expect in Pren Gwydh. Speak first to people in the lower reaches of the village.'","Book 4, Chapter 4: The Lower Village","'I did not think to see you again, Duvodiad, but I was wrong, yes. I heard the cries of that pathetic Ox from here!\
\
'Folk of many clans live in Galtrev, but those who have grown wealthy from the gifts of Saruman float to the top. We of the lower village work hard just to get by, but the task-masters in the upper village live off of our labours and return the products of them to the Wizard.\
\
'Perhaps you can be of some use to the Hebog-lûth, the Clan of the Falcon. We stand against those who have thrown in with Saruman.'","'Folk of many clans live in Galtrev.'","Catrin is in the village of Galtrev.\
\
You have been told to speak with Catrin.","Catrin is in Galtrev.\
\
You should speak with Catrin again.","'Watch yourself, duvodiad.'","'Do not waste my time! Speak with Catrin if you must speak with anyone!'","Find someone in Galtrev who will share information with you","Talk to Dai, Hulun, or Idwal","'You should watch yourself in Pren Gwydh.'","'We need information, ${PLAYER}. Galtrev is a place of no little significance in Dunland, and I want to know if Saruman's promises have already taken hold here.\
\
'Start in the lower reaches of the village and see if anyone will speak to you of the situation here in Pren Gwydh.'","'Who are you, Duvodiad? You do not belong in this land. You are not welcome.'\
\
She scowls at you.\
\
'Speak with Catrin and leave me be! She knows what should be done with duvodiad.'","'This land belongs to the Ox Clan! You will not leave here alive!'","'You should find Dai, Hulun, or Idwal here in Galtrev. They will teach you about Dunland, Duvodiad.'","'My clan is that of the Falcon.'","'Get out of my sight!'"},
[2136]={"'There are some folk with whom you should speak. The Council of Gondor meets in the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle. Introduce yourself to the doorward and do what you can to aid the Council.\
\
'I came here in the company of Peregrin Took, hobbit of the Shire. He is now a Guard of the Citadel -- the less said of that, the better -- and I expect he could use a friendly word from you, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I spoke with Lord Duinhir of the Blackroot Vale a short time ago, and it seems that his sons left the city without his permission, and indeed against his direct command. I understand you met Duilin and Derufin during their ill-advised adventure. Find them within one of the taverns in the lower circles of the city, and perhaps something can be done to soothe their father's temper.'","Talk to Peregrin Took and complete 'Guard of the Citadel'","The Council of Gondor meets in the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Peregrin Took can be found somewhere in the Citadel. Duilin and Derufin can be found within one of the taverns in the lower circles of the city.\
\
Mithrandir has asked you to provide help to a number of people within the city before the city is besieged.","Prince Imrahil is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate of the city, looking for someone to undertake a dangerous mission.","Talk to Duilin and complete 'In Need of Discipline'","'There you are, ${PLAYER}. I have been looking for you!\
\
'The Prince of Dol Amroth was looking for someone to undertake a mission of some danger, and I suggested that you would make the ideal candidate. Hurry down to the First Circle and learn if Imrahil has already sent someone else.'","Talk to Imrahil in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate to the city","'We must not rely solely on the strength of the walls, ${PLAYER}. We must ensure that the people are strong as well. It will not be long before the Enemy is arrayed before the walls, and in that moment the city's defenders will need courage with deep foundations. There are some folk with whom you should speak, my friend; unresolved matters may linger, and cast hearts into confusion when the end approaches.\
\
'Day to day affairs in the city are managed by a group of officials that comprise the Council of Gondor. They meet in the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle. Introduce yourself to the doorward and do what you can to aid the Council.\
\
'I came here in the company of Peregrin Took, hobbit of the Shire. He is now a Guard of the Citadel -- the less said of that, the better -- and I expect he could use a friendly word from you, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I spoke with Lord Duinhir of the Blackroot Vale a short time ago, and it seems that his sons left the city without his permission, and indeed against his direct command. I understand you met Duilin and Derufin during their ill-advised adventure. Find them within one of the taverns in the lower circles of the city, and perhaps something can be done to soothe their father's temper.'","'The Prince of Dol Amroth was looking for someone to undertake a mission of some danger, and I suggested that you would make the ideal candidate. Hurry down to the First Circle and learn if Imrahil has already sent someone else.'","With battle on the horizon, Mithrandir wants you to help the people of Minas Tirith ready themselves for the coming storm.","'Mithrandir said you would be happy to undertake this errand, ${PLAYER}. I am pleased to see he was right.'","Book 4, Chapter 4: Tower of Guard","Talk to Othnar and complete 'The Council of Gondor'","Mithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You have aided the Council of Gondor, Peregrin Took, and the sons of Lord Duinhir of Blackroot Vale, and should now return to Mithrandir.","Talk to Mithrandir in the Court of the Fountain"},
[2137]={"Ingold is the Captain of the Out-wall, and can be found at the North-gate in the Rammas Echor.\
\
Prince Imrahil has asked you to learn why Ingold has not yet returned to Minas Tirith, and to learn the situation in Talath Anor.","'You have done well, my friend. I too have slain many of our enemies, but it seems that two more cross the river from Cair Andros for each one that I defeat. This does not seem to be a battle we can win.'","'After you have defeated the Sûhalar Easterlings, look for Barathant in the town of Crithost. He is a passionate man and will not retreat until the very last moment, but I feel that moment is fast approaching.'","'You are an adventurer and can do a great deal of good in this land beyond the Rammas! Help me defeat Warg-riders, and once we have faced these threats, I give you my word that we can return to the North-gate.'","Defeat Sûhalar Easterlings in Talath Anor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am alive, ${PLAYER}, and I still possess the fighting spirit! I will not retreat to Minas Tirith until the very last moment, and you will not be able to convince me. It is futile!\
\
'Much of my family evacuated Minas Tirith and went to the vale of Tumladen among the last few waggons, but my brothers remain in the White City. I can still slay Wargs and their riders in Talath Anor, and every foe I dispatch means one fewer to menace my brothers.\
\
'Aid me in this! You are an adventurer and can do a great deal of good in this land beyond the Rammas! Once we have faced these threats, I give you my word that we can return to the North-gate.'","Talk to Barathant in Crithost","Defeat Wargs or Warg-riders in Talath Anor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Prince Imrahil needs someone to learn what the situation may be north of the city, in Talath Anor.","Defeated Warg-kind in Talath Anor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Orcs, Wargs, and a strange group of Easterlings have overrun the plain of Talath Anor. It is this last that gives me the most concern. They are called Sûhalar, and little is known of them. If you can defeat these new foes in Talath Anor, we may learn how best to face them, and I ask that you then look for Barathant in the town of Crithost. Once he returns, all of us can then return to Minas Tirith.'","'We are still working to repair the wall. I cannot return to the city just yet! I have disturbing news, and it enforces my desire not to leave my post until the last possible moment.\
\
'There is a second army, ${PLAYER}. I think this second Mordor-host crossed the river at Cair Andros, though I cannot be certain; none of my scouts have made it near enough to the island to see in whose hands it lies. I await word from my man in Crithost, Barathant, but he has not returned yet; I do not know if he still lives.\
\
'I do know that Orcs, Wargs, and a strange group of Easterlings have overrun the plain of Talath Anor. It is this last that gives me the most concern. They are called Sûhalar, and little is known of them. If you can defeat these new foes in Talath Anor, we may learn how best to face them, and I ask that you then look for Barathant in the town of Crithost. Once he returns, all of us can then return to Minas Tirith.'","'When Mithrandir came to the city, he told me that he passed through the North-gate in the Rammas Echor and spoke with its captain. He found Ingold supervising the repair of the wall, and advised him that it came too late; swords would be of more use than trowels in this late hour.\
\
'Ingold has not yet returned to the city, but I need to know the situation north of the Rammas. Go to the North-gate of the Rammas Echor, and learn why Ingold has not yet come back. I applaud him for bracing the wall and the gate in it, but he will be of more use to Gondor alive in Minas Tirith than dead at the North-gate.'","Talk to Ingold at the North-gate in the Rammas Echor","Book 4, Chapter 5: Beyond the Rammas","Defeated Sûhalar Easterlings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","If he still lives, Barathant should be somewhere within the town of Crithost, in Talath Anor.\
\
Ingold asked you to find Barathant after you defeated some of the Sûhalar Easterlings.","Warg-riders can be found throughout Talath Anor.\
\
Barathant has asked you to defeat the Warg-riders that have overrun the lands north of the Rammas Echor.","Barathant is in the town of Crithost, in Talath Anor.\
\
You defeated many foes and should now return to Crithost.","Sûhalar Easterlings can be found throughout the plains of Talath Anor, in Old Anórien.\
\
Ingold, Captain of the Out-wall, has asked you to defeat Sûhalar Easterlings throughout Talath Anor.","'I need to know the situation north of the Rammas Echor. Go to the North-gate of the Rammas, and learn why Ingold has not yet come back. I applaud him for bracing the wall and the gate in it, but he will be of more use to Gondor alive in Minas Tirith than dead at the North-gate!'"},
[2138]={"The water here is a suitable location for dumping the axes","Catrin is in the lower village of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh.\
\
Catrin will be pleased to hear that you have disrupted work at the lumber-camp.","Collect lumber-axes from the camp north-east of Galtrev (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The lumber-camp is north-east of here. Go there and steal some of the axes, or take them from hostile Dunlendings throughout Pren Gwydh, then bring them to the pond east of the lumber camp and throw them into the water. Rust will be our ally!'","Lumber-piles can be found in the upper village of Galtrev.\
\
Catrin in the lower village of Galtrev has a torch for you to carry to lumber-piles throughout the upper village.","'Use that torch to burn piles of lumber throughout the upper village of Galtrev! That will make them scurry!'","'Wonderful, wonderful! Oh, you are a treat, my new friend.'\
\
Catrin cackles with delight.\
\
'The Hebog-lûth, the Falcon-clan, stands against Saruman and seeks to cause trouble for those who side with him. I think you will be a comfort to us...and perhaps we to you and yours.'","The pond where Catrin wanted you to throw the lumber-axes is east of the lumber-camp.\
\
Catrin asked you to steal lumber-axes from the camp north-east of Galtrev and throw them into the pond east of the camp.","Catrin desires to use you in her efforts to make things difficult for Saruman's servants in Pren Gwydh.","'I do my small part to make things difficult for Saruman.'","'You have only done half of what I asked. The theft is done, but the axes could be taken from you and used again! You must throw them into the pond east of the lumber-camp before I will be satisfied with your efforts.'","'You caused some trouble out there, I trust? Ha! Good. There is more for you to do.\
\
'Wood from the lumber-camp has already been collected and is being stored in the upper village until it can be carted south. Take this torch and burn the wood-piles! That will make them scurry!'","Find the pond in which to throw the lumber axes","Talk to Catrin in Galtrev","Throw the bundle of axes into the pond","The lumber-camp in Pren Gwydh is north-east of Galtrev.\
\
Catrin has asked you to steal axes at the lumber-camp or from other hostile Dunlendings throughout Pren Gwydh, then throw the axes in a pond east of the camp.","The lumber axes fall beneath the surface of the water","'Rain in the morning is a sign that wealth is on its way.'","'It is the little things that count, I've always said.'","Talk to Catrin at Galtrev","Book 4, Chapter 5: Catrin's Rebellion","Collected lumber-axes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Catrin is in the lower village of Galtrev.\
\
You have burned wood-piles throughout the upper village and should return now to Catrin.","'People of many clans have listened to the promises of Saruman, and where his words are not enough, his gold does the trick. Even the folk of Galtrev are put to work to further the Wizard's aims.\
\
'At the lumber-camp north-east of here, trees are felled and the wood prepared for carting to Isengard. Go there, steal their axes, and throw them in the pond east of the lumber-camp. Even if they fish them out, the rust will make the axes unreliable and difficult to use. Members of the dragon clan may have brought the axes to other settlements in Pren Gwydh. Those will do as well!\
\
'A simple act of rebellion, maybe, but its effect could be sweeping.'","Grab a torch and burn lumber-piles (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Burned lumber-piles (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[2139]={"'Te di mis notas sobre las cuevas de trolls que debes buscar, ${PLAYER}. Desciende a la cámara más profunda dentro de las cuevas Torogrod, Nurath y Thingroth y sostén en alto el berilo de Glorfindel.'","Encuentra la cámara más profunda de Nurath","Encuentra la cámara más profunda de Thingroth","'¿Buscas la cueva de Thingroth? No sé si ese es su nombre, pero hay una cueva de trolls al este; pasé por ella mientras buscaba los Valles Trenzados.'","'Has hecho lo que te pedí, ${PLAYER}, y por ello te estoy agradecido. ¡No frunzas el ceño! Si no hubieras buscado en las cuevas, nunca podríamos estar seguros de que el Nazgûl no se ocultaba allí, esperando su momento para atacar de nuevo. Ahora hemos eliminado algunos de sus posibles escondites, y por eso debemos sentirnos complacidos.\
\
'Tomaré el berilo de Glorfindel y se lo devolveré a él. Para ti, tengo otra vía de investigación, y podría ser que esta dé fruto.'","Elladan está en Thorenhad, su campamento entre las Gargantas del Bruinen, al norte de las guaridas de osos.\
\
Elladan espera saber qué reveló el berilo de Glorfindel: que el Nazgûl desaparecido nunca estuvo en ninguna de las cuevas que buscaste.","Sostienes el berilo de Glorfindel en alto, pero permanece oscuro.","Libro 4, Capítulo 5: Oculto en la Oscuridad","Has llegado a la cámara más profunda de Thingroth.","Elladan te entregó sus notas con las ubicaciones de las cuevas de trolls.\
\
Elladan quiere que busques tres cuevas de trolls con el berilo de Glorfindel.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Usar la Piedra Élfica Brillante te permite acceder al beneficio de inspiración mientras estás solo o en una hermandad más pequeña.</rgb>","Has llegado a la cámara más profunda de Torogrod.","La fuerza crece en tu pecho. Aquí puedes usar la Piedra Élfica Brillante para recurrir a la inspiración.","Usar el berilo de Glorfindel.","'He reflexionado sobre nuestro enigma, ${PLAYER}, y aunque no sé si esta es la respuesta, mi corazón me dice que debemos agotar este curso antes de asegurarnos de que es infructuoso.\
\
'Muchas cuevas salpican la naturaleza del Bosque de los Trolls, hogar de las criaturas que dan nombre a este lugar. El Nazgûl desaparecido sufrió un daño grave cuando quedó atrapado entre las llamas de Glorfindel, el Montaraz Aragorn y las aguas del Bruinen, y debió escapar a algún rincón aislado del bosque para recuperar fuerzas; creo que huyó a una de las cuevas de trolls.\
\
'Escribiré los nombres y ubicaciones de tres cuevas. Desciende a la cámara más profunda de cada una y sostén en alto el berilo de Glorfindel. Debemos saber si el Nazgûl se escondió en alguna de estas cuevas para poder retomar su rastro. Lleva aliados a estas cuevas, pues los trolls que se ocultan allí son peligrosos. Aquí están mis notas, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Usar la Piedra Élfica Brillante te permite acceder al beneficio de inspiración mientras estás solo o en una Comunidad pequeña.</rgb>","Has llegado a la cámara más profunda de Nurath.","Si no estás en una comunidad, puedes usar la Piedra Élfica Brillante para invocar inspiración.","Encuentra la cámara más profunda de Torogrod","Elladan ha determinado que el Jinete desaparecido podría estar escondido en alguna de las muchas cuevas que salpican los riscos de los Bosque de los Trolls y quiere que busques varias de ellas con el berilo de Glorfindel.","Devuelve el berilo de Glorfindel a Elladan.","'No tienes el berilo de Glorfindel, ${PLAYER}. Necesito que me lo devuelvas.'"},
[2140]={"'¿El Onod te atacó? Esa es una noticia funesta, pues no es propio de los pastores de árboles.\
\
'Son presagios sombríos, ${PLAYER}. Debes contárselo a Elladan de inmediato. Búscalo en Thorenhad, al norte de las cuevas de osos de las Gargantas del Bruinen.'","'Mucho de lo que era hermoso en el Bosque de los Trolls ha sido vuelto feo por las fuerzas del mal.'","Uno de los Onodrim, criatura de días antiguos, fue visto en el valle de los gigantes al sur del Páramo Alto, en lo alto sobre el Bruinen. Según los informes, Barachen lo vio de pie junto a unos árboles imponentes cuando descendía hacia el valle.\
\
Barachen afirmó haber visto a uno de los Onodrim en algún lugar del Bosque de los Trolls, y Elladan cree que es posible que este Onod sepa algo sobre el paradero del Nazgûl desaparecido.","'Me duele escuchar el triste destino del Onodrim que vi.'","Encuentra al Onod","El Onod te observa con ojos inexpresivos. Su piel, semejante a la corteza, está marcada por la corrupción, y su boca se abre y cierra sin emitir sonido. ¡De pronto, los pozos profundos de sus ojos se agitan con ira!","'Siempre he creído que los Onodrim de leyenda han caminado entre la zona boscosa del Bosque de los Trolls, pero jamás había visto uno con mis propios ojos....... hasta ahora.\
\
'Mientras ascendía por el Páramo Alto en dirección a Imladris, llevando mensajes de Rochwen y Alphlanc, me invadió un extraño presentimiento. Me aparté del sendero y descendí hacia el sur por una gran pendiente hasta el valle de los gigantes. Desde la distancia contemplé a uno de los Onodrim, erguido como un árbol majestuoso, con hojas tornándose rojas. Mientras lo observaba, se volvió lentamente y se ocultó tras un peñasco, desapareciendo de mi vista.\
\
'Ten cuidado en tu viaje, pues los gigantes de ese valle son formidables, y habla con este Onod. Puede que sepa dónde está el Nazgûl que Elladan busca.'","'¿El Onod te atacó? Los pastores de árboles de antaño eran pacíficos y preferían permanecer inadvertidos entre los árboles antes que tratar con extraños, ya fuese en paz o en violencia.\
\
'No comprendo el significado de estas señales, ${PLAYER}. Nuestros problemas pueden ser mucho más extensos de lo que suponía.'","Libro 4, Capítulo 6: El saber de los Onodrim","Mientras buscabas en las cuevas de los Trollshaws alguna señal del Nazgûl desaparecido, Elladan oyó hablar de uno de los Onodrim en los parajes salvajes que podría conocer el paradero del Jinete.","'El Páramo Alto se encuentra muy al este, sobre el Bruinen, y un sendero desciende hacia el sur hasta el valle de los gigantes. Cuando entré en el valle, vi al Onod junto a un árbol de hojas rojas, antes de que se volviera y se desvaneciera tras una gran roca. Puede que conozca la presencia del Nazgûl en estas tierras.'","'El campamento de Barachen está al sur, en lo alto de una pendiente bajo la sombra de los altos acantilados —tuércete a la derecha al dejar el camino. Él podrá contarte acerca del Onodrim que vio, si eso es lo que buscas.'","Barachen se encuentra en su campamento, al sur del Gran Camino del Este que cruza el Bosque de los Trolls del sur. Los exploradores que custodian el camino podrán guiarte hasta él.\
\
Elladan te contó que Barachen informó haber visto a uno de los Onodrim en algún lugar del Bosque de los Trolls y quiere que hables con él al respecto.","Elladan está en Thorenhad, su campamento en las Gargantas del Bruinen, al norte de las cuevas de osos.\
\
Elladan se inquietará al conocer el destino del Onod que Barachen vio en el valle de los gigantes.","'Mientras explorabas las cuevas de los trolls de piedra —¡una búsqueda productiva! No te desalientes por no haber revelado aún la ubicación del Nazgûl— recibí noticias de Barachen en el sur del Bosque de los Trolls. Mi hermano lo envió a vigilar las tierras al sur del camino, y parece que esa misión ha dado fruto.\
\
'Barachen ha informado haber visto a uno de los Onodrim errantes. Si esto es cierto, unos ojos más antiguos y sabios que los nuestros quizá hayan visto el paso del Nazgûl y puedan contarnos mucho.\
\
'Viaja hacia el oeste por la carretera que atraviesa el sur de los Trollshaws. Barachen tiene exploradores apostados a lo largo del camino, y uno de ellos podrá dirigirte hasta su campamento. Entonces Barachen te dirá dónde encontrar a nuestro Onodrim extraviado.'","'El campamento de Barachen está en el sur del Bosque de los Trolls, al oeste de aquí. Busca a Rochwen junto al camino... ella ha estado vigilando a quienes viajan por estas tierras y puede guiarte hasta el campamento de Barachen.'","Has derrotado al troll silvano"},
[2141]={"'Some of the scouts have returned, and I am grateful, for I have need of their weapons, as you can see!\
\
'Barathant? No, I have not yet seen him! Did he say he was coming?\
\
'We cannot wait long, ${PLAYER}! If he is coming, he has to get here soon!'","Defeat foes throughout Talath Anor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ingold, the Captain of the Out-wall, is at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor.","'Lead the way to the North-gate in the Rammas Echor! I will be right behind you! Quickly, now!'","'We cannot wait any longer, ${PLAYER}! We must fall back to Minas Tirith! Ride, ride to the city!'","'You found them both? I am glad to hear it!\
\
'Now, ${PLAYER}, lead the way to the North-gate in the Rammas Echor! I will be right behind you!'","Brúnion gladly agrees with you, and runs off","Find Cangrail and tell her to return","'We need to recall two of the scouts I sent forth from Crithost. Go to the north-west and the north-east and tell Cangrail and Brúnion that it is time for them to return to the North-gate. They have done well, but now they must think of their safety! Find them quickly, ${PLAYER}! They are sure to be in danger as the situation north of the Rammas worsens!\
\
'Defeat any enemies you come across, as well. We may be readying for our retreat, but that is no reason not to strike at our enemies while we do!'","'We are nearing the end now. The Mordor-host that pours into Talath Anor shows no sign of slowing. I am almost ready to return to Minas Tirith.\
\
'But first we need to recall two of the scouts I sent forth from Crithost. Go to the north-west and north-east and tell Cangrail and Brúnion that it is time for them to return to the North-gate. They have done well, but now they must think of their safety! Find them quickly, ${PLAYER}! They are sure to be in danger as the situation north of the Rammas worsens!\
\
'Defeat any enemies you come across, as well. We may be readying for our retreat, but that is no reason not to strike at our enemies while we do!'","Talk to Barathant in Crithost","You cannot wait any longer for him to arrive!","Find Brúnion and tell him to return","Retreat to Minas Tirith and talk to Imrahil in the First Circle of the city","Cangrail and Brúnion can be found to the north-west and north-east of Crithost, in Talath Anor.\
\
Barathant asked you to find and recall the scout he sent out from Crithost, and to defeat any enemies you come across in Talath Anor.","Ingold, the Captain of the Out-wall, is at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor.\
\
The scouts in Talath Anor are retreating to the North-gate, and you should do the same. Ingold is waiting for your return.","Barathant never returned to the North-gate, but Ingold cannot wait long for him.","She agrees that it is time to return, and runs off","Book 4, Chapter 6: The Net Closes","'You have already returned? I did not expect to see you so soon after your departure, ${PLAYER}. What can you tell me of the situation in Talath Anor?'\
\
You tell Imrahil about your encounter with the Orcs, Wargs, and Sûhalar Easterlings that occupied Cair Andros and have poured into Talath Anor.\
\
'A second force? It must be a pincer attack! Our Enemy has been planning this for some time, and soon each host will close upon the city.  It will make the triumph of Gondor all the sweeter when those plans are destroyed.'","Wait for Barathant at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor","Barathant is almost ready to return to the city, but first he wants you to recall the scouts he sent out from Crithost.","Talk to Ingold at the North-gate of the Rammas Echor","Barathant is in the town of Crithost, waiting to hear that his scouts have agreed to return to the North-gate of the Rammas Echor.","Prince Imrahil is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, waiting for you to return with news of the situation in Talath Anor.","Defeated foes throughout Talath Anor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'We cannot wait any longer! We must fall back to Minas Tirith! Ride, ride to the city!'"},
[2142]={"'I am glad to have your help, and that of these Rangers.'","Tûr Morva is in Tâl Methedras, to the east of Pren Gwydh.\
\
Catrin has asked you to aid the people of Galtrev and Pren Gwydh as much as you can before moving on to Tâl Methedras.","The guard looks you up and down, suspiciously.\
\
'You say you have helped Catrin in Galtrev? That old woman is always sending us help, but the help is almost never what we need. If you and these Rangers are different, I will bring some of you to see Lheu Brenin. But I hope you do not expect aid from us. The People of the Falcon have their own problems.'","'There is much work to be done if we are to be ready.'","Léolin is suspicious of you, but has agreed to bring you to meet Lheu Brenin.\
\
You have met the guard at the pass into Tâl Methedras, but he is wary of you and the Rangers. He is waiting to travel with you to Tûr Morva.","Book 4, Chapter 6: The Will to Stand","'For my part, I am glad to have your help, ${PLAYER}, and that of these Rangers. Even the Hebog-lûth cannot stand against Saruman alone.'","Catrin of the Falcon-clan wants you to help the oppressed people of Galtrev and those who live throughout Pren Gwydh.","Talk to Penrod in Tûr Morva","'Help the people of Pren Gwydh as much as you can before moving on to Tâl Methedras, to the east. There are good people here, despite the presence of some who think Saruman can better their lives.'","'Lheu Brenin imprisoned the emissary sent from Isengard.'","'I will bring you and your people to Tûr Morva to speak with the Brenin, but I promise you nothing else. The Falcon-clan has its own problems to solve.'","'The clans of Dunland have a proud history, ${PLAYER}, and none prouder than the Falcon. Weaker clans have forgotten where they came from, forgotten their honour, but not my people.\
\
'But dangers press on us from all sides. Good people live here in Galtrev and throughout Pren Gwydh, and they must be protected, their ills cured.\
\
'Once you have aided the people of Pren Gwydh to your satisfaction, go to Tûr Morva, in Tâl Methedras. The people of the Falcon will be glad to have your help! Tûr Morva is to the east of here, beyond the Gravenwood.'","Talk to Léolin, and he will bring you to Tûr Morva","Aid the people of Pren Gwydh as much as you can before moving on to Tâl Methedras","'The Falcon cannot stand alone against the Wizard.'","Penrod is waiting to speak with you in Tûr Morva."},
[2143]={"'The preparations have been coming along very well, ${PLAYER}. These Rangers are hard workers, but none more so than you, good ${RACE}!'\
\
Penrod's approving laughter fades, and he becomes solemn once again.\
\
'Lheu Brenin wishes to see you. The emissary from Isengard that he captured is giving the guards trouble.\
\
'Go see the Brenin outside his home, up the hill to the south.'","Complete the preparations in Tûr Morva (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva","Penrod will be glad to hear that you have aided the people of Tûr Morva with their preparations.","'These Rangers are hardy folk. They are a great help to us.'","Penrod has told you there is much work to do before the Falcon-clan can have much hope of standing against Saruman.","Talk to Penrod in Tûr Morva","'Every man and woman of Tûr Morva has a job to do if the Falcon-clan is to stand against Saruman. Help them all with their tasks, and the preparations will go more quickly.'","'All of Tûr Morva is alive with the sound of work.'","Book 4, Chapter 7: Aiding Tûr  Morva","Each member of the Falcon-clan in Tûr Morva has a task to do to prepare for battle against Saruman. Penrod has asked you to aid them with their tasks.","Lheu Brenin is outside his home, up the hill to the south of Penrod, in Tûr Morva.\
\
Penrod has told you that the Brenin wants to see you concerning some trouble with the captive emissary of Isengard.","'If it took only courage to win battles against Wizards, the Falcon-clan would have marched south, put Saruman in his place, and be on its way home already...but it is not enough.\
\
'Tûr Morva must be made ready. Rhus prepares the leather that Taf will fashion into armour. Our Brenin's daughter, Mair, trains youthful fighters in the combat arts. Idele sees to the gathering of foodstuffs for the journey. All have their work, but still it will be a while before the Falcon can fly to war.\
\
'With your help and the help of the Rangers, it will go more quickly.'","'Lheu Brenin wishes to see you. The emissary from Isengard that he captured is giving the guards trouble.\
\
'Go see the Brenin outside his home, up the hill to the south.'","'All of Tûr Morva is alive with the sound of work, ${PLAYER}. It is good. There are many clans siding with the Wizard in this conflict, and I feared the Falcon-clan would not be ready if it came to war with them. With your help and that of these Rangers, the Falcon can show its talons!'"},
[2144]={"'It will not be long before the city is surrounded. I hope we are ready.'\
\
Imrahil stares at you appraisingly.\
\
'I have a message for you, ${PLAYER}. I received word that Ormatar, the Captain of the Citadel, has been looking for you. You should speak to him in the Citadel, without delay, for that can mean only one thing. Go to Ormatar with haste.'","The enemies of Gondor approach Minas Tirith from the north and from the east, and many folk in the city desire your help before the city is completely surrounded.","'While you were surveying the situation in Talath Anor, I learned of a handful of folk who desire your assistance with matters both large and small. Go to them and see what they need, if you can.\
\
'Mithrandir wished to speak with you at greater length about your encounter with the enemy commander in Osgiliath. Find him in the Citadel, atop the city.\
\
'Arodor, the chief scribe of the Council, was impressed with your work on his behalf and asked for you to speak with him in the Dome of the Sun, in the Sixth Circle. The Council was waiting for Ingold to return to the city; perhaps your experience beyond the Rammas Echor will be of interest to them.\
\
'In other Council matters, the Captain of the Garrison has been trying to improve the morale of folk remaining in the city. Find Echadon and see what you can do to help.'","'I received word that Ormatar, the Captain of the Citadel, has been looking for you. You should speak to him in the Citadel, without delay, for that can mean only one thing. Go to Ormatar with haste.'","Talk to Arodor and complete 'A Long Siege'","Talk to Ormatar in the Citadel atop Minas Tirith","'Minas Tirith will soon be encircled by our enemies, ${PLAYER}. Time is getting short, but we must fill the hours or minutes that remain to us with preparations that will help us survive the approaching onslaught!\
\
'While you were surveying the situation in Talath Anor, I learned of a handful of folk who desire your assistance with matters both large and small. Go to them and see what they need, if you can.\
\
'Mithrandir wished to speak with you at greater length about your encounter with the enemy commander in Osgiliath. Find him in the Citadel, atop the city.\
\
'Arodor, the chief scribe of the Council, was impressed with your work on his behalf and asked for you to speak with him in the Dome of the Sun, in the Sixth Circle. The Council was waiting for Ingold to return to the city; perhaps your experience beyond the Rammas Echor will be of interest to them.\
\
'In other Council matters, the Captain of the Garrison has been trying to improve the morale of folk remaining in the city. Find Echadon and see what you can do to help.'","Talk to Imrahil in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate to the city","The Council of Gondor meets in the Dome of the Sun on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Mithrandir can be found at the Court of the Fountain, in the Citadel atop the city. Echadon can be found at the south end of the Second Circle.\
\
Imrahil has asked you to provide help to a number of people within the city before the city is encircled by a ring of foes.","Book 4, Chapter 7: Ring of Foes","Talk to Echadon and complete 'Reserves of Courage'","Prince Imrahil is in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, by the main gate of the city, preparing for battle.","'You are ${PLAYER}, the ${CLASS}? You must be. Who else might carry themselves as you do?\
\
'I have been looking for you. The Steward has summoned you.'","Ormatar is in the Citadel, the highest level of Minas Tirith.\
\
You learned that Ormatar has been seeking you, and you should find out what he wants.","Talk to Mithrandir and complete 'A Matter of Lineage'"},
[2145]={"'Me alegra que sirvas tan bien a mis hijos, ${PLAYER}. Siento que estás cerca de localizar al Nazgûl que escapó de las aguas embravecidas del Bruinen.\
\
'Y aún más males se revelan. Los Elfos del Bosque Negro se han enfrentado antes a tales males. Mi hijo hizo bien en enviarte a mí.\
\
'Habla con Legolas, hijo de Thranduil, en una de las habitaciones de huéspedes a lo largo del camino que asciende por la ladera sur del Valle de Imladris. Ha estado muy pensativo durante su estancia aquí, y puede que pueda ayudarte a encontrar y derrotar la fuente del mal.'","'Salve a ti, ${PLAYER}. Si no trajeras noticias tan graves, te recibiría con mayor alegría, pero tus noticias son preocupantes.\
\
'Nosotros, los del Bosque Negro, ciertamente nos hemos encontrado antes con estas criaturas, pero no esperaba volver a verlas. Una tribu de trolls vivía cerca de Dol Guldur, y quienes luchamos contra ellos los llamábamos trolls silvanos. En su momento, eran criaturas errantes, reacias a unirse o incluso a vivir cerca unas de otras. Sin embargo, en Dol Guldur, algo hizo que se unieran. Se alzó un rey entre ellos, y unificó a los trolls silvanos en una fuerza terrible. Mi padre envió muchos guerreros para derrotarlos, y así fue.\
\
'Creo que algo ha vuelto a unir a los trolls silvanos de las Quebradas de los Trolls, ${PLAYER}. Pero este lugar está muy lejos del Bosque Negro — los guerreros de mi padre no nos servirán aquí.'","'Creo que Legolas está en una de las habitaciones de huéspedes a lo largo del camino que asciende por la ladera sur del Valle de Imladris. Puedes encontrarlo allí y hablar con él sobre la criatura que encontraste.'","'Habla con mi padre en Imladris, muy al este y por encima del Bruinen. Él puede concertar una audiencia con los Elfos del Bosque Negro.'","Legolas está en una de las habitaciones de huéspedes de la Casa de Elrond.\
\
El Maestro Elrond te ha hablado de un príncipe elfo llamado Legolas, que actualmente se encuentra en Imladris por un tiempo. Proviene del Bosque Negro y puede tener conocimiento sobre la criatura que enfrentaste en las Quebradas de los Trolls.","Habla con Legolas en Rivendel","Elladan está profundamente preocupado por el mal que parece crecer desde lo más profundo de las Quebradas de los Trolls, y sabe que no puedes enfrentarlo ${PLAYERNAME:solo[m]|sola[f]}.","El Maestro Elrond está en Imladris, muy al este del campamento de Elladan en Thorenhad y por encima del Bruinen.\
\
Elladan te ha pedido que hables con su padre para concertar una audiencia con los Elfos visitantes del Bosque Negro, quienes podrían tener experiencia con criaturas como la que encontraste.","Libro 4, Capítulo 7: La Ayuda del Bosque Negro","'Eres afortunado. La criatura a la que te enfrentaste no pudo haber sido un verdadero Onod. No podrías haber resistido el poder de uno de los Antiguos.\
\
'Tampoco deberías haber tenido que hacerlo, pues los Onodrim son amistosos con los Pueblos Libres en las raras ocasiones en que sus caminos se cruzan. Los grandes bosques son menos transitados ahora que en tiempos pasados, y pocos llegan a ver a uno de los grandes pastores de árboles.\
\
'Una pequeña compañía de Elfos del Bosque Negro vino a Imladris para consultar con mi padre. Quizás uno de ellos sepa qué clase de criatura enfrentaste. Habla con mi padre para concertar una audiencia.'"},
[2146]={"Nai has given you permission to enter the cell with Dondhreg to see if you can get any information from the captive emissary.","Talk to Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva","Talk to Nai at the prison cave","'Have you come to gloat, ${RACE}? You are no Dunlending. Do not mistake these people for friends. It will be you in my place next! Mark what I say!'\
\
Dondhreg glowers at you, his eyes full of hate.\
\
'They cannot defeat Saruman. They are fools to try! The other clans are wiser and know which way the tide is going. Already, most of Dunland pledges their swords to my master. His armies come from Dunbog and Carreglyn and Starkmoor, and these unprepared fools will find themselves on the wrong side of the wave!\
\
'It could have been different. I care not. It is enough to know that my captors will be slain by their own kinsmen soon enough, and you gloaters along with them!'","'You cannot stand against Saruman. Too many of the clans are already sworn to him. You have lost before you have begun.'","'You can go on in. He will not bite, if he knows what is good for him.'","Book 4, Chapter 8: The Messenger of Isengard","Talk to Dondhreg","Lheu Brenin wants you to speak with the emissary of Isengard he is holding captive in the cave behind Tûr Morva.","'He is full of bluster, but I pay it no heed. We are out here, and he is in there.'","Nai is guarding the captive emissary of Isengard in the prison-cave, south of Lheu Brenin and in the wall of the cliff to your left.\
\
Lheu Brenin has asked you to press the captive for information. First, you should speak to the guard Nai outside his cell.","'You know of the emissary Saruman sent to us to force our cooperation? He is being kept under watch in the prison-cave. He has not told us anything of use yet, but perhaps you can inspire him to speak.\
\
'Go into the prison-cave and speak to the guard Nai. He will allow you to press the captive for information. Return and tell me if the captive has anything useful to say. If he does not, perhaps his usefulness is at an end, and Nai can be given something else to do.\
\
'The prison-caves are to the south. Follow the path and you will see the entrance among the ruins on your left-hand side, in the cliff.'","'What have you learned from our guest, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
Lheu Brenin listens to your report of Dondhreg's words.\
\
'There is truth there, I fear, if only a kernel. We must learn how large the kernel may be.'","'You have the permission of the Brenin to speak with the prisoner? Very well. You may go in. He should pose you no danger. He knows that if he tries anything, he will do without meals.'","'Enter the prison-caves and speak with Nai. He will allow you to talk to the prisoner, and you may learn something of use to us. If not, well...it is of little account to me whether he lives or dies.\
\
'The prison-caves are to the south. Follow the path and you will see the entrance among the ruins on your left-hand side, in the cliff.'","You have spoken with Dondhreg, but if there was anything valuable in his words it will be up to Lheu Brenin to discern it."},
[2147]={"'Debemos rastrear a los trolls silvanos hasta su guarida, ${PLAYER}, si hemos de limpiar la corrupción que hiere el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
'Puedo llevarte hasta ellos. Sus huellas son fácilmente distinguibles en la tierra embarrada, y los trolls silvanos no son conocidos por su sutileza ni por su inteligencia. ¡Pero no me pidas que lo haga con premura! Sé del Nazgûl que el maestro Elrond ha perdido, y temo que pueda haber prestado parte de su fuerza y poder a estas criaturas para que se muestren tan osadas. Debemos estar atentos.\
\
'Habla conmigo cuando hayas reunido a tantos amigos como puedas confiar y estés listo para que te guíe a lo salvaje en busca de los trolls silvanos, y del poder maligno que temo pueda ser su aliado.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Libro 4, Capítulo 8: El sendero sin marcar","Legolas está en Rivendel, en una de las estancias de huéspedes de la Casa de Elrond.\
\
El príncipe élfico del Bosque Negro, Legolas, espera ayudarte a rastrear a los trolls silvanos en el Bosque de los Trolls y derrotarlos.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'Hemos puesto fin a los designios del Nazgûl al dar muerte al troll del bosque Taushakh, pero la huida de tan gran siervo del Enemigo arroja una sombra sobre mi corazón.'","Habla con Legolas en Rivendel y sigue el rastro de los trolls silvanos.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}? Puedo seguir las huellas de los trolls silvanos y guiarte hasta su guarida. Trae contigo a los amigos en quienes confíes, pues los trolls silvanos son criaturas peligrosas, y puede que encontremos más de uno o dos.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Habla con Legolas en Rivendel","Legolas reconoció a la criatura que describiste como uno de los trolls silvanos y ha accedido a ayudarte a rastrear a los demás.","Legolas está en Rivendel, en una de las estancias de huéspedes de la Casa de Elrond.\
\
El príncipe élfico del Bosque Negro, Legolas, espera hablar contigo sobre lo que ambos visteis en la guarida de los trolls silvanos."},
[2148]={"'Am I right to believe that you have met Peregrin the Halfling? Lord Denethor has named him a Guard of the Citadel, despite his stature. He will bring you before the Steward. Tarry not!'","'The armies of Mordor have encircled the city, ${PLAYER}. The siege has begun.'\
\
You tell Mithrandir that you spoke with the Steward, and that Denethor spoke to you of many things that he saw within the depths of a palantír. At that, Mithrandir looks up sharply.\
\
'So the Anor-stone did remain within the tower. I wondered if it was so. Denethor has had a stubborn and strong will for all the years of his life, but if he seeks to gain some advantage over the enemy by using the palantír...'\
\
The Wizard scowls, and shakes his head.\
\
'Denethor is too occupied with his grief for Faramir to work any evil on that score, but he will also be of no use in the defence of the city. Imrahil and I will mount the defence, and we will need your help!'","Talk to Mithrandir in besieged Minas Tirith, in the south-eastern area of the Second Circle","Mithrandir is in besieged Minas Tirith, in the south-eastern area of the Second Circle.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>","Book 4, Chapter 8: What the Steward Saw","Talk to Peregrin Took and travel with him to your audience with Denethor","Peregrin Took is in the Seventh Circle of the city.\
\
You have been summoned before Denethor, the Steward of Gondor. Peregrin Took has been charged with bringing you into Denethor's presence.","'All right, ${PLAYER}, I will bring you before the Steward! You may wish to keep your wits about you, for he has a somewhat frightening countenance. He is a great man of importance, I don't doubt it, but he is very stern and does not go out of his way to cushion the effect of his words!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","As the armies of Mordor begin to encircle the city, the Steward of Gondor summons you before him.","'Are you looking for Mithrandir? Go to the Dome of the Sun and use the model of the city. That will bring you to the city besieged, where Mithrandir mounts the defence!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>If you wish to return to Minas Tirith during the siege, you may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun.</rgb>"},
[2149]={"'El Nazgûl no podrá ocultarse de nosotros para siempre.'","'Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un buen compañero[m]|una buena compañera[f]}, . En el Gladdalf mostraste tu valentía.'","'El Maestro Elrond debe ser informado de nuestra aventura en la guarida de Taushakh, rey de los trolls silvanos. Que Taushakh haya sido vencido es un consuelo pequeño por haber perdido al Nazgûl tan pronto después de haber revelado su ubicación.'","'El Nazgûl ha huido una vez más, pero será encontrado.'","'Una misión secreta se ha vuelto más urgente por las noticias que traes.'","Legolas se ha sentido consternado por los acontecimientos en la guarida de los trolls silvanos y cree que Elrond debe ser informado de inmediato.","'Has hecho bien. El Nazgûl será encontrado nuevamente.'","'Has sido de gran ayuda para nosotros, ${PLAYER}.'","'Los trolls silvanos son más peligrosos cuando algo los une.'","Libro 4, Capítulo 9: Apresura su Partida","'El Bosque de los Trolls ha sido hecho más seguro gracias a tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}.'","'Me alegra escuchar tus noticias, ${PLAYER}. No te lamentes demasiado por la pérdida del Nazgûl — sus terribles planes con los trolls silvanos fueron frustrados por tus valientes acciones y las habilidades de Legolas.\
\
'Sí, tu encuentro con el Nazgûl me ha revelado lo que debo hacer. Hablaré con Gandalf, pues la misión de la que oíste rumores se ha vuelto aún más urgente por las noticias que traes.\
\
'Para ti, sin embargo, te pediría que mantengas tu atención centrada en el Nazgûl.'","'No creo que este sea el final de nuestra búsqueda del Nazgûl que escapó de las aguas del Bruinen, ${PLAYER}. De hecho, apenas hemos visto el comienzo de los problemas que puede causar.\
\
'Debemos contarle al Maestro Elrond lo que ha sucedido. Una misión de gran secreto ha sido encomendada a algunos de nosotros en Imladris, y temo que ya hemos sido demorados demasiado tiempo.\
\
'Habla con el Maestro Elrond dentro de La Última Morada y cuéntale sobre nuestro viaje a la guarida de Taushakh y lo que vimos allí. El tiempo para demoras ha pasado.'","El Maestro Elrond está dentro de La Última Morada.\
\
Legolas te ha pedido que vayas con Elrond de inmediato y le cuentes lo que ocurrió en la guarida de Taushakh, rey de los trolls silvanos."},
[2150]={"Catrin is in Galtrev, the Dunlending village in Pren Gwydh, west of Tâl Methedras.\
\
Lheu Brenin has asked you to travel through the lands of Dunland, seeing where the loyalties of the Dunlending clans lie and aiding those of like mind.","'We meet again, ${PLAYER}, as I knew we would. I am a free woman of the Uch-lûth, sister to Wadu and with victory notches already upon my sword.\
\
'I am free to go where I please. I need no permission from your northern friends to walk these lands that belong to me and mine.\
\
'Catrin of the Hebog-lûth and I of the Uch-lûth have already made things difficult for those who would sell these lands and its people to Saruman. I am ready to strike against them throughout all of Dunland, in my brother's name, if you are willing!'","'You have returned, and on an errand from Lheu Brenin? Old Catrin is still a good judge of character, is she not?'\
\
Catrin cackles and does a shuffling type of dance.\
\
'To answer your questions, Galtrev is home to people of many clans, as it has been for all of my memory. The Ox-clan has been more brazen in recent days, and it seems to me that they must have received encouragement from some source. Some Wizard, if you ask for Catrin's opinion!\
\
'While you were at Tûr Morva, someone has been helping me with my little resistance against the Ox-clan. She did not want to stay within the walls of Galtrev and has a camp to the south-west. She would not tell me her right name, but asked that I call her Wadu's Ghost. You should seek her out; she was asking about your Ranger friends.'","Lheu Brenin has given you a task that will help gauge the severity of the threat posed to both the Falcon-clan and the Grey Company.","'Catrin does not ask questions of allies as useful as Wadu's Ghost. Her reasons for keeping her name a secret are no business of mine.\
\
'She was asking about your friends; perhaps you two can be travelling companions and cause some trouble for the clans that have allied with Saruman. Nothing would please me more!\
\
'Wadu's Ghost has a small camp west of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh.'","'Wadu's Ghost' has a camp to the west of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh.\
\
Catrin told you of a girl that helped her with her resistance against the Ox-clan in Galtrev. This girl called herself 'Wadu's Ghost' and was asking about the Grey Company.","Book 4, Chapter 9: Return to Galtrev","'Our prisoner spoke of the other Dunlending clans as if they were already in Saruman's satchel. That is my fear, but his words may be borne from bluster and desperation. The Falcon-clan is strong, but even our strength may not be enough to face all the clans of a united Dunland.\
\
'I need someone that I can trust to travel throughout Dunland and see the state of things. Is Galtrev still as it was? Do the herds of Starkmoor feed Saruman's lackeys? What is the mood of the people of distant Dunbog? Are the mines of Carreglyn still being worked and for whom?\
\
'I need you to be my eyes in this, ${PLAYER}. Go first to Catrin in Galtrev, she who sent you to us. See what is happening in Dunland and help those who share our goals. Saruman must be opposed, by the Rangers and by the Falcon-clan, if by no others.'","Talk to Catrin in Galtrev","Talk to Wadu's Ghost in Pren Gwydh","'We must know if our prisoner speaks truth, ${PLAYER}. Have the other clans all sided with Saruman? You must be my eyes throughout Dunland. Start first at the village of Galtrev and speak with Catrin about the situation in Pren Gwydh.'"},
[2151]={"Book 4, Chapter 9: The City Besieged","Talk to Lamlor in the besieged Dome of the Sun and complete 'The Withered Tree'","Lamlor can be found in the Dome of the Sun in besieged Minas Tirith. Ingold can be found atop the wall on the north end of the Third Circle in besieged Minas Tirith. Rathon can be found in the Sixth Circle near the street to the Citadel in besieged Minas Tirith.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>","With Steward Denethor shut in the tower, mourning the final hours of his son Faramir, it is up to Mithrandir and Imrahil to mount the defence of the besieged city.","'You must do what you can to help the city's defenders, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'The Council of Gondor is in disarray. Go to the Dome of the Sun and learn what you can do to help them communicate their resolutions. Lamlor, the Captain of Tidings, will need help to send messages throughout Minas Tirith.\
\
'Ingold is atop the wall on the north end of the Third Circle, and will need your help to manage his fear and the fears of the men behind the walls. Terror will be the greatest foe of our guardsmen, and they will need to master it if they are to mount an effective defence!\
\
'The armies of Mordor have been using catapults and other siege weapons to launch burning stones over the walls and into the city. Find Rathon, the Warden of the Wells, in the Sixth Circle near the street that leads up to the Citadel, and help him extinguish some of the fires before they can spread!'","'Ready yourself! The enemy is preparing another assault, ${PLAYER}!'","Prince Imrahil is in besieged Minas Tirith, atop the wall on the south-east end of the Second Circle.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.</rgb>","'There is no more leaving the city, ${PLAYER}. The Morgul-host has surrounded Minas Tirith, and the Pelennor is filled with their weapons of war. They have not yet broken the gate, but there is still much harm they can cause even from their position beyond the walls. You must do what you can to help the city's defenders!\
\
'The Council of Gondor is in disarray. Go to the Dome of the Sun and learn what you can do to help them communicate their resolutions. Lamlor, the Captain of Tidings, will need help to send messages throughout Minas Tirith.\
\
'Ingold is atop the wall on the north end of the Third Circle, and will need your help to manage his fear and the fears of the men behind the walls. Terror will be the greatest foe of our guardsmen, and they will need to master it if they are to mount an effective defence!\
\
'The armies of Mordor have been using catapults and other siege weapons to launch burning stones over the walls and into the city. Find Rathon, the Warden of the Wells, in the Sixth Circle near the street that leads up to the Citadel, and help him extinguish some of the fires before they can spread!'","Talk to Prince Imrahil in besieged Minas Tirith, atop the wall on the south-east end of the Second Circle","Talk to Rathon in the besieged city and complete 'Fires in the City'","Talk to Ingold in the besieged city and complete 'Mad With Terror'"},
[2152]={"'Bienvenido a Rivendel, donde encontrarás La Última Morada al este del Mar, ${PLAYER}. El camino a Imladris ya no es tan indulgente como lo fue en otros tiempos, y te felicito por tus esfuerzos.\
\
'Espero que las aguas del Vado se hayan calmado desde nuestro paso; las dejamos en agitación. Temo que la causa de estos problemas aún no haya concluido.\
\
'El Señor Elrond es el maestro de esta casa; debe ser informado de tu llegada. Lo encontrarás en su biblioteca, en el piso superior de La Última Morada, al noreste.'","'El camino que tomaste hasta mi puerta ha sido peligroso, ${PLAYER}, y sus peligros demasiado comunes en estos días oscuros. Si consientes en prestarnos tu ayuda, no será el menor de tus desafíos.'","Elrond espera en la biblioteca, en el piso superior de su casa.\
\
Aragorn te pidió que te presentaras ante Elrond, el maestro de La Última Morada.","Aragorn te ha pedido que hables con Elrond sobre un asunto de suma importancia para Rivendel.","'Elrond estará muy interesado en escuchar sobre tu viaje, ${PLAYER}. Habla con él en su biblioteca, en el piso superior de su casa, al noreste.'","Libro 4, Prólogo: Los Problemas de Rivendel"},
[2153]={"Glúmur se encuentra en la parte superior de las escaleras que dominan la cámara de Nud-melek.\
\
Has derrotado a muchos de los leales sirvientes de Mazog, los Pûlpum, y deberías volver ahora con Glúmur.","Glúmur se encuentra en Nud-melek, con vistas a la fortaleza de Mazog.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que hables con su explorador cerca de Zabadgathol, y que le ayudes a explorar la zona.","'Es bueno verte. Me alegra que Bori haya sido lo suficientemente amable como para enviarme un poco de ayuda aquí. \
\
'Allá abajo, los hombres de Mazog han estado trabajando duro. ¿Puedes derrotar a los sirvientes más cercanos de Mazog, ${PLAYER}? \
\
'Se llaman los Pûlpum, y parecen servir como sus guardias personales más leales y formidables, y se pueden encontrar en el área de abajo.'","'Los Pûlpum son aparentemente los sirvientes más leales de Mazog. Búscalos fuera de su fortaleza, Zabadgathol, en Nud-melek.'","'Antes anhelaba la aventura, pero ya no. Dile a Bori que tenga cuidado con Zigilburk en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera. Temo que su poder no nos sea de utilidad.'","Libro 5, Capítulo 1: El legado de Azog","Bori se encuentra en la Cámara de Liderazgo, cerca de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, en Zelem-melek.\
\
Bróin te ha pedido que adviertas a Bori sobre el exceso de confianza que teme que la recuperación de Zigilburk haya despertado en los enanos.","'Me has rescatado de la Cámara del Tesoro Sumergida, pero sigo teniendo miedo. Temo que recuperar Zigilburk no sea tan beneficioso para los enanos: hay algo en ese hacha que me llena de temor, y me preocupa que despierte una codicia malsana en mi pueblo. Ya Bori ha arriesgado mucho por su deseo de conseguir esta arma.\
\
'Por favor, regresa a la Cámara de Liderazgo y dile a Bori mis preocupaciones. Sus palabras al salir de las cámaras inundadas donde el Guardián me había atrapado me llenaron de preocupación.'","Habla con Glúmur","Localiza y habla con Glúmur en Nud-melek","'¿Ves? Tal como dijo Bori, no ha pasado nada malo, ${PLAYER}. Al menos para nosotros; Mazog no puede decir lo mismo.\
\
'Las preocupaciones de Bróin son infundadas.'","Bróin teme que recuperar Zigilburk no sea tan beneficioso como parece, y que provoque un exceso de confianza en los enanos.","Zabadgathol, la fortaleza de Mazog, se encuentra en Nud-melek.\
\
Bori te ha pedido que busques Zabadgathol y que derrotes a algunos de los guardias más leales de Mazog, miembros de los Pûlpum.","'¿Qué noticias traes de mi amigo? ¿Bróin está preocupado? Ha pasado por muchas dificultades, pero debe darse cuenta de la gloria que nos espera. Estamos tan cerca de expulsar a los orcos de Moria que puedo saborearlo. No podemos detenernos ahora, ahora que tenemos los medios para la victoria. ¿No conoces la historia de Azog? No te la contaré ahora, porque es sombría, pero debes saber que Mazog, el engendro de su engendro, seguramente está hecho del mismo bloque que él: terrible e implacable.\
\
'Más de nuestros exploradores han regresado, y creen haber encontrado la ubicación de la fortaleza de Mazog; es un lugar llamado Zabadgathol, en Nud-melek.\
\
'Uno de esos exploradores, Glúmur, se encuentra cerca de Zabadgathol, viaja a Nud-melek y habla con él.'"},
[2154]={"Libro 5, Capítulo 1: Hacia las Montañas Nubladas","Glóin puede encontrarse en el campamento en lo alto del paso que lleva desde Rivendel a las Montañas Nubladas.\
\
Elrond sugirió que buscaras la ayuda de Glóin en la caza del Nazgûl.","'La amenaza que representa el Nazgûl aún no ha pasado. Por favor, continúa tu persecución de la criatura con la ayuda de Glóin en su campamento, en lo alto del paso que conduce a las Montañas Nubladas.'","'Temo que, aunque el Nazgûl al que enfrentaste ha huido del Bosque de los Trolls, aún trama un asalto contra Rivendel. Al norte y al este de Rivendel hay trasgos y cosas peores que podría someter a su voluntad y usar contra nosotros.\
\
'Te pediría que continúes con la persecución del Nazgûl y viajes a las Montañas Nubladas. Allí puedes buscar la ayuda de Glóin, quien ha establecido un campamento al final del paso que sale de Rivendel y conduce a las Montañas Nubladas.\
\
'Ve ahora, pues no solo está en juego la seguridad de Rivendel. Toda la Tierra Media depende de tus acciones.'","'¿Un Nazgûl? ¿Uno de los Nueve Espectros del Anillo de los que se habló en el Concilio de Elrond? No he olvidado las palabras melosas transmitidas por uno de esos Jinetes a nosotros en la Montaña Solitaria. ¡Qué veneno! Querían que traicionáramos al viejo Bilbo Bolsón ante Mordor.\
\
'Te ayudaré en lo que pueda, aunque Dáin me ha encomendado otro asunto. Puedo compartir algo de información.'","Elrond cree que el Nazgûl que ahuyentaste del Bosque de los Trolls ha huido a las Montañas Nubladas. Te ha pedido que continúes la persecución del Nazgûl con la ayuda de Glóin."},
[2155]={"Saeradan is at the camp in the Gravenwood, by the fire.\
\
Halbarad has decided that your path and the Grey Company's must now diverge, and you should say your good-byes to the Rangers.","Radanir nods at you, but keeps his peace.","Talk to Saeradan by the fire at the camp in the Gravenwood","'My men will want to say good-bye, ${PLAYER}. Saeradan is there, by the fire. He knows my intent, though not all the others do.'","Golodir nods at you, but keeps his peace.","Halbarad is at the camp in the Gravenwood, trying to decide how to safely proceed with the Grey Company's mission and how to help Théodred at the same time.","Book 5, Chapter 1: Separate Ways","Calenglad nods at you, but keeps his peace.","Prestadír nods at you, but keeps his peace.","'We have come to the cross-roads, ${PLAYER}, and sooner than I expected. I want to help the Prince of Rohan, for without his aid and that of his doughty warriors, my men and I would still be captives of the Falcon-clan. But we cannot abandon our journey; our duty lies with Aragorn, and we must find him in Rohan or die searching. We cannot stay to help Théodred with his battles.\
\
'I want you to go with the prince, ${PLAYER}. I want you to lend him your strength and your wisdom and your courage. You can travel south more swiftly than we can; even hale and hearty, our diminished number would take some time to make ready, and we are wounded and tired.\
\
'Make your farewells with my kin, ${PLAYER}. I know they will want to say good-bye. Saeradan is there, by the fire. He knows what I have in mind, though the others may not.'","'Halbarad told me his decision, and I will not speak against it. But I will miss you, ${PLAYER}, and I wish you might still travel with us. I know Erebrandir feels the same way! He has not forgotten the farrier who crafted him a new shoe in Hollin, nor the ${RACE} who saved the farrier.\
\
'You have a skill beyond strength of arms or the reach of knowledge, ${PLAYER}. You find friends wherever you tread, and where they cannot be found you make them with kindness and generosity. Halbarad does not realize how close he came to spending the rest of his days in the prison-caves of Tûr Morva, but I do.\
\
'Consider this, my friend, and do not forget it: Prince Théodred was at this camp for days before you escaped from Isengard and held council with me. But he did not move to rescue my kin until he spoke with you. Nay, do not console me! I am not ashamed. Your ability to rally people to your side is yours alone, and it is a power you must not forget. It has saved many lives already, and I know it will again.'","Corunir nods at you, but keeps his peace."},
[2156]={"'Ah, you do not need me to tell you these things. You have seen within the Ring of Isengard and escaped to tell the tale! You will be of great help to Prince Théodred, I do not doubt it.\
\
'I saw Corunir down the path to the north-west not long ago. You should find him and bid him farewell.'","Radanir nods at you, but keeps his peace.","Golodir nods at you, but keeps his peace.","Corunir was last seen down the path north-west of the camp in the Gravenwood, by a large boulder.\
\
You have spoken with Saeradan, and he told you to find Corunir and say good-bye.","Book 5, Chapter 1: Separate Ways","Your path now diverges from that of the Grey Company, and Halbarad wants you to make your farewells before you take your leave.","Calenglad nods at you, but keeps his peace.","Prestadír nods at you, but keeps his peace.","'Corunir will want to say good-bye. I last saw him walking down the path from the camp, north-west of here.'","'You are leaving us now? How can this be Halbarad's decision?'\
\
Corunir stares at his feet for a short moment before he meets your gaze again.\
\
'I suppose the Prince of Rohan has need of you. I cannot blame Halbarad for wanting you to help hold the fords of the Isen. I think your tale of the army Saruman is preparing within Isengard shook him deeply, and if that crossing is lost then the kingdom of Rohan will surely follow.\
\
'We have been through a great deal, ${PLAYER}, have we not? It seemed we would stay within the musty library of Zudrugund with Nár and Frithgeir for the rest of our days, did it not? Even thinking now of climbing up to Nár's Peak makes my legs ache. I want you to have these spare boots of mine, in memory of our time spent in that high place.'","Talk to Corunir on the path north-west of the camp in the Gravenwood","Halbarad nods at you, but keeps his peace."},
[2157]={"Radanir nods at you, but keeps his peace.","Talk to Golodir in the shade of a boulder west of Corunir, in the Gravenwood","Book 5, Chapter 1: Separate Ways","Golodir is to the west of Corunir's location near the camp in the Gravenwood.\
\
Corunir wants you to speak with Golodir before you go.","'There is some new fire in Golodir's eyes, ${PLAYER}. I am afraid for him. Seek him out, to the west, and allay my fears!'","'You are leaving us, ${PLAYER}? It may be Halbarad's decision, but I would not leave, even if he ordered me home again.'\
\
He looks up at you, and you do see a hint of the hardness in his eyes that so upset Corunir.\
\
'There are matters still left undone here. The cowards who slink in the caves beneath Tâl Methedras still live, ${PLAYER}. They spoke to us as friends, gave us shelter, took the sweat from our brows, and repaid us with treachery. I will repay them in kind. My lost brethren and my lost friends demand this of me.\
\
'Lheu Brenin? You jest, ${PLAYER}. He is a fat man whose courage depends on a hundred of his people at his back. I have faced the evil of Mordirith...he is gone, and I still live. Lheu Brenin is nothing compared to Mordirith.'","The time has come for your path to diverge from that of the Grey Company, and you should say your farewells to the Rangers.","Calenglad nods at you, but keeps his peace.","Prestadír nods at you, but keeps his peace.","'I am worried about Golodir, ${PLAYER}. He endured much in the depths of Carn Dûm, as you know, and he will never truly forgive himself for Lorniel's death, but this journey has done much to relieve some of his hurts. I think it is simply this: he has a purpose again. There is work to be done, and until we find Aragorn, as we are sworn to do, it remains unfinished.\
\
'But our captivity in the prison-caves changed something within Golodir. There is a dangerous glimmer in his eye that I have not seen before. It worries me, ${PLAYER}. I am afraid for him.\
\
'We were speaking not long ago, just to the west, but my heart was troubled, and I left him there. Will you seek him out and see if my worries are for naught? I hope they are. My mother always said I worried enough for the whole family, but the dangers through which we have come and to which we ride deserve even more worry than I can manage.'","Halbarad nods at you, but keeps his peace."},
[2158]={"Radanir nods at you but keeps his peace.","Calenglad is at the Tree of Tribute, in the Gravenwood.\
\
Golodir has sent you to say your good-byes to Calenglad.","Halbarad nods at you and keeps his peace.","'How long do you think this tree has been growing here, ${PLAYER}? It must be so old and have seen so much. Are we anything more than the flickering of a candle in the gale to something so ancient? Would it even notice if we left this place and never returned?'\
\
Calenglad looks weary, and his face is more lined than you remember.\
\
'You are leaving us to aid Théodred? It is no surprise to me; I overheard Halbarad and Saeradan discussing courses of action, and it seemed likely. I wish our paths did not diverge, but it seems they must, ${PLAYER}. We all have too many duties in this world.'","Talk to Calenglad by the Tree of Tribute in the Gravenwood","Book 5, Chapter 1: Separate Ways","Corunir nods at you, but there is nothing left to say and he keeps his peace.","'Calenglad is to the south there, staring at that tree. I think he has been there for hours.'","The time has come for your path to diverge from that of the Grey Company, and you should say your farewells.","Prestadír nods at you, but keeps his peace.","'I thought you would come with me to take vengeance upon Lheu Brenin, ${PLAYER}, but it seems your road lies elsewhere. I am sorry you will not be there. I know you would gladly join me, if urgent matters did not drive you elsewhere.'\
\
Golodir does not seem to be listening to you. He gestures to the south, in the direction of the Tree of Tribute.\
\
'Calenglad is over that way, if you wish to bid farewell to him. It feels like he has been staring at that tree for hours.'"},
[2159]={"Talk to Radanir on the road east of the Tree of Tribute, in the Gravenwood","The time has come for your path to diverge from that of the Grey Company, and for you to bid the Rangers farewell.","Halbarad nods at you, and keeps his peace.","'Do us all a favour and remember to say farewell to Radanir, ${PLAYER}. We would never hear the end of it if you do not. He is east of here, on the road.'","Book 5, Chapter 1: Separate Ways","Radanir is on the road east of the Tree of Tribute, in the Gravenwood.\
\
Calenglad has told you to say your good-byes to Radanir, or the Rangers would never hear the end of it.","Prestadír nods at you, but keeps his peace.","'Sit with me a moment, ${PLAYER}. I know you are leaving us, and that Théodred has need of you at the Ford. That is the way of it, is it not? We go where we are needed. The Grey Company owes its freedom to you and to the Prince of Rohan, and this is how Halbarad seeks to repay the debt to Théodred. Perhaps he thinks our debt to you is too deep to repay so easily?'\
\
Radanir raises an eyebrow and subjects you to close scrutiny.\
\
'Once this is all over, if such a thing is possible, you and I will meet at some inn in some peaceful land, and I will buy you a drink and you will buy me three, and we will wonder when we got so old.'\
\
He looks back at the Tree of Tribute, and seems to decide something.\
\
'I think Calenglad is wrong. I think it is just a tree.'","'I am sure Théodred will find a use for you at the Ford of Isen, ${PLAYER}. That is a crucial crossing, and it must be held against the forces of Saruman at any cost. We have seen the danger posed by the Dunlending clans, and the army of Uruks you beheld within Isengard sounds of considerable size.\
\
'Neither of those forces must cross the river Isen.'\
\
Calenglad's bleak expression is lightened by a wry smile.\
\
'You should say good-bye to Radanir. If you do not, we would never hear the end of it. He is east of here, I believe, on the path.'","Golodir nods at you, but there is nothing left to say, and he keeps his peace.","Corunir nods at you, but there is nothing left to say, and he keeps his peace."},
[2160]={"Calenglad nods at you, but there is nothing left to say and he keeps his peace.","The time has come for your path to diverge from that of the Grey Company, and you should bid farewell to the Rangers.","Halbarad nods at you, and keeps his peace.","'Prestadír is to the north-east, near the camp. He will want to say good-bye to you next.'","Talk to Prestadír by the winding road up to the camp in the Gravenwood","Book 5, Chapter 1: Separate Ways","Corunir nods at you, but there is nothing left to say and he keeps his peace.","'I heard it was time for you to leave us, ${PLAYER}. Be well on the road and give your courage to Théodred as you gave it to us.\
\
'If you have the opportunity to rescue Lothrandir from the clutches of Saruman, I hope you will take it. It is not right for us to abandon him to the enemy. I know it does not look good for him, but there is always hope. You escaped from the pits of Isengard, and Lothrandir is made of stern stuff as well.\
\
'I regret that we did not have the opportunity to speak more before this parting, my friend. Perhaps our paths will cross again, in happier days.'","Golodir nods at you, but there is nothing left to say and he keeps his peace.","'Prestadír is up by the camp, north-east of here. He will want to say good-bye to you before you leave us.'","Prestadír is to the north-east of Radanir, by the path that winds up to the camp in the Gravenwood.\
\
You should now say your good-byes to Prestadír."},
[2161]={"Radanir nods at you, but there is nothing left to say and he keeps his peace.","Talk to Halbarad in the camp in the Gravenwood","Calenglad nods at you, but there is nothing left to say and he keeps his peace.","'I am not one for long farewells, my friend. Know that you are one of us, with ties not of blood but rather strengthened by blood: the blood of our foes. Our roads entwined this far, and may do so again, but for now it is the time of leave-taking.\
\
'${PLAYER}, it has been an honour to travel with you. The Grey Company owes you much and more.'","Book 5, Chapter 1: Separate Ways","Halbarad is in the camp in the Gravenwood.\
\
You have made your farewells and should return now to Halbarad.","Corunir nods at you, but there is nothing left to be said and he keeps his peace.","'Stay safe on the road, my friend. We will see each other again.\
\
'Halbarad wanted to see you once you had made your farewells. He is somewhere within the camp, ${PLAYER}. You should return to him and prepare to depart.'","Golodir nods at you, but there is nothing left to be said and he keeps his peace.","'Halbarad is in the camp over there. He wanted you to return to him once you had made your farewells.'","The time has come for your path to diverge from that of the Grey Company, and you should bid your farewells to the Rangers."},
[2162]={"Enter the City Stables of Minas Tirith, in the First Circle","'Would you have these men of Gondor throw their lives away in a hopeless cause? Is it not wrong to send them against Gothmog without telling them first that he cannot be slain? I hold that it is.\
\
'But I know too that Men of Gondor are made of stern stuff, and many of these soldiers will fight him even so, before the end. They despair now, but when he comes to the city they will still defy him; and our hearts will be free of guilt, for we told them what we knew. In that hour there will be glory and honour for all!'","'Some soldiers from the Blackroot Vale told me that one of the wraiths leading the armies of Mordor, Gothmog, cannot be slain... not while some Ranger still lives! Golodir, I think his name was. You do not believe me? Ask them yourself! You will find them to the rear of the stables, up the stairs in the back!'","Book 5, Chapter 1: The Spread of Rumour","'You desire a rested horse to seek for aid from Rohan? What good will that do? Hirgon left on that errand some time ago, and should have returned by now! It is hopeless to think that Théoden and his Riders will come!\
\
'Even if they should do so, what does it matter? I have heard that the enemy commanders cannot be held by death!'\
\
You look at Lobordil quizzically, and his face twists with despair.\
\
'It is true! Some soldiers from the Blackroot Vale told me that one of the wraiths leading the armies of Mordor, Gothmog, cannot be slain... not while some Ranger still lives! Golodir, I think his name was. You do not believe me? Ask them yourself! You will find them to the rear of the stables, up the stairs in the back!'\
\
Lobordil studies your face closely, surely seeing the anger upon it. Duilin and Derufin were supposed to keep what they knew about Gothmog to themselves.","The damage is done, but some of the worried men might still be encouraged","'This I believe, my friend: if the Rohirrim do not come to the aid of Gondor, Minas Tirith will fall. There is little time left! Already the armies of Mordor approach; the city will soon be encircled.\
\
'Soon, I say, but not yet! Go to the lowest level of Minas Tirith and enter the City Stables, just within the entrance to the city! Speak to Lobordil there, and he will arrange for a rested steed to bring you past the line of the Enemy before it can close upon the city! You must follow the road north into Talath Anor and seek for Théoden and his Riders. If you find them, tell them to hasten!\
\
'If you do not find them, it will not matter even if you proceed all the way to Meduseld. Minas Tirith will have fallen by the time you reach it, and no one will be of help then.'","Mithrandir is worried about what will befall Minas Tirith if the Rohirrim do not arrive in time, as Denethor foretold, and has asked you to seek for them.","'I am sorry to see you so upset, my friend. I apologize for that, at any rate, but I still believe my brother and I have done right by these soldiers.\
\
'Would you have them throw their lives away in a hopeless cause? Is it not wrong to send them against Gothmog without telling them first that he cannot be slain? I hold that it is.\
\
'But I know too that Men of Gondor are made of stern stuff, and many of these soldiers will fight him even so, before the end. They despair now, but when he comes to the city they will still defy him; and our hearts will be free of guilt, for we told them what we knew. In that hour there will be glory and honour for all!'","Speak hopeful words to worried soldiers in the City Stables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Derufin on the second level of the City Stables","'I saw you speaking with the soldiers, ${PLAYER}, and I understand now why you were so cross with me and with the brothers from Blackroot. I will not quail from my duty, and I will not allow others to do so. I will fetch you a rested horse. When you return, if there is a White City to come back to, may you hear tales of our heroic stand, though we all become dust!'","The stables smell of hay and manure, and men speak in low, worried voices","Worried soldiers can be found throughout the City Stables of Minas Tirith.\
\
Duilin and Derufin have spread the rumour of Gothmog's invulnerability to death among the soldiers in the City Stables. You should do what you can to encourage the worried soldiers there, despite this troubling news.","'These men deserve to know the enemy they face, do they not? It is one thing to fight when you believe you have a chance at victory. It is quite another when you fight a hopeless battle against an enemy that cannot be slain! There is more glory to fight in that case, armed with the knowledge that you cannot win, and we thought these men deserved to have that knowledge and decide for themselves!\
\
'You must see it. For my part, I do not regret my words, and I know my brother feels the same. If the men curse the name of a faraway Ranger and use that anger to fight with more ferocity, is that not a benefit for the defenders of Gondor?'","'Go to the lowest level of Minas Tirith and enter the City Stables, just within the entrance to the city! Speak to Lobordil there, and he will arrange for a rested steed to bring you past the line of the Enemy before it can close upon the city! You must follow the road north into Talath Anor and seek for Théoden and his Riders. If you find them, tell them to hasten!\
\
'If you do not find them, it will not matter even if you proceed all the way to Meduseld. Minas Tirith will have fallen by the time you reach it, and no one will be of help then.'","The City Stables are in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, opposite the main gate of the city.\
\
Mithrandir asked you to go to the City Stables of Minas Tirith and ask Lobordil for a rested steed to bring you past the enemy line, north into Talath Anor.","Lobordil is in the City Stables of Minas Tirith.\
\
Despite the ill-advised rumour-spreading of the brothers of the Blackroot Vale, you still have a task set before you by Mithrandir: you must procure a rested steed from Lobordil in the City Stables, so you can seek the Rohirrim with all haste.","Duilin and Derufin are on the second level of the City Stables of Minas Tirith, up the stairs in the rear.\
\
You spoke what hopeful words you could to the worried soldiers in the City Stables, but it seemed to be of no use.","Talk to Lobordil in the City Stables","¡No te hace caso!","Lobordil is in the City Stables of Minas Tirith.\
\
Mithrandir asked you to speak to Lobordil in the City Stables, in order to procure a rested horse to bring you in search of Théoden and his Riders.","Duilin and Derufin must be told not to spread this news any further","'Go to the lowest level of Minas Tirith and enter the City Stables, just within the entrance to the city! Speak to Lobordil there, and he will arrange for a rested steed to bring you past the line of the Enemy before it can close upon the city! You must follow the road north into Talath Anor and seek for Théoden and his riders. If you find them, tell them to hasten!\
\
'If you do not find them, it will not matter even if you proceed all the way to Meduseld. Minas Tirith will have fallen by the time you reach it, and no one will be of help then.'","Duilin and Derufin are on the second level of the City Stables of Minas Tirith, up the stairs in the rear.\
\
Lobordil learned much from Duilin and Derufin that he should not have, and now should speak to them and learn who they spoke to about Gothmog.","'The battle approaches, ${PLAYER}. Are you ready for as much glory as we can attain before the end? But you are angry with us, I see it on your face. Why is this so?'\
\
You remind the impulsive brothers from the Blackroot Vale that they promised to keep secret the knowledge they gained of Gothmog in Osgiliath. Derufin makes a rude noise, and Duilin shakes his head at you with a frown.\
\
'That was before we returned to Minas Tirith, ${PLAYER}, and spent time with its defenders. These men deserve to know the enemy they face, do they not? It is one thing to fight when you believe you have a chance at victory. It is quite another when you fight a hopeless battle against an enemy that cannot be slain! There is more glory to fight in that case, armed with the knowledge that you cannot win, and we thought these men deserved to have that knowledge and decide for themselves!\
\
'You must see it. For my part, I do not regret my words, and I know my brother feels the same. If the men curse the name of a faraway Ranger and use that anger to fight with more ferocity, is that not a benefit for the defenders of Gondor?'","Talk to Duilin on the second level of the City Stables"},
[2163]={"Book 5, Chapter 2: Grimbold","This table is used by the Rohirrim to plan their strategy and movements","Find the map table in Grimbold's camp","'I want you to become familiar with the situation here, friend. Find the map table to the south-east; it is where we plan our movements and form our strategy. Speak also to Trumbald on the road north of the camp, and to Cynstan south of here, at the ford, to learn how things stand.'","Talk to Trumbald on the road north of Grimbold's camp","'Prince Théodred is somewhere in the camp, seeing to the preparations of the men. You should find him and see where you can help.'","'I understand Prince Théodred's men have established a camp in the Heathfells, far to the south, at the fords of the river Isen. While the Prince has been scouting in the Gravenwood, leadership of the camp fell to his second, a man named Grimbold.\
\
'Travel south to this camp and tell Grimbold you have come to help.'","'Grimbold's camp is in the Heathfells, south-east of the Gravenwood. Go there and help him to hold the river!'","Talk to Théodred in Grimbold's camp","'Hail. You must be ${PLAYER}. I am Cynstan, and I am the Prince's esquire: I help him with his armour and his steed and with anything else that needs doing.\
\
'Right now he has me bringing messages back and forth across the Ford, getting the men on the other side organized for the defence of the bank.\
\
'Someone has taken one of my bracers, and I think they have hidden it somewhere. It is their idea of a jest, I suppose. Nay, do not bother looking for it. It will turn up eventually.'","Grimbold's camp is in the Heathfells, south-east of the Gravenwood.\
\
Halbarad wants you to offer your help to Grimbold, Théodred's second in command at the fords of the river Isen.","Travel to Grimbold's camp and speak with Grimbold","Talk to Cynstan on the west bank of the Ford of Isen","'Hail. You must be ${PLAYER}. I am Cynstan, and I am the Prince's esquire: I help him with his armour and his steed and with anything else that needs doing.'","'I am devising a plan, ${PLAYER}, and once all is made ready I will want you to be a part of it. I am glad you have come! I would have welcomed any of your Ranger friends, as well, but I understand that they have their own mission; I wish them well in it!\
\
'Enough talk. It is time to strengthen my forces. They will have need of strength in the days to come.'","'Things have been quiet on the road for several days now. If Saruman does have an army, he is keeping it inside Isengard for now. I think those must just be tales, after all.'\
\
Trumbald looks at you curiously.\
\
'Were you really imprisoned by Saruman? There have been some arguments among the men about it.'\
\
You nod and tell him briefly of your stay within the Ring of Isengard and of your escape. His face falls at your tale.\
\
'How many uruks, did you say? By the Hammerhand, he does have an army.'","'Théodred has returned to us from his study of the Dunlending clans, and his news is worrying. He tells me you are the ${RACE} who escaped from Isengard and spoke of the army you saw being trained.\
\
'We will need your help if we are to hold this crossing against Saruman, ${PLAYER}. He commands both Dunlendings and uruks, and we must keep all of them on this side of the river, out of Rohan.\
\
'Familiarize yourself with the situation here, friend. Find the map table south-east of here, in the camp, to see where we plan the movements of our forces. I would also like you to speak with Trumbald on the road north of the camp to learn what he has seen there today. Speak also to Cynstan, Théodred's esquire, on the western bank of the Isen, south of here. He has been running messages back and forth across the ford as needed.\
\
'Once you have done these things, find Théodred somewhere in the camp. He is reacquainting himself with the situation here as well.'","Théodred is in Grimbold's camp, overseeing the preparations of his men.\
\
You have familiarized yourself with the situation in the Heathfells and should now find Théodred.","'Things have been quiet on the road for several days now. If Saruman does have an army, he is keeping it inside Isengard for now.'","The map table is in the south-east corner of Grimbold's camp. Trumbald is on the road north of the camp. Cynstan is south of the camp, on the western bank of the ford.\
\
Grimbold has asked you to become acquainted with the layout of his camp and to speak with several of the scouts to learn of the situation here.","You have said your farewells to the Grey Company, and it is now time to travel south to Théodred and Grimbold's camp in the Heathfells."},
[2164]={"You become aware of a strange creature watching you","'I see you long time before you see me. Do you walk with eyes closed in forest?'","'Here is the horse. Ride swift and sure, ${PLAYER}! If there is any hope out there to find, I trust that you will find it and bring it back to us!'","Lobordil provided you a rested horse to carry you with all haste along the road north of Minas Tirith in search of help.","Cross the bridge into Taur Drúadan, north-west of Hirgon's body","You leap from the back of your borrowed horse at the sight before you","You have found the remains of Hirgon, and his mortally-wounded fellow soldier, north of Minas Tirith, in Talath Anor.","The strange tracks continue to the south-west within the wood.","Study the strange tracks beneath the eaves of the wood","'Here is the horse. Ride swift and sure, ${PLAYER}! If there is any hope out there to find, I trust that you will find it and bring it back to us!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel in search of Théoden's Riders when you accept this quest.</rgb>","The drumming has become quite loud now, and you feel uneasy, as if you are being watched.","You have never seen tracks such as these before. Some figure walked here on two legs, but the grooves on either side cannot be explained.\
\
As you study the tracks and see they continue to the south-west, you hear the distant sound of drums emanating from deeper in the wood.","If the road through the Beacon-marches is held by the Enemy, you will need to pass through the wood to the south-west to reach Théoden.","You should enter the wood to the south-west if you are to find Théoden","You have found even more strange tracks","You feel as if you are being watched","The strange tracks continue to the south-west within the wood, and the drumming has gotten louder.","You should cross the bridge north-west of the bodies of Hirgon and Andothol, and decide what to do next.","Talk to Andothol where Hirgon lies, in Talath Anor","Travel south-west in search of more tracks","Travel further south-west seeking more of the strange tracks","'Are you... from the city...?'\
\
The man coughs wetly, and blood courses from his wounds. He will not live long.\
\
'You must know... this is Hirgon... errand-rider of Gondor. He returned from Rohan... bearing news... of Théoden. He will come! He will come... to the city...\
\
'The wall was... held against us... so we turned away. But the Orcs... caught up with us. They took... took his head. They would have had mine, but... but their leader urged them back... to the wall. But listen! Listen... to my last words...\
\
'A great camp... of foes... lies between Théoden and... and the city.... They cannot pass that way... they must... find another...'","Strange tracks on the dirt floor of the wood bear further inspection","There are strange tracks in the earth beneath the woods' canopy.","A strange squat creature watches you within the Drúadan Forest.","'Ride swift and sure, ${PLAYER}! If there is any hope out there to find, I trust that you will find it and bring it back to us!'","The tracks continue to the south-west, toward the distant drums","Lobordil has provided you with a rested horse to go in search of help along the northern road.","As you study the strange tracks, you notice that you have gotten closer to the drumming, though it is still distant. The tracks continue to the south-west. What creature has made these markings, and is it responsible for the drumming as well?","Travel north into Talath Anor in search of help","Enter the wood to the south-west, in Taur Drúadan","Talk to the strange creature in the Drúadan Forest","You have found more strange tracks, and they bear further inspection","Andothol speaks the truth. Théoden cannot come by the road","The tracks continue to the south-west","Book 5, Chapter 2: Ride Swift and Sure"},
[2165]={"Glóin está en su campamento al norte de Rivendel.\
\
Al derrotar a Gurzmat, lo encuentras acompañado por enanos Duramano hostiles. Glóin debe ser informado de inmediato sobre este acontecimiento.","Encuentra el campamento de los trasgos","Los trasgos tienen muchos campamentos entre las crestas de Pinnath Fenui, muy al este y al norte del campamento de Glóin.\
\
Glóin te dijo que, si buscas los campamentos de trasgos en las Montañas Nubladas, deberías encontrar a un trasgo llamado Gurzmat. Parece ser su líder, y al derrotarlo deberías sembrar la confusión entre los trasgos y, quizás, encontrar el rastro del Nazgûl.","Los campamentos de los trasgos se extienden a lo largo de las crestas de Pinnath Fenui.","'¿Has encontrado los campamentos, pero Gurzmat aún vive? ${PLAYER}, ¡eso no puede ser! Debes ascender hasta ese campamento de trasgos y acabar con Gurzmat.'","'¡¿Qué?! ¿Enanos Duramano con los trasgos? ¡Oh, sí, ahora todo encaja!\
\
'Mientras estabas fuera, uno de mis exploradores informó de algo interesante. Verás, la tarea que me encomendó el rey Dáin fue rastrear el último refugio de los Duramano. El explorador cree haberlo encontrado, pues había una gran cantidad de duramano en torno a una antigua fortaleza enana llamada Gabilazan. ¡Pero eso no fue lo único que descubrió!\
\
'Mientras observaba desde una alta cresta, dos figuras cabalgaron hasta la fortaleza. Una era un enano, la otra una figura encapuchada. Al principio no comprendió lo que veía, pero cuando todos los Duramano dejaron lo que estaban haciendo y vitorearon, supo que el enano no podía ser otro que ¡Skorgrím! Ahora, con lo que me has contado, la otra figura debía de ser el Espectro del Anillo. Parece que nuestras dos misiones son en realidad una sola, amigo.'","'¿Dices que Elrond mencionó a los trasgos cuando te envió aquí? No me sorprende. Yo me topé con unos trasgos problemáticos cuando crucé las Montañas Nubladas en la gran aventura de Thorin. En aquella ocasión, estuvimos gravemente acosados por ellos.\
\
'Ahora, parece que esas viles criaturas están más agitadas que nunca, y quizás tu Jinete sea la causa. Uno de los exploradores aquí informó haberlos visto alejarse mucho de sus guaridas hacia el este, y escuchó que cantaban \\qGurzmat\\q... sin duda, su líder.\
\
'Sí, eso es lo que hay que hacer. Mata a ese Gurzmat, y los trasgos quedarán tan desorganizados que no representarán un problema para nadie... y quizás así halles el rastro del Jinete que buscas. Busca las hogueras de los trasgos al norte y al este, a lo largo de Pinnath Fenui, y seguramente encontrarás a Gurzmat refugiado en lo profundo de uno de los campamentos. Me gustaría poder ayudarte más, pero como te dije, tengo una tarea más urgente encomendada por Dáin que requiere toda mi atención.'","Glóin te dijo que los trasgos parecen muy activos últimamente, y que no le sorprendería que el Nazgûl al que persigues fuese la causa.","Libro 5, Capítulo 2: Trasgos problemáticos","Gurzmat está en algún lugar profundo dentro del campamento de trasgos que se extiende por las crestas de Pinnath Fenui.\
\
Glóin te dijo que, al derrotar al trasgo Gurzmat, sembrarías la confusión entre los trasgos y quizás halles el rastro del Nazgûl que buscas.","'Los trasgos tienen un campamento en algún lugar por ahí, oculto entre las nieves. Busca hacia el este y el norte de aquí, a lo largo de las crestas de Pinnath Fenui. Una vez que encuentres este campamento, adéntrate en él. Si logras acabar con ese Gurzmat, seguramente pondrás fin a los planes de ese Jinete.'"},
[2166]={"'Son Khôr-buri-Ghân told of you, ${PLAYER}. He say you hate gorgûn. Prove to me and Wild Men help friends. Wild Men help horse-men.\
\
'Little time for proving. Horse-men ride for trap. Prove quickly.'","'I speak to father Ghân-buri-Ghân. Explore village. Meet Wild Men and learn our customs. I will see you here when done. Then bring to headman.'","'Headman see you now. Ghân-buri-Ghân has words to speak. May help ${PLAYER}, may help horse-men. Go and see.'","Talk to Wêg-pulo-Ghûr in Drû Bhûta","Book 5, Chapter 3: Older Than the Hills","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân and tell him about yourself","Khôr-buri-Ghân is in the Drúadan Forest.\
\
He has introduced himself as the son of the chief of the Wild Men, and wants to know what you are seeking and if it will prove harmful to the gorgûn.","You tell him that the Riders of Rohan have set forth from their kingdom to the aid of Gondor, but they will be slowed by the Orcs that have blockaded the road to Minas Tirith. You are unsure if anything can be done to clear the road in time, and tell him so.\
\
'Wild Men may know a way. Not Khôr-buri-Ghân's place to say. Come to Drû Bhûta. Speak to Ghân-buri-Ghân. He will speak for Wild Men.\
\
'Drû Bhûta village to west. Must go north-west through rocks, across water. Then back south. Hidden path. Look for narrow path climbing south-west. Khôr-buri-Ghân see you at front of village.'","'Stonehouse-folk built walls high, built walls strong. Now gorgûn surround walls. No more leaving for Stonehouse-folk.\
\
'That not Wild Man way. Stay hidden in wood. Gorgûn killed by arrows before see any Wild Man. Stonehouse-folk could have learned lesson, if listened. Never listen. Now trapped behind own wall.'","'Wild Men live here long time before others. Our land our own. I am called Khôr-buri-Ghân, son of headman Ghân-buri-Ghân.\
\
'Who are you? Why do you come to forest of Wild Men?'","Talk to Âm-buri-Sôl in Drû Bhûta","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân at the entrance to Drû Bhûta","Khôr-buri-Ghân is in the Drúadan Forest.\
\
He has introduced himself as the son of the chief of the Wild Men, and wants to know who you are and what brings you to his lands.","You introduce yourself and say from where you have come.\
\
'You are friend of Stonehouse-folk? Build walls, long time since they see Wild Men. In danger now.\
\
'You have welcome from Khôr-buri-Ghân, for time. If you prove false you will not live long in forest. You are no friend of gorgûn? Tell Khôr-buri-Ghân now.'","'Welcome to Drû Bhûta, village of Wild Men. Cause no harm here. You will find it place of peace.\
\
'I speak to father Ghân-buri-Ghân. Explore village. Meet Wild Men and learn our customs. I will see you here when done. Then bring to headman.'","Ghân-buri-Ghân, the leader of the Wild Men, can be found in the village of Drû Bhûta.","You have encountered one of the Wild Men of the Drúadan Forest. Can he or his people be of help to you?","He waits for you to speak again","Khôr-buri-Ghân's fellow Wild Men can be found throughout their village of Drû Bhûta.","Khôr-buri-Ghân is in the Drúadan Forest.\
\
He has introduced himself as the son of the chief of the Wild Men, and wants to know if you are a friend of the gorgûn.","Khôr-buri-Ghân is at the entrance to Drû Bhûta.","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân and tell him what you seek","You decide that the word gorgûn can only mean Orc-folk, and tell him that you hate gorgûn and their presence on the road has driven you into the forest.\
\
'Khôr-buri-Ghân knew this! Wild Men hate gorgûn. Kill gorgûn whenever come into wood. What do you seek? If it oppose gorgûn, Khôr-buri-Ghân wants it done, will help.'","Khôr-buri-Ghân is waiting to welcome you to the village of Drû Bhûta.","Talk to Mân-weni-Mhên in Drû Bhûta","'Wild Men hear word of much from forest. Horse-men pass by, never seeing. They find gorgûn if keep going. Headman say not to interfere. Maybe will, maybe not. Wild Men do as Ghân say. Wise leader know when to fight, know when not to fight.\
\
'Many folk could learn difference.'","'Wild Men not always beat gorgûn. Son of headman killed by gorgûn. Died outside wood, brought to camp. Bhai-buri-Ghân brother of Khôr-buri-Ghân. Gorgûn pay when Ghân-buri-Ghân decide to act. Not yet. Soon.\
\
'Gorgûn think they win, but gorgûn wrong. Soon will see.'","Find the entrance to Drû Bhûta, the village of the Wild Men","The entrance to Drû Bhûta is flanked by great Púkel-men","He waits for your answer","Khôr-buri-Ghân gave you directions to Drû Bhûta, the village of the Wild Men. He said: 'Drû Bhûta village to west. Must go north-west through rocks, across water. Then back south. Hidden path. Look for narrow path climbing south-west.'\
\
You hope you can follow that!","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân and answer his question","'Welcome to Drû Bhûta, village of Wild Men.'","Talk to Ghân-buri-Ghân"},
[2167]={"'Si logramos entrar en esta fortaleza, resolveremos dos problemas de un solo golpe. Al acabar con la amenaza de este Jinete, aseguraremos la seguridad de Rivendel, y al dar fin a Skorgrím, aplastaremos a los Duramano. Sin embargo, no será fácil, pues el explorador informó que ambos entraron en la torre interior de la fortaleza, la cual es casi inexpugnable.\
\
'Esto es lo que debes hacer, ${PLAYER}. Toda fortaleza enana tiene una entrada secreta y, aunque no conozco el secreto de Gabilazan, sé cómo descubrirlo. Cuando se colocó la piedra angular de Gabilazan, se guardó dentro de ella una copia de los planos de la fortaleza. La fortaleza se construyó alrededor de esa piedra, y ahora solo se puede acceder a ella entrando en la bóveda de Gabilazan. Una vez que tengamos los planos, podremos conocer la entrada secreta de la fortaleza.\
\
'Gabilazan se encuentra en el paso más occidental de los dos que dan acceso a Iorbar. El paso más oriental, Rakhâs-bizar, no está custodiado por enanos y podría darte un camino indirecto para acercarte a la torre.'","Lleva los planos de Gabilazan a Glóin","'¡Ah, maravilloso, encontraste la piedra angular y los planos estaban dentro! No lo mencioné antes de que partieras, pero había muchas posibilidades de que los planos hubiesen sido robados o destruidos hace años. ¡Parece que la fortuna sonríe sobre nosotros en este día!\
\
'¡Oh, y mira aquí! ¡Aquí está la entrada secreta de la torre interior!'","Libro 5, Capítulo 3: La Gran Fortaleza","Lleva los planos de Gabilazan a Glóin.","Recolecta los planos de la piedra angular de Gabilazan","'El paso a Gabilazan va de norte a sur y estará custodiado por los Duramano. Encuentra la bóveda en Gabilazan. Dentro de esa bóveda deberías poder hallar la piedra angular de la fortaleza. En esa piedra deberían estar los planos originales de la fortaleza.\
\
'Con esos planos, deberíamos ser capaces de descubrir la entrada secreta a la torre interior de la fortaleza.'","'Los planos están en Gabilazan, ${PLAYER}... ¡con ellos podremos encontrar la manera de entrar!'","La piedra angular que contiene los planos se halla dentro de la Bóveda de Gabilazan, ubicada en uno de los dos pasos al este del campamento de Glóin. El campamento de Glóin está al norte de Rivendel.\
\
Glóin te dijo que, para aprender cómo acceder a la entrada secreta de la torre interior de Gabilazan, necesitarás tomar los planos de la fortaleza colocados en su piedra angular.","Busca la piedra angular de Gabilazan","Buscando la piedra angular, descubres los planos de Gabilazan.","Planos de Gabilazan recolectados","Glóin te dijo que el Nazgûl al que persigues puede encontrarse en la antigua fortaleza enana de Gabilazan, en compañía de Skorgrím Duramano. Ambos entraron en la casi inexpugnable torre interior de la fortaleza. Glóin cree que la única forma de acceder a la torre interior es aprender la ubicación de su entrada secreta."},
[2168]={"Collected a thrown net (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'My men are practicing a technique to help them fight from horseback, a technique that will snare their opponents. With careful aim, my men can ensnare their enemy's legs with a thrown net. It will then keep the foe-man from attacking until our footmen can close the distance.\
\
'Gather up the nets they have already thrown and bring them to me, ${PLAYER}, and I will give them to new riders. This is something they must master if we are to be as effective as we must be.'","Book 5, Chapter 3: Training on the Banks","'Prince Théodred is somewhere in Grimbold's camp, south of here. Find him and tell him my riders will be ready for what he has planned.'","Bring the nets to Rungar","Collect thrown nets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Riders are practicing their net-throwing down the hill to the east of Rungar.\
\
Rungar has asked you to collect some of the thrown nets and bring them back to him.","'Very good. Their skill throwing the nets is improving with each pass. Once they have mastered it, we will be better prepared to face any unmounted foe that comes.\
\
'Théodred will wish to see you. He is somewhere in the camp to the south, I expect. Tell my Prince that the riders are becoming more skilled at the technique he suggested, and that I have some craftsmen working on more nets.'","'Where are the nets I asked you to bring me?'","Rungar is just to the north of Grimbold's camp, seeing to the training of riders under his command.\
\
Athelard has asked you to help Rungar with the training of his riders.","'I am ready to show you the strength of my arm, ${PLAYER}. I have sharpened my skills against many of my kinsmen. Let me now sharpen them further!'","Grimbold is in his camp in the Heathfells.\
\
Théodred has told you to speak with Grimbold if you wish to help the Rohirrim with their plan to take Saruman by surprise.","'My men need to be stronger if they are to stand against the forces marshalled by Saruman. Challenge a footman and an archer to combat and see how they fare.'","Rohirrim footmen and archers are training on the eyot in the Ford.\
\
Athelard has asked you to help train the footmen and archers under his command.","Athelard is on the eyot in the middle of the Isen, overseeing the training of his men.\
\
You have practiced sparring with the footmen and archers serving with Athelard and should tell him of your experience.","Athelard is on the eyot in the middle of the river, south-east of Grimbold's camp.\
\
Théodred wants you to help Athelard with training some of the youths who have seen less combat.","'Well? What do you think of their abilities? Are they made of stern enough stuff to stand against the forces of Saruman you beheld within Isengard?'\
\
Athelard sighs heavily.\
\
'They will have to do. You should find Rungar and help him with the training of his riders. He is just to the north of Grimbold's camp.'","'From what you have said, we know that Saruman has a much larger force of uruks than we do of Men. Grimbold estimates that each one of us is worth at least twenty uruks, but he is from Grimslade, and the men of that place are not known for their mastery of numbers. I fear he underestimates the savagery of Saruman's forces. And then there are the hostile Dunlending clans to consider.\
\
'Athelard has gone to the eyot in the middle of the river to train some of the men. They have seen less combat than others, and they have much to learn if they are to be of help during a real battle. Go to him and help train these youths.'","Rungar is north of Grimbold's camp.\
\
You have collected some of the nets thrown by the riders and should bring them to Rungar.","You have helped to strengthen the Rohirrim footman","'The training of our footmen and archers is well underway. Now you should help some of the riders with their training. Go north of Grimbold's camp and help Rungar.'","'The size of Saruman's army is of no account if he never moves it. I propose a strike to surprise him, and to show him he is not yet ready to march. Grimbold asked for you to ride with him, if you agree to help us with this plan.'","Talk to Théodred in Grimbold's Camp","Talk to Grimbold","Talk to Rungar","'These men need to be stronger. We are the only defence between Saruman's evil and the people of Rohan! I need to make them stronger.\
\
'Find a warrior and an archer and fight with them, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps your example will teach them something.'","'Prince Théodred's plan is a daring one, but there is wisdom in it. He is like his father in this: he does not shy away from using his strength where it is necessary.\
\
'I would like you by my side during this daring strike, ${PLAYER}. We will plant the seed of doubt in Saruman's mind, and he may think twice before sending his army forth.'","Talk to a Rohirrim archer training on the eyot","Talk to a Rohirrim footman training on the eyot","You have helped to strengthen the Rohirrim archer","'I have been the victor in many competitions, ${PLAYER}. Few can boast as swift an arrow or as true. If you believe you can best me in training, prove it is so!'","Talk to Athelard on the eyot in the Isen","The Rohirrim charged with holding the Ford of Isen are training so they will be ready when the need arises to push back Saruman's forces.","'Saruman has many more forces than we do. We need ours to be stronger than his, despite the numbers!\
\
'Athelard has taken some of the men to the eyot in the middle of the river to train. Go to him and help him with this task!'","Théodred is in Grimbold's camp, south of Rungar.\
\
Rungar has sent you to see Théodred.","'My men must master this technique, for the good of Rohan! Gather up the nets they have thrown and bring them to me. I can send another group of horsemen down to practice.'","'Your news is welcome, my friend. We need every man to be ready, for what I have in mind is dangerous. But the reward, should we prevail, could be significant.\
\
'If we wait until Saruman's army is ready, we cannot hope to hold the ford against him. We do not have the men. Your report of the size of Saruman's force has it much larger than I feared.\
\
'If we can catch him before he is ready, we might strike such a blow that his force will be sent into disarray. He is wise, yes, and is the wise man not cautious? He will see that we have taken him by surprise, and he will retreat behind his walls and he will continue to grow his army until he is certain we cannot oppose him. Every day that goes by is a day in our favour.\
\
'The size of his army is of no account as long as it stays within Isengard. Let it stay there forever. We must make him uncertain enough of his success that he never moves it. That is my proposal. If you are still willing to help us, Grimbold has asked that you ride with him.'"},
[2169]={"Ghân-buri-Ghân is in the village of Drû Bhûta.\
\
You entered Maudhúl Grak near Amon Dîn and recovered the body of Ghân-buri-Ghân's son, slain by Orcs. His other son, Khôr-buri-Ghân, has asked you to return to the Ghân and report your success.","Khôr-buri-Ghân asked you to draw the enemy's attention by entering the Orc-camp, Maudhúl Grak.","Proceed further into Maudhúl Grak and draw the enemy's eye","'My son Khôr-buri-Ghân not only kin. Bhai-buri-Ghân was eldest, but slain by gorgûn. Body taken to camp on road, north of forest. Khôr-buri-Ghân asked to recover body of brother. Ghân granted request. Help with task, and Ghân will offer aid to horse-men.\
\
'Go now to camp of gorgûn in north-east. Help Khôr-buri-Ghân and Wild Men help you.'","'After you go to the Blood-cloak, Wild Men seek out the Horse-men. We will help them. They need fear no gorgûn. Wild Men know secret way.\
\
'Blood-cloak is to east, atop hill on far side of falling water. My son Bhai-buri-Ghân rests there now.'","The wind gently sighs through the branches of the Blood-cloak as you approach","'I thank you. I found what is left of Bhai-buri-Ghân. I bring my brother back to Drû Bhûta. Go to Ghân-buri-Ghân and tell him what we did. Tell him we braved gorgûn, and Bhai-buri-Ghân no longer remain in clutches.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel back to Drû Bhûta when you finish speaking with Khôr-buri-Ghân.</rgb>","There are many dead Orcs here. Khôr-buri-Ghân has been busy!","'There is sorrow here. There is gladness too. Many Wild Men buried at base of Blood-cloak. We remember them all; we remember Bhai-buri-Ghân.\
\
'Ghân-buri-Ghân grateful for what we did. Grateful as father. Grateful as headman of Wild Men. As headman his command is clear: Wild Men will help Horse-men.'","'My brother Bhai-buri-Ghân rests here now.'","Book 5, Chapter 4: The Hated Orcs","You have found more dead Orcs. Khôr-buri-Ghân is further ahead to the north-west","Ghân-buri-Ghân has set before you a task to complete, and if you are successful he has pledged to help the Rohirrim with their passage.","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân at the Blood-cloak in Drû Bhûta","'Many gorgûn inside, ${PLAYER}. Draw their eyes to you. Khôr-buri-Ghân will slay them from hiding. They will pay for death of Wild Men. They will pay for death of Bhai-buri-Ghân.'","Enter Maudhúl Grak and draw the enemy's eye","'My son Khôr-buri-Ghân not only kin. Bhai-buri-Ghân was eldest, but slain by gorgûn. Body taken to camp on road, north of forest. Khôr-buri-Ghân asked to recover body of brother. Ghân granted request. Help with task, and Ghân will offer aid to horse-men.\
\
'Go now to camp of gorgûn. Help Khôr-buri-Ghân and Wild Men help you.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to the Orc-camp when you accept this quest.</rgb>","Talk to Ghân-buri-Ghân in Drû Bhûta","You should return to Drû Bhûta and speak with Ghân-buri-Ghân.","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân outside the Orc-camp near Amon Dîn","Khôr-buri-Ghân is in the depths of Maudhúl Grak, waiting to speak with you.","Khôr-buri-Ghân has gone to the Orc-camp on the road north of the Drúadan Forest.\
\
Ghân-buri-Ghân has offered to help the Rohirrim if you will help his youngest son recover the body of his slain eldest.","Return to Drû Bhûta","Talk to Khôr-buri-Ghân in Maudhúl Grak","Khôr-buri-Ghân asked you to draw the enemy's attention by entering the Orc-camp.","Travel to the Blood-cloak in Drû Bhûta, on a rocky cliff on the eastern side of the huge waterfall","'Wild Men walk the forest with speed. My son Khôr-buri-Ghân already returned. He brings his brother to the Blood-cloak. Go to him there. Wild Men mourn deeply, but not long.\
\
'After you go to the Blood-cloak, Wild Men seek out the Horse-men. We will help them. They need fear no gorgûn. Wild Men know secret way.\
\
'Blood-cloak is to east, atop hill on far side of falling water. My son Bhai-buri-Ghân rests there now.'","The Blood-cloak is to the east of the great waterfall in Drû Bhûta, atop a large rocky cliff. It is the location where the Wild Men perform their funerary rites."},
[2170]={"Recolecta la Piedra Clave","La bóveda enana que contiene la Piedra Clave se encuentra en el Mirador de Iskeld, cerca de la naciente del Bruinen. Glóin está en su campamento al norte de Rivendel.\
\
Glóin te ha pedido que recuperes una Piedra Clave de una antigua bóveda enana. La Piedra Clave permitirá el acceso a la fortaleza enana ocupada por los Duramano.","Lleva la Piedra Clave a Glóin","'¡Sí, sí, esta es la Piedra Clave de la que te hablé! ¡Buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}! Ahora comenzará el verdadero desafío.'","'¡Ah, sí! Será como cuando el Saqueador Bilbo se escabulló en la guarida de Smaug. Solo necesitaremos la Piedra Clave para abrir la puerta secreta, y así entrarás en la torre interior. Encontrar esa piedra, sin embargo, podría resultar un desafío.\
\
'Ahora bien, los viejos relatos de Helegrod —ese gran salón enano al norte que cayó ante el dragón Thorog— dicen que, tras ser abandonado, también fueron abandonados todos los salones enanos de los alrededores. Las Piedras Clave que abrían las puertas secretas de todos esos salones fueron ocultadas en una pequeña bóveda enana cerca de la naciente del Bruinen. Puede que el edificio esté en ruinas ahora, pero la bóveda seguramente aún sigue allí. ¡Una vez que tengamos la Piedra Clave, la torre interior de Gabilazan se abrirá para nosotros!\
\
'Viaja al norte, hacia la naciente del Bruinen, y busca la bóveda en el Mirador de Iskeld. Deberás enfrentarte a las bestias de nieve que habitan entre los ventisqueros, ¡pero no espero que eso sea un problema para ti!'","Libro 5, Capítulo 4: La Piedra Clave","Glóin descubrió la entrada secreta a la torre interior de Gabilazan, pero el acceso está cerrado y requiere un artefacto de los viejos tiempos.","'Por favor, consigue esa Piedra Clave. ¡No podremos entrar en la torre interior sin ella! Busca en la naciente del Bruinen la bóveda enana.'","Piedra Clave recolectada"},
[2171]={"Examine the map table and complete 'Battle of the Ford, Sunset'","You study the maps placed on the table and consider Théodred's plan.\
\
If all goes well, the Prince should have victory by afternoon. If all goes well....\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","You study the maps placed on the table and consider Théodred's plan.\
\
When the sun sets on the Twenty-fifth of February, Théodred expects to return to the Ford with newfound confidence in his defences. Perhaps it will be so.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Grimbold is in his camp by the Ford of Isen.\
\
Grimbold is waiting to speak with you following the events of the day.","Talk to Grimbold in his camp in the Heathfells","The map table is in Grimbold's camp.\
\
Study the map table in Grimbold's camp to continue Prince Théodred's retreat.","The map table is in Grimbold's camp.\
\
Study the map table in Grimbold's camp to witness the aftermath of the battle.","The map table is in Grimbold's camp.\
\
Study the map table in Grimbold's camp to begin Prince Théodred's attack.","You study the maps placed on the table and consider Théodred's plan. Once he has come within sight of Isengard, he will order his men to attack the Orcs arrayed outside the walls.\
\
He thinks to arrive outside Isengard by mid-day.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'Prince Théodred's plans are set forth on the map table, ${PLAYER}. Study them to acquaint yourself with them.\
\
'We will begin at dawn on the Twenty-fifth. We will strike Saruman hard and fast and use his own caution against him. So long as he thinks his army is not ready to march and must remain behind the walls of Isengard, it will be of no threat to Rohan.'","Prince Théodred's plan to strike at Saruman and prevent him from unleashing his armies began on the morning of the Twenty-fifth of February, but much would happen by nightfall.","'Use the map table to see the plan of attack for the battle, ${PLAYER}.'","You study the maps placed on the table and consider Théodred's plan.\
\
This is indeed a daring move, and the Prince expects it to renew Saruman's caution. By nightfall, who knows what the situation may be? It could be that night will bring with it renewed hope for Rohan. There are other possibilities as well, but they are darker and more grim.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Examine the map table and complete 'Battle of the Ford, Afternoon'","Examine the map table and complete 'The Daring Strike, Dawn'","The map table is in Grimbold's camp.\
\
Study the map table in Grimbold's camp to continue Prince Théodred's attack.","Book 5, Chapter 4: The Prince of Rohan","You study the maps placed upon the table and consider Théodred's plan. First, he must determine what defences to leave at the Ford of Isen, then he will ride north to Isengard with a host of riders.\
\
The attack will begin at dawn.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Examine the map table and complete 'The Prince of Rohan, Night'","Examine the map table and complete 'The Daring Strike, Mid-day'","'This was no accident, ${PLAYER}. Saruman sought to slay our prince, and he succeeded. With that accomplished, he is content to have his forces retreat! This is a hollow victory. We hold the Ford, but the loss of Théodred is too much for Rohan to bear.\
\
'We have lost much this day, but we cannot despair. We must not! We must hold this crossing or die.\
\
'Saruman accomplished what he wished this day, but there will come another day, and when it does he will seek to cross the Isen and move into Rohan. My men and I will stand against him, and if you will stand with us we may stand the longer.\
\
'These dark days grow darker still. Rest now, while you can, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[2172]={"'Ah, hola ${PLAYER}. ¡Una batalla gloriosa nos espera!\
\
'¿Están tú y tus aliados listos? Mi padre me envió la Piedra Clave, así que estoy preparado. ¡Vamos ahora a las Montañas a derrotar a Skorgrím y a sus Duramano!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si eliges realizarla en solitario, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será considerable.</rgb>","'¡Fue un buen combate, ${PLAYER}! ¡Un ejercicio así no se presenta todos los días!'","'¡Ahora que tenemos la Piedra Clave, el acceso trasero a la fortaleza duramano estará abierto! Deberías poder confrontar tanto al Nazgûl como a Skorgrím. Sin embargo, la tarea será ardua, y necesitarás ayuda, así que reúne un grupo de aliados. Además, dado que completar esta misión puede significar el fin de Skorgrím, un gran beneficio para el Pueblo de Durin, enviaré a mi hijo Gimli contigo para ayudar en la batalla. Le confiaré tanto la Piedra Clave como el conocimiento secreto enano necesario para abrir la puerta.\
\
'Ve y reúne un grupo de aliados, y prepárate para la batalla que se avecina. Una vez que te alistes, habla con Gimli. Él se encuentra en una de las habitaciones de invitados de la Casa de Elrond. Juntos se dirigirán a la fortaleza, y él abrirá el camino secreto hacia el recinto interior.\
\
'¡Será un gran día para los Pueblos Libres, ${PLAYER}! ¡Espero tu regreso con la historia de tu victoria!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si eliges realizarla en solitario, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será considerable.</rgb>","'¡Qué gloriosa batalla tuvimos contra esos Duramano!'","Glóin está en su campamento al norte de Rivendel.\
\
El Nazgûl abandonó la fortaleza enana, ordenando a Skorgrím que te matara. Afortunadamente, lograste derrotar a Skorgrím, pero un espíritu malvado emergió de su cadáver y maldijo a los barbiluengos antes de desaparecer. Debes contarle todo lo ocurrido a Glóin.","Libro 5, Capítulo 5: El Último Refugio","Habla con Gimli en Rivendel","'¡Has hecho un gran servicio a los barbiluengos, amigo mío! ¡La línea de Durin te está en deuda!'","'Habla con Gimli cuando tus aliados estén listos, y él te guiará hasta la fortaleza enana. Se encuentra en una de las habitaciones de invitados a lo largo del camino que sube por la ladera sur del Valle de Imladris.'","Gimli se encuentra en una de las habitaciones de invitados de la Casa de Elrond.\
\
Cuando hayas reunido a tu compañía, busca a Gimli; él te acompañará a la fortaleza enana donde podrían ocultarse el Nazgûl y Skorgrím.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si eliges realizarla en solitario, recibirás un bono de inspiración, pero el desafío será considerable.</rgb>","'Traes noticias tanto alegres como sombrías, ${PLAYER}. ¡Los Duramano han sido derrotados! Nunca volverán a amenazar a los barbiluengos.\
\
'Aunque la noticia del espíritu que emergió de Skorgrím es inquietante, no es tan perturbadora como la del escape del Nazgûl. Peor aún, me dices que habló de llevar hombres a Helegrod. Lo que busca en aquel antiguo salón enano es un misterio para mí.\
\
'Desafortunadamente, aún queda mucho por hacer si Rivendel ha de estar segura. Pero ten la certeza de que te brindaré toda la ayuda que pueda.'","Con la Piedra Clave en mano, ahora puedes entrar en la fortaleza enana de Gabilazan, último refugio de los Duramano, y enfrentar tanto al Nazgûl como a Skorgrím."},
[2173]={"Talk to Thrymm Red-beard in the south-eastern reaches of the encampment in Taur Drúadan","Talk to Harding in the north-eastern reaches of the encampment in Taur Drúadan","Talk to Herubrand in the western reach of the encampment in Taur Drúadan","Harding is in the north-eastern reaches of the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan.","'There is a familiar face, though it was long ago and many miles from here when last I saw it: ${PLAYER} the ${CLASS}!\
\
'I am delighted to tell you that my son Horn has come to his senses at last! He has had a welcome change of heart and ridden with the company, as he should.\
\
'And most welcome of all: he has left his wild-woman behind!'","'You are a long way from the Northmarch, ${PLAYER}! I did not know you would respond to the muster of Théoden, but I should have, with no question! I know the King will be glad to see you have arrived!\
\
'I came at the behest of Harding, though the injury I suffered at the hands of Núrzum still pains me. The Aldor gave me a new steed to replace poor Windfoot, and its gait is less gentle than that of my old friend. Still, my leg is on the mend.\
\
'I could not refuse Harding's command, and would not, even were both my legs wounded as the one. For now the multitude waits for the King to decide our further course; there is some trouble in our way. While the Riders wait on his command, you should speak with some of the men. I am certain the spirits of many will be buoyed to see you again!'","'Wild Men go through wood by secret paths. Khôr-buri-Ghân will take you to Horse-men. Go at once! Stonehouse-folk not stand long against gorgûn.'","Talk to Ingbert in the eastern area of the encampment in Taur Drúadan","Talk to Wídfara on the edge of the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan","'Speak to Ingbert of the Entwash Vale! His tent is just to the west of here.'","'We meet again, ${PLAYER}, once more on the eve of battle! I have ten Éoreds of men from the Westfold with me, and we ride with Théoden King to the aid of Gondor. Some of these men fought with me at the Fords, and still others defended the Deep from Saruman's malice. They catch what rest they can before we make to move again.\
\
'There is some trouble on the road ahead. I heard scouts tell that Orcs have blocked the straight way to the Pelennor. The danger does not worry me. Nay, I am worried that dealing with this force will slow us overmuch, and by the time we reach the White City it will be filled not with doughty men but with ravening Orcs.\
\
'Time is our greatest enemy on this road, ${PLAYER}, as it ever is.'","Book 5, Chapter 5: The Long Road to Battle","'While the Riders wait on his command, you should speak with some of the men. I am certain the spirits of many will be buoyed to see you again!'","The guard calls out to you to halt, when suddenly his face lights up with recognition","Harding told you to speak to Ingbert at his tents to the west, in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan.","'You have joined this ride as well, I see. Should we get to Minas Tirith in time, there will be quite a battle. But it is not certain we will do so, for there is some trouble ahead in the road.'\
\
You tell Harding that you spoke with Thrymm about his journey from Wildermore.\
\
'Then you must have heard that my son Léodwig led the defence of Harwick against the creeping Orcs and Easterlings? My heart swelled to hear the Red-beard speak of my son's charge from the city! He will bear his wounds proudly, and if my own road is to end in the battles to come, I will know that the Wold is in capable hands. I did not think my boy would have the ability to lead men in battle; indeed, I sent him to investigate Wildermore in part because I thought he could not handle the dangers pressing from the east.\
\
'But I am pleased to have been wrong. Sons have a way of growing up and becoming men, I suppose. Speak to Ingbert of Entwash Vale if you doubt me! He told me that his own son, Horn, has experienced a similar transformation!\
\
'Ingbert's tents are to the west of here.'","Talk to Fastred in the north-eastern reach of the encampment in Taur Drúadan","Talk to Grimbold in the centre of the encampment in Taur Drúadan","'I thought you would be somewhere in this assemblage, ${PLAYER}! My lands were well-represented in the muster, and my heart soared to see the gladness in my King's eye for it. Three score and three hundred valiant men of the Sutcrofts awaiting his command!\
\
'My son Folcred will weather the storm in Edoras, with my mother.  It was the vile Crúmgam that moved her to spirit Folcred away from Snowbourn, but now I am glad that it was done. The Lady Éowyn will keep them safe, and my wife Elflád has gone after them to wait until the war be done.\
\
'For my part, I am hoping to see Crúmgam in our path on the road to Gondor. He and I have unfinished matters to which we must attend. Insults were done to me and my house, and I would have them repaid... repaid in blood!'","Ghân-buri-Ghân and the Wild Men have agreed to help Théoden and his Riders, and will show you the way to their encampment.","Wídfara is at the entrance to the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan.","The Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan is located west of the hill of Eilenach, along the road.","Find the entrance to the Rohirrim encampment west of Eilenach, along the road","Talk to Elfmar in the eastern reach of the encampment in Taur Drúadan","'Wild Men go through wood by secret paths. Khôr-buri-Ghân will take you to Horse-men. Go at once! Stonehouse-folk not stand long against gorgûn.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically go with Khôr-buri-Ghân when you accept this quest.</rgb>","'${PLAYER}! What adventures have brought you to join this assemblage? I have here but one Éored, but it is composed of the fiercest warriors in all of Rohan, I stake my honour upon it! We have been through much to come so to this company.\
\
'We received the call to the weapontake on the night of March 11th, and I began to gather what men I could: two Éoreds of Wildermore's most skilled riders. At dawn, I led these men east to the Wold, but I did not know that danger was so near: under cover of darkness, Orcs and Easterlings had crossed the river at the Undeeps. They overwhelmed the watchers at Stangard and crossed into the Wold.\
\
'The Enemy assailed Harwick, but Aldor Harding had already gone to the weapontake. His son Léodwig remained in the city, and saw that all would soon be lost. That is when my Éoreds charged right into the flank of the Enemy! Our fortunes did not hold, and we were soon routed. The city was now afire. Léodwig rode forth and fought valiantly, but he was grievously wounded. We withdrew to a defensible position on a hilltop; it was to be the location of our last stand.\
\
'Early in the morning on March 12th, as the Enemy prepared to climb the hill and put an end to us, one of our scouts reported hearing a sighing sound on the wind. It was the rustling of branches, thousands of them, and it rushed down from Wildermore in a great flood of sound.\
\
'Behind this great sound came the trees, dozens of trees in every variety, and among them strode great shepherds. At first I thought these were devils of Núrzum's kind, but it was not so. They were led by a strange fellow by the name of Leaflock, and he spoke in halting fashion of many unfathomable mysteries, some of which I have still not unravelled. There will be time for determining the meaning behind his words later, if we survive the war ahead. He did not consider himself or his people warriors, but I can tell you they became terror on the battlefield. The Enemy will not come back to the Wold.\
\
'There was only one Éored left to me after this battle. We rode with haste to the Entwade and changed horses. We passed Aldburg at dusk but did not stop. Upon reaching Beaconwatch we had to stop and rest, and learned there that Théoden camped in the Firien Wood the night before!\
\
'At dawn on the 13th, with our horses refreshed, we crossed the Mering-stream and rode hard through the Beacon Hills. We were so close, but not yet close enough: we were beset by Orcs and Variags near Amon Dîn. We broke through the line of Variags, but they did not pursue us. I think now I know the reason: they knew the road ahead would be held against us.\
\
'In the darkness of night, we came to the western flank of the encampment in the Drúadan, and were nearly turned into pincushions by Grimbold's sentries! At the last moment, one of the archers recognized me by the spectre of my beard, crimson in the guttering light of the single torch they allowed! Can you imagine what Cyneberg would say if this great tale of mine, of riding more than five hundred miles in three days to the aid of my King, ended with me and my men put in the ground by our own sworn-brothers? I can imagine what she would say, and it makes my head hurt more than any of Núrzum's tantrums!\
\
'That is the tale, ${PLAYER}. We have ridden hard, and through battle, to stand with Théoden King. Onward to triumph and glory! I have spoken already with Harding, and given him news of his son, but you should speak to him also. He is in the north-eastern reaches of the encampment.'","Wídfara thought you should visit many of the Riders encamped in Taur Drúadan, believing it would lift their spirits.","'Who comes hither? ${PLAYER}? I can hardly believe it!'","'Ah, welcome to the last journey, ${PLAYER}! The Stonedeans are behind, and Gondor lies ahead! The words of Hildegard served me as a shield in my fight with the Dunlendings, as I knew they would. The seeress spoke of my death by Orkish hand? Then let me fight the Dunlending tribes from morning until night!\
\
'But now that Woodhurst is reclaimed and Gifemund oversees it in my name, I will not refuse the command of my King. I march to war, and I wonder if the Orc that will lay me low stands ready somewhere at the end of this road. He certainly does, but I will not let that dissuade me from facing him!\
\
'I have prepared my son Herefara for this, if my days are soon to be ended. He knows our duty. Join us and rejoice, ${PLAYER}! Glory and honour awaits us!'","Thrymm Red-beard and his Éored are on a rise in the south-eastern reaches of the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan.","'It is good to see you among the soldiers, ${PLAYER}! My father and I responded to the muster of Théoden King with as many men as we could find. We have eight Éoreds between us, a fine number. The Elfward will prove itself worthy of its reputation!\
\
'I hope to fight alongside my shield-brother Éomer in the coming engagement, but that may not come to pass. The marching order is not yet set, but when we come to Pelennor he will likely ride with the King's Men and I will be among the Eorlingas. Still, the press of battle will no doubt allow us both much chance for glory!\
\
'I am certain you will attain no small share of it for yourself, friend ${CLASS}!'","'Horse-men camp down stone-road ahead. Wild Men count many thousand Horse-men. Go to them. You help. Wild Men help also.'"},
[2174]={"Helegrod se encuentra al norte del campamento de Glóin.\
\
A la entrada de la tesorería de Helegrod encontraste tumularios. Deberías derrotar a uno y registrar sus restos en busca de alguna pista que revele qué los ha traído aquí.","Has recogido el Sello de Drugoth","'Helegrod se alza al norte de aquí. Tal vez, explorando sus bordes, podamos aprender más de los planes del Jinete Negro para ella.'","Explora los bordes de Helegrod","Al enterarse de que el Nazgûl huyó a Helegrod, Glóin te contó parte de la historia de esa antigua fortaleza.","Registra a uno de los tumularios","'¡Espectros!. Deberías volver y registrar a uno de ellos. Seguro que esto es obra del Jinete. Pero debemos saber más. Quizás haya alguna pista de lo que los trajo hasta aquí. Derrota a uno y revisa sus restos.'","Helegrod se encuentra al norte del campamento de Glóin. La tesorería exterior está cerca de Nan Gongarag.\
\
Glóin piensa que podrías descubrir cuál es el plan del Nazgûl para Helegrod explorando los bordes de esa sala abandonada en busca de la entrada a la tesorería. Te advirtió que no entres en Helegrod, pues está demasiado bien custodiada por oscuras criaturas.","Lleva el Sello de Drugoth a Glóin","Libro 5, Capítulo 6: Tras los pasos del mal","Has descubierto la Tesorería de Helegrod","'¡Espectros! ¡Sin duda esto es obra del Jinete! Y ese sello que encontraste en uno de ellos... puedo decir que es un artefacto del mal, pero su verdadero significado me sobrepasa. Quizás sea hora de pedir ayuda al Maestro Elrond.'","'Si tienes un momento, permíteme contarte parte de la historia de Helegrod, cuyas ruinas se encuentran al norte de aquí. Tal vez esta historia arroje luz sobre lo que el Jinete busca lograr, aunque no puedo adivinar qué será. Helegrod fue excavada bajo la montaña de Orod Lostol; durante largos años permaneció como el puesto más septentrional de Khazad-dûm. Allí nunca se halló mithril, pero sí muchas otras gemas y riquezas. Esas riquezas atrajeron a un dragón a Helegrod. Thorog era su nombre; mató a todos los enanos e hizo su lecho en la tesorería de Helegrod.\
\
'En Khazad-dûm, al que los Elfos llaman Moria, Durin reunió una compañía de enanos para viajar a Helegrod y dar muerte a la bestia. Thorog fue derrotado, pero Durin cayó por el último aliento del dragón. Era el quinto con ese nombre; el siguiente también tuvo un triste fin, pero no hablaré de eso ahora. Los enanos intentaron reclamar Helegrod en los años siguientes, pero la muerte pesaba sobre aquel lugar y finalmente abandonaron los salones, trasladando las riquezas de Helegrod a Khazad-dûm.\
\
'No sé qué pretende el Jinete al tomar Helegrod. Tal vez solo quiera fortificarla, pero apostaría a que hay más en este hecho de lo que podemos ver. Quizás, explorando los bordes de Helegrod, podamos aprender más de sus planes. No intentes entrar en Helegrod mismo —demasiadas cosas oscuras moran allí—, sino busca la tesorería exterior, cerca de Nan Gongarag.'"},
[2175]={"Talk to Horn in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan","Talk to Gléowine in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan","'The air was still and cold, and the silence stretched between us. I was torn between two duties: service to the woman of my heart and the child our love would bring forth, and to Théoden, the king of my home-land.\
\
'And that is when I realized that they were not different at all. If Rohan is consumed by war and falls to the Enemy's hordes, it will not matter where Nona and I and our child might prepare for our last stand. We will be alone. Together, but alone, and the Enemy will have us.\
\
'But if Théoden defies the forces of Mordor, and finds victory, then there might be peace. Only then will there be safety for the woman I love, and for the child our love is bringing forth. Only then. She thinks I chose to ride for Théoden to seek glory, or for honour, but neither of those are the reason. I ride for Rohan for my Dunlending wife, and for my Dunlending child, that they may be safe from the evils of Mordor.\
\
'It was the most difficult decision I have ever had to make, ${PLAYER}, and it may have been the wrong one. But still I have made it. It was the only thing I could have done, and if it is wrong and Hildegard is right, and I ride to my death in Gondor far from those I love... well, you have my permission to tell my old music-master Gléowine that he was right after all.'\
\
You look at Horn quizzically.\
\
'Oh, Gléowine and I have been having a disagreement about what it means to fight. Do not tell him this, but I think I have been arguing mostly to convince myself, rather than him. I have cut a most impressive figure doing so, I think: the very picture of a valiant man of Rohan. I seem to have convinced my father, at any rate. Find Gléowine if you would like to hear his side of the argument.\
\
'It is good to see you, ${PLAYER}. I wish that we had met again in happier circumstances, but there are few enough of those in these dark days. Stay well, my friend.'","'Gléowine and I have been having a disagreement about what it means to fight. Do not tell him this, but I think I have been arguing mostly to convince myself, rather than him. I have cut a most impressive figure doing so, I think: the very picture of a valiant man of Rohan. I seem to have convinced my father, at any rate. Find Gléowine if you would like to hear his side of the argument.\
\
'It is good to see you, ${PLAYER}. I wish that we had met again in happier circumstances, but there are few enough of those in these dark days. Stay well, my friend.'","Dernhelm looks at you warily, but he says nothing.","'Nay, it is true! My son has finally shown some sense, and has chosen to leave the foolish loves of his youth behind him. He will do his duty as I his father command, and as his King requires. War is calling, and finally my son will prove he is a man of Rohan and worthy of my blood-line!\
\
'Would that he had realized it sooner! I might have been spared much frustration. You do not believe that Horn has so chosen? Ask him yourself, and you will see!'","Horn is in the clearing where his father Ingbert's men are resting before the ride continues.","Horn sighs heavily, sorrow etched deeply upon his face","'My son has finally shown some sense, and has chosen to leave the foolish loves of his youth behind him. He will do his duty as I his father command, and as his King requires. War is calling, and finally my son will prove he is a man of Rohan and worthy of my blood-line!\
\
'Would that he had realized it sooner! I might have been spared much frustration. You do not believe that Horn has so chosen? Ask him yourself, and you will see!'","Elfhelm said someone with something to add to the subject of duty is just to the west, and you should find this person if you can keep the meeting a secret.","You have learned that Horn has joined Théoden's riders for the journey to Gondor.","'Horn is full of pride, like his father Ingbert, and will not be persuaded. He is a man of Rohan, for certain: stubborn and hard-headed, thinking always of duty and honour and service! May it not be the death of him!'","Elfhelm is not far from his tent in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan.\
\
Elfhelm has listened to your conversation with Gléowine, and has something of his own to add.","Elfhelm, standing nearby, catches your eye and your attention","Book 5, Chapter 6: What It Means to Fight","Horn is in the clearing where his father Ingbert's men are resting before the ride continues.\
\
Ingbert claims that his son has finally come to his senses, and challenged you to find out for yourself.","'Hullo there, ${PLAYER}! At last someone will speak to me! I have only had Dernhelm here for company, and he speaks very little. It is almost as if none of the men here can see me! I am almost certainly not supposed to be here; I hope that Théoden will not be cross with me when he finds out.\
\
'But what was I supposed to do? I could not stay behind while all others have gone off to danger! That has been this hobbit's story almost from the very beginning! Frodo, and Sam, and Pip, all gone off now, braving danger in strange lands. I could not let it happen again! I am grateful that Dernhelm saw fit to help me come along.\
\
'He has an understanding with Elfhelm, I think. The old marshal is turning a blind eye to my presence here, and I am glad of it! I just hope I am not too much of a burden... on the road or in the battle that is certain to come.'","'This accursed darkness has cast a pall upon my heart, ${PLAYER}, but it is brightened somewhat to see you again. Much has happened since we parted. Is Corudan with you? Call him over and I will tell you my tale, for he should hear of it as well.'\
\
You tell Horn that you were separated from Corudan before the forces of Saruman fell upon Helm's Deep, and were unable to find the Elf after the fighting ended. Horn is silent for a time, and then shakes his head.\
\
'I am sure he is fine, wherever he has gone. I do not believe he would fall prey to Saruman's evil so easily, or so quietly. That there is no trace of him should lighten our worry, not increase it.'\
\
It seems to your ear that Horn is trying to convince himself more than you, but you do not press the issue. He is silent again for a long moment. When he finally speaks, his voice is full of sorrow.\
\
'Nona and I did not find the Falcon Clan raiding-party, ${PLAYER}. Indeed, I think now that she did not really intend to search for Lheu Brenin at all; her plan was in service of a ruse. I blame her not for it, now, but I confess that when the shape of her mind became clear I spoke harshly.\
\
'She wanted to get me alone to tell me to abandon Rohan. She wanted us to find a place where we might live free from the demands of kings and Wizards. 'If the forces of evil triumph, let us face them together, not for kingdom or for blood-lines but for ourselves!' she said. But I would not listen. I was angry to be made to choose in this fashion. I told her that I did not always know what it meant to be a man of Rohan, but our adventures together taught me much on the matter, and I wanted to serve my King as I should.\
\
'There were more words, and they were hurtful. I made to leave, and Nona told me that if I rode to war with Théoden, I would die before the walls of the White City. 'How can you know this?' I asked her, but before she answered I knew the answer. Hildegard the Soothsayer spoke to Nona of my death. Nona believed it, though I do not.\
\
'That was not her final attack, ${PLAYER}, and this last strike was to be the most deadly, though it also proved decisive in the matter. Nona said to me that she was with child. Hildegard had told her this, but Nona did not need the words of the soothsayer to believe it. I... I believed it too.'","Talk to Elfhelm in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan","'It is not always an easy thing to decide what duty compels us to do. I know of someone who might have something to add to this debate, ${PLAYER}. Look for him just to the west, if you can control your tongue and keep a confidence.'","Find the person of whom Elfhelm cryptically spoke","Gléowine is near Elfhelm's tent in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan.\
\
Horn has asked you to speak with Gléowine if you want to hear his side of the argument.","'I bid you welcome, ${PLAYER}! Have you seen Horn? My former student is a knot of confusions, and speaking with you might help him unravel them!'\
\
You tell Gléowine that you found Horn in the state he describes, but are unsure if your words provided him any comfort.\
\
'I am glad you tried. I think he is being foolish, and have told him so, but he refuses to listen to me. He thinks he is doing the right thing, but I can tell you that Nona does not agree, and I do not either. What good will it do her, and the child on its way, if Horn dies now? Little or none, ${PLAYER}. Glory and honour? They will be of little consolation and no comfort to the family he leaves behind.\
\
'I am no warrior. I record what befalls the warriors in song, and know all too well what that means. I dress it up in nice clothes, and with pretty words, but still I know it for what it is: death, and death, and death.\
\
'Horn is full of pride, like his father Ingbert, and will not be persuaded. He is a man of Rohan, for certain: stubborn and hard-headed, thinking always of duty and honour and service! May it not be the death of him!'\
\
You think that Gléowine may have been blinded to the truth of the matter by Horn's blustery words of justification, but you do not correct him."},
[2176]={"Preocupado por los tumularios que descubriste en la entrada del tesoro de Helegrod y el sello que encontraste en uno de los cuerpos, Glóin sugirió que ya es hora de hablar con el Maestro Elrond.","Elrond está en la biblioteca de Imladris.\
\
Glóin te ha pedido que hables con Elrond sobre lo que descubriste fuera del tesoro de Helegrod.","'Por favor, ve con el Maestro Elrond en Rivendel y háblale de las cosas que has visto. La hora es verdaderamente tardía si recién ahora estamos viendo la verdadera amenaza que se pudre en el norte.'","'¿Así que has regresado con noticias sombrías? Esta es la marca de un Señor de los Tumularios... ¿quizás has visto uno antes? A veces los Señores de los Tumularios usan estos sellos para invocar el espíritu maligno que anima al tumulario.\
\
'El sello que has traído es una marca de Drugoth el Negro, un poderoso Señor de los Tumularios. En cuanto a lo que atrajo al Nazgûl y a este Señor de los Tumularios a Helegrod, temo que ahora sé lo que buscan...'","'¿Sí? ¿Hay algún asunto del que deseas hablar?'","Lleva el Sello de Drugoth al Maestro Elrond","'Soy maestro de la tierra, la piedra y el hacha, ${PLAYER}, no de estos espectros viles ni artefactos oscuros. Ve con el Maestro Elrond en Rivendel y cuéntale todo lo que ha sucedido. Él podrá decirte qué debe hacerse a continuación.'","Libro 5, Capítulo 7: Noticias Malignas"},
[2177]={"Book 5, Chapter 7: Through the Stonewain Vale","'I am sick of waiting around! Let us see if we can get a look at what Théoden is doing. I will use my natural sneakiness to remain out of sight, but I cannot bear not knowing what is going on!\
\
'The King is meeting with his advisors in a clearing to the south-west. It is not far!'","Éomer is at the southern end of the Stonewain Valley.","'Ghân-buri-Ghân has proven trustworthy, ${PLAYER}. We are fortunate he came to our aid!\
\
'We may have come here just in time. Minas Tirith is not yet taken!'","The Stonewain Valley runs north and south, not far from Drû Bhûta, in Taur Drúadan.","Talk to Éomer at the southern end of Stonewain Valley","Find the clearing where Théoden meets with his advisors","Talk to Ghân-buri-Ghân while he meets with Théoden","Ghân-buri-Ghân is meeting with Théoden and his advisors in Taur Drúadan.","'I understand we have you to thank for sending to us these Woses, these Wild Men, ${PLAYER}. Their hatred of Orcs is similar to our own, and quite useful in this case, for the Orcs have made camp in the shadow of Amon Dîn and block our road.\
\
'My six thousand spears could scatter this Orc barricade, but it would take time, and that time cannot be spared. Ghân-buri-Ghân says there is fire on the plain before Minas Tirith, and within the walls. The defenders will not last if we do not come soon.\
\
'Ghân-buri-Ghân says he knows a secret way around the Orc camp. He says he can show us a forgotten road that will get us near to the city without delay. We must take this road!'","Clear fallen stones in the Stonewain Valley","The entrance to the Stonewain Valley is far south of the Rohirrim encampment, and north-east of Drû Bhûta.","As you approach, you see that Théoden speaks with Ghân-buri-Ghân","'Let us see if we can get a look at what Théoden is doing. I will use my natural sneakiness to remain out of sight, but I cannot bear not knowing what is going on!\
\
'The King is meeting with his advisors in a clearing to the south-west. It is not far!'","Talk to Théoden outside his tent in Taur Drúadan","'Horse-men pass through Stonewain Valley. Entrance is north-east of Drû Bhûta, far south of here. Way is rocky. Clear stones from path to make safe for Horse-men's passage. Then Horse-men and ${PLAYER} fight gorgûn in front of great Stone-city. Wild Men live in peace.'","Clear fallen stones near the northern entrance to Stonewain Valley","Théoden meets with his advisors in a clearing at the base of Eilenach, in Taur Drúadan.","'My uncle has spoken with the leader of these Woses, these Wild Men, and has accepted their aid. Ghân-buri-Ghân speaks of a secret way that will allow us to skirt the Orcs blocking the road beneath Amon Dîn.\
\
'He has staked his life upon it, for he will walk beside Théoden on this secret way. If he proves false, I am to kill him where he stands. If this is a trick, I will slay him without hesitation.'","There is trouble on the road ahead. If the Rohirrim are to come to Pelennor in time, they will need another plan.","You clear the path, making it safe for the horses to pass","Talk to Éomer outside Théoden's tent in Taur Drúadan","'Ghân-buri-Ghân make promise to you, ${PLAYER}. Now Ghân fulfill it. Wild Men will help Horse-men.\
\
'Stonehouse-folk once very strong. Carved stones from hills. Carried stones on large wains. Built stonehouses on side of mountain. Road still there, but Stonehouse-folk forget. Wild Men not forget.\
\
'Horse-men pass through Stonewain Valley. Entrance is north-east of Drû Bhûta, far south of here. Way is rocky. Clear stones from path to make safe for Horse-men's passage. Then Horse-men and ${PLAYER} fight gorgûn in front of great Stone-city. Wild Men live in peace.'"},
[2178]={"Libro 5, Capítulo 8: Fuego y Hielo","Elrond te dijo que después de que el rey enano Durin derrotara al dragón Thorog, el cuerpo del dragón fue dejado a pudrirse en la tesorería vacía de Helegrod. Teme que el hielo y el frío de Orod Lostol hayan preservado el cuerpo hasta tal punto que las artes del Señor Demacrado, Drugoth, podrían infundirle un espíritu maligno y levantarlo como un tumulario.","'Me pregunto qué nuevo mal se está gestando en Angmar, y por qué elige manifestarse ahora.'","'Has sido de gran ayuda para nosotros, ${PLAYER}.'","Helegrod se encuentra al norte de Rivendel y del campamento de Glóin.\
\
Elrond te ha pedido que entres en la tesorería de Helegrod y pongas fin a los planes del Nazgûl. Te advirtió que reunieras aliados.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'Lo que el Nazgûl busca se ha vuelto evidente para mí, ${PLAYER}. Glóin te habló de la caída de Helegrod, ¿verdad? Durin, el quinto en llevar ese nombre, abatió al dragón Thorog pero murió en la batalla junto con la mayoría de su compañía. Cuando se hizo evidente que Helegrod era un lugar de maldad y que sus intentos por restaurarlo eran inútiles, los enanos retiraron las riquezas de la tesorería y dejaron el cuerpo del dragón a pudrirse.\
\
'Sin embargo, temo que el frío y el hielo de Orod Lostol hayan preservado el cuerpo del dragón mucho más de lo que cualquiera habría imaginado. Incluso después de la muerte y el paso de tantos años, el cuerpo de Thorog aún poseería gran poder. Temo que Drugoth, el Señor Demacrado, pueda usar sus artes para colocar algún espíritu dentro de ese cadáver, levantando al más terrible de los tumularios al servicio de Angmar.\
\
'Un dragón reanimado al alcance de Imladris es una amenaza demasiado grave para ser ignorada. Debo pedirte que entres en la tesorería de Helegrod y pongas fin a los planes de Drugoth y del Nazgûl. Será una tarea difícil, así que reúne un grupo de poderosos guerreros y ve.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está diseñada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'¡Has hecho algo grandioso hoy, ${PLAYER}! Pocos han enfrentado el poder de un Nazgûl y vivido para contarlo. Por fortuna, las aguas del Bruinen y tu persecución lo debilitaron lo suficiente como para que pudieras derrotarlo y enviarlo de regreso a Mordor.\
\
'En cuanto al asunto del dragón, parece que, aunque el ritual fue parcialmente exitoso, la criatura reanimada no está completamente bajo el control de Drugoth. Sigue representando una amenaza para Rivendel, aunque no tan grande como habría sido si el ritual se hubiera completado.\
\
'Por ahora, podemos volver nuestra atención a otros asuntos, aunque algún día quizás desees regresar a Helegrod y acabar con esta amenaza por completo.'","Entra en la tesoro de Helegrod y pon fin a los planes del Nazgûl.","Elrond se encuentra en la biblioteca de Imladris.\
\
En la tesorería, te encontraste con el Nazgûl y lograste derrotarlo. También interrumpiste el ritual que el Señor Demacrado estaba realizando para restaurar al dragón Thorog, aunque parte del proceso se completó y el dragón voló. Elrond debe ser informado de lo ocurrido.","'Nuestro tiempo puede ser breve. Por favor, apúrate y reúne un grupo de guerreros para entrar en la tesorería de Helegrod. Allí yace el cuerpo del dragón, abatido por Durin hace tantos años, dejado a pudrirse.'"},
[2179]={"'This day will live long in the hearts of my people! This is a day for deeds of honour and glory, ${PLAYER}!'","'Let us ride to the encircling wall together, ${PLAYER}!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Éomer from horseback and join Théoden's Riders","Talk to Théoden on the Field of Onslaught","Théoden's Riders have taken the field!","Éomer is at the southern end of the Stonewain Valley, and he prepares to ride out of the vale and toward the Pelennor's encircling wall.","Book 5, Chapter 8: The Ride of the Rohirrim","'Ready your steed, my friend! The time has come for riding with haste!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Mount your travelling steed and speak to Éomer to join the Rohirrim for the final leg of their journey.</rgb>","The Rohirrim have passed through the Stonewain Valley, and now they prepare for battle."},
[2180]={"Defeat turtles in the Rushgore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated turtles in the Rushgore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${PLAYER}! What a terrible marvel this is!'","The corpse of an enormous beast lies broken on the ground here","'I saw a great shadowy shape fall from the sky not long ago. You can come with me to investigate it, if you wish, but first I need to ensure the safety of the Rushgore. Something has stirred up the creatures of this swampy land, and it is my duty to keep them from becoming a serious threat.\
\
'I am not as young as I once was, but my arms are still strong and can still swing a sword. I may not sit the saddle as I used to, but my legs are stronger than many a young man's. Together we will travel in search of the falling shadow, and see what there is to see.\
\
'But first we must thin back the newly-aggressive creatures of the Rushgore. If you help me in this, we will be sooner underway. Defeat gredbyg, turtles, and avanc throughout the Rushgore, and then return to me. Then we will search for the place where this falling shadow came to ground.'","Defeated avanc in the Rushgore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Edbrit is at Aculf's Camp in the Rushgore.\
\
You have helped deal with some of the newly-aggressive creatures in the Rushgore, and should return now to Edbrit.","'We are fortunate this terrible creature is dead. But where is its rider?'","'We will search the Brown Lands for the falling shadow. I think it fell across the river, far to the south-east.\
\
'I do not know what it could have been, ${PLAYER}. I have seen many strange things in my time, but... something about this shadow filled me with dread.'\
\
Edbrit falls silent, his face suddenly pensive.\
\
'I do not know what we will find, ${PLAYER}, but I fear it will prove a danger to my people and these lands.'","'See what I have found, ${PLAYER}! Something is wrong in this land. I can feel it. This must be why we are here. This is the reason for your dream! Remember the words of Suvulch my father: dreams have power. We ignore their warnings at our peril.\
\
'This beast is dead, but something rode it, and that creature is not here. Your dream brought us here to keep that creature from doing great evil, ${PLAYER}. I feel it in my very bones.'","Edbrit saw a mysterious shadow fall from the sky far to the south-east, in the Brown Lands.\
\
You have decided to travel to the Brown Lands in search of the mysterious shadow Edbrit saw.","Defeated gredbyg in the Rushgore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The reek of this creature overpowers the senses!'","Edbrit saw something fall from the sky, but before he goes with you to investigate it he needs your help in the Rushgore.","'Something has stirred up the creatures of the Rushgore. Deal with the gredbyg, turtles, and avanc that have become aggressive, and return to me. We will then go in search of the falling shadow I beheld.\
\
'When I was young, I rode far afield among the waving grasses of Rohan. Few could match me for wanderlust, and I saw many wondrous sights. Few men could claim to see as many.\
\
'Now that I am grown old, I find I am more interested in the people that walk these lands than in the places I meet them. Each of their stories is singular and unique, and it is for these people I accepted this work. We must keep the Rushgore safe for their benefit.'","Defeat avanc in the Rushgore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Nona is standing by the corpse of the fallen beast in the Brown Lands.\
\
Nona is waiting to speak with you.","'This must be the shape my men and I beheld as it plummeted from the sky. What a terrible creature!'\
\
Edbrit shivers, and his eyes go wide as he turns away from the dead beast.\
\
'Is that... riding gear? Did someone ride astride this terrible creature? And if so... where is the rider?'","'Good, I thank you for your hard work against the unusually aggressive creatures of the Rushgore. I would not have wanted to leave my post with those threats unmet, but now I feel we have earned a time of peace. Enough time for us to seek the falling shadow, at any rate. I will need to return before long.\
\
'While we walk, perhaps you can tell me of your adventures? Why do you smile? I can tell by your face that you have seen more adventure in recent days than even Edbrit, in all his years, can claim to have experienced. I would be pleased to hear anything you would tell me about yourself.\
\
'I will go with you into the Brown Lands to search for the falling shadow. Let us look for it far to the south-east. I believe that is where it came to ground.'","Defeat gredbyg in the Rushgore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Look at this! What is this beast?'","Book 6, Chapter 10: The Falling Shadow","Find the location in the Brown Lands where the falling shadow came to earth","Edbrit has asked you to defeat gredbyg, turtles, and avanc that have been stirred up in the Rushgore.\
\
Something has caused the creatures of the Rushgore to become more hostile than usual, and Edbrit wants you to help him deal with them before the two of you go in search of the falling shadow.","Edbrit is standing by the corpse of a mighty beast in the Brown Lands.\
\
You have found the body of a massive beast, and should speak to Edbrit about it."},
[2181]={"Complete the deed 'The Vanished Rider' to learn the location of the missing Nazgûl","Someone rode astride the beast that now lies dead in the Brown Lands. But where is this vanished rider?","The great beast that crashed in the Brown Lands is missing its rider, but people throughout the lands bordering the Great River may have seen signs of it. You should seek them out and learn where the rider has gone.","'We have learned much of this creature, but not what we need to know. Where has its rider gone, and what cruel fate has kept us a step behind it at every turn?'","Book 6, Chapter 11: The Vanished Rider","You have scoured the lands near the Great River for some sign of the missing Nazgûl, but have always been half a step behind. You should meet with Nona back by the corpse of the crashed beast as you agreed.","'The creature that rode upon this beast is missing. We must find it. Seek through the lands next to the Great River to find people who may have seen sign of its passage!'","'This is the reason for your dream! This is why we are here! I have never seen a creature as terrible as this, lest it be the mighty worm my brother slew beneath Zudrugund.'\
\
As you stare at the corpse of the massive beast and contemplate the mangled harness and its missing rider, a single word echoes in your mind: Nazgûl. Nona watches you closely.\
\
'Do you know something about the rider of this beast, ${PLAYER}? Your face tells me it must be a creature of terrible power. We must find it! We must search for it throughout this land! Look for signs of its passage among the lands of the Great River! After we have scoured these lands, we will meet back here at this creature, ${PLAYER}. Let this purpose guide our steps!'"},
[2182]={"Talk to Galadriel outside the House of Celeborn","Book 6, Chapter 12: Mists of Anduin","You have followed signs left by the rider of the terrible beast that met its end in the Brown Lands, but have not been able to find the rider itself.","Talk to Nona by the Carcass of the Beast and walk with her back to Stangard","Nona is standing by the carcass of the beast in the Brown Lands.\
\
Your search for the missing Nazgûl has proven fruitless, and Nona wants to walk with you back to Stangard where you can find more information.","Galadriel is atop the flet on which is built the House of Celeborn, in Lothlórien.\
\
The night was long, but Galadriel has once again summoned you to speak with her.","'Let us talk on the way back to the village of the horse-lords.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'You have journeyed far, and have come very close to death and sadness. And yet, still you skirt the gravest danger and come safely through the other side. I hope that our mutual friends fare as well.\
\
'I told you earlier I had nothing to do with your dream, and this was true. But when you described your visions to me, I did not tell you everything I suspected. It seemed clear to me that your paths must cross one of the Nine. I believed the girl would die.\
\
'And yet, unbelieveably, she did not. Either through your own actions, or hers, you both escaped the clutches of the Nazgûl. And either through curious good fortune or powers unknown to me, our mutual friends seem to have outdistanced its pursuit.\
\
'But there is no rest for we who worry for their safety. The Nazgûl is not the last danger they will face. They, and you, are not free of evil's clutch just yet. Rest for a time, but not for long.\
\
'There are plans to be made, ${PLAYER}. We will speak again, and soon.'","'This rider... what was the word you used? Nazgûl? The creature was looking for something. We need to think. It brought us on a chase through these lands, but I cannot tell what it sought, or if it found what it desired.\
\
'We have no choice but to return to the village of the horse-lords. I will wait outside while you speak with that man Horn. We are strangers in this land. He is not. He may know of a place we have not yet searched.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>"},
[2183]={"Defeat Orcs on the Pelennor during the battle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The battle goes well for us, for our cause is just and our leaders strong! The Morgul-host is near to a rout!'\
\
Gimilkhôr nods in Fastred's direction.\
\
'I have spoken only a few words to this man Fastred, but he strikes me as a man whose blood runs hot. If he finds this villain he seeks, this Crúmgam, I would not wager on the side of restraint! So it should be for all our foes, and so it will!'","'We do not fight alone! I saw riders from within the city pass through the breach in the gate and come onto the field, and behind them marched footmen of Gondor. These riders bear the mark of the swan; the press of battle has brought them close to our position.\
\
'Find their leader and tell him that Rohan has come to spill the blood of his foes!'","Déorwine and Sakalbâr are fighting on the south-eastern stretch of the line on the Field of Onslaught.","Find an Orc that has broken free of the fighting ranks and defeat it","Defeat your foes on the Pelennor during the battle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Fastred near the fighting ranks to the south-east on the Field of Onslaught","You see no sign of Crúmgam, but the dismounted Rohirrim need your help","'I saw riders from within the city pass through the breach in the gate and come onto the field, and behind them marched footmen of Gondor. These riders bear the mark of the swan; the press of battle has brought them close to our position.\
\
'Find their leader and tell him that Rohan has come to spill the blood of his foes!'","Gondorian soldiers and Rohirrim riders do battle with the Orcs on the Field of Onslaught. You should slay any of the Orcs that break free of the fighting ranks.","'The Orcs fight with malice in their eyes and with blood on their teeth, but the fighting men of Gondor and Rohan will repel them!\
\
'For Imrahil! For Théoden!'","Fastred has asked you to search the battlefield for his hated foe Crúmgam.","'You have done well! Some of the riderless horses have found masters once again. This is the hour of our victory, and none can stand against us!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>If you have a Small Fellowship, now is the time to challenge 'The Blood of the Black Serpent' from the World Join panel.</rgb>","Defeated foes on the Pelennor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Fastred and Gimilkhôr are near the south-eastern stretch of the line on the Field of Onslaught.","Talk to Gimilkhôr near the fighting ranks to the south-east on the Field of Onslaught","Talk to Prince Imrahil on the Field of Onslaught","The Orc falls, but you know that there will be more","Talk to Déorwine at the fighting ranks to the south-east, on the Field of Onslaught","Prince Imrahil has led his swan-knights out of the city, and can be found on the Field of Onslaught.\
\
Théoden marked the emergence of the swan-knights from the city, and wants you to find Prince Imrahil.","'Quail not, my friend! Those I fight alongside buoy my spirits, and I theirs! There is little time for easy conversation, but men brought together during the fighting may share a word or two with the fellow at their shoulder. I have learned some of their reasons for fighting, and they have learned mine.\
\
'I fight for Winsig, the love of my life and thane of Walstow! With every stroke of my sword I further secure her safety, and that of her people!'","'Where is Crúmgam? He must be here, for I have vengeance to deal upon him!\
\
'Déorwine fights to protect Thane Winsig of Walstow? Were he able to ask her, she would say that Crúmgam must be slain, for she was present when that villain came to Snowbourn and threatened my family! While he lives, no one in Rohan is safe from his malice!\
\
'Find Crúmgam! Find him and end him, ${PLAYER}! That is the only thing that matters to me!'","Defeated Orcs on the Pelennor during the battle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Search for Crúmgam on the eastern side of the Field of Onslaught","Book 6, Chapter 1: Bonded By Battle","Théoden is waiting with his banner-bearer, Guthláf, on the Field of Onslaught.","Your words prove fruitful, and he runs in search of another steed","'We are well-met on the field, ${PLAYER}! To arrive with Théoden and his Riders thus, at this very moment, is beyond all of our hopes! Let our enemies fly before us! Slay any that emerge from the fighting ranks, my valiant friend!\
\
'For Gondor and Rohan!'","Encourage dismounted Rohirrim to fight (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Théoden on the Field of Onslaught","Rohirrim that have been dismounted from their steeds need your help on the eastern side of the Field of Onslaught.","Théoden has led the charge of the Rohirrim into battle before the White City.","Talk to Sakalbâr at the fighting ranks on the south-east side of the Field of Onslaught"},
[2184]={"Libro 6, Capítulo 1: Tiempos desesperados","'¡Una petición singular! Me parece muy ${PLAYERNAME:atrevido[m]|atrevida[f]} que busques una audiencia con la Dama Galadriel, ${PLAYERNAME:extranjero[m]|extranjera[f]}. No te dejaré pasar, por Haldir de Lórien.'","Habla con Haldir en un flet al sureste del río Nimrodel","'Esta vez hemos derrotado a los Orcos, pero son demasiado numerosos. Sin la ayuda de los Elfos de Lórien, seremos superados.\
\
'Espero que la Dama Galadriel nos ayude. Busca a los guardianes de Lothlórien en las plataformas entre los árboles al sureste del río Nimrodel.'","'¡Hemos resistido los ataques iniciales de los Orcos! ¿pero cuánto tiempo durará nuestra buena suerte? No lo suficiente, me temo; los Orcos son simplemente demasiado numerosos, y con el apoyo de Dol Guldur, Mazog seguramente puede librar su guerra el tiempo suficiente para derribar nuestras defensas.\
\
'Debemos buscar ayuda por nuestra cuenta. Aunque la amistad de los enanos con los Elfos del Bosque de Oro ha sufrido tensiones a lo largo de los años, nunca ha sido realmente abandonada, espero. Necesitamos su ayuda ahora más que nunca, o estamos perdidos.\
\
'Debes buscar la ayuda de la Dama Galadriel. Nosotros los enanos sabemos poco de ella, pero se dice que posee un gran poder. Algunos dicen que es pérfida y peligrosa, otros que es amable. En este momento tan difícil arriesgaría una audiencia con ella, aunque tengo miedo. Habla con uno de los guardianes en los límites de Lothlórien y pide hablar con la Dama del Bosque, ${PLAYER}. ¿Quién mejor que tú? Tienes la amistad de los Elfos y enanos a la vez. Entiendo que puede haber grandes plataformas entre los árboles al otro lado del río llamado Nimrodel, al sureste del Valle del Arroyo Sombrío. Puedes encontrar guardianes de Lothlórien sobre ellas.'","Has ayudado a los enanos a repeler los primeros ataques de los Orcos, pero Bosi no cree que su pueblo pueda resistir para siempre sin la ayuda de los Elfos de Lórien.","Hay guardianes en los límites de Lórien, al este de Moria. Tales Elfos se encuentran en grandes plataformas, o flets, entre los árboles al sureste del río Nimrodel.\
\
Bosi cree que los enanos no podrán repeler a los Orcos de Mazog por mucho tiempo si realmente cuentan con el apoyo de alguna fuerza de Dol Guldur, y quiere que busques una audiencia con Galadriel de Lórien. Los enanos necesitan aliados si quieren resistir en Khazad-dûm."},
[2185]={"'¡${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]}, ! ¿No vino contigo Aragorn? Vaya, eso es mala noticia. Bueno, no hay remedio ahora. Tendrás que hacerlo tú.\
\
'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]} para un largo y oscuro viaje? Es a través de Ram Dúath hacia Angmar que debo enviarte.'","Libro 6, Capítulo 1: De Golodir y Angmar","'¿Por qué tardas aquí? Ve a Esteldín en las Quebradas del Norte y consulta con mi pariente Daervunn.'","Esteldín se encuentra en las Quebradas del Norte, al norte y al oeste de Rivendel.\
\
Aragorn te ha pedido viajar a Esteldín en su lugar para hablar con Daervunn, de quien espera pueda esclarecer el preocupante mensaje.","Un halcón adiestrado llegó a Rivendel, portando un mensaje inquietante desde el campamento oculto de los Montaraces en Esteldín para Aragorn, Capitán de los Montaraces.","'Saludo y bienvenido, ${PLAYER}. Es bueno que hayas llegado. Esta mañana, un halcón llegó portando un mensaje para mí desde Esteldín, el refugio oculto de mi pueblo en las Quebradas del Norte. Al parecer, otro de estos pájaros llegó a Esteldín desde el Norte, gravemente herido, llevando un mensaje de uno de mis parientes que creíamos muerto desde hacía mucho tiempo.\
\
'Sé poco más, pues el mensaje que me fue enviado fue breve, pero Daervunn me ha pedido que acuda de inmediato. Mi tiempo aquí es corto, y no puedo regresar ahora para consultar con mi gente. Mi camino se encuentra hacia el sur y el este. ¿Irás tú a Esteldín en mi lugar y descubrirás qué noticias han llegado allí? Habla con Daervunn, pues él fue quien me envió el mensaje.\
\
'Temo que la noticia sea grave, pues Corunir fue dado por perdido hace años cuando su capitán, Golodir, desobedeció mi decreto y llevó una compañía hacia el norte, a Angmar. Nunca se supo de ellos de nuevo. Es una alegría que Corunir viva, pero ¿qué le impidió contactarnos hasta ahora?'"},
[2186]={"Find a bedroll in Grimbold's camp and get some rest","A bedroll you can use is located south of Grimbold's position in his camp, by the milestone.\
\
Grimbold wants you to get some rest while you can.","Grimbold is in his camp, north of your bedroll.\
\
You have had a most peculiar dream, if dream it was, and you should tell Grimbold of it.","Book 6, Chapter 1: Troubled Dreams","'We should all get some rest, ${PLAYER}. We will be the better for it.\
\
'Find a bedroll south of here in the camp, by the milestone, and get what rest you can. I think you have need of it, as do we all.'","Your body is exhausted and your mind is ill at ease following the Battle of the Ford.","Talk to Grimbold in his camp and tell him about the strange dream","'It has been a long day, ${PLAYER}, and we all could use a rest. We have held the Ford, but have lost Prince Théodred, and that weighs heavily upon my mind. I fear the doom of Rohan is near. My men are tired, weary in body and mind, and we cannot stop it.\
\
'Go south of here, to the milestone located in this camp. You will find a bedroll you can use there. Take your rest while you can. You may not have another opportunity for a while, and we will need you to be ready.'","'What? You had a bad dream? Such things are to be expected after a battle.'\
\
Grimbold's expression becomes darker and more concerned as you tell him what you remember of the troubling dream.\
\
'Ah, this is not merely a bad dream, ${PLAYER}. This is Elf-magic of the worst sort. You have dallied with strange peoples and mysterious forces, and are now caught in their net! If you were not so valuable in a fight, I would command you to leave and never return! You could not leave my sight quickly enough!'","The bedroll is uncomfortable, and you can feel every jutting stone of the hard ground through it. Even so, you are so exhausted by the events of the day that you fall into a troubled sleep.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>"},
[2187]={"Libro 6, Capítulo 2: Contra su señor","'No puedo darte mejor consejo que buscar Aughaire. Pero salvo por la compañía de Golodir, mis parientes no han pasado al norte más allá de Ram Dúath.'","'Quizás debería empezar por el principio. Hace muchos años, uno de nuestros capitanes, un hombre llamado Golodir, deseaba entrar en el reino de Angmar, pues había oído rumores de que los descendientes de los antiguos Montañeses de Rhudaur se habían asentado allí y comenzaban a multiplicarse de nuevo. También sospechaba que una sombra había vuelto a caer sobre Carn Dûm, ya que criaturas malignas empezaban a extenderse hacia el sur, hasta las Tierras Altas del Norte.\
\
'Aragorn prohibió a cualquiera ir allí, pues esa tierra aún tenía mala fama, aunque ha estado desierta durante cientos de años. Sin embargo, Golodir reunió a quienes quisieran acompañarlo y desapareció de nuestra memoria... hasta hace unas semanas. Un halcón herido llegó, portando un mensaje de Corunir, uno de los compañeros de Golodir, diciendo que vive en un lugar llamado Aughaire, un pueblo de Montañeses al norte de Ram Dúath.\
\
'¿Irás allí y hablarás con Corunir? La urgencia de su mensaje me hace temer lo que ha sucedido. Creo que aún no hemos visto los tiempos más oscuros.'","Corunir está en Aughaire, un pueblo de Montañeses en Angmar, en algún lugar al norte de Ram Dúath.\
\
Daervunn te pidió que cruzaras al norte por Ram Dúath y buscaras al Montaraz Corunir, que ahora vive entre los Montañeses de Angmar.","'¿Quién eres? No importa... lo que importa es que has venido. La situación es grave y necesitamos toda la ayuda que podamos reunir. Estas buenas personas están acosadas por los tiranos de Angmar, que ahora reúnen un poderoso ejército para marchar al sur y aplastar a los Elfos y Gondor entre su martillo y el yunque de Mordor. El tiempo apremia y debemos actuar rápido si queremos frenar la Sombra de Angmar.\
\
'Quizás debería contarte algo de nuestra larga historia. Cuando llegamos por primera vez a Aughaire, los Montañeses eran desconfiados con nosotros, pero no abiertamente hostiles. Golodir se ganó rápidamente su respeto, pues era un gran capitán entre nosotros y sabía inspirar el ánimo. Supimos que los Montañeses estaban bajo la opresión de un remanente de Angmar que había regresado a Carn Dûm desde las Montañas Nubladas... pero peor aún, un hechicero muy parecido al Rey Brujo de antaño también había llegado a la ciudad maligna.\
\
'Los Montañeses llamaban a este hechicero \\qEl Falso Rey\\q, pues sabían bien que el propio Rey Brujo nunca podría regresar a Angmar. Golodir decidió que este Senescal de Angmar debía ser detenido antes de que pudiera reunir fuerzas en el Norte. Reunió a tantos Montañeses como quisieron seguirlo y viajó al este con el resto de nuestros compañeros, creyendo que Angmar aún no era lo suficientemente fuerte para resistir un frente unido. Yo me quedé atrás para llevar la noticia a Esteldín en caso de que la expedición fracasara... lo cual ocurrió. ¿Quieres saber más?'","Daervunn te contó cómo llegó un halcón herido, portando un mensaje de Corunir, un Montaraz de la compañía de Golodir, que desafió las órdenes de Aragorn y entró en Angmar, creyendo que una sombra había vuelto a caer sobre Carn Dûm."},
[2188]={"Talk to Guthláf and bolster his courage","'For Rohan and for Théoden!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Guthláf and charge with him into battle once again","Gléowine is at Kings' End, near the corpse of the fell-beast.","'You have the right of it, ${PLAYER}. Let our foes flee in terror from the might of Théoden, and of Rohan! It is with the pride of my father and his father's father that I carry the banner of my lord into battle!\
\
'Are you ready for another charge into the ranks?'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Mount your travelling steed and speak to Guthláf to follow him once again into battle.</rgb>","'This is a terrible day for Rohan, ${PLAYER}. The deeds of Théoden were mighty, even on his last day of life, but the kingdom will feel this loss keenly. And to lose the Lady Éowyn in such a fashion! My mind reels at the horror of it, and does not wish to think of the road that brought her to this place. Did none know she joined the ranks? Did no one speak against it?\
\
'It is too much to bear. My heart follows her brother on his reckless charge into the ranks of the enemy; may he rise from this death-madness before he does himself some harm! He must be King now. Rohan cannot lose him too!'","Guthláf is on the Field of Onslaught, readying to follow his lord once more into the fray.","Talk to Gléowine at Kings' End","The shadow of death falls upon the Pelennor, and none are safe from its chill grasp.","Book 6, Chapter 2: Death Comes for All","'Guthláf, raise thy banner skyward, and show the forces arrayed against us that Rohan will not falter!\
\
'Keep close to my banner-bearer, ${PLAYER}. There will be glory enough for all, if we stand with courageous hearts against the darkness!\
\
'Forth Eorlingas!'","Guthláf is near Théoden, his liege, on the Field of Onslaught.\
\
Théoden has asked you to stay near to his banner-bearer Guthláf and bolster his courage.","'Keep close to my banner-bearer, ${PLAYER}. There will be glory enough for all, if we stand with courageous hearts against the darkness!'"},
[2189]={"'This is a puzzle: a Dunlending man slain by a sword, among Wargs, with a fist full of gold pieces.\
\
'Who killed him? And why did his foe not take the gold from him? You think it was this girl you seek?\
\
'You should investigate the other golden glint you espied from the warrens, ${PLAYER}. It was to the west, was it not, where two trails meet?'","You have spied another glint of gold to the west of the small pile of gold you discovered.\
\
Someone has been leaving small piles of gold pieces in the Gap of Rohan. Is it Nona?","This member of the Draig-lûth was slain by a sword-stroke. Pieces of gold trail from his clenched fingers, and you pick them up and look at them curiously.\
\
As you straighten up, you see another glint of gold from the west, where two trails meet.","'I heard the clash of swords from the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr. I do not know if it be a sign of this girl Nona, but it is a place to begin your search. Âthdâr is to the west, among the cliffs. Slay some Wargs while you search, ${PLAYER}!'","'You found a pile of gold pieces? That is a strange thing to find in the wilderness! You need to follow the trail, ${PLAYER}! It has led you west, has it not?'","'You found the Dunlending girl? I hope you know what you are doing, ${PLAYER}. Where did you say she was? West of Cuvnerth in the Gap of Rohan?'","'I did not expect to see you again, friend! I am pleased you still live! You must have heard rumour of me... I have truly become Wadu's Ghost, and the Gap of Rohan is my haunt!\
\
'I have made use of the bribing gold we recovered in Carreglyn, ${PLAYER}. I find warriors who have sworn allegiance to Saruman, and I leave piles of coins for them to discover. When they pick them up, I fall upon them and claim my vengeance!\
\
'I have thinned the outliers of the army that gathers in Wulf's Cleft, but it is not yet enough to pay for the death of my brother. Wadu's Ghost still hungers for the blood of those who serve Saruman and kill in the name of the traitor-Wizard, and she will have her fill!'","You see another glint of gold from the west, where two trails meet","Wilfrith is in Forthbrond, to the west of Grimbold's Camp.\
\
Grimbold thinks you should travel to Forthbrond and speak with Wilfrith for information about tracking down Wadu's Ghost in the Gap of Rohan.","Defeat Wargs at Âthdâr (3/4)","You look at the slain Draig-lûth warrior and wonder if he was lured to this place by a pile of gold coins like the one you discovered to the west.\
\
You caught a glimpse of another gold glint further to the west of that pile, and wonder if you should investigate it.","'Do you not have gold pieces for me? You picked them up, did you not?'","You have spied another glint of gold to the west of Âthdâr, where two trails meet.\
\
A member of the Draig-lûth killed by a sword-stroke clutched gold pieces in his hand. What does it mean?","Defeated Wargs at Âthdâr (${NUMBER}/4)","You caught a glimpse of gold from the western side of the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr.\
\
You should investigate the golden glimpse you saw at Âthdâr.","Investigate the glint of gold to the west of Âthdâr","'You saw something peculiar on the western side of the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr? You should see what it was!\
\
'Âthdâr is to the west of here, among the cliffs.'","'I do not pay much heed to things of this nature, ${PLAYER}. I am a man of Rohan! I walk on the soil and ride on the backs of earthly steeds!\
\
'These dreams of yours... they are something otherworldly. It seems to me that this girl you spoke of, this Nona, may be the 'ghost' in your dream. If she is hunting Dunlendings in the pay of Saruman, she is surely somewhere in the Gap of Rohan.\
\
'Travel west, to the camp of Forthbrond, and speak to Wilfrith. He may have seen some sign of this girl.'","Your suspicion was correct, and Nona stands before you!","Wilfrith heard the sound of swords clashing from the direction of the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr, west of Forthbrond. He wants you to defeat Wargs there while you search for Nona.\
\
Wilfrith thinks you might be able to learn news of Nona by travelling to the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr.","As you examine the pile of gold pieces, you see another glint further to the south-west","'Ah, I did not expect to see you again, my friend! But it is a happy meeting!'","Investigate the glint of gold to the south-west","Investigate the glint of gold even further to the west","This member of the Draig-lûth was slain by a sword-stroke. Why did his foe not take the gold clutched in his fingers?\
\
Once again you see another glint of gold from the west, where two trails meet, and wonder if another Draig-lûth warrior lies slain there.","As you defeat another Warg, a glint of gold to the west of the warren catches your eye","Talk to Nona west of Cuvnerth, in the Gap of Rohan","'I will not force you to leave, my friend. You have been too valuable an ally! But heed this warning! Elf-magic or not, this dream of yours is an omen of dangerous times ahead. It must steer your steps, but whether it steers them to good or ill I cannot say. This I know, however: it is not your fate to stand with us again. Can you understand any of what you saw within the fog of sleep?'\
\
You tell Grimbold that you do know of someone to whom the dream seemed to refer: the girl Nona, who called herself 'Wadu's Ghost' for a time and swore vengeance on Dunlendings in the pay of Saruman.\
\
'You must begin by finding this girl, then. If she sought to slay Dunlendings, she is certain to be somewhere within the Gap of Rohan; they gather in Wulf's Cleft, and the Gap teems with them. Go to Wilfrith in Forthbrond, to the west, and see if he has seen any sign of this girl.'","As you examine the pile of gold pieces, you see another glint further to the west","'You found another pile of gold pieces? That is a strange thing to find in the wilderness! Keep following the trail, ${PLAYER}! It has led you west, has it not? You say you plan to search west of Cuvnerth for more clues?'","Defeat Wargs at Âthdâr (${NUMBER}/4)","If the dream that troubled your sleep is as it seems, Grimbold is right: you need to take it seriously and act upon its mysterious message.","You have found Nona in the Gap of Rohan, west of Cuvnerth.\
\
You should tell Nona about the troubling dream.","You have spotted another glint of gold to the south-west of the gold coins you discovered, to the west of Cuvnerth.\
\
You are following a trail of gold pieces through the Gap of Rohan. Does this trail near its end?","'Some of my men fought at the Ford alongside you, ${PLAYER}. They spoke highly of your deeds.'\
\
Wilfrith listens as you describe Nona and her determination to slay Dunlendings in the service of Saruman.\
\
'One Dunlending seems much the same as any other to me, ${PLAYER}, but I have not seen any of them fighting amongst themselves.\
\
'There was one thing, though... not two hours ago I heard the clash of sword on sword coming from the Warg-warrens of Âthdâr, to the west. Perhaps your Dunlending ally was stirring up trouble from the heights? While you are up there, you should slay some Wargs yourself!'","Investigate the flash of gold on the western side of Âthdâr","Book 6, Chapter 2: The Ghost in the Gap"},
[2190]={"Nona is at the front gate of the village of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith.\
\
Nona is waiting to speak with you in front of the gate of Lhanuch.","Talk to Nona at the front gate of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith","Meet Nona at the front gate of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith","Book 6, Chapter 3: Daughter of Suvulch","'I will go with you, but meet me first at the front gate of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith. I want to bid farewell to my father Suvulch before we make such a long journey.'","'I cannot find my father anywhere in the village, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Before Wadu was slain, Suvulch used to go to the Pool of the King to listen to the water and think. Perhaps he is there now.\
\
'Let us look for him there! The Pool of the King is north-west of the village.'","Nona thinks Suvulch may be at the Pool of the King, north-west of Lhanuch.\
\
Nona could not find her father anywhere within Lhanuch, and thinks he might be at the Pool of the King.","'You would do well not to ignore the warnings of such dreams. All know this.'","Sift through pottery shards along the edges of the Pool of the King","'I was right! My father is here. I have already told him of the journey we must begin.'","'I do not know what awaits us in the land of the Elf-queen.'","Suvulch is on the shore by the Pool of the King, in Enedwaith, north-west of the village of Lhanuch.\
\
You have found a shining beryl on the shore of the Pool of the King, and should bring it to Suvulch.","The front gate of Lhanuch is in Nan Laeglin, in Enedwaith, north of Dunland.\
\
Nona has agreed to come with you to Lothlórien seeking the meaning behind your dream, but first she wants to stop by the front gate of her home of Lhanuch to bid farewell to her father Suvulch.","Sifting through the shards, you find a small beryl that shines with its own light","Pottery shards can be found along the edges of the Pool of the King.\
\
Suvulch wants you to sift through the pottery shards for something he can give to Nona as a memento.","'I have said I will go with you, but first let us travel to Lhanuch. I want to bid farewell to my father Suvulch before we make such a long journey.'","Bring the shining beryl to Suvulch","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","Nona searched the village but found no sign of her father","You sift through the small pile of shards, but find nothing of note","'You did not seek me out to join me in my vengeance? Why then did you search for me?'\
\
Nona listens attentively to your account of your troubling dream. When you have finished, she nods sagely.\
\
'Dreams of this sort have meaning, ${PLAYER}. My people know this well. Great harm has befallen those who ignore the warnings of dreams such as this! I will go with you to see this Elf-queen.\
\
'Let us return first to my home of Lhanuch! I must bid farewell to my father Suvulch before we begin such a journey. I want to make certain he is well before I go with you to this wood of gold. I will meet you by the front gate of Lhanuch, in Enedwaith!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Lhanuch in Enedwaith when you accept this quest.</rgb>","Find and talk to Suvulch at the Pool of the King, if he is there","'Before Wadu was slain, Suvulch used to go to the Pool of the King to listen to the water and think. Perhaps he is there now.'\
\
'Let us look for him there! The Pool of the King is north-west of the village.'","'Did you find something? Ah! You did!'\
\
Suvulch takes the beryl from you, and holds it up to the light.\
\
'I do not know how long this rested on the bottom of the pool, ${PLAYER}, or what caused it to drift to the bank and catch on the stones. But it did, and in that it is like my Nona, and like you! You are moved by forces a simple man like Suvulch does not understand, and he does not presume to know where you will be on the morrow!'\
\
Suvulch laughs again.\
\
'The stone is pretty. Nona, my daughter! Wear it in distant lands, and look on it and think of Suvulch. Wield that sword of the horse-lords, and think of your brother Wadu! You will be far away, but you will be near too, close by in heart and close by in thought. Ah, Suvulch's way is the way of battle, not the way of words. He has said enough.'","'I have looked throughout the entire village, but there is no sign of my father. Where is Suvulch?'","You have found Nona in the Gap of Rohan and she has agreed to come with you to Lothlórien in pursuit of the truth of your troubled dream.","'What did you find?'","'Nona has told me what you plan to do, and why. I will not keep you from this journey, ${PLAYER} the ${RACE}. Dreams have power. All the Algraig know this. We ignore their warnings at our peril.\
\
'I wish to speak further with my daughter. Search through the pottery fragments that surround this pool for something she can bring with her on this journey to remind her of Suvulch.\
\
'Sometimes things of value catch on the sides of the pool. Old things, shiny things, pretty things. Busy yourself with this task while I speak with my daughter.'"},
[2191]={"'¿Trajiste el calco que te pedí?'","Corunir está en el pueblo de Montañeses de Aughaire.\
\
Con los calcos que Corunir pidió en mano, deberías regresar con el Montaraz y entregarle tu informe.","Corunir te contó cómo Golodir reunió un ejército entre los Montañeses para atacar Carn Dûm. La expedición fracasó y Corunir quedó solo, incapaz de cruzar Rammas Deluon, ahora poseídas de un terrible poder, para conocer el destino de su capitán y compañeros.","'El tiempo apremia, ${PLAYER}. Busca una de las piedras menores que hay en el paisaje y haz un calco de las runas que tiene.'","Las piedras vigilantes menores están esparcidas por el paisaje del oeste de Angmar, especialmente cerca de los campamentos de Angmarim y Montañeses.\
\
Corunir cree que el secreto de Rammas Deluon puede revelarse investigando una de las piedras vigilantes menores. Te ha indicado que busques una de las piedras menores y hagas un calco de las runas que tiene. Te advirtió que evitaras las piedras vigilantes mortales.","'¿Así que quieres saber cómo ocurrió esta tragedia? En verdad, no lo sé. No sé si fue por alguna maquinación del Falso Rey, o si fue simplemente una mala suerte, pero nuestra marcha terminó abruptamente. Al marchar hacia el este, nos encontramos con un valle lleno de terribles estatuas. Rammas Deluon, lo llamaban los Montañeses. No cabía duda de que algún espíritu de vigilancia maligna habitaba en las piedras, pues todos sentíamos su opresión. Fue aquí donde Golodir me ordenó quedarme.\
\
'Al pasar el grupo por las piedras, quedó claro por qué los Montañeses temían tanto el valle. Cuando los últimos hombres cruzaron Rammas Deluon, las piedras vigilantes lanzaron una terrible opresión, tal que los hombres atrapados en ella murieron por el peso en sus corazones. Intenté cruzar las piedras, pero no pude. Golodir me ordenó quedarme, y así lo hice.\
\
'Los días se convirtieron en meses, luego en años, y Golodir no regresaba. Sabía que debía volver de inmediato a Esteldín, pero no podía abandonar a mi capitán. Intenté en vano cruzar Rammas Deluon, hasta que mi espíritu se quebró por dentro. Finalmente, envié el mensaje a Esteldín, que te trajo aquí.\
\
'Debemos descubrir el secreto de Rammas Deluon, ${PLAYER}. Quizás una de las muchas piedras menores que hay en esta tierra, especialmente cerca de los campamentos de los Angmarim y Montañeses, revele ese secreto. Ve a una de las piedras vigilantes menores y haz un calco de las runas que hay en su base. Ten cuidado con las piedras mortales, pues tienen un poder terrible.'","Libro 6, Capítulo 3: Secretos de las piedras","'¡Has regresado! ¿Trajiste el calco? ¡Bien! Déjame verlo....'","Haz un calco de una piedra vigilante menor","Lleva el calco de la piedra vigilante a Corunir"},
[2192]={"'¡La batalla está lejos de terminar!'","The battle rages as deadlier forces from Mordor take the field","Horn is at Kings' End.\
\
You heard a loud commotion and should ask Horn what transpired to cause it.","'There is so much death all around us.'","Defeat your foes on the Pelennor during the battle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Elfhelm south of Kings' End","'Oh, ${PLAYER}, I am glad... glad to see you. I have lost many friends today already, and the sun is not yet high in the sky. There will be more dead.'\
\
You hear the sorrow in Horn's voice, and something else: tired resignation, dangerous acceptance. You ask him what the sudden commotion was a moment ago.\
\
'It was a frightening thing. Men were bringing the bodies of Théoden and Éowyn to the city, where they will lie in peace. We watched from afar during a brief respite, and saw that the group carrying the bodies of our dead were nearly to the city gates. But before they could enter, a Nazgûl flew down from above and sought to seize the body of Théoden!\
\
'We cried in dismay to see it, for we were much too far away to prevent it; that was the sound you must have heard. Even as we despaired, there was a great flash, and the Nazgûl was thwarted. Gandalf turned it aside, and the bodies of our dead were safely brought within the city. But it was a close thing. How much grief can those wraiths inflict that might top what they have already? I would have said no more, but it seems there is no end to their ravening hate! How can we hope to survive this day?\
\
'I do not know if I have the will to continue fighting, ${PLAYER}. Théoden King... Lady Éowyn... so many others...'","'Gléowine is a bard and no warrior, but he speaks the truth in this. The death of Théoden will affect the Rohirrim greatly. Will they despair and cast down their weapons, as the bard believes, or will they respond with anger and vengeance, as Éomer has done? My son Elfmar has followed Éomer's course, and fights with renewed vigour!\
\
'The enemy is massing to the north-east and to the south of Kings' End, ${PLAYER}. Scout those camps, and slay any enemies you find! The death of that terrible spectre, for I deem it was a death, may have cast our foes into disarray and confusion. I hope it is so!'","'My son has fallen! A fearsome Olog-hai smashed through the ranks, and he crushed Elfmar where he stood in defiance! With every swing of its blood-drenched weapon, the terrible creature cried its name aloud: 'Thrúgrath!' he bellowed, over and over. I can still hear its name, echoing in my head without end! Thrúgrath, slayer of my beloved son!\
\
'Elfmar, I will avenge you! I will make them pay for the hurt they have caused, and send them fleeing into the darkness of death with our curses echoing in their ears!\
\
'In the name of Théoden King and Elfmar my son, I will not rest until every last Orc is slain, and until Thrúgrath chokes upon his own name and cries it no more!'","Talk to Elfhelm near Kings' End","Ingbert is at Kings' End.","'The battle is not yet ended!'","Book 6, Chapter 3: The Grip of Despair","'I do not know if I have the will to continue fighting, ${PLAYER}. Théoden King... Lady Éowyn... so many others...'","Talk to Ingbert at Kings' End","Elfhelm fights in a small knot of soldiers near a fallen Mûmak south of Kings' End.","'I do not think highly of Wizards, but Gandalf did right by Théoden King to protect his body from that wraith's foul intentions. Our dead have been brought within the city, and we will mourn them when the fighting is done.\
\
'Listen not to Horn's despairing words, for they are only on the surface. He has the same solid core as I have, though I might not have said so a week ago. He will be fine. He has already slain more Orcs than I have fingers on one hand, and more will join them in the ground by the end of the battle, I doubt it not!'","'Théoden is slain, and Éomer has charged past the lines and is lost to us. The men of Rohan need someone to lead them, or they will be seized by the same despair that has sapped my own courage, paltry as it is. Where is Elfhelm? Find him and he may help bolster the courage of the Rohirrim at this critical juncture!'","The resolve of the men of Rohan is sorely tested following the death of Théoden.","A great cry goes up from the direction of Kings' End","There was the sound of sudden commotion from the direction of Kings' End, and you should return there at once","Scout the battlefield south of Kings' End","Talk to Horn at Kings' End","You see Horn standing where Théoden fell. He may know what transpired","Bodies litter the field: Orcs, Haradrim, Rohirrim, and Gondorians","Scout the battlefield north-east of Kings' End","Elfhelm is very near to the corpse of the fell-beast at Kings' End.\
\
Gléowine sent you to find Elfhelm and get him to lead the Rohirrim during this critical moment in the fighting.","Horn's father Ingbert calls you to him","Learn what transpired at Kings' End","Defeated foes on the Pelennor during the battle (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The enemy is massing to the south and to the north-east of Kings' End, and Elfhelm wanted you to scout those camps and slay any enemies you find.","'Where is Elfhelm? Find him and he may help bolster the courage of the Rohirrim at this critical juncture!'"},
[2193]={"Las piedras centinela sin vida se encuentran en el oeste de Malenhad, lejos al este de Aughaire.\
\
Corunir te ha pedido que busques uno de los corazones de piedra mencionados en las runas, buscando entre las piedras centinela sin vida.","Examinas la piedra centinela cuidadosamente, pero no ves señales del corazón que Corunir te pidió buscar.","'Esta parece ser una piedra como la que describen las runas, pero no sirve de mucho. El corazón está agrietado.'","Recogiste un corazón de una piedra centinela sin vida","Lleva el corazón de piedra agrietado a Corunir","Recoge un corazón de una piedra centinela sin vida","'Estas runas son de estilo élfico, pero el idioma es la Lengua Negra, en la que no soy experto. Sin embargo, sé un poco y veo que hablan de un \"corazón\" dentro de la piedra.\
\
'Quizá si pudiera estudiar uno de estos corazones de piedra, podría encontrar una forma de romper el hechizo. Hay piedras sin vida al este de aquí de las que puedes recoger un corazón, sin peligro.\
\
'Tráeme un corazón de piedra lo antes posible, para que terminemos nuestra tarea.'","'Al este de aquí hay algunas piedras centinela sin vida. Tráeme un corazón de una de ellas para que pueda estudiarlo.'","Corunir está en el pueblo de los montañeses de Aughaire.\
\
Debes regresar con Corunir y entregarle el corazón de piedra que encontraste.","Examinas la piedra centinela cuidadosamente y descubres, a través de una grieta, una extraña roca oscura. Al recogerla, sientes una breve inquietud, pero desaparece rápidamente.","Libro 6, Capítulo 4: Corazón de piedra","'¿Encontraste un corazón entre las piedras sin vida, ${PLAYER}?'","El calco que hiciste mostró runas de naturaleza vil, escritas en la Lengua Negra, en la que Corunir no es experto; sin embargo, pudo distinguir algo sobre el \"corazón\" de la piedra."},
[2194]={"'I do not believe in long farewells. You have little time to delay. You must ride swiftly, for you have a long journey ahead of you.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Talan Haldir in Lothlórien when you accept this quest.</rgb>","'You long to see the Lady Galadriel? I would not keep you from her, ${PLAYER}, but I fear things are not so simple this time.'","Travel to Lothlórien and speak with Haldir on his flet outside the borders","'Go with courage! Go with haste! And do not fear the darkness!'","Nona has said her farewells to Suvulch, and now it is time for you to ride with all haste to Lothlórien.","'I am ready! Let us ride for the land of the Elf-queen!'","Book 6, Chapter 4: Swift Hooves","Haldir is on a flet outside Lothlórien.\
\
You should speak to Haldir to obtain permission to travel with Nona into Lothlórien."},
[2195]={"Study Dúnhere for signs of life at Riders' Stand","'Scout the approaches! Do it for Hirluin, if not for me!'","Ingbert is at Kings' End, waiting to speak with you and return to battle.","The armies of Mordor fill the field all the way to the river","'Several Gondorian soldiers are resting from combat to the north of here. Go to them and see if they have learned anything of the enemy's organization. The armies of Mordor must have another commander!'","'Death calls for us, ${PLAYER}! There were Gondorian soldiers fighting alongside us to the north. Find them and render your aid!'","'That arrow was meant for me, ${PLAYER}. Farewell, Dúnhere! I treasure your friendship in death even as I did in life. Give my best to my uncle and my sister when you join them beyond, and tell them I will see them soon!\
\
'Death calls for us, ${PLAYER}! There were Gondorian soldiers fighting alongside us to the north. Find them and render your aid!'","Éomer is at Riders' Stand.","'Does Dúnhere live?'","You examine him closely, but the result is grim. Dúnhere is dead","'There was nothing I could do, ${PLAYER}! One moment Hirluin was valiantly standing against this great beast of a troll, and the next moment he was dead!\
\
'My mouth is dry and ashy, but an endless parade of wine-bottles will not refresh me. This battle began as a joyous reminder of my youth, but it is that no longer. Nay, it is the bitter taste of Old Calembel that fills my heart now. Hirluin, no longer Fair! My friend, I will not say farewell. I will keep your memory fresh in my mind for as long as I live, whether that be for my remaining years... or until the rain stops!\
\
'${PLAYER}, the enemy presses us on all sides. Scout the approaches to the hill, for Hirluin if not for me. I would not have them do some injury to his corpse.'","Éomer has climbed a rocky outcropping on the south-western side of the hillock.","Talk to Ingbert and complete 'Instance: The Foe Resurgent'","Return to Ingbert at Kings' End","Find Gondorian soldiers north of Éomer at Riders' Stand","From here you see that the enemy horde reaches as far as the Rammas","The forces of Mordor fill the plain, and smoke burns on the horizon","Ingbert is at Kings' End.","'To battle! Let none stand in our way!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'They did not know what evil force now leads the armies of Mordor? It does not matter, for we will sweep them from the field, whether commanded or leaderless!\
\
'We must return to combat, ${PLAYER}! Speak to me when you are ready to wade once more into battle!'","Talk to Forlong north of Kings' End","Talk to Forlong at Riders' Stand","'The enemy forces were being led by the wraith that killed Théoden and Lady Éowyn. If the armies of Mordor were going to flee in the wake of its death, they would have done so already. I think they must have another commander, ${PLAYER}, and he has seized control of the enemy forces.\
\
'Several Gondorian soldiers are resting from combat to the north of here. Go to them and see if they have learned anything of the enemy's organization.'","'We are surrounded, ${PLAYER}, and I believe the rain falls upon our last stand. As I rallied my men about me on the crest of this hillock, an arrow flew upon the height and felled Dúnhere.\
\
'Check his wounds and tell me if he will live, though I fear the worst for him.'","Book 6, Chapter 4: The Foe Resurgent","Éomer sent you to help Gondorian soldiers atop the hillock at Riders' Stand.","Forlong kneels by the body of his friend Hirluin at Riders' Stand.","With the Witch-king now dead, a new commander has taken control of the enemy forces on the Pelennor Fields.","Forlong and Hirluin are north of Kings' End.","Forlong kneels by the body of Hirluin, slain by the enemy","Talk to Hirluin north of Kings' End","Scout the several approaches up the hill at Riders' Stand (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Éomer at Riders' Stand","'The fighting has been fierce, ${PLAYER}, and my blood is raised! Hirluin here has even broken a sweat, and I daresay some of his pretty hairs might shortly be mussed!\
\
'I will need my own bottle of Beren's Blood, the wine of our youth, to quench this thirst when the fighting's done!'","'A quick moment of respite to catch our breath, and then we will go once more into the fray.\
\
'I have not seen any sign of a new commander among the enemy forces, but I doubt not there must be one. The armies of Mordor still press the attack; if they were leaderless they would surely run.'","Dúnhere was felled by an arrow at Riders' Stand, and Éomer begged you to check for signs of life in his fallen friend.","Éomer and his men have been surrounded on a hillock and cut off from the rest of the defenders.","'${PLAYER}, I have seen something that fills my heart with dread. I would not have thought this day could grow any worse, yet now I see I was a fool to believe it!'","Talk to Éomer on the south-western outcropping of the hillock","Several approaches climb up the hill at Riders' Stand.\
\
Forlong has asked you to scout the approaches up the hill, even if you think it futile to do so."},
[2197]={"Éomer stands on the rocky outcropping on the south-western corner of the hillock, but his mood is greatly changed.","'You see them too. Black sails on the river! The Corsairs of Umbar approach from the south-west!'\
\
As you look at Éomer and see the despair in his eyes, you almost tell him that the ships are not sailed by Corsairs, for the Corsairs are slain and their leader Balakhôr will scourge no more. But then doubt gnaws in your mind. Aragorn intended to bring the ships north to Minas Tirith, but what if some evil befell him upon the river? What if some design of Sauron's lay in wait, ready to ensnare the Grey Company and their allies?\
\
You hold your tongue, and seek to master your own mounting doubt and fear.","Éomer asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> into the distance and see what has so disturbed him.","Defeated foes on the hillock (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated more foes on the hillock (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'${PLAYER}! At last our fortunes change! I would not have believed it had I not seen it with my own eyes!'","Defeat foes on the hillock (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Book 6, Chapter 5: The Black Ships","Éomer is on a rocky outcropping on the south-western side of the hillock at Riders' Stand.","Talk to Éomer on the south-western outcropping of the hillock","'My eyes cannot believe what they see, and yet they must. Another player has entered the field of battle, and he has thrown in his lot with Mordor. <rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> for yourself, ${PLAYER}, and see that of which I speak!'","'Black sails on the river! The Corsairs of Umbar approach from the south-west!'","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> into the distance and see what Éomer has seen","Defeat even more foes on the hillock (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Forces of the Enemy approach the hillock as you seek to master your doubt and fear.","Defeat more foes on the hillock (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated even more foes on the hillock (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Éomer has seen something in the distance that fills him with dread.","Black sails fly on a river of dread"},
[2198]={"Aunque el corazón de piedra que encontraste estaba agrietado e inútil, aún queda otro camino. Corunir ha sabido de un ritual en la fortaleza de Tór Gailvin, que podría darte un corazón completo si lo interrumpes.","Obtén el corazón de piedra","'Si queremos encontrar la forma de pasar Rammas Deluon, debes recuperar el corazón de piedra del hechicero Tath.'","'Es una pena que este corazón esté roto, pero aún puede haber otro camino para nosotros. Mientras estabas fuera, algunos aldeanos regresaron de una cacería y contaron sobre un ritual en Tór Gailvin, una fortaleza al noreste, al este de un lugar llamado Fail-á-Khro.\
\
'El ritual parece estar relacionado con el hechizo que da poder a estas piedras, y el hechicero que lo realiza lleva consigo un corazón de piedra. Si logras interrumpir el ritual y derrotar a Tath, podrías recuperar el corazón de piedra de él.\
\
'¡Ve rápido, porque si está preparando otra piedra centinela, puede que no tengas otra oportunidad!'","Libro 6, Capítulo 5: El destino del hechicero","Corazón de piedra obtenido","'Este sí es un corazón de piedra, pero... la situación es más grave de lo que pensaba.'","Lleva el corazón de piedra a Corunir","Tath está en Tór Gailvin, al noreste de Aughaire, al este de Fail-á-Khro.\
\
Corunir te ha enviado a Tór Gailvin para arrebatarle un corazón de piedra a un hechicero de Angmar llamado Tath."},
[2199]={"'Lleva el corazón de piedra a la piedra centinela antigua en Ram Dúath. Puede darte la ventaja que necesitas para derrotar al espíritu de la piedra.'","Libro 6, Capítulo 6: Desafiando a la piedra","Derrota al espíritu de la piedra centinela antigua","Habla con Corunir","Corunir está en el pueblo de los montañeses de Aughaire, al oeste de Bail Róva.\
\
Con el espíritu de la piedra centinela antigua derrotado, deberías regresar con Corunir y darle la noticia de esperanza.","'¿Has vencido al espíritu? ¡Tu victoria me anima, ${PLAYER}! Me da esperanza de que aún podamos triunfar.'","La piedra centinela antigua está cerca del paso oriental de Ram Dúath, cerca de Bail Róva, al este de Aughaire.\
\
Corunir cree que el corazón de piedra puede atraer el espíritu maligno de otra piedra centinela y te ha pedido que pruebes su teoría en una piedra centinela antigua que guarda los pasos de Ram Dúath.","Presenta el corazón de piedra a la piedra centinela antigua","'No, toma esta cosa maligna... ¡No puedo soportarla más! Mis disculpas, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, pero la sensación que me produce es demasiado parecida al terror de Rammas Deluon. No puedo soportar su presencia.\
\
'Pero ahora conozco el secreto de las piedras de Rammas Deluon. No es un hechizo lo que da poder a las estatuas, sino un espíritu maligno de una Edad antigua, como los que habitan los tumularios al servicio de Angmar. Este corazón de piedra fue preparado para recibir tal espíritu.\
\
'Quizá este corazón pueda atraer a un espíritu de otra piedra. Puede ser una pista para romper la voluntad de las piedras centinela. Lleva este corazón de piedra a la piedra centinela antigua que se encuentra cerca del paso oriental de Ram Dúath, al este de aquí, no lejos de Bail Róva, una fortaleza de los Angmarim.''","Espíritu de la piedra centinela antigua derrotado","'¿Dónde está el corazón de piedra? ¿Has fallado? No debí tener tantas esperanzas.'","Corunir reaccionó de forma extraña ante la presencia y el contacto del corazón de piedra, apartándose de él aterrorizado. Te dijo que el corazón había sido preparado para recibir un espíritu maligno de una Edad antigua, similar a los que habitan los tumularios al servicio de Angmar."},
[2200]={"Has the earth been disturbed here? Does it signify the Fellowship's passage?","'This is a dangerous time to pass through Thinglad, stranger. Orcs have been sighted along the river.'\
\
Fimloth listens attentively as you tell her that friends of yours passed this way, and you seek to know if they did so safely.\
\
'The scouts have not reported any bands of travellers recently, but if your friends travelled in secret they may have gone unnoticed. I have fewer scouts in Thinglad than I once did. If you travel south alongside the river, perhaps you will find some sign of your friends' passage.'","'I thank you for the help. The Orcs must pay for the heartache they have caused us, though the debt be larger than the worth of their own lives!\
\
'I sought to engage this woman you travel with in conversation, but she is slow to trust and slower to friend. I will not ask you to divulge any of your shared mysteries to me, but it is a curious thing: she bears a sword of the Rohirrim horse-lords. Her folk have long been in enmity with that people, have they not? If she slew the sword's owner, you may find your path through this land made more difficult. The men of Rohan are not quick to forgive.\
\
'She wished to speak with you when you returned.'","You gingerly remove an Orc arrow from the body of the slain scout","Defeated Orcs in Thinglad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Your Dunlending friend wants to speak with you. She has spoken only a little to me, but she is clearly agitated about something. Neither of our peoples knows much of the other, and we have little common ground between us.'","Fimloth is at Haldirith in Thinglad.\
\
You have defeated many Orcs and should return to Fimloth at Haldirith in Thinglad.","Haldirith is an Elf-camp located in the northern area of Thinglad.\
\
Alfrohir has brought you from Lothlórien to Thinglad along the Great River, and thinks you should present yourself to Fimloth at Haldirith, in Thinglad.","You see trampled grass underfoot. Did the Fellowship come this way?","You have been following the river south in search of signs of the Fellowship's passage.","'This Elf has given me something to think about, ${PLAYER}. I am worried. My people have never gotten along with the horse-lords, and it seems they have a large outpost just to the south. We will need to go that way if we are to learn the reason behind your dream.'","'Find and slay Orcs along the river. They prowl throughout Thinglad in large numbers. Do it for the scouts whose lives have been lost.'","The Fellowship passed south along the river, and Fimloth thinks if you seek news of your friends you should follow the river-bank south looking for signs of their passage.","'This is not the first friend we have lost, but that makes it no easier. I will tell her family that she has fallen in service to the Golden Wood.'\
\
Fimloth shakes her head sadly.\
\
'The Orcs that killed her are surely still somewhere in Thinglad. If you wish to help us while you seek sign of your friends, slay any Orcs you find in this land!'","'What did you find? Did you find anything of interest in this place?'","Defeat Orcs in Thinglad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'There is a camp of Elves not far from here, in Thinglad. It is an outpost from which my people watch for threats from the south. It is called Haldirith, and if you wish to know what has been happening along the river, that is a good place to start.\
\
'Present yourself to Fimloth at Haldirith, and ask her for tidings.'","Haldirith in Thinglad serves as an outpost of Lothlórien from which the Elves stand watch for threats from the south.","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'Keep searching south alongside the banks of the river. If your friends passed this way, you may find sign of them.'","Orcs can be found in great numbers throughout Thinglad.\
\
Fimloth has asked you to defeat Orcs throughout Thinglad.","'You may find some sign of your friends if you search alongside the river. Beware of Orcs! There has been an increase in their activities in Thinglad of late.'","Follow the river-bank further south of Haldirith","Fimloth is at Haldirith.\
\
You should return to Fimloth at Haldirith and give her the Orc arrow and news of the slain scout you discovered.","'Do you not need tidings of this area? You should go now to the Elf-camp here in Thinglad. It is called Haldirith and is located south of here. Present yourself to Fimloth, and she will surely be able to help you.'","Search south along the river","Book 6, Chapter 6: Downriver Dangers","Follow the river-bank south of Haldirith","Nona is at Haldirith, in Thinglad.\
\
Nona wishes to speak with you.","Bring Orc arrow to Fimloth at Haldirith"},
[2201]={"'I was wounded not long after we arrived here, ${PLAYER}. Some cursed Orc was pretending to be dead, and he leapt up and gave me a good slice with his serrated blade. I repaid him in kind, but I will live and he will not; there he lies, and pretends no more.\
\
'Dark-hearted villain! Cowardly corpse!'","'Some of our kin have been injured by Orcs feigning death among these ruins.'","Talk to Corunir at the Ruin of Pel Dúven","The Orc snarls a challenge and leaps to his feet!","Corunir is beside himself with anger at the Ruin of Pel Dúven.","You hear a great commotion coming from the north-west","'The banner of the White Tree! The ships that come now on the river are for Gondor! Friends unlooked-for have come to our aid!\
\
'We must break through the lines of the Enemy while they are distracted by the ships! Jump onto the horse just to the north-east and ride to the Ruin of Pel Dúven to meet these new arrivals, or take to the Quays of the Harlond to ease their disembarking!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>If you have a Small Fellowship, now is the time to challenge 'The Quays of the Harlond' from the World Join panel.</rgb>","'What was that commotion to the north-west?'","Talk to Radanir on the eastern side of the Ruin of Pel Dúven","'Not all of the bodies that litter the farm are truly dead. Some of the Orcs lie in wait, feigning death, and spring up to surprise the unwary! We have already suffered some injuries from these play-acting corpses.\
\
'Examine some of the bodies and ensure they are truly dead. It will not do to suffer any more losses from these treacherous ambushers.'","Corunir's anger departs, replaced with a haunted visage","Amegil has regained some of his courage, and stands tall","Amegil has cast off his fright, and he speaks now with prideful anger.","Talk to Amegil at the Ruin of Pel Dúven","Book 6, Chapter 6: The Battle Rages","This Orc died of his wounds, as it seemed","Talk to Halbarad at the Ruin of Pel Dúven","Aragorn and the Grey Company have come to the Ruin of Pel Dúven.","Radanir is injured on the eastern side of the Ruin of Pel Dúven.","'I knew the sight of the black sails must cause despair to rise in the hearts of the city's defenders, but I hoped to catch the enemy off-guard in the confusion that followed the banner's unfurling. And so it was!\
\
'The White Tree is for Gondor, but it was surrounded by seven stars and with a crown above, and they are for Elendil. That sigil has not been seen by the forces of Mordor for a great many years, and seeing it again must fill them with fear and confusion.'","'Cursed play-acting Orcs! They should have the decency to stay dead!'","Use the swift horse by the south-west out-cropping of Riders' Stand to travel to the Ruin of Pel Dúven","'We disembarked at the Harlond and came to the ruins of this farm to establish a foothold on the Pelennor. The battle had already swept through this area and left many bodies behind, and now it proceeds on the outskirts of the ruins.\
\
'This battle-tide has had a regrettable effect, ${PLAYER}, for not all of the bodies that litter the farm are truly dead. Some of the Orcs lie in wait, feigning death, and spring up to surprise the unwary! We have already suffered some injuries from these play-acting corpses.\
\
'Examine some of the bodies and ensure they are truly dead. It will not do to suffer any more losses from these treacherous ambushers.'","'Easy, Corunir, let the man have some room to breathe. Control yourself, my friend!'\
\
Halbarad sees you approach and calls to you quickly.\
\
'${PLAYER}, I could use your help learning what has transpired. Corunir is beside himself with anger, and I fear what he might do if we cannot calm him down, and quickly.'","This Orc is not feigning death","Halbarad is at the Ruin of Pel Dúven.","Halbarad has told you that some of the bodies littering the Ruin of Pel Dúven are not truly dead, and wants you to examine them for would-be ambushers feigning death.","Examine slain Orcs at the Ruin of Pel Dúven and ensure they are not feigning death","Amegil is frightened, but you would hear what he has said that has so enraged Corunir.","This Orc is truly slain","Corunir is shouting at a frightened Gondorian man, and Halbarad seeks to restrain him","'We must break through the lines of the Enemy while they are distracted by the ships! Jump onto the horse just to the north-east and ride to the Ruin of Pel Dúven to meet these new arrivals, or take to the Quays of the Harlond to ease their disembarking!'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>If you have a Small Fellowship, now is the time to challenge 'The Quays of the Harlond' from the World Join panel.</rgb>","Corunir has become very angry about something, and threatens a Gondorian man at the Ruin of Pel Dúven.\
\
Halbarad has asked you to help him calm down Corunir before the Ranger does something he will regret.","Aragorn and the Grey Company have arrived at the Harlond. Have they come in time to turn the tide of the battle?","'I came through the gates onto the Pelennor to fight alongside my brothers and the rest of the city-guard, and slew more than my share of Orcs and the evil Men that fight with them. Great deeds were done, and I daresay we could have had the victory even without the arrival of this man and his Ranger kin.\
\
'But the press of battle moved us hither and thither, and my contingent of soldiers soon found itself back-to-back with these Rangers. We fought against the Orcs for some minutes, and shared our names as soldiers do. The bond that is formed in battle between men on the same side is a strong one, and blood spilled in battle unites men like nothing else.\
\
'That is when I learned that I and my brothers were fighting alongside a Ranger named Golodir. Golodir! I knew the name well, for had it not been in the conversation of every man in the garrison? Hated Golodir, Ranger of the North and friend of Gothmog, commander of the enemy forces? Yes, it was the very same!'","'Well, I made it no secret what I thought of him. I told him that he fought on the wrong side, and that he would find his Orc-friends elsewhere on the field. I told him he should do us all a favour and cast himself upon his own sword, and so repent of the dark bond he shares with Gothmog. I'd tell him the same were he here right now, and regret nothing!\
\
'When men such as he join hands with evil ones such as Gothmog, they deserve nothing but the curses of good-hearted soldiers, and that is what he had from us!\
\
'I do not know where he has gone. He has likely gone to join his friend Gothmog, and do some harm to the city or its defenders. I do not doubt it is so, and if this Ranger thinks otherwise, then he is a fool!'","'This man spews lies, ${PLAYER}! We have come to the aid of his city, and he repays us with poisonous and treacherous slander!\
\
'I would have his head for the things he has said! He is lucky that Halbarad stays my hand, or I would put an end to his vile whisperings!'","The Grey Company has come to Pelennor, and they make safe the Ruin of Pel Dúven","You heard a great commotion coming from the north-west side of the Ruin of Pel Dúven, and should investigate.","The newly-arrived allies that sailed on the Black Ships will disembark and make for the Ruin of Pel Dúven.\
\
Éomer has directed you to use the swift horse at the base of the outcropping on the south-west side of Riders' Stand to ride to meet the new arrivals.","'Lies! Listen to those slanderous lies, ${PLAYER}, and tell me that this man should not pay for such vile utterances!'\
\
You put a hand on Corunir's shoulder and tell him quietly that Gothmog is another name for Mordirith of Angmar, and that you have no reason to doubt he shares some connexion with Golodir as a result of their experiences in Carn Dûm. All of the fight and bluster departs from Corunir then, and he sinks to one knee.","Talk to Aragorn at the Ruin of Pel Dúven","Investigate the commotion on the north-west side of the Ruin of Pel Dúven","'We meet once again, ${PLAYER}, and in battle! We were borne on the wind, and I held the unfurling of my standard for the very last moment. I knew the sight of the black sails must cause despair to rise in the hearts of the city's defenders, but I hoped to catch the enemy off-guard in the confusion that followed the banner's unfurling. And so it was!\
\
'The White Tree is for Gondor, but it was surrounded by seven stars and with a crown above, and they are for Elendil. That sigil has not been seen by the forces of Mordor for a great many years, and seeing it again must fill them with fear and confusion.'"},
[2202]={"Friends gather to remember Golodir, but there is little time to mourn","'I will not say that Golodir should not have come on this road, ${PLAYER}. I will not shame his memory by wishing that he had stayed behind; it was his duty as he saw it, and he performed it with dignity and without question. He will always have my gratitude.\
\
'But I keenly feel the sorrow of his loss. My heart desires to mourn Golodir, but I know that there is not time for that now. The battle continues, heartlessly, never caring for the friends we have lost. That is one of its cruelest hurts: that we must set aside our grief and go on, lest we lose that for which they fought.'","Corunir is in the north-west area of the Ruin of Pel Dúven.","Return to the Rangers in the Ruin of Pel Dúven","The Rangers gather in the Ruin of Pel Dúven to mourn Golodir.","'Golodir has had his vengeance, and now he will have his rest. None have earned it so well as he. He endured so much in the high chambers of Carn Dûm, and in the months since he escaped that city, but he was never free of the False King until today.\
\
'No man here would have questioned his loyalty if he chose to remain in the North. Each of us would have understood, knowing what he suffered, and knowing that it was enough. But Golodir knew his duty, and did not seek to count it fulfilled by his hardship. Nay, he journeyed with the Grey Company all the same. It was an honour to call him friend.'","'We have to find Golodir! I hope only that we are not too late!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Book 6, Chapter 7: A Final Vengeance","Talk to Halbarad in the Ruin of Pel Dúven","Talk to Corunir in the Ruin of Pel Dúven and go in search of Golodir","Corunir fears that the men of Gondor may have worked some tragic mischief upon Golodir.","'How can this be? Mordirith was slain! He was finally slain, and Golodir was free of him!\
\
'We have to find Golodir, ${PLAYER}. These men of Gondor may have worked some tragic mischief with their words, but it might still be prevented!\
\
'Tell me when you are ready to go, and we will set forth in search of him!'","Talk to Aragorn in the Ruin of Pel Dúven","'I cannot believe he is gone, ${PLAYER}. I spent so much time on this journey worrying about what he was feeling, and worrying about what he had endured, that I gave little thought to myself. But now...\
\
'There is just emptiness. What do I do now?'\
\
You take Corunir's arm and speak your own quiet words: words of grief, words of comfort, and words of duty. None hear them but Corunir, and when you finish he nods.\
\
'You have seen sorrow too, ${PLAYER}, I hear it in your words. I will think on what you have said, and I thank you for saying it. But Aragorn is right. The battle rages, and it will not wait for us.'","Talk to Corunir in the Ruin of Pel Dúven"},
[2203]={"Busca sobrevivientes de la banda de Golodir","'Has demostrado que tales piedras pueden ser derrotadas, que su poder de opresión solo es tan grande como tú lo permites. Lamentablemente, mi espíritu ha estado quebrantado por demasiado tiempo... No creo que pueda pasar las piedras y soportar su miedo.\
\
'Tú, sin embargo, ya no tienes nada que temer. Ve hacia el este, ${PLAYER}, y cruza Rammas Deluon. Solo puedo esperar que en algún lugar más allá mis parientes sobrevivan. ¡La gente de aquí dice que hay enanos al sur, más allá de Rammas Deluon! ¡Búscalos allí!\
\
'¡Ve, y que los Valar vayan contigo!'","'Ve ahora. ¡Cruza Rammas Deluon, porque ya no tienes causa para temer! Busca a los enanos que, según se rumorea, acampan allí.'","'¿Quién eres? Si no eres servidor de la Sombra de Angmar, ¿cómo es que pasaste por Rammas Deluon y no pereciste?\
\
'¿Corunir te envió? ¡Eso es una noticia alegre! ¡Tu llegada es como un toque de victoria para nosotros!'","'¡Hace mucho que no veo a nadie del Sur!'","'¡Tu llegada es muy oportuna, ${PLAYER}!'","'No puedo pasar Rammas Deluon, ${PLAYER}, porque no creo que pudiera soportar el poder de las piedras.'","'¡No tienes nada que temer de los Vigilantes de Rammas Deluon!'","Rammas Deluon se encuentra muy al este de Aughaire en Malenhad. Corunir sugirió que busques un campamento de enanos al sur, más allá de Rammas Deluon.\
\
Corunir te ordenó pasar por Rammas Deluon, porque ya no tienes causa para temer las mortales piedras. Espera que puedas encontrar un remanente de la fuerza que Golodir condujo a través de las piedras en algún lugar del otro lado.","Tu derrota de la antigua piedra vigilante de Ram Dúath ha demostrado que las piedras pueden ser desafiadas.","Libro 6, Capítulo 7: Más allá de Rammas Deluon"},
[2204]={"'I am not welcome here. I care not!'","'What is the meaning of this? How came this woman to bear a sword of Rohan? Take it from her and show it to Horn at the top of Stangard. If he believes she should then enter the village, I will abide by his decision. Not before.'","'Who is this woman? And why does she carry a sword of my people? You are a long way from home, stranger, and in the company of a Dunlending warrior-witch. I do not like it!'\
\
Afic glowers at you, his heavy-lidded gaze suspicious.\
\
'This outpost may be beyond the borders of Rohan, but the law of Théoden King holds, and I cannot allow this warrior-witch to pass unchallenged. Take that Rohirric sword from her and present it to Horn, atop Stangard, and see what he thinks. He is young, but in matters of sword-craft and history he is unrivalled. If he believes this woman is no threat, I will allow her to enter. Otherwise she must remain outside the walls.'","Book 6, Chapter 7: Enemies of Old","Show Nona's sword to Horn in Stangard","'I will let you carry the sword, but do not let any of these men touch it. This weapon may be the result of their sword-craft, but it is theirs no longer. Now it is the sword of my brother Wadu, and the chain of its heritage has been severed and made anew. Wadu's Ghost wields it now.'\
\
Nona studies you closely.\
\
'Take it from this bag of my belongings. Bring it to this man Horn atop the village, but heed my words! Let none but you touch it, and return it to me when he is satisfied.'","Stangard is in Eorlsmead, south of Thinglad.\
\
You have decided to travel with Nona to the Rohirrim village of Stangard, in order to learn what you can of the situation alongside the river and the meaning behind your dream.","'Welcome to Stangard, such as it is. What is this sword you bear?'\
\
He reaches out for it, but you shake your head and keep it in your hands. He laughs quietly, and you tell him briefly of Nona, Wadu, and the sword.\
\
'I see. This is a Rohirric sword, but it is old... very old. It strikes a memory in me, but I cannot place it. I wonder if it was fashioned before Eorl the Young came out of the north-lands?'\
\
He seems to reach a decision.\
\
'I want to show you something. Return this curious weapon to your friend at the gate, with my regards, and tell her she is welcome to enter the village. I do not think either of you are our foes. Then meet me outside town, by the Cuthstan. It is a large statue of two figures located among the Wailing Hills, west of Stangard, and I think you should see it.'","Nona's sword is packed within her belongings near the entrance to Stangard.\
\
Nona has given you permission to show her sword to Horn, as long as you let no one touch it.","'Horn said she could enter? Hmmph. He is soft.'","'That is very curious. Return the sword to this girl, and we will speak again. She is by the gate of Stangard, is she not?'","Horn can be found atop the village of Stangard, in Eorlsmead.\
\
Nona has given you her sword to show to Horn, with the instruction that no one but you is to handle it.","Nona is at the gate of Stangard.\
\
Horn was very interested in Nona's sword, and wants you to return it to her before meeting him outside the town.","Collect Nona's sword from the bag containing her possessions","'Show my sword to this man Horn, but do not let him touch it. I will not permit anyone else to handle the blade that belonged to Wadu.\
\
'Take it from this bag of my belongings.'","Nona is outside the gate of Stangard, in Eorlsmead.\
\
Afic refuses to allow Nona to enter Stangard before you show her sword to a man called Horn, near the top of the village.","'The outpost of the horse-lords is south of here, in Eorlsmead, and is called Stangard. I will travel with you to this village, if I must, but heed my warning: they will bear no love for me, nor I for them! I will stay my hand and my tongue, for your sake, but I will suffer no insult from the forgoil.\
\
'Let us learn what we may from their outpost, and then leave quickly!'","The Rohirrim village of Stangard sits within Eorlsmead, along the Great River, and that is where your road now leads.","'Show that sword to Horn. He will want to see it. You will find him atop the village.'","'I have permission to enter? Ha! I will remain outside. This village smells too much of horse and false dealing for me.\
\
'Thank you for returning Wadu's sword to me, ${PLAYER}. I knew I could trust you. I am not so certain of these others.'"},
[2205]={"'The battle is over, save for a few pockets of fighting on the outskirts of the Pelennor. Even those will soon be done.\
\
'We have achieved victory this day, but it has cost us so much.'","Book 6, Chapter 8: On a Field of Red","Talk to Aragorn at the Threshold of the City","Aragorn is at the Threshold of the City.","'Let us take the field, ${PLAYER}. For Golodir.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","The sun is high in the sky and Pelennor is red with the blood of the slain, as the forces of Mordor prepare a final attack.","'What does it mean to fight, ${PLAYER}? I will fight to honour the sacrifice of those who no longer can, to honour that for which they fought. I will take the field with you, and I will make the Enemy remember my fallen friends. Tell me when you are ready, and we will make them fear us!'","Corunir is in the Ruin of Pel Dúven, waiting to take the field with you in memory of Golodir.","Talk to Corunir in the Ruin of Pel Dúven and take the field"},
[2206]={"Hide behind a stone and defeat any foes that approach","'I have no interest in this town, ${PLAYER}. These folk are the same as their brethren elsewhere, and have nothing helpful to tell us. I will seek the meaning of your dream in the wild.\
\
'You meet this man Horn at the Cuthstan. I will search elsewhere. Where did he say it was? The Wailing Hills, to the west?\
\
'Take care of yourself, ${PLAYER}. Horn may seem to be a friend, but his people are treacherous and he will prove no different. Keep him at the length of your arm.'","Horn is waiting for you by the Cuthstan, among the Wailing Hills, west of Stangard.\
\
You have dealt with an Orc interloper, and should speak now to Horn.","'I will meet you back at Stangard.'","A stone you can hide behind is near the Cuthstan, just to the east of Horn.\
\
Horn hears someone approaching, and he wants you to hide behind a stone to get the drop on the newcomer if it be a foe.","Another stone you can hide behind is near the Cuthstan, east of Horn.\
\
Horn hears someone approaching, and he wants you to hide behind a stone to get the drop on the newcomer if it be a foe.","'I know why you have come here, ${PLAYER}. There can be only one reason: it is clear you have been sent to help my people fight against the Khundolar. They are the descendants of the Easterling tribe that crossed the Great River five hundred years ago, and scouts report they have been seen on the far shore.\
\
'They seek to accomplish what their ancestors could not, and this time there will be no timely intervention, no final hour rescue.\
\
'We are on our own, ${PLAYER}, and that is why I did not forbid your Dunlending friend from entering Stangard, or seize the Rohirric sword she carries. Perhaps one day we were foes, and we may be again, but today I see Rohan threatened, and I thirst for allies to defend my homeland.\
\
'I was called disloyal and changeable in the hall of Théoden King, but that is not so. I love Rohan. I want only to protect her.'","Horn has asked to meet you by the Cuthstan in the Wailing Hills so he can talk to you about something.","Horn is waiting for you by the Cuthstan in the Wailing Hills, west of Stangard.\
\
The Rohirrim man Horn wants to speak with you at the Cuthstan about something.","'This man Horn wanted you to meet him at the Cuthstan? It is west of this village, it seems, among the Wailing Hills. I will not go with you. I will seek the meaning of your dream elsewhere, and find you if I discover it.'","'I am glad you have come, ${PLAYER}. I wanted to speak with you here, away from the prying eyes and listening ears of Stangard. There are friends in the village, but it is my worry that not all its men have the best interests of Rohan in their hearts.\
\
'The garrison at Stangard consists of men who had no other place in Rohan, for those who commit crimes but otherwise remain loyal to the King. They perform a length of service determined by the King's order, and upon its completion their past transgressions are forgiven.\
\
'My story is no different, ${PLAYER}, but my heart burns for Rohan. I see it threatened on all sides, and worst of all, I fear the greatest danger comes not from without but within. I have seen...'\
\
Horn stops suddenly.\
\
'Someone comes! Quickly, hide behind the stone over there and see if it is a friend or a foe.'","'Hide behind that stone over there and you can get the jump on him!'","Hide behind another stone and defeat any foes that approach","'Hide behind that other stone! Another Orc approaches, unless I miss my guess!'","Horn is waiting for you by the Cuthstan, among the Wailing Hills, west of Stangard.\
\
You have dealt with another Orc interloper, and should speak now to Horn.","Book 6, Chapter 8: Stone of Friendship","'That was well done, ${PLAYER}! I am worried by the increased number of Orcs that move alongside the river. They have been coming down from their holes in the Misty Mountains in great numbers of late. But they are not the only danger we face.\
\
'There are two shallow crossings across the Great River. Five hundred years ago, a tribe of Easterlings crossed into northern Gondor by the northernmost of these undeeps. The Steward of that land knew he did not have the men to repel them. He sent messengers into the north to seek for aid, but it seemed none could arrive in time to save Gondor.'\
\
The sound of approaching feet once more seizes Horn's attention.\
\
'We have another visitor, ${PLAYER}. Hide behind that other stone and see if it is another Orc!'","Horn is waiting for you in the village of Stangard, in Eorlsmead.\
\
You have spoken with Horn at the Cuthstan, and he wants to speak with you some more back in Stangard.","'You are quite an ally, my friend. Where was I? Yes, I remember now. The Steward of Gondor sent an urgent plea to the northern peoples, but the Easterling tribe pressed across the river before any help arrived.\
\
'But when all hope seemed lost, a new force arrived on the Field of Celebrant: the ancestors of my people, led by Eorl the Young. They destroyed the Easterlings, and in thanks the Steward of Gondor gave them the land of Calenardhon to dwell in, that is now called Rohan.\
\
'This statue was later erected as a sign of the friendship between the Eorlingas and the Men of Gondor, and my people have watched the crossings of the Great River ever since.'\
\
Horn looks up at the statue, and is quiet for a time.\
\
'I think the sword your Dunlending friend carries was at that battle, ${PLAYER}. I cannot be sure, but I feel it to be so. Why has it come back? \
\
'We should return to Stangard. The air grows chill, and we can talk more when we return. But remember what I have said.'"},
[2207]={"Bring the battlefield map and the heirloom to Cerdic","Edbrit is in the Rushgore at Aculf's Camp, south-east of Cerdic on the very edge of the swamp.\
\
While you were searching the battlefield of Parth Celebrant, Cerdic received word from Edbrit in the Rushgore about strange happenings.","Book 6, Chapter 9: Ancient Battlefield","Sift through debris beside the bridge to Ost Celebrant","'You will need to search the sites where the battle was fought five hundred years ago. Perhaps you will find some clue to defeating the Khundolar that now threaten this land.\
\
'Show the map I gave you to Cerdic. He is stationed at the watch-post on the road into Parth Celebrant. Perhaps the work will keep him from worrying about his family back in Rohan, if only for a few moments.'","'Now you should go to the swamps of the Rushgore. Look for Edbrit at Aculf's Camp, on the very edge of the swamp, south-east of here. He is a good sort, and was once an accomplished rider indeed! He is older now, but still as sharp as a sword.'","You sift through the debris near the base of the pillar but find nothing of interest","Sift through debris at the arrow-riddled patch of ground","Cerdic has marked three locations in Parth Celebrant on your map: the crumbled base of a pillar, an arrow-riddled patch of ground, and the river-bank by one of the bridges to Ost Celebrant. The first two sites are on the Field of Celebrant directly south of Cerdic, and the third site is to the south-east, alongside the river.\
\
Cerdic and Horn want you to search significant locations from the Battle of the Field of Celebrant.","Sift through debris by the base of the crumbled pillar","Cerdic is at the watch-post on the road into Parth Celebrant.\
\
Horn has given you a map of notable sites at the Battle of the Field of Celebrant to show to Cerdic.","'You have found nothing for me?'","'Search those three sites for anything that might help us. I do not think you will find anything, but if it is true that the Khundolar are gathering on the far side of the river we will need any advantage we can find.\
\
'Perhaps once the Khundolar Easterlings are routed my service will be ended, and I can return to Rohan. That is where I belong! A man should be with his wife and children. Horn tells me I protect them by being here, but three daughters! Had I sons perhaps I would worry less.\
\
'I mean... my wife would worry less. She worries, you know.'","Horn thinks you might find some way to help his people defeat the Khundolar by searching the site of the battle five hundred years ago where their Easterling ancestors were defeated.","Cerdic is at the watch-post on the road as it enters Parth Celebrant from Eorlsmead.\
\
You have found a bronze-worked heirloom at one of the sites of the battle with the Easterlings five hundred years ago, and should show it to Cerdic.","You sift through the debris and find a number of arrowheads, but nothing worth keeping","'The battlefield of Parth Celebrant may hold some clue to defeating the Khundolar. Their ancestors were routed by the timely arrival of the Eorlingas under Eorl the Young, but we have no such advantage in numbers this time. No one is coming to help us.\
\
'We must find some strategy to help us defeat the Khundolar, and sifting through the site of that battle may teach us something we can use against them.\
\
'I have marked this map with the location of the battle. Bring it to Cerdic at the road watch-post in Parth Celebrant, and he will guide you to places he has not already searched. I hope you will be kind to him. Cerdic has been long away from his wife and daughters, and sometimes he lets his worries master him. He is a good friend and true, even if his mind is not always on the task before him.'","'You are a ways from home, ${PLAYER}. This field of Celebrant was the site of a great battle five hundred years ago, where my ancestors rode to the aid of the Steward of Gondor against an invading Easterling tribe.\
\
'Ah, you have met Horn? You must already know of this battle, then. He is a young man, but he has an old man's fascination with history, and is perhaps too keen to speak of the past to anyone who will listen. He said too much to Théoden King, they say, and earned himself a place here at the garrison.\
\
'I have been here much longer than Horn, I regret to say. And me with three daughters left behind in Rohan! It has been too long since I could send word to them. My wife worries. She always has! I wish I was there to console her. She worries, you know.\
\
'Oh, I am sorry! You are not interested in my own travails. Horn gave you a map? Let me see it. Yes, I have already sifted through most of these locations. Let me mark these three for you. Examine those sites, and perhaps you will find something of use to us.'","You find a small bronze-worked heirloom among the debris","'What is this? What have you found?'\
\
Cerdic takes the bronze-worked heirloom you found among the debris at one of the battlefield locations, and turns it around in his hands.\
\
'You found this among the rocks? The years have not been kind to it. See how the bronze is bent here and here? A weapon did most of the work on it, and Time did the rest. I cannot tell what this used to be. Perhaps a decorative addition to a helmet?\
\
'This gives us no advantage, as far as I can see. But it is instructive to think of the things we leave behind. Was this Gondorian, or from a helm of the Eorlingas, or was it Easterling in make? Five hundred years later we cannot tell. Perhaps I will give it to my wife when I return to Rohan. She will be so proud of her Cerdic for bringing her such an interesting item!\
\
'I am sorry, ${PLAYER}! I became quite distracted. While you were away, I received word from a scout in the Rushgore of strange happenings in that swampy land. Find Edbrit at Aculf's Camp, south-east of here on the edge of the Rushgore, and see what has happened.'","Talk to Edbrit at Aculf's Camp in the Rushgore","'Cerdic sent you to me? I am not surprised! Many unusual things have happened in the Rushgore of late.'"},
[2208]={"Talk to survivors of the battle at the Threshold of the City","'${PLAYER}, I have good tidings! My son Elfmar has been avenged. The Olog-hai Thrúgrath has been slain! It seems a Ranger put an end to the vile beast, though the doing took his own life. I raise my sword to his memory. To Golodir, who slew Thrúgrath and avenged Elfmar!\
\
'I regret only that I did not slay the beast myself.'","Talk to Aragorn at the Threshold of the City","'I am just happy to be off the ships, ${PLAYER}. I was not made for the sailing-life. Indeed, I was still a little queasy for several minutes after we arrived at the field of battle, and was not at my very best.\
\
'The fighting set me right before long, but I hope wherever we go next the journey will be by land, and not by river!'","Duinhir is overcome with grief for his sons, and pays no mind to your words of comfort.","Survivors of a long and weary day have come to the Threshold of the City, nursing their wounds and mourning their dead.","'I do not want to see the field of the slain, ${PLAYER}, but I am powerless to turn my gaze from it. I am an old man, long-removed from the days of my youth, but still I linger while younger men await the burial mounds. Horn spoke to me of his duty as a man of Rohan on the ride to Gondor, and to my sorrow the cost of that duty is what I feared: he will never see Nona again.\
\
'Why am I still here, when so many good men are gone? What is to be my duty?'\
\
Gléowine sighs heavily and studies the burning fields.\
\
'It is the same as it ever was, ${PLAYER}: it is the responsibility of those who survive to remember those who have gone. It is the responsibility of the bard to record the names of the slain, so they will not be forgotten. I want the world to remember every man who died here: Harding of the Wold, Guthláf the Banner-bearer of Théoden, hot-tempered Fastred, and doughty Grimbold. I want the world to remember Horn, possessed of a musical heart but doomed by his duty.\
\
'They will just be names to the folk that come after, but to me they were men, good men who fought and died for the promise that their lands would once be safe. I will remember the names of the men who died here today. I do not want them to be forgotten.'","'${PLAYER}, can you tell me if you have seen Déorwine? He is a man of Rohan, yellow of beard and hair in a pony's tail. I met him during the battle and we fought side-by-side, but I have not seen him since the early hours of morning.'\
\
You tell Sakalbâr that Déorwine was slain when the Witch-king descended upon Théoden.\
\
'I feared that fate for him, ${PLAYER}, but I hoped it would not be so. Alas for Lady Winsig of Rohan! I wish it had been different. I am glad to have met Déorwine and call him friend, though it be for but a few moments during battle. It is cruel of war to make us bid farewell to friends so soon upon meeting them!'","'So much death... so many lives lost... and for what, ${PLAYER}? The armies of Mordor are repulsed, for now, but who can say they will not return? Is this the victory we bought with all of our dead? Good men will no longer return to their homes, and for what? A day of peace? A week? I... I cannot believe this is so!\
\
'The Ranger Halros took the death-blow that was meant for me, ${PLAYER}. I spoke only a few words to him, but now he is dead. Did he leave behind a wife? A child? What chain of events put his feet on the path that ended here on the blood-soaked Pelennor? Is that truly to be the end of his tale? Is this to be the end of mine?'\
\
Horn wears a haunted expression, his unblinking eyes glazed with tears. He does not seem to see you anymore.\
\
'I thought I was a man of Rohan, but if this is what it means to be such a man, I cannot bear it. That man is dead. Horn died on the Pelennor, and I will cry no tears for him. The old songs are just songs. They were never more than lies. I see the truth now.'","Aragorn is at the Threshold of the City.","A long and weary day of fighting has come to an end, but the victory comes at a very high cost.","'This is a hard day, but we have victory at the end of it. During the battle, I encountered men bearing the body of Théoden back to the city. They carried too a woman, Éowyn, niece of the King. They thought her dead, but I perceived that she lived; I sent them to bring her to the healers instead of the dead-house.\
\
'Her life is in their hands now.'","'I think Gothmog will find he values his life more highly now that it can be lost, ${PLAYER}. He will not dare to come forth in battle for some time. During that time we will need to determine our course of action, but I do not know what is best to do.\
\
'We need time to heal from our hurts, and to mourn our dead. We cannot take much time for it, and certainly not as much as they deserve, but still we must.'\
\
Aragorn smiles wryly.\
\
'Galadriel saw much of today, I think, but our actions and our choices still have meaning. Nothing is set. Your deeds today, and those of our fallen friends, mean much to me. Thank you for your courage and your loyalty, ${PLAYER}. I take neither for granted, and I appreciate them both. It will take both if we are to defy Sauron as we defied his servant Gothmog, and put an end to the evil he brews in his dark land.\
\
'I salute you, my friend! Let us heal our hurts. Let us remember our dead. And let us think of tomorrow. There is still much that must be done.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>To be continued...</rgb>","Book 6, Chapter 9: The City Stands","'Things might have gone differently, ${PLAYER}, were it not for many sacrifices. The city stands, and Gondor remains unbowed before the might of Mordor.\
\
'I am weary in both body and spirit, weighed down by sorrow. There is anger too, anger at the forces of evil that have taken so many of our friends from us, but it is the sorrow I feel most strongly at the end of this terrible day.'","'I heard his words, and my heart goes out to him, but I am saddened to hear Horn speak thus, ${PLAYER}. Where is the man who spoke to me of fighting for home and hearth, of fighting for the glory of Rohan and the honour of Théoden King? Where is the man who made the hard choice to leave Nona behind and make her world more safe than it was?\
\
'But Théoden is dead, and many others beside. I no longer recognize the Horn that spoke to me on the ride from Rohan and assuaged my own doubts; that Horn is dead, slain by the horrors of war if not by its weapons.\
\
'I do not want to forget that man, ${PLAYER}. I want the world to remember Horn as I knew him once. I want the world to remember every man who died here: Harding of the Wold, Guthláf the Banner-bearer of Théoden, hot-tempered Fastred and doughty Grimbold. They will just be names to the folk that come after, but to me they were men, good men who fought and died for the promise that their lands would once be safe! It was that promise that Horn tried to explain to me, but I did not understand it then. I think I understand it now.\
\
'I will remember the names of the men who died here today. I do not want them to be forgotten.'","'The battle is nearly over, ${PLAYER}, but who can say for certain how long this victory will last? My uncle and my liege has gone to his fathers, and I rejoice that his last day was filled with glorious deeds! Many beheld the might of the Mark on this day!'\
\
Éomer grows quiet, and when he speaks again he speaks in a low voice that only you can hear.\
\
'I will be King of Rohan now. Is it merely hope's fancy that I believe the Curse of Wyrgende has run, and is now ended? Much grief followed in the train of Fengel; his kin died and his kingdom fell from honour. But Théoden King lifted Rohan once more to the height, and mended the might of the Mark. Can you say it is not so?\
\
'Sleep easy, Wyrgende! You have been paid, and under the rule of Éomer no such injustice as was done to you will be done again.'"},
[2209]={"Aragorn te espera en una de las habitaciones de huéspedes de la Casa de Elrond.\
\
Elrond te advirtió sobre un mal creciente en Angmar y te pidió que hablaras con Aragorn.","La sombra de Angmar, mano de Sauron en el Norte, crece sin cesar, amenazando la paz y la seguridad de Eriador.","'Desearía que pudieras permanecer aquí, lejos de los problemas del mundo. Pero, por desgracia, el Enemigo no descansa, y nosotros tampoco podemos hacerlo.\
\
'Angmar crece en poder con cada día que pasa, y sin una forma de frenar su maldad, no tenemos esperanza de ganar esta guerra.\
\
'Habla con Aragorn. Te espera en una de las habitaciones de huéspedes a lo largo del camino que asciende por la ladera sur del Valle de Imladris.'","Libro 6, Prólogo: Volviendo la mirada hacia el Norte","''Ha llegado el momento de que abandones este lugar de refugio. Ve ahora y habla con Aragorn en una de las habitaciones de huéspedes a lo largo del camino que asciende por la ladera sur del Valle de Imladris.'","Habla con Aragorn en Rivendel.","'Con los asuntos resueltos aquí, es hora de volver nuestra atención hacia el norte.'"},
[2211]={"Aragorn's Pavilion is east of Minas Tirith on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle is concluded.","Find Elfhelm south-west of Aragorn's Pavilion, on the Pelennor Fields","Aragorn's pavilion is east of Minas Tirith on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle is concluded.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>A horse at the Threshold of the City during the Battle of Pelennor Fields will bring you After the Battle.</rgb>","The Battle of the Pelennor Fields has ended, and the people of Gondor begin the long process of recovering from their losses.","'Aragorn wishes to call a council of the captains in order to determine what to do next, but many of those he desires to have a voice are elsewhere on the fields or in the city. Daervunn of the North and Elfhelm of Rohan are not far to the south-west, if you can hasten their return to the pavilion.\
\
'I met Legolas the Elf on my way here, and I understand he is a friend of yours and was a companion of Mithrandir in the north. He spoke fair words to me, and I marveled that his journey brought him to these lands during time of war. Aragorn will want him to be present as well, and also his friend the Dwarf. I did not catch his name, but it seemed to me that Elf and Dwarf were bonded as friends and you might not find one without the other. That is unusual of itself, but these are strange times and we may well find our strongest friendships where we least expect them!'","Talk to Prince Imrahil at Aragorn's Pavilion","'Jump astride the horse over there and it will speed you from these killing-fields, taking you to the aftermath of the battle. I will speak to you again once we have established a pavilion at which I can plan our next step.\
\
'I do not think it would be right for me to enter the city at this time.'","Aragorn has need of his captains to determine his next course of action","Talk to Gimli at the city gates, west of Aragorn's Pavilion","'Aragorn will wish for Legolas the Elf and his Dwarf companion to be present at the council of the captains.'","'The battle is all but ended now, my friend. Jump astride the horse over there and it will speed you from these killing-fields, taking you to the aftermath of the battle. I will speak to you again once we have established a pavilion at which I can plan our next step.\
\
'I do not think it would be right for me to enter the city at this time.'","Legolas and Gimli smile warmly at your approach","'I have spoken with Gandalf and the Prince of Dol Amroth, and they are in agreement: we must decide our further course.'","'We have been to see Merry where he lies in the Houses of Healing and I am pleased to report that he will survive his wounds. We spoke with him for a time, and rested upon the wall. He is weary but the worst seems behind him.\
\
'Have you taken the opportunity to explore the city, ${PLAYER}? It is impressive, but there are not enough gardens here and the folk suffer for their lack. They need more that is green and growing! If Aragorn does claim his crown, my people will bring him birds to sing and trees to thrive, and this will be a better city for their presence!\
\
'We are on our way back to Aragorn's pavilion. I am eager to learn what he chooses for his next course.'","Talk to Legolas at the city gates, west of Aragorn's Pavilion","Legolas and Gimli are outside the city gate of Minas Tirith, after the battle.","Talk to Aragorn at his pavilion on the Pelennor Fields","Book 7, Chapter 1: Beginning to Heal","'Now that the battle is done, I have taken a good look at the stone-work of the city. Some of it is finely-made, but there is plenty of careless stone-work as well, and I see much that might be improved in the layout of the streets. Do not mistake me! Any dwarf would see the same.\
\
'Where should we go next? My axe has not yet had its fill, and I will wield it on behalf of Aragorn wherever he deems it most needed!'","'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. The battle is won but time is still short.'","'Daervunn of the North and Elfhelm of Rohan are not far to the south-west, if you can hasten their return to the pavilion.'","'I am happy to see you survived the battle, ${PLAYER}. So many of our friends did not. Loyal Halbarad, weary Golodir, young Celairant... I feel their loss keenly. Eight of my brothers fell upon the Pelennor in service to Aragorn, but if they had the choice of fighting for him once again you would find eight minds unchanged.\
\
'I will continue on to his pavilion, ${PLAYER}, and no matter his command I will see it done.'","Elfhelm and Daervunn are south-west of Aragorn's Pavilion on the Pelennor Fields.","Talk to Daervunn south-west of Aragorn's Pavilion","Travel to Aragorn's Pavilion east of the city, after the battle of Pelennor Fields","Talk to Elfhelm south-west of Aragorn's Pavilion","Find Legolas and Gimli at the city gates of Minas Tirith, west of Aragorn's Pavilion","'The battle is ended, ${PLAYER}. It was a victory hard-bought, and many good men fell upon this field and will not return to their homes. Alas for Elfmar, alas for my son! As much of the Elfward as remains mourns for him, and I weep with them!\
\
'This man Daervunn was a companion of mighty Golodir, who slew the Olog Thrúgrath, though he died in the doing. We have been sharing tales of our fallen, and it has eased my sorrow somewhat, though it cannot erase it. His people appear stern and grim at first, but I have marked that they speak warmly of their friends and the lands from which they hail. Perhaps they are not so very different from the men of the Mark as I supposed.\
\
'I will seek for more of the leaders of my people and go to the Ranger's pavilion at once.'","'I have established this pavilion so I may consult with my captains and plan our next step, for I do not think it would be meet for me to enter the city at this time. I have spoken with Gandalf and the Prince of Dol Amroth, and they are in agreement: we must decide our further course.'","Prince Imrahil is at Aragorn's Pavilion, east of Minas Tirith, after the Battle of Pelennor Fields.","Elfhelm and Daervunn are deep in conversation, but they look up as you approach"},
[2212]={"'La sombra pesa fuertemente aquí, pero incluso aquí, puede hallarse esperanza.'","Libro 7, Capítulo 1: Oculto en la Sombra","Lorniel está dentro del edificio en Gath Forthnír.\
\
Areneth te dijo que hablaras con Lorniel, hija de Golodir.","Encuentra a los Montaraces de Gath Forthnír.","Tras descubrir el secreto de las piedras vigilantes de Rammas Deluon, Corunir te envió a las regiones orientales de Angmar, en busca de los Montaraces y Montañeses de Aughaire que habían marchado para derribar el creciente poder de Angmar. Encontraste al Montaraz Braigiar en el puesto enano de Gabilshathûr, en Malenhad.","'¿Dices que Lorniel vive? ¡Debes regresar a Gath Forthnír de inmediato y hablar con ella!'","'Lorniel está dentro. Querrá hablar contigo.'","'¿Vienes de parte de Corunir, por medio de Braigiar? ¡Entonces ${PLAYERNAME:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]}, y que sea un buen encuentro! En verdad, necesitamos tu ayuda. Estos últimos años casi nos han vencido.\
\
'Pero no me corresponde a mí contarte nuestras penas. Deberías entrar y hablar con Lorniel, la hija de Golodir.'","'Hagas lo que hagas, asegúrate de que la Corona de Hierro nunca se entere de Gath Forthnír.'","'No creo que sólo la buena fortuna te haya traído hasta aquí, mi buen ${RACE}. Ven, tenemos mucho de qué hablar.'","'Es una lástima que Corunir no pudiera templar su corazón contra los Vigilantes de Rammas Deluon. El poder de las piedras vigilantes es terrible. Muchos de los Montañeses intentaron huir de regreso por Rammas Deluon y perecieron.\
\
'Marchamos adelante, pero antes de llegar a Carn Dûm, fuimos atacados por Orcos y criaturas aún más terribles. Golodir se perdió y nuestras filas se dispersaron. El escaso remanente que queda apenas ha logrado evitar las trampas del Enemigo durante estos últimos años, pero temo que Angmar se ha vuelto demasiado fuerte, y no podremos ocultarnos para siempre.\
\
'He sabido que un grupo de mis hermanos está acampado en un lugar llamado Gath Forthnír, muy al norte, en las regiones orientales de Himbar. Ve con ellos, si lo deseas, y bríndales la ayuda que puedas.'","'El Enemigo es fuerte, sin duda, pero su orgullo lo llevará a la caída.'","Gath Forthnír se encuentra en algún lugar muy al norte de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Braigiar te ha enviado a encontrar y prestar ayuda a los supervivientes de la compañía de Golodir en el campamento de Gath Forthnír.","'Tu ayuda es necesaria entre mis hermanos en Gath Forthnír. ¡No te demores!'"},
[2213]={"¿Has visitado ya la colina de Cerin Amroth, ${PLAYER}? Deberías hacerlo, pues es hermosa en cualquier época del año.\
\
Búscala en el centro de Lothlórien; es tanto bella como pacífica, y Milwen estará encantada de contarte parte de su historia. Búscala junto al arco al oeste de la colina de Cerin Amroth.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Si no has completado ya el Volumen II, Libro 6, se recomienda, aunque no es obligatorio, que lo hagas antes de comenzar esta misión.</rgb>","'Como ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} de los Elfos de Lórien, deberías visitar la colina de Cerin Amroth al menos una vez. Es un lugar de tal belleza que el descanso y la contemplación surgen fácilmente.\
\
Habla con Milwen junto al arco al oeste de la colina y te contará parte de su historia. Cerin Amroth está en el centro de Lórien, lejos al noreste de este talan.'","Milwen está junto al arco al oeste de la colina de Cerin Amroth, ubicada en el centro de Lothlórien, lejos al noreste de Talan Haldir y al este de Echad Andestel.\
\
Te han dicho que hables con Milwen en la colina de Cerin Amroth, dentro de los bosques de Lórien.","Has sido reconocido como ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} de Lothlórien gracias a tus esfuerzos en nombre de los Elfos, y deberías viajar a la colina de Cerin Amroth para reafirmar esa amistad.","'Eres bienvenido en Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}, por la amistad que has demostrado y tus esfuerzos contra los orcos y otros peligros en Moria.'\
\
'Pasa bajo los lindes del bosque, hacia el noreste, y viaja a la colina de Cerin Amroth en el centro de Lothlórien; es tanto bella como pacífica, y Milwen estará encantada de contarte parte de su historia. Búscala junto al arco al oeste de la colina de Cerin Amroth, muy al noreste de aquí, dentro del bosque.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Si no has completado ya el Volumen II, Libro 6, se recomienda, aunque no es obligatorio, que lo hagas antes de comenzar esta misión.</rgb>","'Como ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} de los Elfos de Lórien, deberías visitar la colina de Cerin Amroth al menos una vez. Es un lugar de tal belleza que el descanso y la contemplación surgen fácilmente.\
\
Habla con Milwen junto al arco al oeste de la colina y te contará parte de su historia. Cerin Amroth está en el centro de Lórien, muy al este de aquí, pero al norte de Caras Galadhon.'","Habla con Milwen","'¡${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]} a Cerin Amroth, ! Pocos han tenido la dicha de verla en estos tiempos de decadencia, su belleza es solo un vestigio de la majestad que alguna vez tuvo. Porque en este montículo Amroth, Señor de Lórien, construyó su casa, en los días antes de que su amor se perdiera y él mismo desapareciera de la Tierra Media.\
\
Se dice que cuando el viento del sur sopla sobre la colina, si escuchas el sonido de las gaviotas, aún puedes oír a Amroth llamando, llamando a su amor perdido Nimrodel. Pero ella nunca regresó.\
\
Milwen se detiene un momento, pero con una ligera risa se recupera.\
\
¡No te pongas triste, ! Cerin Amroth debe recordarte días más felices. ¡Camina sobre la hierba y alégrate! Tus penas no te seguirán aquí.'","Libro 7, Capítulo 1: La colina de Cerin Amroth","'Eres bienvenido en Lothlórien, ${PLAYER}, por la amistad que has demostrado y tus esfuerzos contra los orcos y otros peligros en Moria.'\
\
'Pasa bajo los lindes del bosque, hacia el este, y viaja a la colina de Cerin Amroth en el centro de Lothlórien; es tanto bella como pacífica, y Milwen estará encantada de contarte parte de su historia. Búscala junto al arco al oeste de la colina de Cerin Amroth.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Si no has completado ya el Volumen II, Libro 6, se recomienda, aunque no es obligatorio, que lo hagas antes de comenzar esta misión.</rgb>","'Como amigo de los Elfos de Lórien, deberías visitar la colina de Cerin Amroth al menos una vez. Es un lugar de tal belleza que el descanso y la contemplación surgen fácilmente.\
\
Habla con Milwen junto al arco al oeste de la colina y te contará parte de su historia. Cerin Amroth está en el centro de Lórien, al norte de Caras Galadhon.'"},
[2214]={"'I cannot picture this fountain in Lhanuch. My people would not build such a thing. What would be the point?'","'I hope you enjoyed your respite, ${PLAYER}. It brings me sadness to tell you it must be ended.'","Book 7, Chapter 1: The Land of the Elf-queen","Nona observes the mighty mallorn trees, but says nothing","'This city could only be built among these great trees. It is no lie to tell you I have never seen trees of such size as these.'","Nona has recovered from her experience in the Rushgore, and is now interested in learning more about the Elf-woods of Lothlórien before you both leave.","Nona smiles weakly at you.\
\
'They tell me I was close to death, ${PLAYER}. I remember very little of it. I remember a creeping shadow, and a chill cold as ice, and...'\
\
Her eyes narrow.\
\
'The men of that town would not heal me unless I gave them my sword. But you spoke against it, and so did that man. What was his name? Horn? I should thank him for that kindness, even though he is of the horse-folk and we should not trust him too far.\
\
'The Lady of the Elf-woods told me I could see her city before we departed, if I were well enough. I tell you I am! This place is a marvel, though my own people would not wish to live here. Bring me to some of the notable locations of this city, ${PLAYER}. We have some time before we must depart, do we not?'","Talk to Galadriel in her garden","Talk to Anglamel on the Telain Melthin","Talk to Luidhros on the Telain Galadhrim","Nona is by the ladder down from the flets on which stand the House of Celeborn.\
\
Nona is waiting for you to show her around Caras Galadhon.","'When did the Elves find the time to construct such a place? It is a wonder, I will grant you that. But I prefer the homes of my people.'","Having shown Nona around Caras Galadhon, you should now speak with Galadriel in her garden as she requested.","Talk to Húrien at Celúrlin, the White Fountain of Caras Galadhon","Talk to Nona atop the ladder leading down from the flet near the House of Celeborn","Nona admires the delicate carving of the swan fountain","'Galadriel wanted to speak with you in her garden? For an Elf, she seems to have a great deal of inner strength. She reminds me of a matriarch of the Algraig.'","'If your friend is a typical member of her race, Dunlendings come from strong stock. She has made a more complete recovery than I expected of her.\
\
'Speak to her at the ladder down from these flets, and show her around the city of the Galadhrim. I have made it known she has my permission to see Caras Galadhon.'","'This is Celúrlin, the white fountain of Caras Galadhon. It is a place for quiet contemplation, where Elves of Lórien are free to enjoy the sound of the water in the pool and the feel of soft breezes on the skin.'\
\
Húrien looks at Nona dismissively, and you can tell that despite Galadriel's words, not every Elf is pleased to have the Dunlending girl within the borders of Lórien.\
\
'Others can admire the fountain as well, of course,' Húrien finishes with a sniff.","Nona looks out into the void between flets and says nothing","Now that Galadriel has given permission for Nona to explore Caras Galadhon, you should bring her to see several of its notable locations: Celúrlin, the White Fountain of Caras Galadhon, and several of the flets where much of the work of the Elves is done: the Telain Galadhrim and Telain Melthin.","'The mallorn trees of Lothlórien are the mightiest to be found anywhere in these, the waning years of Middle-earth. It was once not so, but the passage of time and the spreading of darkness has caused much that was once great to wither and diminish.\
\
'So it would be with the Elves, were we to stay. Already we have stayed too long.'\
\
Luidhros looks sideways at Nona, but she seems not to notice.\
\
'It will soon be the time of Man, and who can say how that race will deal with the challenges that lie ahead?\
\
'These mellyrn support the Telain Galadhrim, the flets on which much of the work in our city is done. Without them, little could be accomplished. I hope the same will not be said of the Elves when we have departed.'","'I am sorry, we see so few visitors to Caras Galadhon that our hospitality is perhaps not what it should be. It must seem a very confusing place, with flets built on multiple levels of the great mellyrn, with winding stairs and bridges crossing the breezy gaps.'\
\
Anglamel laughs, a delicate and musical sound. You catch Nona's brief scowl at the airy tones, but Anglamel does not.\
\
'I have heard it said Caras Galadhon is as maze-like as the cities of the dwarves, but if this slander is true at least our maze is above the ground, lit by the glow of the sun and cool glimmer of the stars! I would forgive any amount of confusion for those dual boons!'","'Within the woods of Lórien, guests of Lord Celeborn can recover from their hurts and the toils of a long road. It is my hope this reprieve was of use to you, ${PLAYER}. In these dark days, no time of rest is as long as we might wish it to be. It is nearly time for you to depart again.'\
\
With one motion of a lovely arm, Galadriel directs your gaze to the flets that cling to the bole of the tree.\
\
'Nona has made as full a recovery as she could have, and a greater one than I expected of her. She is waiting for you at the ladder down from these flets. I have made it known that it is my will she be permitted free movement within the hedges of Caras Galadhon. Show her the city of the Galadhrim, ${PLAYER}. We will speak in my garden when she is satisfied with her exploration of what this city has to offer.'"},
[2215]={"Libro 7, Capítulo 2: Cruzando la Sombra","'¿Fuiste enviado por la mujer del sur? Aquí... toma este pergamino. Mi gente es desconfiada. ¡Debo irme de inmediato!'","'¿Obtuviste el pergamino de Raghnall?'","'¿Encontraste a Raghnall? ¡Ah! ¡Ese debe ser el pergamino del que habló! Déjame verlo.'","'¡Apresúrate, ${PLAYER}... no sabemos cuánto tiempo podrá permanecer oculto Raghnall! Debes ir a hablar con él de inmediato. Debería estar escondido en algún lugar al sur de Bail Cátharnakh.'","Reúnete con Raghnall al sur de Bail Cátharnakh, al oeste de Gath Forthnír.\
\
Lorniel te dijo que había oído hablar de un Montañés llamado Raghnall, que buscaba abandonar el servicio de Angmar y podría tener información que le permita acceder a Carn Dûm.","'¡Déjame ahora! Mi gente me matará si nos ven juntos. Lleva el pergamino a la mujer, a tu Lorniel... ella sabrá qué hacer con él.'","Lorniel se encuentra dentro de Gath Forthnír, al este de Bail Cátharnakh.\
\
Te reuniste con Raghnall y él te entregó un pergamino que explica cómo forjar una llave para las puertas de Carn Dûm.","Lleva el pergamino a Lorniel.","'Si vienes de parte de Braigiar, no tengo duda de que escuchaste que mi padre se perdió. En efecto, lo perdimos, pero no creo que haya sido asesinado. He recibido informes de nuestros aliados que indican que fue capturado y está retenido en las mazmorras de Carn Dûm.\
\
'Uno de esos aliados, un Montañés comprensivo de las tribus hostiles del este llamado Raghnall, afirma haber conseguido un pergamino de las bibliotecas de Carn Dûm que explica cómo acceder a la ciudad. Si puedes reunirte con Raghnall y obtener el pergamino, sería un gran paso hacia la liberación de mi padre de las garras del Enemigo.\
\
'Pero ten cuidado... él estará esperando justo al sur de Bail Cátharnakh, una aldea de Montañeses que se encuentra al suroeste de Gath Forthnír. La mayoría de los Montañeses allí están al servicio de la Corona de Hierro.'","Lorniel te dijo que cree que su padre aún vive, prisionero en las mazmorras de Carn Dûm. Espera encontrar una forma de entrar en la terrible ciudad y rescatarlo."},
[2216]={"'This is not the easy decision, ${PLAYER}, but I think it is the right one. We cannot defeat Sauron in battle, but we must draw his gaze and keep it upon us for as long as we can. All our hopes lie now on Frodo and Sam, and we must do what we can to aid them from afar.'","Aragorn is at his pavilion east of Minas Tirith, after the Battle of Pelennor Fields.","'A decision made without all of the information is undermined even as it is made, ${PLAYER}. When we meet in council, some things that were kept secret must be revealed if we are to properly weigh our choices. I hope you will think no less of me for keeping these secrets, my friend. You are a good friend and true, and if I kept you in the dark, I did so only because at the time I thought it was needed.\
\
'Speak to me when you are ready to meet.'","Aragorn is at his pavilion, east of Minas Tirith, after the Battle of Pelennor Fields.","Book 7, Chapter 2: The Council of the Captains","Aragorn has called a council of the captains to decide his next course.","Talk to Aragorn at his pavilion and help him determine his course","'It is time to decide our course.'","Talk to Aragorn at his pavilion on the Pelennor Fields"},
[2217]={"Galadriel has seen disturbing visions in her mirror, and is worried about what it means for your mutual friends.","Peer into the Mirror of Galadriel and experience 'Session: The Point of Decision' or read the shortened account instead","The Fellowship of the Ring comes at last to the most dangerous decision it must make, on which the fate of Middle-earth will be decided. Frodo Baggins walks alone above Parth Galen, wrestling with the difficult choice, but when one of his companions is seized by apparent madness, the Ringbearer is put to his most difficult test so far...","Talk to Galadriel in her garden","'I spoke to you once of the danger that awaited our mutual friends on their road, ${PLAYER}. Their circumstances are hidden to me, but I have seen enough in my mirror to worry.\
\
'Those few of the Wise who know of their errand have known a simple truth since they departed: as they move further south, they move closer to a point of decision they can delay, but not avoid. They cannot leave the Great River without making this decision: do they continue south and east to Mordor, or do they pass through cities of Men and thereby take a longer road to the fire?\
\
'The Ring-bearer must go to Mordor, but who will choose to go with him? I fear for the company, ${PLAYER}. Peer into my mirror and see if the visions for you are as troubling as they are for Galadriel.'","You tell Galadriel what you saw within her mirror, and a look of sadness crosses her face.\
\
'The mirror shows many things, ${PLAYER}, and not all of them come to pass. But this is one possibility among many, and it is a troubling one to be certain.\
\
'They may have need of your help. I want you to travel south along the river Anduin, ${PLAYER}, and to see what has befallen our mutual friends. None of the visions I have seen in the waters give me any hope that they have avoided the dangers into which they walk. If you can aid them in even the smallest way, it may be enough.\
\
'Nona should go with you, if she still desires to do so. I have known her for just a short time, but I do not think she wishes for anything but to adventure with you. Let her be an aid to you on a dangerous road!'","Book 7, Chapter 2: The Point of Decision","'Peer into the mirror, and see if the visions you see are as troubling as those it has given to me.'","Galadriel is in her garden in Caras Galadhon.\
\
You have peered into her mirror, and should now speak to Galadriel about what you have seen.","You peer into the waters of Galadriel's mirror, and indistinct images begin to appear of distant friends and worrisome signs...","The Mirror of Galadriel is within her garden, in Caras Galadhon.\
\
Galadriel has asked you to peer into her mirror and see what awaits the Fellowship on their journey south."},
[2218]={"Elrond el Medio Elfo está en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Laerdan, también incapaz de traducir el pergamino, te envió a Rivendel para hablar con Elrond el Medio Elfo.","'¿Qué es esto? ¿Fuiste enviado por la hija de Golodir y por el Elfo Laerdan? Qué extraño destino te ha traído hasta aquí. La Sombra de Angmar ha crecido junto con la Sombra en el Este.\
\
'Dame el pergamino... Desentrañaré este misterio por ti.'","Lleva el pergamino a Elrond el Medio Elfo.","Laerdan está en Gath Forthnír.\
\
Lorniel te sugirió que buscaras al Elfo llamado Laerdan con la esperanza de descubrir lo que revela el pergamino de Raghnall.","'¿Qué te trae a Rivendel, ${PLAYER}? ¿Qué misión te ocupa?'","'¿Elrond el Medio Elfo? Sí, debí haberlo pensado yo mismo. Es un largo viaje, pero uno que debes emprender.'","'Lleva el pergamino a Laerdan, ${PLAYER}. Tal vez tenga algún conocimiento de la Lengua Negra.'","'No puedo ayudarte con este pergamino, pues la Lengua Negra no es mi campo de estudio. Llévalo a Elrond de Rivendel.'","Recuperaste el pergamino de Raghnall, pero estaba escrito en Lengua Negra, la cual Lorniel no puede traducir.","'Por desgracia, nunca me tomé el tiempo de aprender los crueles murmullos de los orcos. No deseo hablar con ellos por ningún medio salvo mi espada.\
\
'Si este pergamino proviene de Carn Dûm, Elrond el Medio Elfo podría tener interés en él, y sin duda conoce la Lengua Negra. Ve a Rivendel y busca al Maestro de La Última Morada, si deseas conocer la respuesta a tu enigma.'","'Temo que hayamos sido engañados, ${PLAYER}, pues este pergamino está escrito en Lengua Negra y puede que no diga nada de valor. No puedo asegurarlo, ya que no es una lengua que conozca. Aun así, deseo saber qué dice.\
\
'Tal vez el Elfo Laerdan tenga algún conocimiento de esta escritura. Es un viejo amigo de mi padre y se encuentra en Gath Forthnír.\
\
'Lleva el pergamino con él y pídele su opinión. Si puede ayudarnos a liberar a mi padre, debemos descubrir sus secretos de inmediato.'","Libro 7, Capítulo 3: Abriendo el Camino"},
[2219]={"Find the herald north-west of the city gate, in the First Circle <rgb=#00FF00>(2012 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","Find the herald north of the city gate, in the First Circle <rgb=#00FF00>(1978 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","The herald vouches for a number of soldiers to join Aragorn's army","Aragorn has sent you to find heralds on the Pelennor and in the First Circle of Minas Tirith and set them to calling for soldiers willing to join him on the march to Mordor.","Talk to Éomer at Aragorn's Pavilion","Find the herald inside the city gate of Minas Tirith <rgb=#00FF00>(1698 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","There is a herald north-west of the city gate of Minas Tirith, in the First Circle.\
\
Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.","Talk to Prince Imrahil at Aragorn's Pavilion","Read aloud Aragorn's call for soldiers <rgb=#00FF00>(2003 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","'The Prince of Dol Amroth believes that Aragorn's army will be as a stinging fly to the forces of the Dark Lord? He is not wrong that these seven thousands are a mere pittance to the numbers Sauron houses within the Black Land, but it seems to me that Imrahil has wrongly judged the mind of the Dark Lord.\
\
'Yes, we go to sting the Dark Lord. But he will not squish us, for all our buzzing. No, he will seek to trap the fly and take the sting, all unaware of our deception. On that deception all of our fortunes rest. It is the secret fly that bears the most dangerous sting of all for Sauron, and let him remain blind to it until it be too late!'","Talk to Aragorn at his pavilion on the Pelennor Fields <rgb=#00FF00>(2021 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","'The men I sent marching through Lossarnach from Pelargir have drawn nigh the city; so too have the men I commanded to follow the Corsair ships in smaller watercraft up the Anduin. They loiter now, waiting for orders. Let us give them direction, and hope that they make good of their word when they find that direction is \\qeast, toward the shadow.\\q\
\
'Take this call for soldiers, and read it to heralds on the field and throughout the First Circle of the city. The heralds will then bring its message to the waiting soldiers, and float the number of men that will march with us.'","Find the herald north-west of Aragorn's Pavilion <rgb=#00FF00>(0 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","Book 7, Chapter 3: The Great Jest","Find the herald north-west of the city gate, in the First Circle <rgb=#00FF00>(2007 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","Find the herald outside the city gate of Minas Tirith <rgb=#00FF00>(462 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","Talk to Elfhelm at Aragorn's Pavilion","Read aloud Aragorn's call for soldiers <rgb=#00FF00>(1802 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","There is a herald inside the city gate of Minas Tirith.\
\
Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.","Mithrandir is at Aragorn's Pavilion east of Minas Tirith, after the Battle of Pelennor Fields.","'My swan-knights have scoured the nearby lands of Gondor for fighting men. They report that three and a half thousands will march for Mordor with Aragorn. It is as fine a total as any for which you might hope, and proves the courage of Gondor, so fresh from battle and still hungry for more.\
\
'But this must be the greatest jest in all the history of Gondor, ${PLAYER}! We march to assail the Black Gate and the impenetrable land of Mordor, and with fewer men than might have formed just the vanguard of its army in the mighty days.\
\
'It brings to my mind a child threatening a mail-clad knight with a toy bow, or a buzzing fly seeking to sting a man working in the hot sun. The Dark Lord will smile and knock down the child, or squish the fly in his palm, and that will be the end of it. What else is there to do but laugh at the jest, ${PLAYER}?'","Imrahil, Éomer, and Elfhelm have returned to Aragorn's Pavilion with a count of the soldiers they have attained for Aragorn's march to Mordor.","The herald waits for your message","Find the herald inside the city gate of Minas Tirith <rgb=#00FF00>(1450 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","There is a herald north of the city gate of Minas Tirith, in the First Circle.\
\
Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.","Read aloud Aragorn's call for soldiers <rgb=#00FF00>(1203 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","'So it is decided, for better or ill. The men I sent marching through Lossarnach from Pelargir have drawn nigh the city; so too have the men I commanded to follow the Corsair ships in smaller watercraft up the Anduin. They loiter now, waiting for orders. Let us give them direction, and hope that they make good of their word when they find that direction is \\qeast, toward the shadow.\\q\
\
'Take this call for soldiers, and read it to heralds on the field and throughout the First Circle of the city. The heralds will then bring its message to the waiting soldiers, and float the number of men that will march with us.'","Read aloud Aragorn's call for soldiers <rgb=#00FF00>(0 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","There is a herald on the Pelennor Fields north-west of Aragorn's Pavilion.\
\
Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.","'Much has been asked of my men already, but Rohan will not abandon her friends. Many among the Rohirrim were unhorsed during the battle lately ended, but they are still war-worthy and will not let that stay their weapons! Five hundreds of these will follow behind, and I will lead five hundreds on horse alongside.'","Aragorn is at his pavilion east of Minas Tirith, after the Battle of Pelennor Fields.","Talk to Mithrandir at Aragorn's Pavilion","Read aloud Aragorn's call for soldiers <rgb=#00FF00>(2021 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>","'How many men were the heralds able to reach with their voices? More than two thousands, you say? That is very good, and matches my hopes. These other commanders have also done work to gather soldiers for the march. Speak to them and see how large a host we have assembled; it need not be enough to wage war upon Mordor, but it must be large enough to threaten battle!'","There is a herald outside the city gate of Minas Tirith.\
\
Aragorn sent you to read his call for more soldiers to heralds who can reach the ears of the men that have now arrived at the city.","'Éomer King has given to me the command of the main force of the Rohirrim, some three thousands still a-horse. It is to the West Road we will go, to hold it against the enemy that is still in Anórien.'","Find the herald outside the city gate of Minas Tirith <rgb=#00FF00>(1003 Soldiers Pledged to Aragorn)</rgb>"},
[2220]={"'You have done as I asked? Good! The most important step of a journey occurs before you even leave home: the preparations for your departure.\
\
'Make sure your weapons are cleaned and ready. The last time I travelled south, which was some weeks ago, Orcs were gathering on the far shore of Anduin. We may need to face them.\
\
'Unfortunately, I lent my bow to Fimloth at Haldirith on my return from that journey. Perhaps we can stop by her encampment when we depart and I can recover my bow from her? I will use a spare until then, but there is nothing quite like your own familiar weapons, is there? Sigileth spoke often of her knives, Lanchigil and Egnassigil, and I feel the same way about my bow, though it has no name. My sister was always better with names.\
\
'But now you should return to the House of Celeborn and speak with your Dunlending friend. Tell her we are almost ready to leave.'","Talk to Faengalph and arrange for a boat and paddles for the journey","'Return to your Dunlending friend near the House of Celeborn and tell her we are nearly ready to depart.'","Nona is on the flets near the House of Celeborn.\
\
Corudan has sent you to tell Nona you are ready to leave.","'The Lady has spoken to me about this, ${PLAYER}, and I would refuse her nothing. But there is another reason I would help you.'\
\
Corudan looks at you, his eyes shining with a curious look of gratitude.\
\
'You were a friend to my sister Sigileth in Mirkwood. When the Hidden Guard and the Golden Host journeyed to the fastness of Dol Guldur, you fought alongside Sigileth. How many times did you save her life, or she yours? I do not know, but I am certain it was more than once. I wish that the tides of fate had swept the two of you together during that final assault on the tower, rather than apart, for had the two of you been together on the stairs perhaps she would have returned from Mirkwood.\
\
'But it was not to be. That is the way of things. I would be honoured to accompany you south along the Anduin. Sigileth's friends are mine as well. We will need supplies. Boats and lembas and paddles... speak to Bordhrist and Faengalph about acquiring such things as we will need. Bordhrist will be on Telain Galadhrim, and Faengalph will be near the surrounding hedge beneath Telain Glorelloth, not far from the entrance to Caras Galadhon.'","Galadriel wants you to journey south along the river Anduin to see what fate has befallen the Fellowship, but for that you will need a guide.","'You are preparing for a journey down the Anduin? You have come to the correct Elf, ${PLAYER}. I will supply you with enough lembas and other goods to make such a journey comfortably.\
\
'Travelling by boat will require you to disembark occasionally. There is a portage way you will need to take around the rapids of Sarn Gebir... do not be so foolish as to traverse those in the boats! And of course you will need to beach them before you reach the Falls of Rauros. It is a long climb down the cliff-face, but I have heard there was a way that was used of old.\
\
'I will give you enough lembas and other foodstuffs for two weeks. Corudan can cover that distance in five or six days. That should suffice. Namárië.'","Talk to Nona near the House of Celeborn when you are ready to depart on your southward journey","Corudan is waiting on Telain Neduil for you to return from arranging for a boat and supplies for the journey down the Anduin.","Bordhrist is on Telain Galadhrim, and Faengalph is near the surrounding hedge not far from the entrance to Caras Galadhon, beneath Telain Glorelloth.","Book 7, Chapter 3: The River-walker","'You have brought me nothing?'","'We will need supplies if we are to make a journey down the Anduin as far as the Falls of Rauros. Find Bordhrist and Faengalph, and they will equip us for the journey. Bordhrist is on Telain Galadhrim, and Faengalph is near the surrounding hedge, not far from the entrance to Caras Galadhon, beneath Telain Glorelloth.'","'I will give you enough lembas and other foodstuffs for two weeks. Corudan can cover that distance in five or six days. That should suffice. Namárië.'","Corudan is on Telain Neduil in the eastern side of Caras Galadhon.\
\
Galadriel has sent you to recruit Corudan as a guide along the Anduin as you investigate what has happened to the Fellowship.","'You need a boat for navigating the Anduin? Yes, I will provide one, and paddles beside. How many will be going with you?'\
\
You tell Faengalph the composition of your party, and she nods.\
\
'The Lady Galadriel is wise to send Corudan with you. He is called the River-walker, you know, and it is a name truly given: he knows the lands on either side of Anduin better than any Elf I know.\
\
'His sister Sigileth perished in Dol Guldur. We were not close, she and I, for she had a temper unlike anyone else and to me she was always sharp and stern. It is a shame what happened to her, even so. I am certain she did great damage to her enemies before she fell, and that must be a consolation to Corudan in his grief.\
\
'The boat and the paddles will be ready when the time comes for your departure, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Bordhrist and receive supplies of food for the journey","'The boat and the paddles will be ready when the time comes for your departure, ${PLAYER}.'","'You will need a guide to bring you to the Falls of Rauros, but few of my people ever travel that far. No, do not shake your head in frustration! There is a guide who will suffice. His name is Corudan, and he is the elder brother of Sigileth.'\
\
Galadriel smiles sadly.\
\
'Yes, I see you remember our fierce champion. Without her twin knives and the skill with which she wielded them, the efforts of the Golden Host might have come to naught. Her death in the Battle of the Tower is cause for grief in all who knew her. You will find her brother is cut from similar cloth, but if Corudan shares her ability he does not share her temperament. Find him on Telain Neduil, on the eastern side of Caras Galadhon, and tell him you need him as a guide along the Anduin. He is not called \\qRiver-walker\\q for naught: he is more familiar with the lands through which the Anduin flows than any Elf in Lórien.'","'I followed you here on the behest of a dream, ${PLAYER}. I will follow you wherever our road leads.\
\
'If our adventure ended today I would already have quite a tale to tell Suvulch on my return. I cannot imagine what awaits us, but it will only add to the record of our deeds!\
\
'Wadu's sword is thirsty for more adventure as well. If we come across more Easterlings or their fell ally, as we did in the swamps, I will be more ready than I was last time!'","'You should find Corudan on Telain Neduil and tell him that you have need of his skills as a guide as you journey along the Anduin. Telain Neduil is on the eastern side of Caras Galadhon.'","Return to Corudan on Telain Neduil"},
