\
You tell Faengalph the composition of your party, and she nods.\
\
'The Lady Galadriel is wise to send Corudan with you. He is called the River-walker, you know, and it is a name truly given: he knows the lands on either side of Anduin better than any Elf I know.\
\
'The boat and the paddles will be ready when the time comes for your departure, ${PLAYER}.'","'We will need supplies if we are to make a journey down the Anduin as far as the Falls of Rauros. Find Bordhrist and Faengalph, and they will equip us for the journey. Bordhrist is on Telain Galadhrim, and Faengalph is near the surrounding hedge, not far from the entrance to Caras Galadhon, beneath Telain Glorelloth.'","'I will give you enough lembas and other foodstuffs for two weeks. Corudan can cover that distance in five or six days. That should suffice. Namárië.'","Corudan is on Telain Neduil in the eastern side of Caras Galadhon.\
\
Galadriel has sent you to recruit Corudan as a guide along the Anduin as you investigate what has happened to the Fellowship.","'You will need a guide to bring you to the Falls of Rauros, but few of my people ever travel that far. No, do not shake your head in frustration! There is a guide who will suffice. His name is Corudan, and he is not called \\qRiver-walker\\q for naught: he is more familiar with the lands through which the Anduin flows than any Elf in Lórien.\
\
'Find him on Telain Neduil, on the eastern side of Caras Galadhon, and tell him you need him as a guide along the Anduin.'","Talk to Bordhrist and receive supplies of food for the journey","'The boat and the paddles will be ready when the time comes for your departure, ${PLAYER}.'","'I followed you here on the behest of a dream, ${PLAYER}. I will follow you wherever our road leads.\
\
'If our adventure ended today I would already have quite a tale to tell Suvulch on my return. I cannot imagine what awaits us, but it will only add to the record of our deeds!\
\
'Wadu's sword is thirsty for more adventure as well. If we come across more Easterlings or their fell ally, as we did in the swamps, I will be more ready than I was last time!'","'You should find Corudan on Telain Neduil and tell him that you have need of his skills as a guide as you journey along the Anduin. Telain Neduil is on the eastern side of Caras Galadhon.'","Return to Corudan on Telain Neduil"},
[2222]={"Go to the western entrance of Osgiliath","'Perhaps you could suggest to my father that he and I return home? Or maybe, if that is too far, we could turn our waggon in the direction of Imloth Melui and make sure the ladies of that place fare well in our absence?'","Go to the eastern entrance of Osgiliath","'After you gather four trumpeters, travel to the western gate of Osgiliath and Aragorn's army will begin its march.'","'We have moved in secrecy ever since I came to know you, ${PLAYER}. It was a secrecy borne of necessity, for we needed every advantage we might attain in our struggle against the Dark Lord. Whispered councils gave rise to hidden errands and close-guarded conspiracies.\
\
'But no longer! While Frodo continues his quest in the shadows, Aragorn strides into the light and he must draw Sauron's gaze to him, and away from the real purpose, with every means at his disposal. Let the departure of Aragorn's army be a loud one and snare the attention of the Dark Lord!\
\
'Wars are fought with weapons, but this battle for Sauron's Eye will be fought with noise and tumult, with musical instruments and those who wield them. Walk the Pelennor and find men who wield trumpets of silver and brass. They will announce the coming of the King as loudly and as often as they can, and perhaps this loud departure will serve as a shield for Frodo and Sam as they walk in the Black Land.\
\
'After you gather four trumpeters, travel to the western gate of Osgiliath and Aragorn's army will begin its march. I will see you at the eastern gate of the city after the army is on the march.'","Bandron is at the western entrance to Osgiliath.\
\
You gathered a number of trumpeters to travel with Aragorn's army and announce the coming of King Elessar, and now should speak with some familiar faces at the entrance to Osgiliath.","Talk to Culang on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle","'There are still enemies hiding in Osgiliath. If you were to defeat some of these foes, I would appreciate it!'","As you approach the east gate, you see Mithrandir astride Shadowfax","'Oh... hello, ${PLAYER}. I did not think I would see you again this soon. I had rather hoped my father would let us remain awhile longer in Imloth Melui, but when he heard that the battle was over he made us depart at once. The flowers of Imloth Melui are breath-taking and beautiful... and the roses are quite a sight as well!\
\
'My father promised Lord Angbor that we would bring our stock of Cemenduril liquor to the Houses of Healing as soon as we were able, and we have done so, also satisfying our writ with Galengam. But now my father has that look in his eye once again, and he has made us come to broken Osgiliath over the Anduin, instead of heading for home.\
\
'Perhaps you could suggest that he and I return home? Or maybe, if that is too far, we could turn our waggon in the direction of Imloth Melui and make sure the ladies of that place fare well in our absence?'","Trumpeters can be found on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle.\
\
Mithrandir has asked you to find trumpeters throughout the Pelennor Fields that might be willing to announce the departure of Aragorn's army from Minas Tirith with great noise and tumult.","Aragorn's army is passing through Osgiliath, and Mithrandir intended to meet you at the eastern gate of the city.","Talk to Bandron at the west entrance of Osgiliath","'I was inside the city when our friends from Rohan joined the battle, and my heart soared to see their charge. So inspired was I that I mounted a horse and followed the Prince of Dol Amroth and his knights through the gate and into the throng of the battle!\
\
'I was near at hand to Théoden, King of Rohan, when the great beast descended and spelled his doom. I saw then the most beautiful woman I have ever seen, or ever will see; she stood between her fallen lord and the dreadful foe, and slew that terrible creature in defence of her king! A great evil took me then and I swooned. I think I dreamed, but I cannot remember the details of it.\
\
'When I awoke, I was in the Houses of Healing. Friends tell me I was saved by the hands of a stranger, of curious visage and few words. I would find this man and give him my thanks, but he has left no sign. There are whispers that King Elessar may have worked his healing arts in the Houses, but who would believe such a thing? No King would trouble himself with my hurts, surely?\
\
'In any case, I will be pleased to sound my horn on behalf of the King!'","'You have caused an impressive amount of noise, ${PLAYER}! The trumpeters will announce the arrival of King Elessar as his army marches through Ithilien. None will miss these tidings!\
\
'Sauron will not fail to heed this march, ${PLAYER}. The Prince of Dol Amroth has rightly pointed out that the size of this army is too small to pose a serious challenge to the host that lies within Mordor, but that in itself will draw his gaze hither. He will think that Aragorn possesses the Ring, and believes that it will bring him the power he needs to overthrow Sauron. He will think this because that is the action he would take, were their positions reversed.\
\
'The army will march slowly, but it will march loudly, and that is the best gift we can give to Frodo right now. I hope beyond hope that he is able to make use of that gift, and that it does not come too late for him.'","'Ah, ${PLAYER}! Any good friend of Lord Angbor would be a friend of mine, but you were my friend first, I daresay! I have not forgotten our encounter in Tarlang's Neck. We met at a low ebb in my fortunes, any man would admit that, but I am proud to say that those fortunes have changed for the better. And all because of my son! He has always made me proud, that one, and I defy any ${RACE} to doubt it!\
\
'We did need to leave Imloth Melui in rather a hurry, but that is no fault of my Nethadan. I did not like many of the glances the fair lasses of that place gave to my boy, and I deem that should the battle have kept us there any longer I might have lost my apprentice and gained a daughter-of-the-law, and that does not bring in the coins! No, we left at the first opportunity, and now another opportunity has presented itself. Do you know what that opportunity is?'\
\
Bandron pauses for dramatic emphasis, waiting for you to guess. At last he continues with a shout of triumph.\
\
'Nails, ${PLAYER}! It just so happens that with tremendous foresight, my clever and enterprising son Nethadan has caused us to come into possession of two barrels full of nails, as I am sure you remember, and do you know what is in great demand following a battle? Nails of the very sort we possess in such quantities, and which we can sell to the craftsmen repairing the city and the bridges at a better than usual rate! Just doing my part as a man of Gondor, my friend, and if it allows me to set up my own shop in competition with Galengam, well, that is the merest coincidence.\
\
'There are still enemies hiding in Osgiliath, however. If you were to defeat some of these foes, I would appreciate it!'","'I have mastered many musical instruments, but I am most skilled, and loudest, with the trumpet! It will be my pleasure to sound mine at volume on behalf of the King! O, to think I have lived to see a king once more in Gondor!\
\
'My heart leaps at the thought of it! You will have no problem getting me to start; getting me to stop will be another thing entirely!'","Talk to Ruhír on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle","Talk to Celebrom on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle","'I fought in the battle and saw more than my share of death as the afternoon wore on toward evening. Sometime during the waning hours I lost both my sword and the trumpet I carried on my hip, and suffered a knock upon the head by a heavy club.\
\
'When I came to again, my sword was gone. It must have been taken by a foe or a friend who thought I was slain. My trumpet lay by my feet, battered and bruised even as I was, but still whole. I have taken that as a sign, and now I will be a trumpeter and not a swordsman.\
\
'I will be honoured to wind my horn to announce the coming of King Elessar, ${PLAYER}. Let the sound strike fear into the hearts of our enemies and give them such a fright they will never again threaten Gondor!'","Nethadan is at the western entrance to Osgiliath.\
\
You gathered a number of trumpeters to travel with Aragorn's army and announce the coming of King Elessar, and now should speak with some familiar faces at the entrance to Osgiliath.","Defeated enemies remaining in Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Book 7, Chapter 4: A Loud Departure","Mithrandir asked you to travel to the western gate of Osgiliath after you gathered four trumpeters.","Some enemies are still hiding in Osgiliath, waiting to jump out and attack the craftsmen responsible for repairing the city and the bridges.\
\
Bandron asked you to defeat some of the enemies lurking in Osgiliath in order to protect his interests.","Defeat enemies remaining in Osgiliath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Limlaer on the Pelennor Fields, after the battle","Talk to Mithrandir at the eastern entrance of Osgiliath","You see some familiar faces within the west entrance of Osgiliath","'You seek trumpeters to proclaim the presence of Aragorn, now that he has revealed his true claim? I am not as practiced as some others in Gondor, for I have only lately begun to learn the skill, but I would be honoured to use my meagre ability to announce the arrival of my chief and lord.\
\
'My friend Areneth bore this trumpet on his person when he was slain in Tûr Morva. I picked it up to save it from the hands of treacherous men, and thought I might teach myself its use as a means of remembering poor Areneth.\
\
'I will use it to proclaim the coming of King Elessar, and it will remind me of the friends that gave their lives so this day might happen.'","'Thank you for your help, my good friend! I will need to think of a name for my shop, if I am no longer to work for Galengam. I like the sound of \\qBandron and Son, Purveyors of Fine Goods.\\q What do you think?'","Talk to Nethadan at the west entrance of Osgiliath","Mithrandir has given you a surprising directive: one of attention-seeking noise rather than the maintenance of secrecy!","'Wars are fought with weapons, but this battle for Sauron's Eye will be fought with noise and tumult, with musical instruments and those who wield them. Walk the Pelennor and find men who wield trumpets of silver and brass. They will announce the coming of the King as loudly and as often as they can, and perhaps this loud departure will serve as a shield for Frodo and Sam as they walk in the Black Land.'","Mithrandir is astride Shadowfax at the east gate of Osgiliath."},
[2223]={"Corudan is at Haldirith, in Thinglad.\
\
You have searched for the Orc that took Corudan's bow, but did not find it.","The first stage of your journey south with Corudan and Nona involves a brief stop in Thinglad to collect Corudan's bow.","Orcs can be found throughout Thinglad, alongside the Great River. Defeat them while Corudan and Nona do the same, and perhaps you will find Corudan's lost bow.","You defeated an Orc in Thinglad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You did not find Corudan's bow? We did not either. He seemed surprised, but I was not. Whatever Orc took the bow must have known an Elf would come looking for it, and fled the area.\
\
'This Orc is lucky it did! For its hunters numbered three: ${RACE}, Uch-lûth, and Elf! Flight alone could have saved it. I am sorry Corudan does not have his favourite bow, but I still enjoyed the hunt.\
\
'Do you think you can humour me on one count, ${PLAYER}? I understand we must hurry, but this should not take long.'","'This is a setback. This Elf gave his bow to someone, and that Elf lost it. This is why none but me wield Wadu's sword.'","Talk to Corudan in Haldirith","Nona looks at you with disappointment on her face, and you can tell that she has not found Corudan's bow either.","'Nona is quite a warrior. I did not expect it!'","Nona is in Haldirith, in Thinglad.\
\
You should speak to Nona about her experience hunting with Corudan.","'Search Thinglad for Orcs! The Dunlending girl and I will do the same. Whoever first finds my bow will be the victor in our little game.'","Corudan is in Thinglad, in the Great River.\
\
You have come to Thinglad with Nona and Corudan, and should speak to Corudan, who wanted to recover the bow he lent to Fimloth.","Nona looks around Haldirith with interest, but says nothing.","Defeat Orcs in Thinglad while Nona and Corudan hunt for the bow as well (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You did not find the bow? Nona and I did not either. The Orc that seized it must have already left this area. Pity. This spare bow does not fire as accurately as my other did. I am still a deadly shot, ${PLAYER}. Do not worry on that score!\
\
'Did you know how dangerous Nona is in combat? I did not think the Dunlendings were more than barbaric hill-dwelling Men, but she is a deadly warrior indeed! I underestimated her, and will not do so again. If we are surprised by Orcs as we journey further along the Anduin, I will be glad to have her along!'","Talk to Nona in Haldirith","'I am grateful for the healing arts of Galadriel and her people, and for the lady's willingness for me to see her city. But there is something strange about this place, and I must tell you the truth: it is no place for me. I want my feet upon the ground and my foes in front of me. This land of Elves is a long way from Enedwaith, a long way from my people.\
\
'I am ready to depart, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps things will feel more familiar to me as we journey south along the river.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You will automatically travel to Haldirith in the Great River when you accept this quest.</rgb>","Book 7, Chapter 4: Along the Shore","'I am not pleased about this, ${PLAYER}. I lent Fimloth my favourite bow to use while I remained in Lothlórien, and now she has lost it!'\
\
Corudan lowers his voice and turns to his apologetic friend.\
\
'No, Fimloth, I am not upset. If those Orcs were as numerous as you report, you were right to flee. A bow is a bow, and the lives of my friends come first! I will search the woods of Thinglad for the Orc that picked it up as you escaped.\
\
'Are you of a mind to join the hunt, ${PLAYER}? Your Dunlending friend has already agreed to fight the Orcs with me as well. Perhaps we can make a game of it! The first of us to find my lost bow will be the victor, but I shall be the happiest of all to have the bow back in my hands!'"},
[2224]={"'Busca al Señor Dwalin en la Mansión de Thorin y dale saludos de mi parte. Es amigo de Rivendel y te ayudará.'","'Las esperanzas de Lorniel no eran del todo en vano, pues este pergamino revela efectivamente una forma de atravesar las puertas de Carn Dûm. El pergamino habla de una llave especial, forjada con un hierro negro y siniestro que solo se encuentra en las fosas corruptas de Angmar... y de los secretos de su fabricación.\
\
'Creo que una llave así podría hacerse de mithril, pues la fuerza de la plata de Moria podría superar cualquier resistencia que ofrezca la cerradura. Lamentablemente, no tenemos mithril disponible. Tal vez deberías buscar la ayuda del Señor Dwalin en la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin.\
\
'Los enanos conocen mejor que nadie los secretos del mithril... son ellos con quienes deberías hablar. He transcrito el contenido del pergamino al Oestron... los enanos no deberían tener dificultad para leerlo.'","Libro 7, Capítulo 4: Maestría Enana","'Saludos, ${RACE}. ¿Vienes de parte de Elrond, de Rivendel? Entonces contarás con la ayuda del Pueblo de Durin. Déjame ver ese pergamino...'","Dwalin está en la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin\
\
Elrond transcribió el pergamino al Oestron, pero te indicó que buscaras la ayuda de Dwalin y los enanos de Ered Luin para forjar la llave de paso a Carn Dûm","'Buen día. ¿Qué puede hacer el Pueblo de Durin por ti?'","Viajaste a Rivendel para buscar la ayuda de Elrond el Medio Elfo en la traducción del pergamino de Raghnall. El Maestro de La Última Morada te dio una bienvenida misteriosa, pero se ofreció a ayudarte.","Lleva el pergamino a Dwalin"},
[2225]={"Talk to Horn in Stangard","'You will find Horn atop the hill. Take him with you and begone! This is no place for him, or for you!'","'You have brought me nothing.'","Corudan is at Haldirith, in Thinglad.","You tell Nona that Horn has been cast out of Stangard and is no longer welcome there.\
\
'This confirms all I ever suspected about the horse-lords, ${PLAYER}! They are cruel even to their own, and are not deserving of our sympathies! I will speak with Horn, thank him for his words on my behalf, and give him my sorrow that he has suffered for me. But I will also tell him that he is now better off, and need shed no tears for his lost fellows!\
\
'We will be ready to leave when Corudan says we should leave. Speak with him when you are ready to go.'","Collect Horn's harp from the Stangard tavern","Talk to Afic at the gate of Stangard to learn of Horn's whereabouts","Collect Horn's writing supplies from Wada's house","Horn is no longer welcome in Stangard, and has asked you to collect his harp from the Stangard Tavern, and his writing supplies from Wada's house.","Bring his harp and writing supplies to Horn in Stangard","'When we were last in this region, I was wounded in the swamp, and you brought me to the nearby outpost of the horse-lords. I was a wounded enemy to everyone there save one: the Rohirrim man called Horn. He spoke on my behalf, and when you suggested that I be taken to the Elf-woods for healing...'\
\
You interrupt Nona at this point and tell her that it was actually Horn's idea. A confused look crosses her face.\
\
'Really? Well, that is one more thing for which I should thank him. And that is what I want, ${PLAYER}: a brief detour to the outpost of Stangard so I can give him my thanks. Perhaps you can have him meet me here. I do not think I would be welcome once again within their walls.'","'I am very sorry that Horn gave up his life at that outpost on my behalf, but he will be better off with us. The horse-lords do not deserve him.\
\
'Speak to Corudan when you are ready to go.'","'Thank you for bringing me these. I am not welcome in Stangard, but where can I go? By order of Théoden King I am not to return to Rohan until my term of service in Stangard is finished.'\
\
Horn looks uncomfortable.\
\
'Where are you travelling, ${PLAYER}? Could you use another companion on the road? I do not wish to intrude, but I believe my place is with you and with the Dunlending girl for whom I gave up... well. It was no life I gave up. I only did what was right, though my fellows fail to see it.'\
\
You tell Horn that he is welcome to travel with you as far as he will.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I owe you a great deal for this. An aimless life would ill suit me. Your goals are now mine, and the dangers you face I will face as well.'","Nona has requested that you stop by the Rohirrim outpost of Stangard so she can thank Horn for speaking on her behalf.","'I do not have many possessions, but if you bring me my harp and writing supplies, I can leave Stangard. My harp is in the tavern, and the writing supplies are in Wada's house, where I have been staying.\
\
'I must leave Stangard by sunrise.'","'Our band of companions grows: a Dunlending girl, a Rohirrim man, an Elf, and you. It sounds like a joke, does it not?'","Talk to Corudan at Haldirith","Book 7, Chapter 5: A Stop In Stangard","'I want to thank the Rohirrim man Horn for speaking on my behalf, ${PLAYER}. Go to Stangard and tell him to meet me here. I cannot think I am welcome within the walls of that outpost.'","Collected Horn's writing supplies","'I am in your debt, my friend. Let us go to see the other members of your party!'","Horn is in Stangard, waiting for you to bring him the items for which he asked.","Nona is in Haldirith, in Thinglad.\
\
Horn has decided to travel with you, and now you should go back to Nona so she can be told.","'I did not think to see you again, ${PLAYER}. How is the Dunlending girl? Did she survive?'\
\
You tell Horn that the healing arts of Galadriel were sufficient, and that Nona has come to Thinglad and wishes to thank him in person for his kind words and actions.\
\
'Oh, I see... I am glad.'\
\
Horn seems conflicted about something, and when you ask him if everything is all right he sighs heavily.\
\
'It seems there is no place for me anymore, ${PLAYER}. I am no longer welcome in Stangard. My fellows feel that I have been somehow tainted by stepping foot within the Elf-woods, and by speaking on behalf of a Dunlending... well, they no longer trust me. They want me to leave by sunrise tomorrow.'\
\
You ask if there is anything you can do to help.\
\
'Well, I do not have many possessions. If you bring me my harp and my writing supplies, I will be ready to go. My harp is in the tavern, and my writing supplies are in Wada's house, where I have been staying.'","You should speak with Afic, the guard at the gate of Stangard, about meeting with Horn.","Talk to Nona at Haldirith","'Oh. It's you. Still travelling with unsavoury types, are you?'\
\
Afic looks you up and down, and the disgust on his face is clear.\
\
'You are looking for Horn? Good! Take him with you! Take him and begone! You will find him up the hill.'","Corudan looks at you silently, brooding about his lost bow.","Collected Horn's Harp","Horn is atop the hill of Stangard.\
\
You have spoken with Afic, the guard at the gate of Stangard, and he had some inexplicably harsh words concerning Horn."},
[2226]={"'Representatives from every land stand with the Host of the West: Elves, dwarves, Men, and hobbits. Young Master Brandybuck recovers still from his wounds, secure in the Houses of Healing, so it falls to Peregrin Took to ride with Aragorn as a representative of the Shirefolk.\
\
'He rides just ahead, to the east, if you wish to speak with him on the way to the Cross-roads of the King.'","Henneth Annûn is located north of the Cross-roads, in North Ithilien.\
\
Aragorn asked you to travel ahead of the host and come to the Ranger hideout at Henneth Annûn.","Aragorn is at the Cross-roads of the King, in Ithilien.","Tell Limlaer to announce the coming of the king","'The armies of the Enemy have done what they could to despoil the beauty of this land, but Ithilien resists their depravations. It was once called \\qthe garden of Gondor,\\q and so may it be again!\
\
'I have set trumpeters at each of the roads that leave this meeting of the ways. As Gandalf recommended, we will sound our arrival and our intentions! Speak to each of the trumpeters and they will herald our coming!\
\
'Once this is done, you should move ahead of the host and defeat any enemies you find lurking still in the wild. Men of Gondor have told me that a Ranger encampment is not far to the north, at a place called Henneth Annûn. We will meet there.'","Talk to Golasdín at Henneth Annûn","You realize you are being watched moments before a Ranger emerges from hiding","Talk to Aragorn at the cross-roads","Defeated foes throughout North Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Peregrin Took east of Osgiliath","'The march to the Black Gate will bring Aragorn's host through Ithilien and Dagorlad. Travel first to the Cross-roads of the King, east of Osgiliath.'","Trumpeters can be found at each of the roads that leave the Cross-roads of the King. After they have been told to sound their instruments, Aragorn asked you to defeat foes in North Ithilien and make your way to the Ranger hideout at Henneth Annûn.","Tell Celebrom to announce the coming of the king","Peregrin Took is east of Osgiliath, before the road rises into the hills of Ithilien.\
\
Gandalf told you that Pippin is riding with the Host of the West, and might want to speak to you.","The land of Ithilien was green and beautiful before the armies of Sauron came. Does it retain any of the loveliness it once possessed?","Tell Ruhír to announce the coming of the king","The Cross-roads of the King are east of Osgiliath, in Ithilien.\
\
Aragorn and the Host of the West are marching into Ithilien, and plan to stop at the Cross-roads.","Find the Ranger encampment at Henneth Annûn, in North Ithilien","'If you are a scout for King Elessar's host, you have my welcome. It is my dearest hope that he intends to make such a racket as his army moves through Ithilien, for there are no foes that could fail to notice his progress hither.'","Tell Culang to announce the coming of the king","'Peregrin Took rides just ahead, to the east, if you wish to speak with him on the way to the Cross-roads of the King.'","Defeat foes throughout North Ithilien (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Aragorn has called a halt at the Cross-roads of the King","Go to the cross-roads in North Ithilien","'I have set trumpeters at each of the roads that leave this meeting of the ways. As Gandalf recommended, we will sound our arrival and our intentions! Speak to each of the trumpeters and they will herald our coming!\
\
'Once this is done, you should move ahead of the host and defeat any enemies you find lurking still in the wild. Men of Gondor have told me that a Ranger encampment is not far to the north, at a place called Henneth Annûn. We will meet there.'","Henneth Annûn is located far north of the Cross-roads, in North Ithilien.\
\
Aragorn asked you to move ahead of the host and come to the Ranger camp at Henneth Annûn.","'Men of Gondor have told me that a Ranger encampment is not far to the north, at a place called Henneth Annûn. We will meet there.'","Book 7, Chapter 5: The Garden of Gondor","'Hullo, ${PLAYER}. What have I gotten myself into now, I wonder? Aragorn says that it is good for every land to be represented when we go to confront the Enemy in Mordor, but I don't feel like a fit representative for the Shire.\
\
'I wish Merry were here, but he is still recovering in the city. He has done his share of great deeds, but what have I done? Gandalf says I might have saved Faramir's life, and I am glad that whatever small part I played might have helped, but I certainly didn't feel like much of a hero at the time!'"},
[2227]={"Dwalin se puede encontrar en la Mansión de Thorin en Ered Luin.\
\
Litli tomó el mithril de ti y comenzó a calentarlo. Sin embargo, mencionó que dar forma al mithril será un problema, uno que quizás Dwalin pueda resolver.","'¡Saludos, amigo! ¿En qué puedo ayudarte? ¿Dices que has venido desde las Montañas Azules para recuperar esa vieja llave arruinada que encontramos entre las pertenencias de los Montebruno?\
\
'Es cierto que se encontró entre cosas que creemos eran de Calder Cob, que es la única razón por la que la guardé. Es bastante inútil.\
\
'Aquí... que te ayude en tus esfuerzos.'","Litli se puede encontrar junto a la forja cerca del trono dla Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Ahora que has recuperado el mithril y la llave de Éogan, Litli, uno de los herreros de Dwalin, puede comenzar a trabajar en la llave.","Dwalin se puede encontrar en la Mansión de Thorin en Ered Luin.\
\
Dwalin te envió a conseguir una pepita de mithril de la Casa Mathom en la Comarca y una llave para ayudar a hacer un molde de Jon Helecharroyo en Archet.","El Guardián Brombard Colazorro está en la Casa Mathom en Cavada Grande, en la parte occidental de la Comarca. Jon Helecharroyo está en el pueblo de Archet, al noreste de Bree.\
\
Dwalin te informó que necesita una pepita de mithril, que podría estar en posesión de la Casa Mathom en la Comarca, y una llave para hacer un molde, que podría obtenerse de Jon Helecharroyo, el nuevo Capitán de Archet.","Lleva los materiales recolectados a Dwalin","'¡Hola! ¿En qué puedo ayudarte? ¿Una pepita de mithril? Nunca he oído hablar de eso.\
\
'¡Oh! ¡Te refieres a ese trozo de plata que el viejo Bilbo trajo de sus aventuras! Pensé que era demasiado ligero para ser plata real.\
\
'Bueno, entonces debe tener poco valor, y no veo por qué deberíamos conservarlo. Eres muy bienvenido a llevarlo... aquí.'","Dwalin, Maestro de la Mansión de Thorin, ha accedido a ayudarte a forjar la llave, pero faltan algunos componentes vitales.","'¿Un martillo de forja de mithril? ¡Bah! He visto uno solo en toda mi vida. Y no he visto uno desde... oh querido....'","Llevar los materiales recolectados a Litli","'¿Pudiste obtener el mithril o la llave?'","'Que podamos forjar esta llave, no tengo dudas, pero hay algunos artículos que necesitaremos antes de poder comenzar. Las instrucciones del Maestro Elrond dicen que necesitamos mithril, pero no hay ninguno disponible en las Montañas Azules. Además, necesitaremos algo para hacer un molde.\
\
'Ahora, uno de los regalos que Bilbo llevó de vuelta de la Montaña Solitaria fue una pepita de mithril. Dudo que entendiera su valor, así que probablemente lo dejó atrás cuando regresó a Rivendel. Sin embargo, puede que lo haya dado a la Casa Mathom en Cavada Grande. Quizás el Guardián de la Casa Mathom pueda ayudarte con eso.\
\
'En cuanto al molde, Atli Spiderbane envió un mensaje de que los guardias de Archet encontraron una llave arruinada entre los cuerpos de los Montebruno. Jon Helecharroyo aún puede tenerla. Si su líder era de Angmar, como he oído, puede que esa llave sea justo lo que necesitamos para hacer el molde.'","'Así que eres el que Dwalin estaba mencionando. Veo que tienes el mithril y esa llave repugnante de los Angmarim. Muy bien, entonces, dámelos. ¡Comenzaré a fundir ese mithril!\
\
'El problema es que habrá un problema al dar forma a este metal. Quizás deberías hablar con Dwalin.'","'¿Hmm? ¿Por qué me molestas?'","'Me sorprende que hayas viajado tan lejos por esa llave. Que te sirva bien.'","'Ve ahora, no te quedes parado aquí. Lleva el mithril y esa llave que reuniste a Litli. Está junto a la forja cerca del trono.'","'Espero que ese metal plateado te sea útil. Realmente no era tan interesante... ni siquiera lo tenía expuesto.'","Libro 7, Capítulo 5: Lo que se Necesita","'Fundir ese mithril llevará un poco más de tiempo. Por supuesto, si no tengo un martillo de forja para trabajarlo, no importa cuánto tiempo lleve fundirlo.\
\
'Si conseguir esta llave es importante para ti, hazle saber a Dwalin que voy a necesitar un martillo de forja de mithril.'","'¡Ah! ¡Tenía razón! Los hobbits tenían efectivamente la pepita de Bilbo. Espero que no tuvieras que lastimar a nadie para conseguirlo....\
\
'¿Colazorro ni siquiera sabía lo que era? Bueno, no debería sorprenderme... un hobbit no conocería verdaderamente los metales preciosos si le dieras un tesoro.\
\
'Y veo que recuperaste la llave de Jon Helecharroyo. Tenemos todo lo que necesitamos. Ve ahora y lleva estos objetos a Litli junto a la forja allí. Él comenzará con la llave.'","'Con gusto te ayudaré con esa llave, pero primero debes obtener la pepita de mithril y la llave arruinada que necesitamos.'"},
[2229]={"Explore the main cavern of Henneth Annûn","'From Henneth Annûn we have harried many a foe, passing like shadows through the Window of the Sunset and back again under cover of darkness. As you are a friend to the King and to Gondor, I say that you may see what you will of our secret retreat. Find the descending tunnel, the main cavern, and the look-out point.\
\
'But I warn you! Do not set foot into the Forbidden Pool. That is an insult to us and we have never allowed it unpunished.'","Aragorn is outside Henneth Annûn, and wishes to speak to you.\
\
You have learned that Orcs and Easterlings aim to ambush the Host of the West as it travels through Cirith Negen, and should report their plan to Aragorn.","The refuge of the Rangers is not luxurious, but it is comfortable enough","The Rangers of Ithilien scout the wood-lands for servants of the Enemy, striking from their hidden camp at Henneth Annûn. In this way, they can help clear the way for the Host of the West as it makes its way toward Mordor.","'Our enemies seek to ambush King Elessar as he marches north, and they plan to use our own ambush location for that purpose! What an insult to Gondor that would be!'","Orndil thought he saw something to the north-east.\
\
You should investigate further.","'That is what I suspected! Our enemies seek to ambush King Elessar as he marches north, and they plan to use our own ambush location for that purpose! What an insult to Gondor that would be!'","The hidden path is narrow and treacherous, and descends into the earth","Orndil nods at you as you catch up with him","Orndil was right: there are signs the enemy seeks to ambush Aragorn at Cirith Negen","From this vantage point you can see the Forbidden Pool and much of the surrounding area","Nearby Rangers scowl angrily and chide you with disapproval and disappointment","Explore the look-out point at the highest point of Henneth Annûn","Talk to Orndil at the look-out spot","Book 7, Chapter 6: The Window on the West","Explore the descending tunnel to Henneth Annûn","'Do you see that? Look to the distance and see!'","Orndil is north-east of Henneth Annûn, and wishes to speak with you.","Find the look-out spot further to the north-east that Orndil mentioned","Golasdín welcomed you to explore the hidden path, the cave hideout, and the look-out at Henneth Annûn. He warned you not to enter the Forbidden Pool.","'I have spoken with King Elessar and given him some advice. He is different than I expected, but no less wise!'","You spy movement to the north-east, but cannot tell for certain","Talk to Aragorn outside Henneth Annûn","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> into the distance","The Rangers of Ithilien have a useful scouting location to the north-east of Henneth Annûn.\
\
Aragorn asked you to find Orndil and to scout ahead of the host for dangers posed by lurking enemies.","'Did you see that? I believe I saw movement over there, among the trees to the north-east. Let us make our way there and see if our eyes play tricks upon us, or if there is some foe lying in wait!\
\
'That is the pass of Cirith Negen, and my people have long used it to surprise our foes. They may seek to turn the tables upon us, and use our own ambush spot against us!'","'Travel further ahead to the north-east, and look for signs of trouble. Golasdín tells me that there is a location to the north-east that might offer a good vantage point of the road ahead. Orndil, a Ranger of Ithilien, went to that location and might have seen something.'","Talk to Aragorn at Henneth Annûn","'The ways of secrecy are ending, it seems. King Elessar marches to Mordor in a great procession and with the sounding of trumpets, and so too must the Rangers of Ithilien give up some of their secrets. Still, those ways do not go easily!\
\
'From Henneth Annûn we have harried many a foe, passing like shadows through the Window of the Sunset and back again under cover of darkness. As you are a friend to the King and to Gondor, I say that you may see what you will of our secret retreat. Find the descending tunnel, the main cavern, and the look-out point.\
\
'But I warn you! Do not set foot into the Forbidden Pool. That is an insult to us and we have never allowed it unpunished.'","Aragorn is outside Henneth Annûn, and wishes to speak to you.","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not enter the Forbidden Pool</rgb>","The Ranger Orndil nods at you as you arrive at his look-out spot","'Our journey through Ithilien has reassured me that it remains beautiful, but this sword cuts with both edges, for enemies can still lurk unseen among the pastoral beauty of this land. As the Rangers of Ithilien surprised their foes, so too can those foes seek to surprise us.\
\
'Travel further ahead to the north-east, and look for signs of trouble. Golasdín tells me that there is a location to the north-east that might offer a good vantage point of the road ahead. Orndil, a Ranger of Ithilien, went to that location and might have seen something.'","'Thank you for the report, ${PLAYER}. I wondered if our foes would seek to mount a final resistance to our march, and it seems as if they will attempt it at Cirith Negen.\
\
'The Rangers of Ithilien have spoken to me of that pass. They have often used it to surprise unwary foes, and it was there they recently ambushed a marching force accompanied by a fearsome Mûmak and drove the beast from the bonds of its handlers. The creature stampeded from Cirith Negen and away from the war, and now there is no whisper of it.\
\
'Will the Orcs seek to do the same to the Host of the West? They cannot be allowed to succeed at this, ${PLAYER}.'","Find the look-out spot north-east of Henneth Annûn that Aragorn mentioned"},
[2230]={"Has recogido el Martillo de Thrór","Libro 7, Capítulo 6: El Martillo de Thrór","Reclama el Martillo de Thrór de la tumba de Skorgrím","'No puedo forjar tu llave hasta que tenga un martillo de moldeado.'","'Lleva el martillo a Litli de inmediato, para que pueda comenzar a trabajar en tu llave.'","Obtuviste la pepita de mithril y la llave arruinada como pidió Dwalin, pero su herrero, Litli, te informó que aún falta algo más para trabajar el mithril.","Litli se encuentra junto a las forjas, cerca del trono de la Mansión de Thorin, en Ered Luin.\
\
Debes llevar el martillo que encontraste a Litli, para que pueda forjar la llave que necesitas.","El Martillo de Thrór se encuentra en la tumba de Skorgrím Duramano. La tumba está al sureste de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Dwalin te dijo que necesitaba un martillo que Thrór, abuelo de Thorin y último Rey Bajo la Montaña antes de la llegada de Smaug, llevó consigo al exilio, y que Thráin, su hijo, trajo a las Montañas Azules.","'Para trabajar con mithril, se necesita un martillo especial. Tan especial, de hecho, que solo tuvimos uno aquí en la Mansión de Thorin: el Martillo de Thrór, el martillo del abuelo de Thorin, que Thráin trajo aquí. Por supuesto, como nunca tuvimos mithril para trabajar, nunca lo usamos.\
\
'Cuando la mayoría de los barbiluengos regresaron a la Montaña Solitaria, el martillo quedó atrás, y —como una ofensa, estoy seguro— los Duramano lo tomaron y lo colocaron en la tumba de Skorgrím como tributo.\
\
'Al menos, eso fue lo que uno de ellos nos dijo. Intentamos recuperar esa tumba, pero parece estar maldita. Criaturas viles comenzaron a acechar en las sombras. Diría que deberíamos dejarla en paz, pero esta tarea tuya es lo suficientemente importante como para justificar abrirla de nuevo. No encontrarás enanos dispuestos a entrar allí, así que tendrás que recuperar el martillo tú mismo. La tumba está al sur de aquí, en Berghold.''","'Ah, ¡has encontrado el martillo! Excelente, ${PLAYER}. ¡Una oportunidad para trabajar con plata de Moria... nunca pensé que llegaría el día!\
\
'Vamos, ¡pongámonos a trabajar!'","'Si vamos a forjar esta llave que necesitas, necesito el Martillo de Thrór. Eso significa que tendrás que enfrentar los peligros de la tumba de Skorgrím.'","'¡El Martillo de Thrór! ¡Nunca pensé que volvería a verlo! Tus esfuerzos no serán olvidados, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Rápido, lleva el martillo a Litli, y él comenzará a trabajar en tu llave.'","Lleva el Martillo de Thrór a Dwalin","Lleva el Martillo de Thrór a Litli"},
[2231]={"'Now we see if Bordhrist has given us the amount of supplies we will need for the conclusion of our exploration. Take the supplies from the boat and see!'","'Horn wants to see how many supplies we have left? How long does he think we are going to stay here?'","Book 7, Chapter 7: Shadow of the Argonath","Horn has asked you to speak with Nona and Corudan before gathering sticks to make a campfire.","'Horn is waiting for those sticks. He said he was going to gather them as well, but he has been here talking to Framric the whole time!'","Bring the fallen sticks to Horn in the shadow of the Argonath","Your boat is beached not far from the Argonath.\
\
Horn has asked you to remove the supplies from the boat.","'With those sticks we should be able to make a good camp-fire. I have gathered some as well.'","You have come to the East Wall, where the Argonath towers on either side of the Anduin and the falls of Rauros boom unceasingly.","Talk to Corudan in the shadow of the Argonath","'Check the boat for supplies. We will need some of what we brought for thoroughly exploring the East Wall.'","'Horn is free to do as he wishes, and if he is not angered by the horse-lords for casting him out, that is his choice. But I do not like it, and I will not refrain from telling him so!'","'Are you looking for sticks near the trees by here? I will search for some as well.'","Remove the remaining supplies from your boat near the Argonath","'Framric's people rode from the Wold to investigate the Orcs crossing the river here in the East Wall. Speak with him to learn how we can help them, but of course we will keep our eyes peeled for sign of your friends, as well. That is why we are really here, after all.'","Horn has asked you to speak with Nona and Corudan before gathering sticks to make a camp-fire.","'We should all be searching near the trees of this area for fallen sticks so we can make a camp-fire.'","'I do not trust this Framric. I do not like the way he looks at me, from out of his eye's corner. If he is not careful I will teach him the way of my people with Wadu's sword.\
\
'But Horn wants us to help him. I do not understand this loyalty to the horse-lords. They cast him out! He should hate them for that.\
\
'I will not impose my beliefs upon him. But I do not understand his.'","'You spoke in general terms on the boat to Horn and Nona, but I know why we are really here, ${PLAYER}. The Lady Galadriel entrusted me with knowledge of our true mission. I will not betray that trust.\
\
'While we are here in the East Wall, I think it is fine for us to help Framric's people. That is clearly what Horn desires. But we must also keep alert for signs of our mutual friends. They came to this land, that we know. What happened to them then? That is a mystery, and it is one we must find the answer to and then help them, if we can.\
\
'But first, Horn is right. We need to gather sticks to make a camp-fire, or we will have a cold night.'","You reach into the boat and remove the remaining supplies for apportioning.","'You will find fallen sticks near the trees by here, ${PLAYER}. Gather some sticks and we can build a fire.'","Collect fallen sticks by the trees near the Argonath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You found enough sticks for our fire? Good, I will combine these with the ones Nona and Corudan have found, and we will soon have a decent camp-fire.\
\
'Will you remove the supplies from the boat so we can assess what we have left?'","'That is not enough for me.'","Collected fallen sticks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Fallen sticks can be found near the trees not far from the Argonath.\
\
Horn has asked you to collect fallen sticks near the Argonath for preparing a camp-site.","Talk to Nona in the shadow of the Argonath","'We have several purposes here in the East Wall. Let us help Framric and his men while we search for signs of your friends and what happened to them.'","Horn is by the beach near the Argonath.\
\
You have collected fallen sticks for making a camp-fire, as Horn requested.","Horn speaks quietly, for what he has to say is meant for your ears alone.\
\
'We spoke of a great many things on the boat, and I do not begrudge you for speaking in generalities, but you told me enough to know your errand here is important. Friends of yours came this way, friends bearing a burden of some malice. Whatever they carried, it was sought by Orcs, and perhaps others as well. We need to find what happened to these friends of yours and if their burden has been lost.'\
\
Horn raises his voice to include the Rohirrim man standing nearby.\
\
'This man saw our boat drifting down the river, and hailed me from the shore. His name is Framric, and he has come with a party of Rohirrim from the Wold. I would have us help his people, if they desire our help.\
\
'But first we must prepare our own camp. Speak with Nona and Corudan for their thoughts, and then collect sticks for a fire. I will do the same.'"},
[2232]={"Dagoras is in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn.\
\
Aragorn asked you to speak with Dagoras so he might select Rangers of the Grey Company suitable for the task of ambushing the force that seeks to waylay the Host of the West at Cirith Negen.","Legolas looks at you with a raised eyebrow and a hurt expression","Book 7, Chapter 7: The Ambush","'If we are to ambush the ambushers, we will need a small force of skilled hunters and trackers who can move stealthily through the woods unseen. Hethradir, by the look-out point over the Forbidden Pool, will know which of the Rangers of Ithilien will be best suited for this purpose.\
\
'Some of my kin will want to take part in this adventure as well. Speak to Dagoras in the cave of Henneth Annûn, and he will assemble these others.'","'If we are to ambush the ambushers, we will need a small force of skilled hunters and trackers who can move stealthily through the woods unseen. Hethradir, by the look-out point above the Forbidden Pool, will know which of the Rangers of Ithilien will be best suited for this purpose.\
\
'Some of my kin will want to take part in this adventure as well. Speak to Dagoras in the cave of Henneth Annûn, and he will assemble these others.'","'Let us make our plans with the Rangers of Ithilien and with Aragorn's kin, and then we will depart for Cirith Negen to surprise our foes.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Legolas in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn","'I will choose Rangers of our band that are up to the task.'","'I will find others of my people who wish to help, and we will have greater chance of success if they are beside us, on secret feet.\
\
'Battle on the open plain is very different from forest-fighting. I will not say it will be a relief to engage in the latter once again, but every man of the company has seen enough of the former by now to last him until the end of his days.'","'I am no stranger to errands of secrecy, ${PLAYER}, and I know that neither are you! There was once a time when I would say we could have handled this ambush by ourselves, but there is wisdom in being prepared. I will find others of my people who wish to help, and we will have greater chance of success if they are beside us, on secret feet.\
\
'Battle on the open plain is very different from forest-fighting. I will not say it will be a relief to engage in the latter once again, but every man of the company has seen enough of the former by now to last him until the end of his days.'","Hethradir is at the look-out point above the Forbidden Pool, near Henneth Annûn.\
\
Aragorn asked you to speak with Hethradir so he might select Rangers of Ithilien suitable for the task of ambushing the force that seeks to waylay the Host of the West at Cirith Negen.","'I have heard that a force of Orcs and Easterlings seeks to waylay King Elessar's army as he proceeds northward through the pass of Cirith Negen. These monsters and their foul allies are monstrous fools if they think to use our own tricks against us!\
\
'This is the Land of the Moon, and many are the moons that have risen and set upon my life. Still I am here, Faramir's most loyal friend, and I will aid him until I breathe my very last. Younger men you will find, quicker perhaps, but none will know this land as I do.\
\
'It is neither my lot nor my desire to lead in anything but this: I will lead our men into the woods and against our foes, and back again. I will choose Rangers of our band that are up to the task.'","Talk to Aragorn outside Henneth Annûn","Talk to Legolas and travel to Cirith Negen","Legolas is in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn.","The Rangers of Ithilien have learned that Orcs and Easterlings seek to surprise the Host of the West on its march, and Aragorn has charged you with defeating the ambush before it can be sprung.","Talk to Dagoras in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn","Dagoras is in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn.\
\
You have helped to rout the intended ambush at Cirith Negen, and should now speak with Dagoras.","'I hope you were planning to ask me to join on this endeavour, ${PLAYER}! I do not want to be left out of such an adventure. Perhaps Aragorn asked for me by name, and you thought he asked for Dagoras instead?'\
\
Legolas laughs, a musical sound.\
\
'I will gladly accompany you to ambush the ambushers, my friend. Tell me when you are ready and we can leave.'","Legolas is in the hidden cave at Henneth Annûn, ready to leave for Cirith Negen.","'We foiled the ambush and dispersed our foes, true, but does it seem to have been too easy? Certainly our friends in Ithilien have ambushed many foes from that spot with success, but this effort on the part of the Orcs and the Easterlings does not seem to have had any real chance of victory. Their force was too disorganized to cause us any trouble. Indeed, it seems to me that even had we stumbled unknowingly into the trap, we still might have survived to rout our foes.\
\
'Will you mention my concerns to Aragorn? There is something peculiar in all this.'","'Thanks to our efforts and those of our friends, the Host of the West will now be able to proceed safely through Cirith Negen. And yet, my mind turns over and over upon an idea that will not leave me in peace.\
\
'We foiled the ambush and dispersed our foes, true, but does it seem to have been too easy? Certainly our friends in Ithilien have ambushed many foes from that spot with success, but this effort on the part of the Orcs and the Easterlings does not seem to have had any real chance of victory. Their force was too disorganized to cause us any trouble. Indeed, it seems to me that even had we stumbled unknowingly into the trap, we still might have survived to rout our foes.\
\
'Will you mention my concerns to Aragorn? There is something peculiar in all this.'","Talk to Hethradir by the look-out point over the Forbidden Pool","Aragorn is outside Henneth Annûn.\
\
Dagoras wanted you to raise his concerns with Aragorn concerning his experience in Cirith Negen.","'Dagoras is troubled by the ease with which the ambush was upset? I think there is an answer for that, though it may not soothe his worries.\
\
'I deem that the chief purpose of that ambush was to encourage us to keep on our course, to draw us on with a false estimate of the Enemy's weakness. If it did cause us harm, so much the better, but I think it unlikely that it was intended to do anything other than to feint at our strength and bring us on with confidence.'"},
[2233]={"'Una llave para Carn Dûm... ¿quién habría imaginado que alguien querría entrar en esa ciudad maldita?\
\
'Bueno, hay poco más que pueda hacer por ti. Deberías volver a tu tarea\
\
'Buena fortuna para ti, ${PLAYER}.'","Después de recuperar el Martillo de Thrór y los materiales necesarios, el herrero de Dwalin, Litli, forjó para ti una llave de mithril que debería permitirte atravesar las puertas de Carn Dûm.","'¡Has regresado con la llave! Esperemos que la llave de la que se tomó el molde no haya sido una guía falsa...'","'¿Dónde está la llave?'","'Esa llave debería cumplir con todo lo que necesitas, ${PLAYER}. Deberías volver a tu tarea y hacer uso de ella.'","Libro 7, Capítulo 7: La Llave Forjada","'Buena fortuna para ti, ${PLAYER}. Tú y tus aliados en Angmar la necesitarán.'","Lorniel espera tu regreso en Gath Forthnír, en el este de Angmar\
\
Deberías llevarle la llave a Lorniel","Entrega la llave de la puerta de Carn Dûm a Lorniel"},
[2234]={"The Fellowship of the Ring has broken. Is it too late for Boromir of Gondor to make up for the madness that seized him near the high seat of Amon Hen? Desperate to save the hobbits from death, he fights the ferocious Uruks of the White Hand with the last of his strength....","Tracks in the dirt reveal a great number of running feet passed this way!","A discarded pack lies partially buried in the grass of Parth Galen.","Sandy footprints lead down to the water!","You see sandy footprints among the stones of the beach. They are unmistakably those of a hobbit.","'You found sandy footprints leading down to the water near Parth Galen? And you did not investigate them further? ${PLAYER}! This is serious!'","Corudan is in the shadow of the Argonath, in the East Wall.\
\
You have learned much about what befell the Fellowship, and should now return to tell the story to Corudan.","Scour the beach near Parth Galen for clues and experience 'Session: Two Hobbits' or read the shortened account instead....","Follow tracks to Dead Orc Glade and experience 'Session: The Horn of Gondor' or read the shortened account instead","'It is a sad tale you weave! The burden our mutual friends bear caused some amount of discord among them, and they were splintered. It seems from the signs you read that one or more of them repented of their deeds and sought to repair the divide when the Orcs appeared.\
\
'One halfling stayed clear of the fighting, and it seems another joined him. If they did not cross the river by themselves I cannot come up with another explanation. The two of them have now left the East Wall, heading east. You know the identity of these two, ${PLAYER}: can it be anyone but the bearer of the great burden and his loyal servant? Only Galadriel can hope to see them now.\
\
'I am uncertain of the path of the rest of the company, but my own reading of the signs has shown me something that seems fairly clear: three of that company have left for Rohan... on foot. I believe they pursue the other two halflings of the company.'","Find the lawn of Parth Galen, in the East Wall","Scour the beach near Parth Galen for clues and experience 'Two Hobbits'","Talk to Corudan in the shadow of the Argonath","Book 7, Chapter 8: Reading the Signs","'I think it is good to help Framric while we can, but always keep your eyes open for the real reason we are here.\
\
'As you pass southward through the woods of the East Wall, remain alert for a grassy lawn alongside the Anduin. That peaceful space is called Parth Galen, and it may be a good place to begin our search.'","The lawn of Parth Galen is south of the Argonath, on the south-western side of the lake of Nen Hithoel.\
\
Corudan believes you should begin your search for the Fellowship on the lawn of Parth Galen.","You feel the rough leather of the discarded pack between two fingers, and wonder who might have left it here, unattended. Was it left out of need, or out of forgetfulness?","These tracks by the shore are very different than the booted feet that went off to the north of the camp and the discarded pack. You should investigate these sandy footprints eventually, but first you should go where the danger seems to have gone, and follow the other set of tracks that lead away from the discarded pack to the north!","There are enough supplies for a short stay, and you divide them among the rest of your companions.","Sandy footprints on the beach near Parth Galen may give some clue as to what happened to the Fellowship!","Corudan is in the shadow of the Argonath.\
\
You have divided up the supplies you brought from Lothlórien and should now speak with Corudan.","A great battle was fought at Dead Orc Glade... but not everyone came this way. Are there clues on the beach back near Parth Galen?","Examine the discarded pack and experience 'Session: The Breaking of the Fellowship' or read the shortened account at the Parth Galen camp-site instead","Your exploration of the East Wall will need to be comprehensive if you are to learn what happened to the Fellowship here, and if it is still in your power to help them.","A discarded pack in the grass catches your eye","The Fellowship of the Ring has come to the lawn of Parth Galen, but unless its eight surviving members can overcome the evils that threaten to divide them, it will go no further. Even now, the One Ring seeks to ensnare another heart....","'The lawn of Parth Galen is south of the Argonath, on the south-western side of the lake of Nen Hithoel. That may be a good place to begin your search for our mutual friends.'","'A great battle was fought in that glade, that much is clear. But not every one of our friends is accounted for, ${PLAYER}. Return to the beach near Parth Galen and scour it for more clues.'","A slain Uruk in the southern part of the glade catches your attention","When all else fails, good old-fashioned hobbit-sense must win the day. And so it is that Samwise Gamgee learns of the Ringbearer's plan, and the two set off for Mordor and the Mountain of Fire... alone.","Somewhere within the East Wall, there are more signs of what happened to the Fellowship.","This Uruk bears the mark of the White Hand, and was slain by many desperate cuts of a blade.","'You found a discarded pack? It sounds like they had to leave in a hurry! Return to the site of the pack, at Parth Galen, and look for tracks that might tell us where they went!'"},
[2235]={"Rangers of Ithilien hid supply caches east and north of Bâr Tarnaher.\
\
Bregaras asked you to retrieve Ranger supply caches and bring them back to Bâr Tarnaher.","'I thought I heard something high above us, ${PLAYER}, and I felt a shadow pass across my heart. I know this feeling. It was on the banks of the Anduin that I felled one of the flying beasts. It must have proved only an inconvenience for its terrible rider, for I know their number and all were seen on the Pelennor.\
\
'The Nazgûl are flying above us, just out of sight. They watch the progress of Aragorn's host as it moves north toward Dagorlad. Gimli and I, and you, know of these creatures, but we know also that they can be fought. Not all of Aragorn's soldiers may believe this, and I fear that such feelings of dread as the Nazgûl inspire will grow in the breast of each man. Will their loyalty hold, or will the fear of Sauron's servants cause them to break ranks and flee as cowards?\
\
'My father does not think highly of Man, but I have seen the courage they can wield. Will it be enough?'","Talk to Bregaras at Bâr Tarnaher","'What did you learn at Bâr Tarnaher, my friend?'\
\
You tell Aragorn that the Nazgûl fly high above the clouds and out of sight, but they are keeping pace with the host. You tell him too that their fearful presence, and the nature of the mission itself, is having an effect upon his soldiers, sapping them of their courage.\
\
'I have noticed this as well, ${PLAYER}. I cannot blame these men if their hearts quail at the thought of this painful mission. I will not willingly command them to throw their lives away for the merest of chances, though I know how important that chance may be.\
\
'Find soldiers here at Henneth Annûn and see if you can reassure them.'","Talk to Gimli at Bâr Tarnaher","'From Bâr Tarnaher the Rangers of Ithilien have launched many strikes upon the Orcs. Go with Legolas and Gimli to Bâr Tarnaher, north-west of here, and learn what the Rangers there know of the road ahead.'","Talk to Unréth at Bâr Tarnaher","Gimli is at Bâr Tarnaher, in North Ithilien.","Unréth and Maegur are at Bâr Tarnaher.\
\
Gimli noticed that the soldiers that came with you to Bâr Tarnaher have become increasingly troubled.","Bregaras is at Bâr Tarnaher, north-west of Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien.","Talk to Maegur at Bâr Tarnaher","'I cannot blame these men if their hearts quail at the thought of this painful mission. I will not willingly command them to throw their lives away for the merest of chances, though I know how important that chance may be.\
\
'Find soldiers here at Henneth Annûn and see if you can reassure them.'","Reassure worried soldiers at Henneth Annûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Book 7, Chapter 8: Resolve","Aragorn is at his camp on the border between Dagorlad and North Ithilien.","'At Faramir's instruction, his Rangers placed hidden caches of supplies throughout Ithilien. It seems to me that we should retrieve these supplies, for the time of the Rangers is surely coming to an end. If King Elessar finds victory or defeat at the Black Gate, there will be little need for such caches in the woodlands.\
\
'Find the hidden supply caches east and north of Bâr Tarnaher and bring them back here, and we can distribute their contents among King Elessar's soldiers.'","'Let us move forward along the road, north to the border of Dagorlad! We will establish a camp at the woods' edge, and make ready for the final leg of the march to Mordor.\
\
'I will speak with you at our camp on the border of Dagorlad, when we arrive.'","Travel to Bâr Tarnaher, north-west of Henneth Annûn","Retrieve Ranger supply caches east and north of Bâr Tarnaher (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'From Bâr Tarnaher, the Rangers of Ithilien have launched many strikes upon the Orcs. Go with Legolas and Gimli to Bâr Tarnaher, north-west of here, and learn what the Rangers there know of the road ahead.'","Aragorn is at Henneth Annûn, in North Ithilien.","Deposit the collected supplies near Bregaras at Bâr Tarnaher","Unréth's courage fails, and he looks to you for reassurance","Legolas motions for you to halt, and his eyes search the sky","'The soldiers that came with us, Unréth of Rohan and Maegur of Gondor, well, they have become increasingly more and more troubled as the day wore on. I have given some thought to how I might ease their minds, but my skill is with axes, not with speech-craft!\
\
'Perhaps you can do something to ease their worries, ${PLAYER}?'","With the ambush of the Orcs and the Easterlings now foiled, Aragorn sets his sights upon the road ahead.","Retrieved hidden Ranger supply cache (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I think you should return to Aragorn and tell him about the worries of these men, ${PLAYER}. He must not be surprised if they abandon him when he needs them most, and he finds himself standing alone outside the Black Gate of Mordor.\
\
'Well, alone except for you, me, and Gimli. We will not run, of course.'","Talk to Aragorn at his camp on the border of Dagorlad","'Do not let my assessment challenge your resolve, my friend. That the Enemy believes he has us at a disadvantage means that he prepares to seize the bait and fall into the trap we have set for him. We must not give him any sign that his real danger lies elsewhere, or we will endanger more than our own lives. All of Middle-earth will be at risk.\
\
'And so we continue. There is a tower to the north-west of Henneth Annûn, a ruin called Bâr Tarnaher. From there the Rangers of Ithilien have launched many strikes upon the Orcs. Go with Legolas and Gimli to Bâr Tarnaher and learn what the Rangers at that place know of the road ahead.'","Legolas is at the ruin of Bâr Tarnaher, in North Ithilien.\
\
You have come to the ruin of Bâr Tarnaher, but Legolas has found something amiss.","'${PLAYER}, I am a man of Rohan and will do as Éomer King commands, but my resolve is tested with every step towards the Black Land of Mordor! Is it true that our commanders do not hope to achieve victory through battle? Why then must we throw our lives away?\
\
'I would do anything for the Mark, and gladly, but would it not be better to take these soldiers and man a strong defence at Minas Tirith? There are strongholds in Rohan at which we could last for years if need be! I fought at the Hornburg, and am well-tested by the battle that was fought there.\
\
'An unnatural dread seizes my heart, but there is more to this than fear! I cannot believe that Éomer King or King Elessar of Gondor would so easily throw their lives away, and ours with them. How can this be their choice, ${PLAYER}?'","'I hope the Nazgûl do not cause us any further trouble as we move closer to Mordor, but I fear for the resolve of Aragorn's men.'","Talk to Aragorn at Henneth Annûn","'Thank you for your efforts, ${PLAYER}. I have given some thought to the problem of what to do if more men prove faint of heart as we approach Mordor. It will soon be put to the test, I think.\
\
'Let us move forward along the road, north to the border of Dagorlad! We will establish a camp at the woods' edge, and make ready for the final leg of the march to Mordor.\
\
'I will speak with you at our camp on the border of Dagorlad, when we arrive.'","Soldiers of Aragorn's host can be found at Henneth Annûn.\
\
Aragorn asked you to try and bolster the courage of his men.","'We are close to the Black Land of Mordor now, my friend. May our courage not desert us, and may our friends have the chance they need, though it cost us our lives.'","Bregaras motions to you, desiring to speak","Talk to Legolas at Bâr Tarnaher","'I am no coward, ${PLAYER}, but I have to ask if there is any wisdom in this march to Mordor! I would serve King Elessar in all things and do whatever he commands, but I fear that he does not know what it is he asks of us!\
\
'I thought his host was of a goodly size when we marched through Osgiliath, but now that we have crossed into the wild I see that it is smaller than I thought at first. It can be no match for the armies of Mordor!\
\
'I will die for Gondor, if I must for Gondor to survive, but I do not want to lay down my life needlessly! If this march is folly, as I deem it to be, how can it be the King's command? How will six thousand fallen soldiers at the Black Gate save Gondor? It cannot! It cannot!'","'There's something up there, watching us even now? I don't like the sound of that.'\
\
Bregaras shudders and scans the sky for some sign of the Nazgûl, but can see nothing. He sighs heavily and shakes his head.\
\
'At Faramir's instruction, his Rangers placed hidden caches of supplies throughout Ithilien. It seems to me that we should retrieve these supplies, for the time of the Rangers is surely coming to an end. If King Elessar finds victory or defeat at the Black Gate, there will be little need for such caches in the woodlands.\
\
'Find the hidden supply caches east and north of Bâr Tarnaher and bring them back here, and we can distribute their contents among King Elessar's soldiers.'","Bâr Tarnaher is north-west of Henneth Annûn.\
\
The Rangers of Bâr Tarnaher have launched many attacks upon the Orcs from that ruin, and may know of any dangers to the Host of the West on the road ahead.","Bregaras asked you to leave the supplies you collected at Bâr Tarnaher.","'Leave the supplies you retrieved right there and we can redistribute them to King Elessar's soldiers.'","You become aware that Gimli has been trying to capture your attention","Maegur's courage fails, and he looks to you for reassurance"},
[2236]={"'Golodir ha regresado, pero no es el hombre que conocí. No hay esperanza para mi gente.'","'Tus esfuerzos han renovado mi esperanza, . Ha llegado el momento de enfrentarnos al Falso Rey. Afortunadamente, acabo de recibir noticias de Raghnall de que mi padre estaba siendo trasladado fuera de Carn Dûm hacia Rhunendin. Con la llave que has forjado, ninguna puerta nos será vedada. ¡Nunca tendremos una mejor oportunidad de liberar a mi padre!\
\
'¿Estás conmigo? Si es así, vuelve a hablar conmigo cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una Comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Libro 7, Capítulo 8: Las Puertas de Carn Dûm","Lorniel te espera en Gath Forthnír, en el este de Angmar.\
\
Lorniel te dijo que volvieras a hablar con ella cuando estuvieras ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para comenzar tu asalto a Carn Dûm.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una Comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'Golodir ha regresado con nosotros, pero a un precio demasiado alto....'","Habla con Lorniel","Con la llave de Carn Dûm en mano, ha llegado el momento de alzarnos contra las fuerzas del Falso Rey e intentar rescatar a Golodir.","'Lorniel era como una hermana para mí. No sé si alguna vez superaré el dolor de perderla.'","Golodir está en Gath Forthnír.\
\
Has rescatado a Golodir, pero a un costo terrible. El Falso Rey, Mordirith, apareció y la mató. Lograste debilitar a Mordirith y escapar con Golodir de regreso a Gath Forthnír.","'Deseaba que Golodir fuera libre... que regresara con nosotros... ¡pero no a cambio de Lorniel! ¡Jamás así!'","'La determinación de Lorniel era como un fuego que encendía la esperanza en todos nuestros corazones. Ahora esa esperanza se ha extinguido...'","'¿Por qué viniste? ¿Por qué permitiste que Lorniel viniera? Habría preferido quedarme allí en tormento por mil años antes que ver a mi única hija perecer a las puertas de ese lugar maldito....\
\
'Aquí, tomé esta llave maldita de Lorniel antes de dejarla atrás... pero no, ya no la quiero. ¡Tómala!'","'¡La Corona de Hierro pagará por la muerte de Lorniel! ¡Recuerda mis palabras!'","'Los Enanos de Gabilshathûr no olvidarán a Lorniel. ¡No, una gran estatua será erigida en su nombre!'","'Parece que fue ayer cuando Lorniel y yo éramos niños corriendo por Esteldín... y ahora se ha ido...'","'Si tan solo hubiera hecho más... si tan solo hubiera ido en su lugar...'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir, ? Quién sabe cuánto tiempo tendremos antes de que mi padre sea trasladado una vez más.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una Comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'¿Por qué? ¿Por qué tuvo que morir? ¡Maldito sea Mordirith! ¡Que caiga más allá del Vacío!'","'Temo que Golodir nunca se recupere de la muerte de Lorniel.'","'El dolor de Golodir no me es ajeno. Yo también perdí a una hija a manos de Angmar, hace ya mucho, mucho tiempo...'"},
[2237]={"'Travel with care, my friend, and remember! Do not get too close to the Black Gate!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'I ask that you scout ahead and learn what threats may lie in wait for us as we approach the Morannon. I suggest that you bring two of my Rangers with you: Faeron for his stealth, and Mincham for his understanding of the Black Speech. Together, the three of you may learn much that one alone could not.\
\
'You should find them to the south and to the east of this hillock. Ask them if they will accompany you on this mission, and bear this command in mind: you are not to get too near to the Black Gate!'","Langlas is at Aragorn's camp on the Dagorlad border.\
\
Langlas has called out to you. He has something to say before you leave to scout the plains of Dagorlad.","Aragorn is at his camp on the Dagorlad border.","Talk to Aragorn at his camp on the Dagorlad border","'Thank you for undertaking this mission, ${PLAYER}. Dagorlad is an inhospitable land, and it will be difficult to remain unseen, but I trust you, Faeron, and Mincham as I would trust no others.\
\
'Speak to me when you are ready to depart.'","'Wait a moment, ${PLAYER}, if you would.'\
\
Langlas removes a small packet from within the folds of his cloak and holds it out to you.\
\
'Mincham tells me that you and Faeron will be leaving to scout the slag-hills of Dagorlad in advance of the host? That will be dangerous, for there is little cover on the battle-plain. Take this packet of herbs with you. It was given to me by Mandan before the ships docked at the Harlond, and I have been carrying it around since then as a memento, for Mandan fell upon Pelennor.\
\
'The herbs within are foul-smelling when burned, which was true of most of Mandan's poultices, to speak honestly. If you need to draw the attention of an enemy, it might serve you well. I want you to have it. If Mandan's gift can help you this day, he would want it as well.'","Talk to Faeron at Aragorn's camp on the Dagorlad border","'I will go with you onto the plains of Dagorlad and scout ahead of the host, but be warned! There will not be much cover in that place, and we may be exposed to unfriendly eyes. It will take all of my stealthy arts to keep us safe, but I will do what I can.'","Aragorn has asked you to scout the lands ahead so he will know what awaits the host on its final march to the Black Gate.","Faeron and Mincham can be found at Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
Aragorn has asked you to bring several of his Rangers on a mission to scout ahead of the host.","Talk to Langlas at Aragorn's camp on the Dagorlad border","'I will do as Aragorn commands, though it bring us onto the blasted plains of Dagorlad, where long ago a great battle was fought. I am no stranger to such places of evil, as you know.\
\
'We will learn what we can and then return to tell Aragorn what lies before the host. It would be folly to do otherwise.'","Talk to Mincham at Aragorn's camp on the Dagorlad border","'I do not expect us to find victory through battle, but still I want to keep Sauron's Eye focused on us for as long as we can, ${PLAYER}. To that end, it would not do for the host to be attacked before we attain the Black Gate.\
\
'I ask that you scout ahead and learn what threats may lie in wait for us as we approach the Morannon. I suggest that you bring two of my Rangers with you: Faeron for his stealth, and Mincham for his understanding of the Black Speech. Together, the three of you may learn much that one alone could not.\
\
'You should find them to the south and to the east of this hillock. Ask them if they will accompany you on this mission, and bear this command in mind: you are not to get too near to the Black Gate!'","'I am glad to see you have returned in safety, ${PLAYER}, and so too have Faeron and Mincham! What can you report of the slag-hills?'\
\
Aragorn's eyes widen in disbelief when you tell him that you seized upon a chance opportunity to enter Narchost, but he nods with grim satisfaction when you report what you heard within.\
\
'So this gambit has proven itself, ${PLAYER}. Sauron believes I have the Ring, and all of his attention is focused upon the Host of the West. He has fallen for the trap. Now everything depends upon Frodo.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>To be continued in Volume IV, Book 8, 'The Black Gate'...</rgb>","Book 7, Chapter 9: By Secret Steps","Talk to Aragorn and scout the slag-hills of Dagorlad","Aragorn is at his camp on the border of Dagorlad."},
[2238]={"'Framric is from a Rohirrim encampment located to the south-west, on the border of the East Wall and the Norcrofts. Horn and Nona went to speak with a man there named Ingild who may know something of interest to us.'","You peer out over the plains, and see a far-off cloud of dust","'I do not know anything about that Dunlending girl, but Horn is one of my people and I trust him. I will tell you what I told him: a party of Uruks has fled from the East Wall on foot into the Norcrofts. If you go to the ridge west of here, you might be able to <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> over the plains and see where they went.'","'What dangers await us in Rohan? And Horn says we will need war-steeds if we are to cross the plains? What would Suvulch say of his daughter, could he see her now? What would Wadu say?'","Mansig's encampment is east of the ridge that forms the border between the East Wall and the Norcrofts.\
\
You should speak with Mansig about acquiring war-steeds that will allow you to follow the Uruks into Rohan.","'Look at the rolling fields and plains of the horse-lords. They were meant for my people, but they were taken from us.'\
\
Nona scowls, but then her expression softens.\
\
'Horn and I hunted for signs of your friends while you were at Parth Galen, ${PLAYER}. He is not like the rest of the horse-lords. If he wishes to go into Rohan, a land from which he is exiled, I will do so without complaint. See how much he risks for the causes of strangers? He is a most unusual man, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I will keep an eye on him for you.'","Travel to the ridge west of Mansig's encampment that forms the border of the East Wall with the Norcrofts","Mansig's encampment is located south-west of the Argonath, on the border of the East Wall and the Norcrofts. A man named Ingild claims to have information of interest to you and your companions.","Talk to Mansig at his encampment","Book 7, Chapter 9: Three Hunters","Your companions stand on the ridge that overlooks the Norcrofts of Rohan, and want to speak with you concerning your next move.","'Horn and Nona went to the camp Framric spoke of, led by a Rohirrim man named Mansig. His encampment is located on the border of the East Wall and the Norcrofts. They were going to speak with a man there named Ingild who claims to have seen something of interest to us. You should speak with this man now and see what he knows. I will come as well.'","'A group of Uruks passed this way; the signs are clear about that much, at least. They trampled grass underfoot and kicked aside stones, with little care for where they placed their booted feet. They were in a hurry, and they held captives: two halflings whose identities I think we both know, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The Uruks are right to worry, for their run took them into Rohan, and they are several days ahead of us... and, I feel, mere hours ahead of their pursuers. For they were pursued: by three of our mutual friends, I think. But why? Did the Uruks think they had captured something more than captives?\
\
'We must follow them. If we can lend our aid to the captives or the pursuers, we must do so. But we will need war-steeds if we are to have any hope of catching them on the great plains of Rohan.'","'From here on this ridge, who knows what you might see if you were to <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> out over the plains?'","'Three hunters ran from this point into Rohan, pursuing the fleeing Uruks. Did they catch them? We will need war-steeds if we are to have any hope of making good time on the plains of Rohan.'","'Stand on this ridge and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> out over the plains of Rohan. We must see if there is anything to see, ${PLAYER}!'","You stand on the ridge that forms the border with the Norcrofts","To the west of Mansig's encampment, a ridge overlooks the Norcrofts of Rohan. Ingild thinks you should <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> out over the plains and see if you can see the Uruks that fled East Wall.","Corudan has found some sign of the Fellowship in East Wall as well, and wants you to investigate.","'Stand on this ridge and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> over the plains, ${PLAYER}. There may be something we can see.'","'An Elf, a dwarf, and a Man. Did those three hunters have any hope of catching the fleeing Orcs? We will need war-steeds to have any hope of catching them, let alone their prey!'","'You have urgent business within Rohan? It is not for me to ask questions. Know that my people are suspicious of outsiders, and you travel with not one but two, and are one yourself.'","Talk to Ingild at Mansig's encampment, in the East Wall","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> out over the plains of Rohan","'If you go to the ridge to the west of this encampment and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> out over the plains, perhaps you will be able to see some sign of the Orcs that fled the East Wall.'","'It is strange to look out over the beloved fields of my home and know I am not welcome there, ${PLAYER}. It is your duty to follow the rumour of your friends, and it is my desire to help you do it. So I will follow you if you must pass into Rohan.\
\
'Corudan tells me that the Uruks are likely pursued by an Elf, a dwarf, and a Man, and though the tracks are faint and hard to read, I trust his instincts and his tracking skill. They would need to be incomparable hunters themselves to catch the Uruks if they did not depart immediately, and it seems they did not.\
\
'And we are leaving well after both groups, so heed this warning: we will have no hope of catching up with the Uruks that fled the East Wall without war-steeds of our own. We should speak with Mansig about acquiring such steeds.'"},
[2240]={"Defeat mounted foes in the Entwash Vale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated mounted foes in the Entwash Vale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Horn is at the entrance to Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale.","'Eaworth sits on cliffs at a bend of the Entwash, to the north. Were we to follow the river past the city, we would eventually arrive at the forest of Fangorn. I have heard tales of Fangorn that make me most curious to see it, but to hear Horn speak of it I cannot imagine he will want us to get any closer to it than Eaworth.'","Eaworth is located in the Entwash Vale, halfway up the Entwash river.\
\
Elfmar has asked you to defeat mounted foes in the Entwash Vale as you travel to Eaworth.","'Speak to your companions outside the Mead Hall, and then ride for Eaworth. Leave no mounted foes in your wake!'","Talk to Horn in Eaworth","Nona, Horn, and Corudan are outside the Mead Hall in Faldham.\
\
Elfmar has asked you to thank your companions from him before you leave for Eaworth.","Talk to Corudan in Faldham","Elfmar has thanked you for training his men, and thinks you should travel north-west to Eaworth for news of the passing Uruks.","Book 8, Chapter 11: Across the Vale","Talk to Nona in Faldham","'I do not understand why Horn is reluctant to return to his home. If I were to return to Lhanuch now, I would be glad to see Suvulch. I would introduce him to Corudan, and to Horn...'\
\
Nona falls silent for a moment.\
\
'Perhaps I see why Horn is not eager to see his home again.'","'I thought we might need to go to Eaworth. It is my home, but I have not been there to stay in several years. I returned briefly for a few days after Théoden King ordered me to Stangard and before I left Rohan. My father was pleased to see me go, I think.\
\
'His name is Ingbert, and he is the Reeve of the Entwash Vale. He trained both Prince Théodred and Éomer when they were young. He trained me as well, but I did not impress him as much as they did. He is a hard man. I hope my family troubles will not distress you. Nona... well, he will not think much of Nona.\
\
'I will follow your lead at Eaworth, ${PLAYER}. I do not want my family to cause any trouble for you or our companions.'","Nona is silent and, unusually, has nothing to say.","'My father is a hard man. I do not think he will be pleased to see us.'","'Well, we are here. I did not hurry to see home again, but now that I have it fills me with sorrow.'","Talk to Horn in Faldham","'I would like to see Fangorn, but I will go where you lead.'","'Your road surely runs north-west now to Eaworth. No doubt your friend Horn will be glad to see his home again, and you may be able to learn where the Uruks crossed the river, if they still live.\
\
'As you travel through the Entwash Vale, slay any mounted enemies you encounter. With such speed they could double back and cause trouble for Faldham, or for towns in the Sutcrofts, and I do not wish that.\
\
'Your friends are just outside, I believe. Speak with them and give them my thanks for helping to train my men.'"},
[2241]={"You have come to Eaworth, the town where Horn grew up, to see what they have seen of the uruks that crossed Rohan.","'No point in delaying any further. Let's go see my father and see what he has to say. If we are lucky, his people have seen some sign of the Uruks. If we are not... he will not be pleased at my return.'","'My father Ingbert will be in his Mead Hall, unless he has greatly changed. I suspect he has not.'","Corudan is in Eaworth.\
\
You have spoken with Ingbert and learned that the Uruks passed north of Eaworth, followed by the Third Marshal of the Riddermark.","Talk to Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Talk to Léowulf and attend the meagre feast","Book 8, Chapter 12: Homecoming","Ingbert's steward Léowulf is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
Reeve Ingbert has reluctantly agreed to provide a feast for you and your companions, the very minimum amount of hospitality required by his customs.","Talk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth","'You are new here, ${RACE}. You have come far from your home, and in the company of... peculiar friends.\
\
'An Elf? A girl from the tribes of Dunland? What makes you think these could travel across the plains of Rohan? Or into proud Eaworth?\
\
'No, give me no excuses. I know why you feel you have the right. My son Horn gave you permission, as if he can speak for my lands. The last I knew, he was banished beyond the ridings of Rohan, to Stangard on the Great River, far away. Has Théoden King relented of his command? Or, as I find more likely, has Horn simply flouted the King's command?\
\
'I will not have it be said that Ingbert, Reeve of the Entwash Vale, lacks the courtesies of hospitality. My steward Léowulf will prepare a meagre feast for you. Speak to him while I speak to my son in private. My disapproval is not meant for the ears of strangers, ${RACE}.'","'Éomer, the Third Marshal of the Riddermark, passed Eaworth not long ago. He was hunting the same Uruks you seek. They are likely dead by now, and he should be back shortly.'","You tell Corudan that Ingbert believes the Uruks you seek have likely been slain.\
\
'We will not know for certain until we find them ourselves, ${PLAYER}. But we cannot leave yet. I have looked all around Eaworth, but I cannot find Nona. It is as if she just vanished.'","Reeve Ingbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You have come to Eaworth to learn what its people know of the Uruks you are seeking.","'I thank you for your discretion, ${PLAYER}. Many a maid has cast herself into the torrent of the Entwash when learning of her unrequited love. I am not yet ready for Ingyth to learn of her betrothed's death.'\
\
Ingbert sizes you up appraisingly.\
\
'I was blinded earlier. You are not the stripling for which I mistook you. My displeasure with Horn does not extend to you.\
\
'You are welcome to come and go within the Entwash Vale, if you are a friend to her people.\
\
'The Uruks you seek passed north of Eaworth not long ago, and shortly afterward Éomer, the Third Marshal of the Riddermark, rode after them. I am expecting him back any day now.'","Reeve Ingbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You have feasted with Ingbert and now he is waiting to speak with you.","'I will show you to a comfortable room while the feast is prepared.'","Talk to Corudan in Eaworth"},
[2242]={"'The Dunlending woman? I have not seen her. When I heard there was a woman from Dunland here, I thought she would frighten me. I always heard tell the people of Dunland were wild and savage, and there is a ferocity about her, but there was something else, too. She did not seem afraid of anything.'","Corudan is in Eaworth.\
\
Horn is convinced that Nona has left your group for some reason, and that she will return.","'Horn has gone looking for her, but when last he came this way he had found nothing yet. Did she tell you anything that might give us an idea of where she has gone? Or do you think she has fallen into trouble of some kind? The men of Rohan do not look kindly upon her people.\
\
'You should ask the people of Eaworth if they have seen her, and I will do the same. I do not know if they will tell me anything, but we cannot let her disappearance go without investigation, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Horn is... distraught... as you might expect him to be. He had grown fond of our fiery companion. You do not need Elf-eyes to have seen it.'","'There is a man out by the cliffs. It may be Horn, but I cannot see his features from here. I have not seen the Dunlending anywhere.'","Find Horn or Nona somewhere in or around Eaworth","Talk to Corudan in Eaworth","You tell Corudan what transpired on the cliffs, and he smiles grimly.\
\
'That is what I thought, ${PLAYER}. Nona is indeed fine, and will return to us when she has resolved a few things in her mind. I know now why she has left, and why she did not bring her brother's sword with her: for love.\
\
'You have seen the way the people of Rohan look at her: with fear, and with distrust. She is not one of them. Despite Horn's banishment to Stangard, he is still much more of Rohan than she will ever be. So too has she seen the damage love can do: what would learning of Prince Théodred's death do to Ingyth, his betrothed?\
\
'Nona grew too fond of Horn, over too quick a time, to lose him to battle and death. Perhaps she left to shield herself from growing even more attached to him. Perhaps she simply needs time to resolve her feelings.\
\
'I think she will return, ${PLAYER}, but I do not know when. We must be kind to Horn in the meantime. He will feel this loss sharply, I think.'","Book 8, Chapter 13: The Ghost Vanishes","'I will keep Nona's sword safe until her return. Tell Corudan what has transpired here, and that Nona's path simply does not run with ours for a while. When it does once more, we will see her again.'","'She is gone... she's really gone...'\
\
Horn holds Nona's sword in his hands, and seems to see nothing but the lonely weapon.\
\
'I found it here on the stones, ${PLAYER}. But why would she leave it?'\
\
You peer out over the edge, to the rushing river that has cruelly claimed so many maidens before their times, and Horn follows your gaze with his eyes.\
\
'No, ${PLAYER}. She did not jump into the Entwash. I do not believe it. She left us for some reason, and she left this sword here so I would find it. But why leave us? Why leave me?'\
\
He clenches one fist.\
\
'I will take her brother's sword, and I will keep it for her until she returns. She will return, ${PLAYER}. I will not wield Wadu's blade. But I will hold onto it for Nona. Tell Corudan that Nona has left us, but that she will return. Her path simply does not follow ours for the moment.'","Horn is looking for Nona in Eaworth.\
\
Corudan thinks you should ask around to see if anyone has seen Nona, and if you cannot find her, you should look for Horn.","No one has seen Nona since the feast at Eaworth. Corudan and Horn are worried.","'I have not seen the Dunlending, but Horn has gone out to the cliffs. He seemed upset about something.'"},
[2243]={"Issuriel se encuentra en el alto flet sobre Cerin Amroth, en Lothlórien.\
\
Issuriel desea escuchar el relato de tu escape de Rushdurinul con el cautivo Mazog, ya que los otros Elfos presentes se mostraron reacios a contarle el resto de la historia.","Issuriel de Lothlórien se encuentra en el alto flet sobre Cerin Amroth.\
\
Haldir te ha hablado de los preparativos que se están haciendo para la partida de la Hueste Dorada hacia el Bosque Negro y desea que hables con Issuriel, una elfa que está siendo considerado para liderar a los Malledhrim. Ella tiene preguntas para hacerte sobre la captura de Mazog.","'Es un placer conocerte por fin, ${PLAYER}, y espero que ayudes a la Hueste Dorada cuando llegue el momento de avanzar en el Bosque Negro. El señor Celeborn me ha pedido que participe en la planificación de la ofensiva, así que para entender completamente la mente del cautivo Mazog, escuché el relato de Corunothiel sobre su captura.\
\
'Con interés, aprendí sobre tu infiltración a través del camino secreto hacia la sala del trono de Mazog, pero Corunothiel cesó su relato en el punto donde el líder orco fue capturado. Le presioné por más información, pero dijo que el recuerdo era sombrío y no deseaba revivirlo tan pronto.\
\
'Dime qué pasó después de la captura de Mazog, ${PLAYER}. ¿Cómo pudiste escapar del corazón mismo de la sala del trono de Mazog... y con el rey de los Orcos aún a remolque?'","Mientras Celeborn prepara la Hueste Dorada para avanzar sobre el Bosque Negro en una jugada desesperada para evitar un ataque de Dol Guldur, todavía hay algunos asuntos por resolver.","Libro 8, Capítulo 1: Escape de Rushdurinul","Issuriel se encuentra en el alto flet sobre Cerin Amroth, en Lothlórien.\
\
Has contado el resto del relato de tu escape de Rushdurinul con Mazog, y Issuriel ha escuchado algo que le preocupa.","'Issuriel desea hablar contigo sobre la captura de Mazog, ${PLAYER}. Búscala en el alto flet sobre Cerin Amroth.'","'Estoy lista para escuchar el resto de la historia, ${PLAYER}. Quiero saber cómo pudiste escapar de Rushdurinul, el mismo asiento del poder de Mazog, con el rey de los Orcos aún cautivo. ¡No debe haber sido fácil!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no se puede completar con una comunidad.</rgb>","'El señor Celeborn se está preparando para una gran incursión en el Bosque Negro, no para conquistar, sino para evitar el ataque de Dol Guldur que seguramente vendrá. Estamos reuniendo suministros y preparando todo para el paso de los Malledhrim, la Hueste Dorada, y el Señor y la Dama están seleccionando cuidadosamente a quienes la liderarán.\
\
'Una de las personas que creo que es probable que viaje con la Hueste Dorada se llama Issuriel; es una estudiante de historia y de los misterios del mundo natural y habló a menudo con Mithrandir en la rara ocasión en que sus asuntos lo llevaron al Bosque de Oro. Ella busca conocer la verdadera naturaleza de las cosas y ama desentrañar acertijos y secretos por encima de todo lo demás.\
\
'Issuriel ha estado preguntando por ti, ${PLAYER}. Quería escuchar el relato de la captura de Mazog en las profundidades de Moria de tus labios y tenía preguntas para hacerte. Búscala en el alto flet sobre Cerin Amroth.'","Habla con Issuriel en Cerin Amroth","'El relato de tu escape de Rushdurinul con Mazog aún cautivo fue más angustioso de lo que esperaba, ${PLAYER}, ¡y te agradezco que me lo hayas contado! Si vamos a trabajar con los enanos para llevar a Mazog a Dol Guldur, como Bróin pretende, debemos aprender la lección de tu relato: ¡no se debe subestimar al rey de los Orcos!\
\
'Confío en que la gente de Bróin esté fabricando nuevas cadenas para Mazog, para comenzar con la lección más obvia de tu escape.\
\
'¡Pero hay más, ${RACE}! Las palabras de Mazog me hacen preguntarme. ¡Mira primero a tu propia puerta antes de llevar la lucha a la de tu enemigo, dicen los Sabios!'","Habla con Issuriel y cuéntale la historia de tu escape de Rushdurinul"},
[2244]={"'If Aragorn says there is no other way, I will not gainsay him. This is the road we must take!'","Daervunn and Pippin are at the edge of the Camp of the Host, where the northward road leads into Dagorlad.","Aragorn is on the rise in the middle of the Camp of the Host.","'The Ring, and Frodo, have not been seized by the Dark Lord. Every step that Frodo takes toward the Fire kindles our hopes.'","'What did Daervunn have to say? Are the men ready to march?'\
\
You report the Ranger's words, and Aragorn nods grimly.\
\
'It pains me that such a course is necessary, but I take satisfaction in knowing the great loyalty and courage of the men with whom I march.'","Talk to Mithrandir and experience 'Interlude: No Other Way' or read the shortened account instead","Daervunn and Pippin are staring out at the road ahead","Mithrandir is at the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad.","The Host of the West has come to the border between Ithilien and Dagorlad. There is now no other way to go but forward to the Black Gate of Mordor.","Mithrandir calls to you with concern in his voice","'This is the road to Mordor? No one could mistake it for anything else, ${PLAYER}! It looks as I would have expected it to look, had I ever wanted to fill my heart with fright and my mind with unease at the considering... and I did not!\
\
'Daervunn has had some kind words to say concerning my \\qcourage,\\q and I did not want to offend him by disagreeing, but I think he sees what is not there. If I were truly brave, would I feel so frightened at the prospect of taking this road? Certainly not! But Aragorn believes that we have to do this, and I have smarts enough to know he is more wise than I am. If he says there is no other way, this hobbit will not gainsay him. This is the road we must take!'","Find Daervunn at the northern edge of the Camp of the Host","Book 8, Chapter 1: No Other Way","'My thoughts are also with Frodo and Sam, and I fear for their safety in the company of Gollum. But I agree with Mithrandir that they must still be alive, for we would know if Sauron had the Ring.\
\
'But my reasoning is not that of the Wizard. I travelled with Frodo and Sam for almost four months, and we had many adventures and braved many dangers. And even after so many shared hardships, I think Master Gamgee had only just begun to warm up to me, and perhaps did not yet entirely trust this \\qStrider.\\q\
\
'He will not take his eyes off Gollum, even if Frodo perhaps will. I do not think Gollum will be able to take advantage of our Samwise, even if he thinks he can. They will be fine, inasmuch as any might be whose misfortune it is to journey in the Black Land.'","Talk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Host","Daervunn is at the northern edge of the Camp of the Host, where the road leaves the encampment and passes into Dagorlad.\
\
Aragorn has asked you to see if Daervunn has readied the men to march.","'This road will take us across the blasted plains of Dagorlad, to the very gate of Mordor. The men stir with restlessness, but they will obey their liege, whether he be Éomer or Aragorn. Others there are, too, who have joined this host in cause of allied friendship; if they have not turned back now, I believe they will never abandon us.\
\
'I have shared words with Peregrin Took here, and he too has a courage about him.'","The worried thoughts of the Host of the West turn towards Frodo and Sam, who have passed beyond even Gandalf's sight. He knows only that the hobbits make for the dangerous pass of Cirith Ungol, their guide the creature Gollum, spared years ago by the mercy of Bilbo. Their guide possesses knowledge of this hidden way into Mordor, but another secret he keeps to himself: the identity of the terrible guardian that lurks within the tunnel through which they must pass...","'Mithrandir desires to speak with you, my friend.'","Mithrandir is at the Camp of the Host on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
Something has worried Mithrandir and he wishes to speak to you about it.","Aragorn is on the rise in the middle of the Camp of the Host.\
\
Daervunn reported that the men are ready to march.","Talk to Mithrandir at the Camp of the Host","Talk to Pippin Took at the northern edge of the Camp of the Host","'Too much time has passed without word of our friends. Did their guide lead them into some danger, as I fear? We cannot know for certain, ${PLAYER}, but neither can we dispel our worries.'","'Look for Daervunn where the northward road departs from the camp and ask him if the men are ready to leave.'","'You were at the council of the captains, ${PLAYER}, and you heard the arguments for and against this march to the Black Gate. You must know of its importance, as I do.\
\
'But still I am troubled. Before battle consumed Minas Tirith, I spoke with Faramir of his watch in Ithilien, and he told me that his men encountered two hobbits in the wild: Frodo and Sam. Briefly he held them, but he did not hinder their errand overlong and soon released them to their purpose.\
\
'But a third there was, and he served our friends as their guide: Gollum. Faramir spoke against the creature, but Frodo believed he could be trusted, and intended to follow him through a secret pass into Mordor. The pass is called Cirith Ungol. It is an evil place. I know enough of that pass to know that danger lurks there in the darkness, and I fear that Frodo may trust his guide too readily. Alas that our roads ran apart!\
\
'A fortnight has passed since Frodo and Sam departed from Faramir's care. My wondering mind worries at how little we know of their fates, ${PLAYER}, and conjures terrible scenarios of what could have befallen. What has happened to our friends? What has happened to the Ring?'","'This road will take us across the blasted plains of Dagorlad, to the very gate of Mordor. I hope you are ready.'","Mithrandir is at the Camp of the Host on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
Mithrandir is worried about what might have befallen Frodo and Sam since they parted ways with Faramir in Ithilien.","'The only hope of victory lies with Frodo, but we still have a part to play in this great struggle, ${PLAYER}. I asked Daervunn to prepare the men for departure, for I believed it might take longer than expected for the Host of the West to set out upon this last march. Heavy are the feet that dread the approaching road, but still they must step one before the other!\
\
'Look for Daervunn where the northward road departs from the camp, my friend, and ask him if the men are ready to leave.'","'In my heart I guessed that Frodo and Gollum would meet before the end, but I hope that Frodo does not trust blindly. If he remains alert to the possibility of deceit, perhaps he can prevent it before it leads our friends to harm.\
\
'Or has it already done so? It has been two weeks since they left Henneth Annûn, and still there has been no word. If they fell prey to some treachery of Gollum's, surely we would have heard by now. Cirith Ungol...'\
\
Mithrandir's voice trails away as his eyes search the horizon. After a moment his attention returns, and a smile briefly illuminates his features.\
\
'I should not have given in to these fears, ${PLAYER}. The Ring remains out of Sauron's grasp. Let that keep our hearts afloat and allay some of our worries! For if Frodo were betrayed to Sauron, I feel certain that the Dark Lord would make use of the Ring at once, and we would know the end had arrived. That has not happened. The Ring, and Frodo, have not been seized by the Dark Lord. Every step that Frodo takes toward the Fire kindles our hopes.'","Talk to Daervunn at the northern edge of the Camp of the Host"},
[2245]={"'No me queda nada, gracias a tu descuido. Si deseas hablar con alguien, habla con Laerdan. Él deberá continuar la lucha ahora, sin mí.\
\
'Ahora dejame.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Lleva el equipo de Golodir a Laerdan","Libro 8, Capítulo 1: La Llama Titilante","Encuentra a Prakhum, emisario de la Ciudad de los Trasgos, y recupera la espada de Golodir de él","Encuentra a Laugi Lenguadorada, emisario de los Duramano, y recupera el escudo de Golodir de él","El equipo de Golodir fue entregado a emisarios de los trasgos, enanos y nómadas de Angmar. Estos emisarios pueden encontrarse en las agujas que rodean Barad Gúlaran, al sur de Gath Forthnír.\
\
Como primer paso en su plan para renovar el espíritu de Golodir, Laerdan te ha pedido que recuperes las armas y pertenencias del Montaraz de manos de los emisarios dentro de las torres de Barad Gúlaran.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Encuentra a Karstíona, emisaria de los Trév Duvárdain, y recupera la cota de malla de Golodir de ella","El asalto a Carn Dûm trajo la libertad del Montaraz Golodir, pero resultó inútil, pues Lorniel pereció y Mordirith, el Senescal de Angmar, se replegó en la fortaleza de la ciudad.","'¡Déjame en paz! No me interesa tu insensatez.'","Laerdan está en Gath Forthnír.\
\
Golodir, destrozado por la muerte de su hija, te dijo que lo dejaras en paz y que fueras a hablar con el Elfo Laerdan.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si decides emprenderla en solitario recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","Cota de malla de Golodir recuperada","'Así que has regresado, y con éxito. Pero, ay, este equipo ya no es apto para usarse. Temo que el débil destello de mi plan esté a punto de apagarse.\
\
'Aun así, puede que quede algo de esperanza.'","'¿Has encontrado el equipo de Golodir? Cada pieza está en posesión de un emisario de las tribus de Angmar —trasgo, enano y nómada— en las torres de Barad Gúlaran.'","'Ah, . Es bueno que hayas regresado. He conocido a Golodir por muchos años, pero nunca había visto su espíritu tan quebrado. Aunque la muerte de Lorniel fue quizá la última piedra arrojada contra su corazón destrozado, presiento que hay algo más grave en la raíz de su desesperación.\
\
'Debemos recomponer el espíritu de Golodir, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}... aunque no sé cómo. Apenas tengo un débil atisbo de un plan, pero quizá funcione.\
\
'Golodir fue un guerrero formidable, y podría recordársele ese pasado si tuviera de nuevo sus armas. Le fueron arrebatadas y entregadas como obsequios a los emisarios de las tribus de Angmar, como símbolos de la victoria de Mordirith sobre los Pueblos Libres. Cada uno de esos emisarios ocupa una torre en Barad Gúlaran, al sur. Si tenemos suerte, encontrarás las armas y el equipo de Golodir en poder de esos emisarios.'","Espada de Golodir recuperada","'Déjame en paz, ${RACE}. Mi vida y mi alegría me han sido arrebatadas.'","Escudo de Golodir recuperado"},
[2246]={"'The horses of Rohan are renowned for their loyalty, strength, and speed, and it seems to my eye that the steeds they have given us are no exception.\
\
'If the steeds of the others are satisfactory as well, one of the men here requested our aid. Speak to Enstan south-east of here, by the exit from Harwick.'","Enstan is by the south-east exit of Harwick, in the Wold.\
\
Your companions have war-steeds of their own and now you have heard that Enstan wants your help with something urgent.","In order to obtain war-steeds for yourself and your companions, you will need to accomplish two things: complete the preparations for and defence of Langhold, and learn about mounted combat in Harwick.\
\
The defence of Langhold involves a chain of ten quests that begins with a quest bestowed by Dala called 'The Wold.' If Dala has no more quests for you, search around Langhold for other quest-givers.\
\
You can learn about mounted combat at the Tourney Field in Harwick.","'All of us must band together if we are to survive the encroaching dangers, but there are so few of us fighting men available. And now, Floodwend has sent urgent messages calling for our aid! Mansig and most of his men are still away, investigating the East Wall. If he were here, I know he would ride at once in defence of Floodwend, but he is not!\
\
'Can you ride those new war-steeds of yours with any skill?'","'Two things must you accomplish to earn the war-steeds you seek. First, help in the defence of Langhold. Second, you must travel south to Harwick to learn how to safely and swiftly engage in combat from the back of a war-steed.'","You and your companions will need war-steeds if you are to travel across the plains of Rohan with any speed.","'I hope I do not shame myself with my poor riding! If I fall from the back of this steed, I will never forgive you for making me ride, ${PLAYER}.'","'Your companions have obtained war-steeds, yes? You should speak with them in Harwick.'","'My people do not fight from horseback, so this has not been an easy adjustment for me. Still would I rather fight on foot, and let my enemies charge toward me at their peril! But I understand we have a need for the speed of hooves if we are to find your friends, and for that I will put up with it. I hope I do not shame myself in front of our companions with my poor riding. Horn rides as if he were born in the saddle, and Corudan has the natural grace of his people.\
\
'I feel like an aurochs up here.'","'We face difficult times not just in Langhold, but throughout all of the Wold as well. Théoden King has left those of us in the Wold without much support. I do not blame him! Rumour tells of great armies marshalling in the west, and we are spread too thin over too wide an area.\
\
'If you desire to travel across the Kingdom of Rohan, you will need war-steeds for yourself and your companions. There are two things you will need to accomplish in order to obtain the privilege of such steeds. First, help in the support of Langhold. Once this city has been made safe, travel south along the road to Harwick, and you will be instructed in the skills necessary to safely and swiftly ride a war-steed.'","Learn how to participate in mounted combat at the Tourney Field in Harwick","'These war-steeds will serve us well on the plains of Rohan. Enstan requested our aid. Find him to the south-east, by the exit from Harwick.'","Your companions have obtained war-steeds of their own, and are waiting to speak with you in Harwick, by the tourney ground near the stables.","Book 8, Chapter 1: War-steeds from the Wold","Complete all quests in Langhold, in the Wold","'It is good of the men of Harwick to provide us with these steeds. We must help them if we can. Enstan requested our aid. Speak with him to the south-east, by the exit from Harwick, and learn if helping him is in our power.'","'It is good of Aldor Harding to provide these war-steeds to us. When I was last in these lands, he was a man of short temper and did not believe the King was strong enough to protect Rohan from what threatened her. I cannot imagine he has changed, but it is good to see he is making Harwick ready for whatever may come. These steeds are of good breeding, and should serve us well. Nona has not lived her life among horses, but still she has done very well to pick it up in short order. War-steeds are different from the horses she may have had occasion to ride in the past, and she has adjusted well. Corudan, too, is already at home on the back of his steed. We will make good time over the plains.'"},
[2247]={"'I watched the departure of the Faint-hearted, ${PLAYER}, and I felt no scorn for them, though there was a time in my life when I might not have understood their choice. I see that their path too was in service of the Host of the West. Our own road takes us to Mordor, for we have the courage to go that way.\
\
'I am not afraid of Mordor or its Black Gate. Neither am I afraid of the Dark Lord or his armies. I am not afraid of Mordirith, no matter what he names himself. I am not afraid of death, for I have lived a life enriched by friendship and laughter, and I know that endings must always come, soon or late.\
\
'I am made strong by the love of my friends and the memories I carry with me, and no Orc or wraith or beast can conquer that strength. At long last I am at peace, ${PLAYER}. I will follow Aragorn to the end, with an unburdened heart.'","'Some of my kinsmen are deep in thought, contemplating the roads that have led them here, while they ready themselves for the road to come. Will you speak with some of them and put into words how grateful I am for all they have done? This is likely to be our last battle, and I want them to know that I appreciate their service not only as their captain or their king, but also as their friend and kinsman. This may be my last chance to tell them so, and I do not want to miss that opportunity.'","Aragorn is on the rise in the middle of the Camp of the Host.","As you approach, Corunir breaks free of his reverie","Lothrandir is south of Aragorn's position on the rise in the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.","As you approach, Lothrandir surfaces from his thoughts of home","The Host of the West prepares to set forth on the last leg of the march to the Black Gate, and Aragorn wants his friends and kin to know that he is grateful for their trust and their service.","Corunir is east of Radanir's position in the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.","Talk to Lothrandir south of the rise in the Camp of the Host","Book 8, Chapter 2: Last Chances","'It is our misfortune that we must march to the Black Gate with little hope of our own survival, ${PLAYER}. So many good men have placed their lives in my hands, trusting that this course is important. I believe that it is, but it does not make the burden of that choice any lighter.\
\
'Some of my kinsmen are deep in thought, contemplating the roads that have led them here, while they ready themselves for the road to come. Will you speak with some of them and put into words how grateful I am for all they have done? This is likely to be our last battle, and I want them to know that I appreciate their service not only as their captain or their king, but also as their friend and kinsman. This may be my last chance to tell them so, and I do not want to miss that opportunity.'","Talk to Radanir to the south-east of Lothrandir's position in the Camp of the Host","'Once I spoke to you of my travels, ${PLAYER}, of my adventures in the wooded lands of Enedwaith and the rocky heights of Thrór's Coomb, but they are dwarfed now by the memory of these last few weeks. From the dungeons of Isengard to the fighting on the Pelennor, our journey has been full of hardship. \
\
'My mind turns now to my home, at Sûri-kylä in Forochel. I do not think I will see it again, but I am at ease knowing that I have done what I can for the Snowmen, and they will persevere as they always have done.\
\
'I will follow Aragorn wherever he leads.'","Talk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Host","'Have you ever broken a promise, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
Calenglad looks at you sadly, and holds up a finger to halt your reply.\
\
'I have sought to live my life with honour, making good upon my promises and the oaths I have taken. I swore an oath to aid Aragorn my chief in all things, and I have done so as best I could. That oath has taken me far from my home and to the very doorstep of Mordor.\
\
'But my heart remains on the shores of Lake Nenuial. I promised to return when my duty in the south-lands was done, but... it does not seem that any of us will return, after all. What were the words of Gwindeth? That the return of Elendil's kingdom would be worth some measure of sorrow? Did she speak the truth? I do not know, even now.'","Talk to Calenglad north of Corunir's position in the Camp of the Host","'None of us are free of worry, ${PLAYER}, or free of regret. But still we move forward in spite of those feelings. That is all we can do. That is what we must do.'","'We have been through a lot together, ${PLAYER}, and most of it was unpleasant. I am not complaining, not really. If it was to be easy, it need not have been the Dúnedain's task to face it! I said as much to Elweleth once, but she has gone away, and will never return.\
\
'Do you think that the folk of Middle-earth will appreciate everything Aragorn has done? I do not expect our names to be remembered, but if there is any justice, Aragorn will be remembered fondly and well by the people of Gondor and Rohan, at least.'\
\
Radanir is silent for a long while, and you are about to leave him be when he speaks at last.\
\
'It seems there will be no peaceful tavern for us at the end of this road, ${PLAYER}. After everything we have gone through, I suppose I am not really surprised.'","Aragorn surfaces from his thoughts, and turns to face you","Lothrandir is deep in thought, contemplating the home he left behind.","As you approach, Calenglad returns from his thoughts","Radanir is south-east of Lothrandir's position in the Camp of the Host on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.","Aragorn is lost in his thoughts.","Calenglad is lost in his thoughts.","Radanir is lost in his thoughts.","Corunir is lost in his thoughts.","Calenglad is north of Corunir's position in the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.","Talk to Corunir east of Radanir's position in the Camp of the Host","As you approach, Radanir emerges from his thoughts","Talk to Aragorn in the Camp of the Host"},
[2248]={"'¿Así que Golodir vive? Es algo asombroso. Lo creía muerto desde hace tiempo, una víctima más de Angmar. Es una pena, sin embargo, que su libertad haya sido ganada al precio de la vida de su hija. Lorniel fue un regalo. Hermosa en espíritu y forma. Qué tristeza.\
\
'Ah, he hablado demasiado. Déjame ver esa espada y ese escudo. Haré lo que pueda para ayudar a Golodir.'","Lleva la espada y el escudo a Daervunn.","Libro 8, Capítulo 2: Reavivar la Llama","'¿Qué puedo hacer por ti hoy?'","Daervunn está en Esteldín.\
\
Debes regresar con Daervunn para recoger la Cota de Malla de Golodir y ver si tiene alguna idea sobre cómo reparar la espada.","Lleva la espada y el escudo a Toram.","'No deberías demorarte aquí, sino dirigirte a Esteldín. Quizás allí su amigo Daervunn pueda reparar el equipo de Golodir.'","'No deberías demorarte aquí, sino dirigirte a Esteldín. Quizás allí el amigo de Golodir, Daervunn, pueda reparar su equipo.'","'No deberías demorarte aquí, sino dirigirte a Esteldín. Quizás el amigo de Golodir, Daervunn, pueda reparar el equipo de Golodir.'","'Estoy casi terminando con la Cota, pero deberías ir a ver a Toram y recuperar la espada y el escudo de Golodir.'","Recupera la espada y el escudo de Golodir de Toram en Esteldín.\
\
Daervunn te pidió que llevaras la espada y el escudo de Golodir a Toram, un forjador de armaduras en Esteldín, para que los repare.","Lograste recuperar el equipo de Golodir, pero como te señaló Laerdan, el equipo estaba corroído y deteriorado más allá de su uso.","'La esperanza que queda para Golodir debe residir en su propia gente. Puede que ellos puedan reparar este equipo o extraer de él algo que pueda renovar a Golodir.\
\
'Lleva este equipo al campamento oculto de los Montaraces en Esteldín, en las Quebradas del Norte — estoy seguro de que ya has estado allí. Diles que Laerdan de Eregion te envió.\
\
'¡El tiempo se agota para Golodir!'","Lleva el equipo de Golodir a Daervunn.","Daervunn está en Esteldín, en las Quebradas del Norte, muy al sur y al oeste de Angmar.\
\
Laerdan te instruyó para que llevaras el equipo de Golodir al Montaraz Daervunn para que lo repare.","'¿El equipo de Golodir? Ayudaré en lo que pueda.\
\
'Hmm, sí. Creo que puedo reparar el daño en su Cota de Malla, pero reparar el escudo y la espada está fuera de mi alcance. Sin embargo, creo que uno de los forjadores de armaduras aquí en Esteldín podrá ayudar. Ve y lleva la espada y el escudo a Toram. Mientras haces eso, me pondré a trabajar en la Cota.'","'Bueno, el escudo no fue un problema, aunque nunca he visto uno como este. No es el escudo de Golodir; es mucho más antiguo y lleva las marcas del Reino del Sur. Muy interesante... sea como sea, le servirá bien.\
\
'La espada, sin embargo, es otro asunto. Fue forjada por los Elfos hace mucho tiempo y está más allá de mi capacidad para repararla. Lo lamento, pero he hecho lo que he podido.\
\
'Quizás Daervunn tenga otra idea sobre cómo reparar la espada de Golodir.'","'Yo repararé la Cota de Malla, pero la espada y el escudo están más allá de mi habilidad. Llévalos a Toram, uno de los forjadores de armaduras de Esteldín. Él debería poder arreglarlos.'","'¿Tienes la espada y el escudo de Golodir?'","'He hecho todo lo que he podido por ti. Esa espada está más allá de mi habilidad para repararla. Yo hablaría con Daervunn, si fuera tú. Puede que tenga alguna idea sobre cómo aún podría ser reparada.'","'Afortunadamente, sin demasiada dificultad, he podido reparar la Cota de Malla. Me decepciona, sin embargo, que Toram no haya podido reparar la espada. Al menos logró reparar el escudo.\
\
'Es interesante que el escudo que encontraste no fuera el de Golodir, sino que proviene del Reino del Sur. Es un verdadero misterio... pero uno que deberá resolverse en otro momento, supongo.\
\
'Volviendo a la espada, si hemos de hacer que sea reforjada, sólo puedo pensar en un lugar donde haya Herreros Elfos con la habilidad suficiente para repararla.'","Toram está en Esteldín\
\
Daervunn sintió que podía reparar la Cota de Malla de Golodir, pero la espada y el escudo estaban más allá de su habilidad. Te pidió que hablaras con Toram en Esteldín para que repare esos objetos."},
[2249]={"Corudan looks at you silently. He raises an eyebrow at you, and there is a strange fire in his eyes.","Collect salvaged belongings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The road leaves Harwick and runs south-east until it reaches Floodwend. The land becomes rockier the further south you go, so your steeds will need to be sure of foot to make it there safely. Stick to the road, if you can. I do not know what threat has so worried the raven-master of Floodwend, but it was grave enough for him to send three birds with the plea for help.\
\
'He may have sent more. I do not know him personally; he could be excitable by nature, or the keep at Floodwend could be in worse peril than ever before! Go with haste to help! We have no men to spare, and if Floodwend falls Harwick could be next!'","Orientales derrotados en el Páramo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected salvaged belongings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Book 8, Chapter 2: Troubles at Floodwend","Floodwend is south-east of Harwick, along the road.\
\
You have agreed to ride to the defence of Floodwend.","Harwick has received urgent pleas for help from Floodwend, and cannot spare anyone to ride there but you.","Talk to Corudan by the entrance to Floodwend","Talk to Goldlac at the entrance to Floodwend","'Between your skill in combat and the harsh waters of the Great River, perhaps the Easterlings will decide attacking Floodwend is too much trouble. What times we live in! Even if that were so, we would still have to worry about attacks by raiding Orcs! Will Floodwend ever see peace again?\
\
'While you were gone, a raiding party of Orcs passed near to Floodwend. Alwold and his men rode out to fight them, and had success: all of the Orcs were defeated. The Orcs must have recently fought with some Elves, for one of Alwold's men claimed quite a trophy from the body of one of the Orcs: a bow of quality Elf-make, with the finest detailing. He has been showing off since they returned. His name is Elfsige, and he'll likely challenge your Elf to an archery contest before too long. Poor, foolish fellow.'","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'You heard what he said, ${PLAYER}? That is almost certainly the bow I lent to Fimloth! The Orc that claimed it carried it into the Wold, and now this man Elfsige has taken it!'","'You have come from Harwick? The Thane was hoping for more men, but I suppose you will have to do. The Easterlings have been testing the Great River, trying to find safe places at which to ford in between the two undeeps. They have a large camp to the north-east, but our people have kept an eye on them and they seek another way to strike at us. Perhaps they thought just below the rapids would be safe, or perhaps they fear their commanders more than the rushing waters: a great many perished trying to cross just below Sarn Gebir.\
\
'Not all, however, not all by half. Many of the Easterlings survived the crossing and have been marshalling their forces for an attack on Floodwend. Many of their belongings are scattered and damaged by the waters, but still they seek to recover enough to arm themselves to attack the city. We need you to strike them along the banks of the Anduin, just to the east, below the cliffs. You should also steal from them what belongings survived the crossing.'","Easterlings are crossing into the Wold south of the rapids of Sarn Gebir, and you need to defeat them and gather their scattered belongings.","'If your Elf is not careful, Alwold's man Elfsige is going to challenge him to an archery contest with the bow he took from that dead Orc. And if Elfsige is not careful, he's going to win! May your Elf have mercy!'","'If Mansig were here, he would ride with his whole company to the defence of Floodwend... but he is not here. He is still in the East Wall, investigating the Orc activity. If you can ride those war-steeds of yours with any skill or swiftness, you can come to Floodwend in time to help against whatever it is they face. Ride with haste south along the road to Floodwend!'","Bring salvaged belongings to Goldlac at the entrance to Floodwend","Corudan is by the entrance to Floodwend.\
\
Corudan wants to speak with you about the bow that Elfsige took from a dead Orc near Floodwend.","'Easterlings have been trying to find places at which to ford the Great River. They seek to attack Floodwend! Go east of Floodwend to seize their belongings that survived the crossing, and defeat any Easterlings you find there.'","Derrota orientales en el Páramo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Goldlac is at the entrance to Floodwend, in the Wold.\
\
You have defeated Easterlings and collected their salvaged supplies, and should return now to Goldlac."},
[2251]={"'No tenemos la habilidad para forjar esta espada. Deberías llevarla a Elrond en Rivendel.'","Recupera la espada de Golodir de Hemeldir","Los Montaraces de Esteldín pudieron reparar el escudo y la cota de malla de Golodir, pero la espada era de arte élfico, más allá de su habilidad.","'Hemeldir, mi maestro herrero, forjará de nuevo la espada de Golodir.'","'¿Qué necesitas de mí, ${RACE}?'","Elrond está en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Daervunn te sugirió que llevaras la espada de Golodir a Elrond de Rivendel para que fuera forjada de nuevo.","'¿Dejaste la espada de Golodir en Rivendel? ¡Ve allí de inmediato y recupérala!'","'El Maestro Elrond querrá inspeccionar esa espada antes de que la devuelvas a Golodir.'","Lleva el equipo de Golodir a Hemeldir","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, tu historia me entristece, pues conozco a Golodir, y fue un buen hombre. Me alegra saber que vive, pero me aflige que este Falso Rey haya logrado quebrarlo de tal manera.\
\
'Que un espectro haya regresado al poder en Angmar me preocupa aún más. Nunca he oído hablar de Mordirith... es un misterio sobre el cual debo reflexionar.\
\
'Ve ahora con Hemeldir, mi maestro herrero, y pídele que rehaga la espada de Golodir. Lo encontrarás cerca de las fraguas de Imladris.'","Elrond está en Rivendel.\
\
Hemeldir te devolvió la espada forjada de Golodir y te dijo que la llevaras con Elrond para su aprobación.","'Como siempre, el dominio de Hemeldir se manifiesta en la obra de sus manos. Esta espada será conocida de ahora en adelante como \\qDúnachar\\q, Vengadora del Oeste, pues vengará la muerte de Lorniel, hija de Golodir.'","'La tarea está hecha, ${PLAYER}. Poco se parece al arma de la que nació, pero creo que servirá mejor a su dueño.\
\
'Llévala ahora con el Maestro Elrond para su aprobación.'","'¿El Maestro Elrond requiere que esta espada sea forjada de nuevo? Muy bien. Es un pequeño ensayo en el arte élfico... no tomará mucho tiempo.\
\
'Pero ¿qué es esto? Me atrevo a decir que este escudo no pertenecía a tu amigo Golodir. Este escudo es mucho más antiguo, de tiempos cercanos a la caída del Reino del Norte. También proviene de Gondor, no del Norte. De hecho, me resulta familiar... creo recordar uno similar entre la línea real de Gondor.\
\
'Hablaré con el Maestro Elrond sobre esto más adelante. Por ahora, me ocuparé de la tarea que se me ha encomendado.'","Hemeldir se encuentra cerca de las fraguas de Rivendel.\
\
Elrond te instruyó que llevaras la espada de Golodir a su maestro herrero, Hemeldir, para que la forjara de nuevo.","'Aquí tienes el equipo de Golodir. Viaja a Rivendel y habla con el Maestro Elrond. No dudo que podrá ayudarte. Sus herreros están entre los más grandes artesanos élficos de estos días.\
\
'No te demores aquí. Si esto puede ayudar a renovar el espíritu quebrado de Golodir, entonces debes apresurarte hacia Rivendel.'","Lleva la espada de Golodir a Elrond","Lleva el equipo de Golodir a Elrond","Libro 8, Capítulo 3: Forjando la Espada","'Estoy seguro de que Hemeldir ha terminado de forjar la espada de Golodir. Deberías recuperarla de él y regresar conmigo.'","Hemeldir se encuentra cerca de las fraguas de Rivendel.\
\
Deberías consultar con Hemeldir para saber si ha terminado de forjar la espada de Golodir.","'¿Has regresado con la espada?'"},
[2252]={"'I will give your friend a chance to win this bow, but only one chance. I am not an unreasonable man! This is more than generous!'","'I am sorry that your friend lost his bow, but it seems to me that anything taken from an Orc belongs to the one strong enough to take it. If your friend wanted it back, why did he not reclaim it from the Orcs when he had the opportunity?\
\
'I am not unreasonable. What if I give your friend the opportunity to win it back in a contest of some sort? Alwold has given me a message to deliver to Elthengels in the Norcrofts. How about this? A test of your mounted skill: whichever of us first reaches Elthengels gets to keep the bow. If I arrive there first, your friend gives up all claim to it. Does he agree to this proposal? If he does, let us speak with my commander, Alwold, outside Floodwend. He will start the race.'","'Is Corudan really going to accept it if we do not win this wager? Will he be willing to give up his claim to his favourite bow?'","Corudan is in Floodwend, north of the Mead Hall.","'This is a ridiculous requirement. Why should I have to engage in a competition to determine my right to possess property that is rightfully mine? If these are the laws of Men I am grateful to be one of the Galadhrim! But I am not worried, ${PLAYER}. We will best this arrogant sapling that thinks it is a weathered oak, and my favourite bow will once again be in my possession.\
\
'Let us speak with this Alwold outside Floodwend. The sooner this unnecessary race is begun, the sooner we will win it!'","Book 8, Chapter 3: Strange Companions","'I do not like this. Elfsige will be very, very fast while mounted. He will have trained on horseback for his entire life. It will not be easy to win this wager!'","You explain the terms of Elfsige's wager, and Alwold chuckles.\
\
'I am not surprised. Times have been tough in the Wold of late, with Orcs and Easterlings and worse prowling around the borders. When my men are not fighting for their lives, they're engaging in fruitless wagers. I cannot stop them. As long as they, and you, abide by the agreed-upon terms, I have no complaint. But I do not want any bloodshed! If you go back on your word, you'll have me to deal with!'","Elfsige claimed a high-quality bow from the body of an Orc he slew: Corudan's favourite bow, loaned to Fimloth and lost in Thinglad.","Elfsige is in Floodwend, north of the Mead Hall.\
\
You have heard that Elfsige has a bow that sounds like it belongs to Corudan, and should ask him to return it.","'I am not worried. We will win this ridiculous wager. Let us go to speak with Elfsige's commander, Alwold. He is outside the city.'","'That is my bow. I would know it anywhere.'","Talk to Elfsige in Floodwend","Talk to Corudan in Floodwend","'Speak to my commander, Alwold, outside Floodwend. He will begin the race!'","'Surely Elfsige will see reason. That is clearly an Elf-made bow, and if Corudan says it belongs to him...'\
\
Horn's brow creases in thought.\
\
'Of course, Elfsige did come into possession of the bow by slaying an Orc in defence of his town. He may not wish to part with it solely on the word of an Elf.'","Talk to Alwold outside Floodwend","Alwold is on the road outside Floodwend.\
\
Elfsige has agreed to race you to Elthengels, with the winner of the race taking all claim to Corudan's bow. His commander, Alwold, will start the race.","'That is the bow Corudan lost? No wonder he wanted it back! How many Orcs did the two of us slay in Thinglad, searching for it? And now this arrogant horse-man thinks slaying a single Orc entitles him to keep it for himself?'","'This will not take long. Let us have some words with this man Elfsige. He is sure to return my bow when he understands the situation.'"},
[2253]={"Lleva el equipo de Golodir a Laerdan","Libro 8, Capítulo 4: Un Faro de Esperanza","Elrond renombró la espada de Golodir como Dúnachar, Vengadora del Oeste, y profetizó que algún día vengaría la muerte de Lorniel, hija de Golodir.","'Debes regresar de inmediato con Laerdan y llevarle el equipo de Golodir.'","Lleva el equipo de Golodir","'¡Has regresado, ${PLAYER}! ¿Qué noticias traes? ¿La espada ha sido forjada de nuevo? ¿Dúnachar se llama...? Sí, puedo sentir la virtud que hay en ella.\
\
'¿Y qué dijiste sobre el escudo? ¿No es de Golodir? Tendrá que servir.\
\
'Lleva el equipo a Golodir en sus aposentos.'","'¡Déjame en paz!'","Golodir está en Gath Forthnír, en las regiones orientales de Himbar.\
\
Laerdan te indicó que devolvieras el equipo de Golodir.","'¡Apresúrate, ${PLAYER}! Laerdan espera tu regreso.'","'Lleva el equipo a Golodir... Espero que al menos despierte una pequeña chispa de la brillante llama que alguna vez fue.'","'¿Qué es esto? ¿Mi cota de malla? ¡Pensé que se había perdido para siempre! Y este escudo... no es mío, pero ¡es una maravilla!\
\
'Pero esta espada... ¿es mi espada? Fue forjada hace mucho por los Elfos de Rivendel, una reliquia de mi familia. Pensé que se había perdido para siempre, ¡pero ahora ha regresado como Dúnachar!\
\
'Está bien nombrada como Vengadora del Oeste. En verdad, vengará a mi hija...'","'Dúnachar es una espada excelente, y preveo que algún día el Senescal de Angmar lamentará que haya sido forjada de nuevo.\
\
'Ve ahora. Regresa con Laerdan y llévale el equipo de Golodir. Espero que Golodir vea su desesperación por lo que realmente es: las maquinaciones del Enemigo.\
\
'Laerdan te espera en Gath Forthnír, en Angmar.'","Laerdan está en Gath Forthnír, en las regiones orientales de Himbar.\
\
Elrond te entregó la espada Dúnachar y te dijo que la llevaras, junto con el resto del equipo de Golodir, a Laerdan.","'¿Pudieron los Montaraces recuperar el equipo de Golodir?'"},
[2254]={"You ask the guard if Elfsige has arrived yet, and he shakes his head in confusion.\
\
'No, but his horse arrived shortly before you did... and without him! Something must have happened to him. You have to retrace your steps, and look for him! He must be somewhere between Elthengels and Floodwend. Look among the trees to the south of the road between here and Floodwend. You could have passed him without seeing him!'","Time before Elfsige arrives at Elthengels:","'You need to go to Elthengels. Did Elfsige get there before you?'","'You have to retrace your steps, and look for Elfsige! He must be somewhere between Elthengels and Floodwend. Look among the trees to the south of the road between here and Floodwend. You could have passed him without seeing him!'","Talk to Thurhun at the entrance to Elthengels","You have arrived at Elthengels before Elfsige!","'Why are you still here? Do you not want to win your wager with Elfsige? Elthengels is south-west of here! Ride with utmost haste!'","Elfsige has returned to Elthengels, in the Norcrofts.\
\
You should return to Elthengels and speak with Elfsige there.","Talk to Elfsige in Elthengels","The race is on! The first person to reach the town of Elthengels, in the Norcrofts, wins claim to Corudan's bow.","'It will not take Elfsige long to reach Elthengels. You had better ride with great haste if you are to get there first and win your wager! Ride south-west to reach Elthengels!'","Horn looks at you silently, his expression unreadable.","'My leg is feeling better. Thank you. I will meet you back in Elthengels.'","Elthengels is south-west of Floodwend, and you do not have much time in which to reach it before Elfsige does!","Find Elfsige somewhere between Elthengels and Floodwend","Elfsige may be in trouble among the trees south of the road between Elthengels and Floodwend.\
\
Elfsige never arrived at Elthengels, and now you should see if you can find him. He may be in danger!","'I am sorry if I came across as a bit of a fool, ${PLAYER}. I did not think you would be much of a rider, but not only are you a skilled rider, you are a good person as well. I thank you for coming to find me. I have already given your Elf his bow, and I renounce any claim to it I may have had. It is done.'","Hreohmanu gazes at you balefully. This is Elfsige's horse, but you see no sign of the brash young Rohirrim.","Reach the entrance to Elthengels before Elfsige does","You have arrived at Elthengels, but there is no sign of Elfsige.\
\
You should speak with Thurhun, the guard at the entrance to Elthengels, to see if he has seen Elfsige.","Book 8, Chapter 4: A Wager in the Wold","'I was trying to take a short-cut to Elthengels when Hreohmanu was surprised by a patrol of Orcs! He reared, and I fell... did he make it to Elthengels? I can... I can probably walk now. I could not put weight on it, but now it is feeling better. I will meet you ahead in Elthengels, and we can discuss... the wager. I will be there soon. Thank you for coming back to find me.'"},
[2255]={"Aragorn and the Host of the West have come to the Black Gate of Mordor, and the time has come to deal with the Dark Lord.","Aragorn is at the base of the slag-hill outside the Black Gate.\
\
Aragorn has asked you to accompany him as he rides to demand the surrender of Sauron, and he wants you to be well-prepared before you go with him.","'Do not give up hope, ${PLAYER}. We must stand as tall as we may, or Frodo and Sam will have gone to their doom for nothing. I will not allow this to be! The Quest of the Ring has failed, but we must not give in to despair or we betray the men who fight alongside us.\
\
'The day is dark. Let our blades and our hearts oppose the evils that would forever silence them, and avenge our friends upon these foes!'","'Are you ready to go? Be well prepared, for we are on the very doorstep of evil and there may be no coming back from this.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Book 8, Chapter 4: The Black Gate","Aragorn is atop the eastern slag-hill as the Battle of the Black Gate rages outside Mordor.\
\
The Mouth of Sauron has revealed that Frodo and Sam have been captured in Mordor. The quest of the Ring has failed.","'There is no sense in delaying what must come. There must be a parley. I will go forth with a small group of my most trusted allies and call for Sauron's surrender. I would be honoured if you would accompany me, my friend.\
\
'I do not expect the Dark Lord to give in to our demands, but still I must offer him the opportunity. Speak to me when your preparations are made and we will go together.'","Talk to Aragorn on the eastern slag-hill","Talk to Aragorn at the base of the slag-hill and ride with him to the Black Gate"},
[2256]={"'Aunque el Falso Rey no era más que un eslabón en las cadenas que atan a mi pueblo, ahora sé que un día esas cadenas de esclavitud serán destrozadas por completo, ¡para siempre!'","'¡Las facciones de Angmar caerán en disputas internas ahora que el Senescal del Rey Brujo ha sido derrotado!'","'Mordirith ha sido debilitado, aunque no destruido. El camino, sin embargo, queda abierto para que otros finalmente derriben a este Falso Rey. Ojalá hubiera sido yo quien arrojara a esa vil criatura de nuevo a la Sombra, pero me basta con haber hecho lo que hice.\
\
'Te pido que, si regresas a Carn Dûm, termines el trabajo que empezamos: derriba a Mordirith. Aunque una criatura como él no puede ser destruida por completo —pues puede simplemente envolverse otra vez en su manto—, una derrota así será una gran victoria para los Pueblos Libres de Eriador.\
\
'Aun así, hay más que debo pedirte...'","'Enfrentar a un enemigo tan grande y derrotarlo... tal fuerza no habita en mí. Nos sentimos honrados de contar con alguien como tú a nuestro lado.'","'¡Nunca creí que llegaría este día! ¡El Falso Rey ha caído!'","'¡${PLAYER}! Gracias. Gracias por vengar la muerte de Lorniel. Era una gran muchacha... le has hecho honor a su nombre.'","'Durante los largos años aquí, ocultándome, había perdido casi toda esperanza de que alguna vez diésemos un golpe así contra la Corona de Hierro. Y, sin embargo, ¡Mordirith ha caído!'","'La esperanza ha vuelto. El espíritu del padre de Lorniel ha sido restaurado. Creo que Lorniel estaría feliz... sí, lo sé, lo estaría.'","'La victoria se ha comprado a un alto precio, pero ningún precio es demasiado si conlleva la caída de la Corona de Hierro.'","Habla con Golodir","'La derrota de Mordirith es una gran victoria, pero no te equivoques: la guerra contra Angmar aún no ha terminado.'","'¡${PLAYER}! ¡El azote de Mordirith! ¡Tu victoria jamás será olvidada! ¡Jamás!'","Libro 8, Capítulo 5: La Caída de Mordirith","'Has hecho bien en devolverle la esperanza a Golodir y en vengar la muerte de Lorniel. Gracias.'","Habla con Golodir en Gath Forthnír","'La deuda de gratitud que te debo, ${PLAYER}, no es algo fácil de saldar. Pero ten por seguro que no olvidaré todo lo que has hecho por mí.'","Golodir está en Gath Forthnír.\
\
Tras derrotar a Mordirith y encontrarte con la misteriosa Sara Roblecorazón, tú y Golodir regresaron a Gath Forthnír. Deberías hablar con Golodir nuevamente.","Las esperanzas de Laerdan de usar la espada y la armadura de Golodir para renovar el espíritu del Montaraz no fueron en vano. La visión del brillante escudo de Gondor y de su ardiente espada, Dúnachar, encendió en Golodir un nuevo fuego... quizá uno peligroso.","'El momento de la venganza ha llegado. A pesar de la fuerza que has visto en el corazón de Angmar, creo que puede flaquear. Mordirith, el Falso Rey, es una criatura de gran poder, pero creo que podría ser debilitado, si no destruido por completo.\
\
'Regresaré a Carn Dûm y me enfrentaré a Mordirith. Es hora de cortar la Corona de Hierro de la cabeza de esta serpiente. ¡Te pido que me acompañes!\
\
'Juntos, entraremos en esa ciudad vil y enfrentaremos a Mordirith en la sala del trono de Carn Dûm. Reúne a los compañeros y suministros que necesites, porque la batalla que nos espera será terrible.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si eliges emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'El viaje a Carn Dûm será difícil, pero Mordirith debe ser derrotado. ¿Estás listo para partir?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si eliges emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>","'¡La derrota de Mordirith es solo el primer golpe en nuestra guerra contra Angmar! ¡Pronto la Corona de Hierro será derribada y los míos quedarán libres de ella!'","Mordirith se encuentra en la sala del trono de Carn Dûm.\
\
Golodir te ha pedido que lo acompañes en su regreso a Carn Dûm para enfrentar a Mordirith, el Falso Rey, Senescal de Angmar.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión está pensada para una comunidad. Si eliges emprenderla en solitario, recibirás una bonificación de inspiración, pero el desafío será grande.</rgb>"},
[2257]={"'Stand fast, men! They seek to cow us with their numbers, but each of us is worth a dozen of their mindless thralls!\
\
'My limbs are heavy and my breath is short, ${PLAYER}, but I will do what I can to support Aragorn and my kinsmen.\
\
'Fight on! Fight on!'","Talk to Gimli on the north-eastern slope of the eastern slag hill","Lines of archers fire into the enemy ranks from their position on the slag hills. Look for full quivers by the bodies of men who have fallen, and gather them for Legolas.","Aragorn is atop the eastern slag hill.","Fight your way to Prince Imrahil on the south-eastern slope of the western slag hill","Collected quivers from fallen archers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have enough arrows for the moment, but Gimli is right: my supply will run low soon if the tide of enemies does not slow!\
\
'Many archers of Gondor and Rohan have already fallen to the arrows of Mordor; some of their quivers remain full, or nearly so. Go to the archery lines and look for our fallen unfortunates. If you return to me with a number of their full quivers I will be able to maintain my current pace, and continue to support Gimli with my bow.\
\
'I thank you for undertaking this helpful task, grim though it may seem!'","'Is this to be the last battle, ${PLAYER}? My heart tells me this is so, and though it be a sorrowful thing I will be glad to see the end of war-time, and to have rest.\
\
'A palpable hit, and another! I find no joy in battle, my friend, but I find that I am uncommonly good at it, truly! I will use that skill to defend the men at my side, until my last breath is stolen away by some lucky stroke!\
\
'Fight onward, ${PLAYER}! Make our foes pay for the evils they have done, and hope still to do!'","'Thank you, my friend. Set the quivers at my feet and I will use them as the need arises.'\
\
You place the quivers of arrows at Legolas's feet and he nods with satisfaction, but his eyes never leave the distant line of battle.\
\
'I heard Aragorn shouting his commands from the top of the slag hill to the south-west, ${PLAYER}. Climb the hill and see if you can aid him!'","Talk to Legolas on the north-eastern slope of the eastern slag hill","Mighty Ologs stride forth, bellowing with rage!","'We have held the line of battle for now, keeping our foes from ascending the eastern hill, but it seems that our foes have redoubled their efforts to take the western hill.\
\
'We are hard-pressed and can spare no man, but someone must go to the western hill and keep it from being taken! Can you go to the aid of Imrahil with haste enough, ${PLAYER}? I know you can! Fight your way to the slope of the western hill, and help the Prince of Dol Amroth throw back the tide!'","Legolas fights alongside Gimli on the north-eastern side of the eastern slag hill.\
\
You collected a number of full quivers to return to Legolas.","Prince Imrahil is hard-pressed on the slopes of the western slag hill, before the Black Gate.\
\
Aragorn has asked you to fight your way across the battlefield to the western slag hill, where you must come to the aid of Prince Imrahil.","Defeated enemies at the Battle of the Morannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Daervunn on the eastern edge of the battle","Collect full quivers from the fallen in the ranks of archers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Lothrandir on the eastern edge of the battle","More foes surge from the line!","Legolas fights alongside Gimli on the north-eastern side of the eastern slag hill.","Talk to Aragorn on top of the eastern slag hill","Bring a new supply of full quivers to Legolas on the north-eastern slope of the eastern slag hill","The western slag hill comes under fierce attack!","You hear the battle-cries of Gimli the Dwarf coming from the north-eastern side of the eastern slag hill.","The Host of the West has been surrounded by the armies of Mordor and must now fight for its survival.","Book 8, Chapter 5: Surrounded","'The Black Gate has opened, and the armies of Mordor stream forth from Sauron's lands, seeking to put an end to those of us who vex him still. This is where we will make our stand!\
\
'Sauron's warriors have formed a ring around the slag hills, ${PLAYER}. Fight them as they approach, and keep them from advancing! Stand with our friends and allies, and aid them as you can! We must hold out for as long as we are able!'","'I see that you have already slain your share of Orcs, ${PLAYER}! Legolas has also cut an impressive swath, but he tells me his supply of arrows will not last long. Perhaps you can help him with this?\
\
'The battle has only just begun, but there is no need to worry about our respective tallies this time. There will be plenty of foes for all of us!'","Daervunn fights on the south-eastern edge of the eastern slag hill.","Orcs and Uruks have formed a ring around the slag hills, surrounding the Host of the West. Aragorn has asked you to defeat your foes and aid your friends and allies as best you can.","'${PLAYER}! The fighting here goes poorly, but with you here my spirits are lifted!'","Defeat enemies at the Battle of the Morannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lothrandir is shouting words of support and guidance to the men of the line on the eastern side of the battle."},
[2258]={"'I must deliver my message to Thane Mildrith, even though she will not like it. Perhaps I will see you later.'","Talk to Ingild on the first floor of the Elthengels tavern","'Something is happening outside! It sounds like trouble!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","You have bought a round of drinks with Horn's coins and should now distribute them to the patrons of the Elthengels tavern.","'Now there is a familiar face! ${PLAYER}, I have not seen you since the East Wall. Did you find the Uruks you were seeking when we spoke at Mansig's encampment? No? A shame, I am sorry. I have returned home to... what was that noise? Did you hear that?'","'You have my gratitude. Without your help our losses might have been more severe. I have heard Elfsige's message from Floodwend and can spare no men, but perhaps I can send a waggon of blacksmithing supplies.\
\
'I will see you on your way with supplies of my own, but only if you will help me with a matter of crucial import for my town.'","'Thank you kindly, stranger. I don't mind if I do have a sip of that.'\
\
Wigherd drinks deeply, but shakes his head when you ask about the Uruks.\
\
'I did not see them run by, but I heard from those who did. Running more away than toward, it seemed to them as saw it. No one wanted to ride out to challenge them, and who can blame them? We lost Thane Pendrad in the Autumn to Orcs, and his widow may be Thane now, but she is not the fighter he was. And then to lose her son! It is a wonder she can go on at all, but she's not commanding troops. The Uruks passed us by, and we should be lucky they did not turn to raid the town.'","Talk to Horn in Elthengels","Book 8, Chapter 5: Thane Mildrith","Thane Mildrith is in the mead hall of Elthengels.\
\
After the Orc attack, Thane Mildrith has asked you to meet with her.","Distributed round of drinks (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Ah, Ingild has returned! I have not seen him in awhile. Do you know him?'","'Now that I'm here, I need to accomplish my duty. I was given a message to deliver to Thane Mildrith of Elthengels, asking for her to send some of her warriors to Floodwend to help defend against the increased number of Easterlings crossing the river. Her husband was slain by Orcs some time ago, and her son died under... unpleasant circumstances... more recently. I do not think she will respond favourably to this message, but still I must deliver it. Thank you once again, friend.'","Horn has given you some coins of the Mark with which to buy a round of drinks for the patrons inside the Elthengels tavern. Perhaps they will have some information to tell you about the Uruks.","'I'll have some of that, since you're buying.'\
\
Tidwine drains the mug in one huge gulp, and at first you cannot tell if he has heard you ask about the Uruks.\
\
'Ah! Just the stuff. What did you say? The Uruks that ran by Elthengels? Aye, I saw them. Never seen Uruks run like that before. Even if Thane Mildrith was in any state to order our riders, she would have been a fool to send men after them. And she is no fool. Suffered more than her share of grief, if you ask me, but no fool. She was Pendrad's rock, before he was slain by Orcs, and she had much to do with shaping the man Pendulf became. Pity what happened to the boy, but you'll hear no rumours from me.'","Talk to Thane Mildrith in the Mead Hall of Elthengels","'If you insist!'\
\
Dudmund finishes the mug and slams it down on the table.\
\
'Best beer in the Norcrofts, and I don't care who hears it! You go tell Reeve Athelward that I'd rather have the brew of Elthengels than that of Cliving!'\
\
The other patrons give Dudmund some worried looks, but it only serves to rile him up further.\
\
'No, you listen to me! If he challenges me to trial by combat, like he did with Mildrith's son, well, I'll teach him a thing or two. I won't even let him scratch me with that blade of his. I swear he had some vile coating on it, to make Pendulf's wound fester like that. I swear it!'\
\
He lapses into depressed, drunken silence, and has nothing more to say to you.","'The Uruks that left the East Wall may have passed near to Elthengels. We should learn if any of the townspeople know anything of their passage. Here, ${PLAYER}. Take these coins of the Mark, and use them to buy a round of drinks at the tavern for the patrons there. It could be one of them saw something of those Uruks.'","The group of Uruks you are pursuing passed near to Elthengels, and now you should try and learn what the villagers know of them.","'Spread those drinks around, and you'll make yourself some friends. Look for a few of my regulars upstairs.'","Horn is waiting to speak with you in Elthengels.","A new arrival has come to the Elthengels tavern.","'We need to know what the people of Elthengels know about the Uruks that fled from the East Wall. Nothing helps loosen tongues quite like free-flowing ale or beer. Use the coins of the Mark I gave you to order some drinks for people in the Elthengels tavern.'","'I have not seen you around here before, stranger. Your coins are good, though, I will give you that. Here's a round of my finest. Pass it around as you will. There should be some of the usual folk upstairs: Wigherd, Tidwine, maybe one or two others who don't come in as frequently. They'll be glad of your generosity.'","Talk to Ingild and investigate the sound he heard","'¿Qué?'","Buy a round of drinks from Thurnoth in the Elthengels tavern","Distribute the round you bought (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Ingild is waiting to talk to you on the first floor of the Elthengels tavern.","'You don't have enough.'"},
[2259]={"'Gracias por devolverme al reino de los vivos, ${PLAYER}. Mi dolor ya no es tan terrible.'","'Angmar ha sido frenado por el momento, gracias a ti.'","Con la ayuda de Golodir, has debilitado enormemente a Mordirith, el Senescal de Angmar, y vengado la muerte de Lorniel.","Libro 8, Capítulo 6: Un Ojo Vigilante","'Mordirith ha sido derrotado, pero solo por un tiempo. Aun así, es un respiro.'","'Esta victoria es importante, aunque no tan completa como había esperado al principio. Sin embargo, incluso esta victoria nos dará un breve respiro del embate del Enemigo. Te pediría que se lleve la noticia de nuestro éxito a mi jefe, Aragorn, hijo de Arathorn.\
\
'¿Lo has conocido entonces? ¿Está en Rivendel? Ve, entonces, a hablar con mi Señor Aragorn en una de las habitaciones de huéspedes a lo largo del camino que sube por la ladera sur del Valle de Imladris, y cuéntale nuestras hazañas aquí.'","'Gracias por devolvernos a Golodir.'","Aragorn se encuentra en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls, en una de las habitaciones de huéspedes de la Casa de Elrond.\
\
Golodir te indicó que llevaras la noticia de la caída de Mordirith a su jefe, Aragorn.","'Aragorn debe enterarse de nuestra victoria contra el Falso Rey. Ve a Rivendel y habla con él en una de las habitaciones de huéspedes a lo largo del camino que sube por la ladera sur del Valle de Imladris.'","Habla con Aragorn en Rivendel.","'Así que Golodir no pereció, y la Sombra de Angmar está, al menos por el momento, debilitada. Pienso que incluso si Mordirith finalmente cae, algún día podría regresar..... o que otra Sombra del Enemigo ocupará su lugar.\
\
'Aun así, tus esfuerzos fueron valientes y dignos de elogio, ${PLAYER}. Tu nombre no será olvidado por los Dúnedain del Norte.'"},
[2260]={"Bring the sword to Thalanir on the slope of the western slag hill","Thalanir is to the west of Pippin and Beregond's location, on the slope of the western slag hill.\
\
Something has distressed Thalanir, and the soldier of Gondor calls for your help.","You also hear Rohirric words of surprise from the south-west","Éomer has asked you to fight your way back to the eastern slag hill in search of Legolas and Gimli.","Protect Reeve Ingbert while he gets to his feet","'Do not worry about me, ${PLAYER}! We are hard-pressed by our foes, but even so they are unable to match us! I have the high ground, for now, and that gives me the advantage!\
\
'The flow of the battle pushed Éomer of Rohan further down the slope, and I fear he will be cut off from the rest of his forces. Find him to the east, and ensure he is safe!'","Thalanir has gone beyond need of a sword. He is slain","Aragorn is atop the eastern slag hill.","While you distract his foes, Ingbert manages to escape","Talk to Pippin on the southern slope of the western slag hill","Thalanir has lost his sword, and the soldier of Gondor has sent you to find a fallen sword on the battlefield to replace the weapon he lost.\
\
Fallen swords can be found around the base of the western slag hill near the bodies of their former wielders.","You hear Éomer's voice above the din, coming from atop the hill","Aragorn calls to you, but you can barely hear him over the sound of the throng","'Help! Can you help me? I have slain a number of Orcs, but the last one staggered away with my sword still stuck in its gut, and now I have no weapon!\
\
'Can you find me a sword? There must be a blade somewhere at the base of the hill, abandoned or dropped by a coward or by a corpse! Without a weapon I cannot do any good for Gondor, and I have no way to protect myself from the throng!'","'Help! Will no one help me? Alas for my injuries!'","Legolas is on the south-western slope of the eastern slag hill.","Éomer is south-east of the western slag hill.\
\
Prince Imrahil asked you to lend your aid to Éomer of Rohan.","Pippin and Beregond are halfway up the southern slope of the western slag hill.","'All those quivers you brought me are spent, ${PLAYER}! There is knife-work to be done all around the hill, and plenty for all!\
\
'I have this fight in hand, but I am certain there will be enough foes for you to slay if you go a-looking for them, or wait for them to seek you out!'","The Orcs charge once again up the side of the hill","'How goes the fighting on the western hill, ${PLAYER}? I trust that Éomer and Imrahil stand still against the forces of Mordor?'\
\
You tell Aragorn that they are still defiant, but injuries have begun to mount among their soldiers.\
\
'So it is with us, but we fight on. It will not be long now, but we will stand until the end.'","Reeve Ingbert has been injured, and his foes press the attack!","Thalanir was slain before you could return to him with a weapon, but there is no time to mourn his ill fortune.","Rohirrim soldiers are being overmatched by their foes to the south-west of Éomer's position at the base of the western slag hill.","'The tide of enemies has swelled, and soon it will crash upon the shore of our shield wall; the tide will not draw back again until we are slain.\
\
'I have taken it upon myself to watch Peregrin the Halfling. He is a soldier of Gondor and now more a member of the Guard than I, but it grieves my heart to think he might fall in this battle. I will protect him if I can, both for his sake and that of my son, whose friendship he possesses.\
\
'Stay wary, ${PLAYER}. I wager our foes have not depleted the stock of their sorceries!'","Talk to Aragorn atop the eastern slag hill","Reeve Ingbert needs time to recover, but he is hard-pressed by his foes!","Calenglad is atop the eastern slag hill.","You found a sword for Thalanir and should bring it to him on the southern slope of the western slag hill.","Defeated enemies at the Battle of the Morannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Orcs surge into the space between the two slag hills, thirsty for blood","Reeve Ingbert is wounded south-east of the base of the western slag hill.","'I am glad the flow of the battle has brought you to me, ${PLAYER}. I wanted to speak with you again.'\
\
You study the Ranger's face and see little of the doubt that troubled him at the Camp of the Host. He seems curiously calm for one who stands amid such tumult.\
\
'After battle was joined, I stood with Aragorn and felled Orc after Orc; soon I lost count of the bodies, but there were ever more to replace them. With each swing of my blade, my sword lost its individuality. It was no longer my weapon only, but it was the weapon of every Dúnadan that ever took up sword for his king.\
\
'With every swing, it seemed to me I was conducting a great music, and the tides of battle moved through and around me in a great swelling chorus. It was a drowning tide, and it swept the foes of Men beneath it, cleansing the land of their foul mark.\
\
'I saw the great beauty of the land returning in full measure, the deep forests growing anew and the rivers flowing swift and clean. I saw twilight pooling in the hills, and the stars reflected in mountain lakes, crisp and cool.\
\
'My eyes were opened to this vision of a new age, and though I saw it only for the span of a breath, I knew in that moment that Gwindeth had been right: such a kingdom would be worth some measure of sorrow. She will see it, though she fade into myth, and men question whether she ever existed at all. But still she will be there, among the falls and waters of Lake Nenuial, and she will remember.\
\
'I am at peace, my friend. The evil of Sauron cannot last, even if every last one of us perishes before his gates. But let us hope we do not, ${PLAYER}! A new age is coming!'","Éomer is on top of the western slag hill.","Come to the aid of the Rohirrim men south-west of Éomer's position","Talk to Éomer atop the western slag hill","'We are being overwhelmed, ${PLAYER}. I sustained an injury from an Orc's lucky swing, and now my arm hangs loosely; I cannot lift up my shield. My men have fallen back a short distance, but they cannot stand long against the tide. They will soon need to retreat once more.\
\
'I ask that you fight across to the eastern slag hill once again; if the battle is turning against us here, it must also be going ill with Aragorn. Look for his friends, the Elf and the dwarf. I saw them from afar, but could not tell how they fared.\
\
'They will need you as the battle goes on.'","'I welcome the concern of the Prince of Dol Amroth, but it is unnecessary! My own battle is well in hand.\
\
'But I have another worry: the terrible flying creatures that carry the robed Nazgûl on their backs. They fall upon my soldiers and bear them aloft with their clutching claws... and then they drop them to the battlefield below. There is no protection from this!\
\
'The safety of my men is my prime concern, for many soldiers of Rohan are unhorsed and such is not their preferred means of doing battle. Over the din of battle I thought I heard Rohirric voices crying out in alarm, to the south-west. That is where you are needed, not here with me!'","The Battle of the Morannon continues unabated as the forces of Mordor press the attack.","Talk to Calenglad atop the eastern slag hill","Talk to Éomer south-east of the western slag hill","Learn what has so distressed Thalanir on the slope of the western slag hill","Not far from Pippin and Beregond's location on the western slag hill, a Gondorian soldier calls desperately for your help.","Book 8, Chapter 6: The Drowning Tide","More foes surge about the base of the hill!","Talk to Beregond on the southern slope of the western slag hill","Talk to Thalanir on the southern slope of the western slag hill","Talk to Legolas on the south-western slope of the eastern slag hill","Legolas has asked you to defeat any enemies you can find as the press of battle surges against the eastern slag hill.","You pick up the sword and hope it will ease Thalanir's mind","Defeat enemies at the Battle of the Morannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find a fallen sword for Thalanir","To the west, a soldier of Gondor cries for help!","'I am glad to see you are still kicking, ${PLAYER}! I am afraid I can't do very much among all these warriors, but I aim to do the best I can for Frodo and poor Sam.\
\
'I miss Merry, but at least he is back in Minas Tirith and won't need to see this fighting, not for today at least. I don't expect I can draw level with some of his deeds, not unless I were to smite that horrible Messenger, but that is all right.\
\
'Be careful, ${PLAYER}! This beastly brood is out for blood!'"},
[2261]={"Cliving is a most impressive sight. Now to find Reeve Athelward","Travel to Cliving in the Norcrofts","'You see before you a woman cursed, ${PLAYER}! In the Autumn my husband Pendrad was slain by Orcs while riding near to the Pillars of the Kings astride the Great River. He had requested that the Reeve send him more riders for that sojourn, but Athelward refused. O cruel fate! Even worse what happened then!'\
\
Mildrith turns and gazes at nothing, overcome by sorrow and anger.\
\
'My son Pendulf argued that Athelward was complicit in his father's death. Had the Reeve sent the riders he should have, Pendrad would not have been overcome by the Orcs! My son was correct, but... Athelward is proud, and would not allow this stain on his honour. He challenged my son to a sword-trial to first blood, if he did not recant his words. Pendulf sustained a slight wound, just a cut, really, but the wound festered and not long afterward he was dead.\
\
'The cruelest cut of all: Athelward adopted my daughter Siflád as his ward, saying she would be safer and better cared-for at Cliving than with me and our grief. All I ask of you is this: go to Cliving and keep your eyes open. I want to learn if Siflád is being treated well. I cannot put my suspicions of Athelward to rest.'","Talk to Cuthred in Cliving","'I have lost everything but my daughter, and I want to make sure she is happy and being treated well. I do not trust Athelward, Reeve or not! Go to Cliving and ensure that Siflád is not being mistreated!'","'Welcome to Cliving, friends from afar! I am Athelward, Reeve of the Norcrofts and Thane of Cliving. My house and hospitality is yours while you stay.'\
\
Athelward listens as you relate the reason for your visit, and a cloud crosses his face.\
\
'Oh, Mildrith. What happened to her should not have happened to any lady of Rohan. Losing first her husband, and then her son... I should have been more understanding of the boy's youthful boldness, but he called my honour into question. The sword-trial is the customary means of resolving such disputes. I did not know his wound would fester in such a way. I would have it back, if I could. Taking young Siflád as my ward seemed the kindest thing to do, but I can understand a mother's grief may make it seem otherwise.\
\
'I will answer any questions of yours, and you are of course free to see Siflád. If it is not too much trouble, could I ask you to help Cuthred, the captain of my guard, with his duties after you have spoken with Siflád?'","'You will find Siflád somewhere around Cliving. She likes to climb the towers and speak with the guards there. Do not forgot to introduce yourself to Cuthred, my captain of the guard, after you have spoken to Siflád.'","'The Reeve sent you to me to help with our problems? Good! We can refuse no offers of help. Cliving has been less affected than some other towns in this riding, but still there are Orcs about and we need to deal with them if we are to keep our people safe.'","Thane Mildrith is suspicious of Reeve Athelward, and wants you to see how he is treating her daughter, newly-taken as his ward.","Talk to Athelward in the Mead Hall of Cliving","'I have been treated well here at Cliving. I like how bustling this city is. It is so much more exciting than my home of Elthengels!'","Cliving is in the Norcrofts, to the north-west of Elthengels.\
\
Thane Mildrith of Elthengels is suspicious of Reeve Athelward of Cliving, who took her daughter Siflád as his ward, and wants you to ensure that Siflád is being treated well.","Siflád is somewhere in Cliving.\
\
Athelward has given you permission to speak to Siflád, his ward.","'I saw you coming to Cliving from afar, and I wondered what your story might be. And now you have come to tell it to me! How wonderful!'\
\
You tell Siflád that you have come from her mother in Elthengels, and that Mildrith worries about her.\
\
'My poor mother. I miss her. Some days I miss her terribly, but knowing that she is still at home eases that ache somewhat. Worse are the days when I miss my father and my brother, for they are never coming home.\
\
'But I am as happy at Cliving as I can be. The Reeve is kind to me, if distant. I think he blames himself for all the grief my family has endured, and wants to make amends for it. I am treated well. Look at the view from the walls! There is just so much more going on here than at Elthengels!\
\
'Yes, I am happy here. I hope my mother is not upset by that, but it is the truth. But tell her I miss her.'","Reeve Athelward is in the Mead Hall of Cliving.\
\
Thane Mildrith wants you to ensure that her daughter Siflád is not being mistreated. The first step is to introduce yourself to Athelward.","Book 8, Chapter 6: The Victor's Ward","Cuthred, the captain of the guard, is by a guard tower in Cliving, west of the Mead Hall.\
\
Reeve Athelward wanted you to help the captain of his guard once you had spoken with Siflád."},
[2262]={"Book 8, Chapter 7: Mordor Triumphant","'The enemy lines have drawn back slightly, but it is only in preparation for their final push. Soon they will march inwards once more, tightening the noose around our position. We must be ready!\
\
'Tell me when you are prepared and we will stand together to rebut them!'","Talk to Aragorn and defy the final enemy assault","Aragorn stands atop the eastern slag hill and prepares to stand against the final enemy attack.","The Host of the West has come to the end of the road as the forces of Mordor prepare their final assault.","'It has been an honour to fight alongside you. Even now, at the end, I do not regret what we have done, or that for which we fought. Let us stand together for a little while longer.\
\
'I am pleased to call you friend, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>To be continued in Volume IV, Book 9, 'The Ring of Power'...</rgb>","'Already the lines begin to push forward once again. Our foes make their final assault!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Aragorn atop the eastern slag hill","Aragorn is on the eastern slag hill, looking out toward the Black Gate."},
[2263]={"Ride to the final marker, north of the third one","Ride to the final marker, north of the third, outside Cliving in the Norcrofts.","'The first marker is east of Cliving. When you encounter it, turn your war-steed to the right, and ride until you reach the next marker. Keep doing that until you have described a great loop in front of the city.\
\
'Defeat any mounted enemies you encounter. Orcs generally do not come very near to Cliving, but they may still be encountered on the bounds.'","Ride to the third marker, west of the second, outside Cliving in the Norcrofts.","Cuthred is in Cliving, near the entrance to the city.\
\
You have ridden the bounds, and should now speak to Cuthred, Cliving's captain of the guard.","Ride to the third marker, west of the second","Book 8, Chapter 7: Riding the Bounds","Ride to the second marker, south of the first","Cuthred is eager to make use of your mounted skill to defend Cliving from the Orcs marauding the Norcrofts.","Talk to Cuthred in Cliving","The last marker is to the north of this one","'An important part of the guard duty my men undertake consists of riding the bounds of Cliving, looking for threats lurking too near the city. If you have a war-steed and the skill to ride it, I would encourage you to help us with this duty, ${PLAYER}. Ride east of Cliving until you see the marker that delineates the bounds, and then turn to the south. Continue this process, turning to your right at each marker, until you have described a great loop around the city.\
\
'Defeat any mounted enemies you encounter on this circuit, ${PLAYER}. You will be doing the people of Cliving a great service.'","'You have ridden the bounds? What did you encounter? My men ride that circuit many times a day, ensuring the safety of the city. Usually it is quiet, but occasionally Orcs or other foes stray within the line and must be fought or driven away.'","Ride to the second marker, south of the first, outside Cliving in the Norcrofts.","You have ridden the bounds and should return to Cuthred","The next marker is to the west","Cuthred has sent you riding the bounds of Cliving: riding east of the city to the first marker, and then turning to your right at each new marker until you have described a great loop around Cliving. He wants you to defeat any mounted enemies you encounter on this circuit as well.","The next marker of your circuit is to the south","Ride to the first marker, east of Cliving"},
[2264]={"Talk to Horn in the Mead Hall of Cliving","Talk to Thane Mildrith in the Mead Hall of the Elthengels","'Mildrith is a handsome woman, thane of an important town, and has no husband. She needs someone to support her during her time of grief, and the Norcrofts need to have unified, strong leaders if it is to survive the dangerous times ahead.'","Talk to Athelward in the Mead Hall of Cliving","'I have been speaking with your companions while you aided my captain of the guard, ${PLAYER}. I am inspired by their example! A man of Rohan, a girl of Dunland, and even an Elf! How is it that folk of such different backgrounds can work together?\
\
'It pains me to see you leave. Can you not stay and help with the maintenance of Cliving? I could use each of your talents to better the state of my people! Discuss among yourselves, if you must, but do not decide to leave so quickly! A strong Cliving makes for a strong Rohan, and these are troublesome times.'","'We need not stay here any longer. Cliving has strong walls, and its defensive position is better than the other towns we have seen. Athelward has little cause to fear Orcs from this fastness. He does not need our help any longer, and we should be off.'","'Athelward has already done what he must to protect his people. Cliving is well-built, on solid foundations with high walls. Any Orcs that stray within the bounds will be repelled.'","Reeve Athelward is in the Mead Hall of Cliving.\
\
Athelward wanted to speak with you and your companions before you depart Cliving.","Nona, Horn, and Corudan are in the Mead Hall of Cliving with Athelward.\
\
You should speak with your companions to determine your next course of action.","Talk to Nona in the Mead Hall of Cliving","'We have been in conversation with Athelward for some time. He has been a gracious host, but we should be leaving.'","Reeve Athelward is in the Mead Hall of Cliving.\
\
You have spoken with your companions and should now tell Athelward your decision.","'I have grown weary of this city already. Too many walls, and not enough open land for my taste, ${PLAYER}.'","'I think it is time to go. The Uruks we follow did not come this close to Cliving, either because it was not on their road or they were afraid of the town's defenders.'","Book 8, Chapter 8: A Second Proposal","'Return to Reeve Athelward in the Mead Hall here in Cliving. He wanted to speak with you before you left Cliving.'","'I do not like to stay in any one place for so long. Let us be gone!'","'I have seen more secure homes, but they were in the mallorns of Lórien. This city has little to fear of Orcs, if you ask for the opinion of an Elf. Athelward should see what he can do to protect the people who live elsewhere in the Norcrofts, but he can do that without our presence.'","'Ah, I understand that you need to be off. You cannot blame me for wanting to keep skilful folk at the disposal of my people. If you have business back at Elthengels, can I ask you to deliver a message for me?'\
\
You murmur your assent, and Athelward rumbles pleasantly.\
\
'Good, good. This may surprise you, ${PLAYER}, but I have no male heir to carry on my line. I love my daughters more than my own life, but a son would release me from the worry that my line will end with me. My wife has been dead this past year, and it is time I began thinking of the future.\
\
'Thane Mildrith of Elthengels has had more than her share of grief these past few months. If it is in my power to heal the sorrow I have caused her, I would do so. I desire her hand in marriage. I will respect her decision in this, but please express to her how strong a union between our families and our cities would be. The Norcrofts could only benefit from such a union.\
\
'It is, ah, not the first time I have asked for her hand. But it will be the last, no matter her decision.'","Athelward has requested to see you about something before you leave Cliving.","Thane Mildrith listens to your message from Reeve Athelward with growing horror and disgust.\
\
'You cannot be serious! That scoundrel! That braggart! His inaction doomed my husband Pendrad to death by the Orcs, and he personally gave my son the wound that killed him! He has the gall to ask for my hand not once, but twice! And to use friends to do it!'\
\
Mildrith brings herself under control, and continues in a quiet, deadly voice.\
\
'I sent you to learn if my daughter Siflád was being treated well by the murderer of her father and brother. Is she?'","Thane Mildrith is in the Mead Hall of Elthengels, south-east of Cliving, in the Norcrofts.\
\
Reeve Athelward wants you to bring his proposal of marriage to Thane Mildrith.","Talk to Corudan in the Mead Hall of Cliving","'For a city of Men, this does seem to be in a defensible place.'","'I want to help the people of Rohan, for they are my flesh and blood, but the people of Cliving are better-defended than most. I would not worry for Cliving's survival in our absence.'","'I was told that Reeve Athelward wanted to speak with you before you depart Cliving. Thank you again for your help, and I hope the Reeve rewards you in suitable fashion for the aid you have graciously given. For Rohan to be safe and well-guarded, the Norcrofts must be as well. I appreciate your help in that regard, and I know the Reeve will agree.'"},
[2265]={"'I do not trust the Reeve. Travel south-west to the river crossing and seize emblems from any Orcs you encounter in the Norcrofts. Bring those emblems to Elfmar and tell him the danger we face is all too real, and we must not rely on Reeve Athelward to protect us.'","Collected Orc Emblems (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Book 8, Chapter 9: South Across the Plains","'If Siflád says she is being treated well, I will keep my complaints to myself. Thank you for easing the worry in a mother's heart. My daughter is strong-willed, and I trust that she will have the sense to send word if her situation changes to ill.\
\
'Turning now to the well-being of my people, I find clarity: we must not rely on the Reeve to protect us. I do not trust him, but more so: I feel in my heart he will see first to the defence of Cliving and not leave his walls to protect the rest of us. The other towns of the Norcrofts do not have Cliving's natural defences.\
\
'You have been a good help to me, but I know you are eager to progress westward in pursuit of the Uruks you seek. Go south-west to Faldham by way of the river crossing, to scout and see if the crossing is held by foes. Also, I ask that you collect emblems from any Orcs you find in the Norcrofts. Show those emblems to Elfhelm, the Thane of Faldham, as proof that we must stand on our own and not rely on Athelward.\
\
'Oh, wait! Elfhelm has gone to the Fords of Isen. His son, Elfmar, must have rule of Faldham in his absence. Show him the emblems.'","Thane Mildrith refuses to either trust or marry Athelward, and wants to ensure that the young Elfmar of Faldham is not relying on Athelward.","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","Scout the river crossing south-west of Elthengels","Bring the Orc Emblems to Elfmar in the Mead Hall of Faldham","Elfmar is the acting thane of Faldham while his father Elfhelm is away.\
\
Thane Mildrith wants you to tell Elfmar of the dangers that face the Norcrofts.","Collect Orc Emblems from the Orcs of the Norcrofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The road runs west of Elthengels for a good way before turning south. At a certain point the southward road crosses the river before it reaches Faldham.\
\
Thane Mildrith wants you to travel to Faldham and collect emblems from Orcs in the Norcrofts to show to Elfmar.","Scouted the river-crossing","'Welcome to Faldham, friends. These are not the first such emblems I have seen. I know the Orcs move across the Norcrofts in great numbers. I am trying to do the best I can to combat them while my father is away at the Fords of Isen.'"},
[2266]={"Defeat foes at the Battle of the Morannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Go to Mithrandir atop the slag-hill and see what he thinks of this new arrival, ${PLAYER}. Quickly!'","You dimly remember Elrohir, one of the sons of Elrond. He stands on the north-west side of the slag-hill and wishes to speak with you.","'You are an adventurer of some renown, I assure you! Perhaps if we survive this battle you can retrace your steps and remember the great adventures you had, ${PLAYER}... but first we must defeat our foes, and survive the onslaught!'","You sustained a blow to the head and remember little of the adventures that brought you to this point, but you are in the middle of a battlefield and must fight to survive!","'I see something on the distant horizon, but I cannot yet make it out. Does a new threat seek to strike from the rear?\
\
'Go to Mithrandir atop the slag-hill and see what he thinks of this new arrival, ${PLAYER}. Quickly!'\
\
You shake your head to clear it, still groggy from the effects of the injury you sustained. Mithrandir, Gandalf... he is the Wizard, of course. You remember him now!","'${PLAYER}! Are you feeling all right? You sustained quite a wallop, my friend, but the beast that managed it has paid for the hit with his life!'\
\
Gimli squints at you curiously.\
\
'Where is the light of recognition in your eye? You don't remember me? I am Gimli, Glóin's son, and we have been through much together! Surely you cannot have forgotten the breadth of our adventures? Across many lands we have journeyed, and now we have come to the Black Gate of Mordor in the company of Aragorn of Gondor and Legolas of Mirkwood.\
\
'You do not remember any of this? You are an adventurer of some renown, I assure you! Perhaps if we survive this battle you can retrace your steps and remember the great adventures you had, ${PLAYER}... but first we must defeat our foes, and survive the onslaught!'","You have awoken on the field of battle outside the Morannon, the Black Gate of Mordor, but all you remember is a hazy confusion of images. What brought you to this point?","'What now, ${PLAYER}? You bring tidings from the sons of Elrond? They did not wish to tell me themselves?'\
\
The Wizard readies a further rebuke for the Elves, but it remains unsaid. His eye lights upon the distant horizon and wonder brightens his face.","Book 9, Chapter 1: A Knock on the Head","Talk to Mithrandir atop the eastern slag-hill during the Battle of the Morannon","Mithrandir stands atop the eastern slag-hill while the Battle of the Morannon rages all about him.\
\
Elrohir has seen something on the horizon and has asked you to tell Mithrandir about this new threat.","Talk to Elrohir on the north-west side of the slag-hill","Defeated foes at the Battle of the Morannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2267]={"Golodir se encuentra en Gath Forthnír, en Angmar, muy al norte de Rivendel.\
\
Gandalf el Gris te ha ordenado que regreses a Gath Forthnír y ayudes a Golodir a buscar a Sara Roblecorazón y el palantír desaparecido.","'Brinda tu ayuda a Golodir en Gath Forthnír. El valeroso Montaraz tiene ante sí una tarea formidable.'","'¿Gandalf el Gris te envió para ayudarme a buscar a Sara Roblecorazón y el palantír desaparecido? Bien, la búsqueda será breve, pues uno de mis exploradores ya la ha encontrado: fuera de Barad Gúlaran, el lugar donde el Rey Brujo estudió sus terribles artes. No ha hecho ningún esfuerzo por ocultar su paradero, pero no se me ocurre por qué sería así.\
\
'Encontrarás Barad Gúlaran en el centro de Nan Gurth, un valle malvado acechado por tumularios y otras criaturas temibles. Barad Gúlaran se encuentra en el centro de una serie de puentes que lo rodean como los radios de una rueda de carro. Sara Roblecorazón fue vista junto a la torre situada en el más sudoriental de estos puentes. Ve y trae de vuelta el palantír.'","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, necesito hablar contigo. He oído hablar de tus aventuras en Carn Dûm y estoy preocupado. Más allá de tus extraños encuentros con ella durante tus viajes, nunca había oído hablar de esta Sara Roblecorazón, y me inquieta.\
\
'Son pocos los que hoy en día siquiera han oído hablar de los palantíri, y menos aún los que se preocuparían lo suficiente por ellos como para robarlos. Más aún, ahora se han vuelto peligrosos, pues Sauron posee la Piedra de Ithil, que sin duda ha doblegado a su voluntad.\
\
'Regresa con Golodir en Gath Forthnír y ayúdalo a buscar a Sara Roblecorazón y el palantír. Temo que de estos acontecimientos solo pueda surgir el mal.'","Mordirith, el Rey Falso, ha sido derrotado y enviado de regreso a Mordor, sin cuerpo, pero la misteriosa Sara Roblecorazón robó el palantír que Mordirith tenía en su poder. Esto preocupa enormemente a Gandalf el Gris.","'Me alegra que hayas venido, ${PLAYER}. Ha llegado el momento de que hablemos de varias cosas. Has sido de gran ayuda para mí y para mis amigos en muchos sentidos. Tenemos mucho de qué hablar muy pronto.'","Libro 9, Capítulo 1: Roblecorazón al descubierto","'Busca a Sara Roblecorazón fuera de Barad Gúlaran, ${PLAYER}. Barad Gúlaran se encuentra en el centro de una serie de puentes que lo rodean como los radios de una rueda de carro. Sara Roblecorazón fue vista junto a la torre situada en el más sudoriental de estos puentes. ¡Ten cuidado! Hay más en esa anciana de lo que aparenta.'","Sara Roblecorazón se encuentra en Barad Gúlaran, en Nan Gurth, en Angmar. Barad Gúlaran se encuentra en el centro de una serie de puentes que lo rodean como los radios de una rueda de carro. Sara Roblecorazón fue vista junto a la torre situada en el más sudoriental de estos puentes.\
\
Sara Roblecorazón ha sido encontrada fuera de Barad Gúlaran. Golodir te ha dicho que tengas cuidado.","'Barad Gúlaran se encuentra en Nan Gurth, en el centro de una serie de puentes que lo rodean como los radios de una rueda de carro. Sara Roblecorazón fue vista junto a la torre situada en el más sudoriental de estos puentes. Encuéntrala y recupera el palantír.'"},
[2268]={"Defeat foes at the Battle of the Morannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Go to Mithrandir atop the slag-hill and see what he thinks of this new arrival, ${PLAYER}. Quickly!'","Mithrandir stands atop the eastern slag-hill while the Battle of the Morannon rages all about him.\
\
Elrohir has seen something on the horizon and has asked you to tell Mithrandir about this new threat.","'The Battle of the Black Gate is nearly done, ${PLAYER}. We must fight for as long as we can, in memory of our friends and in defence of those endangered by Mordor. This may be Sauron's hour, but we will make him earn it with blood!'","Foes encircle the Host of the West as the Battle of the Black Gate rages around you.","Elrohir stands on the north-west side of the slag-hill and wishes to speak with you.","The Host of the West fights desperately for its survival as the forces of Mordor close in for the kill, and the Battle of the Morannon nears its end.","'We must fight for as long as we can, in memory of our friends and in defence of those endangered by Mordor. This may be Sauron's hour, but we will make him earn it with blood!\
\
'Defeat the foes you can during the Battle of the Morannon, my friend!'","'What now, ${PLAYER}? You bring tidings from the sons of Elrond? They did not wish to tell me themselves?'\
\
The Wizard readies a further rebuke for the Elves, but it remains unsaid. His eye lights upon the distant horizon and wonder brightens his face.","'I see something on the distant horizon, but I cannot yet make it out. Does a new threat seek to strike from the rear?\
\
'Go to Mithrandir atop the slag-hill and see what he thinks of this new arrival, ${PLAYER}. Quickly!'","'We must fight for as long as we can, in memory of our friends and in defence of those endangered by Mordor. This may be Sauron's hour, but we will make him earn it with blood!'","Talk to Mithrandir atop the eastern slag-hill during the Battle of the Morannon","Book 9, Chapter 1: Sauron's Hour","Defeated foes at the Battle of the Morannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2269]={"'Did you have more questions of me? I will do whatever Éomer commands, and he has commanded that I answer you.'","'As Reeve Ingbert promised, Éomer has returned from his ride north. He is outside the Mead Hall, ${PLAYER}. Introduce yourself and see what he knows of the Uruks we pursued!'","Book 9, Chapter 1: Éomer","Éomer, the Third Marshal of the Riddermark and the nephew of King Théoden, has come to Eaworth with news of the Uruks you are pursuing.","'I will be at your disposal if Éomer my commander wishes it. Otherwise I have naught to say to you.'","'No Uruks escaped the circle of my riders, but it is possible your friends may have escaped before we closed in. It is a small chance, but it is what Aragorn hoped for, and perhaps his hope was more than hope, and there was truth in it.'\
\
Éomer makes a wry face.\
\
'Perhaps, but Éomer Éomund's son puts stock in cold steel and sunlight on the plains. Without some unlikely dwimmer-craft, I fear the halfling friends Aragorn sought met a sad end.\
\
'The three hunters, however, lived when I left them.'","Éomer is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You have spoken with this lieutenant Éothain, and should now speak again with Éomer.","'Éomer is the nephew of King Théoden. He should be outside the Mead Hall with some of his men. Speak with him about the Uruks we pursued.'","Éothain is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth, with Éomer.\
\
Éomer has told you to ask any questions you have of his man Éothain.","'Éothain will answer any questions you have about your friends or the Uruks they pursued.'","Éomer is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
Corudan told you that Éomer, the nephew of the King, has returned from his ride north in pursuit of the Uruks.","'I am pleased to make your acquaintance, my friend. Yours is the second party I have encountered who sought the Uruks, ${PLAYER}, and to you I say what I said before: the Uruks have all been destroyed, and I saw no sign of any other living thing at the site. The news brought great sadness to the three we encountered.\
\
'The Man was Aragorn son of Arathorn, and his companions were a dwarf, Gimli Glóin's son, and an Elf called Legolas.\
\
'Speak to my man Éothain if you would hear more of these travellers or their prey.'","Talk to Éomer outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth","'If Éomer my commander wishes me to answer your questions, I will do so. Ask what you will and hear my answers. Whether they give you joy or sadness is no concern of mine.'","Talk to Éothain outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth"},
[2270]={"Sara Roblecorazón te ha pedido que la escoltes hasta el interior de Barad Gúlaran.","Libro 9, Capítulo 2: El poder de Roblecorazón","'Esta es, sin duda, una noticia terrible. Pensar que Sara Roblecorazón fue todo este tiempo un agente de Angmar. Si de verdad es la misma Amarthiel de la que solo hablan las leyendas, entonces los días venideros serán oscuros.\
\
'Debo reflexionar sobre lo que has aprendido...'","Golodir está en Gath Forthnír.\
\
Deberías regresar con Golodir y contarle lo sucedido en Barad Gúlaran.","'Gracias por venir, ${PLAYER}. Has sido de gran ayuda para mí durante mis viajes. Sé que tienes muchas preguntas. Hablaremos, pero antes tengo un último favor que pedirte.\
\
'Necesito tu ayuda para llegar al corazón de este lugar. Me temo que no podré hacerlo por mi cuenta. Por favor, ayúdame esta última vez, y te prometo que responderé a todo lo que quieras preguntar.\
\
'Este es un lugar malvado, lleno de horrores indecibles, ¡pero te guiaré con certeza! Solo te pido tu protección.'","Has encontrado a Sara Roblecorazón en Barad Gúlaran, el antiguo retiro del Rey Brujo de Angmar.","Ayuda a Sara Roblecorazón a llegar al corazón de Barad Gúlaran.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para ayudarme, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una Comunidad.</rgb>"},
[2271]={"Talk to Mithrandir on the field of Cormallen","Book 9, Chapter 2: The Eagles Are Coming!","'Once more into battle, my friend!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.</rgb>","'The Eagles are coming! The Eagles are coming!\
\
'Gwaihir the Windlord and his noble subjects fly to the aid of the Host of the West! Let us see if the Nazgûl enjoy this challenge to their superiority in the air, ${PLAYER}! Speak to me and we will wade once more into battle!'","Talk to Mithrandir atop the eastern slag-hill and defy the enemy once again","Mithrandir is atop the eastern slag-hill as the Battle of the Morannon rages all around him.\
\
The Eagles have flown to the aid of the Host of the West, but will it be enough to turn the tide of battle?","'The sum of all my hopes has come to pass, ${PLAYER}, beyond all belief! A great darkness has been conquered; no longer will Sauron trouble Middle-earth, as he did for thousands of years.\
\
'The Quest of the Ring came in the end to the successful conclusion for which this old fool dared not hope, yet hoped for still. What a wonder it is to see this day!'","Gwaihir the Windlord and his subjects have come to the aid of the Host of the West... but will it be enough to turn the tide of battle before the Black Gate?","Mithrandir is on the field of Cormallen, waiting to speak with you."},
[2272]={"'You say some of those tracks led toward Fangorn? They are likely not those of the halflings, for Éomer was certain no one left the site of the battle without his knowledge.\
\
'They may then be the tracks of Aragorn, Legolas, or Gimli. What brought them toward Fangorn?\
\
'What does Horn think? Will he dare the Forest of Fangorn? I will go, and gladly! But he has expressed worry about such places before.'","'We destroyed all of the Uruks just outside the eaves of Fangorn, to the north-west. Go there and see for yourself. If I am here on your return, you are welcome to ride with us when we depart.'","You find a great deal of footprints in the chaos that seem to go nowhere","The ground at Éomer's Vengeance is torn up by a confused muddle of footprints. Can anything be learned from it?","Examine confused footprints at Éomer's Vengeance (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Did you search the site for any sign of your friends? It is to the north-west of Eaworth.'","'Can you tell anything from the confused muddle of footprints?'","Uglúk is beyond caring, not that he would have cared in life.","Talk to Horn at Éomer's Vengeance","Talk to Corudan at Éomer's Vengeance","'My skills do not lie with tracking. I can tell nothing from the confused footprints here. Can you?'","Horn is waiting to speak with you at Éomer's Vengeance, north-west of Eaworth.","'Éomer performed his duty admirably. I fear he may have been too thorough. If your halfling friends were here, they could not have escaped the battle or the burning afterward.'","'You say some of the tracks lead toward Fangorn? That is a peculiar place, and many things are whispered about it in Eaworth, and no doubt in other places less close to the forest.'","'Éomer spoke truly. The Uruks are destroyed.'","'My men caught up with the Uruks just outside the eaves of Fangorn, to the north-west. Their leader, a fierce Uruk whose name seemed to be Uglúk, if the panicked words of his fellows can be trusted, fought me blade to blade after I dismounted.\
\
'I proved the better swordsman, to the pride of Éomund and the shame of whatever disgusting lout claimed to sire Uglúk.\
\
'Ride to this site and look for signs of your missing friends or Aragorn and his two companions. If my men and I are still here when you return, you are welcome to ride south with us to Edoras.'","Éomer's Vengeance can be found to the north-west of Eaworth, just outside the eaves of Fangorn.\
\
Éomer has said you should look for signs of your friends at the site where he encountered and destroyed the Uruks led by Uglúk.","Corudan wishes to speak with you at Éomer's Vengeance.\
\
You have found a number of footprints that seem to go toward the Forest of Fangorn, and should speak to Corudan about it.","Éomer has told you where to go to find the Uruks his men destroyed. It is possible you will find your lost friends at the site.","Uglúk and Éomer fought personally at the end of the battle, but Uglúk did not walk away.","'Gruesome.'","You stare at defeated Uglúk and wonder if Boromir rests comfortably, from wherever it is he watches, now that the leader of the band that set upon him is no more.","You find a great deal of footprints, some of which lead north-west","The reek of the burning rises still from the site where Éomer destroyed the Uruks","You pry your eyes away from Uglúk and resolve to search for sign of the halflings","Examine the remains of Uglúk","'What thinks Horn? Will he dare the Forest of Fangorn?'","Book 9, Chapter 2: Uglúk's End","'Éomer did his work well. Perhaps too well, if your halfling friends were destroyed along with the Uruks.'","Uglúk has no opinion about your next move.","'I see how Corudan looks at me. He thinks I fear to go into Fangorn.'\
\
Horn looks at you with his piercing grey eyes.\
\
'I went into another ill-omened wood with you, not long ago, ${PLAYER}, do you remember? There I took a grievous wound, an injury from which I will never recover. Nor would I wish to heal that hurt!\
\
'I will follow you into Fangorn. What can be done to me that I should fear?'","Find Éomer's Vengeance, north-west of Eaworth"},
[2273]={"Puedes encontrar aliados en Ost Guruth, en las Tierras Solitarias, Esteldín, en las Quebradas del Norte, y en lugares familiares para todos los pueblos: Combe para los hobbits, la raza de los Hombres y los Beórnidas, y Gondamon para Enanos y Elfos.\
\
Golodir te ha pedido que regreses a tres lugares donde Sara Roblecorazón fue vista en el pasado y hables con aliados en esos sitios.","'No one should ever read this.'","Golodir está preocupado por que los Caballeros de Mordirith sean puestos al servicio de Amarthiel.","Golodir está en Gath Forthnír en Angmar.\
\
Deberías regresar con Golodir y decirle que la tarea ha sido completada.","Libro 9, Capítulo 3: La petición de Golodir","'Los Caballeros de Mordirith deben ser detenidos, ${PLAYER}. Han sido enviados lejos, a saber con qué fechorías.'","Habla con Golodir","'Has prestado un gran servicio a los Pueblos Libres de Eriador. Gracias.\
\
'Mientras no estabas, hablé con Laerdan sobre Amarthiel, y parece que es con él con quien deberías hablar. Parece saber mucho más sobre esta mujer que nadie.\
\
'Hablaremos más de esto en breve.'","Habla con aliados en Combe o Gondamon, en Ost Guruth y en Esteldín"},
[2274]={"El condestable Sotomonte se encuentra fuera de la Comba y la Cresta, en Combe, al suroeste del campamento del caballero.\
\
Tras haber derrotado al Caballero de Mordirith, regresa con el condestable Sotomonte y hazle saber que la amenaza ha sido eliminada.","El Caballero de Mordirith puede encontrarse cerca de un ídolo maligno en el bosque de Chet, al noreste de Combe.\
\
El condestable Sotomonte te dijo cómo encontrar la amenaza en el bosque de Chet, que podría ser el caballero que buscas.","Libro 9, Capítulo 3: Viaje a Combe","'¿Era el caballero que buscabas y lo has matado? Estoy impresionado. No es habitual que tengamos gente de tu calaña por estas tierras.\
\
'Gracias por tu ayuda. Por favor, dile a tu amigo Golodir que tu hazaña está cumplida, y me aseguraré de que hagamos algo con ese ídolo espantoso. Parece atraer una cantidad terrible de atención.'","'¿Por qué vienes a molestarme, imbécil? Tengo muchas cosas de las que ocuparme para Mordirith...\
\
'¿Qué? ¿Has derrotado al senescal y dejado su trono en manos de Amarthiel? ¡Prepárate para morir!'","'¿Golodir? Nunca he oído hablar de él, pero suena como uno de esos Montaraces, como Toradan. Si se parece en algo a como era Toradan, no veo motivo alguno para dudar de él.\
\
'Bueno, no estoy seguro de ese caballero del que hablas, pero hay una nueva amenaza en el bosque de Chet, mucho más poderosa que cualquier cosa con la que te hayas cruzado en el pasado. Quizá sea el caballero que estás buscando.\
\
'Puedes encontrarlo en su campamento, cerca del ídolo maligno del bosque de Chet. No es difícil de encontrar, al noreste de aquí.'","Encuentra al Caballero de Mordirith","El condestable Sotomonte mencionó que hay una nueva amenaza en el bosque de Chet y que quizá sea el caballero que buscas."},
[2275]={"Daervunn te ha advertido de una nueva amenaza al norte, cerca de la entrada a Ram Dúath, y de que quizá sea el Caballero que buscas.","Habla con Daervunn en Esteldín","'¿Golodir te envió? Eso está bien, pues significa que su espíritu ha sido renovado.\
\
'Hay grandes peligros por doquier, y muchos han hablado de un nuevo mal procedente de Angmar cerca de la entrada a Ram Dúath. Estoy bastante seguro de que se trata del Caballero que buscas.\
\
'Ve a la entrada de Ram Dúath y lo encontrarás... pero ten cautela, hay muchos angmarim en ese lugar. No será un camino fácil.'","'Mordirith no puede ser detenido. Incluso si crees haberlo derrotado, nunca estará verdaderamente muerto. Fue el Rey del Sur en vida mortal y será Rey del Norte como señor espectral.\
\
'La voluntad de Mordirith perdura, lo cual es más de lo que puedo decir de ti, patético ${RACE}.'","Libro 9, Capítulo 3: Viaje a Esteldín","El Caballero de Mordirith puede encontrarse cerca de Ost Crithlanc, al noreste de Esteldín.\
\
Daervunn te habló de una nueva amenaza en el norte, que podría ser el Caballero que buscas.","Daervunn se encuentra en Esteldín, al sur de la boca de Ram Dúath.\
\
Tras haber derrotado al Caballero de Mordirith, deberías regresar con Daervunn y hacerle saber tu éxito.","'Lo has hecho bien, ${PLAYER}. Golodir estará complacido con tu éxito.\
\
'Ahora puedo dedicar mi atención a enviar más ayuda al Norte, ya que has allanado el camino.\
\
'Regresa con Golodir y hazle saber de tu victoria.'","Encuentra al Caballero de Mordirith"},
[2276]={"El Caballero de Mordirith podría encontrarse al norte de Gondamon.\
\
Mathi Manofirme sugirió que la amenaza al norte de Gondamon podría ser el Caballero que buscas.","'¿Así que no solo encontraste a tu Caballero, sino que además lo derrotaste? Estoy impresionado. Gracias por tus esfuerzos. No es habitual que una figura tan poderosa como tú honre estas tierras.\
\
'Por favor, dile a tu amigo Golodir que has cumplido con tu parte aquí en Gondamon.'","'¿Golodir? No estoy familiarizado con él, pero los Montaraces nos ayudaron a alcanzar la paz aquí, así que con gusto te ayudaré en esto.\
\
'Creo que tal vez sepa dónde se oculta tu hombre. Ha habido muchos informes de nuevas amenazas al norte de aquí. En su mayoría son rumores, pero varias de mis patrullas no han regresado. Quizá podrías investigar este problema por nosotros.\
\
'Infórmame si tienes éxito.'","Mathi Manofirme te ha advertido de una nueva amenaza al norte de Gondamon y de que quizá sea el Caballero que buscas.","Mathi Manofirme se encuentra en Gondamon, al sur del campamento del Caballero.\
\
Tras haber derrotado al Caballero de Mordirith, deberías regresar con Mathi Manofirme y hacerle saber que has tenido éxito.","Libro 9, Capítulo 3: Viaje a Gondamon","Encuentra al Caballero de Mordirith","'¿Por qué vienes a molestarme, imbécil? Tengo muchas cosas para hacer aquí para Mordirith...\
\
'¿Qué? ¿Has derrotado al senescal y dejado su trono en manos de Amarthiel? ¡Prepárate para morir!'"},
[2277]={"Frideric el Anciano se encuentra en Ost Guruth, al norte y al oeste de Harloeg.\
\
Tras haber derrotado al Caballero de Mordirith, deberías regresar con Frideric el Anciano y hacerle saber tu éxito.","Frideric el Anciano te ha advertido de una nueva amenaza en los pantanos del sur y de que quizá sea el Caballero que buscas.","El Caballero de Mordirith puede encontrarse en algún lugar de Harloeg, al sur y al este de Ost Guruth.\
\
Frideric el Anciano sugirió que podrías encontrar al Caballero de Mordirith en el pantano del sur.","'Gracias por ayudarnos. Temía enviar a más hombres a Harloeg, pues mi pueblo es escaso.\
\
'Has ayudado enormemente a la gente de Ost Guruth y, por lo que cuentas, a todos los Pueblos Libres.\
\
'Gracias de nuevo, ${PLAYER}.'","'Es una pena que hayas viajado tan lejos solo para ser derrotado. La derrota de Mordirith no significa nada. No tienes idea de qué fuerzas están actuando en Eriador, y morirás sin saberlo.'","Encuentra al Caballero de Mordirith","'Nunca he oído hablar de Golodir, pero si es un Montaraz, como dices, ¿por qué habríamos de ayudarlo? Los Montaraces no nos ayudaron cuando lo necesitamos, y nos vimos obligados a depender de las sombras de los Perjuros para conquistar nuestra libertad.\
\
'Aun así, hemos perdido a muchos hombres valiosos explorando Harloeg en estos días. Se rumorea que Angmar está implicado, así que supongo que ese es el mejor lugar para buscar. Ve a Harloeg y busca a tu Caballero malvado.\
\
'Cuando hayas purgado este mal, regresa conmigo.'","Libro 9, Capítulo 3: Viaje a las Tierras Solitarias"},
[2278]={"'Do not let me keep you, ${PLAYER}! Our heroic friends have been through much, but I know they will want to speak with you now that the danger has passed! Frodo and Sam have rested from their journey, but it will take more than these few days to recover from the exertion of their ordeal!\
\
'You will find them in a bower on the south-eastern side of the field.'","Book 9, Chapter 3: On the Field of Victory","Talk to Mithrandir on the field of Cormallen","Sam beckons for you to speak to him instead of Frodo","'Now that he is awake, you should speak to Frodo. He is still recovering from his ordeal, but I know he will wish to see you.'","Talk to Frodo in the bower south-east of the field of Cormallen","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. I am glad you have returned to me, for there is a small matter about which I wish to speak with you.'","Éomer of Rohan and Prince Imrahil of Dol Amroth are on the field of Cormallen.","'That was quite a feast, and most well-deserved! It is not every day that an evil such as Sauron is laid low, after all! It seems as if Elrond and Gandalf made the right choice back in Rivendell, doesn't it? Frodo Baggins may not be a dwarf, but he has proven to have the determination of my kind!\
\
'All these hobbits seem to have it! Young Peregrin Took could use a portion less of it, if you ask me. He is fortunate I saw him lying beneath that troll before the Black Gate, and heaved the great beast off him. I might have sworn up and down that he was dead, and yet he lives and is up and about already. He has caused me so much trouble, and yet still I am fond of him for all the bother.\
\
'There will be days of merriment aplenty, ${PLAYER}, but sometime in the weeks ahead I must set my eyes to the north and return to the Lonely Mountain. My mind is full of ideas, and what dwarf wants that? I must speak to the King of Durin's Folk and let these ideas out before they do me some harm! Ha ha ha ha!'","Talk to Radanir on the field of Cormallen","Peregrin Took and Meriadoc Brandybuck are on the field of Cormallen.","Mithrandir is on the field of Cormallen.","'Please forgive Sam, ${PLAYER}. He has spent so long worrying about me that I think it became natural for him, especially after our experience in Mordor.'\
\
Frodo shivers, despite the warmth in the air.\
\
'I know Sam does not want to talk about it, but I would never have made it to the Fire without him. If you had the joy of knowing old Hamfast, you would know that Gamgees love to talk, but the Gaffer and his son would prefer most any topic to speaking about themselves. So it falls on me to tell you that I may have carried the burden, but it was the strength of my dear Sam that guided me through despair and across the dead lands. And at Mount Doom...'\
\
Frodo's face is pale, and he stops speaking. He seems relieved when Pippin breaks the silence with a boisterous cheer.","'I am glad to have this time to catch up with Frodo and Sam. Pippin and I are knights of the City and of the Mark, respectively, and we have been kept busy with those duties. At last we can chat, and they do not want to talk about it, or at least not in the detail our curiosities demand!\
\
'Well, I can respect that. After the Pelennor Battle I could barely stand to tell Pippin what befell poor Théoden. In time, perhaps it will become easier for them to talk about the journey. It was like that with Éowyn. By the time I left Minas Tirith to come here, she had emerged from silent sorrows and had taken to speaking with Steward Faramir in the gardens. It seems to me that time and distance helps many shadows lessen.\
\
'I wonder why Éowyn has not yet arrived? Éomer King called her hither, but she has not yet come to Cormallen.'","Radanir and Aragorn are on the field of Cormallen.","'Now that he is awake, you should speak to Frodo. He is still recovering from his ordeal, but I know he will wish to see you. You will find him in a pleasant bower in the south-east of the field of Cormallen.'","'Sauron is no more, and can no longer burden Middle-earth. Some of my folk may come to live in this land for a time, and I delight in knowing that it will remain green and growing for years to come, untroubled by Sauron's evil. But I will not stay long here. \
\
'The first days of Gondor's new year will be filled with happiness, and I share the joy of its people, but my heart has another longing. The Sea calls to me, and I would follow.\
\
'But I will not follow that longing just yet, ${PLAYER}. Food, and drink, and celebration must come first. We have all seen enough of darkness. Let us enjoy some lighter fare, and savour the taste!'","Talk to Éomer on the field of Cormallen","'If Frodo says he's fine, I suppose it is all right. But I do wish he would get more rest! He went through a great deal in Mordor, as you know!'","Radanir looks at you grimly.\
\
'I was speaking with some of the others, and they agree that you have a decision to make. Weigh your options carefully, ${PLAYER}, for this could be a costly choice.'\
\
A rare smile illuminates Radanir's features.\
\
'You need to choose the tavern at which we can all meet, now that the Grey Company has accomplished its mission and we have fulfilled our oaths. You agreed to buy me three mugs of ale, as I recall, so you will want to select an establishment with a barkeep who sets a reasonable price. I recommend the Forsaken Inn, east of Bree. The fare is of low quality, but it was Candaith's favourite, and that is enough for me.\
\
'We will not depart just yet! There is work still to be done for Aragorn to claim his throne, and many of us wish to help him set his kingdom in order. Some of us will remain here in the south-lands, even when others return to their homes. I think I will travel with Lothrandir when he returns to Sûri-kylä; it is a long road, and he would welcome the company. Also, there is a lake on the way to Forochel, and I promised a friend I would see it for myself.'","Frodo is about to speak when Sam interrupts and beckons you to him.","Talk to Peregrin Took in the bower","Samwise Gamgee is in the bower in the south-east of the field of Cormallen.","Talk to Legolas on the field of Cormallen","'My uncle Théoden is avenged. Sauron is no more. It cannot be questioned that soldiers of Rohan and of Gondor played their parts, but in the end the fatal blow was struck by two hobbits alone in the Black Land. It is an amazement to me!\
\
'I have heard that the Nazgûl came to fiery ends, speeding back to Mordor at their Master's call when he learned of his true peril. With my mind's sight I can see them, caught in the blast of the flaming mountain: eight fireballs scorching the sky, plummeting earthward and shrieking their final desperate cries.\
\
'I wish that those of my soldiers who were carried aloft by those creatures during the Battle of the Black Gate could have known the fate their murderers would shortly suffer. It gives me great satisfaction to picture it on their behalf. Ride, Eorlingas, ride! You are avenged!'","Frodo Baggins is in the bower on the south-east of the field of Cormallen.","Talk to Meriadoc Brandybuck in the bower","'I beg your pardon, ${PLAYER}, but Mister Frodo needs his rest. So many folk have come calling on him, some of them even bending the knee, and those who bowed the lowest were kings and princes themselves! Now, my master deserves every bit of it, but some of these even bowed to me, and I can't say I liked that at all! Frodo carried the real burden, and he did all the hard work, if you ask me.\
\
'Can you believe that old Strider turned out to be a king as well? When I first met him, I said to myself, \\qThis Strider has a kingly air about him, doesn't he, Sam?\\q but I didn't say anything of it to my master or to Merry or Pippin. There was enough going on in Bree that there wasn't time for it.\
\
'So many high important folk paying attention to hobbits! There's no mistaking that these are queer times!'","Frodo Baggins is in a bower on the south-eastern side of the field of Cormallen, recovering from his ordeal.","Talk to Frodo Baggins in the bower","The field of Cormallen has become a field of victory, and friends and allies share fellowship and speak of their accomplishments in the overthrow of Sauron.","Talk to Gimli on the field of Cormallen","'I do not think I want to speak of Mordor anymore, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Samwise Gamgee in the bower","'The fall of Sauron worked a great madness in his servants, ${PLAYER}, and many of them despaired once he was gone. Did some spell hold them ensorcelled while he yet lived, and death broke his hold upon them? I cannot say, but I did witness that many of the Orcs cast themselves into pits or fell upon their weapons once he was gone.\
\
'There were others among his servants that were made more ferocious by the fall of their master, and these fought long and with desperation. Some of them fled back through the ruins of the gate; I do not doubt that my King will send me against these others, in time.\
\
'But that is a thought for tomorrow. Today we celebrate the fall of Sauron!'","Talk to Prince Imrahil on the field of Cormallen","'Three cheers for Frodo Baggins, who destroyed the Ring! And save a cheer or two for Samwise Gamgee, who got to go with him and managed to miss out on a great deal of the fighting! Oh, I'm only teasing. I know that Sam saw some danger, although he doesn't want to talk about any of it. Both he and Frodo are awfully tight-lipped about their journey in Mordor.\
\
'I don't blame them. Battles are nasty things. Merry and I certainly ended up seeing more than our share, and it was all very dirty and confusing. I wouldn't recommend it! Do you know that a troll fell on top of me?\
\
'It's easy to laugh about now that it's done, but no one was laughing when we were in the thick of the fighting. I am glad we are still here, ${PLAYER}. Three cheers for Frodo and his friends!'","Legolas and Gimli are on the field of Cormallen."},
[2279]={"'Such marvels! When I was a boy, I heard tell of the tree-men in Eaworth, of course, but I thought they were just tales.'","'I believe you need to slay one more Orc beneath the eaves of Fangorn if you are to draw level with Corudan and myself. One Orc more, ${PLAYER}.'","'Hroom... boom... broom.'\
\
The great creature stares down at you with baleful eyes. Then it speaks again.\
\
'What are these small creatures that come among the trees? So many... so many... hroom... but Gandalf saw to the Elf, the Man, and the Dwarf...\
\
'Treebeard has his guests... and others come among the trees. Baldbark was told not to let others disturb the meetings... hroom... boom... broom.\
\
'You should leave... it is not a time for you... hroom...'","'I would investigate a mysterious voice if I heard one. So would my sister. You should do the same, ${PLAYER}. You heard it coming from a misty dell to the south of the Orc camp beneath the eaves?'","Talk to Corudan at Éomer's Vengeance","'My father told me his men had heard Orc axes beneath the eaves of Fangorn. There must be a camp of the creatures somewhere to the north of here, among the trees. That is the way the tracks go, are they not?\
\
'We should go to this camp of Orcs and slay them. While we do, let us keep our eyes open for your friends. If we cannot help them directly, perhaps this will help them in an indirect fashion.'","You heard a voice coming from a misty dell south of the Orc camp beneath the eaves of Fangorn, and should investigate.","'If half of the stories I have heard about Fangorn are true, the Orcs that Horn thinks to find beneath the eaves will likely not be there long. But let us slay them while we may. They are Orcs, after all.'","Talk to the owner of the mysterious voice, south of the Orc camp","You hear a voice coming from a misty hollow south of the Orc camp!","There is a camp of Orcs beneath the Eaves of Fangorn, north of Éomer's Vengeance.\
\
Horn wants you to go to the Orc camp beneath the Eaves of Fangorn and defeat the creatures there. You are also to keep your eyes open for your friends while you do.","Defeat Orcs beneath the Eaves of Fangorn (7/8)","Corudan is at Éomer's Vengeance, south-east of the eaves of Fangorn.\
\
You encountered an Ent called Baldbark, and he sent you out of Fangorn with little ceremony.","Defeated Orcs beneath the Eaves of Fangorn (${CURRENT}/8)","Book 9, Chapter 3: Orcs Beneath the Eaves","Tracks led from Éomer's Vengeance into the Forest of Fangorn, and you should do what you can to follow them.","'It is a day for wonders, ${PLAYER}! Mithrandir lives, as you said, and he has returned to where he is most needed: a kingdom beset on all sides by danger! If Aragorn, Legolas, and Gimli are not safe with Mithrandir, they will not be safe anywhere!'\
\
Corudan's face lights up with a brilliant smile.\
\
'And the second wonder: I did not dare to hope the tree-herders still walked in Middle-earth! But today I have met an Ent, heard his speech, and was told in no uncertain terms I was not welcome!'\
\
Corudan is more pleased than you can ever remember seeing him.\
\
'What a delight! Asked to leave his forest by an Ent! Did he say his name was Baldbark? Then I will call him Rúdhrif in the language of my people, and I will keep this encounter near to my heart!'","'An Orc camp must lie north of here, beneath the eaves of Fangorn. Let us go there and defeat the creatures. Keep your eyes open for your friends, as well. If we cannot help them directly, slaying these Orcs may help indirectly.'","Defeat Orcs beneath the Eaves of Fangorn (${CURRENT}/8)","'Did we not agree that we would each slay eight Orcs? I really believed we did. And you have slain only seven.'","'A voice, you say? We should investigate it! Where did you hear it? A misty dell south of the Orc camp beneath the eaves of Fangorn?'"},
[2280]={"Libro 9, Capítulo 4: El rastro de Amarthiel","'Ve y habla con Laerdan. Es urgente que encuentres a Amarthiel.'","Laerdan se encuentra al otro lado de la cueva en Gath Forthnír.\
\
Golodir te indicó que hablaras con Laerdan para saber cómo puedes ayudarlo a seguir el rastro de Amarthiel.","Calenglad se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces en Tinnudir, en la orilla oriental del Lago Evendim.\
\
Laerdan te indicó que fueras al campamento de los Montaraces en Evendim para hablar con el montaraz Calenglad.","'¿Laerdan y Golodir te enviaron? Entonces debe de haber más de lo que pensábamos tras la creciente presencia de los angmarim. Me alegra que hayan enviado a ${PLAYERNAME:un héroe probado[m]|una heroína probada[f]} para ayudar.'","'Me cuesta confesar que sé más sobre Amarthiel que quizá cualquier otro ser vivo, y aun así no conocía nada de sus secretos como Sara Roblecorazón. Se ha vuelto mucho más poderosa de lo que había imaginado... de hecho, la creía muerta desde la Batalla de Fornost.\
\
'No importa. Está viva, y mi persecución debe continuar. Creo que se dirige a Evendim. Tiene un palantír; supongo que el de Osgiliath, el señor del sur, que se creía perdido en el Anduin; y si alberga alguna esperanza de conservar el poder, necesitará comunicarse a menudo con el Ojo sin Párpado. También podría usar el palantír para encontrar a Narchuil, ese símbolo de poder que perdió hace mucho tiempo.\
\
'Entonces, el único lugar que le queda es Annúminas, pues puede que el pedestal donde una vez reposó el palantír de Annúminas todavía esté en pie. Deberías ir a Evendim cuanto antes y hablar con Calenglad. Se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces en Tinnudir, en la orilla oriental.\
\
'Es mi mayor deseo que volvamos a encontrarnos en un día más feliz, ${PLAYER}.'","'Calenglad se encuentra en Evendim, en el campamento de los Montaraces en Tinnudir. El campamento está en la orilla oriental del Lago Evendim, en una isla. ¡Date prisa!'","'Lo has hecho bien con tareas muy difíciles, pero todavía queda más por hacer. Mientras estabas fuera, hablé con Laerdan sobre Amarthiel y sobre adónde podría dirigirse con el palantír. Necesitamos encontrarla con rapidez y poner fin a sus intrigas.\
\
'Sin embargo, Laerdan sabe mucho más de lo que yo creía. Ve y habla con él para saber cómo puedes ayudarlo a encontrar a Amarthiel.'","Golodir quedó complacido con tu éxito en el sur, pero sigue preocupado por Amarthiel y por su posesión de un palantír.","'Debes hacer lo que Laerdan diga. Date prisa, pues considero que el tiempo apremia.'"},
[2281]={"'Hello again, ${PLAYER}. Gandalf came by and had a task for Sam; the two of them have gone off somewhere. If you're looking to speak with them they are not here right now. My mind is still caught in a whirlwind of confusion. I cannot believe that the Quest is over! I am not used to the idea that the Ring is gone! In Mordor, I would shut my eyes and still see it, burning inside my mind, tearing me apart. But it has been destroyed.\
\
'Pippin insists that I write everything down before I forget the details, but... I do not want to remember them, ${PLAYER}. I do not! If my friends knew the truth about what happened within Mount Doom...'\
\
Frodo shakes his head, and holds up his injured hand. It has been wrapped in a bandage and treated with care by Aragorn, but you remember the grisly sight of it.\
\
'I laboured beneath the burden of the Ring as Sam and I crawled through Mordor and up the slope of Mount Doom. Much of the journey is hazy to me, even now, and dear Sam told our friends most of the tale. But he did not tell it all. I think he wanted to spare me the shame of it. Ah, that is the truth: shame, deserved shame!\
\
'Sam said that Gollum tracked us to the Mountain, and at the end the pitiful creature overpowered us and stole the Ring before we could cast it into the Fire. But that is not the truth, not all of it.\
\
'I... I will tell you the truth, ${PLAYER}. I want to do what is right.'","Frodo is inside the bower that was prepared for him on the field of Cormallen.","Enter his bower in the south-east of the field of Cormallen and find Frodo","Talk to Frodo and experience 'Interlude: The Precious, At Last' or read the shortened account instead","'Frodo's ordeal in Mordor was a costly one, and it has left its mark upon him. No, I do not speak only of the finger he lost to Gollum's biting teeth! I speak of a mark that none can see, but still persists, casting a pall upon his heart.\
\
'He has retired to the bower that was prepared for him. I will see that Samwise has a task to undertake that will free Frodo from his watchful gaze, and perhaps we can learn what still troubles our victorious Ringbearer.'","In the depths of the Mountain of Fire, Frodo Baggins at last reaches the Cracks of Doom, the only place where the One Ring can be destroyed. As he stands at the brink, he makes a decision that will determine the fate of the Ruling Ring and the power of Sauron that is bonded within.\
\
But he is not alone...","'You know the truth now, ${PLAYER}. So many good people suffered, so many good people died, so that I could get to the Mountain. And at the end, I could not bring myself to do what everyone depended upon me to do! How can I live with the shame of it?'\
\
You tell Frodo that what little you learned of the Ring during your own adventure has taught you that it was an artifact of great power and great evil, and that it could work its temptation upon even those of good hearts and strong will.\
\
'Maybe you are right, ${PLAYER}. Your words do not erase my shame, but even though the Ring is gone I can still remember how I felt in that moment, standing above the Fire. I did not wish to destroy it. I would have rather died than allow it to be taken from me. I cannot imagine how Sméagol survived for so long after the Ring came to Bilbo. Or perhaps I can. It was the desire for it that drove him, and that feeling is familiar to me, and painful.\
\
'Pippin worries that I will forget the details of my journey if I do not write them down? But the details are etched upon my memory. I cannot believe that I would forget how I felt in that moment. But perhaps I should write it all down. Perhaps I should write it all, and it will serve as a reminder and as a warning. A reminder that Good purpose can go ill, but that Evil purpose might still serve Good. And a warning not to judge either too readily.'","Talk to Frodo inside the bower","'Frodo has retired to the bower that was prepared for him. I will see that Samwise has a task to undertake that will free Frodo from his watchful gaze, and perhaps we can learn what still troubles our victorious Ringbearer.'","Mithrandir has asked you to speak with Frodo and ease his mind, if you can.","Frodo is inside the bower that was prepared for him in the south-east of the field of Cormallen.","Book 9, Chapter 4: Frodo Baggins and the Ring of Power","'I will tell you the truth of what happened inside Mount Doom, ${PLAYER}. I want to do the right thing.'","Frodo smiles weakly at you as you approach"},
[2282]={"Talk to Éomer and ride south to the Stone of Wyrgende","Éomer is standing by the Stone of Wyrgende.\
\
Éomer wishes to speak with you before departing for Snowbourn.","'Thank you for your help, friend. I am glad to have you and your companions as allies when danger strikes!\
\
'Orcs and Wargs are the type of danger I am not afraid to face. Threats of a more otherworldly nature... those I cannot abide. Still, Éomund's son will face such dangers with as bold a heart as he can manage, the bolder still with allies such as you at his side!'","'Horn wanted to return to Eaworth as quickly as possible to see if Éomer remained there. We should return to Eaworth at once, now that we are assured of the safety of our mutual friends.'","'Éomer and his men are still here, ${PLAYER}. I spoke with him briefly, and he said we were welcome to make the southward journey with him. He has a few places he would like to stop on the way, including... well, including the Stone of Wyrgende.'\
\
Horn sighs heavily.\
\
'Do you remember, ${PLAYER}? It was the story I told by that camp-fire on our journey by boat down the Anduin, with Corudan and... with Nona. King Fengel and his line were cursed: no heir of Fengel's line would survive to sit long upon the throne of Rohan. Many thought that the curse had been broken by Prince Théodred, but it seems it was not so.\
\
'Éomer wishes to visit the Stone, and you must understand why: with the Prince dead, he as Théoden's nephew is now next in line for the throne. He is of King Fengel's line, and the Curse must now be ever in his thoughts. Speak to him, but gently! Who can know what it must be like to live under such a curse?'","'Éomer is outside the Mead Hall. Speak to him and tell him we are ready to accompany him when he departs.'","Horn is already back at Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale.\
\
You have been reassured that your friends are safe, and now you should travel back to Eaworth with Horn and Corudan.","Talk to Éomer by the Stone of Wyrgende","Book 9, Chapter 4: The Stone of Wyrgende","'You are welcome to ride with my men and me on our southward road, but there is one place I have planned to stop before we reach Snowbourn.\
\
'Have you heard of Wyrgende's Stone? It is involved in a tale of Rohan, and I am... quite interested in seeing it again.'","Talk to Éomer outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Éomer is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale.\
\
Éomer is ready to ride south when you are, but he has a number of destinations he wants to visit before turning for Edoras and home.","'Did you learn anything about your friends from the site where we destroyed the Uruks?'\
\
Éomer listens to your account, and marvels particularly at your description of Baldbark.\
\
'What a strange tale you weave, ${PLAYER}! To think such peculiar things persist under the light of the sun in these days!\
\
'Tell me when you are ready to depart, and my men will be ready. There are a few sites I would have us visit on our way south to Snowbourn, and from there we will go to Edoras.'","'Rúdhrif's words were reassuring, were they not? He told us, in his way, that Merry and Pippin were safely in the company of \\qTreebeard,\\q who can only be an Ent. And the Man, dwarf, and Elf of which he spoke must be Aragorn, Gimli and Legolas. If they are now in the presence of Mithrandir, surely we need worry about them no longer.\
\
'Let us return to Eaworth and see if Éomer remains there with his men. Horn wished to be off immediately. We should speak with him when we are back at Eaworth.'","You have received reassuring words from Baldbark concerning your friends, and can now turn your thoughts fully toward aiding Éomer and Rohan.","Talk to Horn in Eaworth","Éomer is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
Éomer said you were welcome to ride south with his men when he departed Eaworth."},
[2283]={"'Estas son noticias verdaderamente graves. Enviaré aviso a Elrond de Rivendel y a Golodir, mi pariente. Necesitamos ayuda, y con rapidez, si Mordor está tan profundamente involucrado.\
\
'Gracias por tu ayuda en esto y por despachar a uno de los lugartenientes Númenóreanos Negros de Amarthiel. Hemos asestado un golpe, pero a menos que lo sigamos con otro más certero, Amarthiel sin duda se recuperará y buscará aplastarnos por completo.'","Calenglad se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces en Tinnudir, en la orilla oriental del Lago Evendim.\
\
Deberías hablar con Calenglad de nuevo, ahora que has descubierto los planes de Amarthiel.","Libro 9, Capítulo 5: La esperanza de Amarthiel","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para buscar a Amarthiel? Se ha ordenado a mis hombres que te protejan cueste lo que cueste.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una Comunidad.</rgb>","Descubre los planes de Amarthiel en Annúminas.","Calenglad se encuentra en el campamento de los Montaraces en Tinnudir, en la orilla oriental del Lago Evendim.\
\
Habla con Calenglad cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir hacia Annúminas.","Calenglad te ha informado de que recientemente ha aumentado el número de angmarim en las afueras de Annúminas.","'La presencia de los angmarim en Annúminas es sumamente inquietante, y por lo que me has contado, creo que es el mejor lugar para buscar a Amarthiel. Aún no puede haberse internado demasiado en la ciudad en ruinas, y no podemos permitir que avance más.\
\
'Te permitiré llevar contigo a cinco de mis hombres. Hagas lo que hagas, debes regresar con información sobre sus planes. Esto es de la mayor urgencia para los Dúnedain y para Eriador. No podemos permitir que el Ojo sin Párpado ejerza más influencia en esta región.\
\
'Habla conmigo de nuevo cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir.'","'Tus noticias son funestas, pero al menos podemos preparar una defensa contra Amarthiel.'"},
[2284]={"Book 9, Chapter 5: South to Snowbourn","'I am ready to continue our ride south to Snowbourn, if you are. I ordered Reeve Fastred to empty his lands, sending his people across the Entwash where they can be better-defended, but he is young and I fear foolish. I ride to see if he has obeyed my command.\
\
'We will speak again in Snowbourn!'","Éomer will meet you in Snowbourn outside the Mead Hall.\
\
You should ride south and speak again with Éomer in Snowbourn, in the Sutcrofts.","'A brisk ride! Welcome to Snowbourn, my friend. Now to the business at hand.'","Meet with Éomer in Snowbourn","The next leg of your journey with Éomer will take you to the town of Snowbourn, in the Sutcrofts.","'If Reeve Fastred has not obeyed my command to send his people to safety across the Entwash, he will soon have the chance to explain it in person. I will meet you in Snowbourn!'"},
[2285]={"'Frodo has earned his rest, ${PLAYER}. His adventure has ended. And yet, Middle-earth still has need of heroes. Gondor will need you, as will others among the Free People: dwarves, Elves, and hobbits. Be ready for their call, my friend. A great evil of the world has departed, but there are others that will need heroes to face them.\
\
'Do not face them alone! Some measure of the strength of Sauron was bound to his Ring, but much of his strength was derived from his mastery over the weak, and the weak of will. I foresee that some of those freed from his dominance will seek to gain advantage from his fall. The shroud over Gorgoroth is a veil that must be pierced if Middle-earth is to live free from fear.\
\
'Frodo will write the tale of his adventure, but the next adventure will be yours alone to write. My own time on these shores is drawing to a close, for my purpose is ended.'\
\
You look at him with the dawning understanding that his charge was to combat Sauron, and now that the Dark Lord is defeated, the Wizard must leave Middle-earth.\
\
'Oh, do not look at me like that, foolish ${RACE}! I am not leaving tomorrow! I will not depart until I know things are well in hand, and your kind has not yet proven that you are able to manage on your own!'\
\
He stands there spluttering for a moment. There is a twinkle in his eye when he speaks again, and he seems less like Mithrandir, or any of his many other names, and most like he was when you first met him: Gandalf.\
\
'I will say this to you, and it will be my last word on the subject: As for this business with the Ring, I commend you on a job well-done, my dear ${PLAYER}. Very well-done indeed!'","Talk to Mithrandir on the field of Cormallen","'Today is a day of celebration. My friends and my kin have earned this day of victory! Enjoy this day, ${PLAYER}, for you too were instrumental in its arrival!'","Talk to Mithrandir inside the bower that was provided for Frodo on the field of Cormallen","Book 9, Chapter 5: The Next Adventure","Frodo has decided that he is ready to relax from the ordeal of his adventure, but your own adventures continue.","Aragorn is on the field of Cormallen.","'We have come through the long night to the dawn at last, ${PLAYER}! Many were the days I believed all my choices were going wrong, but despite those errors, we have seen the destruction of the Ring and the downfall of Sauron!\
\
'When Frodo completed his task, Mordor was shaken to its very foundations by the eruption of Orodruin. The Black Gate and the Towers of the Teeth crumbled and fell, but who can say what lies behind them in the land that was Sauron's? There is a shroud over the plateau of Gorgoroth, and it masks our sight.'\
\
Aragorn smiles wryly.\
\
'I have not yet been crowned King, but already I am thinking about Gondor's future! Can we not have one day of satisfied peace? Sauron is no more! There will be a new ordering of the calendar to mark the occasion. In the Kingdom of Gondor, the New Year will now begin on March twenty-fifth, the day on which Sauron fell and hope was restored to Middle-earth. There are still many preparations to be made before I can ascend to the throne of Gondor, but today is a day of celebration. My friends and my kin have earned this day of victory! Enjoy this day, ${PLAYER}, for you too were instrumental in its arrival!'","'Thank you for easing my mind and my heart, ${PLAYER}. Gandalf has returned, and now I think I see the makings of a conspiracy! But thank you for the kind words, and I give my thanks to Gandalf as well. I am very fortunate to have such friends as you!\
\
'I am ready to have a rest, and an end to adventuring. I shall be content just to see Bilbo again, and to return to the Shire. I will write down my part of the Quest of the Ring, all of it, and I will be thankful for the opportunity to live in peace!'","Talk to Aragorn on the field of Cormallen","Mithrandir is in the bower that was prepared for Frodo on the field of Cormallen.","'Aragorn has asked to speak with you, ${PLAYER}.'","'I am ready to have a rest, and an end to adventuring. I shall be content just to see Bilbo again, and to return to the Shire. I will write down my part of the Quest of the Ring, all of it, and I will be thankful for the opportunity to live in peace!'","'I am glad to hear that Frodo has decided to write down his tale, after all. It has been my experience that sometimes a hobbit simply needs a bit of a push to get started on a thing, but once he has set his mind to do it the results are often admirable.\
\
'I trust you told Frodo that no one could willingly have destroyed the Ring? I meant to return more quickly and tell him that, but Samwise grew suspicious that I was wasting his time and required more assurances or he would hastily return to his master. Wasting his time! Me!'\
\
Mithrandir chuckles mirthfully.\
\
'I was, of course, but that is neither here nor there. All that matters in the end is that you have assuaged Frodo's concerns and helped him come to terms with his experience. He deserves that and more for the deed he has done on behalf of Middle-earth.\
\
'But enough chattering. Aragorn has asked to speak with you, ${PLAYER}.'","Mithrandir is on the field of Cormallen."},
[2286]={"Bring Warg-rider and corruptor weapons to Éomer in Snowbourn","'The people of Snowbourn will not leave their homes. It is the will of the Reeve.'","Warg-riders on the plains of the Sutcrofts wield fire-pots, and Mordor corruptors wield spears.\
\
Éomer has asked you to collect implements of destruction from Warg-riders and Mordor corruptors in the Sutcrofts. He wants to show them to the Reeve as evidence of what his people will face if they do not retreat across the Entwash.","'Speak to Grimstan and we may learn why Fastred has disobeyed my command. Find him outside the Reeve's house to the south-east.'","Collect spears from Mordor corruptors in the Sutcrofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Éomer is outside the Mead Hall in Snowbourn.\
\
You have collected implements of destruction from Warg-riders in the Sutcrofts, and should bring them to Éomer as he requested.","'That is what I suspected, ${PLAYER}. I will go to speak with Reeve Fastred, but he may need more evidence to be convinced of the danger his people face.\
\
'Ride onto the plains of the Sutcrofts and defeat Mordor corruptors and Warg riders, seizing their implements of destruction: spears and fire-pots. Bring them back to me and I will show this evidence to the Reeve. If that does not change his mind, we may need to try something else.'","Collected fire-pots from Warg-riders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Very good. These weapons will show Reeve Fastred what his people will face if he does not move them across the Entwash, where they can be better defended.'","Éomer is in Snowbourn, north-west of Fastred's house, outside the Mead Hall.\
\
You have heard Grimstan's explanation for Fastred's refusal to comply with Éomer's command, and should report it now to the Third Marshal.","Collected spears from Mordor corruptors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Who are you? I have not seen you before. What are you doing in Snowbourn?'\
\
You ask him why Fastred has not moved his people across the Entwash where they can be better-protected.\
\
'The Reeve has his own opinion on this, whatever the Third Marshal thinks. Ah, Éomer is a long way from here. He does not know what is really going on in the Sutcrofts. The women and the children could be moved, certainly, but Éomer wanted everyone to depart, even the warriors! These are their lands! Better to stay and die on your own land than to live at the say-so of another man's plot!\
\
'Snowbourn will not retreat, though it be burned to the ground. Its people will defend it to the last!'","Talk to Éomer in Snowbourn","Talk to Grimstan in Snowbourn","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","Grimstan is outside Reeve Fastred's home in Snowbourn, south-east of Éomer's location.\
\
Éomer has asked you to inquire of Grimstan why Reeve Fastred has not followed his command for his people to move across the Entwash for safety.","Book 9, Chapter 6: No Retreat","Collect fire-pots from Warg-riders in the Sutcrofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I look around and I do not see the preparations for which I asked, ${PLAYER}. I will speak with Reeve Fastred to learn why he delays, but let us try something else first.\
\
'It is said that you catch more horse-flies with honey-cakes than you do with lamp tallow. Introduce yourself to Grimstan, one of Fastred's personal guards, and ask him why the people have not begun to move where it is safe. Grimstan knows me, and the answer he would give to me might be different than the one he gives to you. I want to know what is really going on in Snowbourn, and you are a more sure path to that answer.'","Éomer has come to Snowbourn to see if Reeve Fastred has complied with his command to begin preparations to move his people across the Entwash where they can be better defended."},
[2287]={"Talk to and train with a member of the Snowbourn militia","'I have received some training in the martial arts, but I have not seen real battle. Perhaps I will surprise you with my natural ability?'","Éomer will speak with Reeve Fastred about moving the people of Snowbourn across the Entwash, but he wants you to help train the people in the event Fastred still refuses.","Talk to Horn in Snowbourn","Talk to and train with a Snowbourn veteran","Book 9, Chapter 7: The Coming Tide","You have achieved victory, and the veteran has improved slightly","'I have never so much as held a blade before. But I will do my best!'","'I saw Éomer emerge from his meeting with Fastred. He did not look happy.'","You have achieved victory, and the villager has improved a great deal!","'Fastred is young and hot-headed, and thinks death in battle is the most noble of ends. Certainly I cannot gainsay the value of death and glory, but not for his people. Most of the people who live in Snowbourn are not warriors.\
\
'While I speak with the Reeve, I would have you spar with some of the people here: villagers, militia, and veterans alike. Horn told me you helped train Elfmar's men, and if Fastred is truly willing to endanger the lives of his people in this way, I want them to have some basic training in battle.\
\
'I hope none of them have need of it. But if they do, we will rest easy knowing that we did all that we could for them.'","'Few of the villagers would speak to me, and none wished to spar with me. I consider myself a hopeful Elf, but...'\
\
Corudan's raised eyebrow speaks volumes, but he finishes the thought anyway.\
\
'Right now this hopeful Elf is hoping they flee before the Orcs arrive. Either way, Snowbourn will be empty. Better to be burned empty than filled with the bodies of the unfortunate.'","You have achieved victory, and the member of the militia has improved somewhat!","'Fastred is a fool. ${PLAYER}, I had planned to return to Edoras after this visit to Snowbourn, but now the need to do so is even more urgent.\
\
'We have to leave now.'","Talk to Éomer in Snowbourn","'I saw Éomer emerging from his talk with Reeve Fastred. He did not look happy.\
\
'I trained with some of the people of Snowbourn as well. I hope for their sake that Fastred listens to reason and moves them across the Entwash. Their skill with weaponry takes little time to discern and less time to overcome.'","Éomer is in Snowbourn, outside the Mead Hall.\
\
The Third Marshal of the Riddermark has returned from meeting with Reeve Fastred... and he does not look happy.","'Unlike my neighbours, I have seen battle on the fields of Rohan. I am ready to fight to defend my home. Let us see what you can do, ${PLAYER}!'","Villagers, militia, and veterans can be found throughout Snowbourn.\
\
Éomer has asked you to train with villagers, militia, and veterans of Snowbourn, in order to prepare them in the event he cannot convince Fastred to move them across the Entwash.","Talk to Corudan in Snowbourn","'We have done what we could, ${PLAYER}. Even sparring with Horn and yourself may not be enough to save these people. None of them desired to train with me at all.'","Talk to and train with a Snowbourn villager","Horn and Corudan are in Snowbourn, by the fountain in the centre of town.\
\
You have trained with some of the people of Snowbourn, as have Horn and Corudan.","'Train with the people of Snowbourn. I want them to have some basic fighting skills, if Fastred refuses to listen to me.'"},
[2288]={"Book 9, Chapter 8: Night Falls on Meduseld","Éomer wants to ride to Edoras with you to consult with King Théoden about Fastred's refusal to move his people across the Entwash.","Talk to Horn by the Entwade","'We must ride for Edoras at once! We will consult with my uncle Théoden and he will resolve this issue with Fastred.'","'That was not a good result, was it?'","Éomer wants to return with all speed to Edoras to report to his uncle, King Théoden.","Horn is at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts.\
\
The unthinkable has happened: Éomer has been imprisoned at the command of the King and you have been ordered never to cross the Entwash under pain of death.","'We have to return to Edoras at once. I need to report to the King that Fastred is refusing to move his people across the Entwash. We simply do not have the riders we would need to effectively defend them here. In West Rohan we will have a better chance of protecting the people.\
\
'Come with me to Edoras, ${PLAYER}. We will sort this out with my uncle Théoden.'","Talk to Éomer in Snowbourn and ride to Edoras","'This is terrible, ${PLAYER}. It is as I feared when I sang the song that resulted in my banishment to Stangard: the King is truly under the power of a malevolent force.\
\
'Gríma Wormtongue, not Théoden, rules in Rohan. And now Éomer is captive in Edoras!'"},
[2289]={"You have been ordered by Théoden King not to cross the Entwash under pain of death.","'I do not know what we can do, ${PLAYER}. Éomer is imprisoned, we cannot cross the Entwash, the people of the Sutcrofts are in grave danger from the fervour of their Reeve, and I... I thought Nona would have returned by now.'\
\
Horn looks downcast.\
\
'I am fortunate the King did not comment on my return from Stangard, or I would be in the dungeon alongside Éomer, or worse. We have failed in everything, ${PLAYER}. I swore to stand by you once I was cast from Stangard, but everything I have tried to do has ended in failure or disappointment. I am sorry.'","'Tell Horn what I said to you, ${PLAYER}. I think that he needs it.'","You relay Corudan's words to Horn, and his gloomy expression gradually softens.\
\
'What would Corudan be saying today if we had not run into that Ent, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
He laughs.\
\
'You are both right, my friend. Tomorrow will be brighter. There is no sense in mulling on the past or in worrying for the future. We will take one day after another, as the sun rises and then sets, and await the dawn with hope.\
\
'We must do what we can for the people of East Rohan! We must help them prepare their defences, we must help them fight what battles we can, and we must help them rebuild if the battles go ill. Who stands between the people of Rohan and their enemies?'\
\
Horn grips the hilt of his sword with resolve and sets his shoulders.\
\
'We do. We must not fail them. We will not fail them. Our work here is just beginning, ${PLAYER}. If on the morrow we need to cross the Entwade, for the good of Rohan and at the risk of our own lives, we will.\
\
'But today we will do what we can for the people on this side of the line. May fortune smile on Corudan, and on you, and on me, and on Nona, wherever she may be!\
\
'Good fortune! And victory!'","Corudan is at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts.","'By order of Théoden King, you three are to stay on this side of the Entwash. If this command of the King changes, I will be informed by raven, I do not doubt. But until then, you stay there, and I will stay here.'","'This man is not to blame for the order of the King, but he will enforce it. I do not doubt that.'","Hunbald stands at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts.\
\
King Théoden has ordered you not to cross the Entwash under pain of death.","Talk to Hunbald at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts","'Why is Horn so upset? Have we not done what we set out to do? We tracked our mutual friends across the Eastemnet and only gave up the chase when we were assured of their safety.\
\
'We did much good in Rohan. That is more than can be said for some of the Aldors and Thanes and Reeves we have encountered! We will see what the future brings us, will we not?'\
\
Corudan smiles at you.\
\
'Think of Rúdhrif, ${PLAYER}, Baldbark the Ent. Finding one of the tree-herders still alive in Fangorn was not even a glimmer of a hope in my mind when you, Horn, Nona and I began our journey down the Anduin. But that was such a happy discovery, all the more because it was unexpected.\
\
'Perhaps Nona will come back to us when she has divined her inmost mind. Théoden may come to his senses and release Éomer. We may find our paths crossing once again with that of Gandalf, or with that of Aragorn son of Arathorn. Tomorrow will be less bleak. We will face it together, will we not?\
\
'Give Horn these words, and tell him that if Corudan the Elf can see hope for the future, surely Horn the Man of Rohan can find some small measure of light on which to rest his thoughts.'","Talk to Horn at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts","Horn is at the Entwade crossing.\
\
Corudan has told you why he has hope for what tomorrow may bring, and has asked that you share his thoughts with Horn.","Book 9, Chapter 9: The Dividing Line","'If my sister were here, she would not let this guard stand in her way. I am not advising you to act as she would, ${PLAYER}! It was just a comment.'","Talk to Corudan at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts","'I do not know what to do, ${PLAYER}. Does Corudan have any ideas?'"},
[2290]={"Habla con Gandalf en Rivendel","Libro 9, Prólogo: Noticias del palantír","'¿Un palantír ha sido robado? Estas son, sin duda, noticias graves.\
\
'Tendré que meditar sobre el curso de acción más eficaz.'","'¿Has llevado las noticias a Gandalf? Excelente. Pero todavía queda más por hacer...'","Gandalf se encuentra en la habitación de Bilbo, en el primer piso de la Última Morada, en Rivendel.\
\
Aragorn te ha enviado a hablar con Gandalf.","'¿Aragorn te ha enviado?\
\
'¿Qué es esto que dices? ¿El palantír, robado?'","Aragorn cree que Gandalf debería ser informado del misterioso robo del palantír por parte de Sara Roblecorazón.","'Gandalf el Gris, que actualmente se encuentra en la habitación de Bilbo en el primer piso de la Última Morada, aquí en Rivendel, debería ser informado de las acciones de esta Sara Roblecorazón. ¿Dices que te has cruzado con ella varias veces antes? De lo más curioso.\
\
'El robo de un palantír no es asunto menor, ${PLAYER}. Pocos tienen conocimiento de ellos; aún menos pueden usarlos con propósito y precisión. Si esta Roblecorazón es una de esos pocos, sus designios sobre un objeto tan poderoso auguran algo muy funesto.\
\
'Ve ahora y habla con Gandalf.'"},
[2291]={"'Por fin, los preparativos están completos. Los Malledhrim, la Hueste Dorada de Lothlórien, ahora están listos para cruzar el río Anduin y atacar a las fuerzas de Dol Guldur.\
\
'La Hueste Dorada tiene dos objetivos: llevar la batalla al Enemigo en Dol Guldur en un momento de nuestra elección, antes de que pueda atacar los bosques de Lothlórien con fuerza, y cambiar a Mazog, el prisionero de la Guarnición de Hierro, por los cautivos en las mazmorras de Dol Guldur.\
\
'Se ha solicitado tu ayuda para ambos objetivos. Habla con Braiglinn, junto al muelle subiendo la pendiente desde los muelles de Lothlórien. Él te contará los detalles de cada plan.'","'No ha sido fácil, ${PLAYER}, pero hemos logrado la travesía y expulsado a los Orcos de su fortaleza en la cima de Amon Angened. La Hueste Dorada está ahora lista para comenzar el paso hacia el Bosque Negro.\
\
'Espero que no nos equivoquemos en esto. Mucho está en juego.'","Braiglinn se encuentra en Imlad Lalaith, en las orillas del Anduin, en Lothlórien.\
\
Se te ha dicho que hables con Braiglinn sobre la travesía de la Hueste Dorada hacia la Tierra Media.","'Finalmente has llegado, ${PLAYER}; había comenzado a preguntarme si no querrías ser parte de la primera travesía. ¡Pero me alegra ver que no es así!\
\
'¿Ves el río Anduin? Sus corrientes son fuertes, aunque este sea un lugar lo suficientemente tranquilo para cruzar, y una vez que lleguemos a la otra orilla, necesitaremos estar preparados para cualquier cosa. El desembarco puede ser tranquilo, pero también puede ser tumultuoso. Será responsabilidad de Fuirgam, al otro lado del Anduin, asegurarse de que todo vaya lo mejor posible.\
\
'Una vez que estemos seguros en las playas, organizaré una segunda travesía para llevar a la compañía que escoltará a nuestro prisionero a Dol Guldur. ¿Quieres viajar en los primeros barcos? De ser así, habla con Calengoth en los muelles.'","Ha llegado el momento de que los Malledhrim, la Hueste Dorada, crucen el río Anduin y ataquen a las fuerzas del Enemigo en Dol Guldur.","Libro 9, Prólogo: La Costa Oscura","'Ha llevado mucho tiempo, , pero los preparativos finalmente están completos. Los Malledhrim, la Hueste Dorada de Lothlórien, ahora están listos para cruzar el río Anduin y atacar a las fuerzas de Dol Guldur.\
\
'No conozco aún los detalles del plan, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} , pero parece que la Hueste Dorada tiene dos objetivos: llevar la batalla al Enemigo en Dol Guldur en un momento de nuestra elección, antes de que pueda atacar los bosques de Lothlórien con fuerza, y cambiar a Mazog, el prisionero de la Guarnición de Hierro, por los cautivos en las mazmorras de Dol Guldur.\
\
'Se ha solicitado tu ayuda para ambos objetivos. Ve ahora a Imlad Lalaith en las orillas del Anduin y habla con Braiglinn allí. Él te contará los detalles de cada plan.'","Alfirimbes está esperando para hablar contigo en Echad Sirion.\
\
Los Elfos han establecido su punto de apoyo en las oscuras orillas del Bosque Negro y están listos para comenzar su avance en el bosque.","'Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para cruzar el Anduin con la primera compañía, sube al barco. Sé que Fuirgam, encargado del desembarco, te estará agradecido por tu ayuda en la otra orilla.'","Calengoth se encuentra en los muelles cerca de Imlad Lalaith, en las orillas del Anduin, en Lothlórien. Una vez que hayas hecho la travesía, encontrarás a Fuirgam trabajando para asegurar un punto de apoyo en el Bosque Negro.\
\
Calengoth, el oficial de lanzamiento, está esperando para verte en uno de los barcos que te llevarán a través del Anduin con la primera travesía. Una vez que lo hayas hecho, busca a Fuirgam, el Elfo encargado de asegurar un punto de apoyo para los Elfos.","'Sube la pendiente desde estos muelles y habla con Braiglinn. Él te contará los detalles de los objetivos de la Hueste Dorada en el Bosque Negro.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para regresar a Lothlórien? Este barco te llevará allí.'","Sube al barco de Calengoth y ayuda a Fuirgam con sus tareas en los Mirk-eaves","'Sube al barco si quieres cruzar el Anduin.'","'Habla con Calengoth en los muelles; él tendrá un barco que puedes usar para cruzar. Una vez al otro lado, deberías ayudar a Fuirgam con las muchas tareas necesarias para asegurar un punto de apoyo en el Bosque Negro.'","Habla con Braiglinn en Imlad Lalaith","Habla con Alfirimbes en Echad Sirion","'Estoy lleno de anticipación, ${PLAYER}, y mis dedos buscan las cuerdas de mi arco con ansias. La Hueste Dorada está ahora lista para partir, cruzar el río y llevar la lucha al Enemigo. Ha pasado mucho tiempo desde que hemos hecho más que vigilar nuestras fronteras; demasiado tiempo.\
\
'Ve a Imlad Lalaith en las orillas del Anduin, en Lórien, y habla con Braiglinn. Él te contará los detalles de los objetivos de la Hueste Dorada.'","'Este barco te llevará al otro lado del río, hacia el Bosque Negro.'"},
[2292]={"'My daughter is at Imdolen, overlooking the road that climbs into the Misty Mountains, north of Imladris. She desired to speak with you before the Grey Company departs.'","Talk to Arwen at Imdolen","'We are making ready to depart. It will not be long now before we take the southern road.'","'My gift to Aragorn goes south with the Grey Company.'","'You bring both a gift and a message for my chief from the Lady Arwen? I see.'\
\
Halbarad listens as you recount Arwen's words and gravely accepts the standard you carry.\
\
'I will carry this burden on our journey. It will come to Aragorn, though all the perils of our road lie in between. When will this standard be unfurled, I wonder, and against what sky will it be raised aloft?'","'I see my sister has at last finished the gift she was making for Aragorn! How long will it be until it is unfurled, I wonder?'","'My gift to Aragorn was wrought in secret. Few only know of its making.'","The Grey Company has come to Rivendell, and there are only a few things left to be done before they begin their journey south.","'It was a long ride from the north-lands, ${PLAYER}, but I too have come to Rivendell to depart with the Company. They have need of my knowledge of the southern lands.'","'This is the moment for which the Dúnedain have waited, ${PLAYER}. It will not be long now before we ride forth to meet our destiny.'","The Lady Arwen is at Imdolen, on the slope that overlooks the road into the Misty Mountains, north of Rivendell.\
\
Elrond has asked you to speak with his daughter Arwen before you depart with the Grey Company.","'By your efforts, the summons was brought throughout Eriador, ${PLAYER}, and now the Dúnedain have responded. Many of their number have come to Imladris, and they prepare to depart for the southern lands that they may come to Aragorn in his time of need.\
\
'You will ride with them, if you see fit to do so, but I have been made aware that my daughter desires first to speak with you. She is at Imdolen, on the slope north of Imladris, overlooking the road that climbs up into the Misty Mountains.'","Bring Aragorn's standard to Halbarad in Rivendell","'I carried the message to several other Rangers upon leaving Laenan, ${PLAYER}, and they have come to ride with the Grey Company.'","Book II, Chapter 1: Wrought in Secret","'Bring this gift and my words to Halbarad, by the stables in Imladris, for he has consented to bear them both on the journey south.'","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","Halbarad is by the stables in Rivendell.\
\
Arwen has given you the standard she made for Aragorn and has asked you to bring it to Halbarad in Rivendell before the Grey Company departs.","'You have returned from your errand, ${PLAYER}, and have come to speak with me, as I asked? My delight cannot be hidden, friend ${RACE}, for my own undertaking has also come to an end, and its fruit waits now for a bearer!'\
\
Arwen solemnly hands you a tall staff, wrapped closely with a black cloth bound with thongs.\
\
'I have made this gift for Aragorn. The days are short, and it may be that our hopes will soon be ended. This standard I have made for him will fly aloft at a time of his choosing, and he will know for what he fights. May it bring courage to my Elfstone and those with whom he stands!\
\
'Bring this gift and my words to Halbarad, by the stables in Imladris, for he has consented to bear them both on the journey south.'"},
[2293]={"Bashem has asked you to send books to Chakâr at Dâr Tabib.\
\
Dâr Tabib is located in the south-west area of the Tor-gardens.","Books for the Bored","'Will you be passing through the south-west part of the district? I meant to bring some books to Chakâr at Dâr Tabib, but...' He frowns at the stack of papers in front of him. 'I have some research to attend to, unfortunately.'\
\
'People all over the city have been kind enough to donate books to us in our recovery efforts. Some are common enough that we can spare copies for the healers' patients. I am sure they would be thankful for something to chase away their boredom.'","Chakâr has asked you to give the books to listless patients in and around Dâr Tabib.\
\
Dâr Tabib is located in the south-west area of the Tor-gardens.","Talk to Chakâr at Dâr Tabib","'Bashem must be just as busy as us to send someone in his stead!\
\
'The patients who remain bore grievous injuries from the fighting months ago and must stay under our supervision. As you can imagine, there are very few sources of entertainment here, and many have become listless. Some cannot leave their beds. Others can only wander around the apothecary grounds to break up the monotony.\
\
'Would you mind handing out the books? It would do our patients some good to see a new person rather than the same healers every day.'","Delivered books (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","After receiving a surplus of book copies, the scholars of the Tor-gardens are looking to give them away.","Completado","You have delivered the last of the books, granting the patients of Dâr Tabib a bit of joy amidst the struggle of healing.","You have delivered the last of the books to the patients of Dâr Tabib.","Deliver books to listless patients (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[2294]={"'Tomo tu entrega como una señal de que la demanda de botas es mayor que nunca. Ay.\
\
'Deluraw te agradece, pero suspira dramáticamente cuando le entregas los materiales.\
\
'Puedes decirle a Santmereth que su envío de botas llegará en breve.'","Santmereth se encuentra en el Jardín del Festival de Duillond.\
\
Debes informarle a Santmereth que el envío de botas está nuevamente en camino gracias a tu ayuda al zapatero.","'¿Vuelve a estar todo según lo planeado? Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}... No sé qué haríamos sin ti.\
\
'¡Vuelve a menudo! La demanda de botas es realmente alta, y los suministros siempre se agotan.'","Recoge ramas de madera de cerezo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deluraw se encuentra en Duillond, cerca del área de cocina.\
\
Debes llevarle los suministros para las botas, pues él es el zapatero del Festival.","Informa a Santmereth que el envío de botas está en marcha","Cordel recogido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva los materiales a Deluraw","El evento de Pisoteo de Musarañas siempre se queda sin sus botas especiales no dañinas para repeler musarañas del Jardín del Festival de Duillond.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Has recogido plantas de lino (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge plantas de lino (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has recogido ramas de madera de cerezo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Demanda y Suministro de Botas (Diaria)","'Una vez más, el envío de botas llega tarde, y estoy segura de que Deluraw está teniendo problemas con sus suministros. ¿Recuerdas las cosas que necesitaba recoger para mantener la producción de botas?\
\
'Si pudieras salir a reunir los materiales de Deluraw, te lo agradecería muchísimo, ${PLAYER}. Por favor, regresa cuando termines para que sepa cuándo esperar la entrega de botas.'","'Por favor, no te demores, ${PLAYER}. Estamos bajos de botas, como siempre. Las musarañas prevalecerán si no tenemos cuidado.'","Recoge cordel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los suministros para las botas de Deluraw pueden encontrarse en Duillond y Celondim. El cordel está en los muelles del puerto de Celondim, las ramas pueden recogerse bajo los árboles en flor de los campos de Duillond, y las plantas de lino crecen a lo largo del camino que une ambas ciudades élficas.\
\
Debes recolectar los ingredientes de Deluraw y llevárselos para asegurar una entrega rápida de botas para pisotear musarañas."},
[2295]={"You should talk to Isnír.","Isnír can be found at the Udûn Foothold.\
\
You should speak with Isnír.","'This place, Nargroth, seems important to the powers in Mordor. We must learn more. If you are ready to depart, all I ask is to please be careful.'","You relay the conversation you have overheard between Borangos and Urudanî, to Isnír.\
\
'Oh my, this is indeed worrying. You say that Borangos has some sort of plan that involves Mount Doom? Nothing good can come of this. The more we study the mountain, the more I fear it to not be natural. Its fires seem to have strange properties. Sauron must have been behind these flames, but will the mountain slowly fade in Sauron's death? Bright flames still flow from chambers within. Orodruin seems to be just as active as ever.\
\
'It may be some time before we can act upon this enemy, but rest assured, I will start discussion with those of rank in Udûn. I thank you for bringing this to our attention. We shall speak again soon, ${PLAYER}.'","Upon receiving the remnants of the ancient ward originally used to keep Borangos at bay, Isnír wishes for you to return to Nargroth in the hopes of learning more about the domain of Great Rogmul.","Talk to Isnír","'${PLAYER}, I have something I would like to share with you. I have been looking through my notes here and have come to a few truths about these ancient fragments you have brought back from Nargroth.\
\
'From the visions you have described and from what I have learned of Nargroth, I believe that the fortress of Nargroth was built on top of something else. It seems that Nargroth has been a mighty structure in Mordor for many years. What was built in the Caverns of Fire before Nargroth's construction is much, much older. Looking at these fragments, I would say it is of a chamber of some kind. Perhaps with a ward or seal. I would put this structure as being built around the Second Age. Possibly early Second Age.\
\
'From what you have told me, I believe all this has something to do with Borangos. This Rogmul is most powerful. In historic text, none have been seen such as Borangos since the times when great beasts of fire and shadow walked the lands for Regmyl to serve.'","Borangos The Horror"},
[2296]={"Uno de los nuevos aprendices de Galathir, Nethlas, ha estado molestando a la gente en el Recinto del Festival con las preguntas de investigación de su maestro.","Ayuda a Haerandel con 'Las Flores de Anarlossë'","Arn Juncoso está en el Recinto del Festival de las Tierras de Bree.","Ayuda a Haerandel con 'Partir en primavera'","Tres herboristas de Gondor están causando cierto alboroto en el Recinto del Festival de las Tierras de Bree, y Arn Juncoso te ha pedido que te asegures de que estén contentos... y en silencio.","Habla con Mílgamel en el Recinto del Festival","Ayuda a Nethlas con 'Un Estudio Natural'","Un grupo de herboristas visitantes de Gondor ha viajado muy lejos en nombre de su maestro, pero su llegada ha causado disturbios en el Recinto del Festival de las Tierras de Bree. ¿Se podrá restaurar el buen ánimo propio de la primavera, o su búsqueda de conocimiento sacará de quicio a todos?\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el evento asociado.</rgb>","Ayuda a Edlothon con 'La Promesa de los Girasoles'","Haerandel se ha sentido ofendido por algo que dijeron los herboristas de Gondor, y desea corregirlo.","'¿Has venido a ayudar a los herboristas, ${PLAYER}? ¡Siempre nos hace falta ayuda, pues la búsqueda del conocimiento nunca termina, como bien sabrás!\
\
'Fui aprendiz de Galathir, el maestro de hierbas de Minas Tirith, y me envió a estudiar las plantas y musgos de Ithilien y de las Eriales frente a Mordor. No estuvo de acuerdo con algunas de mis conclusiones al volver, y quiso despedirme. No solo eso: tomó un nuevo aprendiz....... en realidad, dos, y los envió al norte, a las Tierras de Bree, para confirmar algunas de sus teorías botánicas.\
\
'Mi estancia en las tierras salvajes y la lectura del excelente tomo 'Hierbas y Malezas' me enseñaron que no necesito ser aprendiz de Galathir para estudiar el mundo natural. Así que seguí a sus nuevos aprendices hasta aquí, y he estado intentando ayudarlos con sus estudios. Me temo, pobre gente, que son muy parecidos a mi antiguo maestro: han estado molestando a la gente con las preguntas de Galathir, cuando deberían estar en el campo, estudiando plantas y flores con sus propios ojos.'","Edlothon no sabe cómo las Anarlossë pudieron haber sobrevivido después de tanto tiempo, pero está dispuesto a convencerse si encuentras pruebas.","'¿Podrías asegurarte de que esos herboristas de Gondor estén contentos y, más importante aún, que no molesten más a mis visitantes con sus extrañas preguntas? ¡Habrá algunas Hojas de Primavera extra para ti si lo logras!'","'¡! ${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido, bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida, bienvenida[f]}. Hay muchas actividades agradables con las que celebrar la llegada de la primavera, y muchas de ellas se encuentran aquí mismo, en el Recinto del Festival. Estoy seguro de que lo pasarás de maravilla.\
\
'Pero, si pudiera robarte un momento, ¿podrías ayudarme con algo? Es un asunto pequeño, una nimiedad, pero estoy un tanto preocupado por unos recién llegados. Son tres, y han viajado un largo camino. Tengo entendido que han venido desde Gondor. Se hacen llamar herboristas y, aunque no rechazaría a nadie, debo admitir que ya se han vuelto algo molestos. ¿Podrías asegurarte de que estén contentos y, sobre todo, de que dejen de inquietar a mis visitantes con sus preguntas tan extrañas?\
\
'Te lo agradezco muchísimo, . ¡Me aseguraré de que recibas algunas Hojas de Primavera extra por tu ayuda!'","Habla con Arn Juncoso en el Recinto del Festival","Elevado por la Primavera","'¡Te vi marcharte sin ocuparte de mi problema, ${PLAYER}, y debo admitir que al principio me sentí bastante molesto contigo! ¿Olvidaste que te pedí asegurar que los herboristas visitantes no causaran más disturbios? Pero poco después de tu partida, noté algo sorprendente: ¡dejaron de beber y de alborotar, y comenzaron a hablar en voz baja entre ellos!\
\
'Eso encendió mi curiosidad, y pasé por su mesa como quien no quiere la cosa. Parecían cuestionar los méritos de alguna creencia antigua, y la discusión los había sacudido lo suficiente como para volver a la cortesía. ¡Qué giro tan extraño!\
\
'No sé qué papel jugaste en ese debate sobre tipos de flores, ni si decidieron finalmente que la planta llamada Anarlossë y la que llaman Anorloth son en realidad la misma. Pero creo que les diste algo en qué pensar, y mientras piensen, ¡han dejado de causar disturbios! En conclusión, te has ganado estas Hojas de Primavera. ¡Gástalas cuando quieras y disfruta del festival!'","Haerandel no puede creer que la Anarlossë aún pueda crecer en algún lugar de la Comarca, y quiere que encuentres a su hermano para contarle esta posibilidad antes de que zarpe hacia el Oeste."},
[2297]={"Winsig has lamented the lack of supplies since the Orc-invasion of the Sutcrofts and believes that the Orc-fortifications might prove useful to the people of Walstow once they are dismantled.","Orc-barricades can be found in the Orc-camps to the north and south-west of Walstow.\
\
Winsig wants you to destroy the Orc-barricades and collect wood-scraps from the wreckage.","'Such foolish creatures... we shall benefit greatly from these resources. I will have my men begin work on erecting even more defences along our borders.'","Winsig can be found in the Mead Hall of Walstow.\
\
You should return to Winsig with news of your success.","Destroyed Orc-barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected wood-scraps from dismantled Orc-fortifications (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Orcs have made a great effort to reinforce their new-found holdings in the Sutcrofts. They brought a significant amount of supplies in through the East Wall before we were able to contain them.\
\
'Following the sacking of Hytbold to the north, they had even more materials with which to work. I want you to raze their structures and return with some of their stolen wood. We can use it to bolster our own defences and keep Walstow standing.\
\
'Carry as much as you can and return to me!'","Collect wood-scraps from dismantled Orc-fortifications (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Winsig","Destroy Orc-barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Borrowing Barricades"},
[2298]={"La Doncella Roja está condenada (o eso parece) por la corrupción que han causado los Hombres en su tierra. Estos hombres se presentan ante ella, dispuestos a sacrificarse por la Doncella Roja, y merecen este destino... pero la nobleza de tu sangre será una recompensa aún mayor para ella. Cuando estos Hombres caigan por voluntad propia ante ella, sabrá la diferencia entre los que fortalecen y los que destruyen.","'Mis hermanas están lejos de mí... No oigo sus cantos ni siento su suave aliento entre los árboles. Áridos están esos árboles, casi sin vida, ahogados por raíces hinchadas con algo que tiene un amargo sabor a hierro. ¿Dónde están mis hermanas, y qué tengo delante?\
\
'No puedo ver más allá del rojo de esta tierra, pero percibo algo dulce entre los helechos amargos y las raíces hinchadas. ¿Eres real? ¿Sigo prisionera en la tierra?\
\
'Hay vida en ti... lo siento. Debe de haber vida en algún otro rincón de estas tierras. Quizá pueda encontrar esa vida de nuevo y devolverla a la salud.'","Los Créoth se sacrificarán a la Doncella Roja para restaurar sus fuerzas y su vínculo con la corrupción del pantano. Estos hombres no merecen más que la muerte, y tu presencia al oponerte a la Doncella Roja podría hacer que una parte de ella se dé cuenta de la insensatez de sus actos. Deberías dejar que los hombres mueran para fortalecer a la Doncella Roja, y luego derrotarla. Quizás así comprenda que la corrupción ha crecido demasiado y que debe regresar al mundo natural del que una vez formó parte.","Ayuda a purificar a la Doncella Roja","Jefa del Pasado: Naruhel"},
[2302]={"Derrota a Storvâgûn","En lo alto de los riscos sobre Helegrod, el traidor Storvâgûn ha puesto a los gigantes de las Montañas Nubladas al servicio de Angmar a cambio de grandes riquezas.","Has regresado a lo alto de los riscos sobre Helegrod para enfrentarte a Storvâgûn.","¡Storvâgûn ha sido derrotado!","Jefe del Pasado: Storvâgûn"},
[2303]={"¡Thrâng ha sido derrotado!","En lo profundo de la Grieta de Nûrz Ghâshu, Thrâng, el jefe de los Ghâshfra, está listo para enfrentarse a todos los que desafíen su poder.","Jefe del Pasado: Thrâng","Derrota a Thrâng"},
[2305]={"Escuchas a alguien acercándose","Los prisioneros están retenidos en jaulas por todo Kôth Rau. Deberías liberarlos y derrotar a los soldados Ordâkhai que encuentres.","Derrota a los Ordâkhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Prisioneros liberados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Viste lo grande que era ese orco? ¡Menos mal que llegué a tiempo para ayudarte a combatirlo!\
\
'Sí, sí, estuve allí. Seguramente estabas demasiado ${PLAYERNAME:concentrado[m]|concentrada[f]} en la lucha para notarme. No te culpo, luchaste admirablemente. Sin embargo, deberíamos regresar a Jiret-menêsh lo antes posible. ¡No quiero enfrentarme a otro orco de ese tamaño!'","Libera a los prisioneros (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has liberado a los prisioneros y derrotado a muchos soldados de Ordâkh, ganándote la atención de un campeón utûgi, Kulgath el Devastador.","Los Temámir de Jiret-menêsh quieren ayudar a las personas que están siendo retenidas prisioneras por los Ordâkhai en Kôth Rau.","Has liberado a los prisioneros y derrotado a muchos soldados de Ordâkh. Deberías regresar a Damudûr, la grieta oscura en la base de la montaña.","Regresa a la entrada de Damudûr al pie de la montaña","Derrota a Kulgath el Devastador","Ordâkhai derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Kulgath el Devastador ha sido derrotado","Prisioneros del tormento"},
[2306]={"Habla con el Frontero Boffin.","Las Rondas del Frontero","Reprende a los borrachos por su mal comportamiento (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Gracias, ${PLAYER}, has sido de gran ayuda! Los Fronteros siempre andamos con mucho trabajo. ¡Ayer ni siquiera pude tomar mi siesta vespertina!'","El Frontero Boffin está muy ocupado con el bullicio de la fiesta en la Feria de los Granjeros.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el evento con el que está asociada.</rgb>","'Solo, eh... mantente ${PLAYERNAME:atento[m]|atenta[f]} a cualquier señal de mal comportamiento. Los borrachos no tardarán en hacerse notar.'","Los invitados se encuentran por todo el mercado de la Feria de los Granjeros en Delagua durante el festival.\
\
Deberías reprender a los borrachos por su mal comportamiento para mantener la fiesta bajo control.","El Frontero Boffin está en Delagua, en la Comarca.\
\
Habla con el Frontero Boffin y dile que la fiesta está bajo control.","'¡Hola, ${PLAYER}! ¿No estarás causando problemas en la Feria de los Granjeros? Por supuesto que no; tú no te rebajarías así como esos invitados que se comportan terriblemente mal.\
\
'Si te apetece hacer algo, ¿me echarías una mano dando una vuelta por la feria? ¡Algunos han bebido demasiado y hay que reprenderlos por su mal comportamiento y por armar alboroto!'","Borrachos reprendidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡Reprendiste a un invitado sobrio! (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Deja en paz a los invitados sobrios (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2307]={"Los Fronteros de la Comarca necesitan tu ayuda. Lleva la ficha que has encontrado a los Fronteros en Cavada Grande y ayuda a la Tierra Media a proteger las fronteras de la Comarca.","Los Fronteros de la Comarca necesitan tu ayuda. Lleva las fichas que has encontrado a los Fronteros en Cavada Grande y ayuda a la Tierra Media a proteger las fronteras de la Comarca.","Los Fronteros de la Comarca necesitan tu ayuda. Lleva las fichas que has encontrado a los Fronteros en Cavada Grande y ayuda a la Tierra Media a proteger las fronteras de la Comarca.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando se lance la expansión el Abismo de Helm.</rgb>","Habla con Meg Ganapié en Cavada Grande","'No tienes cinco fichas, ${PLAYER}'.","'Thank you for coming to see us.  We are collecting tokens and in return, we will have some special things to offer you once we collect our full bounty.  If you give us five tokens now, we can help complete the Bounty more efficiently.  Then you can come back any time you've collected fifty more tokens.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will consume five Bounder's Tokens.</rgb>","Recompensa del Frontero"},
[2308]={"'What do you have there, friend? It smells delicious! Oh, inba-hûtu for me? Thank you very much!'","Batâla has asked you to deliver meals to the residents of Ahâba.\
\
You should collect the packaged meals. They are in a bag near Batâla's hut.","'Who are you? Oh, you have food for me? I guess that makes you a friend!'","Bounty of the Beltáni","Collect packaged meals","'You return with an empty bag. Your job must be finished and my people fed... or did you eat all the inba-hûtu yourself?\
\
'Only joking, friend. Thank you for your help!'","Deliver meals to Beltáni (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'The fruits you picked will be stewed and baked with pastry. I call them inba-hûtu. The cooking will bring out the fruits' natural sugars. Nature's bounty is delicious, is it not?\
\
'I have packaged up some meals for you to deliver to the hunters and shepherds out working. They are in that bag by the hut. Only one each!'","You have delivered meals to the Beltáni.\
\
You should return to Batâla.","Collected packaged meals","'Ah, I smell Batâla's inba-hûtu! Thank you for saving me the trip back, friend!'","'A meal delivery! Thank you, stranger. Now I just need to keep the sheep from eating it!'","Batâla has asked you to deliver meals to the residents of Ahâba.","You have collected the package of meals to deliver to the residents of Ahâba.\
\
You should deliver the meals to Beltáni shepherds and hunters around the village.","'Ah, more of Batâla's delicious cooking? Thank you, friend.'","'My sheep seem very interested in whatever you are carrying, friend! Ah, no wonder, inba-hûtu! If they are well behaved, perhaps I will share!'","Talk to Batâla","'Batâla has found a new helper, eh? Thank you for the food!'","Delivered meals to Beltáni (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[2309]={"La abundancia del mar","Lleva los salmones de la bahía helada a Tapio.","Salmones de la bahía helada recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva los salmones de la bahía helada a Tapio","'Ah, los vientos cantan alabanzas a nuestros esfuerzos. Sin duda el favor de quienes ven la verdad está con nosotros; acepta también este pequeño obsequio de nuestra parte y vete en paz.'","Tapio te dijo que pescaras donde el mar burbujea y hierve.","Los Vigilantes del Mar han localizado una gran cantidad de peces en la bahía helada, pero no pueden abandonar su puesto para ir a pescar.","'Con los Gauredain fuera, podemos recuperar este puesto avanzado para los Vigilantes del Mar. Sabemos muchas cosas sobre el mar: cómo se retuercen y serpentean sus corrientes, las señales de su ira y los lugares donde esconde a sus peces.\
\
'Hemos vuelto nuestros ojos al océano y encontramos una gran cantidad de peces empujados contra la costa por la corriente. Reunir esos peces mantendría satisfecho a Barad Gaurhoth y nos aseguraría el favor de los adivinos.\
\
'Los peces pueden encontrarse cerca de la orilla, donde el mar hierve y burbujea. Pesca allí y te recompensaremos con las bendiciones de los sanadores.'","'Si no hay peces, no estamos haciendo lo necesario.'","'DNT'","Recoge salmones de la bahía helada (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","¡El mar aquí hierve de salmones de la bahía helada!"},
[2312]={"El cartel de recompensa dice:\
\
'¿Quién de vosotros quiere caminar por el Bosque Salvaje sin miedo? ¡No es posible cuando una daga oxidada Tarkrîp puede clavarse en vuestra espalda en cualquier momento!\
\
'De entre todos los orcos Tarkrîp, hay uno que acecha en el bosque, matando a cualquiera que se adentre por su cuenta. Se llama Akvosh. Se ofrece una recompensa a quien consiga acabar con ese vil orco.'","'Vaya, ¿has venido a cazar al cazador? ¡Inténtalo, insignificante ${RACE}!'","Un cartel de recompensa te pide que encuentres a Akvosh, un orco despiadado que se esconde en el Bosque Salvaje.","¡Akvosh ha sido derrotado!","Invoca y enfréntate a Akvosh","Akvosh derrotado","Akvosh se encuentra en la mina occidental del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías invocar y enfrentarte a Akvosh.","El orco se enfrenta a ti","Completado","Has derrotado a Akvosh y has ayudado a los Pueblos Libres del Bosque Salvaje.","Recompensa: Akvosh"},
[2313]={"You have defeated Akílu the Feaster and cleaned up the Fane of Shahûru.\
\
You should return to Shâpar in Ahâba for your reward.","A bounty has been posted for the slaying of a dangerous vulture near Ahâba.","Bounty: Akílu the Feaster","Talk to Shâpar","Defeat Akílu the Feaster","A bounty is posted on this board. It reads:\
\
'Wanted: A brave soul to venture to the Fane of Shahûru and slay the great vulture known as Akílu the Feaster. She and her spawn are disrupting the natural balance of the area by hoarding more carcasses than they can consume and attacking travellers on the road.\
\
'Whoever slays the Feaster and removes the uneaten carcasses from the Fane of Shahûru will receive a reward from the Beltáni of Ahâba.'","You have accepted a bounty to defeat Akílu the Feaster and clean up the Fane of Shahûru.\
\
You should travel to the Fane of Shahûru, north of Ahâba and complete the bounty.","Burned animal carcasses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, you have slain the Feaster? Excellent work. She will bother us with her gluttony no longer!\
\
'Here is your well-earned reward.'","Burn animal carcasses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Akílu the Feaster"},
[2314]={"Andy Idden y su perro-lobo están reuniéndose con los trasgos de Tham Andalath, las ruinas en lo alto de una colina al este de Canadiach, en Parth Aduial, al sur de Ost Forod y al norte del camino.\
\
Has aceptado la comisión para reclamar la recompensa por Andy Idden.","'Gracias por tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}. Andy Idden causaba muchos problemas.'","Recompensa: Andy Idden, Amigo de Trasgos","Poppy Silleras está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Has derrotado a Andy Idden y ahora debes informar a Poppy Silleras.","El cartel anuncia una recompensa por un hombre llamado Andy Idden, acusándolo de tratar con trasgos y conspirar para asesinar a gente honrada de Ost Forod. Invita a quienes estén interesados a hablar con Poppy Silleras en Ost Forod para conocer los detalles y solicitar la comisión","'¿Te interesa reclamar la recompensa por Andy Idden? Si logras derrotarlo, desde luego la habrás ganado. Andy es de mal genio y brutal, y tiene amigos igual de malintencionados: trasgos, si hay que creer los relatos —y yo sí los creo.\
\
'He oído que Andy Idden ha ido con su perro-lobo a las ruinas de Tham Andalath por algún asunto con los trasgos que rondan allí. Vendería a sus propios vecinos a los trasgos si creyera que puede sacar provecho de ello, y probablemente eso mismo esté haciendo ahora mismo.\
\
'Tham Andalath está en lo alto de una colina, un corto trecho al este de Canadiach, el cruce al sur de aquí en Parth Aduial, y al norte del camino. Está lleno de trasgos, así que reclamar la recompensa por Andy Idden no será fácil. ¡Buena suerte, ${PLAYER}!'","'Andy Idden siempre fue problemático, y a menudo trajo esos problemas a Ost Forod.'","Poppy Silleras está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Un cartel que ofrece una recompensa por la captura o derrota de un saqueador de tumbas llamado Andy Idden llamó tu atención. Si deseas presentarte para esta recompensa, debes hablar con Poppy Silleras.","'Mi consejo para ti, ${PLAYER}, es que nunca hagas amistad con un trasgo.'","'Recuerda, las ruinas de Tham Andalath están al sur de aquí, en Parth Aduial. Si viajas al cruce de Canadiach, encontrarás las ruinas un poco al este de allí, en una colina al norte del camino.'","'¡Has sido de gran ayuda para quienes vivimos en Ost Forod, ${PLAYER}!'","'Andy Idden era un enemigo mortal, ${PLAYER}, reuniéndose con trasgos, y sé que has ganado tu recompensa.\
\
'Si haces tu informe a Basilio Resinas, el juez aquí en Ost Forod, él te dará tu recompensa.'","Basilio Resinas está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Has derrotado a Andy Idden y ahora debes informar a Basilio Resinas para recibir tu recompensa.","'Basilio Resinas, nuestro juez, está aquí en Ost Forod. Háblale respecto a tu recompensa.'","'Oí que acabaste con Andy Idden, ${PLAYER}, ¡y no un momento antes! Siempre fue un bribón, pero al hacerse amigo de los trasgos fue demasiado lejos. La gente de Ost Forod está más segura gracias a tu ayuda, y es un placer recompensarte por tu servicio.'","Se ha ofrecido una recompensa por Andy Idden, un saqueador de tumbas del que se rumorea que tiene tratos con trasgos."},
[2315]={"Los barghests pueden encontrarse por todas las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Sur. Sus ojos brillantes pueden entregarse a cambio de una recompensa y materiales de artesanía.","Los barghests pueden encontrarse en las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Sur.\
\
Algunos barghests pueden helar el alma con solo una mirada. Edith Rosadulce, en el Alto del Hombre Muerto, ha ofrecido darte una recompensa por recolectar ojos de barghest tomados de los barghests que habitan en el sur.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión puede completarse tres veces.</rgb>","'Estos servirán bien. No tengo claro cuál es el verdadero poder detrás de estos ojos, pero sé que he visto el mal que estas criaturas pueden causar.\
\
'Has ganado bien esta recompensa.'","Recompensa: Ojos de barghest","'Muchos creen que la fuerza de los barghests reside en su aullido. Si bien es cierto que sus aullidos son peligrosos, el poder de sus ojos es igualmente letal. Con solo una mirada se sabe que pueden infundir un miedo tan profundo en sus víctimas que puede matarlas.\
\
'Te pediría que busques barghests y recojas sus ojos. Te pagaré generosamente por esta recompensa.'","Recolecta ojos de barghest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ojos de barghest recolectados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los barghests en las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Sur son terriblemente peligrosos. Te pagaré bien si recolectas sus ojos para mí.'","Entrega los ojos de barghest a Edith Rosadulce"},
[2316]={"You have defeated Barzglúk and assisted those who wish to reclaim Gundabad.","Defeated Barzglúk.","Defeat bats in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bounty: Barzglúk","A bounty notice asks you to seek out Barzglúk, a terrifying great bat found in Máttugard.","Barzglúk and bats can be found in Máttugard.\
\
You should defeat bats.","Defeat Barzglúk","Defeated Barzglúk","Completado","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'Who among you has not known the fear of a bat's shriek in the darkness? It is a warning to quickly seek the safety of light and fire. But this is Gundabad, where the bats have owned these halls for a very long time! Must we always have to watch our backs?!\
\
'Of all the bats that lurk in these halls, none is more dangerous than the one named Barzglúk. A reward to any who can bring down this great bat, along with others of his cauldron!'","Defeated bats in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2317]={"'Estas servirán perfectamente y sin duda cumplirán el pedido que tengo. Gracias por todo lo que has hecho hasta ahora, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}.'","Recompensa: Lo bastante grande para alfombras","Los osos pueden encontrarse por todos los campos del norte de Bree.\
\
Sage Semilleno te pidió que recolectaras pieles de oso de los osos en los campos del norte de Bree y zonas circundantes y se las entregaras. Ha ofrecido pagarte un precio justo por este esfuerzo.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión puede completarse tres veces.</rgb>","Lleva las pieles de oso a Sage Semilleno","'Aparte de los jabalíes, también estaba cazando osos para recolectar pieles enormes que pudieran convertirse en alfombras, tapices y mantas si fuera necesario.\
\
'Te pagaré generosamente por tu ayuda para recolectarlas.'","'Los osos deambulan por todas estas tierras, y estoy seguro de que podrás encontrar muchas pieles con algo de esfuerzo.'","Pieles de oso intactas recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recolecta pieles de oso intactas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sage Semilleno busca pieles de oso para venderlas a los fabricantes de alfombras de Bree."},
[2318]={"Clark Cercapiedra está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Un cartel que ofrece una recompensa por la captura o derrota de un saqueador de tumbas llamado Bill Traspié llamó tu atención. Si deseas solicitar esta recompensa, debes hablar con Clark Cercapiedra.","Clark Cercapiedra está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Has derrotado a Bill Traspié y ahora debes informar a Clark Cercapiedra.","'¿Vienes por la recompensa de Bill Traspié? Me alegra oírlo: cuanto antes nos deshagamos de él, mejor, si me preguntas.\
\
'Bill ha estado robando y asesinando por las colinas de Tyrn Fornech desde hace meses, y ya es hora de que alguien lo detenga. Lo último que escuché es que había viajado al sur hacia Parth Aduial y se había atrincherado en una gran ruina al sur del cruce... Tham Varan, creo que se llamaba.\
\
'Si vas a cobrar la recompensa, mantén un ojo en la espada de Bill: es mortal con ella, y no quisiera tener tu muerte sobre mi conciencia.'","'Basilio Resinas, nuestro juez, está aquí en Ost Forod. Habla con él respecto a tu recompensa.'","'¡Bill Traspié ya no molestará a viajeros inocentes!'","Basilio Resinas está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Has derrotado a Bill Traspié y ahora debes hablar con Basilio Resinas para recibir tu recompensa.","'Has hecho un buen trabajo con ese Bill Traspié.'","'¿Así que tú eres quien finalmente dio fin a Bill Traspié? ¡Muy bien! Si haces tu informe a Basilio Resinas, el juez de Ost Forod, él te dará tu recompensa.'","Recompensa: Bill Traspié, Maestro de Espadas","El cartel anuncia una recompensa por un hombre llamado Bill Traspié, descrito como un 'saqueador de tumbas notorio, sumamente hábil con las espadas', e invita a los interesados a buscar a Clark Cercapiedra en Ost Forod para conocer los detalles y postularse para la comisión.","'¿Has acabado con Bill Traspié? ¡Muy bien! Aquí tienes tu recompensa: bien merecida, además.'","'Bill Traspié había sido un problema serio desde hacía tiempo.'","'Es bueno saber que Bill Traspié ya no será un problema.'","Bill Traspié está en las ruinas de Tham Varan en Parth Aduial, al sur del cruce de Canadiach.\
\
Has aceptado la comisión de la recompensa por Bill Traspié.","'Buena suerte con ese villano, Bill Traspié. Deberías encontrarlo en Parth Aduial, en las grandes ruinas al sur del cruce. Creo que se llaman Tham Varan.'","Se ha ofrecido una recompensa por Bill Traspié, un saqueador de tumbas notorio conocido por su habilidad con las espadas."},
[2320]={"Defeat Black Númenórean soldiers in Parth Daenath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Black Númenórean soldiers.","Defeated Black Númenórean captains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have defeated Black Númenórean soldiers and their captains, successfully pushing back their assaults in Parth Daenath. The man who posted the bounty will be pleased that the Great Alliance has been made safer, and if he truly manages to refrain from gambling on the makeup of the enemy forces, his coin-purse should not get much lighter.","A bounty notice asks you to push back the Black Númenórean's advance in Parth Daenath.","Defeat Black Númenórean captains in Parth Daenath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Black Númenórean soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Black Númenóreans can be found in Parth Daenath.\
\
You should defeat Black Númenórean soldiers and their captains.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'After so many years of siege, our forces are spread thin, and every now and again there are fresh assaults at the locations we are weakest! I would wager all of my coin that it's these Black Númenóreans who are responsible. Take up the sword and put a stop to these attacks, because my purse runs low. I need to stop making these wagers!'","Completado","Bounty: Black Númenóreans in Parth Daenath"},
[2325]={"'I've killed once and I'll do it again, if you don't stay out of my way. You'll leave me be if you know what's good for you!'","Find and capture Candúr","Candúr brutally attacked a guard ere he fled, likely through one of the gates of Calembel","See if anyone saw Candúr just west of Calembel","'Finally, someone hoping to track down the escaped killer. Yes, I saw him, running along the rooftops across from this very spot. He disappeared over the wall to my right.\
\
'I wish I could describe the chill that shook me when I met his eyes. It was as if he dared me to scream with his glaring eyes. It took my voice away.'","'Ah, so you are the brave stranger who wishes to hunt down Candúr! Good luck; he is a violent criminal, from what I understand. He did not pass through this gate, for I have it well guarded, as you see.'","It is likely that Candúr stole a sword and fled north, upstream....","'You are hunting Candúr? Good. He is a murderous man, and must be kept away from people. Killed his own brother, that one.\
\
'He did not come this way. I stand guard, for the soldiers have gone off with Angbor. I would have seen him if he dared to cross this gate.'","Candúr disappeared over the wall west of this very spot....","Candúr did not come this way","You have defeated Candúr, the dangerous escaped criminal from Lamedon","Candúr almost certainly came this way, and has claimed a life in passing hither. It is likely that he is not far.","See if Candúr was spotted escaping (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Search north upstream for Candúr","'Aye, I was guarding the dungeons when Candúr escaped. Overpowered me, he did. Nearly ripped my shoulder out of its socket when he threw me down.\
\
'I didn't see which way he went, but he was a mean fellow, and strong as an ox. Dark hair, dirty, dark beard.\
\
'I don't want a man like that running loose in Lamedon.'","Collect your reward from Laindir","Candúr, a dangerous criminal, has escaped the dungeons of Calembel. There are no reports of sightings as of yet, or indications as to which way he ran.\
\
A reward will be offered to anyone who can track and capture this violent man.","Laindir can be found in Calembel.\
\
You should return to Laindir and collect your reward for defeating the deadly and murderous Candúr.","If Candúr came this way, it would seem that he has taken a life. This poor man likely crossed his path, and met a violent end at the hands of the escaped killer.","Bounty: Candúr's Escape","'Hey! You there! Help! Someone stole my sword!\
\
'I demand justice! Where is Angbor? He has abandoned us to thieves and robbers. Is no one safe?\
\
'I suspect my neighbour's boy. He claims he saw a wild-looking man running north upstream, but it sounds like a tall tale to me....'","'Candúr has been defeated? You have done well, ${PLAYER}. Here is a reward on behalf of Calembel for your endeavour, as promised.'","According to townsfolk of Calembel, Candúr escaped to the west of town.\
\
You should seek and recapture Candúr, the man who murdered his own brother.","'Oh! Imagine if Candúr came through here. He might have murdered us where we sit!\
\
'Nay, I do not believe he came this way. I do not even like to think of it....'","The dungeon where Candúr was kept can be found in the north-west corner of Calembel.\
\
You should see if there is any evidence in the dungeon as to where Candúr might have gone when he escaped.","Townsfolk who may have seen or heard something of Candúr can be found throughought Calembel.\
\
You should speak with townsfolk to see if you can glean any clues to Candúr's whereabouts.","Candúr crawled over the wall just west of the woman who witnessed his escape.\
\
You should search directly west to see if Candúr left any traces to allow him to be followed.","Search the dungeon for hints of Candúr's intentions","Find a witness in Calembel","A dangerous man by the name of Candúr has escaped his incarceration in the jail of Calembel, and should be caught immediately.","Candúr, now armed, likely fled north upstream.\
\
You should search along the river for signs of Candúr. His trail is not yet cold!"},
[2327]={"Cualquiera de las criaturas en las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Sur puede llevar abalorios y reliquias del reino de Cardolan.\
\
Edith Rosadulce intercambiará materiales de artesanía por cualquier reliquia de Cardolan que encuentres.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión puede completarse tres veces.</rgb>","Recolecta reliquias de Cardolan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Reliquias de Cardolan recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cardolan, antaño el reino dominante en la zona de las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Sur, dejó atrás muchas reliquias. Las criaturas de las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Sur probablemente lleven algunas de estas reliquias si uno las busca.","'Las reliquias de Cardolan pueden alcanzar un buen precio entre los acomodados de Bree. Ya que estamos aquí, pensé que podría ofrecerte un pequeño trato.\
\
'Si recolectas estas reliquias durante tus viajes, te cambiaré materiales que pueden serte de gran utilidad.\
\
'¿Te parece aceptable?'","Recompensa: Reliquias de Cardolan","'Estas se venderán muy bien, y te debo mucho. Aquí tienes, esto debería ser un intercambio justo, y si crees que no lo es, sabes dónde encontrarme.'","Lleva las reliquias a Edith Rosadulce","'Cualquiera de las criaturas aquí, en las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Sur, podría tener un artefacto de Cardolan, ya sea consigo o en sus entrañas.'"},
[2328]={"Bar Elir, a farmstead, is south-west of Calembel.\
\
You should return the chickens to the farmers at Bar Elir.","The farmer states that she saw a trail of footprints heading west from the coop","Bar Elir, a farmstead, is south-west of Calembel.\
\
You should speak with the farmers at Bar Elir to hear their report of the chicken-thief directly.","You have defeated the chicken-thief","The chicken-thief's hideout is west of Bar Elir, in southern Lamedon.\
\
See what the chicken-thief was cooking while you wait for him to return.","The chicken-thief has gathered chickens west of Bar Elir, in southern Lamedon.\
\
The thief is nowhere to be found, but the chickens should be returned to their coop.","'Our chickens! Thank you, ${PLAYER}! Did you catch that good-for-nothing thief? Ah...that is too bad. But it was indeed good of you to return our hens to us.'","Question witnesses at Bar Elir","Collect your reward from Laindir","'Yes, I was the one who noticed the chickens were gone this morning. Every last one of them! What will we do for eggs now?\
\
'I saw some footprints and a few stray feathers leading away west, but they have since been stamped out and blown away.'","'You did well, ${PLAYER}! Hador will trouble the farms around these parts no more. It would seem that his greed for chicken-meat carried him away!'","Laindir can be found in Calembel in Lamedon.\
\
You should return to Laindir in Calembel and tell him that you found the hideout, and defeated the thief.","Find the chicken-thief's hideout","The chicken-thief is reported to have likely gone west of Bar Elir in southern Lamedon, likely taking cover in the shelter of trees and rocks in the hills.\
\
You should search for the chicken-thief.","Collect stolen chickens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have found the hideout of the chicken-thief!","Catch the chicken-thief","Bounty: Chicken-thief","Collected a stolen chicken (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Numerous farmers have reported chickens going missing, and wish the culprit to be caught.","Numerous farmers in the valley of Lamedon have reported chickens going missing, and have often seen a man creeping through the coops at night. He has evaded capture each time he has plundered a coop. The most recent report is from last night, from Bar Elir (a farmstead to the south-west of Calembel).\
\
A generous reward will be bestowed to anyone who can capture the chicken-thief.","Return the chickens to the farmers at Bar Elir"},
[2329]={"Defeat Hakâri within Ghâs Hejai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Informed Zûfan of the completed bounty","Inform Zûfan in Jadambor that you have culled the number of cultists","Una recompensa publicada por Bôgalekh para ir a Ghâs Hejai en el norte y reducir el número de Hakâri en la zona.","You inform Zûfan about the completed bounty.\
\
'Great work ${CLASS}. I know they will return soon enough, but the longer we can keep fighting them back thanks to the likes of adventurers like you, the better.\
\
'Be sure to check the board for more requests, we need all the help we can get down here.'","You accepted a bounty notice asking you to reduce the number of Hakâri in Ghâs Hejai. It can be found to the north of Jadambor.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
We can not let the cultists rebuild their strength here in Dil-irmíz.\
\
Any willing adventurers need only to go north to Ghâs Hejai and defeat any you encounter. If you succeed, return to Zûfan here in Jadambor and he will reward you for your efforts.\
\
They can be dangerous. You may want to bring some companions.","Reach the Hakâri camp to the north of Jadambor","Inform Zûfan in Jadambor that you have culled the number of cultists.","Defeat Hakâri to weaken their grasp on the area","Hakâri defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bounty: Clearing Ghâs Hejai"},
[2330]={"Defeat spiders to help make the area safer","Informed Zûfan of the completed bounty","Arañas derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You accepted a bounty notice asking you to reduce the number of spiders in Jalkhûl. It can be found to the south-east of Jadambor.","Inform Zûfan in Jadambor that you have culled the number of spiders","Bounty: Clearing Jalkhûl","Se ha publicado una recompensa con la solicitud de ir a Jalkhûl en el sur y reducir el número de arañas en la zona.","Reach Jalkhûl to the south-east of Jadambor","You inform Zûfan about the completed bounty.\
\
'That is the best news I have heard all day. I will let the people here know that the caves to the south will be a bit safer for now. My thanks adventurer.\
\
'Be sure to check the board for more requests, we need all the help we can get down here.'","The bounty notice reads:\
\
We need someone to do something about the spiders that have taken over the southern passage through Dil-irmíz.\
\
They have overrun Jalkhûl and now that area is not open to anyone, guard and smuggler alike. Zûfan here in Jadambor has offered a reward for anyone who can help us thin their numbers.\
\
They can be dangerous. You may want to bring some companions.","Defeat spiders within Jalkhûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2334]={"Un integrante emprendedor y quizás delirante de los Eglain planea crear platos de comida extraños para ayudar con la escasez que los Eglain enfrentan casi regularmente.","Carne crujiente de gusano recolectada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recompensa: Gusanitos crujientes","Lleva la carne a Glaednoth","'¿Por qué no son nada jugosos? De hecho, son bastante crujientes. Me pregunto cómo se cocinan. Tendré que encontrar la manera...\
\
'Debo darte lo que te prometí. Gracias, ${PLAYER}.'","Los gusanos se pueden encontrar por todo el pantano de Harloeg. Glaednoth se encuentra en Ost Haer, en el extremo sur de Harloeg.\
\
Glaednoth te ha pedido que recojas carne de los gusanos de Harloeg.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son misiones repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión se puede completar tres veces.</rgb>","Recolecta carne crujiente de gusano (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Busca los gusanos por todo el pantano de Harloeg. Ahora mismo veo algunos, justo debajo de la superficie del agua o correteando por las playas fangosas.'","'¿Los has visto corretear con sus patitas y sus barriguitas rozando el suelo? Sí, tienen un caparazón duro, pero apuesto a que debajo hay carne tierna, jugosa y lista para sazonarla con hierbas y especias que resalten los delicados sabores que encierra.\
\
'Mi objetivo es demostrar que podemos vivir de algo más que de lo que podemos intercambiar con Bree, y necesito ayuda para hacerlo. \
\
Encontrarás gusanos por todo el pantano aquí en Harloeg. Mátalos y tráeme la carne que hay dentro de sus pequeños caparazones para que pueda probar la viabilidad de una comida a base de estos crujientes gusanitos.'"},
[2337]={"'Hail, my friend. What can I do for you?'\
\
Gúrion notices the pelts you carry, and quickly offers to take them from you.\
\
'I had a feeling you might be the one to fulfil that bounty, ${PLAYER}. Blackroot Vale has no shortage of hunters, but there is far easier prey than wolves and prey that is of greater use to our people... and to our stomachs! Even so, you have done us a great service, and I think we shall all sleep more soundly knowing that Dokhvor and Húlthak no longer lurk just beyond the light of our lanterns in the night.\
\
'You have my thanks!'","You have collected a deer carcass","The eldest of the wolves invading the Blackroot Vale, Dokhvor and Húlthak, threaten the people of Lancrath and have made the pass of Tarlang's Neck unsafe for travellers.","With a mournful and defiant howl, Dokhvor falls defeated","Gúrion can be found in Lancrath in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have defeated Dokhvor and Húlthak and taken their pelts. You should deliver the pelts to Gúrion in Lancrath.","Húlthak looses a terrible howl as he falls, and Dokhvor attacks in a vengeful fury!","Deer can be found throughout the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Gúrion of Lancrath has posted a bounty seeking skilled hunters to defeat the wolf elders, Dokhvor and Húlthak, who now dwell in Eryn Asgath. You should collect a deer carcass to use as bait.","Collect a deer carcass","Bounty: Dokhvor and Húlthak","The posted note advertises a bounty on a pair of elder wolves that have taken up in the Blackroot Vale known as Dokhvor and Húlthak, describing them as 'vicious and bloodthirsty pack-leaders and mates, and the foul parentage of many of the most aggressive wolves in the western reaches of Gondor'. It suggests that those who would seek to hunt Dokhvor and Húlthak should collect a carcass from one of the deer in the Blackroot Vale, as the wolves are notoriously reclusive and will only appear to feast upon a fresh kill.\
\
You notice that the note demands the pelts of Dokhvor and Húlthak as proof of their demise, and it invites those who have fulfilled the bounty to speak to Gúrion in the hamlet of Lancrath.","Dokhvor and Húlthak can be found in Eryn Asgath in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have obtained a deer carcass from one of the many deer of the Blackroot Vale. You should use it as bait to draw out Dokhvor and Húlthak in Eryn Asgath.","Place the deer carcass in Eryn Asgath to draw out Dokhvor and Húlthak","Deliver Dokhvor and Húlthak's pelts to Gúrion in Lancrath","Drawn forth by the scent of a fresh kill, Húlthak attacks!"},
[2338]={"You have defeated Drâghru. You should return to Nashôn in Kruha-sûrja to report your success.","A bounty has been offered by Nashôn for the defeat of the bog-lurker called Drâghru.","'Ah, you have defeated the infamous Drâghru? Thank you! Here is some coin for your trouble.'","Bounty: Drâghru","Defeat the bog-lurker Drâghru","Talk to Nashôn","Defeated Drâghru","Drâghru can be found in Ilmabiri; the Wells, west of the guard post Kruha-sûrja.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
Reward offered to any individual that puts down the bog-lurker dubbed 'Drâghru'. This dangerous creature is unusually large and aggressive. It has been determined to be a threat to the people of Umbar Baharbêl that must be dealt with. See Nashôn to collect this bounty."},
[2341]={"'Ah, the fearsome hunter returns with the head of the baby-killer! The residents of Shagâna will sleep better tonight! Here is your reward.'","You have claimed the head of Ershubât the Cradle-thief.\
\
You should return to Ashâb at the Dawn-warden for your reward.","Collected the head of Ershubât","Collect the head of Ershubât","Defeat cobras in Nax Shalâl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated cobras in Nax Shalâl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bounty: Ershubât the Cradle-thief","A bounty is posted on this board. It reads:\
\
'Wanted: The head of the vile beast known as Ershubât the Cradle-thief. This massive cobra is believed to be responsible for the deaths of many Shagâni babes, killed in their own cribs. Any adventurer who ventures into the hidden oasis Nax Shalâl and slays the snake and his spawn will be rewarded.'","You have accepted a bounty to collect the head of Ershubât the Cradle-thief and slay his spawn.\
\
You should travel to the hidden oasis, Nax Shalâl, and complete the bounty.","A bounty has been posted for the slaying of a dangerous cobra in a hidden oasis.","Talk to Ashâb"},
[2342]={"Fer-nefâsi hunts her prey in the Hills of Haramûl, located in north central An Shêru.","'Did you rid us of that miserable bird Fer-nefâsi? What a relief! I am not sure we, the guard, could have taken her down ourselves without casualties. I did not look forward to it, but you have saved me the trouble! Here is your reward.'","You have defeated the roc Fer-nefâsi. You should return to Jiret-menêsh to collect your reward.","Talk to Mísikir in Jiret-menêsh","Defeat Fer-nefâsi","A bounty offered for the defeat of Fer-nefâsi, an especially menacing roc.","Reward!\
\
A reward is offered to whoever defeats the roc known as Fer-nefâsi. This savage creature has been witnessed on several occasions harrying dwarves attempting to travel through the Hills of Haramûl. It is only a matter of time before someone is killed!","Fer-nefâsi defeated","Bounty: Fer-nefâsi"},
[2343]={"Gethin Ojobuey derrotado","Recompensa: Gethin Ojobuey","Un cartel de recompensa te pide que encuentres a Gethin Ojobuey, un peligroso saqueador de tumbas del Bosque Salvaje.","El saqueador de tumbas se enfrenta a ti","Invoca y enfréntate a Gethin Ojobuey","El cartel de recompensa dice:\
\
'Derribó las viejas ruinas solo porque no encontró las riquezas que buscaba. Gethin Ojobuey, el saqueador de tumbas con fama de ganarse enemigos allá donde va. ¿Cuánto tiempo más podemos permitir que este malvado desalmado deambule por el Bosque Salvaje?\
\
'Ofrezco una recompensa a quien libre a estos bosques de Gethin Ojobuey. ¡No quiero volver a ver nunca más a ese saqueador de tumbas derribando ruinas en el Bosque Salvaje!'","Completado","Has derrotado a Gethin Ojobuey y has ayudado a los Pueblos Libres del Bosque Salvaje.","¡Gethin Ojobuey ha sido derrotado!","Gethin Ojobuey se encuentra en la Mina Este del Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Debes invocar a Gethin Ojobuey y enfrentarte a él.","'¿Qué quieres?! ¡Estoy muy ocupado!'"},
[2349]={"'Los trasgos son criaturas inmundas y un peligro para los viajeros en lugares remotos.'","Vainas de trasgo reunidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Podríamos sacar una buena ganancia cazando trasgos, creo yo!'","Recompensa: Vainas de trasgo","Gadaric Mascador ha pedido que se aplique justicia contra los trasgos que ahora infestan Minas Eriol. Son responsables de la muerte de muchos de los suyos, y ha ofrecido recompensas por su destrucción.","'Necesitaré una buena cantidad de vainas, así que caza a los trasgos de Minas Eriol, al sur, o a los trasgos bajo la sombra de la Cima de los Vientos, al noreste. Encontrarás muchas criaturas allí, estoy seguro.'","'Mi propósito está claro: aplicar una venganza medida contra los trasgos. Aun así, siento que no es suficiente.\
\
'Los trasgos son responsables de la muerte de muchos. Quiero devolverles lo que nos hicieron. Te pagaré con bienes y reconocimiento entre mi gente si estás dispuesto a ayudarme en esta tarea.\
\
'Cualquier trasgo desde el noreste de este campamento hasta las profundidades de Minas Eriol servirá, ya que muchos llevan la prueba que deseo: vainas de cuero, vainas usadas para guardar sus dagas asesinas. Busca a los trasgos en esos lugares y reclama sus vainas. Tráemelas, y me aseguraré de que recibas una recompensa adecuada.'","Lleva las vainas de trasgo a Gadaric Mascador","Reúne vainas de trasgo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Has traído varias vainas de trasgo para mí? ¡Muy bien! Soy un hombre de palabra y pagaré mi deuda como prometí. Estas servirán para aliviar el dolor de nuestras pérdidas y se usarán para recordar a nuestra gente que aún hay formas de luchar contra el mal que se extiende por estas tierras.'","Los trasgos pueden encontrarse al noreste, bajo la sombra de la Cima de los Vientos, o en las ruinas de Minas Eriol, al sureste de la Posada Abandonada.\
\
Gadaric Mascador quiere reunir las vainas que llevan los trasgos en las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión puede completarse tres veces.</rgb>"},
[2350]={"'¡Esos trasgos no vendrán aquí cuando vean mi espantapájaros!'","'No tengo mucho más que ofrecerte que mi agradecimiento. Mi espantapájaros se quedará fuera de la Posada Abandonada como advertencia para los trasgos de Annunlos; lo pensarán dos veces cuando vean que nos hemos burlado de ellos así.\
\
¡Gracias por todo lo que has hecho, ${CLASS}!'","'No soy solo la camarera y doncella aquí en la Posada Abandonada, también soy hábil con la aguja y el hilo. Ahora mismo, Anlaf me tiene haciendo una sorpresa especial para los trasgos de Annunlos.\
\
He estado intentando terminar este espantapájaros horrible durante semanas, pero nadie aquí quiere arriesgar su vida contra los trasgos para traerme lo que necesito para completarlo. Tengo todas las piezas menos la tela de suficientes tabardos de trasgo para terminar el espantapájaros.\
\
Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]}, ve a las ruinas de Minas Eriol al sureste o a las llanuras de Annunlos y tráeme algunos tabardos de los trasgos para que pueda terminar esta cosa espantosa.'","'¡Eres mucho más valiente que cualquiera aquí en la Posada Abandonada, ${PLAYER}!'","Recompensa: Tabardos de trasgo","Recoge tabardos de trasgo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva tabardos de trasgo a Lieva Lirioagrio","Hay trasgos en las ruinas de Minas Eriol, al sureste de la Posada Abandonada, y en los campos de Annunlos.\
\
Para terminar su espantapájaros, Lieva Lirioagrio necesita algunos de los tabardos que usan los trasgos de Annunlos, pero nadie en la Posada Abandonada es lo suficientemente valiente para arriesgarse a recoger la tela para ella. Te ha pedido que recojas los tabardos en su lugar.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión puede completarse tres veces.</rgb>","'Necesito algunos tabardos de los trasgos en las ruinas de Minas Eriol, al sureste de la Posada Abandonada o en las llanuras de Annunlos. Cualquier tabardo servirá. Estoy haciendo un espantapájaros para mantener a los trasgos alejados de la posada.'","Tabardos de trasgo recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los trasgos en las ruinas de Minas Eriol, al sureste de la Posada Abandonada, causan muchos problemas a la gente de la posada. Lieva Lirioagrio está cosiendo un espantapájaros para ahuyentar a los trasgos."},
[2353]={"You have defeated Gristlefell and assisted the expedition.","Defeated láthbears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Gristlefell","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'Who among you has not known the fear of a bear's call in the woods? It is a warning to keep away, a distant threat. But it is different here in the Ered Mithrin. Here, the láthbear will give you little notice of its ire; before you know you are hunted, it is upon you, its red eyes full of hate, its sharp teeth slavering!\
\
'Of all the láthbears that prowl these mountains, none is more dangerous than the one named Gristlefell. A reward to any who can bring him down, along with others of his sloth!'","A bounty notice asks you to seek out Gristlefell, a ravenous wild beast in Ered Mithrin.","Defeat Mithrin láthbears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gristlefell and Mithrin láthbears can be found in Ered Mithrin.\
\
You should defeat láthbears.","Defeated Gristlefell.","Completado","Defeated Gristlefell","Bounty: Gristlefell"},
[2354]={"You have defeated Gírkhash and many of his spawn.\
\
You should return to Shâpar in Ahâba for your reward.","You have accepted a bounty to defeat Gírkhash and other bronze lizards in Idagâl.\
\
You should find and defeat these lizards.","Bounty: Gírkhash","Defeat Gírkhash","Talk to Shâpar","A bounty has been posted for a large frilled lizard that has been antagonizing the Beltáni in Ahâba.","Defeat bronze lizards in Idagâl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You have defeated the lizard Gírkhash? Excellent work, ${CLASS}. Here is your well-earned reward!'","Defeated bronze lizards in Idagâl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Gírkhash","A bounty is posted on this board. It reads:\
\
'Wanted: A brave adventurer to find and defeat the giant bronze lizard known as Gírkhash. This lizard and his spawn have been attacking the sheep and ransacking the foodstuff in Ahâba and must be hunted down.'"},
[2355]={"Defeated Gúrkug","Defeated Gúrkug.","A bounty notice asks you to seek out Gúrkug, a brutal goblin driver found in Máttugard.","Defeat Gúrkug","Bounty: Gúrkug","Completado","You have defeated Gúrkug and assisted those who wish to reclaim Gundabad.","Gúrkug and goblins can be found in Máttugard.\
\
You should defeat goblins.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'Who among you has the courage to face Gúrkug? The brutal goblin driver wields his drudges as throwing spears, swarming in on any in his way.\
\
'A reward to any who can defeat Gúrkug and other goblins in Máttugard!'","Defeated goblins in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat goblins in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2358]={"'¿Enrico Riscarpado ya no está? ¡Excelente, ${PLAYER}! Era una amenaza, y si los viajes hacia Forochel vuelven a ser comunes algún día, es bueno saber que el camino será más seguro sin alguien como él en él.\
\
'Aquí tienes tu recompensa, y gracias por tu servicio.'","'Ojalá algún día el camino hacia Forochel vuelva a llenarse de viajeros.'","Ballard Wilmer está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Un cartel que ofrece una recompensa por la captura o derrota del saqueador de tumbas Enrico Riscarpado llamó tu atención. Si deseas solicitar esta recompensa, debes hablar con Ballard Wilmer.","Se ha ofrecido una recompensa por Enrico Riscarpado, un saqueador de tumbas conocido por su puntería mortal con el arco.","Recompensa: Enrico Riscarpado, Ojo Mortal","Basilio Resinas está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Has derrotado a Enrico Riscarpado y ahora debes informar a Basilio Resinas para recibir tu recompensa.","'¿Derrotaste a Enrico Riscarpado? ¡Ja! Para ser sincero, no creí que lo lograrías. ¡Así son las cosas, no es cierto?\
\
'Basilio Resinas, el juez de Ost Forod, está aquí en el pueblo. Habla con él sobre el asunto de tu recompensa.'","'¡Buena suerte con Enrico! Es un tirador mortal con el arco y ha acabado rápidamente con otros que intentaban reclamar la recompensa.\
\
'Probablemente lo encuentres cerca de la puerta de Forochel, en Cirith Rhîw, al final del camino que corre hacia el norte por Tyrn Fornech.'","'¡Lamento haber pensado que no podrías derrotar a Enrico Riscarpado!'","Enrico Riscarpado se encuentra cerca de la puerta hacia Forochel, en Cirith Rhîw, al final del camino del norte a través de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Has aceptado la comisión de reclamar la recompensa por Enrico Riscarpado, un tirador letal con el arco.","'Enrico Riscarpado era un tirador mortal, ¡pero no lo suficiente para ti!'","'Basilio Resinas, nuestro juez, está aquí en Ost Forod. Deberías hablar con él respecto a tu recompensa, ${PLAYER}.'","'¿Quieres solicitar la comisión sobre Enrico Riscarpado? ¡Muy bien, muy bien! No son muchos los viajeros que van hacia Forochel en estos días, pero los pocos que lo intentan han sufrido sus flechas.\
\
'Algunos de sus compañeros merodean por el camino cerca de la puerta de Forochel en Cirith Rhîw. Solo sigue el camino norte a través de Tyrn Fornech para llegar.\
\
'Capturar o derrotar a Enrico será un servicio para la gente honesta de Ost Forod. Pero ten cuidado: no eres ${PLAYERNAME:el primero[m]|la primera[f]} que intenta quebrar el arco de Riscarpado... ¡quizás seas ${PLAYERNAME:el[m]|la[f]} último, eh?'","Ballard Wilmer está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Has derrotado a Enrico Riscarpado y ahora debes informar a Ballard Wilmer.","El cartel anuncia una recompensa por un hombre llamado Enrico Riscarpado, descrito como 'un saqueador de tumbas dotado de una puntería sorprendente con el arco', e invita a los interesados a buscar a Ballard Wilmer en Ost Forod para conocer los detalles y postularse para la comisión.","'En otra época pensé en reclamar la recompensa por Enrico Riscarpado, pero me di la vuelta y huí antes de encontrarlo.'"},
[2360]={"Iorwerth can be found at the Writhendowns Tomb, guarding the barrow from outside.\
\
You should summon and defeat Iorwerth and collect his crest.","'Well done, ${PLAYER}! This trophy will be a lively addition to my ever-growing collection.'","Return to Britric","Collected the crest of Iorwerth","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","Defeat Iorwerth and collect his crest","Bounty: Iorwerth","Iorwerth, the guardian of the Writhendowns Tomb, has woken, and haunts the small island on which the tomb rests.","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I hear you are quite the foe-hunter in these parts. Perhaps we can work together, eh?\
\
'I am a collector of odds and ends -- trophies of the enemy. I believe that someday they will be of great historical value, you see.\
\
'A draugar named Iorwerth, the guardian of the Writhendowns Tomb, has woken and taken to walking about of late. Will you bring me his crest? I'll see that you are amply rewarded.'","Britric is in Forlaw.\
\
You have defeated Iorwerth, and should now return to Forlaw to collect your bounty."},
[2361]={"Bring Jûkhtar's venom to Nazâkh in Zajâna","The malevolent spider Jûkhtar has been growing her brood and attacking Zajâni citizens near her burrow in Jâr Obadal. You are to defeat her and collect a sample of her venom.","Bring Jûkhtar's venom to Nazâkh in Zajâna to collect your reward.","Bounty: Jûkhtar of the Thousand Children","Defeat Jûkhtar and collect her venom","The bounty notice reads:\
\
On behalf of the Doorwards of Zajâna, hallowed protectors of commerce and the Great Road, you are empowered to seek out and defeat the great spider Jûkhtar. Many innocents have been attacked and poisoned by her and her children. We ask that you collect a sample of her venom, that the scholars of Zajâna may study it and compose a healing salve for those poisoned by bites from her children.\
\
After her defeat, bring a sample of her venom to Zajâna. Present it to Nazâkh, Huntswoman to the Doorwards, outside the council chambers in Zajâna for a proper reward.","The malevolent spider Jûkhtar has been growing her brood and attacking Zajâni citizens near her burrow in Jâr Obadal. You are to defeat her and collect a sample of her venom. Bring it to Nazâkh in Zajâna, that she may give it to those who would prepare a salve to heal citizens poisoned by her children.","'This will save more than you know. I will give this to the Pohâni right away. They will set to work right away creating a salve to heal those afflicted by Jûkhtar and her children. Please accept this reward, with our thanks.'"},
[2362]={"You have reclaimed someone's severed hand from the dread-tortoise.\
\
You should return to Ashâb at the Dawn-warden for your reward.","A bounty has been posted for the slaying of a massive dread-tortoise.","Defeat Kasâshu the Grinder","Bounty: Kasâshu the Grinder","The only item of note inside the tortoise is a severed hand!","'Arâniz told us that the Aradûni have posted a bounty on a certain dread-tortoise at Karmu Râx called 'Kasâshu the Grinder'. Apparently he ate something of value to them? It did not seem worth the risk to us, but perhaps you would like to take them up on it.'","A bounty is posted on this board. It reads:\
\
'Wanted: an adventurer to slay the dread-tortoise known as Kasâshu the Grinder. This massive beast has eaten something of great value to a soldier of Aradûn, and the object must be reclaimed from its innards. The Grinder was last seen among the other dread-tortoises at Karmu Râx. The Servants of Aradûn offer a reward for any who can assist with this task.'","You produce the severed hand and show it to Ashâb. He grimaces at the ghastly sight, but seems relieved that you have returned with it.\
\
'Ah! I was worried no one would ever complete this bounty. That dread-tortoise was proving very difficult to kill.'\
\
Ashâb removes the glove from the hand, revealing a simple gold wedding ring on one of the fingers.\
\
'This is the true item of great value. One of our soldiers lost his hand to that beast, but refused to return home without it. You have done him a great service, ${PLAYER}.'","Collect the 'item of great value'","You have accepted a bounty to defeat Kasâshu the Grinder and reclaim something of great value from his belly.\
\
You should travel to Karmu Râx and complete the bounty.","Defeated Kasâshu the Grinder","Talk to Ashâb"},
[2363]={"'You defeated Kaursu? Some of our finest warriors were broken by his blade. You aren't one to be trifled with, it seems. Thank you. These warriors deserve better than to be worn by a monster. We can give their remains a proper resting place now.'","Bring Kaursu's vile armour to Numûru in Urmâkh","The bounty notice reads:\
\
On behalf of the Queen of Renewed Hamât, Mizâdi Shâra, you are asked to seek out and defeat the infamous Orc Kaursu. Kaursu has been seen inside Kûr Anzar and is known to be allies with the vile Barkhûshim stationed there. Kaursu has killed more than fifty Hamâti warriors, using their skulls and bones as vile trophies upon his very armour.\
\
The proof of his death shall be his chest-piece and pauldrons, that we may lay our fallen soldiers to rest properly. Bring the vile armour to Numûru, Hand of the Queen in Urmâkh for a proper reward.","Defeat Kaursu and collect his vile armour","Bring Kaursu's vile armour to Numûru in Urmâkh to collect your reward.","Mizâdi Shâra, Queen of Renewed Hamât, has posted a bounty seeking skilled soldiers to defeat the infamous Orc Kaursu, slayer of over fifty Hamâti warriors, and return to her Hand, Numûru, with his armour. He keeps his council with the Barkhûshim in Kûr Anzar.","The infamous Orc Kaursu has killed many Hamâti warriors from his perch in Kûr Anzar. You are to defeat him and return to Numûru with his vile armour.","Bounty: Kaursu"},
[2364]={"'Well done, ${PLAYER}! This trophy will be a lively addition to my ever-growing collection.'","Keen-eye has been spotted atop a frozen waterfall in the High Knolls, and it is believed that his beak will be a valuable part of a collection of bounties.","Keen-eye can be found in the High Knolls, atop the rocky tunnel and frozen waterfall that cover the southern road in the High Knolls.\
\
You should summon and defeat Keen-eye, and collect his beak.","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","Bounty: Keen-eye","Britric is in Forlaw.\
\
You have collected the beak of Keen-eye, and should now return to Forlaw to collect your bounty.","Collected Keen-eye's beak","Defeat Keen-eye and collect his beak","Bring the beak to Britric","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I hear you are quite the foe-hunter in these parts. Perhaps we can work together, eh?\
\
'I am a collector of odds and ends -- trophies of the enemy. I believe that someday they will be of great historical value, you see.\
\
'A spying craban from Isengard named Keen-eye is thought to lead all of the spying birds in Wildermore. He has been seen nesting atop a frozen waterfall in the High Knolls. Will you bring me his beak? I'll see that you are amply rewarded.'"},
[2366]={"Defeated Kigrush","Return to Neshurga and inform him of Kigrush's defeat","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'A group of brigands has been betraying our agreement here in Urash Dâr and they must be stopped. They are working out of Zikrum-dûl and are led by the a ruthless man named Kigrush.\
\
'Put an end to him and speak to Neshurga in Ub Nishir when you do.'","A bounty notice in Ub Nishir has asked for someone to defeat ruthless leader of a group of brigands in Zikrum-dûl to the east known as Kigrush.","A bounty notice asks you to defeat Kigrush, the leader of a brigand group attacking refugees. He is reported to be found in Zikrum-dûl to the east.","Defeat Kigrush","'I am glad to hear of the end of Kigrush. He broke our agreement to work together against the Orcs who ravage this land and instead choose to prey on the refugees fleeing from the chaos.\
\
'The road through Zikrum-dûl will now be safer thanks to you. Take this, ${CLASS}.'","Bounty: Kigrush","Return to Neshurga in Ub Nishir north of Maurûsh and inform him that you have completed the bounty and defeated Kigrush."},
[2367]={"Bring Korutásh's jewelled dagger to Nazâkh in Zajâna to collect your reward.","Bounty: Korutásh the Cruel","'Saráz záro-dan. It was past time for Korutásh's reign of terror to end. Let me see it. Yes, it is a fine blade - good craftmanship, well-balanced. I will give it to one of the Bandázan, protectors of Zajâna. We will see it used for a more valorous purpose in the future.'","The bounty notice reads:\
\
On behalf of the Doorwards of Zajâna, hallowed protectors of commerce and the Great Road, you are empowered to seek out and defeat the infamous goblin Korutásh the Cruel. Long have his raiding parties harried and attacked the people of Sen Chatâk and travellers along the Great Road. He can be found in the hills of Glúkroz, north-east of Sen Chatâk.\
\
Proof of his demise shall be Korutásh's infamous bejewelled dagger. Present it to Nazâkh, Huntswoman to the Doorwards, outside the council chambers in Zajâna for a proper reward.","The dread goblin Korutásh has slain many innocent people in Sen Chatâk with his raiding parties. You are to defeat him and return to Nazâkh with his bejewelled dagger.","Defeat Korutásh and collect his jewelled dagger","The dread goblin Korutásh has slain many innocent people in Sen Chatâk with his raiding parties. You are to defeat him and return to Nazâkh with his bejewelled dagger. Korutásh can be found north-east of Sen Chatâk, in the hills of Glúkroz.","Bring Korutásh's jewelled dagger to Nazâkh in Zajâna"},
[2368]={"'Well done, ${PLAYER}! This trophy will be a lively addition to my ever-growing collection.'","Britric is in Forlaw.\
\
You have collected the knife of the goblin Spy-master Krah, and should now return to Forlaw to collect your bounty.","Defeat Krah and collect his knife","Bring the knife to Britric","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","The Spy-master Krah can be summoned just north of Dunfast in the Whitshaws.\
\
You should summon and defeat Krah, and collect his knife.","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I hear you are quite the foe-hunter in these parts. Perhaps we can work together, eh?\
\
'I am a collector of odds and ends -- trophies of the enemy. I believe that someday they will be of great historical value, you see.\
\
'A nasty goblin, a Spy-master named Krah from Isengard, has evidently been spotted outside of Dunfast in the Whitshaws lately. Will you bring me his knife? I'll see that you are amply rewarded.'","Isengard's goblin Spy-master, Krah, has been seen near Dunfast in the Whitshaws, and it is believed that his knife will be a valuable part of a collection of bounties.","Collected Krah's knife","Bounty: Krah, the Spy-master"},
[2369]={"'Well done, ${PLAYER}! This trophy will be a lively addition to my ever-growing collection.'","Britric is in Forlaw.\
\
You have collected the tooth of Kurr, and should now return to Forlaw to collect your bounty.","Defeat Kurr and collect his tooth","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I hear you are quite the foe-hunter in these parts. Perhaps we can work together, eh?\
\
'I am a collector of odds and ends -- trophies of the enemy. I believe that someday they will be of great historical value, you see.\
\
'A troll named Kurr has been seen knocking about some large rocks in the Whitshaws. Will you bring me one of his teeth? I'll see that you are amply rewarded.'","Bounty: Kurr","Collected Kurr's tooth","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","Kurr has been seen by some tall rocks in the north-east plains of the Whitshaws, and it is believed that his tooth will be a valuable part of a collection of bounties.","Kurr romps in the north-eastern plains of the Whitshaws, hiding among some tall rocks near the fishermens' home.\
\
You should summon and defeat Kurr, and collect his tooth.","Bring Kurr's tooth to Britric"},
[2370]={"Agátur the Boastful asks you to seek out Kurthár, a terrible cave-beast found in Máttugard.","Bring the claw of Kurthár to Agátur","'Hmm, have you seen the beast, ${PLAYER}? Bah, I speak of Kurthár, the mighty cave-beast! Kurthár is a terrible menace in Máttugard. The beast has ransacked multiple supply carts and must be stopped! Find Kurthár and bring me its claw. Only then shall I rest easily.'","Collect the claw of Kurthár for Agátur","Defeated Kurthár","Defeat cave-beasts in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Kurthár","Collected the claw of Kurthár","Defeated cave-beasts in Máttugard (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Agátur can be found at Steepset in Máttugard.\
\
You should bring the claw of Kurthár to Agátur.","'Oh ho! This is the claw of Kurthár indeed! Many at Steepset will rejoice to see this beast no more when travelling through Máttugard. You have done a good deed, ${PLAYER}.'","Kurthár and cave-beasts can be found in Máttugard.\
\
You should defeat cave-beasts.","Bounty: Kurthár"},
[2371]={"Deliver Kurzglok's mandibles to Melril in Sardol","Its many barbed legs stilled at last, Kurzglok bubbles and falls silent","Bounty: Kurzglok the Many-legged","The posted note advertises a bounty on a spider of Blackroot Vale known as Kurzglok, described as 'a terrifying great spider and devourer of its own kind lurking in the caverns of Lhingroth', and it invites any who claim to have slain Kurzglok to speak with Melril in the hamlet of Sardol.\
\
You notice that a hasty addition has been scrawled in different hand-writing at the bottom of the note, demanding that Kurzglok's mandibles be collected as proof of its defeat.","Kurzglok can be found somewhere in the caverns of Lhingorth in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
A bounty posted by Melril of Sardol seeks for a skilled hunter to seek out and defeat the spider, Kurzglok, in the caverns of Lhingroth.","'Hello, ${PLAYER}. What is that you've got there?'\
\
Melril raises an eyebrow with some measure of concern growing on her face. You present Kurzglok's mandibles to her, and her face contorts into an annoyed revulsion.\
\
'I absolutely did not ask for these! But you say the bounty demanded them as proof? Nonsense! One of the other hunters must be playing a prank on me again. They know how much I hate spiders, after all, and if it had been anything else, I'd have dealt with it myself. Well, we'll see who's laughing when I find out who it was!\
\
'Nevertheless, I would have taken you at your word, friend. And so long as Kurzglok won't trouble us any longer, that is enough for me. You have my thanks!'","The terrible spider known as Kurzglok poses a grave threat to the hunters of Sardol.","The web springs at your touch and a loud reverberation echoes through Lhingroth!","Find and defeat Kurzglok in Lhingroth","Melril can be found in Sardol in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have defeated Kurzglok and taken its mandibles. You should deliver them to Melril in Sardol."},
[2372]={"Defeated Langarch","You ask Derufin about the bounty notice.\
\
'The bounty! I am quite glad you are here! The Rangers asked if Duilin and I could rid them of this nuisance. Apparently this boar's been getting in the way of the Rangers slinking about. Obviously I said yes to appease these hospitable men. The thing is, we're quite busy with hunting bigger game and can't be bothered with this animal. If you take care of this task for me, Duilin and I would be most grateful.'","Derufin can be found in Bâr Húrin.\
\
You should speak with Derufin.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'A large boar keeps interfering with Ranger activities. Please speak with me for further details. Derufin'","A bounty notice asks you to seek out Derufin who has information about Langarch, a maddened wild beast in Southern Ithilien.","'Well done. Well done indeed! No need to tell the Rangers. I shall inform Anborn myself. You've done much. It is the least I can do! Take care, friend.'","Speak with Derufin","Defeat Langarch","Langarch can be found somewhere in Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should defeat Langarch.","Bounty: Langarch"},
[2373]={"Legwêna is located in the western side of Ilmabiri; the Wells.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
Wanted: The slaying of the morroval known as Legwêna. Do not attempt unless you are an experienced warrior. She has killed some and injured many. Morutágya wants her head! See Porókho for reward.\
\
Scrawled underneath this in another handwriting is an additional message that reads:\
\
Please do not actually bring us a head. That is gruesome.\
-Eshéra","Defeat the morroval Legwêna","Morutágya Clan has called for the death of the morroval known as Legwêna.","Defeated Legwêna","You have defeated the morroval, Legwêna. You should return to Porókho at his camp in Hêbatokh to claim your reward.","'Oh-ho!  You have slain Legwêna? This is good news! You did not bring her head though? That is ok. I will reward you anyway.'","Talk to Porókho","Bounty: Legwêna"},
[2375]={"The bounty notice reads:\
\
'I seek a certain bear as a trophy. Come speak with me for further details. Duilin'","A bounty notice asks you to seek out Duilin who has information about Maeganc, a ravenous wild beast in Southern Ithilien.","Duilin can be found in Bâr Húrin.\
\
You should speak with Duilin.","Defeated Maeganc","Speak with Duilin","Maeganc can be found somewhere in Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should defeat Maeganc.","Defeat Maeganc","Bounty: Maeganc","You ask Duilin about the bounty notice.\
\
'Ah yes the great bear, Maeganc. My brother and I have been very busy. So busy in fact that we've not the time to hunt this exquisite game. The Mûmak calls us as the ultimate hunt. If you hunt this bear for us, I promise you will be handsomely rewarded. The bear's head would look grand in our hall back in the Blackroot Vale!'","'Ah you have returned and brought the bear to us. I am sure it was no trouble at all for you. Now if you will excuse us we must prepare ourselves for a real hunt with a Mûmak!'"},
[2377]={"'So, Manyêki is defeated? Very good! The road south is safer now!\
\
'Perhaps we should offer a bounty for all of the Ordâkhai soldiers so we can finally be free of them, too!'\
\
The dwarf laughs at the preposterous notion of putting a bounty on hundreds of people as he gives you the promised reward.","Notice:\
\
A reward is offered for the slaying of Manyêki, a grodbog as ferocious as it is repulsive. Do not be fooled by its size! Manyêki is small but mighty.\
\
This detestable creature can usually be found south of Jiret-menêsh in the Hills of Haramûl.","Talk to Mísikir in Jiret-menêsh","Bounty: Manyêki","Defeat Manyêki","You have defeated the grodbog Manyêki. You should return to Jiret-menêsh to collect your reward.","A reward has been offered for the defeat of a grodbog called Manyêki.","Manyêki can usually be found south of Jiret-menêsh in the Hills of Haramûl. You should go there and defeat it.","Manyêki defeated"},
[2378]={"'Well done, ${PLAYER}! This trophy will be a lively addition to my ever-growing collection.'","Bring the pauldrons to Britric","Collected Marr's pauldrons","Marr has been seen camping outside of Scylfig, and it is believed that his pauldrons will be a valuable part of a collection of bounties.","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I hear you are quite the foe-hunter in these parts. Perhaps we can work together, eh?\
\
'I am a collector of odds and ends -- trophies of the enemy. I believe that someday they will be of great historical value, you see.\
\
'A half-orc named Marr, a rather deadly warrior, has evidently been camping just outside of Scylfig of late. Will you bring me his pauldrons? I'll see that you are amply rewarded.'","Defeat Marr and collect his pauldrons","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","Marr can be found camping on a hilltop south-west of the ruined town of Scylfig.\
\
You should summon and defeat Marr and collect his pauldrons.","Britric is in Forlaw.\
\
You have defeated Marr, and should now return to Forlaw to collect your bounty.","Bounty: Marr"},
[2381]={"Bounty: Nâralarg, the Blighted Root","The bounty notice reads:\
\
On behalf of the Doorwards of Zajâna, hallowed protectors of commerce and the Great Road, you are empowered to seek out and defeat the dread restless tree Nâralarg, the Blighted Root. He has been seen harrying the citizens of Sormedân and spreading blight and disease from Adagím into our unblemished farmlands. He can be found in the blighted grove of Shádhag, near Adagím.\
\
Proof of his demise shall be a piece of Nâralarg's blighted root. Present it to Nazâkh, Huntswoman to the Doorwards, outside the council chambers in Zajâna for a proper reward.","'Drógai! I don't believe it. That accursed tree has finally been slain. There is much that is foul in Adagím, and I think it best that those unnatural trees stay there. You have done much to prevent disease and blight from spreading into Sormedân and beyond, and for that, my friend, you have my thanks.'","You are to defeat Nâralarg, the Blighted Root before he can spread noxious disease throughout Kighân. Return to Nazâkh in Zajâna with a sample of his blighted roots to show proof of his demise. He can be found in the blighted grove of Shádhag, near Adagím.","You are to defeat Nâralarg, the Blighted Root before he can spread noxious disease throughout Kighân. Return to Nazâkh in Zajâna with a sample of his blighted roots to show proof of his demise.","Defeat Nâralarg and collect his blighted root","Bring Nâralarg's root to Nazâkh in Zajâna to collect your reward.","Bring Nâralarg's root to Nazâkh in Zajâna"},
[2382]={"You defeated Orc lieutenants and successfully thinned the ranks of the Orc soldiers. The man who posted the bounty must be pleased, but you do wonder how many potential bounty-seekers his notice may have sent into danger.","Defeated Orc lieutenants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Orc soldiers can be found in Arandor.\
\
You should defeat Orc soldiers and lieutenants.","Defeat Orcs in Arandor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'Pay attention to this notice! Do not assume one of your brethren will heed it! Yes, I am writing this to you! The Orcs' numbers are getting out of control in Arandor, and a group of their lieutenants has been rallying for an assault on our camp. Put an end to it, and you will be handsomely rewarded. Yes, you!'","Bounty: Orcs in Arandor","A bounty asks you to thin the Orc numbers and slay their lieutenants in Arandor.","Completado","Defeated Orc soldiers.","Has derrotado orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Orc lieutenants in Arandor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2389]={"You inform Zûfan about the completed bounty.\
\
'That is great to hear. Our scouts will be relieved to hear the news and can worry about looking over their shoulders a little less thanks to you.\
\
'Be sure to check the board for more requests, we need all the help we can get down here.'","Informed Zûfan of the completed bounty","Bounty: Quelling Bog-lurkers","You accepted a bounty notice asking you to reduce the number of bog-lurkers near Jadambor to help make the roads safer.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
Some bog-lurkers have been spotted in the area, and we can not risk our scouts getting preyed upon by these beasts.\
\
We are in need of someone to do something about them. If you do, report back to Zûfan here in Jadambor and you will be rewarded for your efforts.\
\
They can be dangerous. You may want to bring some companions.","Defeat bog-lurkers within western Dil-irmíz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Inform Zûfan in Jadambor that you have defeated bog-lurkers in the area","Bog-lurkers defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se ha publicado una recompensa para reducir el número de acechadores de pantano en la zona.","Inform Zûfan in Jadambor that you have defeated bog-lurkers in the area."},
[2390]={"Informed Zûfan of the completed bounty","You inform Zûfan about the completed bounty.\
\
'Good tidings you bring me. The shades are surely not to stop any time soon, but your efforts will give us time to catch our breath.\
\
'Be sure to check the board for more requests. We need all the help we can get down here.'","Defeat shades within western Dil-irmíz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Se ha publicado una recompensa para reducir el número de sombras en la zona.","Bounty: Quelling Shades","Inform Zûfan in Jadambor that you have defeated shades in the area","The bounty notice reads:\
\
Dil-irmíz has become overrun by shades, and we need help fighting them back.\
\
Any willing adventurers who can help reduce their numbers would be welcomed. If you manage to succeed, report back to Zûfan here in Jadambor and you'll be rewarded for your efforts.\
\
They can be dangerous. You may want to bring some companions.","Shades defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You accepted a bounty notice asking you to reduce the number shades in the area to prevent Jadambor from being overrun."},
[2391]={"The bounty notice reads:\
\
'A dangerous wasp has been roaming the Gorge of Woe to the north-east and must be slain to protect travellers along the road.\
\
'Speak with Neshurga in Ub Nishir should you defeat this beast.'","Return to Neshurga and inform him of Rakhûl's defeat","A bounty notice in Ub Nishir has asked for someone to defeat the wasp Rakhûl in the Gorge of Woe to the north-east.","Bounty: Rakhûl","'I hear you have completed the posted bounty and slain Rakhûl.\
\
'You have my thanks. Here is something for the trouble and I will pass on the news of Rakhûl's defeat to the bounty poster.'","Defeat Rakhûl","A bounty notice asks you to defeat a deadly wasp called Rakhûl in the Gorge of Woe.","Return to Neshurga in Ub Nishir north of Maurûsh and inform him that you have completed the bounty and defeated Rakhûl.","Defeated Rakhûl"},
[2392]={"Someone has robbed the vault of Calembel, stealing a great many valuables.","Someone has broken into the vault of Calembel while the majority of the guard force is absent from the city. A great many valuables were stolen, and reports have come in that the Corsairs who roam the outskirts of Lamedon openly carry the stolen goods on their persons.\
\
A reward will go to any warrior who can recover the treasure that was stolen.","Stolen treasure from the vault of Calembel can be found on Corsairs in northern Lamedon.\
\
You should recover stolen treasures from the Corsairs.","Laindir can be found in Calembel in Lamedon.\
\
You should return to Laindir and collect your reward for recovering the stolen goods.","Recovered stolen treasure (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recover stolen treasure from Corsairs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Rilgell, the vault-robber","'Well done! You are quite a boon to Calembel.'","Defeated Rilgell","Collect your reward from Laindir","Bounty: Recovery of Riches"},
[2394]={"A bounty notice asks you to seek out Thurindol who has information about Ronkúrz, an Orc captain from the Morgul-vale.","Defeated Ronkúrz","Thurindol can be found in the keep at Bâr Húrin.\
\
You should speak with Thurindol.","Bounty: Ronkúrz","Speak with Thurindol","Ronkúrz can be found somewhere in Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should defeat Ronkúrz.","You ask Thurindol about the bounty notice.\
\
'I gladly accept your offer to defeat Ronkúrz. He commands one of the forces that stormed Osgiliath. The last update I have on his whereabouts is that he was stationed somewhere in South Ithilien. Good luck.'","'Excellent work! So an enemy camp not far from here lies hidden on the Morgulduin? I shall muster some men and strike the camp tomorrow night. I thank you for your efforts.'","Defeat Ronkúrz","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'Rangers, we are in need of one of you to defeat Ronkúrz, a captain in the ranks of the Morgul-host. Speak with Thurindol if you plan to accept this mission.'"},
[2397]={"The bounty notice reads:\
\
On behalf of the Doorwards of Zajâna, hallowed protectors of commerce and the Great Road, you are asked to seek out and defeat the dread jázga Shahâk, pup of Bloodtooth. Long have travellers of the Great Road feared Shahâk and her sharp fangs, as she has slain many. She is said to haunt the lands near Dân Shatagan, north-east of Zajâna.\
\
The proof of her death shall be one of her bloody fangs. Present it to Nazâkh, Huntswoman to the Doorwards, outside the council chambers in Zajâna for a proper reward.","Bounty: Shahâk, Bloodtooth's Pup","Bring Shahâk's fang to Nazâkh in Zajâna to collect your reward.","Bring Shahâk's fang to Nazâkh in Zajâna","Defeat Shahâk and collect her mighty fang","'You've no idea how many travellers she and her pack have savaged. Many families will sleep safer tonight because of what you've done. You have my gratitude for your fearless deeds.'","Shahâk, pup of the dread jázga Bloodtooth, has been harassing travellers on the Great Road north of Zajâna. Defeat her and return to Nazâkh in Zajâna with one of her fangs as proof of her demise.","Shahâk, pup of the dread jázga Bloodtooth, has been harassing travellers on the Great Road north of Zajâna. Defeat her and return to Nazâkh in Zajâna with one of her fangs as proof of her demise. She is said to haunt the lands near Dân Shatagan, north-east of Zajâna."},
[2398]={"'Well done, ${PLAYER}! This trophy will be a lively addition to my ever-growing collection.'","Bring the bracer to Britric","Defeat Shakolam and collect his bracer","Bounty: Shakolam","Shakolam can be found on the southern part of the Orc-made road in the Balewood.\
\
You should summon and defeat Shakolam, and collect his bracer.","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","Shakolam has been seen patrolling the Orc-made road through the Balewood, towards the southern edge.","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I hear you are quite the foe-hunter in these parts. Perhaps we can work together, eh?\
\
'I am a collector of odds and ends -- trophies of the enemy. I believe that someday they will be of great historical value, you see.\
\
'A cruel war-mongering Uruk-hai named Shakolam has been seen patrolling the southern Orc-made road in the Balewood. Will you bring me his bracer? I'll see that you are amply rewarded.'","Britric is in Forlaw.\
\
You have collected the bracer of Shakolam, and should now return to Forlaw to collect your bounty.","Collected Shakolam's bracer"},
[2399]={"Bounty: Shálith","You have defeated Shálith and collected a trophy as proof","'Saig Hathíl with be safer for travellers without Shálith.\
\
'Please take this reward for your efforts, my friend.'","You defeated Shálith and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.","Return to Sálunath with proof of Shálith's demise","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'A monstrous sicklefly called Shálith has been spotted in Saig Hathíl to the north-west. The scouts in the area have requested help in defeating it.\
\
'Bring proof to Sálunath in Sul Madásh if you complete this request.'","A bounty notice asks you to defeat a monstrous sicklefly called Shálith that has been spotted in Saig Hathíl in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.","Defeat Shálith"},
[2400]={"Recompensa: Pudín de mosca guadaña","Recolecta vísceras de mosca guadaña (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las moscas guadaña se pueden encontrar en todo el pantano de Harloeg. Glaednoth se encuentra en Ost Haer, en el extremo sur de Harloeg.\
\
Glaednoth te ha pedido que recojas mollejas de las moscas segadoras de Harloeg.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son misiones repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión se puede completar tres veces.</rgb>","Un miembro emprendedor y quizás delirante de los Eglain planea crear platos de comida extraños para ayudar a solucionar la escasez a la que se enfrentan los Eglain casi con regularidad.","'¡Sí! Son lo suficientemente suaves y tienen la consistencia que deseo.\
\
'Tengo que darte lo que te prometí. Gracias, ${PLAYER}.'","Lleva las vísceras a Glaednoth.","'Busca las moscas guadaña por todo el pantano de Harloeg. Ahora mismo veo algunas revoloteando sobre el humedal o quizá posadas sobre él.'","'He aplastado a un buen número de esas moscas guadaña y he visto sus entrañas.\
\
'Me parece que, con la preparación adecuada, se podría preparar un sabroso pudín con lo que tienen dentro. Si te encuentras en el pantano y te ves rodeado por estas criaturas, ¿recogerías sus mollejas?\
\
'Creo que con ellas prepararé un buen pudín.'","Vísceras de mosca guadaña recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2402]={"'No tengo ninguna duda de que las setas que hay en las ruinas al oeste estarán deliciosas.\
\
'Tienen todas las características de un plato sabroso, pero hay que recolectarlas. Aric ha dejado claro que cree que me meteré en problemas si voy allí, pero me ha dicho que ofrecer estas brillantes gemas podría ayudarme a encontrar ayuda.\
\
'Todo lo que quiero son diez setas de las ruinas del oeste para poder preparar un plato maravilloso al que llamaré puré de setas empapado. ¿Estarías dispuesto a ayudarme?'","'¿Tienes mis setas? Estoy seguro de que están deliciosas. Ojalá crecieran en lugares donde no vagaran los muertos.'","Setas empapadas recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las setas empapadas se pueden encontrar en las ruinas al oeste de Ost Haer. Glaednoth se encuentra en las ruinas de Ost Haer, en la zona sur de Harloeg.\
\
Glaednoth te ha pedido que busques setas empapadas para intentar preparar un plato interesante con ellas.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son misiones repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión se puede completar tres veces.</rgb>","Recolecta setas empapadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Qué es ese hedor? ¿Eres tú? ¿No? ¿Son las setas?\
\
'Oh, Dios mío, bueno, esto va a necesitar muchas especias para disimularlo, pero ¿quién dice que eso va a hacer que la comida sea menos sabrosa?\
\
'Gracias por esto.'","Recompensa: Puré de champiñones empapado","Un miembro emprendedor y quizás delirante de los Eglain planea crear platos de comida extraños para ayudar a solucionar la escasez a la que se enfrentan los Eglain casi con regularidad.","Lleva las setas a Glaednoth"},
[2403]={"'I am glad to hear that you have brought an end to Strákhal, ${CLASS}.\
\
'He was a dangerous threat to our people. Please accept this as a reward.'","Defeat Strákhal the Strangler","You have defeated Strákhal and collected a trophy as proof","Return to Sálunath with proof of Strákhal's demise","You defeated Strákhal the Strangler and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'A vicious and deadly Orc named Strákhal, known as The Strangler to locals, has been spotted in Fushaum Sûlm to the south-west. We can not allow these Orcs to prey on our people.\
\
'Bring proof to Sálunath in Sul Madásh if you complete this request.'","Bounty: Strákhal the Strangler","A bounty notice asks you to defeat a vicious Orc named Strákhal in Fushaum Sûlm in southern Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof."},
[2404]={"Bring Suginzi's great tusk to Numûru in Urmâkh","The great plague boar Suginzi is spreading disease and mayhem throughout Imhûlar. You are to defeat him and return to Numûru with his great tusk.","Bounty: Suginzi","'You defeated Suginzi? That is quite the feat, you must be quite the fighter. He has eluded us for years. You have my gratitude. Citizens of Urmâkh no longer have to fear travelling south and being gored by those great tusks. Here, this should be a suitable reward for such a feat.'","Mizâdi Shâra, Queen of Renewed Hamât, has posted a bounty seeking skilled hunters to find and defeat the great plague boar, Suginzi. You are to defeat him and return to her Hand, Numûru, with one of his great tusks. He was last seen south-west of Urmâkh, near Shakhdag.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
On behalf of the Queen of Renewed Hamât, Mizâdi Shâra, you are empowered to seek out and defeat the great plague boar Suginzi. Suginzi has spread disease and mayhem throughout Imhûlar, and his reign of fear must end.\
\
The proof of his death shall be one of his great tusks, hewn from his head. Bring the tusk to Numûru, Hand of the Queen in Urmâkh for a fitting reward.","Bring Suginzi's great tusk to Numûru in Urmâkh to collect your reward.","Defeat Suginzi and collect one of his great tusks"},
[2405]={"'Well done, ${PLAYER}! This trophy will be a lively addition to my ever-growing collection.'","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I hear you are quite the foe-hunter in these parts. Perhaps we can work together, eh?\
\
'I am a collector of odds and ends -- trophies of the enemy. I believe that someday they will be of great historical value, you see.\
\
'A Warg-rider named Sulmus, a vicious hunter, has evidently been seen riding around the Fallows of late, slaughtering beasts and men wherever he goes. Will you bring me his saddle? I'll see that you are amply rewarded.'","Britric is in Forlaw.\
\
You have collected the saddle of Sulmus, and should now return to Forlaw to collect your bounty.","Defeat Sulmus and collect his saddle","Sulmus can be found in the Fallows by taking the road directly south, and then searching for eaten prey south of the first split in the road.\
\
You should summon and defeat Sulmus, and collect his saddle.","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","Sulmus has been seen riding through the Fallows, and it is believed that his saddle will be a valuable part of a collection of bounties.","Collected the saddle of Sulmus","Bounty: Sulmus","Bring the saddle to Britric"},
[2406]={"Bounty: Sóthadar the Trickster","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'There is a bog-lurker known as Sóthadar who has been known to roam in Lhámuth to the north-west. This beast is especially cunning and has earned the title of the trickster as it hides itself well to attack any travelling through its waters. Slay this beast to make the marsh safer for the scouts.\
\
'Bring proof to Sálunath in Sul Madásh if you complete this request.'","You have defeated Sóthadar and collected a trophy as proof","You defeated Sóthadar the Trickster and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.","Defeat Sóthadar the Trickster","A bounty notice asks you to defeat a cunning bog-lurker known as Sóthadar who roams Lhámuth in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.","'We are all safer for the end of Sóthadar in Lhámuth.\
\
'They were a tricky beast and a danger to many. Take this as payment.'","Return to Sálunath with proof of Sóthadar's demise"},
[2407]={"The dread scorpion Tamâhu is harassing citizens and growing her brood west of Urmâkh. You are to defeat her and return to Numûru in Urmâkh with her mighty stinger.","'That is quite the stinger. I wouldn't want to tangle with the beast to whom it was attached. Clearly you know your way around a fight. Please know that the people of Urmâkh will sleep easier tonight because of your valourous deeds. Please accept this reward, you've more than earned it.'","Bring Tamâhu's stinger to Numûru in Urmâkh","Bring Tamâhu's stinger to Numûru in Urmâkh to collect your reward.","Mizâdi Shâra, Queen of Renewed Hamât, has posted a bounty seeking skilled hunters to defeat the dread scorpion Tamâhu and return with her mighty stinger. She has last been seen west of Urmâkh, near Dûlagig.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
On behalf of the Queen of Renewed Hamât, Mizâdi Shâra, brave citizens amongst you are asked to seek out and defeat the dread scorpion Tamâhu. Tamâhu has long plagued the lands west of Urmâkh, endangering all the peoples of Imhûlar. Defeat her before her brood spreads and more harm comes to innocent citizens of Urmâkh.\
\
The proof of your triumph shall be her oversized stinger. Bring the twisted weapon to Numûru, Hand of the Queen in Urmâkh for a proper reward.","Bounty: Tamâhu","Defeat Tamâhu and collect her mighty stinger"},
[2408]={"¡Tansy Piesdeliebre ha sido derrotada!","Tansy Piesdeliebre se encuentra en Guardasur, en el Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías invocar y enfrentarte a Tansy Piesdeliebre.","Recompensa: Tansy Piesdeliebre","El cartel de recompensa dice:\
\
'Ella estaba en lo alto de la colina, y supe que me observaba desde lejos. Tansy Piesdeliebre, la asesina implacable, me vigilaba. Tuve suerte, pues aquel día no era yo su objetivo. ¿Cuánto tiempo más tendremos que vivir con miedo mientras recolectamos los recursos del Bosque Salvaje?\
\
'Ofrezco una recompensa a quien consiga librar a estos bosques de Tansy Piesdeliebre. ¡No quiero volver a ver a esa bandida en las alturas del Bosque Salvaje jamás!'","'¿Quieres meterme entre rejas? ¡Buena suerte!'","Completado","Has derrotado a Tansy Piesdeliebre y has ayudado a los Pueblos Libres del Bosque Salvaje.","La bandida se enfrenta a ti","Invoca y enfréntate a Tansy Piesdeliebre","Un cartel de recompensa te pide que encuentres a Tansy Piesdeliebre, una peligrosa bandida del Bosque Salvaje.","Tansy Piesdeliebre derrotada"},
[2409]={"'Ah, ${PLAYER}. I must admit, I did not expect to hear from you on this task.\
\
'The others have been after Tarlang's Fang for some time now, and all they have returned with are injuries. He is very elusive quarry despite his old age, let me assure you.\
\
'He was last spotted in the mountainous hills to the south of the Hill of Erech, but I doubt he has remained there. Good luck to you, traveller!'","Defeat Tarlang's Fang","Calennen can be found in central Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have found a bounty posted for Tarlang's Fang and should now seek Calennen for more information.","The hunters of Alagrant have posted a bounty in hopes of finally defeating the elusive mountain-lion known as Tarlang's Fang.","Defeated Tarlang's Fang","Calennen can be found in central Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have slain the fierce mountain-lion known as Tarlang's Fang and should now report your success to Calennen.","Tarlang's Fang can be found somewhere in the hills to the south of the Hill of Erech.\
\
Calennen has given you all the information he has about the whereabouts of the fierce mountain-lion. You should now track and slay Tarlang's Fang.","DNT -- will not be seen","The posted note advertises a bounty on a mountain-lion of Blackroot Vale known as Tarlang's Fang, described as 'a mountain-lion of considerable size and power who has a penchant for playing with his meals,' and invites all interested hunters to seek out Calennen in Alagrant for more information on the beast's whereabouts.","Talk to Calennen","Bounty: Tarlang's Fang","'I am stunned that he lurked there still, ${PLAYER}. He was far more elusive in the past... I wonder what changed.\
\
'Perhaps he wanted to end his long reign with one last brutal fight... we may never be able to say.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Let none doubt you as a true hunter in Gondor.'"},
[2410]={"You have defeated Thagára and collected a trophy as proof","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'A crocodile called Thagára who roams the Lair of the Shadlúgai to the west has been a threat to travellers for too long. We ask that someone put an end to this terror.\
\
'Bring proof to Sálunath in Sul Madásh if you complete this request.'","Bounty: Thagára","'The marsh is safer with Thagára's defeat.\
\
'Thank you, ${CLASS}, the chieftain's reward is yours.'","Return to Sálunath with proof of Thagára's demise","You defeated Thagára and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.","Defeat Thagára","A bounty notice asks you to defeat a deadly crocodile named Thagára, who roams the Lair of the Shadlúgai in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof."},
[2411]={"Derrota a Thauk en Tûm Fuin","'¡Has ayudado enormemente a quienes vivimos en Tyrn Fornech, ${PLAYER}!'","'Tu servicio a Ost Forod nunca será olvidado.'","'Buena suerte con Thauk. Es un monstruo cruel y no será fácil reclamar su recompensa.\
\
'Búscalo en el campamento de trasgos de Tûm Fuin, al norte de Ost Forod.'","'Basilio Resinas, nuestro juez, está aquí en Ost Forod. Habla con él sobre el asunto de tu recompensa.\
\
'Aún no puedo creer que hayas logrado derrotar al vil Thauk. ¡Qué valentía, ${PLAYER}!","'¡No puedo creer que hayas derrotado al malvado Thauk! ¡Increíble!'","'¿Has venido a preguntar por Thauk? ¡Es una criatura terrible, sedienta de sangre y peligrosa! Se dice que está aliado con los trasgos que merodean por las colinas de Tyrn Fornech. Si logras derrotarlo, puede que eso también los afecte a ellos.\
\
'Busca a Thauk dentro del tosco campamento de trasgos en Tûm Fuin, al norte de Ost Forod. Probablemente ronda por todo el campamento, vigilando a los trasgos e incitándolos a causar más problemas.\
\
'Thauk es una bestia enorme y peligrosa. ¡Necesitarás estar muy alerta si esperas reclamar su recompensa!'","El huargo Thauk está en el campamento de trasgos de Tûm Fuin, al norte de Ost Forod.\
\
Has aceptado la comisión de la recompensa por Thauk.","Habla con Basilio Resinas en Ost Forod","Se ha ofrecido una recompensa por Thauk, un huargo cruel aliado con los trasgos que merodean por Tyrn Fornech.","Rowena Guardacotos está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Un cartel que ofrece una recompensa por la captura o derrota de un huargo cruel llamado Thauk llamó tu atención. Si deseas solicitar esta recompensa, debes hablar con Rowena Guardacotos.","'¿Has regresado de Tûm Fuin? ¿Significa eso que derrotaste a Thauk?\
\
'¡Asombroso, ${PLAYER}! Si hablas con Basilio Resinas, el juez aquí en Ost Forod, él te dará tu recompensa.\
\
'¿Thauk no volverá a molestarnos? ¡No puedo creerlo!'","'¿Derrotaste a Thauk? Entonces mereces esta recompensa, ${PLAYER}. Esa recompensa llevaba mucho tiempo sin reclamar. ¡Te doy las gracias en nombre de la gente respetuosa de las leyes de Ost Forod!'","El cartel anuncia una recompensa por un huargo cruel llamado Thauk, descrito como una 'criatura sedienta de sangre conocida por estar aliada con los trasgos que acechan Tyrn Fornech', e invita a quienes estén interesados a buscar a Rowena Guardacotos en Ost Forod para conocer los detalles y postularse para la comisión.","Thauk derrotado en Tûm Fuin","Recompensa: Thauk, el Vil Huargo","'Derrotar a Thauk no fue algo menor, ${PLAYER}. Era verdaderamente cruel.'","Habla con Rowena Guardacotos en Ost Forod","Rowena Guardacotos está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Has derrotado al huargo Thauk y ahora debes informar a Rowena Guardacotos.","Basilio Resinas está en Ost Forod, el antiguo puesto de vigilancia en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.\
\
Has derrotado a Thauk y ahora debes informar a Basilio Resinas para recibir tu recompensa."},
[2413]={"Los jabalíes pueden encontrarse en los campos más septentrionales de Bree.\
\
Sage Semilleno te pidió que cazaras jabalíes para obtener sus colmillos y se los entregaras en el campamento cerca de los lagos en los campos del norte de Bree.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión puede completarse tres veces.</rgb>","Colmillos perfectos de jabalí recolectados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recompensa: El rizo perfecto","'¡Estos son perfectos!\
\
'Te debo mucho, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Por favor, toma esto y sabe que me has ayudado enormemente.'","Recolecta colmillos perfectos de jabalí (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Entrega los colmillos a Sage Semilleno","'Vine al norte para encontrar colmillos, un objeto muy apreciado por los cazadores de Bree. Los colmillos que busco se colocan junto a astas en los establecimientos para colgar capas y abrigos. Me han encargado recolectar una buena cantidad de ellos, pero el número de orcos en la zona, francamente, me hace dudar en alejarme demasiado de nuestro campamento.\
\
'Pareces un poco más resistente que yo, y estoy dispuesto a pagarte por recolectar los colmillos que necesito. ¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a ayudarme?'","Sage Semilleno te pidió que recolectaras colmillos perfectos de jabalíes en los campos del norte de Bree para ayudarla con los pedidos que debe cumplir.","'Encontrarás jabalíes por todas estas tierras. Cázalos para obtener sus colmillos y vuelve a mí cuando tengas varios.'"},
[2418]={"You should follow the white stag as it flees in eastern Blackroot Vale.\
\
The white stag has fled from your approach, but if you give chase, it is possible you might still catch it.","Pursue and capture the white stag","The hunters of Alagrant have posted a bounty in hopes of capturing a rare white stag that has appeared in the vale.","Dírion can be found in Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have found a posted bounty for a white stag in Blackroot Vale, and should now speak to Dírion for more information.","'So, you seek to capture the white stag? A noble goal to be certain, but one that countless others have failed to achieve.\
\
'You see, nature has not brought forth such a wondrous symbol of Gondor since the White Tree, and I can think of no better symbol to hearten the people of the vale. I would never ask you to harm such a beautiful beast, but perhaps you can capture it for the people of Morlad.\
\
'I have heard such varying accounts of its whereabouts, but it was last seen far to the east and beyond the Stone. Good fortune and swift strides, ${PLAYER}... you shall need both!'","Bounty: The White Stag","The posted note advertises a bounty on a particularly elusive white stag, described as 'a powerful and brilliantly white stag whose speed is unmatched by any in the vale,' and invites all interested hunters to seek out Dírion in Alagrant for more information on the stag's last known whereabouts.","The white stag flees at your approach, but you should pursue it","Talk to Dírion","Search for the white stag in Blackroot Vale","DNT -- will not be seen","Dírion can be found in Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale.\
\
You were unable to capture the stag due to its agility, but should report back to Dírion in Alagrant.","Before you can get any closer, the stag gathers its strength and sprints away","The white stag was last seen somewhere in eastern Blackroot Vale.\
\
Dírion offered you some advice on where to track the white stag, and you should now seek it out.","'It got away, didn't it?\
\
'I assumed as much, ${PLAYER}, for none have been able to keep pace with it yet. Still, the fact that you have seen one in the vale heartens me.\
\
'Do not fret, I shall track it myself now that I know its whereabouts.'"},
[2419]={"¡Thunash ha sido derrotado!","Invoca y enfréntate a Thunash","Recompensa: Thunash","Completado","Un aviso de recompensa pide que busques a Thunash, un cruel semiorco del Bosque Salvaje","El aviso de recompensa dice:\
\
'¿Has oído hablar del emisario de Zarquino, que recorre el Bosque Salvaje como si fuera el dueño del lugar? Me opongo a ello: ¡no si podemos hacer algo al respecto!\
\
'Thunash, el semiorco, cree que el Bosque Salvaje le pertenece para arrasarlo y conquistarlo. Se ofrece una recompensa a quien consiga acabar con este vil semiorco.'","Thunash se encuentra en Cotfast, en el Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías invocar a Thunash y enfrentarte a él.","Has derrotado a Thunash y has ayudado a los Pueblos Libres del Bosque Salvaje.","'Zarquino se enterará de esto. ¡Recuerda lo que digo!'","El semiorco se enfrenta a ti","Has derrotado a Thunash"},
[2421]={"Bounty: Tukûrga","A bounty notice asks you to defeat a vicious kergrim known as Tukûrga in Tûkurdul, to the north-west near Ashâgir.","'So Tukûrga will no longer be a terror to these lands.\
\
'Take this as a sign of my thanks, ${CLASS}.'","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'Tukûrga is a vicious and dangerous kergrim who can be found in Tûkurdul to the north-west of here. This monster must be stopped.\
\
'Neshurga in Ub Nishir will reward you if you slay Tukûrga.'","A bounty notice in Ub Nishir has asked for someone to defeat the kergrim Tukûrga in Tûkurdul to the north-west, near Ashâgir.","Return to Neshurga and inform him of Tukûrga's defeat","Defeat Tukûrga","Defeated Tukûrga","Return to Neshurga in Ub Nishir north of Maurûsh and inform him that you have completed the bounty and defeated Tukûrga."},
[2422]={"Recompensa: Caparazones de tortuga","'Saludos, ${PLAYERNAME:viajero[m]|viajera[f]}. Parece que te has alejado mucho de la seguridad de Bree, lo que significa que probablemente seas como mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} y yo: espíritus aventureros. Estaríamos fuera y en movimiento si no fuera por esos orcos al oeste. Tal como están las cosas, la seguridad de nuestro campamento parece más importante que el dinero que podríamos ganar cumpliendo nuestras recompensas.\
\
'Por supuesto, si estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a ayudarnos, tenemos algunos materiales que con gusto te daríamos si quieres echarnos una mano.\
\
'Estoy buscando caparazones de tortuga para proveer a los herreros de Bree, que a menudo los usan para crear moldes con los que fabricar sus escudos. Puedes encontrar tortugas por toda la zona del lago aquí, en el norte de Bree.'","Lleva los caparazones a Walt Rosablanca","'Las tortugas pueden ser un enemigo peligroso si no tienes cuidado. Búscalas, pero cuida tus dedos.'","Caparazones gruesos de tortuga recolectados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las tortugas pueden encontrarse alrededor de los lagos y otros cuerpos de agua en los campos del norte de Bree.\
\
Walt Rosablanca quiere que recolectes caparazones de tortuga y se los entregues detrás de las piedras, cerca de las cascadas donde la garganta se une a los lagos.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión puede completarse tres veces.</rgb>","Walt Rosablanca está recolectando caparazones de tortuga para entregarlos a los herreros de Bree. Los caparazones pueden usarse como buenos moldes para crear escudos.","'Estos servirán perfectamente. Ahora dime, ¿cuál de estas recompensas te gustaría reclamar por tus esfuerzos?'","Recolecta caparazones gruesos de tortuga (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2423]={"A wanted poster for the defeat of one 'Têzdab the Butcher'.","Wanted: Têzdab 'the Butcher'\
\
For the slaying of innocents in An Shêru. Experienced bounty hunters only!\
Last seen in the vicinity of Khanâg Gur, he is ill-tempered and should be approached with caution.","Defeat Têzdab the Butcher","'Têzdab has finally been defeated, has he? A remarkable feat! Well done. Here is your reward.'","Têzdab the Butcher defeated","Têzdab the Butcher is reported as having been last seen in the vicinity of Khanâg Gur in An Shêru.","Talk to Halshûm in Khanâg Gur","You have defeated Têzdab the Butcher. You should return to Khanâg Gur to collect your reward.","Bounty: Têzdab the Butcher"},
[2424]={"'The traders will be relieved to hear of Uzukar's defeat.\
\
'You have their thanks and mine as well. The reward they provided is yours to claim.'","A bounty notice asks you to defeat Uzukar, a ferocious jackal that has been spotted roaming near Urgudag to the west.","Defeat Uzukar","Return to Neshurga in Ub Nishir north of Maurûsh and inform him that you have completed the bounty and defeated Uzukar.","Return to Neshurga and inform him of Uzukar's defeat","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'A ferocious jackal called Uzukar has been spotted near Urgudag to the west. Traders in the area are in need of someone to get rid of this beast.\
\
'Inform Neshurga in Ub Nishir if you complete this request.'","Defeated Uzukar","A bounty notice in Ub Nishir has asked for someone to defeat a ferocious jackal known as Uzukar who has been spotted near Urgudag to the west.","Bounty: Uzukar"},
[2425]={"'Well done, ${PLAYER}! This trophy will be a lively addition to my ever-growing collection.'","Bring the helm to Britric","Vîz can be found camping near a fang-shaped rock in the Fallows, which can be found by following the road south a ways.\
\
You should summon and defeat Vîz, and collect his helm.","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Wildermore's Recovery will cancel this quest.</rgb>","Bounty: Vîz","Collected the helm of Vîz","Defeat Vîz and collect his helm","'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I hear you are quite the foe-hunter in these parts. Perhaps we can work together, eh?\
\
'I am a collector of odds and ends -- trophies of the enemy. I believe that someday they will be of great historical value, you see.\
\
'An Orc named Vîz, a vicious warrior, has evidently been camping out near a fang-shaped rock in the Fallows. Will you bring me his helm? I'll see that you are amply rewarded.'","Britric is in Forlaw.\
\
You have collected the helm of Vîz, and should now return to Forlaw to collect your bounty.","Vîz has been seen at a fang-shaped rock in the Fallows, and it is believed that his helm will be a valuable part of a collection of bounties."},
[2428]={"Defeat pack wargs in Rath Dúath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat pack leaders in Rath Dúath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You reminded the warg packs that threaten folk travelling through Rath Dúath that theirs is not the only strength in the valley.","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'Where once there was a single large warg pack prowling the forests near Rath Dúath, something has changed, and several wargs have broken off to lead their own, smaller packs. These are unafraid to challenge folk on the road, and they can cover a greater distance than before.\
\
'Hunt these packs and teach them we will not run from them. We will fight!'","Warg packs can be found in Rath Dúath.\
\
You should defeat pack leaders and pack wargs.","Completado","Defeated warg packs.","Defeated pack wargs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bounty: Wargs in Rath Dúath","A bounty notice asks you to hunt wargs across Rath Dúath.","Defeated pack leaders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2431]={"Lleva las calaveras a Edith Rosadulce","'Tengo una pequeña colección de materiales que estoy dispuesto a cambiar por las calaveras de los tumularios. Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a recolectarlas, yo estoy dispuesto a darte esta recompensa.'","Calaveras de tumulario recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Sí, esto demuestra muchas victorias. Has hecho un gran servicio a la gente de las Tierras de Bree hoy.'","'No es habitual que estemos en una posición como esta. Hemos venido antes sin peligro alguno, salvo las ratas, los gusanos o algún que otro barghest. Esto, sin embargo, es muy extraño.\
\
'Estoy seguro de que la gente de las Tierras de Bree puede beneficiarse de la eliminación de estos enemigos aterradores, estos tumularios, así que te ofreceré una recompensa por su derrota.\
\
'Derrota a los muertos vivientes aquí y tráeme sus calaveras. Te recompensaré bien por estos esfuerzos.'","Los tumularios pueden encontrarse por todas las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Sur.\
\
La guía, Edith Rosadulce, valora las calaveras de tumulario y te pagará por ellas. Está acampada en el Alto del Hombre Muerto, donde las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Norte se encuentran con las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Sur.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Las misiones de recompensa son repetibles, pero tienen un número limitado de completaciones. Esta misión puede completarse tres veces.</rgb>","Recolecta calaveras de tumulario (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hay una recompensa por las calaveras de los tumularios que vagan por las Quebradas de los Túmulos del Sur.","Recompensa: Calaveras de tumulario"},
[2432]={"You have defeated many wights in Emyn Duir, and the one who posted the bounty is certain to be pleased.","Se pueden encontrar espectros en Emyn Duir.\
\
Deberías derrotar a los espectros.","Derrota a los espectros en Emyn Duir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bounty: Wights in Emyn Duir","A bounty notice has asked you to drive the wights out of Emyn Duir.","You defeated wights.","Completado","Derrota a los tumularios (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Estandartes espectrales derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat banner-wights in Emyn Duir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The bounty notice reads:\
\
'These lands have no shortage of foul creatures, but if you ask me the wight is the worst, bedraggled and disgusting. They are beasts of horror, and I hesitate to call them something so common as pests, but they harass our gravesites and bother our dead. It turns my stomach to think of them!\
\
'If you wish to earn some coin and have the time to spare, I implore you to hunt as many of the vile creatures as you can. I am sick of the things!'"},
[2434]={"The bounty notice reads: \
\
'Rangers, we are in need of one of you to defeat Yambahul, a vile Haradrim chieftain. Speak with Anborn if you plan to accept this mission.'","Speak with Anborn","'You continue to impress me with your skills. Yambahul's defeat will boost my mens' spirits in these difficult days. Good work.'","Defeat Yambahul","Defeated Yambahul","A bounty notice asks you to seek out Anborn who has information about Yambahul, a vile Haradrim chieftain.","Anborn can be found in the keep at Bâr Húrin.\
\
You should speak with Anborn.","You ask Anborn about the bounty notice.\
\
'You wish to help our cause? Very well. I do not speak ill of your abilities as a warrior, but do take note, Yambahul is no ordinary foe. He is a high ranking chieftain and commands vast numbers. It will not be an easy fight.'","Yambahul can be found somewhere in Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should defeat Yambahul.","Bounty: Yambahul"},
[2436]={"Gárnoth's Farm was known for the quality of cattle and meat once produced there, but these days there are not many domesticated cows left in the Fallows. Most of those cows are still on the farm, and should not be left to become food for the Orcs.","The Orcs occupying Gárnoth's Farm have managed to keep many cows corralled. They seem to be using them as a local food source instead of relying on shipments from elsewhere.","Free cows in Gárnoth's Farm (0/9)","The cows are free and those that know the paths will be making their way back to Forlaw. Some may wander the plains and will hopefully join the wild herds in the Fallows.","Gárnoth's Farm has a few cows left behind from when the farm was abandoned. Their masters frequently took them to Forlaw's market and would know the paths to get there. If the cows are freed, they should make their way to the city, or may end up wandering the plains, but that would be better than leaving them to an unpleasant fate.","Cow freed (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Free cows in Gárnoth's Farm (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Completado","The Orcs can no longer rely on the local food source, and will once again have to rely on shipments from elsewhere.","The cows left behind at Gárnoth's Farm are grazing in pens throughout the farm.","Bovine Breakout"},
[2438]={"¡Has completado muchas entregas de carpinteros de Umbar!","Completa las cuotas diarias para el Gremio de carpinteros de Umbar.","Pedidos diarios del Gremio de carpinteros de Umbar completados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Los carpinteros proveen a las masas de Umbar Baharbêl, y tú estás haciendo tu parte para ayudar.","Completa las solicitudes del Gremio de carpinteros de Umbar.\
\
Puedes adquirir estas misiones del líder del Gremio de carpinteros de Umbar en la sala del gremio de artesanos de Umbar Baharbêl.","Has completado muchas peticiones de carpinteros de Umbar.","Arcos para Umbar (Semanal)","Completa los pedidos diarios del Gremio de carpinteros de Umbar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2439]={"A camp-fire near Utlac is just the place to burn the Orc-bows you have taken.\
\
Utlac cannot bear to handle the Orc-bows any longer and has asked you to burn them in a nearby camp-fire.","Talk to Utlac","'Give me three good archers from Snowbourn, and I could keep a dozen Orcs at bay, even in poor light or foul weather. The bows of my people are well-made, but it is the strength of a Rohirrim archer's arm and the sharpness of his eye that truly makes him dangerous.\
\
'Orcs are different. Their bows are crudely-fashioned, and they seek to make up for their poor training with numbers only. Still, an arrow fired poorly from hiding can pierce even the bravest man, on occasion.\
\
'Defeat archers throughout the East Wall, ${PLAYER}, and bring me their bows for breaking. I do not want a stray arrow to fell even a single man more.'","Orc and Uruk-archers can be found throughout the East Wall.\
\
Utlac has asked you to defeat Orcs or Uruks throughout the East Wall and to take their bows so he can destroy them.","Utlac is at the Rohirrim-encampment, waiting to speak with you.","Bows of Foul Craft","Throw the Orc-bows on the camp-fire near Utlac","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'The miserable Orcs that sneak throughout the East Wall use their bows to attack the men of this company. Defeat the Orcs, seize their bows, and bring them back to me!'","'I gave you back the bows, ${PLAYER}. Throw them in the camp-fire over there so I do not need to see them any longer. The thought that one of my friends could be slain by a stray arrow fired from one of those crude devices has turned my stomach.'","Utlac is at the Rohirrim-camp in the East Wall.\
\
You have recovered many crude bows from the Orcs that inhabit the East Wall and should bring them to Utlac so he can destroy them.","Collect bows from Orcs or Uruks in the East Wall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected bows from Orcs or Uruks in the East Wall (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Can you smell that? Even the smoke of the burning smells foul. Thank you for helping destroy those crude bows, ${PLAYER}. Every blow to the Orcs helps our chances of surviving here in the East Wall.'","Bring Orc-bows to Utlac","Utlac says the greatest danger faced by the Rohirrim who have come to the East Wall is the threat posed by Orc-archers lurking among the trees.","'Look at these things, ${PLAYER}. I knew the Orcs cared little for the craft of bow-making, but I did not expect them to be this crude. It is a wonder these bows do not fall apart in their filthy hands.\
\
'Still, an arrow fired from one of these can still kill. We had best not forget that.\
\
'I cannot bear to handle these bows any longer, ${PLAYER}. Take them and throw them in the fire over there. The Orcs will loose no more arrows at the Rohirrim from these crude things. Oh, and one more thing! Do not burn these bows in any of the cookfires. That would simply be offensive. Make sure the fire you choose is not being used to cook someone's meal.'"},
[2441]={"Bring the supplies to Léofhelm","In Fastred's absence, Snowbourn must be provisioned and supplied for the coming war.","'You have my thanks.\
\
'Through your efforts, we did not have to spread ourselves as thin upon the fields.'","Collect leather-scraps in Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect piles of logs outside Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected spears in Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If you wish to aid us while you wait for Fastred's return, I have a task for you.\
\
'The Riders have been facing more opposition in the fields as of late, and we constantly need more materials for repairs to the farmsteads, as well as new arms and armour for the Riders themselves.\
\
'If you would, gather wood, spears, and leather scraps for me, and I will send them along to the appropriate craftsfolk.'","Collect spears in Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Piles of logs can be found near felled trees outside the walls, while spears and leather can be gathered within the city.\
\
Léofhelm has asked you to gather the materials needed to supply Snowbourn.","Bracing for Battle","Collected piles of logs outside Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Léofhelm can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.\
\
You should return to Léofhelm and let him know that you have done as he asked.","Collected leather-scraps in Snowbourn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2442]={"The ruins of the armoury can be found in south-western Osgiliath.\
\
Meldir has asked you to recover hidden stores of weapons from the ruins of the armoury.","'Ah, yes, these will do nicely.\
\
'With so many foes surrounding us, we will need a large supply of blades - for even the strongest sword shall eventually wear.\
\
'You have my thanks.'","Collected barrels of weapons at the ruined armoury (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bracing for Defeat","Deliver the weapons to Meldir","Collect barrels of weapons at the ruined armoury (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Meldir can be found along the south-western walls of Osgiliath.\
\
You have recovered many weapons, and should now deliver them to Meldir.","Determined to bolster the Rangers' defences, Meldir has travelled to the ancient armoury of Osgiliath to seize what remains before it falls into the hands of the Enemy.","'I am in a dire position, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The armoury suffered greatly in the assault on the western half of the city, and now only its walls stand as a reminder that it was ever here. When we still held the western shore, we stored a great deal of weapons within the armoury. Yet now, the Orcs and trolls roam its ruins and our weapon-stores are exposed.\
\
'I have not been able to get close enough to gather many, but perhaps you can. If you return these weapons to me, I shall be able to hasten my return to the tunnels.'"},
[2443]={"Collected boar belly (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cúronel has asked you to bring her boar belly meat from healthy boars and to put down diseased boars at her farm, Munadhor Farm in Pinnath Gelin.","'You come bearing boar belly? Ah, how wonderful. I would not have been able to gather so much on my own. I will make mother's favourite dish tonight with some of this, and prepare the rest for curing.\
\
'You have my thanks!'","Return to Cúronel","'I like braised boar belly, but mother likes when I prepare it with herbs and wine, and roll it with twine and then bake it until crispy. I admit, I do also enjoy it prepared as such. At least these boars will be useful, especially if we can drive them out before they do too much damage.'","You should return to Cúronel with the boar belly pieces that you gathered.\
\
Cúronel is at Munadhor Farm, in central Pinnath Gelin.","Braised Boar Belly","Collect boar belly (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Put down diseased boars (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Greetings, traveller. I am Cúronel, and I am sorry I can not welcome you fully to our farm. It has sadly been overrun by boars and brigands, and without my husband about to help drive them off, we have had to abandon our home. I have come here with my husband's mother to see if they've moved on, but no, they've made themselves quite at home... at our home.\
\
'If you are going on ahead, will you bring me back cuts of boar meat? The fatty belly meat, in particular. I can prepare it so that it will last a good long time, and help see us through this. But take care, some of the boars seem to be ailing and their meat would be foetid. Just put those ones down, but bring boar belly from the others.'","Boar belly is a fatty cut of meat which, when cured with spices and herbs, is added to many popular dishes in Pinnath Gelin."},
[2444]={"'Almost all of our kind are here now. Hom. At least of those that remain....\
\
'One slain by Orcs, one corrupt beyond saving... hoom. This bodes ill for us, ${PLAYER}. The last of us is still nowhere to be found.\
\
'Hom. If I remember, he was wont to take root on the hills above the eaves far to the south-west. You should begin your search there, little one.'","Barallas wants you to seek out Mossbeard, far to the south-west of the Orc-roadway, in hopes that all of his kind will be reunited.","Talk to Mossbeard","'Hoom! Barallas? He and the others still walk this wood?\
\
'Hom. I will return in my own time, little one, but there are a great many things to tend to nearby, and much of my own curiosity to be quelled.\
\
'Listen, and perhaps you will understand my plight.'","Mossbeard can be found somewhere past Finglas' Mead far to the south-west of the Stonecliff.\
\
Barallas wants you to search for the last Ent that has not rejoined the others at their hideout.","Branching Out"},
[2445]={"'Have you found my daughter?'","Bravery Beyond Her Years","'With so much ado in Underharrow, my daughter has again slipped out of my sight!\
\
'When will Dúnburg learn? To brazenly seek glory at her age is at best fool-hardy and at worst... I wish not to think of such things! I pray she turns to the mastery of music rather than that of the blade!\
\
'Each time so far, I have had to drag her out of the trees to the south and sit her down within my view. She prattles on endlessly about the Dead, but I tire of such stories, especially since they might drive her into harm's way. If you would, search to the south of town, and please, send her home!'","'Oh, thank goodness Dúnburg is safe!\
\
'She should know better than this! No matter what she may see in Éowyn, a girl of her age does not belong on the battlefield, and I hope she realizes this soon. I know not if the life of a minstrel shall ever befit her, but the path of the shield-maiden is an arduous one, and she has much still to learn.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'","Ellen Fremedon is concerned by her daughter's jaunts into the nearby woods, fearing Dúnburg's enthusiasm for the blade will lead her to trouble.","Ellen Fremedon can be found outside the Mead Hall at Underharrow.\
\
You have rescued Dúnburg and sent her on her way. You should return to Ellen Fremedon.","Talk to Ellen Fremedon","Defended Dúnburg","Dúnburg can be found to the south of Underharrow amidst the trees.\
\
Ellen Fremedon has asked you to find Dúnburg and send her back to Underharrow.","DNT -- Players will not see","Find Dúnburg south of Underharrow","'Did my mother send you?\
\
'I cannot understand why she wishes for me to sit by in Underharrow while our people remain fearful of what lurks in the Harrowdale. I know she won't believe me, but you do, don't you?\
\
'Wait! What is that rustling in the bushes?'"},
[2446]={"Completa 'Artículos de Durabilidad' para Hunward","'Si has de convertirte en ${PLAYERNAME:el Luchador más temido de todos[m]|la Luchadora más temida de todas[f]}, sé que no tendrás dificultad alguna en encontrarlos. Y si no lo haces, entonces quizá no estabas ${PLAYERNAME:destinado[m]|destinada[f]} a destacar entre todos los demás Luchadores de nivel intermedio de estas tierras. Participarás en una pelea de taberna aquí, una refriega en un callejón allá, y te preguntarás qué podría haber sido. Siempre te preguntarás si podrías haber sido más.\
\
'Con mi ayuda, puedes serlo. Piénsalo bien, .'","Lecciones de lucha","Hunward, en el Muelle de los Comerciantes del Bosque Salvaje, ha accedido a forjarte un excelente equipo digno de un Luchador legendario, si le llevas los materiales que necesita.","Hunward estará encantado de instruirte en los aspectos más refinados de la lucha a puño limpio, pero insiste en que necesitarás un equipo mejor si has de liberar todo tu potencial en el arte de golpear.","'Permíteme felicitarte por tus logros, ${PLAYER}, pues realmente has llegado a lo tuyo y tus puños sin duda serán temidos por todos aquellos con quienes luches.\
\
'Le agradeces a Hunward por el excelente equipo que forjó para ti y por sus amables palabras, y le preguntas cómo llegó a estudiar el arte de la lucha a puño limpio. Él ríe.\
\
'¿Esperabas que un Hombre de Rohan prefiriera luchar a lomos de un caballo? Es cierto, la mayoría de los míos lo prefieren, pero yo elegí modelarme según el más legendario de todos los Luchadores. Has oído hablar de Helm Mano de Hierro, por supuesto. ¿Sabes cómo obtuvo ese sobrenombre? Cuando fue insultado por Freca, en cuyas venas corría sangre dunledina, Helm le ordenó que saliera, pues no se permitían peleas en la casa del rey.\
\
'Freca se llenó de temor, y con razón, pues Helm era un hombre grande y fuerte, y ninguno de los hombres de Freca estaba lo bastante cerca como para ayudarlo. Pero vio que Helm no llevaba espada, pues la había dejado dentro del salón, y eso lo tranquilizó. No debería haberlo hecho, porque los puños de Helm eran más mortíferos que cualquier espada. Golpeó a Freca con un solo puñetazo, y esa fue su herida mortal.\
\
'Helm se alza muy por encima de todos, ${PLAYER}, como un Luchador legendario. ¡Hagamos lo que esté a nuestro alcance para demostrarnos dignos de su memoria!'","Hunward se encuentra en el Muelle de los Comerciantes, en el Bosque Salvaje.","Habla con Hunward en el Muelle de los Comerciantes","'Necesitarás un equipo mejor si has de cumplir tu potencial como maestro del refinado arte de golpear cosas, ¡mi ${PLAYERNAME:nuevo amigo[m]|nueva amiga[f]}! Pero presta atención a mi advertencia, pues los materiales que necesitaré para forjarte tales artículos e implementos no serán fáciles de conseguir. Si has de convertirte en ${PLAYERNAME:el Luchador más temido de todos[m]|la Luchadora más temida de todas[f]}, sé que no tendrás dificultad alguna en encontrarlos.\
\
'Y si no lo haces, entonces quizá no estabas ${PLAYERNAME:destinado[m]|destinada[f]} a destacar entre todos los demás Luchadores de nivel intermedio de estas tierras. Participarás en una pelea de taberna aquí, una refriega en un callejón allá, y te preguntarás qué podría haber sido. Siempre te preguntarás si podrías haber sido más.\
\
'Con mi ayuda, puedes serlo. Piénsalo bien, .'","Completa 'Implementos de Golpeo' para Hunward"},
[2447]={"Kamabhosh and his lieutenants can be found in the Cisterns.\
\
You should find and defeat Kamabhosh and his lieutenants.","Defeated Uruk-hai lieutenant (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Kamabhosh","Breach in the Darkness: Kamabhosh","Defeated Kamabhosh","'The Withered Tree has let a raiding party of Orcs into the Cisterns, led by Uruk-hai. I heard them shout orders from within the tunnels and if we don't act, they will reach the city proper. They must be dealt with at once.'","Defeat Uruk-hai lieutenants (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A raiding party has invaded the Cisterns and it is up to you to defeat the enemy captain Kamabhosh and his lieutenants."},
[2449]={"Orcs have invaded the Cisterns and it is up to you to defeat the raiding party.","Breach in the Darkness: The Invaders","Defeated Orc (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Orcs can be found throughout the Cisterns.\
\
You should defeat Orcs in the Cisterns.","'The Withered Tree has let a raiding party of Orcs into the Cisterns. I can hear their evil speech echoing throughout the tunnels and caverns. It won't be long until they've made their way to the surface and start attacking Gondor!'","Derrota orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2450]={"Breach in the Darkness: The Withered Foe","'No, it is you who spouts lies and deceit!'","'You do not understand, do you? This is the end of Gondor!'","Talk to members of the Withered Tree (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Your words have convinced me to depart from these fools down here. I honestly was not sure these people were ever my friends.'","'Hey, you're not one of us!'","The Withered Tree can be found in the Cisterns.\
\
You should try and talk some sense into members of the Withered Tree.","'I see what you mean. I shall leave these misguided men and continue fighting to keep Gondor alive.'","'I was just minding my own business, until you came along and told me what I should be doing!'","Talked to members of the Withered Tree (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'You best get out of here quickly before you get hurt!'","'I can see that those up above have poisoned your mind. There is no stopping the Enemy.'","'Perhaps the followers of the Withered Tree can be redeemed. Though they are wrong in their ways, they are still just men of Gondor. Try to talk to some of them if they are willing. The men of Gondor must band together if we are to win this war.'","The Withered Tree has taken hold of the Cisterns and it is up to you to try and talk some sense into the Gondorians who have lost their way.","'You have no business down here, ${RACE}.'","'Are you done preaching to me? Good, now die!'"},
[2451]={"The Withered Tree can be found in the Cisterns.\
\
You should find and destroy documents belonging to the Withered Tree.","Destroy papers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroyed papers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Withered Tree has taken hold of the Cisterns and it is up to you to destroy their lies.","'I noticed posters blowing through the Cisterns filled with lies from the Withered Tree. You must find their camps in the Cisterns and destroy their fear-mongering papers.'","Breach in the Darkness: Treachery"},
[2452]={"Do not allow the door to the Hornburg to be destroyed","The door to the Hornburg has been destroyed","You have succeeded in defending the door to the Hornburg","Defeat the waves of attackers assailing the gate-house (${VALUE}/6)","A gate-house between the Wall and the Hornburg has been converted into a makeshift ward used to treat wounded soldiers. The final doorway leading to the Hornburg has been sealed, but the enemy seeks to breech the opening while slaughtering the wounded in the gatehouse along the way. This rearmost door must be defended at all costs.","Breaching the Hornburg","The enemy plans to breach the Hornburg through a gate-house being used as a makeshift infirmary for the wounded. The wounded men and the supplies of bandages and medicines are in danger, but the door to the Hornburg must be protected at all costs. The wounded will cry out when they begin to succumb to injuries, but you may instruct them in healing.\
\
Merit Rating\
\
This quest starts with <rgb=#FFFF00>Full</rgb> Merit Rating.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Major Merit Loss:</rgb>\
- Door takes structural damage\
- Wounded Rohirrim is defeated\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Moderate Merit Loss:</rgb>\
- Crate of bandages and supplies destroyed"},
[2453]={"Do not allow the door to the Hornburg to be destroyed","The door to the Hornburg has been destroyed","The enemy plans to breach the Hornburg through a gate-house being used as a makeshift infirmary for the wounded. The wounded men and the supplies of bandages and medicines are in danger, but the door to the Hornburg must be protected at all costs. Heal the men if you are able, and be warned that the goblins mean to destroy the banners upon the wall during their assault.\
\
Merit Rating\
\
This quest starts with <rgb=#FFFF00>Full</rgb> Merit Rating.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Major Merit Loss:</rgb>\
* Door takes structural damage\
* Wounded Rohirrim is defeated\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Moderate Merit Loss:</rgb>\
* Crate of bandages and healing supplies destroyed","You have succeeded in defending the door to the Hornburg","Defeat the waves of attackers assailing the gate-house (${VALUE}/6)","Breaching the Hornburg","The enemy plans to breach the Hornburg through a gate-house being used as a makeshift infirmary for the wounded. The wounded men and the supplies of bandages and medicines are in danger, but the door to the Hornburg must be protected at all costs."},
[2454]={"<rgb=#00FF00>El Cuarto Patio ha sido reclamado</rgb>","Reclama el Primer Patio","Reclama la Puerta del Nigromante","'Has hecho un gran trabajo asegurando la Puerta del Nigromante. Regresa al campamento y discutiremos la siguiente fase del asalto.'","<rgb=#00FF00>La Puerta del Nigromante ha caído. El corazón de Dol Guldur está abierto para el asalto</rgb>","Reclama el Tercer Patio","Reclama el Segundo Patio","El Primer Patio es el primer paso en el camino para tomar la Puerta del Nigromante.","<rgb=#00FF00>El Segundo Patio ha sido reclamado</rgb>","Reclama el Cuarto Patio","Reclama la Ascensión del Hechicero","Forzar la Puerta del Nigromante","El Segundo Patio proporciona un punto de vista sobre toda la Tierra Media debajo. Es crucial tomarlo para que los refuerzos puedan acercarse con seguridad.","<rgb=#00FF00>La Ascensión del Hechicero ha sido reclamada</rgb>","El patio del Tercer Patio protege las entradas a varias cámaras interiores de la fortaleza, la mayoría de los alojamientos de las legiones enemigas.","<rgb=#00FF00>El Primer Patio ha sido reclamado</rgb>","La Puerta del Nigromante marca la entrada al corazón de las fortificaciones exteriores de Dol Guldur. Para asaltar la fortaleza, la puerta debe caer","El Cuarto Patio es un conjunto aparentemente improvisado de tiendas y escombros, pero varios líderes del Enemigo acampan allí para mantenerse cerca de sus tropas.","<rgb=#00FF00>El Tercer Patio ha sido reclamado</rgb>","La Puerta del Nigromante guarda el corazón de las defensas de Dol Guldur. Debe caer para poder sitiar la verdadera fortaleza.","La Ascensión del Hechicero es la última defensa de la Puerta del Nigromante y está bien fortificada en una pendiente empinada."},
[2456]={"'Los exploradores orcos que merodean por todo Caranost llevan arcos con los que han demostrado ser bastante letales. Derrota a estos exploradores y recoge sus arcos. Luego sube a la torre desde la que puedes espiar Sírlond y quema los arcos en el fuego que los orcos construyeron.\
\
'Estaré atento al humo de la quema, y así sabré cuándo los orcos han recibido el mensaje. ¿Qué mensaje? Simplemente este, mi servicial ${PLAYERNAME:mensajero[m]|mensajera[f]}: que sus arqueros no podrán atacarnos desde lejos.'","Habla con Maedhril en Sírlond","Arcos de orcos recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Al poco tiempo, una columna de humo se eleva hacia el cielo; los arcos orcos ya no existen","Maedhril te pidió que derrotes a los exploradores de Caranost y recuperes sus arcos.","La torre que domina el puente de Caranost tiene una gran hoguera en la que Maedhril quería que quemaras los arcos orcos.","Maedhril está en Sírlond, al este de Caranost propiamente dicho.","'Vi el humo, ${PLAYER}. Que eso sea un mensaje para ellos.\
\
'Tienes mi agradecimiento, y el de mi esposo también. Hemos estado aquí durante varios días, pero esta es la primera vez que siento que podemos estar cambiando el rumbo contra los orcos que habitan en Caranost.'","Quema los arcos orcos en la hoguera en lo alto de la torre que domina el puente de Caranost","Maedhril tiene un plan para lidiar con los arqueros orcos, y requiere tanto tu ayuda como un fuego muy grande.","Rompe las flechas, quema los arcos","Recoge los arcos orcos de los exploradores de Caranost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2457]={"Among the buildings in Lhan Gogledh, Trehéarn Brenin has begun to accept offers from unnatural forces in the area.","Destruye los estandartes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Break the Influence","Estandartes destruidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should seek out and destroy any banners that you find in the area."},
[2458]={"Talk to Lhucu at her hut","Lhucu is at her hut, south of Lhan Gogledh.\
\
You should inform Lhucu that the sentries have been scattered.","'With the sentries scattered away from Lhan Gogledh, we have an opportunity to strike into the heart of the encampment and confront my father.'","'Have you defeated the Dievlig sentries?'","Break the Sentries","Defeat sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Among the buildings in Lhan Gogledh, patrolling sentries watch for enemies attempting to enter the encampment.","Lhan Gogledh lies along the path north of Lhucu's hut.\
\
Lhucu has asked you to seek out and defeat the sentries that patrol the outskirts of Lhan Gogledh.","'My father has many sentries that patrol the outskirts of Lhan Gogledh below. These sentries are among his most trusted men, and they have been responsible for the defiling of the cairns.  \
\
'Will you seek out these sentries and drive them away from the encampment?'","Defeated sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2459]={"Alfredo Pradoblanco ha desaparecido, pero entre sus cosas encuentras un diario.","Alfredo Pradoblanco ha desaparecido de su puesto de vigilancia en Men Erain, pero el diario que se encuentra entre sus pertenencias podría contener alguna pista sobre su paradero.\
\
Has encontrado el puesto de vigilancia de Alfredo Pradoblanco, pero no hay rastro del propio Pradoblanco. Su diario podría contener alguna pista sobre su destino.","Debido a su disminución numérica, los Montaraces del Norte deben contratar ocasionalmente a hombres de Ost Forod para vigilar sus antiguas tumbas.","Alfredo Pradoblanco se encuentra en Men Erain, al sur de Tinnudir, al otro lado del lago. Siguiendo el camino costero hacia el noreste, hacia Men Erain, el campamento de Pradoblanco se encuentra en la ladera, subiendo unos escalones de piedra tallada.\
\
El montaraz Helechír te ha pedido que le lleves provisiones a un hombre llamado Alfredo Pradoblanco en Men Erain.","'¡Los saqueadores de tumbas de Evendim pagarán por las vidas que han arrebatado!'","'¿Alfredo Pradoblanco no estaba en su puesto de vigilancia? Eso es muy extraño.\
\
'Por favor, regresa a su campamento y busca alguna pista sobre lo que le ha ocurrido. ¿Quizás dejó su diario? Pradoblanco es un buen amigo y una persona de confianza. Debemos averiguar qué le ha pasado.\
\
'El puesto de vigilancia está al noreste, en Men Erain. Busca los escalones tallados en la ladera a poca distancia de Men Erain y busca en el puesto de vigilancia de Pradoblanco cualquier cosa que pueda ser de ayuda.'","'¿Has encontrado un diario, ${PLAYER}? Déjame leerlo, quizá nos dé alguna pista sobre el destino de Alfredo Pradoblanco.\
\
'¡Es una noticia terrible! Ahora tengo que creer que no solo Pradoblanco, sino también mi pariente Iorthrenar, fueron atacados y asesinados por saqueadores de tumbas. Ambos yacen ahora en tumbas poco profundas.'","Lleva los suministros y el diario de vuelta a Helechír.","Helechír se encuentra en una isla situada al suroeste de Men Erain.\
\
Has encontrado el diario de un montaraz que se encontraba en peregrinación hacia las tierras ancestrales de su familia, cerca de Annúminas. Según su diario, sospechaba que lo estaban siguiendo. Helechír estará muy interesado en saberlo.","Lleva los suministros a Alfredo Pradoblanco","Busca el diario en el campamento de Alfredo Pradoblanco","Desayuno en las ruinas","'Por favor, lleva esos suministros a Alfredo Pradoblanco. Probablemente se le estén acabando las provisiones y las necesitará en breve. Regresa a tierra firme y sigue el camino costero hacia el noreste, hacia Men Erain, hasta que veas los escalones tallados en la ladera que suben hasta el campamento de Pradoblanco.'","'Lamento la muerte de Alfredo Pradoblanco y mi pariente Iorthrenar'","'Espera un momento, quiero hablar contigo. Mi pueblo está muy preocupado por la protección del antiguo patrimonio Dúnedain de Annúminas y las tierras circundantes, pero estamos al límite de nuestras fuerzas. En ocasiones hemos contratado a algunos de los más aventureros de Ost Forod, al noreste, para que nos ayuden a proteger las antiguas mansiones y criptas del saqueo.\
\
Uno de ellos, llamado Alfredo Pradoblanco, vigila algunas de las tumbas de Men Erain. Si no te importa, llévale estos suministros. Regresa a tierra firme y sigue el camino de la costa hacia el noreste, hasta Men Erain. Poco después de llegar a ese lugar, el cementerio de muchos de los antiguos reyes de mi pueblo, verás unos escalones tallados en la ladera. Sube los escalones hasta el campamento de Alfredo Pradoblanco.\
\
'Lleva fuera algún tiempo y seguramente se esté quedando sin provisiones; vuelve a verme cuando le hayas entregado estos suministros y te recompensaré por las molestias.'","Diario recuperado en el campo de Alfredo Pradoblanco","'Debe haber alguna señal de Alfredo Pradoblanco en su puesto de vigilancia en Men Erain. Por favor, busca por la zona si está allí."},
[2460]={"Rompiendo alianzas","Entra en la cueva","'¿Helechal se ha escapado? Eso no es una buena noticia, pero aun así las cosas podrían ser peores. Dado que los Orcos ya no representan una amenaza para las Tierras de Bree, hemos tenido éxito aquí. Ahora nos centraremos en vigilar a Helechal y sus asociaciones.\
\
'¡Bien hecho!'","'Los esfuerzos que has realizado en el sur nos han proporcionado información sobre Bill Helechal, un Hombre de Bree con ideales terribles y egoístas. Helechal estaba trabajando para ayudar a los bandidos leales a Zarquino a unirse a los Orcos Tarkrîp que vienen del norte. Tal alianza estrangularía los recursos de las Tierras de Bree desde ambos lados y significaría la perdición para su gente. Tus esfuerzos aquí en el norte han hecho mucho para ayudarnos a ver que los Orcos son derrotados y su fuerza disminuida.\
\
'El reciente descubrimiento de una cueva construida en la cara del acantilado en Cirith Nûr me lleva a creer que la cueva servirá para un terrible propósito; un lugar para que Helechal se reúna con los líderes orcos y facilite un acuerdo para invadir Bree aún más.\
\
'Parece que ahora has sido elegido para evitar esta invasión y romper esta alianza de una vez por todas. Necesitarás regresar al campamento en Cirith Nûr e ingresar a la caverna para interrumpir la alianza. Debes asegurarte de que los Orcos y los hombres malvados no tengan éxito en sus planes. ¿Estás preparado?'","Has encontrado la cueva","La cueva de la reunión se encuentra en el campamento orco de Cirith Nûr, al noroeste del Viejo Fuerte del Camino Verde.\
\
Andreg te ha encargado que descubras la cueva donde los bandidos y los Orcos preparan sus planes y que mates a sus líderes.","Habla con Andreg en el Viejo Fuerte del Camino Verde","Andreg se encuentra en el Viejo Fuerte del Camino Verde, al sureste de Cirith Nûr.\
\
Informa a Andreg de tu éxito tan pronto como puedas.","'Por ahora tenemos a los bandidos de la zona más o menos controlados. Pero he oído que hay muchos problemas en las Quebradas del Norte. Podrías ir a Puente de Caballetes para investigar.'","Has encontrado la cueva. Ahora solo queda entrar, dispersar a los bandidos y Orcos, y derrotar a sus líderes.","Los Montaraces, que vigilan los movimientos de los enemigos del norte y del sur, están preocupados por la aparición de un enemigo al que han luchado durante mucho tiempo en el norte.","Localiza la cueva"},
[2461]={"Yûl puede encontrarse en el piso más alto de Hurmulkezer en la zona sureste de las Profundidades Llameantes, al sur del Patio de Durin.\
\
Debes encontrar y derrotar a Yûl.","Has derrotado a Yûl, el líder de las fuerzas Ghâsh-hai en Hurmulkezer.\
\
Aunque aún quedan muchos orcos, fracasarán sin un líder.","Los Ghâsh-hai están liderados por el despiadado comandante orco Yûl, y su derrota supondría un duro golpe para la organización de la principal amenaza enemiga en las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
Debes buscar a Yûl y derrotarlo; tal golpe quebraría el espíritu de los orcos.","'¡Los Ghâsh-hai están sumidos en el caos y la confusión!'","Los Ghâsh-hai están liderados por el despiadado comandante orco Yûl, y su derrota supondría un duro golpe para la organización de la principal amenaza enemiga en las Profundidades Llameantes.","Yûl derotado","Completado","Derrota a Yûl","Quebrando su espíritu"},
[2462]={"Lake-town Smugglers and knife-throwers can be found inside the Smugglers' hideout in Lake-town.\
\
You should defeat Lake-town Smugglers and knife-throwers.","Breaking Up the Gang","Talk to Dagrun","The Lake-town Smugglers have been disrupting Dale for far too long and need to be pushed out. Defeat any smugglers found within their hideout.","Defeat Lake-town Smugglers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Lake-town Smugglers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It's time to diminish the Lake-town Smugglers’ numbers so they can no longer conduct their treacherous business. Defeat any smugglers you encounter within their hideout.'","Defeat Lake-town knife-throwers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dagrun can be found in the Council of Wares Headquarters.\
\
You should talk to Dagrun.","'Good work, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps now that the refuse has been swept away, we can keep this town a bit cleaner.'","Defeated Lake-town knife-throwers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2463]={"Defeat Pakon, the Maldorr Orc-chieftain","The entrance to the Boar-tribe lair is south of Beaconwatch, not far from the Mering-Stream.\
\
Cúthing wants you to travel to the Boar-tribe lair and defeat the chieftain.","'The Boar-tribe Orcs were in league with a Nazgûl? It appears that there is more to these Orcs than it first seemed. We must remain vigilant; however, this threat has been quelled for now.\
\
'We cannot thank you enough, ${PLAYER}. We would not have been able to repel the Orcs without you.'","You have arrived at the entrance of the Boar-tribe Orc-lair","Travel to the Boar-tribe Orc-lair","The Boar-tribe chieftain is somewhere within their lair.\
\
If you encounter the chieftain of the Boar-tribe, defeat him.","Breaking the Back of the Boar","Cúthing's plan calls for a single person to sneak into the Boar-tribe Orc-lair and defeat their chieftain.","Cúthing is standing near Meregyth, outside the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch.\
\
You should return to Beaconwatch and tell Cúthing about your victory.","'I wish I could go with you, but my wounds will only prove to be a hindrance. I do not know the Orcs' numbers, but you have demonstrated that you are more than equipped to handle them.\
\
'Head to the south of Beaconwatch, and not far from the Mering-stream, you will find the main entrance to their lair. Once inside, look for the Boar-tribe chieftain and defeat him.'","Talk to Cúthing"},
[2464]={"The prison fortress of Naerband has been rounding up anyone and everyone in an effort to enforce a twisted law over the lands.","Orodir is located next to Naerband.\
\
You should destroy shackles and defeat foes in Orodir.","Destroy shackles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have successfully defeated many foes outside the gates of Naerband and destroyed the shackles used to bind their prisoners.","Defeated foes and destroyed shackles.","Destroyed shackles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Breaking the Chains","Defeat foes at Orodir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Many prisoners are chained to walls in Orodir. We must break the chains and prevent any more from being enslaved.'","Completado","Enemigos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2465]={"Breaking the Cycle","'Some of the Corsairs who have flocked to Abadec's Watch seek safety rather than a cause to continue fighting. If you find any Corsairs who seem hesitant to draw their weapons, please convince them to find me. I promise to help them find peace in Gondor, or a safe voyage home to Umbar.'","Dolvir has asked you to convince war-weary Corsairs to seek him out for help.\
\
You can find weary Corsairs in Abadec's Watch in the south-west corner of Belfalas.","Talk to Dolvir outside Abadec's Watch","Not all of the Corsairs in Abadec's Watch are willing to continue fighting.","'Thank you for helping me convince them, ${PLAYER}. I hope we can put the days of war behind us, for the sake of both of our peoples.'","Convinced weary Corsairs (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Convince weary Corsairs to leave Abadec's Watch (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You have successfully convinced many weary Corsairs to leave Abadec's Watch.\
\
Dolvir waits for you amongst the trees to the north of the camp. You should talk to him."},
[2468]={"Completed Breaking the Ice","Talk to Gwilum at Barnavon or Melvun at the Barnavon Mine","'You know by now that Saruman of Many Colours seeks to sway the clans of Dunland to wage war against the Horse-lords of Rohan. Here in Barnavon, my people -- the People of the Ox -- have pressed the last remnant of the Boar-clan into service in the mine, extracting ore to make weapons and gear for Saruman's allies.\
\
'It is an abuse that Madin Brenin will come to rue, I believe, for it goes against what his grandfather stood for when he granted refuge to the Boar-clan. However, should the mines cease to be worked, it will go poorly for the Turch-lûth -- the Boar-clan. We have received word of troubles there, and the miners are frightened. If something is not done soon, I fear the backs of the Boar-clan will feel the Brenin's wrath.\
\
'The Barnavon Mine is the second place where I asked you to seek for signs of Warg-riders... will you help with this?'","Assist Bervun at the Barnavon Mine","Assist Cada at the Barnavon Mine","Assist Melvun at the Barnavon Mine","Word has come to Barnavon of troubles at the mine.","'You have completed many tasks on behalf of the Turch-lûth, the People of the Boar. There are not many of us alive today, but those of us who are will continue to grow and thrive.\
\
'I know that you fear that the iron we mine will continue to be made into weapons of war for Saruman -- and that is true -- but Gwilum has friends among us who will see that such weapons do not prove their worth.\
\
'Thank you.'","The Barnavon Mine lies far to the east of Barnavon-town, beyond the tower of Hen Turrau.\
\
Gwilum has asked you to lend aid to the miners at the Barnavon Mine so that Madin Brenin will not punish the Boar-clan for the disruption of ore production.","Melvun is at the Barnavon Mine, east of Barnavon. Gwilum is at Barnavon, west of the Barnavon Mine.\
\
You should speak with either Melvun or Gwilum regarding your successes at the Barnavon Mine.","Assist Argel at the Barnavon Mine","Breaking the Ice","'You have proven yourself a friend to the unfortunate, and thus I will consider you a friend as well. Will you continue to aid us?\
\
'Fear not concerning the weapons the ore from the mine will bring into being... the resistance will see to it that not all is as it seems. Concern yourself only with the well-being and good will of the Turch-lûth of Barnavon... they may find they have a stronger will than Madin Brenin believes.'"},
[2469]={"Breaking the News","Faltharan is located at the steps to Tol Ciryarani.\
\
You should speak with Faltharan.","Talk to Faltharan","Faltharan looks to you, and lets loose a relieved sigh.\
\
'Very good. It pains me to know that my father is still missing, but I will try to carry on his legacy as best I can. The bloodline of Sirgon shall endure.\
\
'We have tough days ahead of us, but no matter what, Pelargir will stand as a testament to Gondor's defiance in the face of war.'","'You have done Gondor a great service today, ${PLAYER}. The lordship of Pelargir has survived its greatest challenge, and we are now ready for what is next.\
\
'Please inform the Lord-Regent that we located his family, and that we have people tending to their injuries. I am sure that Faltharan would appreciate the news coming from you.'","DNT Not Used","Now that Faltharan's family is safe from the Corsairs, you have been asked personally to deliver the good news."},
[2470]={"Aid Spakorth in learning the fates of his brethren in the Oath-taker's Horn","Aid Gimli in freeing the Stout-axes who refuse to follow King Greytooth","'Our hand is forced, ${PLAYER}. The Dwarves of Mordor have been turned against themselves! Váskmun's treachery cannot go unanswered! \
\
'We must stop the Firehorns from seeking the Dwarf-ring. No matter their supposed might, some family heirlooms are best forgotten, I think. It is not unlike the axe of mithril, Zigilburk, of which you once spoke. If the search does not bring them to ruin, finding it will not change their fortunes! If the Men of Mordor still desire the Ring, they shall not rest until it is recovered - whether it is by their own hands or taken from those foolish enough to wield it in Mordor. No matter where he leads them, Váskmun is putting his folk into great danger. The fool would lead his people into the fires of Mount Doom if he thought the dwarf-ring might be hidden there!\
\
'These Firehorns are even worse than the Dourhands we encountered in our adventures, my friend. At least I knew where I stood with the Dourhands! Perhaps Legolas was right after all....\
\
'It is decided then! For the good of the Dwarves of Mordor, we must storm the Oath-taker's Horn!'","At the command of King Greytooth, the Stout-axes have taken a new name: the Firehorns. In a mad fervour, they now make ready to set out in search of the lost Dwarf-ring, Manthríf.","Talk to Gimli in the Oath-taker's Horn","Aid Gimli in hindering the Firehorn smiths","Gimli might be found in the heights of the Oath-taker's Horn.\
\
You have done much to hinder the Stout-axes loyal to King Greytooth and aid those who have defied him. You should now seek Gimli in the Oath-taker's Horn.","Gimli and Spakorth can be found along the causeway outside the Oath-taker's Horn in Dor Amarth.\
\
Gimli and Spakorth have asked you to aid them in hindering the Firehorns in their quest to recover the lost Dwarf-ring, Manthríf.","Breaking the Oath-taker's Horn","'It was no easy task, but I have brought Spakorth hither unharmed! Where is Váskmun?'\
\
You tell Gimli and Spakorth that Váskmun has led an army of Firehorns onto the plains of Dor Amarth. Gimli lets out an indignant snort, and Spakorth falls silent.\
\
'Bah! We came all this way to stop his quest, and we haven't stopped a thing!'"},
[2471]={"Talk to Tordoron to the north of Cirith Negen","Destroyed bear-traps along the road through Cirith Negen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, you have come.\
\
'You have made the roadway safe for our allies, but I fear the Khundolar will not be so easily deterred. They have made camp along the slopes of the Ephel Dúath and have readied their defences. Their numbers are many, even with so many of their forces spread across the northern wilds of Ithilien.\
\
'We must strike soon or it shall become all but impossible to drive them out.'","The Khundolar have devised a trap for the Host of the West and have laid cruel bear-traps along the road through Cirith Negen.","Bear-traps can be found along the road through Cirith Negen in north-eastern North Ithilien.\
\
Anborn has asked you to investigate reports that the path through Cirith Negen is being readied for a Khundolar ambush. You should disarm traps and defeat any foes you encounter.","Destroy bear-traps along the road through Cirith Negen (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Breaking the Trap","Tordoron can be found to the north of Cirith Negen.\
\
You have disarmed the traps and fought off Khundolar trapping the pass of Cirith Negen. You should now seek out Tordoron beyond the pass.","'${PLAYER}, I have received a troubling report from my Ranger, Tordoron.\
\
'He sent word that the Khundolar have laid traps along the roadway through Cirith Negen. Mere traps could not stop the Host of the West, but I fear that they may soon devise a greater scheme to hinder our allies. The pass provides swift passage to the north, but it is narrow and any that pass through it must fear an ambush.\
\
'I would ask that you scout Cirith Negen and destroy any traps you find. If the Khundolar are still trapping the pass, you must defeat them as well. Nothing can be left to chance, my friend, especially now that the Enemy has suffered his greatest defeat in recent memory.\
\
'When that is done, seek Tordoron and aid him as you may. He has scouted the pass of Cirith Negen and now searches the northern reaches of Ithilien for the Enemy's encampment.'"},
[2473]={"'It is good news that you bring. I do not fear so much now for the safety of my people.'","Thurbald is hiding to the south of Uvel-cadlus.\
\
You should return to Thurbald with news of your success.","A company of Dragon-clan warriors is encamped at the northern end of the Gravenwood, marching down from Enedwaith.","Crates of black fire can be found within Uvel-cadlus.\
\
Thurbald has asked you to enter Uvel-cadlus and destroy the Draig-lûth's supply of black fire.","Destroy crates of black fire (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Breath of the Dragon","Talk to Thurbald","Destroyed crates of black fire (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have seen wagons bearing crates coming from the south to Uvel-cadlus. I wondered at first why the Dunlendings would be bringing provisions and supplies northward to a company that is moving southward towards their muster, but later I saw something that terrified me.\
\
'The Draig-lûth took from the crates a black powder which they were able to ignite into a terrible fire which scorched tree and earth and shattered stone. I fear the Dragon-clan will use this black fire against our people, should all-out war ensue.\
\
'Will you enter Uvel-cadlus and destroy this black fire? The Rohirrim would be greatly indebted to you if you should succeed.'"},
[2474]={"'Derrota a los Orcos Blogmal y Krahjarn al norte de Gabilshathûr. Es solo una gota en el mar en comparación con sus números, pero si logramos distraerlos de nuestro refugio, habremos ganado algo de respiro... al menos, eso espero.'","'¿Viniste solo desde el oeste? Supongo que hay más en ti de lo que uno imaginaría a simple vista.\
\
'Aquí, realmente podrías ayudarnos. Estoy encargado de la protección de Gabilshathûr, y esto se ha vuelto un gran desafío desde que un explorador orco descubrió nuestro puesto hace unos días. Ahora los Orcos nos hostigan constantemente, y no estoy seguro de cuánto tiempo más podremos resistir.\
\
'Si puedes matar a algunos de esos Orcos, podríamos ganar algo de respiro. No soy exigente, matar a cualquier Orco Blogmal o Krahjarn que encuentres en el este de Malenhad será suficiente... aunque para ser más útil, deberías matar a algunos de sus guerreros y hostigadores. Ah, y también a algunos profanadores...'","Hostigadores orcos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El refugio enano de Gabilshathûr está en grave peligro. Un ejército de Orcos no está lejos, y grupos de incursión orcos están hostigando el puesto.","Profanadores orcos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hay Orcos Blogmal y Krahjarn por todo el este de Malenhad, al norte de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Gisur te ha pedido que derrotes a muchos Orcos para intentar dar algo de respiro a los enanos de Gabilshathûr.","Derrota Hostigadores Orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El capitán de la guardia Gisur está en Gabilshathûr, al sur de Duvuinen.\
\
Has derrotado a un gran número de Orcos y deberías regresar con Gisur para informarle de tu éxito.","Derrota Guerreros Orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Tiempo para un respiro","Guerreros orcos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota Profanadores Orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Ah, bien, has regresado! Lo has hecho bien, pero temo que tus esfuerzos hayan sido en vano. ¡Los Orcos se están acercando!'"},
[2480]={"Los carpinteros de Bree se enorgullecen de la calidad de su trabajo","Lleva la lanza de Bree a Marga Maderín","'¿Ya has terminado de encontrar la lanza de Bree? Ya veo...'","'Te pedí que me trajeras una lanza de Bree, ¡pero no esperaba que completaras el encargo tan rápido! Veamos... bien equilibrada, afilada, y con un astil hecho de fresno negro. ¡Esta lanza de Bree será un arma formidable contra los bandidos!\
\
'Los carpinteros de Bree se sienten honrados de tener un arma así en nuestras reservas, ${PLAYER}.'","'Los carpinteros de Bree han estado trabajando hasta el agotamiento desde que esos bandidos empezaron a causar problemas. Verás, el Vigilante Jefe Grimbriar ha ordenado a todos los carpinteros de Bree y de las aldeas cercanas que fabriquen lanzas de Bree para protegernos de futuros ataques.\
\
'Ahora bien, no soy de los que desobedecen las órdenes del Vigilante Jefe Grimbriar, pero simplemente no aceptaré ninguna lanza que no esté hecha de fresno negro. Cada vez es más difícil encontrar fresno negro, pues tantos recién llegados a las Tierras de Bree están talando los mejores árboles para construir nuevas casas. Sin fresno negro, temo que los astiles de las lanzas no serán lo bastante resistentes.\
\
'Si tienes la suerte de encontrar algo de fresno negro, los Hombres de Bree te quedaríamos en deuda si nos trajeras lanzas de Bree para ayudarnos a reforzar la defensa contra nuevos ataques.'","Recoge una lanza de Bree","Lanza de Bree — Introducción","Marga Maderín está en el Pabellón de Caza de Bree, al oeste de la Puerta Sur.\
\
Maggie Maderín te ha pedido que le lleves una lanza de Bree para ayudar a los carpinteros de Bree a armar a los Vigilantes."},
[2481]={"De Bree a Puente de Caballetes","La ciudad de Puente de Caballetes está amenazada por el Enemigo y necesita ayuda desde lejos.","'¿Te envió Bree, eh? Es bueno saber que nuestros mensajeros llegaron sanos y salvos. Y ahora que estás aquí, es bueno tener otro brazo armado para la causa.'","'¿Has oído hablar de Puente de Caballetes, al norte? Su ubicación lo convierte en un objetivo tentador para los asaltantes orcos y los bandidos. Estoy seguro de que tu ayuda en su defensa sería muy apreciada.\
\
'Reúne tus pertenencias y viaja al norte hasta Puente de Caballetes. El Camino Verde es la ruta más expedita y la más transitada. Mantente en él y deberías estar a salvo.\
\
'Cuando llegues, busca al guardia Otley. Él te indicará la dirección correcta.'","Puente de Caballetes se encuentra al norte, a lo largo de la ruta llamada Camino Verde. \
\
Habla con el guardia Otley en Puente de Caballetes y averigua cómo puedes ayudar en la defensa de la ciudad."},
[2482]={"Huevos de dragonzuelo destruidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Drake eggs litter the landscape of the Withered Heath.","Destruye los huevos de dragonzuelo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should destroy any drake eggs that you find on the Withered Heath.","Destroyed many drake eggs.","You have successfully destroyed many drake eggs on the Withered Heath. The Zhélruka will surely be thankful of your efforts.","Completado","Drake eggs litter the landscape of the Withered Heath. Destroying the eggs within these ancient drake breeding grounds should lessen the impact of dragonkind in the Grey Mountains.","Breeding Grounds"},
[2483]={"Talk to Fotri","Fotri will lead you to the dragon Bregmor's corpse.","'You are indeed welcome here, and heartily! But what in the long leagues has brought you so far north?'\
\
You tell Fotri that you are looking for the remains of the dragon Bregmor.\
\
'Ah, I see. We keep close guard upon the dragon's corpse, but you do not have the look of someone planning any mischief or wickedness, so I will take you there... though under the watch of my wary eye, all the same.'","'Bones, stolen from Bregmor's corpse? And you are quite sure it was the work of this Karazgar? It is not that I disbelieve you, ${CLASS}, for the bones are missing clear enough, now that you have pointed it out. But out from under our noses!\
\
'This is a fell and devious foe you hunt, and I wish you all the fortune there is in your contest against him!'","You should speak with Fotri, who can be found in Forochel.","Bregmor's Legacy","'The bitter cold of Forochel has preserved the dragon marvelously well. Come, and you will see with your own eyes.'"},
[2484]={"'I believe that while the creatures that hunt the valley to the north-east may still be difficult to deal with, Heilun Brenin's defeat may make the Draig-lûth less of a concern.\
\
'Thank you from the depths of my heart for all of your help. You will be remembered and spoken of well by me among the Uch-lûth.'","Defeated Heilun Brenin's personal guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Heilun Brenin","'Within the village of Gwâl Draig, there must be someone who has set his people to this course of action. It is my hope that by defeating the brenin of the Draig-lûth these folk will no longer harass the Uch-lûth. \
\
'Before his disappearance, my chief scout discovered Heilun Brenin and his guards standing near a large bonfire at the centre of their encampment.\
\
'Seek out Heilun Brenin and his men and dispatch them, then return to me.'","Talk to Gronu at his camp","'Heilun Brenin is a vile monster and should be punished for the wicked deeds he has committed against the Uch-lûth and Turch-lûth.'","Heilun Brenin and his guards can be found at the centre of Gwâl Draig, east of Gronu's camp.\
\
Gronu asked you to defeat Heilun Brenin and his personal guards.","Defeat Heilun Brenin","Brenin of the Draig-lûth","Defeat Heilun Brenin's personal guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gronu's camp lies to the west of Gwâl Draig, beneath Harndirion.\
\
You should seek out the Gronu and inform him that Heilun Brenin and his men have been defeated.","Within Gwâl Draig, there must be a leader driving his people to perform such cruel acts upon the clans of the Algraig."},
[2486]={"Bandidos y semiorcos derrotados en Andrath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Vigilantes Hojafrágil y Robledales se encuentran ocultos al este del extremo norte de las ruinas.\
\
Has llevado justicia a los miserables en las ruinas de la Atalaya Sur y ahora debes regresar con el Vigilante Hojafrágil.","Semiorcos y bandidos pueden encontrarse en las ruinas de Andrath.\
\
El Vigilante Hojafrágil está enfurecido por las acciones de los bandidos y semiorcos que ocupan las ruinas de la Atalaya Sur y quiere que asestes un golpe decisivo contra ellos.","'No podemos devolver la vida a quienes fueron tomados, pero podemos descansar sabiendo que se ha hecho justicia en alguna medida.\
\
'No puedo decir que el futuro de las Tierras de Bree sea más brillante, pues incluso ahora veo que las filas de este enemigo crecen para reemplazar a los que fueron purgados. Las Tierras de Bree están en grave peligro por este Zarquino.'","'Haré que estas bestias paguen con la sangre que han derramado. Descarga nuestra venganza sobre ellas.'","'Grimbriar hizo bien en enviarnos aquí, pero pensamos que llegaría más apoyo una vez que se diera cuenta de que no podíamos enviar informes. Tus noticias sobre lo que ocurre en el norte dejan claro que los bandidos se están infiltrando con las caravanas que dejan pasar.\
\
'Aquellos que no tienen la suerte de contar con monedas para pagar el paso son tratados sin piedad, sus vidas se pierden y sus bienes son reclamados por estas viles criaturas. Tu información confirma lo que temíamos. Los tipos morenos entre ellos son semiorcos, ¡bestias repugnantes!\
\
'Ha llegado el momento de devolver el golpe por cada vida que estas bestias han arrebatado. Adéntrate en las ruinas y purga a este enemigo. Me aseguraré de que recibas una buena recompensa.'","Derrota bandidos y semiorcos en Andrath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las preocupaciones del Vigilante Hojafrágil sobre los bandidos en la Atalaya Sur se ven confirmadas por la gran cantidad de enemigos que pululan por las ruinas. Te ha pedido que contraataques, debilitando sus fuerzas y dando a los Vigilantes de Bree una oportunidad justa para proteger el campo.","Bandidos y semiorcos","'No puedo imaginar el terror que deben sentir las caravanas al acercarse a este lugar. Temo que no podamos contener esta marea por mucho tiempo. Las Tierras de Bree tendrán que buscar aliados en otra parte.'","Habla con el Vigilante Hojafrágil"},
[2488]={"Derrota a los bandidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Brigands in the Bolt-holes","Brigands are hiding out in the Bolt-holes.","As you approach the Bolt-holes, you recall a conversation you overheard on the road...\
\
--\
\
'Why 'The Bolt-holes?'' This from a younger woman in hand-me-down armour and threadbare boots.\
\
Her travelling companion, whose grey cloak obscured her appearance, worked some jerky in the corner of her mouth before answering. 'If the guard are after you, you bolt into a hole. You know, to hide. So if you commit a crime in Ethring or Barad Rill, 'The Bolt-holes' are where you go when you need to hide.'\
\
'I suppose…'\
\
'You don't like the name?'\
\
'I think it sounds silly. Out east I heard there's a group of bandits making camp in a place called 'Thama Aklam'. That sounds so much more impressive.'\
\
Grey Cloak sighed. 'It only sounds more impressive because the name isn't in Westron. Everyone who knows only one tongue thinks words from other languages to be dramatic and special just because they sound different. 'Thama Aklam' likely means something boring like 'The Big Camp.'\
\
'As if you know more than one language,' Threadbare Boots scoffed.\
\
'I do,' Grey Cloak said. 'For example, Nustatyë ve linquë tauramundo.'\
\
'What does that mean?'\
\
'It means, 'Your beauty outmatches the stars themselves' in Quenya.'\
\
'Oh,' Threadbare Boots said, blushing. 'I think you are beautiful too.'\
\
--\
\
Which is all to say, you may want to defeat some brigands in The Bolt-holes.","Bandidos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have defeated many brigands in the Bolt-holes, making it safer for all who travel between Dor-en-Ernil and Ringló Vale.","Completado","Discover the Bolt-holes","Brigands are hiding out in the Bolt-holes.\
\
Defeat brigands.","You have defeated many brigands in the Bolt-holes."},
[2489]={"'Your timing is sound, ${PLAYER}. We have only just returned from patrolling the area.\
\
'The enemy is indeed present and will be upon us soon. Prepare yourself... their numbers are greater than we imagined!'","Talk to Reeve Fríthild","Talk to Reeve Fríthild at her camp","'Yet another faithful retainer has perished. Captain Grimmar was the backbone of my garrison... he will be greatly missed.\
\
'We must make the White Hand pay for its treachery! I will return to Stoke at once... meet me there, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to the Reeve of Stoke","'It was a waste of time and effort -- and a life -- to harry the goblins. Saruman and Mordor both breed them like flies. There is a closer threat that will eat at us like a canker.\
\
'My scouts tell me that half-blood brigands from the Stonedeans are attempting to infiltrate Stoke and sway the people against Reeve Fríthild. This threat must be put to end, or we will see the Dunlendings marching upon this town.'","Use the camp-fire to summon Reeve Fríthild and her companions","<rgb=#FF0000>Reeve Fríthild has been defeated</rgb>","'These brigands which Grimmar speaks of, are they the same that troubled Oserley and infiltrated Torsbury? Then, indeed, I agree with him. This is a treachery that can only harm the people of the Acres.\
\
'I will gather our companions and ride out to meet these villains. Join us at our encampment to the south of town.'","The Council of Stoke determined that Reeve Fríthild should take to the field and lead her people against their aggressors, but now it must choose what front to focus upon.","'I am grateful for your assistance, ${PLAYER}, but the time has come for a greater show of strength.'","Reeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke.\
\
You should bring Captain Grimmar's recommendation to Reeve Fríthild.","<rgb=#FF0000>Reeve Fríthild must survive</rgb>","Brigands in the Wild","Reeve Fríthild is at her encampment to the south of Stoke.\
\
You should speak with Reeve Fríthild regarding the battle.","You have successfully defended Reeve Fríthild","Reeve Fríthild is at her encampment to the south of Stoke, just off the road on the other side of the bridge on the road to Kingstead.\
\
Reeve Fríthild asked you to meet her at her encampment.","DNT -- Player should never see","The Reeve of Stoke is in the Mead Hall.\
\
The Reeve instructed you to meet in Stoke to plan for the next attack."},
[2490]={"Explora pasadizos intactos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cartel colocado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Futuros prometedores, vías oscuras","Las vías acaban en un pasadizo sin salida","El túnel se encuentra justo al oeste del campamento de Gufi, y se puede llegar a él siguiendo las vías que conducen directamente hasta allí.\
\
Gufi te ha pedido que explores el túnel hacia el que se adentran las vías.","El pasadizo está intacto, pero notas que en este túnel en concreto se respira un aire de inquietud","'¿Temor, dices? ¡Bah! ¡Un enano no teme un poco de monotonía en el interior de una mina! Según tú, ese es el mejor y único camino, ¡así que ahí es donde empezaremos! Te agradezco tu informe, ${PLAYER}, por muy absurdo que haya sido tu modo de expresarlo!'","Gufi confía en que los enanos podrán recuperar Moria rápidamente. Está deseando explorar posibles yacimientos mineros.","En los túneles de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, cerca de los pasadizos sin salida, hay carteles.\
\
Deberías colocar los carteles donde las vías conducen a pasadizos sin salida.","Gufi se encuentra en el campamento central de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Deberías volver a ver a Gufi con los resultados de tu reconocimiento.","'¡Ah, saludos, ${RACE}! Soy Gufi, a tu servicio. Te digo que es un gran día para ser enano, ¡y me siento privilegiado de poder presenciar en persona la reconquista de Khazad-dûm!\
\
'Al llegar aquí, me fijé en la vía que se extiende directamente hacia el oeste. Intuyo que allí hay yacimientos mineros sin explotar, pues las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata son las más ricas de toda Moria, y probablemente de toda la Tierra Media.\
\
'¿Serías tan amable de explorar posibles caminos en los túneles y colocar carteles en los pasadizos sin salida para que sepamos por dónde empezar nuestra búsqueda?'","Explora pasadizos sin salida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'No tiene sentido seguir adelante hasta que hayamos tenido la oportunidad de explorar nuestras mejores opciones.'","Vuelve con Gufi","Pon carteles en los pasadizos sin salida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2491]={"'¿Dónde están esos productos de enano que pedí?'","Azufre y chispas","'¡Eres demasiado valiente, ${PLAYER}! Primero lobos, y ahora un oso. Deberías ser más firme con esta gente y hacer que se ocupen de sus propios problemas de una vez por todas.\
\
'Muy bien. Por último, pero no menos importante, necesitaré algo de azufre y limaduras de hierro. No se encuentra azufre por aquí, así que siempre voy a los enanos para conseguir esas cosas. También pueden proporcionar las limaduras más baratas que cualquiera de los herreros locales, así que esta vez resolveremos dos problemas a la vez.\
\
'Por favor, dirígete a Ojo de Aguja y habla con el comerciante enano Onar. He tratado con él en el pasado, y me imagino que podrá darnos lo que necesitamos.'","'Parece que te sorprende, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, pero no debería ser así. Si un enano dice que puede proporcionarte un tipo particular de producto, puedes contar con él para que te lo consiga. Lleva el azufre y las limaduras de hierro a Hyacinth Tuk en Alforzaburgo tan pronto como puedas.'","Dado que Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón pagó para adquirir los ingredientes para sus fuegos artificiales, Hyacinth Tuk te ha reclutado para que la ayudes a reunirlos.","Hyacinth Tuk está en Alforzaburgo, cerca de los Grandes Smials.\
\
Hyacinth Tuk te envió a Ojo de Aguja para conseguir azufre y limaduras de hierro del comerciante enano Onar. Onar hizo un trato rápido y justo y te ha enviado de vuelta con sus paquetes.","'Será mejor que le digas a Lobelia que todos los ingredientes han sido comprados y que sus fuegos artificiales estarán listos en tres meses.'","Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón está en su casa de Bolsón Cerrado, en Hobbiton.\
\
Con tu ayuda, Hyacinth Tuk ya tiene todo lo que necesita para empezar a preparar los fuegos artificiales de Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón. Te ha pedido que vuelvas con Lobelia para informarle de que sus fuegos artificiales estarán listos en tres meses.","Lleva azufre y limaduras de hierro a Hyacinth Tuk","'Por favor, ve a Ojo de Aguja para recoger el azufre y las limaduras de hierro de Onar.'","'¡Oh! ¡Así que la pequeña Hyacinth quiere más ingredientes para sus bonitas luces! ¿Quiere ser maga, no? ¡Ja!\
\
'Pues resulta que tengo azufre y limaduras para vender, y a un precio muy razonable, además. Díselo a todos tus amigos, las condiciones son muy sencillas...\
\
'¿Qué? No te quedes ahí ${PLAYERNAME:parado como un tonto[m]|parada como una tonta[f]} con la boca abierta. ¿De verdad creías que te iba a enviar a cumplir una misión o alguna otra hazaña por cosas tan simples? Toma estos paquetes y... ¡que tengas un buen día!'","'¡Tres meses! ¡Tres meses! ¡Eso no vale! ¡No vale en absoluto! ¡Mi cumpleaños es en dos meses! ¿Lo entiendes? ¡Dos!'","'Bueno, bueno, no fue tan difícil, ¿verdad? ¡Y te mantuviste firme con él! \
\
'¡Empezaré con estos fuegos artificiales de inmediato! ¡Dile a esa vieja bruja que debería tener todo lo que necesita en solo tres meses!'","El comerciante enano Onar está en la aldea de Ojo de Aguja, en la esquina noroeste del Pantano de los Juncos.\
\
A Hyacinth solo le falta el azufre y las limaduras de hierro para empezar a preparar los fuegos artificiales de Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón. Te ha sugerido que podrías conseguirlos de Onar, un comerciante enano."},
[2492]={"Do not allow the catapult to be destroyed","The enemy has constructed heavy siege ladders that are able to be attached securely to the wall. Once the ladders are attached, Goblin Bombers and Orc Berserkers will be able to quickly scale the wall and mount a massive assault. Destroying the hooks will be essential to detaching the menacing ladders. The enemy has also sent a group of Trolls to assault the tower from behind, which pose a danger to the catapult, the ammo caches, and the tower guards.\
\
Merit Rating\
\
This quest starts with <rgb=#FFFF00>Full</rgb> Merit Rating.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Major Merit Loss</rgb>\
* An enemy powder keg detonates\
* A catapult guard is defeated\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Minor Merit Loss</rgb>\
* An enemy powder keg is ignited\
* A catapult ammo cache is destroyed\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Minor Merit Gain</rgb>\
* An enemy powder keg is diffused","Ladder disabled (${VALUE}/10)","Saruman's army has constructed a large ladder with the ability to latch itself to the wall, making it difficult to detach. Destroy the hooks on the ladders and render them useless, and defeat the war trolls as they ascend to launch their assault.","Bring Down the Siege Ladders","Disable Siege Ladders (${VALUE}/10)","Do not allow powder kegs to detonate (${VALUE}/5)","Defeat Trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[2493]={"'It is interesting that these spirits spoke to you upon presenting them with the amulet, but it does lend credence to a belief that I have held. These shades are held here due to an ancient rheg -- curse -- upon their people. \
\
'Perhaps we might free these poor spirits from their sorrowful state?'","Talk to Lhudd at the Hall of Sanctuary","'I thank you again for recovering both pieces of this amulet. I have a feeling that, once repaired, this may weaken the shades that patrol the barrows in the Lich Bluffs. \
\
'To the north-west, there are many shades that stand vigil over several barrows. For some reason, these creatures are not aggressive, unless provoked. \
\
'Seek out a couple of these shades and present them with the amulet. If you should learn anything, return to me with your knowledge.'","Present the amulet to the mournful shade","'Have you presented the amulet to the shades yet, Duvodiad?'","Lhudd is at the Hall of Sanctuary, south-east of the barrows.\
\
You should return to Lhudd and explain the happenings outside of the barrows.","Present the amulet to the sorrowful shade","Bring Them to Rest","The sorrowful and mournful shades can be found to the north-west of the Hall of Sanctuary, near the entrances of several barrows on the ridge above.\
\
Lhudd has asked you to present the shades with the broken amulet that you recovered and observe what unfolds.","Throughout the Lich Bluffs, the despondant shades of ancient Algraig clansmen watch over ancient barrows. Perhaps the amulet that you recovered may begin to unravel the mystery of the Oathbreakers that plague the land."},
[2496]={"Bringing Beasts to Bear","'The mines are fallen to Angmar again and I will not stand for it, ${PLAYER}. We must get the mine back.\
\
'I suggest that we use the drakes stalking the depths as cover for our attack. Search the lands south of Tol Ascarnen or west and south on the plains of the Steps of Gram for the Thistledown grazers. Collect haunches from those beasts and deliver them to a flat stone near where the Tyrant holding the mine keeps his company.\
\
'The blood from the haunches should draw the drakes within range of the foe and bring about the battle needed to bring these foes down!'","Collect Thistledown Haunches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Place the Thistledown haunches on the flat stone in the Isendeep","Collect Thistledown Haunch (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Free People control the mine, there is no reason to bring the beasts to bear.","Free People must not control the Mine","Angmar once again holds the Isendeep Mine and Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn believes that the time has come to purge them from the depths to take the mine back for the Free People. He suggests a drastic measure to do so in an effort to defeat the foe.","The haunches are placed, the drakes are sure to come. You should hide.","Search the areas south of Tol Ascarnen or west along the plains, south of Dâr-gazag for the Thistledown Grazers. Collect some of their haunches and bring them to the slab within the depths of the Isendeep.\
\
Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn believes that the drakes can be used against the Orcs of Angmar and wishes to use them as a diversion while you attack the Tyrant."},
[2498]={"Crashing rocks clog the tunnel","Blow up the south-western tunnel","The tunnel is blocked!","'Much as I wish to be free of this dank place, we still have work to do. From what I've overheard, this tribe of Ronkrúm goblins recently tunnelled to the surface, and if we don't send them back underground they shall continue to spill over into Pinnath Gelin.\
\
'These wretched louts are industrious, but lazy creatures, and they rely heavily on their black powder to blast open new tunnels in the mountainside. We can use this against them! Go and gather cases from around the cave and their camp outside. Then, delve deeper into the mountain until you find the places from whence they come. Between sealing these off and the punishment you shall be dealing out, they will be hesitant to continue their plans to surface.\
\
'My wound is troubling, but I think I can walk now. I shall meet you outside the cave when you are done.'","Collected barrels of black powder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect barrels of black powder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The black powder did a fine job of blocking the south-western tunnel. You should move on to the western tunnel and blow that one up as well.\
\
The western tunnel is in the Krauzhaf cave in Pinnath Gelin.","You have battled your way through Krauzhaf and blown up the three tunnels that the Ronkrúm goblins were using to crawl out of the mountain.\
\
Igerna is waiting to speak with you outside the Krauzhaf cave, in Pinnath Gelin.","With both the western and south-western tunnels blocked, you have but one left.\
\
You should blow up the north-western tunnel in the Krauzhaf cave in Pinnath Gelin.","Bringing Down the Mountain","'I heard the explosions from here! May that make them think twice about coming to the lands of Gondor.'","Crashing rocks choke the tunnel","Speak to Igerna outside the cave","Left unchecked, the Ronkrúm goblin horde will continue to crawl out from the depths of the mountain, onto the rolling green hills of Pinnath Gelin.","Blow up the western tunnel","With a hefty supply of dangerously explosive barrels of black powder, you are ready to seal off some of the goblins' tunnels.\
\
You should start with the south-western tunnel, in the cave in Pinnath Gelin.","Blow up the north-western tunnel","Igerna has asked you to gather barrels of the goblins' black powder.\
\
Barrels can be found in the camp outside, as well as inside, the cave at Krauzhaf, in Pinnath Gelin."},
}
